{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.770915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0051a1adbe08c96111922dea142fa5738df798885969717d0b48a352e228a7b7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 43 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the same parameters as in Definition \ref{Def.ParametersBulk}. Fix $m \in \mathbb{N}$, $t_1, \dots, t_m \in [0, \infty)$ with $t_1 < t_2 < \cdots < t_m$, and set $\mathcal{T} = \{t_1, \dots, t_m\}$. We also define for $t \in \mathcal{T}$ the quantity $T_{t} = T_t(N) =  \lfloor t N^{2/3} \rfloor$ and the lattice $\Lambda_t(N) = a_t(N) \cdot \mathbb{Z} + b_t(N)$, where 
\begin{equation}
a_t(N) = \sigma_1^{-1} N^{-1/3}, \mbox{ and } b_t(N) = \sigma_1^{-1} N^{-1/3} \cdot \left( - h_1 N - p_1 T_{t} \right).
\end{equation}

We let $\mathbb{P}_N$ be the Pfaffian Schur process from Definition \ref{Def.SchurProcess}. Here, we assume that $M = M(N)$ is sufficiently large so that $M \geq T_{t_m}$. If $(\lambda^0, \dots, \lambda^M)$ have law $\mathbb{P}_N$, we define the random variables
\begin{equation}
X_i^{j,N} = \sigma_1^{-1} N^{-1/3} \cdot \left( \lambda_i^{T_{t_j}} - h_1 N - p_1 T_{t_j}  - i\right) \mbox{ for } i \in \mathbb{N} \mbox{ and } j \in \llbracket 1, m \rrbracket.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.331426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00521a33c2266185c239efb2f1f85def1465a411696fbe4fabec3df9a17e2580","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:riccati of arXiv:2605.03703, 'Scaling Limits of Bivariate Nearly-Unstable Hawkes Processes and Applications to Rough Vol'] Let $w:[0,1]\to\mathbb R$ be bounded measurable with
\begin{equation}
\sup_{t\le1}\int_0^tK(t-s)\,|w(s)|\,ds\ \le\ \frac{3\rho}{4}.
\end{equation}
Then the equation
$\varpi=K*\bigl(w+\tfrac{\nu^2}{2}\varpi^2\bigr)$ has a unique solution
$\varpi\in C([0,1])$ with $\|\varpi\|_\infty\le\rho$.  The smallness
condition~(equation eq:small-drive of the paper) holds in each of the following two cases:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item $\|w\|_\infty\le\varepsilon_0$;
\item $w=c\,\mathbf 1_J$ for a constant $c>0$ and an interval
$J\subseteq[0,1]$ with $c\int_0^{|J|}K(r)\,dr\le 3\rho/4$.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, (equation eq:riccati of the paper) has a unique solution with
$\|\varpi\|_\infty\le\rho$ whenever $\|u\|_\infty\le\varepsilon_0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.786416+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00540bde4ff69b2fac18d6610fb14ff135e79a770da6146d72b9bf3d97736e0c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:mf_theta_fbsde of arXiv:2507.22577, 'A Mean-Field Theory of $\Theta$-Expectations'] Let $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}^k$ be the initial state and $\Phi: \mathbb{R}^k \to \mathbb{R}$ be the terminal cost function. Let the coefficients be functions $b: [0,T] \times \Omega \times \mathbb{R}^k \times E_A \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{R}^k$, $\sigma: [0,T] \times \Omega \times \mathbb{R}^k \times E_A \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{R}^{k \times d}$, and $F: [0,T] \times \Omega \times \mathbb{R}^k \times \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R}^{d} \times E_A \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{R}$. A solution to the Mean-Field $\Theta$-FBSDE is a quadruple of $\mathbb{F}$-adapted processes $(X, Y, Z, A)$ valued in $\mathbb{R}^k \times \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R}^{d} \times E_A$ that satisfies, $P_0$-a.s., the following coupled system:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{(Forward Evolution):} For all $t \in [0,T]$,
    \begin{equation} 
        X_t = x_0 + \int_0^t b(s, X_s, A_s, \mu_s) \mathrm{d} s + \int_0^t \sigma(s, X_s, A_s, \mu_s) \mathrm{d} B_s.
    \end{equation}

    \item \textbf{(Backward Evolution):} For all $t \in [0,T]$,
    \begin{equation} 
        Y_t = \Phi(X_T) + \int_t^T F(s, X_s, Y_s, Z_s, A_s, \mu_s) \mathrm{d} s - \int_t^T Z_s \mathrm{d} B_s.
    \end{equation}
    In both equations, $\mu_s := \Law_{P_0}(Y_s)$ is the law of the value process $Y$ at time $s$.

    \item \textbf{(Pointwise Optimality):} For almost every $(t,\omega) \in [0,T] \times \Omega$,
    \begin{equation} 
        A_t(\omega) \in \underset{a \in \mathcal{U}_{g(\mu_t)}}{\argmax} \; F(t, \omega, X_t(\omega), Y_t(\omega), Z_t(\omega), a, \mu_t).
    \end{equation}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.724863+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0054b28e407cb4a2095f0f08594508aa24d985f12442f2462ae63dbec4f2089d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:dist_across_chain of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1 > 0$. There exists $N\in\mathbf{N}$ such that the following is true. Let $\widetilde{z}\in D$ and $\delta>0$ such that $B(\widetilde{z},\delta) \subseteq D$, and let $\lambda \in (0,1]$. Let $\widetilde{G}_{\widetilde{z},\delta,\lambda}$ be the event that there is a set of at most $N$ points $z_1,z_2,\ldots \in A(\widetilde{z},\delta^{1+a_1},\delta)$ with $\abs{z_{i_1}-z_{i_2}} \ge \delta^{1+a_1}$ for each pair $i_1 \neq i_2$ and such that whenever $\eta \cap B(\widetilde{z},\delta^{1+a_1}) \neq \varnothing$, the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item The set $\{z_1,z_2,\ldots\}$ separates $\eta \cap B(\widetilde{z},\delta^{1+a_1})$ from $\partial B(\widetilde{z},\delta)$ in $\Upsilon_\Gamma$.
\item Let $K'$ be any connected component of $\Upsilon_\Gamma \setminus \{z_1,z_2,\ldots\}$ adjacent to $\eta \cap B(\widetilde{z},\delta^{1+a_1})$, and let $i_1,i_2$ so that $z_{i_1},z_{i_2} \in \partial K'$. Let $U'_1 \in \metregions$ be such that $\overline{U'_1}$ contains all \emph{simple} admissible paths within $K'$ from $z_{i_1}$ to $z_{i_2}$. Then
\[ \metapproxacres{\epsilon}{U'_1}{z_{i_1}}{z_{i_2}}{\Gamma} \le \lambda^{{d_{{\mathrm{dbl}}}}}\median{\epsilon}+\lambda^{a_0}\epsilon^{-a_0}\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon} . \]
\end{itemize}
Then $\mathbf{P}[\widetilde{G}_{\widetilde{z},\delta,\lambda}^c] = O((\delta/\lambda)^{{\alpha_{\mathrm{apr}}}})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.030740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00584744a55aaa43f7ba0aff456f824b5012486af4d00fd5faea87c3c9a6812d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma proptfund1 of arXiv:2609.03909, 'Conic Pseudo-Finslerian Mechanical Systems'] Let  $\mathcal{U} \subset TM \setminus 0$ be an open subset invariant under positive scalar multiplication and let$ \mathcal L$ be a Lagrangian, of class $C^2$ on $\mathcal U$, which is positively $2$-homogeneous. Then its fundamental tensor satisfies the following properties:
