{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.751027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0058f4388ea941ef1e2987ae1fd8773987e009ee40a549d6f07a03749f33eda6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2608.18834, 'The Parabolic Anderson Model's Total Mass at Small Times: Geometry, Fluctuations, and Reno'] Suppose that Assumption \ref{Assumption} holds, and
let $\ka>0$ be fixed.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $\rho>0$, then
\begin{align}

\lim_{\th\to0}\mbf E\big[\tfrac{\ka^2}{2}\be^\th_1(B)\big]=\frac{\ka^2\mf b}{(1+\rho)\rho}.
\end{align}
\item If $\rho=0$, then
there exist bounded and continuous functions $\msf b_i:[0,\infty)\to\mbb R$, $(i=1,2)$,
such that for every $\th>0$, one has
\begin{align}

\mbf E\big[\tfrac{\ka^2}{2}\be^\th_1(B)\big]
=
\begin{cases}
\ka^2\mf b\,\ell(\th)+\ka^2\msf b_1(\th)&H_0<1,\\
\ka^2\mf b\,(1+\th)\log(1+1/\th)+\ka^2\msf b_2(\th)&H_0=1,
\end{cases}
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}

\ell(\th)=\frac{1}{2\Ga(H_0)\Ga(1-H_0)}\int_0^{2\pi}\left|\frac{\sin\theta}{\cos\theta}\right|^{2H_0-1}
\Ga_0\Big(\th\big(|\sin\theta|+|\cos\theta|\big)\Big)\d\theta,
\end{align}
and $\Gamma_0$ denotes the zero-parameter upper incomplete Gamma function, i.e.,
\[\Gamma_0(\th)=\int_{\th}^\infty \mr e^{-z}z^{-1}\d z,\qquad \th>0.\]
\item 
If $\rho<0$,
then there exists a bounded and continuous function $\msf z:(0,\infty)\to\mbb R$ such that
for every $\th>0$,
\begin{align}

\mbf E\big[\tfrac{\ka^2}{2}\be^\th_1(B)\big]=\ka^2\mf d\,\th^{\rho}+\,\ka^2\msf z(\th).
\end{align}
Moreover,
$\msf z$ satisfies the limit
\begin{align}

\lim_{\th\to0}\msf z(\th)=
\begin{cases}
\frac{\mf b}{(1+\rho)\rho}&H_0>1/2,\\
0&H_0=1/2.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.944050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00596818bfec88679053a035e33d9e3ef6be319af3d46df6cf37eaf338f165a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Eigenelements of $\Lb$) of arXiv:2606.24599, '\bf Perron--Frobenius theorem for a general tree-valued growth-fragmentation-isolation pro'] There exist $\lab\in\mathbb{R}$ and positive vectors $h,\pi\in\R_{+}^{\TT}$ such that
	\begin{align}
		\Lb^* \pi = \lab  \pi, \qquad \Lb h = \lab h,\qquad \langle\pi,1\rangle=\langle\pi,h\rangle=1.
	\end{align}
	Moreover, for any $\alpha>\max\{0,\frac{\gamma-\theta}{\gamma+\theta}\}$, there exist $c,C>0$, such that for every $\tt\in\TT$ we have
    \begin{equation}

    h(\tt)\geq
    \begin{cases}
    c,&\gamma>\theta\\
    \frac{c}{|\tt|},&\gamma\le\theta
    \end{cases}, 
    \qquad h(\tt)\le C|\tt|^{\alpha},
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}

    \langle\pi,| \, \cdot \,|^2\rangle<+\infty.
    \end{equation}
    In addition, $\lab > 0$ if $\gamma > \theta$, $\lab = 0$ if $\gamma = \theta$, and $\lab < 0$ if $\gamma < \theta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

