{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.250574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_008c05525f3429995aeda0fa45d19119765930b29d0d0dad9b4b976fde6d2f62","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2605.22760, 'Extremes of Gaussian fields with a product term in the variance'] Assume \ref{ass:variance}--\ref{ass:nondegenerate}, let \(\beta=2\), \(0<\alpha<2\), and fix \(c_1,c_2\ge0\).  Define
\[
        p_{\boldsymbol c}(u)
        =\PP\left\{\sup_{\bft\in E}\bigl(X(\bft)-c_1t_1-c_2t_2\bigr)>u\right\},
        \qquad
        a_0=\frac{2\alpha}{\alpha+2}.
\]
Then, as \(u\to\infty\),
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item if \(0<a<a_0\), then
\begin{equation}
        p_{\boldsymbol c}(u)
        \sim
        \calH_\alpha\bigl(L(c_1)+L(c_2)\bigr)
        u^{2/\alpha-1}\Psi(u);
\end{equation}
\item if \(a_0\le a<1\), then
\begin{equation}
        p_{\boldsymbol c}(u)
        \sim
        \calH_\alpha^2\,
        \frac{2(1-a)\Gamma(1/a)}{a^2}\,
        u^{4/\alpha-2/a}\log u\,\Psi(u);
\end{equation}
\item if \(a=1\), then
\begin{equation}
        p_{\boldsymbol c}(u)
        \sim
        \calH_\alpha^2 K(c_1,c_2)
        u^{4/\alpha-2}\Psi(u);
\end{equation}
\item if \(a>1\), then
\begin{equation}
        p_{\boldsymbol c}(u)
        \sim
        \calH_\alpha^2 L(c_1)L(c_2)
        u^{4/\alpha-2}\Psi(u).
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

