{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.916762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_009cb6d7d894ae7d256a46db42e634245908b5acce51d592e05b5ec40ad465c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem rep-value-fct of arXiv:2412.05698, 'Controlled rough SDEs, pathwise stochastic control and dynamic programming principles'] Suppose that  (assum-path-stoch of the paper) holds. Then $ \bar{\mathcal{V}}$ given by (equation mv' of the paper) is a continuous modification of both $\mathcal{V}^1$ and $\mathcal{V}^2$ with a.s. regularity inherited by the regularity of $\mathcal{V}$ provided by  (thm:RoughValueReg of the paper). In particular, 
