{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.127226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00adbe9cfcb25557c0c2970ed307818b3a77c511fa48b47ab979266d1157d061","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2608.26662, 'Boundary–Moment Universality and Curvature Corrections in Random Geometric Graphs on Riema'] For each fixed admissible $\mathfrak h$, there are $C<\infty$ and $r_0>0$
