{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.309029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00d54f7fe643794ace93bc23cfe7ba3a26c0f3ba71fa40b24408f997e7e7d31c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Concentration of empirical reward mean) of arXiv:2608.21995, '2608.21995'] Fix any state $s$ and action $a\in \mathcal{A}(s)$ with $N(s,a)$ visits, the $i^{th}$ visit receives reward $\hat r_i(s,a)$. Let $\bar r(s,a) = \frac{1}{N(s,a)} \sum_{i=1}^{N(s,a)} \hat r_i(s,a)$ be the empirical mean of the rewards, and $r(s,a)$ the true expected reward. Then, for any $\varepsilon>0$, conditional on $N(s,a)$ we have
