{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.475469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00da55a3434f27c8ab2328f2a5e65e7db27d186d7ada50c9185e598e5243a7ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (Marginal and stationary scales) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] For every $n \geq 1$, the centered random part of $X_{n}$ is symmetric $\alpha$-stable with scale
