{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.545813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00f58f02a3598f33f028a194f6f9110abec209489e0f38f7271d386e8e842a63","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:f-basic of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] For $j=1,2$, the functions $F^{(j)}(y_1,y_2,x_1,x_2,x_3)$ are finite and locally bounded. Furthermore, for $\eta$ sampled from $\mu_{\mathbbm{H},y_1, y_2}^\#$ and parameterized by its half-plane capacity, let $g_t:\mathbbm{H}\setminus\eta_t\to\mathbbm{H}$ be the corresponding Loewner map such that $g_t(\eta_t)=W_t$. Then
