{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.190634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00f99323eb5255f3fd6c791b4f4ebac7efe36bfdfb8420b8aeb26c78b602cb78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 44 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ and $d\neq 6$, there exist $\Cl,\Cl, \Cl,\cl>0$ such that for any $v\neq v'\in \widetilde{B}(\Cref{const_additional_lemma_four_point1})$, any sufficiently large $N\ge 1$, and $w,w'\in \widetilde{B}(10N)\setminus \widetilde{B}(N)$ with $|w-w'|\ge N$, 
	 	\begin{equation}
	 		\mathbb{P}\big( \widehat{\mathsf{H}}_{v',w'}^{v,w}   \big)\gtrsim |v-v'|^{\frac{3}{2}}N^{-[(\frac{3d}{2}-1)\boxdot (2d-4)]},
	 	\end{equation}
	 	where $\widehat{\mathsf{H}}_{v',w'}^{v,w}$ is defined as $\mathsf{H}_{v',w'}^{v,w} \cap \{v\xleftrightarrow{\ge 0} \partial B(\Cref{const_additional_lemma_four_point2}N)  \}^c \cap \{v' \xleftrightarrow{\le 0} \partial B(\Cref{const_additional_lemma_four_point2}N) \}^c 
			 	  \cap \big\{ |\widetilde{\phi}_{v}|,|\widetilde{\phi}_{v'}| \in [\cref{const_additional_lemma_four_point4}, \Cref{const_additional_lemma_four_point3}] \big\} $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.151634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00fbb5c3ffb4602a153a4df3e372b54293d1b8a4871a6ee5b1428a3c3465ce53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] Let $P\in Pr(\Omega_{Spin})$ be such that 
