{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.984647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_010804e0f9325ce0542dbded038f43d7862120105d630b891d7f3b2ef28ec280","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 44 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] There exists a constant $g_0 = g_0(\mu) \geq 1$ such that if $\epsilon \geq n^{-1/3}$, $\beta \epsilon \geq (n \log n)^{1/\alpha}$ and $p_0 = (1 + g_0 \epsilon )/n$, then
\begin{equation}
