{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.761950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_011c8964e09dc842e662a28c06d61c63f7f182b48d305b881252eaa526ed0e41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:moment-bound:H^m:d=3 of arXiv:2411.02459, 'Existence and higher regularity of statistically steady states for the stochastic Coleman-'] Let $d\le 3$ and assume the hypotheses of (thm:well-posed of the paper). Suppose further that \nameref{cond:phi:d=3}, \nameref{cond:Q:higher_regularity} hold for $m\ge 2$. Then for all $k=2,\dots,m$ and $n\ge 1$, there exist constants $c_{k,n}$, $C_{k,n}$ and integers $q_{k,n}$, independent of $U_0$, $t$ and $\mu\in\mathcal{M}_\delta$, such that
\begin{equation}  
\emph{d} \Psi_k(U(t))^n\le -c_{k,n} \Psi_k(U(t))^n\emph{d} t+C_{k,n}\emph{d} t+C_{k,n}\Psi_{k-1}(U(t))^{q_{k,n}}\emph{d} t+\emph{d} M_{k,n}(t),
\end{equation} 
and
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb{E}\Psi_k(U(t))^n \le C_{k,n}e^{-c_{k,n}t}\Psi_k(U_0)^{q_{k,n}}+C_{k,n},
\end{equation}
where $\Psi_{k}$ {is given as in} (equation form:Psi_m of the paper) and $M_{k,n}(t)$ is the semi-martingale given by
\begin{equation} 
M_{k,n}(t)=\int_0^t n\Psi_k(U(r))^{n-1}\langle A^{k/2}u(t),A^{k/2}Q\emph{d} w(r)\rangle_H. 
\end{equation}
Furthermore, it holds that
\begin{equation} 
\begin{aligned}
\mathbb{E} \Psi_m(U(t))^n&+c_{m,n}\int_0^t \mathbb{E} \Psi_m(U(r))^{n-1}\big(\|A^{\frac{m+1}{2}}u(r)\|^2_H+\|\eta(r)\|^2_{M^{m}_\mu}\big)\emph{d} r\\
& \le C_{m,n}\Psi_m(U_0)^{q_{m,n}}+C_{m,n}t,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E} \exp\Big\{\beta_{m,0}\Psi_m(U(t))^{\gamma_{m,0}}\Big\}\le C_{m,0}\exp\Big\{C_{m,0}e^{-c_{m,0}t} \big(1+\Psi_m(U_0)^{q_{m,0}}\big)\Big\},
\end{equation}
for some positive constants $\gamma_{m,0}\in (0,1)$, $\beta_{m,0}$ $q_{m,0}$, $c_{m,0}$, $C_{m,0}$ 
also independent of $U_0$, $t$ and $\mu\in\mathcal{M}_\delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.490959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_011cdc012af7c812e8a930bc66136795c6f793a1e1ecf80e4e7a31cda2396a05","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition X5pn of arXiv:2411.16647, 'The stochastic evolution of an infinite population with logistic-type interaction'] [KK]

