{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.424681+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0135c9645a635ac5c10f3ff6f91648c254d2a431a96501473684ade4b34c1bb9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 157 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] If the discrete ensemble satisfies Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, \ref{Assumptions_basic}, \ref{Assumptions_offcrit} and \ref{Assumptions_analyticity}, then we have as $\N \rightarrow \infty$:
