{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.185056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0136b78fd411eecd508a432909b82194574cbaeecf92f17b3bd3ffc2c9f32338","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prop:good_annulus_macroscopic_scale of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] There exist universal constants $\alpha>2$ and $R_0 > 1$ such that for all $R \geq R_0$,  there exists a constant $c_R>0$ depending only on $R$ such that the following is true.  Suppose that we have the same setup as in (prop:conformal_rectangles of the paper) and let $U_1,\ldots,U_N$ denote the connected components of the complement in $A$ of the union of the crossings of $A$ made by loops in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$ together with the interiors of the excursions into $A$ from the inner and outer boundary of $A$ made by such loops,  as in (rem:crossings_general_case of the paper) with $n=0$.  In the case that no loop in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$ crosses $A$,  we instead set $N=1$ and let $U_1$ be as in (rem:no_crossings of the paper). Let $E(\Psi)$ denote the event that the following hold.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item 
		There are at most four crossings of $A$ made by loops in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$.
		\item 
		For every $j \in \{1,\ldots,N\}$ such that the boundary conditions of $\Psi|_{U_j}$ are given by the zero function,  we have that (recall the definitions of $\phi_j$,  $V_j$ and $L_j$ from (subsec:conformal_rectangles of the paper))
		\begin{align*}
			D^{V_j}_{\phi_j(\Gamma|_{U_j})}((0,L_j) \times \{0\} ,  (0,L_j) \times \{1\}) \geq c_R,
		\end{align*}
		and in the case where there is no crossing of $A$ by loops with height in $\{-\lambda, \lambda\}$, we have for all $\gamma \in \SP_A$,
		\begin{align*}
				D^{V_\gamma}_{\phi_\gamma(\Gamma|_{U_\gamma})}((0,L_\gamma) \times \{0\} ,  (0,L_\gamma) \times \{1\}) \geq c_R.
		\end{align*}

		Moreover,  in the case that there are exactly four crossings of $A$ made by loops in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$,  there exists for each such $j$ a collection of conformal rectangles $R_{j,m} \subseteq U_j$ for $1 \leq m \leq 8$ for which properties~(equation it:disconnecting_conformal_rectangles of the paper) and~(equation it:left_to_right_crossings_shorter_than_top_to_bottom of the paper) in the statement of (prop:conformal_rectangles of the paper) hold,  with $B$ the universal constant appearing there.
	\end{enumerate}
	Then,  we have that $\BP[E(\Psi)] \geq 1 - 2^{-\alpha R}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.833197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0138ccf9a09a9219422a3a21bcd2bd29b1817861fea6fc78b8fd61d1f859ea0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 32 (Global single-coordinate branching criterion) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Fix $m<r$ and assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}. Let $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$ be a tangent block. Suppose there exist a visible state $y\in\cS_m$ and an admissible appended edge $a$ such that, writing $y_a:=U_m(y,a)$,
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\alph*)}]
\item \begin{equation}
\Ker\bigl(Dq_{y,y_a}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr) \subset \Ker\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr),
\end{equation}
\item \begin{equation}
Dq_{y,y_a}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\neq0,
\end{equation}
\item \begin{equation}
\rank\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(r)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr)\ge2.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Then the depth-$m$ window is not first-order locally sufficient relative to depth $r$ on $T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.473007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_013bb5af618a449545dbc71ed01b467e12c97b308684e98a08d4f913965b9b92","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:spacetime of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Suppose $\mathsf{L}_A$ is a lift of $\mathsf{L}_O$. Then, for any 
    $x_t, y_t, z_t \in L^2([0,T]; \mathcal{H}_O)$ such that $x_t \in \dom(\mathcal{A})$, $y_t \in \dom(\mathsf{L}_O)$ for a.e. $t\in [0,T]$, and $\mathsf{L}_O y_t \in L^2([0,T]; \mathcal{H}_O)$, 
    there holds
    \begin{align} 
        \langle \mathcal{A} x_t, z_t + \mathsf{S} \mathsf{L}_A y_t \rangle_{T, \mathcal{H}} = - \langle \partial_t x_t, z_t \rangle_{T,\mathcal{H}_O} + \mathcal{E}_{T, \mathsf{L}_O}(x_t, y_t)\,.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.471071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_013e2200fe720a2b22dd5c659f1a4d8c73a17a150e2efcc951c23dfa7fd5660b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: reduced psi of arXiv:2608.28278, 'Reduction of symmetric time-dependent Hamiltonian systems I: presymplectic principal $\R$-'] In the hypothesis of Corollary (corollary: reduction corank 2 of the paper), the principal action $\psi: \mathbb{R} \times T^*Q \to T^*Q$ restricts to an action of $\mathbb{R}$ on $J^{-1}(\nu)$ and it induces an action $\psi_\nu: \mathbb{R} \times (T^*Q)_\nu \to (T^*Q)_\nu$ of $\mathbb{R}$ on $(T^*Q)_\nu$ characterized by
    \begin{equation}
        (\psi_\nu)_s \circ \pi_\nu = \pi_\nu \circ {\psi_s}_{\vert J^{-1}(\nu)}, \quad \text{for all} \quad s\in \mathbb{R}.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, the infinitesimal generator $R$ of $\psi$ restricts to $J^{-1}(\nu)$, and its restriction is $\pi_\nu$-projectable on the infinitesimal generator $R_\nu$ of $\psi_\nu$, that is,
    \begin{equation}
        T_{\alpha_q}\pi_\nu(R(\alpha_q)) = R_\nu(\pi_\nu(\alpha_q)),\quad \text{for all} \quad \alpha_q\in J^{-1}(\nu).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.396902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0142219478c72cac23681217ec7e129cc40834f1186cdf550ea94a13762d32d3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 42 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] \begin{enumerate}
	\item Almost surely, for each $\SCL_1, \SCL_2 \in \Gamma_{\BD}$, we have $D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}(\SCL_1, x) + D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}(x, \SCL_2) = D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}(\SCL_1, \SCL_2)$ for all $x \in K_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}$.
\item Almost surely, $\Gamma_{\SCL_1,\SCL} \subset \Gamma_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}$, $\widetilde\Gamma_{\SCL_1,\SCL} \subset \widetilde\Gamma_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}$, $K_{\SCL_1,\SCL} \subset K_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}$, and $\widetilde K_{\SCL_1,\SCL} \subset \widetilde K_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}$ for all $\SCL_1, \SCL_2 \in \Gamma_{\BD}$ and $\SCL \in \Gamma_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}$. 
\item Almost surely, $\#\CS_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}^n \le 2^{n \cdot o(1)}$ as $n \to \infty$ for all $\SCL_1, \SCL_2 \in \Gamma_{\BD}$. 
\item Almost surely, for each $\SCL_1, \SCL_2 \in \Gamma_{\BD}$,
\begin{equation*}
	\sup\nolimits_{S \in \CS_{\SCL_1,\SCL_2}^n} D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}\left(\SCB^S(\SCL_1; D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}), \SCB^S(\SCL_2; D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD})\right) \to 0 \quad \text{as } n \to \infty,
\end{equation*}
where, as in the statement of \Cref{prop:hitting-two-metric-balls}, we set $\SCB^{S}(\SCL; D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}) \defeq \SCB_{D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD}(\SCL, S)}(\SCL; D_{\Gamma_{\BD}}^{\BD})$.

\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.710007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0142d7bfadb8db1232c121498f02f07d3ab76fb72dc83c6a2268ed81c69ca7a5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: replacement of arXiv:2604.10509, 'Nonequilibrium fluctuations and moderate deviations for the occupation time of the SSEP wi'] Let $f$ be a $\nu^n_{\rho_*}$-density. Then, for any $\gamma > 0$,
\begin{align*}
	\int (V_i (g,\eta) - V_i^\ell (g,\eta)) f (\eta)d \nu^n_{\rho_*} \leq \gamma \int \Gamma_n^{\rm ex} (\sqrt{f}) d \nu^n_{\rho_*} + \frac{1}{2 \gamma} \int \sum_{y,z \in \mathbb T_n^d \atop |y-z|=1} h_{y,z}^\ell (g, \eta)^2 f (\eta)d \nu^n_{\rho_*}.
\end{align*}
In this formula,
\[h_{y,z}^\ell (g, \eta) = \sum_{x \in \mathbb T_n^d} \phi_\ell (y-x,z-x) \bar{\eta}_{x-e_i} g(x-e_i)\]
