{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.119658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_017f69d4aa9254d5181366db322dc45c8cf27b181443f3a2104fc67e5189e9c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma interpolation of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] For $t \geq 0$, let $\mathcal{X}_t:=\{X_t(v):v\in \mathcal{N}_t\}$ and $\bar{\mathbf{v}}$ the effective drift. Fix $T>0$ and $\kappa>0$. Consider the event
    \begin{equation*}
        A_n:=\Bigl\{\sup_{\ell \in [nT,(n+1)T]} d_\mathrm{H}(\mathcal{X}_{nT}- nT \bar{\mathbf{v}},\mathcal{X}_\ell-\ell\bar{\mathbf{v}})> \kappa nT \Bigl \}, 
    \end{equation*}
    then, $\sum_{n=1}^\infty \left(\sup_{x\in \mathbb{R}^d} \proba{x}{}{A_n}\right) < + \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.648086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_017f712831dac8bad8d592213f3c0d4a55d83d60bb8fa692ba96211467f00ed7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem ++ of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta> 0$ and $L\geq 1$. There exist measures $\langle \cdot \rangle^{+,+}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta}$ and $\langle \cdot \rangle^{+,-}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta}$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{M\to\infty}\langle \cdot \rangle^{+,+}_{\mathcal{R}(L,M),\beta}=\langle \cdot \rangle^{+,+}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta}  \quad \text{and} \quad \lim_{M\to\infty}\langle \cdot \rangle^{+,-}_{\mathcal{R}(L,M),\beta}=\langle \cdot \rangle^{+,-}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta},
\end{equation}
where the limits hold in the weak sense.
Furthermore, for every $x\in \{-L,\ldots,L\}^{d-1}$ we have 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to\infty} \langle \tau_{(x,N)} \rangle^{+,-}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta}=\langle \tau_{(x,0)} \rangle^{+,+}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta} \quad \text{and} \quad \lim_{N\to\infty} \langle \tau_{(x,-N)} \rangle^{+,-}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta}=-\langle \tau_{(x,0)} \rangle^{+,+}_{\mathcal{R}(L),\beta}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

