{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.936315+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_018e41898d8f34a13b3998904a447628a45e6f14ab83013d4baa11d8f1ba0736","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:exponential1 of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $Y_0 = \mu + m\delta_{x_0}$ with $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F^+$, $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ and $m \in \mathbb{N}\cup\{ \infty\}$. Furthermore, let $I_t(Y_0)$ be defined as in (equation eq:defI_t of the paper). Then for every $\gamma > 0$, $K>0$, there exists $T_0 >0$ such that 
