  \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.514074+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0195ca7628527b56c51de827afe7356b4bc93a14176716cbad76c7764c8c5029","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop poc of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:con of the paper)}    are satisfied, then the rate of convergence of the interacting particle system (equation eq:int of the paper) to the non-interacting particle system (equation eq:non-int of the paper)  is given~by
