{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.806935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01a600d7dbc07a35657b0b9142c7a8d7b48e0bd38d41349de10d3490630a8421","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma priori-basic of arXiv:2609.01488, 'Stabilization by a background magnetic field: global well-posedness of the full compressib'] Assume $(\rho,\mathbf u,p,\mathbf h)$ is a smooth solution to   the system (equation no-heat-mhd3 of the paper) on $\mathbb T^3\times[0,T]$ for some $T>0$.  Then there holds,
