{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.757005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01bc61b0643e8445de8a4492ee670a7e2c8043603c9a9b1a4fac8c90e808b455","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:r-tail-compensator-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] There exist constants \(C<\infty\) and \(c>0\) such that, for every \(n\ge1\),
