{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.232297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01daaad951f56ecf5c3d253dfc958283034a14e8afc9cc20082508cb85472d89","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 57 ($e_s(ab)$, $e_s(bc)$, and $e_s(ca)$) of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] Given $M \subset H_0$, $abc \in Tri(M)$, and $s \in T(abc)$. By definition, $\exists PQR \in \pi^{-1}(abc)$ such that 
