{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.364515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01e196859112df379fa81821b1a11c74448926d62df1eb639786a2b0e4ee90f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:flow-D-with-power of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] For all $(s, t) \in [0, 1]^2_{\leq}$ and $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$, we have that $\phi^{s, x}_t \in \mathbb{D}^\infty$. In addition, for any $ n \geq 1$, there exists a random variable $\Lambda_n$ such that for all  $(s, t) \in [0, 1]^2_{\leq}$, $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$, with probability one,  we have 
\begin{equs}
    \|D^n \phi^{s, x}_t\|_{{\mathbb{R}}^d \otimes \mathcal{H}^{\otimes n}} \leq \Lambda_n |t-s|^{H_-},
\end{equs}
 Moreover,  for any $p \geq 1$, there exists a  constant $C=C(n, p, \|\sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^{n+4}},H_-)$, such that  $\|\Lambda_n\|_{L_p(\Omega)}\leq C$.       
 Finally, one has the identity
 \begin{equ}
    D_r\phi^{s,x}_t=J^{r,x}_t\sigma(\phi^{s,x}_r)\mathbf{1}_{r\in[s,t]}.
\end{equ}","status":"unverified"}

