{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.359210+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01fb7413de6dd2a9c19209957aa5a8cfa640a0e0396017f75cf127cb053c2fb3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Consider, for $n\geq 2$, the random transposition shuffle $(X_t^{(n)})_{t\geq 0}$ on ${\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n$, in discrete or continuous time, and denote the associated separation distance to stationarity at time $t\geq 0$ by $\mathrm{d}_{\textup{sep}}^{(n)}(t)$. For any $c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $ we have
