{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.335380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02047f7def2c329a94b3ce36209aae16057809a9d8aff6126d107f1493e77f68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 (Exploration of the left part) of arXiv:2512.05466, 'Stochastic Flows and Marked Stable Processes'] With probability 1, the following statement holds for every spindle $\cT$: if $(a,r)$ denotes its bottom point and $(c,z)$ its top point, then

