locally uniformly in $x$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:12.000816+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0212fa47b27acf1930e9db61251f0204376161933fcc201b1ab098ad0f26296e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:nearest-two-hole of arXiv:2609.02820, 'Sharpness and critical scaling of parking'] There is $C<\infty$, depending only on $d$, such that, for every $t\geq0$ and
