{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.703879+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_022264960c15c341d2bcbb0ac9d35430db086c39af2ad0bdd82494fa25b180de","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2609.01128, 'Nonabelian Chabauty for the Thrice-punctured Line over Cyclotomic Fields'] Let $K=\bQ(\zeta_8)$ and $S=\left\{(1-\zeta_8)\right\}$. If $c_{\chi_i},c_{\kappa_i}\ne 0$ for $i=1,2$, then the depth-3 polylogarithmic Chabauty--Kim locus $X(\cO_K\otimes \bZ_p)_{S,\PL,3}$ is the solution set of the following equations in addition to \eqref{eq:keyeq} (with the coordinates $(X_i,Y_i,Z_i,W_i)=(\log(z_i),L_1(z_i),L_2(z_i),L_3(z_i))$ for $i=1,2,3,4$): 
