{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.570270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_022c991a197b9656c323c35ca3f0a52499799f5a22777a47b0f01817701175c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, suppose that $E_+$ is a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. Let $\mu_1^{\rr{GOE}}$ denote the largest eigenvalue of a standard $N\times N$ GOE matrix. Then, for test function $F:\R\to\R$ satisfying $ \|F\|_\infty+\|F'\|_\infty\leq C$,
