where each $\ell_k^{(i)}$ is a copy of the plaquette loop $p_i$. The set of all revivals of $s$ with revival set $R$ will be denoted $\mc{R}(s,R)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.031930+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_024cf32dd4bf0b47c514d01af97dc5b21d5f73bd2670c18475e2309a834802d6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Local smoothing by convolutions) of arXiv:2606.07290, 'Boundary behaviour of the Volterra square-root process'] Let $T > 0$ and let $K: (0,T] \longrightarrow (0,\infty)$ be $C^\infty$ satisfying \eqref{eq: smoothing kernel}. Let $\delta\in(0,T)$. If $g\in C^{m,\eta}([\delta/2,T]) \cap L^1([0,T])$ for some integer $m\ge 0$ and some $\eta \in [0,1)$, then, assuming $\eta+\rho\notin\mathbb N$,
