{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.271555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02504e23c42b0b7a7d1f94405eadadae91c38dfa3041292b95b309c1521148a0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_martingale_zeta1 of arXiv:2512.21159, '\textsc{From multitype branching Brownian motions\\ to branching Markov additive processes'] Suppose that, given the path of the type process $J_{\xi}$, $\mathbf{n} = (n_t: t\geq 0)$ is a Cox process on $\mathbb{R}_+$ with intensity $\beta(J_{\xi}(t)) \mathrm{d} t$ along the path of $J_{\xi}(t)$. Then, in the sense of Definition~(defn:mart-cond of the paper), 
        \begin{equation}
