        \end{equation}
    Then $L^{(m\beta)(J_{\xi})}$ is the law of a  Cox process with intensity $(m\beta)(J_{\xi}(t))\mathrm{d} t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:09.019229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02514c20cbb0e211d4e1922469639937ed0cc6ed85e2891f808d1ee1e24100df","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cm_regularity of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] For any $n \geqslant 0$ and $K, \beta >0$, the control $h_n$ satisfies for some deterministic constant $C_K>0$
