{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.812101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_025b1f0d4de4c2017557d0c5569db22d238bea7978fbf03286a8a79a11a0e02d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary q-bound of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $Q_L(n) = \frac{\br{1-\frac{1}{(n^\alpha-2)^2}}^n \br{1-n^{-\alpha}} \sqrt{1-2n^{-\alpha}-n^{-1}}}{e^{\frac{1}{12\lfloor n - 2n^{1-\alpha}\rfloor}} \br{2+n^{\alpha-1}}}$, we have for $\alpha \geq 1/2$ that
