		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.711442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0285ee348cace67a24cc00c0feeb5f792a0bef27df297576d988db20af001377","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mydef {Combinatorial Least Common Denominator, \cite[Definition 1.4 of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] {tran2020smallestsingularvaluerandom}}]
For a vector $v \in \mathbb{R}^n$, and parameters $\alpha, \gamma>0$, define

\begin{align*}
    \operatorname{CLCD}_{\alpha, \gamma}(v):=\inf \left\{\theta>0: \operatorname{dist}\left(\theta \mathrm{D}(v), \mathbb{Z}^{\binom{n}{2}}\right)<\min (\gamma\|\theta  \mathrm{D}(v)\|_2, \alpha)\right\} .
\end{align*}
Here by $\mathrm{D}(v)$ we denote the vector in $\mathbb{R}^{\binom{n}{2}}$ whose $(i, j)$-coordinate is $v_i-v_j$, for $1 \leq i<j \leq n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.634946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_028a55fa51c5a0d332d1532bf26bf5c8c0f5fa98ad9e43796c30f141e467ae10","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: equivalent asymptotique r fini pour les caractères suffisamment de points fixes of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $r\geq 0$. For each $n\geq 1$, let $\sigma_n\in {\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n$.
Assume that $f_1(\sigma_n)/\sqrt{n}\to \infty$. Then as $n\to \infty$, uniformly over all $\lambda \vdash n$ such that $\lambda_1 = n-r$, we have
