    \chi^{\lambda}(\sigma_n) = \left( f_1(\sigma_n)/n\right)^{r + o_r(1/\ln n)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.897115+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_028b1f7f5d9370cd50c5624821ba13ccc77213bda56914b1217659a131417009","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 57 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let~$q'\in \{q_0,q_\infty\}$ and~$p'\in\{p_0,p_\infty\}$. The~$1$-form~$\omega_{q',p'}^{\mathcal Z/\vartheta}$ is given by
