{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.773197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_028cffd758b104987007043620e553ac557d8e3c287d0a1abc609199598e775c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Mainthm: activate_constant_fraction of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \ge 2$. Assume $Q$ is a symmetric, translation-invariant, and heavy-tailed transition kernel on $\mathbb Z^d$ with exponent $\alpha > 0$, and let $Q_L$ be its standard projection onto $\mathbb{T}^d_L$. Consider the frog model on $\mathbb{T}^d_L$ equipped with $Q_L$. Assume the lifespan $\ell_o$ of the planted particle diverges as $L$ approaches infinity.
\begin{enumerate}[itemsep=5pt, left=0.3cm]
\item If $\alpha \in (0, d)$, then for any particle density $\lambda > 0$, $\rho \in (0, 1)$, and $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists a positive constant $C_0$ such that
  \begin{align*}
    \lim_{L \to \infty} \mathbb P_L^+\left(\frac{|\mathcal{A}\left((\log L)^{\Delta + \varepsilon}\right)|}{L^d} \geq \rho\right) = 1,
  \end{align*}
  for any particle lifespan $\ell > C_0$.

\item If $\alpha \ge d$, then for any $\rho \in (0, 1)$, there exist positive constants $C$ and $C_0$ such that
  \begin{align*}
    \lim_{L \to \infty} \mathbb P_L^+\left(\frac{|\mathcal{A}(CL)|}{L^d} \geq \rho\right) = 1
  \end{align*}
  for any particle lifespan $\ell > C_0$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.688423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0290e0de1772b851844d250183945cc672596c15b257158c05a7fd50c942e147","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Under the assumptions of Corollary~\ref{corollary1}, suppose that there exists $\alpha>0$ such that
