{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.275335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_029b5e0a0e806e9493e35479a964f07afc18dbce920966b9a24c97fc997723a9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 of arXiv:2604.24624, 'Limit distributions of the threshold radius for the maximum degree and the associated poin'] Assume that $d \geq 2$, $(k_n)_{n \in \BN}$ is a $\BN$-valued sequence satisfying $k_n \to \infty$ as $n \to \infty$ and $k_n = o(\log n)$.
