{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.656404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02c2b3f9e0d097b266658443c95d37b4c94e412486b6ed167fb216a8377e07ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 3 of arXiv:2605.07571, '\textbf{On the Besov-Orlicz path regularity of some Gaussian processes}'] There exists two positive constants $A_{H, K}$ and $B_{H, K}$ such that  for all $0<h<1/2$ and $t \in [0, 1-h]$ 
