{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.570141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02cb0eafe10f58f608c9294dccdc752bbe8f3e76231baf38b14297ba912bd661","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:opt_ll}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}, the following statements hold.
        \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
                \item For every $\eps>0$ and $D>0$,
                      \begin{align}
                              \bb P\left(\spec W\cap[E_*+N^{-2/3+\eps},E_*+\eps_*]\neq\varnothing\right)\leq N^{-D}. 
                      \end{align}
                      If $E_*=E_+$, then
                      \begin{align}
                              \bb P(\la_1>E_++N^{-2/3+\eps})\leq N^{-D}. 
