                \item For each nonzero eigenvalue $\la_j$, let $\bfru_j\in\R^M$ and $\bfrv_j\in\R^N$ be normalized left and right singular vectors of $Y$, respectively. Then, for every fixed $K\in\N$, uniformly for $1\leq j\leq K$ and deterministic vectors $\bhv\in\C^M$, $\btw\in\C^N$,
                      \begin{align}
                              \abs{\scalar{\bhv}{\bfru_j}}^2\prec N^{-1}\|\bhv\|^2,\qquad \abs{\scalar{\btw}{\bfrv_j}}^2\prec N^{-1}\|\btw\|^2. 
                      \end{align}
        \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.571276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02cd619f079a9dfc5dc0cde3d140806d5ac1db539a48a83614d72ca46f75c0d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] Let $\Theta=\frac{na_n}{\gamma}$ and $m=\frac{na_n\Lambda_\kappa}{\gamma^2}$. We have 
