{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.121760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02cfe5ca097e53dab03a524568aefb507a989f605aeb1af6489ed6dfc0d10da0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:explore-plus-spin-clusters of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] There exists a universal constant $c_{11}>0$ such that for any increasing event $\mathcal I\in\mathscr F_0$ and any boundary condition $\xi$ we have 
