{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.159596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02d323fa6b9bc9c9e7217a1c0cd3376cee35e05dad353913ab4a37fb50e1a70b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 22 (Every truncated Debye expansion) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Assume the $M$th-order preparation in \cref{cor:expansion}.  For
$0\le L\le M$, set
\[
 n^{[L]}=\sum_{j=0}^L\eps^{2j}N_j,\qquad
 u^{[L]}=\sum_{j=0}^L\eps^{2j}U_j,\qquad
 \phi^{[L]}=\sum_{j=0}^L\eps^{2j}\Phi_j.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 \sup_{t_0\le t\le T}\bigl(&
 \norm{n-n^{[L]}}_{H^s}+\norm{u-u^{[L]}}_{H^s}
 +\norm{\phi-\phi^{[L]}}_{H^s}\\
 &+\eps\norm{\nabla(\phi-\phi^{[L]})}_{H^s}\bigr)
 \le C_{L,M,t_0,T}\eps^{2L+2}.

\end{split}
\end{equation}
Thus the construction is an asymptotic expansion in the usual nested
sense, not only an estimate for the full $M$th-order sum.","status":"unverified"}

