\left( r\right) },
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\Upsilon \left( r\right) =\int_{0}^{\infty }\dfrac{z}{r}\mathbb{P}\left(
X_{r}\in \mathrm{d}z\right).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.833981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02f51fc0fd9861e7e49b977e0a727f1924b428fa8b48185bc6ee4d407fc563b2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (Study determinant--permanent comparison) of arXiv:2607.20329, '2607.20329'] For every $n\ge1$,
