{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.339971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03044a276fad407087f2d4e03523a3372d158a88aa3cb93736543ea576250e84","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition propoAiry: Airy estimate of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1/2]$ and consider the PDE (equation eqAiry: PDE, u, sigma, r of the paper) with $r$ satisfying (equation eqAiry: conditions on r of the paper). There exist constants $s_\star,L_\star,C\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for every $s_0\geq s_\star$, the following hold.
