{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:56.995976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_034a9d9e42dbeb2e211032e04dee3a8833719b0f3cf5b5834d41d5deaf63556f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 (Enclosures on $\mathcal B$) of arXiv:2609.02784, 'Maximizing the fundamental Laplace--Neumann \\ eigenvalue on quadrilaterals'] Let $\eta\ge0$ and $\beta>0$ be fixed, and suppose that, for every $(\e,t)\in\mathcal B$ and every $\nu\in[\nu]$, we have
\begin{equation}
