{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:10.019714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_035bbbf3cd34b4f9d35453f25f155efe97c2391465e58b358349d524874d4be8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm restate of X and nu of arXiv:2607.19658, 'Hitting time mixing for random $k$-cycles'] Let $n_1,n_2,\ldots$,$k_1,k_2,\ldots$, and $t_1,t_2,\ldots$ be sequences of positive integers such that:
