{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.904398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0365ac97fe69757b211cbfa12de2032b5bedfa8e0ab2efbf8ac9173ee6464ec2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:need at least rlogr Poisson subcritical of arXiv:2608.25065, 'Detection of first homology via random geometric graphs in the thermodynamic regime'] \label[prop]{need at least rlogr Poisson version}
    Let $0< \underline{\lambda} \le \overline{\lambda} < \infty$.
    Then there exist $q>0, c_2 > 0$
    depending on $\underline{\lambda},\overline{\lambda},d$
    such that for all sufficiently small $r > 0$,
    we have
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathbb{P}\left( 
        \begin{array}{c} 
        \exists z \in \ker(Z_1(G^n_M(r)) \to H_1(M)) \\
        \mbox{ such that } z \notin Z_1^{q r|\log r|}(G^n_M(r))
