    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.559389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0367248b8b17150a24a56e1963542955a4eba9060df973384eb9d53f997c6a4e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 38 of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] Suppose~$\U=\U(\R)$, \ref{ass:CE}, \ref{ass:ConditionalClos} and that for every $r>0$ there exists a constant $c_r>0$ such that 
