{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.700623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03766dddfb1e09b0ec385a3ddb190fb5ea09a9090dafef63eccaa644f152ef59","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.06011, 'Strong averaging principle for multiscale time-inhomogeneous SDEs with multiplicative $\al'] Suppose that Assumptions \ref{cond} and \ref{con:periodic} hold. Then there exists $C_{\kappa,p,s,T}>0$ such that for any $\ve\in(0,1)$ and $p\in(1,\alpha)$,
