{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.076669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03854ea74993069e7e0c3da42f224f51baad05352ac261099b36c26a9830d6f8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:small-ball-U of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Let $\{U(t,x), (t, x)  \in \mathbb{R}\times \mathbb{R}^d\}$ be the Gaussian random field defined in (equation e:de-U of the paper) and recall that $\theta_1$ and $\theta_2$
are given in (equation e:theta12 of the paper).
  \begin{enumerate}[(1)]
