      \exp\left(-\frac{c}{\varepsilon^{d/\theta_2}}\right)\le \mathbb P\left\{\max_{x\in[-1,1]^d}|U(t,x)-U(t,0)|\le\varepsilon\right\}\le \exp\left(-\frac{C}{\varepsilon^{d/\theta_2}}\right).
    \end{equation*}
    \item (Space-time joint small ball probability). Assume the condition (equation e:DL of the paper) and (equation e:U-exist of the paper) hold. There exist
    positive constants $c$ and $C$ such that for $\varepsilon>0$,
    \begin{equation*}
      \exp\left(-\frac{c}{\varepsilon^{Q}}\right)\le \mathbb P\left\{\max_{t\in[0,1], x\in[-1,1]^d}|U(t,x)|\le\varepsilon\right\}\le \exp\left(-\frac{C}{\varepsilon^Q}\right),
    \end{equation*}
    where $Q=\frac{1}{\theta_1}+\frac{d}{\theta_2}$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.432621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03858fee016cd2cbc8468affb75a1c2568915a89667f4360356fe85213de6f69","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:centered-lyapunov-moment-equivalence of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let \(p\geqslant2\). Under the parameter conditions of (assump:admissibility of the paper), the strict positivity of the equivalence constants \(c_1^{(2)}>0\) and \(c_1(a_p,p)>0\) is guaranteed. Define the constant \(K_{p,\gamma} := \max\{1+2^{p-1}\gamma^{-p}, \, 2^{p-1}\}\), and set
