{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.131108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03a1d7a5f1a265d1fdeb0b6a86d278f4fbc0bf9cdaefc651a6c6f0faf7871acc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm th1027 of arXiv:2510.10898, 'A central limit theorem for unbalanced step-reinforced random walks'] Assume that $\alpha \in (0,2],  p\in (0,1), r\in [0,1]$ and $(2r-1)\alpha p<1$.
	Let $\xi_1, \xi_2, \cdots$ be i.i.d. random variables such that
\begin{eqnarray*}
	\frac{1}{a_n}\sum_{k=1}^n \xi_k  \stackrel{d}{\rightarrow} S,
\end{eqnarray*}
 where $S$ is a symmetric $\alpha$-stable random variable 
with characteristic function 
$
\mathbb{E}(e^{it S})=e^{-|t|^{\alpha}}.
$
Then
\begin{eqnarray*}
		\frac{T_n}{a_n} \stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} (c(\alpha,p,r))^{1/\alpha} S,
		\end{eqnarray*}
where
\begin{eqnarray} 
c(\alpha,p,r)=\frac{1-p}{p}\sum_{k=1}^{\infty} \mathbb{E}(|T_k^0|^{\alpha})\mathrm{B}(k, 1+1/p)     
	\end{eqnarray} 
and $B$ denotes the beta function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.419443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03a22d198af76e43d48a26e7cbde700e9deec515ba170784e2863f8508ee271c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 24 of arXiv:2605.16560, 'Seasonal Statistics of Shannon Rate in a Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Cellular Network'] The coverage probability with respect to Palm probability distribution of epoch of interest, is given by 
