{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.726210+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03a2e26ecba767dccfb1ac602feec00bf2bbd30d876794bf569bc490c9bf027a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:tightness_bdry_good_fl of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] There exists $\zeta>0$ such that the following is true. Fix $M,p > 0$, $r \in (0,1)$, and suppose $\delta < r$. Let $h$ be a GFF on $r\mathbf{D}$ with boundary values as in Section~(se:intersections_setup of the paper), and let $\theta_1,\theta_2$ be as in~(equation eq:angles_intersection of the paper). Let $w_1,w_2 \in B(0,r/4)$, and let $E_\delta$ denote the event that the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item Let $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1+\pi}$, $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1}$, $\eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2}$, $\eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2-\pi}$ be the flow lines with respective angles starting at $w_1$ (resp.\ $w_2$) and stopped upon exiting $B(0,3r/4)$. Then
\begin{itemize}
\item The right side of $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1}$ intersects the left side of $\eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2}$ with angle difference $\theta_1-\theta_2$, and they do not intersect in any other way.
\item $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1+\pi}$ does not intersect $\eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2}$, $\eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2-\pi}$; and $\eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2-\pi}$ does not intersect $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1+\pi}$, $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1}$.
\item Let $U$ be the region bounded between $\eta_{w_1}^{\theta_1}, \eta_{w_2}^{\theta_2}$, and sample the internal metric in $U$. There exist $x,y \in \eta^{\theta_1}_{w_1} \cap \eta^{\theta_2}_{w_2}$ such that if $U_{x,y} \subseteq U$ denotes the region between $x$ and $y$, then $\mathrm{diam}(U_{x,y}) \le \delta$ and
\[ D_\epsilon^{\partial U_{x,y}} \ge \delta^\zeta+\epsilon^{a_0} . \]
\end{itemize}
\item The event $G_{0,r}$ from the statement of Lemma~(le:good_scales_merging of the paper) occurs for $h$.
\end{itemize}
Then
\[ \mathbf{P}[E_\delta] = o^\infty(\delta) \]
uniformly in the choice of $w_1,w_2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.518328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03a7aa84c9421156283a99bf5db2ac1b6e4e619e93de80d45d6e579fa2727b68","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:truncated-exponential of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] For $k_0 \geq 0$, define the truncated exponential 
