{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.283096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03bc82490ec24cd8e9c8d586a04c8c274a0e4d7ea879c4e27d3db546eda85e38","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] Let $\xi(\rho):\R_{\ge 0}\rightarrow [-1,1]$ be a continuous function. Then there exists a sequence $(\Ac_{j})_j$ of collections of disjoint smooth compact domains such that, for every $B_r(x) \subseteq \R^2$, 
