{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.917045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03c34e5753a66b1b11b687a7aae115c74d9bba1700a95f68351d55bc4b481d86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Integral one-sided color expansion) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every fixed $n\ge2$ and every zero-framed knot $K$, there are Laurent
polynomials
\begin{equation}
 b_k^{(n)}(K;q)=\varepsilon_n a_{(k)}(K;q^2)
 \in\Z[q^{\pm1}]
\end{equation}
such that, for every $r\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 J_r^{SU(n)}(K;q)=
 \sum_{k=0}^{r}b_k^{(n)}(K;q)
 \prod_{j=0}^{k-1}(1-q^{2(r-j)}).
\end{equation}
Here $a_{(k)}(K;q^2)$ is the coefficient defined by the finite dual
formula in \textup{(BG3)}.  Explicitly, for each partition $\mu$ one has
the finite representationwise identity
\begin{equation}
 J_K(V(\mu);q^2)\id_{V(\mu)}
 =\left(\sum_{\lambda\subseteq\mu}
 a_\lambda(K;q^2)\sigma_\lambda\right)\Big|_{V(\mu)}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.992808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03c4707da7ac1c05bc19e5ff70c00aa8b58e14c3392175bb919a1345cf0e1f77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-Sanovcritsatisfied of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] We consider either periodic or particle boundary condition.

\begin{enumerate}

\item For any $N\in\mathbb{N}$ and any $z\in Z_{N,R}$, the map ${\mathcal T }_{W_z}\times  {\mathcal G }^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}_{W_z}\ni(\mu,{\rm d}\xi)\mapsto {\tt K}_{W_z}^{\ssup {\Lambda_N,{\rm bc}}}(\mu,{\rm d} \xi)$ is equal to the kernel $\Pi_{W_z}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}({{\tt Q}}^{\ssup{\Lambda_N,{\rm bc}}})_{{\mathcal T }_{W_z}\to  {\mathcal S }_{W_z}}$, where we recall that $W_z=z+W$.

