{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.581235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_042c06441b50d8047bd5a04f3fbd7c6518dfc6cbe1d7b7b0295dc528a8cd4e16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Second-order junction expansion) of arXiv:2609.01319, 'Matched Queries for Curvature and Density at Branching Junctions'] Under \cref{ass:jet}, for every compact $\cQ\subset\R^D$ and every fixed integer $m\ge 0$, there are $C_{m,\cQ}<\infty$ and $\sigma_0>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\norm{\widetilde Q_\sigma-Q_0-\sigma Q_1}_{C^m(\cQ)}
\le C_{m,\cQ}\sigma^{1+\alpha},
\qquad 0<\sigma\le\sigma_0,

\end{equation}
where $\widetilde Q_\sigma$ is the locally rescaled Gaussian convolution after removal of its $z$-independent normalization. Consequently, for $m\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
\norm{F_\sigma-F_0-\sigma G}_{C^{m-1}(\cQ)}
\le C'_{m,\cQ}\sigma^{1+\alpha},

\end{equation}
with
\begin{equation}
F_0=\nabla\log Q_0,
\qquad
G=\nabla\left(\frac{Q_1}{Q_0}\right).

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.523847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_042ccc8ee03acea4c8401ec13e199e3419ef53efefebabd45c756e08c3a50cff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm exp_mixing of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] If the noise satisfies Assumption~(as:noise of the paper) with $\limsup_{k\rightarrow \infty}|\phi_k| \leq \frac{1}{2}\alpha_0$ and
    \begin{equ}

        \inf_{k\neq 0} |\phi_k| > 0\;,
    \end{equ}
    then (equation e:SNS of the paper) has exactly one invariant measure $\mu_\star$ on $\mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}$. Moreover, there exist some constants $C, \Tilde{\gamma}, T_* > 0$ such that 
    \begin{equ}

    	\|\mathcal{P}_t(x, \cdot) - \mu_\star \|_{TV} \leq C\big(1 + V_{2\alpha_0}(x)\big)e^{-\Tilde{\gamma} t}
    \end{equ}
    for any $t \geq T_*$ and $x\in \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}$, and $\mu_\star$ satisfies the tail bound
\begin{equ}

	\mu_\star(V_{2\alpha_0}(x) \geq K) \leq C\exp(-C^{-1}\sqrt{K})\;.
\end{equ} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

