{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.758484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_045b6093b58c17e0ade070d40d267841c6dc4f097ad83a3f40547db03bbfd3b3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:f-upper of arXiv:2604.24389, '``True" self-avoiding walks on general trees'] There exists a constant $C<\infty$ and $K_0\in \mathbb{N}$ such that for all $K\ge K_0$,
