{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.729286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_046518fdd1ed2c8131459efd82891255d69b3cd36b1ada8498b7eaf996867af1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2605.17494, 'Generalized intersection exponents and local cut points for three-dimensional Brownian loo'] For all $j\ge4$, there exist constants $C_1,C_2,C_3,C_4 >0$
