{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:18:54.265686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0467a6cbd469c46448e4d24927144b3d4fc76e5f82dc93bc55d8611732acea16","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] In the context of decay, the quantity to look at is the decay rate $\lambda$, which is the probability per unit time that the particle will disintegrate. With this:
