{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.957259+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0495df4dbc4194a9b26cef936c8d3b31401ad4448b0c9ea9385afbaa85a79189","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2607.22362, 'A Small-Noise Analysis of Controlled Functional Differential Equations with Gaussian Noise'] There exists a map $\G \colon \N \times \Omega \to C ([0, 1]; \bR^d)$ with the following properties:
	\begin{enumerate} 
