{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.979699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04be64878fd88d6a6df575b5e96fd775ed5a46f984e66aafdde1a5510bb6758e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eqn|ABAlternation of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] If $A$ and $B$ are two integers such that $0\leq A\leq B$, then
