{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.201229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04c480e4e37f4b065fa72d49942cde9385a0457c64d91adfc3cda0ba2b0a54a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For every $T>0$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $f\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D;\R^2))$, the solution $\psi$ of \eqref{eq l1} satisfies
