{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.389702+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04c508b02554766370fbbbf001df08611c1dd638fdc6595606d8b047c11cef24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:local_subgraph_clt of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Assume that there are sequences $\varsigma_n \gtrsim \sqrt{n}$ and $\delta_n \to 0$ such that
