{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.284653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04cf05b2c9b962c450b1580853725ecf52658a81477648cd9daf03a52789ca59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme corr:plusdefonctions of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] We work under the assumptions of Theorem~(theo:convergence of the paper) and consider a subsequence of the sequence $\left(\left(\mu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t}\right)_{t \in [0,T]}\right)_{K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}}$ that converges in law towards $(\mu^{*}_{t},R^{*}_{t})_{t \in [0,T]}$ in $\mathbb{D}([0,T], (\mathcal{M}_{\omega}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}),v) \times [0,R_{\max}])$. Let $\varphi : (t,x) \in \mathbb{R}^{+} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} \mapsto \varphi_{t}(x)$ be continuous and such that
