{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.850730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04d6284c0a8aee50b878b6e2049066165c6c0013f45e88194cbc77c0c072b4e2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:oco-games of arXiv:2608.25182, 'Minimax Alternating Regret \\for the Experts Problem and Online Convex Optimization'] Consider a two-player game with action sets $\mathcal{X}$ and $\mathcal{Y}$ of dimensions $d_x$ and $d_y$, respectively, and losses in $[-1,1]$ that are convex in each player's own action. Suppose both players use Option I of Algorithm~(alg:continuous-althedge of the paper) with $\eta=1/10$ in the alternating learning dynamic of [hait2025alternating]. Then the empirical distribution assigning mass $1/(2T)$ to each of the $2T$ indexed profiles $\{(x_t,y_t),(x_{t+1},y_t)\}_{t\in[T]}$ is an $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{CCE}}$-approximate coarse correlated equilibrium with
