{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.224150+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04f2fd9fba1313fa4086e9ffd5df1ace0dd62d38f4f87409fd40fd25d33f579c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] [Loops] 
Given $M \subset M_0$ and $\psi \in TRAJ(M)$. $\psi$ is called a \textit{loop} if it is a closed trajectory consisting only of regular triangles. $LOOP(M)$ denotes the collection of all loops on $M$, i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
LOOP(M):=\{ \psi \in TRAJ(M) \  |\  \text{$\psi$ is a loop on $M$}\} \quad \subset TRAJ(M).
\end{equation*}
 A collection of loops is called a \textit{loop complex}. $|LOOP|(M)$ denotes the collection of all extended regions of loops on $M$, i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
|LOOP|(M):=  \{|\psi| \in REG(M)\ |\ \psi \in LOOP(M)\} \quad \subset REG(M).
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:54.982803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04f3b313e664a261bcf02aaf017c156a7d219a8d0e5f54debbe9388b1938b4af","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:pll-constraint-model of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] {fairtlough_propositional_1997}}] 
  $\mathfrak{M} = (W, W_\bot, \leq, \sqsubset, V)$ is a \emph{Kripke constraint model}
  if $(W, \leq, \sqsubset, V)$ is a $\sqsubset$-preordered and $\sqsubset$-strong f-model,
  $W_\bot \subseteq W$ is upward closed with respect to $\leq$,
  and $W_\bot \subseteq V(p)$ for every $p \in \mathord{\mathrm{PropVar}}$.
  A satisfaction relation ${\Vdash_\mathfrak{M}} \subseteq W \times \mathscr{L}_{\bigcirc}$ for $\mathfrak{M}$ is defined as follows:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item $x \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \bot \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} x \in W_\bot$;
    \item $x \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \psi_1 \to \psi_2
      \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall x' \geq x\, (x' \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \psi_1 \mathrel{\Rightarrow} x' \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \psi_2)$;
    \item $x \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \bigcirc \varphi
      \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall x' \geq x\, \exists y' \sqsupset x'\, (y' \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \varphi)$;
    \item The other cases are identical to the classical one.
  \end{itemize}
  We write $\mathfrak{M} \vDash \varphi$ iff $x \Vdash_\mathfrak{M} \varphi$ for every $x \in W$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.872029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04f499d2b5c2879ec147e67cccbcb7c5df85eda21bf5d959ee09ffb4e8512f76","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 (Weak endpoint for one ordered contraction) of arXiv:2607.16724, 'Algebraic Transfer for Operator-Valued Gaussian Chaoses: Oriented Schatten Profiles and Si'] Let $1<r<\infty$ and, for finite-support kernels, set
