{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.315031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04f66c905d6f95b5e9ebe676b8a0868a9cd222914962308c4b4efc5047825818","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:capuniv of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] Let $\alpha \in [0,d)$, and let $f$ be an SGF on $\mathbb{R}^d$ or $\mathbb{Z}^d$ satisfying one of the conditions~(item:1 of the paper), (item:2 of the paper), (item:3 of the paper) or (item:4 of the paper) in Theorem~(t: univ pro of the paper).  Then
