{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.445562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_051b61b83fa93efb1cb451262acdf81decb5bd643bf5380b3e9c3e3c09e3bbb8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Towards the rate of the ratchet) of arXiv:2606.15842, 'A small noise approximation for Muller's Ratchet'] Let $X$ be a solution of \eqref{eq:ratchetSDE} with $\alpha,  \lambda > 0$ and $X(0) = \text{Poi}(\theta)$. Then, for $\xi, \eta, t \geq 0$, 
  \begin{align*}
  \mathbb E & \big( g_\xi(X(t)) g_\eta(X(t))\big) \\ & = \exp\Big( -\theta(2 - e^{-\xi} - e^{-\eta})\Big) \\ & \cdot \Big(1 +  \frac{1}{\nu \alpha} \int_0^{t \alpha} \Big(3 \exp\Big(\theta(1 - e^{-s})^2 \Big) - 2 \exp\Big(\theta(1 - e^{- (s + \xi)})(1 - e^{-s}) \Big) \\ 
  & \qquad - 2 \exp\Big(\theta(1 - e^{-(s + \eta)})(1 - e^{-s}) \Big) + \exp\Big( \theta(1 - e^{-(s + \xi)})(1 - e^{-(s + \eta)})\Big)\Big) ds\Big) \\ & \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad + \mathcal O\Big(\frac{1}{\nu^2}\Big)
  \end{align*}
  in the limit of large $\nu$. Here, the $\mathcal O()$ is stable under taking derivatives wrt $\xi, \eta$, as well as limits $\xi, \eta \to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.645702+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_051f1a7b8922a2b6438528c7a4affd0d1344c09b48ea0dbbcd55b7274d17b7e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem conditional regularity of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] {PV26}}]
