{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.937636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_052534a43549ac0ddb58324b58e425622850a0464e0356af3c239828f333b7ca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 19 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $T = \E X>0$ and $X \sim f \dd \pi_{T}.$ Then, if $f: \N \rightarrow (0,\infty)$ log-concave
