	and $\mathcal{I}[\sigma_{k_m}\cdots\sigma_{k_1}(\varepsilon)\,,\, \sigma_{2q-1} \cdots \sigma_1 (G_\varepsilon)]$ is defined according to (equation I[alpha,G] of the paper) above. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.422987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_052a60963a80bc442fd7abb4906ae136b453bace4501b0e402520d890c9af1cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:minimal-m of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:moment-thresholds}
For every \(p\ge3\), matching only the mean and variance suffices for the regularized bulk-pressure conclusion (equation eq:pressure-univ-weak of the paper).  The least matching order sufficient for the ratio conclusion is
\begin{equation}
