{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.351160+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_052da73cae2d51a3049123f75e89354508dcfc7cc8f1919217867f079a573223","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem_generaldiffusion of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Let $X$ be a random variable that belongs to $\mathcal{A}$, which has zero mean and admits a density. Let $\mathcal{Y}$ be  a random variable distributed as $\nu$ 
    described in  Assumption (assum_generaldiffusion of the paper). Set $F=X+m$ for $m=\E{\mathcal{Y}}$. Choose $x\in \mathbb{R}$ and assume the moment condition 
\begin{align*}

\E{\mathcal{V}_1(x,F)^2}+\E{\mathcal{V}_2(x,F)^2}+\sum_{i=3}^6 \E{\mathcal{V}_i(F)^2}<\infty \,,  
\end{align*}
where $\mathcal{V}_i,1\leq i\leq 6$ are the functions defined in Lemmas (lemma_xinlandu_gendif of the paper), (lemma_steinmethod_xlessthanl_gendif of the paper) and (lemma_steinmethod_xmorethanu_gendif of the paper).  Set $h_F=\Gamma\brac{F,-L^{-1}2a(F)}$ and
