   and is called the \emph{base change morphism}. This is a morphism in \(\mcalD_{\qcoh}(\mcalX')\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.855237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05457e0cd4a1c406dd483c9ca2bfe9bbd543a41ca8f805e50c7fcbecbc50eadb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma th:averaged of arXiv:2410.23974, 'Polynomial rate of relaxation for the Glauber dynamics of infinite-volume critical Ising m'] Consider the critical temperature Ising model on $\Lambda_{L}=\llbracket-L,L\rrbracket^{d}$ with $+$ boundary condition in any fixed dimension $d\geq2$. Assume the assumption (equation eq:arm of the paper) is satisfied, then there exists a universal constant $c_{0}(\delta,d)>0$ such that
