{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.684381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_054871fb417c9f91faad875abfd3c576bb6a4e55cba8d26510425110ecbaeeaa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:xi-lower-weak-upper of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] There exist absolute constants $\beta_0,c_0>0$ such that the following holds for all $\beta>\beta_0$. Let $h = H+1-n$ for fixed $n\geq 0$. Then for all $1 \leq \ell \leq \sqrt{L} \exp(-\frac12\frac{\log L}{\log\log L})$ we have
\begin{equation}

 1 - e^{-c_0\frac{\log L}{\log \log L}} \leq \frac{\xi_{\ell,h}}{{\widehat\pi}_\infty(\phi_o < -h)} \leq 1 + L^{-1+o(1)}\,.
 \end{equation}
Moreover, this holds when replacing $\xi_{\ell,h}$ by $-\frac1{|S|}\log{\widehat\pi}_\infty(\phi_x\geq -h,\,\forall x\in S)$ for any set $S\subset \mathbb Z^2$, not necessarily connected, of size at most $\ell^2$. In addition, the upper bound holds for all $\ell \geq 1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.358023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0548c287c8f1baafb8b2f3ab48fdb5e6b7ca8820de0d8d501681277265df7dba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:risk-severity of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] Let $\rho=\Pr(S=1)$ and $r=\Pr(S=1,F=1)$. When $r>0$, define the signed stopped-flip severity $\eta_s=\mathbb E[Y\mid S=1,F=1]$ and the positive-harm severity $\eta_+=\mathbb E[Y_+\mid S=1,F=1]$, where $Y_+=\max(Y,0)$. When $r=0$, set $\eta_s=\eta_+=0$ by convention. Then
\begin{equation}
\boxed{\Delta V(S)=\mathbb E[S(c-Y)]=c\rho-r\eta_s.}

\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\Delta V(S)\ge c\rho-r\eta_+.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.283849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0549cd0d8f3bd2790ca3c82a750d91bee1bb4bfb58f53cdb8822653ed738312a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2607.26944, 'Improved bounds on the inradius and inverse inradius process of the convex hull of planar '] For $m \ge 1$, let  
