{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.706551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_054eaffbcec411f24e9b7660a0dc99a4f633fccbaa38299e7993116ef4bf1d4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:Bsup of arXiv:2510.24424, 'On the Fourier Coefficients of Critical Gaussian Multiplicative Chaos'] Let $B_t$ be a standard linear Brownian motion. Then there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $t>e$, $a>0$,
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb{P}\Big(\sup_{s\in [e,t]}B_s\leq a\Big) \leq C\frac{(a+1)}{\sqrt{t}+1}.
