    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.455105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0552da640980bbfde45a50ec507498f129cf328d41c6a869084b28e7dba35295","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 (Strong failure of regularity persistence) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] For any $s\in (1, \nicefrac {3}{2}]$, there exists an initial datum
