		where  $\varepsilon=\varepsilon_{ \beta, \delta , \tau}$  is given by ((1 of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.369295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_055ea43d4e7b07752f235510157fa86ba1e4030c1f3c4f8d7841cab532af5973","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 18 of arXiv:2607.27932, '2607.27932'] Let $H_\varepsilon$, $\underline H_\varepsilon$, $\mathcal M_\varepsilon$ and $\varepsilon_c$ be as in Proposition
