{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.325302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_056da65d3a074d41614b0050fa9429eb8064e97c5c0362d0a64d3581f9ee99b1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:uniform-decorated-path-bound of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] Fix $b>-1$ and let $\boldsymbol k$ range over a compact subset of
$\mathbb R_{>0}^m$.  Let also $\boldsymbol\tau$ range
over a compact subset of
$\{\tau_1\geq\cdots\geq\tau_m\}$.  There exist constants $C,c>0$ and $N_0\geq1$ such that for all
$N\geq N_0$, $r,\rho\geq0$, and $h\geq0$,
\begin{align}
  &\sum_{\substack{\Gamma\in\mathfrak C_N(r,\rho)\\
                    \mathsf H_N(\Gamma)\geq h}}
     |w_N(\Gamma)|
  \notag\\
  &\qquad\leq
  \frac{C^{r+\rho+1}(r+\rho+1)^{4m}}{\sqrt{\rho!}}
  \left
    \{\frac1{T_r!}
      +\left(\frac{C}{\sqrt{\log(r+2)}}\right)^r
  \right\}e^{-ch^2}.

\end{align}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{N\geq N_0}\sum_{r,\rho\geq0}
  \sum_{\Gamma\in\mathfrak C_N(r,\rho)}|w_N(\Gamma)|<\infty,

\end{equation}
and the tails in $r+\rho$ vanish uniformly in $N\geq N_0$.
The constants and both conclusions are uniform in
$\boldsymbol\tau$ on the prescribed compact set.","status":"unverified"}

