{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.302800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_057ce3c6563356fd5ed75eed4962150990fff76a36f9bb7dd1b300fd9851cfee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary mgf of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] For any direction parameters $\rho_1, \dots, \rho_n \in (0,1)$, any down-right path $\mathcal{Y} = (\mathbf y_i)_{i\in \mathbb{Z}}$, and any $\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_n\ge0$, we have
