{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.968910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_058149ae6c9b1319b28f11e471babf5da65d0159ad62af231178b3514fe2eceb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 ($L$-fold, coupled spherical integration for $\mathrm{rank}(D_l D_l^\dagger)=M(N)>1$) of arXiv:2608.03273, 'On the Asymptotic of Coupled Spherical Integrals: An Operator-Valued Extension of the Free'] Let $L=O(1)$, $M(N)=O\left(N^{1/2-\epsilon}\right)$ for any $\epsilon>0$, and $D_l=O_l\Sigma_l V^\dagger$ be the singular-value decomposition of $D_l$ for all $l$, i.e. $D_l$ has $M(N)$ non-zero singular values $\sqrt{\theta_{l,i}}$, and the right unitary/orthogonal matrix $V^\dagger$ of the SVD of $D_l$ is identical for all $l$.
Let $Z_N$ and $Z$ be defined as in Theorem~\ref{thm:pL_rank1_integral} and all $\theta_{l,i}$ are small enough such that
\begin{align}
    -P_i=-\mathrm{diag}\left\{\frac{2\theta_{1,i}}{\beta},\ldots,\frac{2\theta_{L,i}}{\beta}\right\}
