{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.020174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05939d740ed11007745fba6473d4a2e21a07ac1fe79604ebacc8d243f38f01f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:PLIneqfromSC of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] Let $0 < a \leq b < \infty$, $\mathcal{U}$ be a projective unitary representation with twirl $\Phi$, and $f$ be $\mu_0$-strongly convex on $[a I, b I]$ with $S_\star = \argmin_{S \in \mathcal{P} \cap [a I, b I]} f(S)$.
