{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.230200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05a6975b4d9cb6462f8f676edc1fed0c4a5d24fae0ba31c19f22c8274a1bf0e2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] There exist  $c,C>0$ and a coupling $\mathbf{P}$ of $\mathcal{L}_{n}$ under the law $\mathbf{P}_n$ and $\mathcal{L}_{2n}$ under the law $\mathbf{P}_{2n}$  such that all $\delta>0$ and $n \geq 2\delta^{-2}$, 
