{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.775326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05bd6d2f50bdeab7cc1e59ec0298b0fafd4b28a31a06da397c7f3b4dacce4170","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:omega-limit-set of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Given a semiflow $P^*$ on $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$, then
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textnormal{(\roman*)}]
    \item a measure $\nu\in\omega(B)$ if and only if there exist two sequences $t_k\to\infty$, and $\nu_k\in B$ such that $\mathcal W_2(P^*_{t_k}\nu_k,\nu)\to0$, as $k\to\infty$;
    \item if $B$ is connected in  $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$, then $\omega(B)$ is connected in $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$;
    \item if there exists a compact set $K\subset\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ attracting a bounded set $B\subset\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$, then $\omega(B)$ is a nonempty, compact, invariant subset of $K$ and $\omega(B)$ attracts $B$;
    \item if there exists a nonempty compact set $K\subset\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$ that attracts each compact subset of $\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$, then $\mathop{\bigcap}\limits_{t\geq0}P^*_tK$ is the maximal compact invariant set.
