{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.930414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05d3211e8d7b201e0b7f5b18b911ad9fa55efcc4db0bfd5864c8f65a79d2a73e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 (Quantitative passage toward the subcritical cutoff) of arXiv:2608.20638, 'Provable Edge-of-Stability for Adam on a One-Dimensional Quadratic'] Assume the hypotheses of Proposition~\ref{prop:Psi-decay} and
$w_{\max}>4$.  Fix $0<\delta<\overline W$ and $T\in\Nzero$, and let
\begin{equation}
    \tau:=\min\{n\in\Nzero:w_{T+n}>\overline W-\delta\}.

\end{equation}
If $w_T>\overline W-\delta$, then $\tau=0$.  Otherwise, set
\begin{equation}
    q:=1-\delta\!\left(
       \frac{c\eta}
       {\sqrt{\max\{v_T,\Psi_T\}}+c\eta/4},
       \overline W-\delta
       \right).

\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
