{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.050393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05ed64b1a390793db7fe01037faf11e6bccc71f20912d5c7d79e17f7c807111d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:gaussian-Ritz-general of arXiv:2608.30831, 'Sharp discrete Hardy constants in dimensions three and four\\ and strict upper bounds from'] Let $N\ge1$, let $m\ge1$, and let $q_1,\ldots,q_m\in(0,1)$ be distinct.
Set
\[
 V_N(q):=\operatorname{span}\{g_{q_1,N},\ldots,g_{q_m,N}\}.
\]
Define the symmetric matrices
\begin{align}
 \mathsf E_N(q)_{ij}
 &=2N\,G(q_i,q_j)\vartheta(q_iq_j)^{N-1}
   +2N(q_i+q_j-1),\\
 \mathsf D_N(q)_{ij}
 &=F_N(q_iq_j).
\end{align}
Then $\mathsf D_N(q)$ is positive definite and
\begin{equation}
 \min_{0\ne v\in V_N(q)}\frac{\mathcal E_N[v]}{\mathcal D_N[v]}
 =\min_{c\ne0}\frac{c^T\mathsf E_N(q)c}{c^T\mathsf D_N(q)c}.
\end{equation}
Equivalently, this minimum is the smallest generalized eigenvalue of
\begin{equation}
 \mathsf E_N(q)c=\lambda\mathsf D_N(q)c.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.797895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05f118e8f093aa73bc8fb595ed9b062abf91a4c346340df0e8c1df8aaee8b488","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 39 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that $\mO$ is a separable Banach space and 
that $(\Omega, \mathscr{F}, \mathbb{F},\mathbb{P})$ is a filtered complete probability space satisfying the usual condition \ref{ass-usual}, and    
 $(\bu_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$is a sequence of $\mathbb{F}$-adapted, $\mO$-valued continuous processes. We say that this sequence satisfies the \textbf{Aldous-Rebolledo} condition in the space $\mO$  if and only if 
for every  $\eta>0$, for  every sequence $(\tau_n)_{n=1}^\infty$ of $[0,T]$-valued  stopping times, for every $[0,1]$-valued  sequence $\vartheta_n$ such that  $\vartheta_n \to 0$ as $n \to \infty$, 
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P} (\Vert \bu_n(\tau_n + \vartheta_n) - \bu_n(\tau_n) \Vert_{\mO} > \eta)= 0.
  \end{equation}
Equivalently, for every sequence $(\tau_n)_{n=1}^\infty$ of $[0,T]$-valued  stopping times, for every $[0,1]$-valued  sequence $\vartheta_n$ such that  $\vartheta_n \to 0$ as $n \to \infty$, for every  $\eta>0$, condition \eqref{eqn-Aldous-Rebolledo} holds. \\
 Equivalently, 
 for  every sequence $(\tau_n)_{n=1}^\infty$ of $[0,T]$-valued  stopping times, for every $[0,1]$-valued  sequence $\vartheta_n$ such that  $\vartheta_n \to 0$ as $n \to \infty$, 
    \begin{equation}
    \lim_{n \to \infty} \Vert \bu_n(\tau_n + \vartheta_n) - \bu_n(\tau_n) \Vert_{\mO} = 0 \mbox{ in } \mathbb{P}. 
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.319499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05f46183fe7adf339884d928158180ae364218b4a5710ad8ec21242e9f19d152","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.09933, 'Explicit cutoff profiles for colored top-\texorpdfstring{$m$}{m}-to-random shuffles'] For \(0\le u\le n\),
