{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.840625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05f5940d6e3a7bcb3221b9318256f883f28c9fe9776fdcc98e1f73a4b79d44ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:regularity-OU of arXiv:2504.04860, 'Stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: dependence on the '] Let $0<a<b<1$ and $\kappa=1$. For any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$ and $p\ge1$, there exists a non-negative random variable $K_{a,b,\varepsilon,p}$ with  $\mathbf{E}[|K_{a,b,\varepsilon,p}|^p]<\infty$ such that we have
