{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.159560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05f696186af5dac48619965f93cf644d37663d76b7505a0c8bcfcb2e86e29693","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.02406, 'On the range of competing random walks'] Let $\mathbb W$ denote the Wiener measure on $\mathcal C\eqdef\mathcal C([0,1])$. We define a mapping $\tau$ on $\RR\times\mathcal C$ by 
