{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.757621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05f7cdf8ca6791aa5aa30864f3402ff57a21f48d0a1ab37d9db9b6699a06adef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 (Weyl's integration formula, \cite{raymond1984volume,guedon2007concentration}) of arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $\beta$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatte'] For any $p\geq1$ and any $F\colon \R^N\rightarrow\R_+$ symmetric and positively homogeneous of degree $k$, we have:
