{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.095154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0601570dc7d9126b62d1a7d793dfba7c44f51b24284e3d95c5fa7bb946bfc56c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 45 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] Let $P\colon T^\f M\to TM$ be a partial almost Poisson anchor.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The bilinear map $\{\cdot,\cdot\}_P$ is called the \emph{almost Poisson bracket} associated to $P$ and $(M,\{\;,\;\}_{P})$ is called an \emph{almost  partial Poisson structure} on $M$
 \item A partial almost Poisson structure $(M,\{\;,\;\}_{P})$ is called a \emph{partial Poisson manifold} if the bracket $\{\;,\;\}_{P}$ satisfies the Jacobi identity 
