{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.314536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_061c3c61e832f963461441865f250afce9357a8af0d40dbf9a0a67c7e5b20e94","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:shape of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] Let $D$ be a compact domain. Then for every $\ell, \Delta > 0$, $\nu \in \mathcal{P}(D) \cap \mathcal{M}_{>0} \cap \mathcal{M}_{<\infty}$, and $\eta \in \mathcal{M}_{<\infty}$,
