{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.776697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_061f4c757e651b2f9d03e50f36ad592577b0384cf497ac756f54118656095295","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:correlation_stopping_tilde of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There is some $\lambda_0 > 1$ and $C, c > 0$ such that for all $\lambda \geqslant \lambda_0$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[
        \exists j \in L^0_\ell \text{ such that } \mathsf{AllReversed}^j(\widetilde{\mathbf{X}},\widetilde{\mathbf{Y}}) \text{ holds}
