{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.464714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06708af75cf73aeef4c2100476c7d16550b887e53b96c7b6eb8a17b30943b4db","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition q3-pos-def-ch-cx of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] If $Y$ is an integer homology sphere, $q_3(Y)$ is the unique integer satisfying the following. For a positive integer $k$, we have $q_3(Y)\geq k$ if and only if there are $\zeta, \eta \in C(Y)$ such that 
