{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.389044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06792c47395ac0075e50796ca5d8aadfd785c10eec14a9b95148d47eda5a78ad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-max-principle of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Let $\mathcal A\subset  \mathcal V\mathcal G$ be non-empty and finite. 
