{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.887405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06c31953e534fd856bf8f5e13d8c514fc1e6505ebec8d30a43e76a033b3f72d6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2607.02410, 'Polynomial mixing for polygonal side matchings'] Let $P$ be a $2n$-gon whose vertices are labelled from $1$ to $2n$ in a clockwise manner, and let $X$ be a chord diagram on $P$. The \textit{gluing graph} of $X$, denoted $G(X)$, is a directed graph whose vertices are the vertices of $P$ and whose edges are
