{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.302919+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06c54e97c2eb5e8f7631a729d6f33d364064512074e2be19a1a464fa68d74a59","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop5.1 of arXiv:2604.22130, 'Reflected Stochastic Differential Equations Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Nonlinear C'] Let $(X,A)$ be the solution to doubly reflected $G$-SDE with parameters $(x_0,f,h,g,l,r)$. Then, there exists a positive constant $C$ depending on $T,G,L,p$, such that 
\begin{align*}
&\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|X_t|^p\right]+\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|A_t|^p\right]\\
\leq C&\Bigg\{|x_0|^p+\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\int_0^T|f(t,0)|^pdt\right]+\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\int_0^T|h(t,0)|^pdt\right]+\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\left(\int_0^T|g(t,0)|^2 dt\right)^{\frac{p}{2}}\right] \\
&+\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{s\in [0,T]}|l^{-1}(s,0)|^p\right]+\hat{\mathbb{E}}\left[\sup_{s\in [0,T]}|r^{-1}(s,0)|^p\right]\Bigg\}.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615969+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06c6afe29a1de3df7e51a6a6c92f2e02263cbd0165038172f801870a4e8e14e5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For $n\ge1$,~$t>0$ and~$\lambda>0$, denote
