{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.969641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06dc79b1447218b27d152272e36a13a3676d5e4c8d899ce083f9afd0cbfe82c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[0 3 of arXiv:2606.10058, 'Mean First Passage Times and Fundamental Tensors of Higher Order Markov Chains'] For an $m$th order tensor ${\cal A}=[a_{i_1i_2\ldots i_m}] \in \mathbb R^{u \times u \times n \times \cdots \times n}$, the diagonal tensor obtained from $\cal A$, denoted by ${\cal A}_d=[a^{[d]}_{i_1i_2\ldots i_m}]$, is defined as: for any $1 \le i_1, i_2 \le u$ and $1 \le i_3, \ldots, i_m \le n$, 
$$a^{[d]}_{i_1i_2i_3\ldots i_m}=a_{i_1i_2i_3\ldots i_m}\delta_{i_1i_2}=\left\{\begin{array}{cl}
a_{i_1i_1i_3\ldots i_m}, & i_1=i_2;\\
