{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.413374+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06dcc14fee0a811704d48198e080f0b9911e028e0ff800de8265ae1708622afa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:qRacah_ensemble of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] The $q$-Racah ensemble
	$\mathfrak{R}^{qR(N)}_{M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta}$
	depending on the parameters satisfying (equation eq:qRacah_parameters_nonnegative of the paper),
	is a probability measure on $N$-tuples of particles $(x_1<\ldots<x_N )$ in $\{0,1,\ldots,M \}$,
	with probability weights given by
	\begin{equation}

		\mathfrak{R}^{qR(N)}_{M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta}(x_1,\ldots,x_N )=
		\frac{1}{Z(N,M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta)}
		\prod_{1\le i<j\le N}\left( \mu(x_i)-\mu(x_j) \right)^2
		\prod_{i=1}^{N}w^{qR}(x_i).
	\end{equation}
	Here $Z(N,M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta)$ is the normalization constant ensuring that the total probability is~$1$. The condition $M \ge N-1$ in (equation eq:qRacah_parameters_nonnegative of the paper) is required so that $N$ particles can fit into $\{0,1,\ldots, M \}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.076405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06dd9c3bfc7a2cd3c036f3ba7a5729a11c96d9c3ff1178d09ae4517217b3960d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2606.02464, 'Inspections'] Let $\nu_1:=1/(1-\rho)^2$ and $\nu_2:=(2-\rho)/(1-\rho)^2$. The optimal policies are characterized as follows.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[\rm(i)] For $\nu \leq 1$, $p^*=0$ and $\tau^*=\infty$; $u^*_{\mathrm{RR}}=u^*_{\mathrm{GA}}=0$.
    \item[\rm(ii)] For $1 < \nu <  \nu_1$, both policies have interior optima; $p^*\in(0,1)$ given by \eqref{eq:p_star} and $\tau^*>0$.
    \item[\rm(iii)] For $\nu_1 \leq \nu < \nu_2$, $p^*=1$ and $\tau^*>0$.
    \item[\rm(iv)] For $\nu \geq  \nu_2$, $p^*=1$ and $\tau^*=0$; $u^*_{\mathrm{RR}}=u^*_{\mathrm{GA}}$ and $\mathrm{PoF}=1$.
\end{enumerate}
In cases \rm{(ii)} and \rm{(iii)}, $\mathrm{PoF}>1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.952848+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06e076b090ba733b1fccd7c90c22a3133d1d67be4f953d37f2e5f759154b426e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mixed_tail_ambient_restriction of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Let $K\subseteq T$ be finite and contain $t_0$. For
