{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.985943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06e4825eae4d402206b3f1c7525d96e387604f1f92664d2493d3b529cccbd09b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 51 (cf.\ {\cite[Theorem 1.5) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {K24}}]
    Let $\cT^\omega_{n, \beta}$ be the RSTRE on the complete graph $K_n=(V_n, E_n)$ with $n$ vertices and i.i.d.\ disorder variables $(\omega_e)_{e\in E_n}$ uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$. Denote by $M_n$ the MST coupled to $\omega$ as in \ref{SS:CoupleRG}. If $\beta \ll n^2/\log n$, then
