		d_{\text{Kol}} \, \left(  \mu , g^{\circledast}_{\, 1} \right) \right\}^{2} \leq C_{\circledast} \, \Big| \, m_4[\mu] - m_4[ g^{\circledast}_{\, 1} ] \, \Big|, 
	\end{align}

where $d_{\text{Kol}} \, (\cdot, \cdot)$ denotes the Kolmogorov distance. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.414426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06fd02b85b9ea8231e873ec5cb01ef76e1b52069e97cfecd5c24e6407c25c38f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 80 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Let $\mathcal A^{\textnormal{s}}_\eps\subset \W_\N$ denote the set of configurations such that
\begin{itemize}
\item there are at most $C \N^{\frac{1}{2}}(\log\N)^2$ holes in $[\mathfrak{a}+\eps,\mathfrak{b}]$;
\item there are no particles outside $(-D,D)$;
\item the event studied in Lemma~\ref{Lemma_tail_bound_general} with $t= \N^{-\frac{1}{2}}\log\N$ is not realized, \textit{i.e.}
\[
\forall f \in \mathscr{H}_{\textnormal{Lip},\frac{1}{2}} \quad \exists h \in [H] \qquad \bigg|\int_{\amsmathbb{R}} f(x)\dd(\mu_{\N,h} - \mu_h)(x)\bigg| \leq \frac{\log\N}{\N^{\frac{1}{2}}} \cdot |\!|f|\!|_{\frac{1}{2}} + \frac{C}{\N} \cdot \big(|\!|f|\!|_{\textnormal{Lip}} + |\!|f|\!|_{\infty}\big).
\]
\end{itemize}
For $0<\eps_1<\eps_2$, let $\mathcal{E}^{\textnormal{s}}\big[\begin{smallmatrix} K_1 & K_2 \\ \eps_1 & \eps_2 \end{smallmatrix}\big] \subset \W_\N$ be the set of configurations having $K_1$ holes in $[\mathfrak{a}+\eps_1, \mathfrak{b}]$ and $K_2 \leq K$ holes in $[\mathfrak{a}+\eps_2,\mathfrak{b}]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.799133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06fdf1ecc18a7ac8a52727c6ed97c2123d53d64be8fe2300d0da6e49c3c93dde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem p1q1 of arXiv:2509.24452, 'A family of non-uniform distributions on the set of parking functions generated by random '] Consider $\pi_1$ under the measure $\mathcal{P}_n^{(1)}$.

\noindent i. $\frac{\pi_1}n$ converges in distribution to the distribution  on $[0,1]$ with  density\newline $-\log x,\ x\in(0,1]$;

\noindent ii. $\mathcal{E}_n^{(1)}\pi_1=\frac{n+3}4$;

\noindent iii.  $\mathcal{P}_n^{(1)}(\pi_1=k_n)\sim\frac{\log n}n,\ \text{for}\ 1\le k_n=o(n)$;

