{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.005247+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0717375bacadeb4760828ba72daa086a1f1b03f05fd8ffa4e5b2114b47038acd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition propWienerreset of arXiv:2606.27549, 'On Analytically Tractable Multidimensional Diffusions via Doob $h$-Transforms, with Resett'] Let $\widehat{\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ and ${\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ be the $n$-dimensional diffusion processes introduced in Proposition (prop_reset of the paper), whose transition p.d.f.'s satisfy the relation in (equation rel_f of the paper). If the intensity of the resetting processes $N_t$ and $N_t'$ is a positive constant $\lambda$, then the stationary p.d.f.\ of ${\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ is given by

     \begin{align}
        f({\bf x}\,|\,{\bf y}^R)
        & =\displaystyle \frac{h_c({\bf x})}{h_c({\bf y}^{\rm R})}\,
        \frac{2\lambda e^{\Phi\left({\bf x,y}^{\rm R}\right)}}{(2\pi)^{n/2} {\Delta^{1/2}}}  
        \left(\frac{\Xi\left({\bf x,y}^{\rm R}\right)}
        {\lambda+\frac{1}{2}{\bf m}\cdot A^{-1}\cdot{\bf m}^{\top}}\right)^{\frac{2-n}{4}}
        \nonumber
        \\
        & \times\,  K_{1-\frac{n}{2}}\left(2
        \left(\Xi\left({\bf x,y}^{\rm R}\right) 
        \left(\lambda+\frac{1}{2}{\bf m}\cdot A^{-1}\cdot{\bf m}^{\top}\right)\right)^{1/2}\right),

\end{align}

     where the weight function $h_c$ is explicited in (equation 3.3generica of the paper), 
     $\Delta=| A|$, ${A^{-1}}:=(\gamma_{ij})$,
     \begin{align*}
         \Phi\left({\bf x,y}^{\rm R}\right)
         &=\sum_{i=1}^n\gamma_{ii}\; m_i(x_i-y_i^{\rm R})
         +\sum_{i,j=1}^n\gamma_{ij}\left[ m_j (x_i-y^{\rm R}_i)+ m_i (x_j-y^{\rm R}_j)\right], \\ 
         \Xi\left({\bf x,y}^{\rm R}\right)
         &=\frac{1}{2} \, ({\bf x}-{\bf y}^{\rm R})\cdot A^{-1}  \cdot({\bf x}-{\bf y}^{\rm R})^{\top},
     \end{align*}
     and $K_{h}$ denotes the  modified second-kind Bessel function of index $h$ 
     (see, for instance, Gardiner [Gardiner]).","status":"unverified"}

