{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.678318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07253d557c20ff2a970c70456351842e640a482c8c25d0d8bc06f1d362b7b21c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] Suppose Hypotheses \ref{PEeqAssum-2.2}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.3}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.4} and \eqref{PETNs-3.01} hold. Then, for every $\epsilon\in(0,\epsilon_0)$, the measure evolution process $S_\epsilon$ on $\mathcal P_{4,z}(H)$ has a unique $\mathfrak D$-pullback measure attractor $\mathscr A_\epsilon$. For every $\tau\in\mathbb R$,
