{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.086808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_072e2c78d207ebdb3d373d17417cc9c4c00c27228844c83a43b0f5f2c1bfff6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:consis of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Let $\eta\in\{0,1\}^2$ and suppose that $(\sigma,b)$ satisfy Assumption~(assu:H of the paper) and conditions~(item:1a of the paper), (item:1b of the paper), (item:2c of the paper), and~(item:2d of the paper) on ${\mathbb R}$. Then the following properties hold:
