{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.934492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07462cd723d9f67bc13c7735c954bb7afe5a0f2f815acf87e220a6239ecf7081","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn def:weak_sol of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] We say that (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) has a weak solution $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$, if there exists a filtered probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, (\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t\geq 0}, \mathbb{P})$ such that $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is an adapted $\mathcal{C}_{tem}^+$ - valued 
		continuous process with $X_0 = \mu$ a.s. and such that $\dot{W}$ is a space-time white noise and for every $(t,x) \in (0,\infty)\times \mathbb{R}$ almost surely
		\begin{equation*}
		\begin{split}
			&X_t(x) = \int_\mathbb{R} p_t(x-y) X_0(y)dy + \int_\mathbb{R} \int_0^t p_{t-s}(x-y)h(X_s(y))dsdy \\
			& \hspace{2cm}+ \int_\mathbb{R} \int_0^t p_{t-s}(x-y) \sqrt{X_s(y)}\dot{W}(dsdy).
		\end{split}
