{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.462547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0746dad409b5b1176ae393a66b535571fc55b6bc2cc87a4a070b9516964b4bfa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ergopt of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{P}_t = \exp(t \mathcal{L})$ be a QMS with invariant state $\sigma \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M})$. Then, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{t \to \infty} \mathcal{P}_t (\mathrm{id} - E_{\mathcal{N}}) = 0\,,
    \end{align*}
    with $E_{\mathcal{N}}$ being the conditional expectation to $\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L})$, and the limit 
    \begin{align} 
        \lim_{t \to \infty} \frac{1}{t} \int_0^t \mathcal{P}_s \,\mathrm{d} s =: E_{\mathcal{F}}
    \end{align}
    exists and defines the conditional expectation $E_{\mathcal{F}}$ onto $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L})$ with respect to $\sigma$. 
    Moreover, the following convergence holds:
    \begin{align} 
        \lim_{t \to \infty} \mathcal{P}_t  = E_{\mathcal{F}}\,,
    \end{align}
    if and only if $\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L})$ coincides with the fixed-point algebra $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L})$, i.e., $\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L}) = \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.613840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0747cbae62606cd9fe9e4dfe3113733dc2b24bc262cc795e8bb0f059fbdfcbfe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2605.16868, '\ttl'] Under Assumption \ref{assumption:GNGop}, there exist some constants $\kappa_1, \kappa_2>0$ such that for sufficiently large $N$, 
