{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.922632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07595a0224d34a52a1a3a19e134c595c349e4c29b16264d111967e6c07a29dd2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:int_order of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$. Let ${\scaleobj{0.9}{\boxempty}} \in \{-,+\}$, $x_0 < y_0$ and $s \in \mathbb{R}$. Then, 
           \begin{equation}
                \tau^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{(x_0,s)}(t)\leq \tau^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{(y_0,s)}(t) \qquad \forall t\geq s.
           \end{equation}
           Furthermore, if $\tau^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{(x_0,s)}(r) = \tau^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{(y_0,s)}(r)$ for some $r \ge s$, then $\tau^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{(x_0,s)}(t) = \tau^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}_{(y_0,s)}(t)$ for all $t \ge r$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.564008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_075b5a1e16377a71ee99ba8eee0a0f3ab14ceaf9f0aa3700ca65659c4c34f611","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.m-mu-tail of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] Let $\mathcal{X}_\mu(\omega)$ be the smallest integer $n\ge \mathcal{X}_{\beta_h}(\omega)$ satisfying
	\begin{equation}
		\|e^{-2V}-\mathbb{E}[e^{-2V(0)}]\|_{\hat{\phantom{H}}\v@true\h@true\negph@nt{H}\underline{H}^{-1/6}(\square_M)}\le 3^{M/24}\qquad\text{for every integer }M\ge n\, .
