	with $\sigma\in(0,1)$ as in (equation eq.m-beta0-tail of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.583961+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_075c28f4579fa553d8ff8157ab458334194a2a0e2646bc7914d2c4a975a0c13c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Equip $\mathbb{R}^{d}$ with reference process \eqref{eq:OU}, so that $\diffref$ is $N(0,\Id)$. Let $\mu,\nu \in \cP_2(\mathbb{R}^{d})$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assumption}. Let $P^{T}$ be the $\Schro$ bridge from $\mu$ to $\nu$ with \eqref{eq:OU} reference as defined in \eqref{eq:dynam-schro-bridge-defn}, and let $Q^{T}$ denote the noising-denoising approximation in \eqref{defn:diffusion-approx}. Then
