{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.388987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_075caaee484dbba3e0fb6e4601dceae9df5b54c4eb895c92118a3ef61a75af4d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 73 of arXiv:2608.28200, '\textbf On the Formality of Configuration Spaces of $\aka$'] The cohomology group of $\A(\maka)$ is given by
\ali{
&H^\bullet(\maka) \\
=&\hotimes_{j=1}^m \LR{\Hol(\C^n_j)\oplus \oplus_{i=1}^{j-1} \overline{\C[\partial_{z^1_j},\cdots, \partial_{z^n_j}]\omega_{ij}}} \\
=&\oplus_{k=0}^{m-1}\oplus_{\substack{1< j_1<\cdots<j_{k}\le m\\ i_1<j_1,\cdots,i_k<j_k}} \LR{\hotimes_{l\ne j_1,\cdots,j_k}\Hol(\C^n_l)} \hotimes \LR{\hotimes_{l=1}^k\overline{\C[\partial_{z_{j_l}^1},\cdots, \partial_{z_{j_l}^n}]\omega_{i_lj_l}}}
}
where $\Hol(\C^n_i)$ denotes the space of holomorphic functions of $\zz_i\in \C^n$, 
and the cohomology group of \\$\Adef(\maka)$ is
\ali{
&\Hdef(\maka) \\
=&\otimes_{j=1}^m \LR{\C[z_j^1,\cdots,z_j^n]\oplus \oplus_{i=1}^{j-1} {\C[\partial_{z^1_j},\cdots, \partial_{z^n_j}]\omega_{ij}}} \\
=&\oplus_{k=0}^{m-1}\oplus_{\substack{1< j_1<\cdots<j_{k}\le m\\ i_1<j_1,\cdots,i_k<j_k}} \LR{\otimes_{l\ne j_1,\cdots,j_k}\C[z_l^1,\cdots,z_l^n]} \otimes \LR{\otimes_{l=1}^k{\C[\partial_{z_{j_l}^1},\cdots, \partial_{z_{j_l}^n}]\omega_{i_lj_l}}}
}
which is naturally identified as a dense subspace of the former.
\iffalse
Moreover, the embedding 
$$
\Adef(\maka) \hlra \A(\maka)
$$
induces an evident dense injection on cohomology groups.
\fi","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.146309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_075d35f59d913f71c48addd86d12cfd9a67284054539d9b8c571381d5ef71167","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:jordan2 of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For a finite tree $\mathrm{t}=(V_n,E_n)$, we define the \emph{Jordan-$2$ centrality} $\phi_{\mathrm{t}}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}} : V_n \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ by
\begin{equation}
    \phi_\mathrm{t}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}}(v):=  \phi_\mathrm{t}(v) \cdot \big(\phi_\mathrm{t}(v^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({1}})}}) \vee  \phi_\mathrm{t}(v) \big).
\end{equation}
If $v^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({1}})}}$ is not uniquely defined, we let $v^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({1}})}}$ be such that the resulting choice minimizes $\phi_\mathrm{t}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}}$.  The Jordan-2 ordering $\widehat\sigma_2$ is given by ordering vertices decreasingly by $\phi_\mathrm{t}^{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}}$, and breaking ties uniformly at random.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.269202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07606e0397ee38efdcdf4848fdc057d0568bf32ba02decec364222f066b348a7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:simple-azuma-gtp of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be the simple repeated gamble space with $\mathcal{Y} = [-1,1]$, $\hat\mathcal{Z} = \{y\mapsto \beta y \mid \beta \geq 0\}$, and some $T\in\mathbb{N}$.
  Then for all $\epsilon > 0$ we have
  \begin{align}

    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{P}}}\left[\sum_{t=1}^T Y_t \geq \epsilon\right] \leq \exp \left(- {\epsilon ^{2} \over 2T}\right)~.
  \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.568431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0761df471af3a43d57c8d900540905a1033abe129458a904563d2f751b5e4ef2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thr:Singularity degree of arXiv:2411.10311, 'Planar Novikov-Shubin invariant for adjacency matrices of structured directed dense random'] Let $S$ be an irreducible non-negative matrix, with support. Let the minimal ratio of $\prec$-edges to { total edges}, as defined in (equation def of orders of the paper), on cycles be 
\begin{equation}
\kappa:= \min_{\gamma} \frac{\langle \gamma \rangle}{\lvert \gamma \rvert} \in (0,1]
\end{equation}
where the minimum is taken over all cycles $\gamma$.

Then near the origin, the self-consistent density of states, $\sigma$, given in (equation eq:defsig of the paper), blows up like:
\[
\lim_{z \to 0} \frac{\log \sigma(z)}{\log |z|} = -2+2\1\kappa\,.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.061882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0761e36fb23842a971ba63d5ae1e7f3b70f9fa375102e7188e14c791b9a2e9c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm_stationary of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Suppose that $\mathrm{\mathbf{A}}_p(b,\alpha,\varepsilon)$ is
		satisfied with $\overline{b}:=b-\alpha >0$ {and that $\sup_{k>r}\|\Theta^\pi_{t_r,t_k}(\mu) \|_p<\infty$ for any $\mu\in\mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R}^d)$.}
		Then the following statements
		hold.

		\medskip

		\textbf{A. } There exists a $(\psi ,p)-$stationary measure $\mu _{\ast }$
		for $\{X_{n}\}_{n}.$

		\smallskip

		\textbf{B. } Furthermore, for every $\mu$, there exists $C(\mu)\in {\mathbb R}_+$
		\begin{equation}
			W_{p}^{p}(\mathcal{L}(X_{n}),\mu _{\ast
			})=W_{p}^{p}(\Theta^\pi_{t_{0},t_{n}}(\mu ),\mu _{\ast })\leq C(\mu)(e^{-
				\overline{b} t_{n}}+c_{\ast }\gamma _{n}^{\varepsilon
			})+\limsup_{m\rightarrow \infty }\delta _{0,n,m},  
		\end{equation}
		where $\mu=\mathcal{L}(X_0)$. { Besides, if there exists $C\in \mathbb{R}_+$ such that for all $\mu$, $\sup_{0\le r \le k} \left\Vert \Theta_{t_{r},t_{k}}^{\pi
			}(\mu)\right\Vert _{p}^p\leq C(1+\left\Vert \mu\right\Vert
			_{p}^p) $ (this holds when the assumption~(equation New0bis of the paper) holds), we can take $C(\mu)\le \tilde{C}(1+\|\mu\|_p^p)$ for some constant $\tilde{C}\in {\mathbb R}_+$. } (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.295297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0763797ec79f6e90620cc4db1936243ea0a686719ded4ba726d44f396444405a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:exit_pt_comp_ptp of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Let $j \in \mathbb{Z}$, and let $f:\mathbb{Z}_{\ge j} \to \mathbb{R}$ be an initial condition. Let $\ell \ge m \ge n \ge j$ be integers. Then, for all integers $p \ge Z_{f,j}(\ell,n)$, we have 
 \begin{equation} 
 G_{f,j}(\ell,n) - G_{f,j}(m,n) \le G\bigl((p,j),(\ell,n)\bigr) - G\bigl((p,j),(m,n)\bigr).
 \end{equation}
 Furthermore,  for all $p \in \llbracket j, Z_{f,j}(m,n) \rrbracket$, we have 
 \begin{equation} 
 G_{f,j}(\ell,n) - G_{f,j}(m,n) \ge G\bigl((p,j),(\ell,n)\bigr) - G\bigl((p,j),(m,n)\bigr).
 \end{equation}
 Lastly, if $p \in \mathbb{Z}_{\le r}$, then
 \begin{equation} 
 G\bigl((p,j),(\ell,n)\bigr) - G\bigl((p,j),(m,n)\bigr) \le G\bigl((r,j),(\ell,n)\bigr) - G\bigl((r,j),(m,n)\bigr).
 \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.788917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0764f9297f1ef74f2883b6a661045422be5523b03d255e4ffa9fc29ed022283f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition j1 of arXiv:2411.18374, 'Drawdowns of diffusions'] For a Borel-measurable  $f:{\bf R}_+\times{\bf R}_+\mapsto{\bf R}_+$ and   $\delta>\rho\geq 0$ 
\begin{equation}

{\bf E}_0\left(f(M_{\theta_\delta},{\theta_\delta})\,|\, {\cal F}_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\rho}\right)=
Q_{\rho,\delta}\left( M_{\theta_\rho},{\theta_\rho}; f\right),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align*}
 Q_{\rho,\delta}\left( y,s; f\right)&={\bf E}_{y-\rho}\left( f(y,s+H_{y-\delta})\,;\, H_{y-\delta}<H_y\right)
\\
&\hskip2cm+  {\bf E}_{y-\rho}\left( F_\delta(y,H_y)\,;\, H_y< H_{y-\delta}\right)
\end{align*}
and for $a>0$
\begin{align*}
 F_\delta(y,{a}):={\bf E}_{y}\left( f(M_{\theta_\delta},a+\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\delta)\right).
\end{align*}
In particular, for a Borel-measurable $f:{\bf R}_\mapsto{\bf R}_+$
\begin{equation}

{\bf E}_0\left(f(M_{\theta_\delta})\,|\, {\cal F}_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\rho}\right)=Q_{\rho,\delta}\left( M_{\theta_\rho}; f\right),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}\hskip-.2cm

 Q_{\rho,\delta}\left( y; f\right)&:=f(y){\bf P}_{y-\rho}\left( H_{y-\delta}<H_y\right) + {\bf E}_y\left( f(M_{\theta_\delta})\right) {\bf P}_{y-\rho}\left( H_y< H_{y-\delta}\right),
\end{align}
and, hence,   $(M_{\theta_\delta})_{\delta\geq 0}$    is a Markov process with respect to its own filtration ${\cal F}^M_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}}=({\cal F}^M_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_\tau})_{\tau\geq 0}:=(\sigma\{ M_{\hbox {\rm tanh\,}_u}; u\leq \tau\})_{\tau\geq 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.471787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_076c8bc2ddb310dd174016c202e02967950b60deced96a038a9e3e461063c1a2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:hypocoercivesemi of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] We say that $\{P_t\}_{t \geq 0}$ \emph{converges to equilibrium} if for each $x \in \mathcal{H}$, there exists a decay function $r: \mathbb{R}_+ \to \mathbb{R}_+$ with $\lim_{t \to \infty} r(t) = 0$ such that
\begin{align} 
    \|P_t x - P_\infty x\|_{\mathcal{H}} \leq r(t) \|x - P_\infty x\|_{\mathcal{H}}.
\end{align}
When $r(t) = Ce^{- \nu t}$ for some $C >  1, \nu > 0$, we say the semigroup is \emph{hypocoercive}. In the case of $r(t) = e^{-\nu t}$ (i.e., $C = 1$), it is called \emph{coercive}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.662306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_076cfdcd5cc96841d8350f46a8df30908b7bcc74dd5dfd77971d1c464dc2f016","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] Let $\tau\in \mcB\sqcup\mcB^+$ and $n\in\bfN^{d+1}$,
		\begin{itemize}
			\item[-] If $|\tau|-|n|>0$, then 
			\begin{equation}
				\widetilde{ g}^\mcY\big( D^n \Psi(\tau) \big)
				= \widetilde{ g}\big( D^n \tau \big).
			\end{equation}
			\item[-] If $|\tau|-|n|<0$, then 
			\begin{equation}
				\partial^n_{y} \Big({\Pi}^\mcY_x\left(\Psi(\tau)\right)(y)\Big)_{|y=x}=
				\partial^n_y \big({ \Pi}_x \tau (y) \big)_{|y=x}.
			\end{equation}
		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.117394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0772ca416cce5a35e834902711f1ea25d39f6503f0000c359b19a6f2c9182164","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Bartlett--Koopman correspondence) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Let $\eta$ be stationary with local second moments. For every
$f\in\mathcal S(\bR^d)$,
\begin{equation}

    d\varsigma_{(\mathbb S f)^\circ}(\xi)
