{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.045740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07780ef263c19871f68dd5d96320b6154a22ee4664d78bebe87a1f88f22506b6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 of arXiv:2609.00758, 'Deformations of Compact Calabi--Yau and Fano Varieties with Isolated Singularities'] Let $X,Y$ be complex spaces and $f:Y\to X$ a morphism with $f_*\O_Y=\O_X.$ Let $A$ be an Artin local $\C$-algebra, $\cX\to\spec A$ a deformation of $X,$ and $\cY\to\spec A$ a deformation of $Y.$ Let $\cY\to\cX$ be a $\spec A$ morphism such that the diagram $\begin{tikzcd}
