{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.165887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0779dbf9d12327fa77bab16719005b454556f892d7eb72e6410f6d92c858ea9e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 (Lemma 4.11, \cite{HanIyerEA26}) of arXiv:2604.17526, '2604.17526'] For every $2\leq k\leq K$, let $q_{k}$ be the probability density function of $X_{k}^1$. For any $\hat T_0>0$, there exists a constant $C_q=C_q(U, \hat T_0)$ such that if $T \geq \hat T_0$, then
