{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.069173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07855fc5a52ef0b0b2745e1eef368b30a5dddaca3ac37d5d6d4049107bd22964","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.01742, 'Large deviation principles for SPDEs with locally Lipschitz coefficients'] (Large deviation principle) The solution $\{u^\varepsilon\}_{\varepsilon> 0}$ to  Eq.\,\eqref{SHE} is said to satisfy an LDP on $\mathcal E^{\beta}([0,T]\times K,\mathbb R)$ with the rate function $I$, if the following two conditions hold:

	(a) (Upper bound) For each closed subset $F$ of $\mathcal E^{\beta}([0,T]\times K, \mathbb R)$,
	\begin{align*}
		\limsup_{ \varepsilon\to0}  \varepsilon\log \mathbb{P}(u^\varepsilon\in F)\le -\inf_{z\in F} I(z).
	\end{align*}

	(b) (Lower bound) For each open subset $G$ of $\mathcal E^{\beta}([0,T]\times K, \mathbb R)$,
	\begin{align*}
		\liminf_{ \varepsilon\to0}  \varepsilon\log \mathbb{P}(u^\varepsilon\in G)\ge -\inf_{z\in G} I(z).
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.294320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0787b209fe9ad860539dfee8e97e43b84d08c386663fb8f8fec9e1a9cd19b027","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Markov of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Let $m \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $f_1,\ldots,f_m:\mathbb{Z}_{\ge j}$ be a coupling of initial conditions, independent of the weights at and above level $j$ : $(\omega_{k,\ell})_{k \ge \ell \ge j}$ (not necessarily independent among the $f_i$). 
Then, the process
\begin{equation} 
n \mapsto \Bigl(G_{f_i,j}(n + k,n)\Bigr)_{i \in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket, k \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}}, \quad n \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge j-1}
\end{equation}
is a Markov chain on the state space $(\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}})^m$. Furthermore,
the recentered process 
\begin{equation} 
n \mapsto \Bigl(G_{f_i,j}(n + k,n) - G_{f_i,j}(n,n) \Bigr)_{i \in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket, k \in \mathbb{N}}, \quad n \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge j}
\end{equation}
is a Markov chain on the state space $(\mathbb{R}^\mathbb{N})^m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.777324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_078865f372f925fae48069d7f097cbbcde59b66f7d0b0fb3dde621da40ae570b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: Perc_Distance of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \ge 2$ and $p > p_c^{\mathrm{site}}(d)$, where $p_c^{\mathrm{site}}(d)$ is the critical parameter of Bernoulli site percolation on $\mathbb Z^d$. Then, there exists a constant $\rho = \rho(p, d) \in [1, \infty)$ such that 
\begin{align*}
	&\limsup_{\|y\|_1 \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\|y\|_1} \log \mathbb P_p( o \leftrightarrow y, d(o, y) > \rho \|y\|_1) < 0, \\
    &\; \text{ and } \; \; \limsup_{\ell \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\ell} \log \mathbb P_p( o \leftrightarrow y, d(o, y) > \ell ) < 0,
\end{align*}
where $d(x, y)$ is the graph distance between $x$ and $y$ on the percolation clusters. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.237111+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0788cb4fbf0563f226fb37d1c5db99921dfb236f33d4b7d207ca191b84f361ea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l4.7 of arXiv:2604.22510, 'Asymptotics of Multi-Scale McKean--Vlasov Diffusions with Super-Linear Kernels: a Lifted S'] Fix $K < \infty $. Consider any sequence $\{(\varphi^{k},{{\boldsymbol{ {\Pi}}}}^{k})\}_{k\in\mathbb{N}}$ such that for every $k\in \mathbb{N}$, $(\varphi^{k},{{\boldsymbol{ {\Pi}}}}^{k})$ is viable and
	\begin{equation}
