{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.246050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07a1c0c164ab32ae3db247651ae3859ce4cfbe7d4ac791f0c3b2e3cd63d857b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 21 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Let $D,f$ be as in \Cref{def:harpoon}. There exists $\phi\in\Adm(D;f)$ such that, for any sequence $(D_N)_{N\ge1}$ of tilable domains such that $D_N\stackrel{N\to\infty}\rightharpoonup (D,f)$ and  for every $\varepsilon>0$, it holds
