{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.971114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07e90d629aa70e0d1cea28bca4973426e16363685fd052e77aa1f5819024afcd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 34 of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] For $T > 0$, we say that a measurable function $u: Q_{T}\to \R$ is a \emph{distributional solution} of $u_{t} - \frac{1}{2d}\Delta(u^{m+1}) = 0$ in $Q_{T}$ if 
