{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.578984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0818bc637fdc0d1ff81427f275765ea83ca007a0d3aacb7bf71b755e3fc75e3f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:QuasiHomeo of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] The forms~$\big({\mssE,\msD(\mssE)}\big)$ and \linebreak $\big({\mssE^\sharp,\msD(\mssE^\sharp)}\big)$ are \emph{quasi-homeo\-morphic} if there exists an $\mssE$-nest~$\left(F_k\right)_k$, an $\mssE^\sharp$-nest~${\big(F^\sharp_k\big)}_k$ and an injective map~$j\colon \cup_k F_k\to\cup_k F^\sharp_k$ such that
