 where on each side, $\hat{\eta}\sim 	\hat{\mathbf{e}}_{x_i,x_{-i}}^{N}$, $\hat{\eta}'\sim \hat{\mathbf{e}}_{x_i',x_{-i}'}^{\{x_i,x_{-i}\},N}$ and $ \mathcal{P}_{x_i,x_i',x_{-i}'',x_{-i}'''}^{a,a',b,b'}$ are independent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:56.998586+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_084b0936ce58ea0e990139a46efca347797d3ea6241d2aa259500c1170d09202","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.02785, 'Characterization of Stanley-Reisner varieties by their automorphism group'] Let $i\in[n]$, let $\beta\in\ZZ^n_{\geq0}$ with $\beta_i=0$, and set $S:=\supp(\beta)$. The formula
