{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.799671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0863f1782adafc868cfc28c227d594c68a0f9951e897bac922835c6710087b24","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:alpha of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] The \emph{slow-mode energy fraction} at step $k$ is
\begin{equation}
\alpha_2(k) := p_2(k) = \frac{n_2(k)}{E_k} = \frac{|c_2|^2 \lambda_2^{2k}}{\sum_{i=2}^n |c_i|^2 \lambda_i^{2k}} \in (0,1).
