{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.301057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0882d58c41465a4337d9a375dea45cbc1f117f383ac2985fae1867ad7958043b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:refined of arXiv:2602.19192, 'Bakry--\'Emery Curvature of the Fractional Laplacian\\ via Fractional Brownian Covariance'] At $\gamma = 1$, decompose $f \in \mathcal{T}_N^+$ along the
eigenbasis $\{\phi_k\}_{k=1}^N$ of $M(1) = R_{1/2}^{-1}\,R_{1/2}^{\circ 2}$.
Then the $k$-th component of the carr\'e du champ contracts at rate
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma(P_t f, P_t f)_k \leq e^{-2(2k-1)t}\,\Gamma(f,f)_k,
