{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.991303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0890080b8702b92e410c7fb2729c3acd34b1b5c1fa0b6d9c81e6516f0db0e613","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 107 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $G = (V,E)$, $|V| = n$, be a graph with maximum degree $\Delta \in \N$, and let $p = \frac{1-s}{\Delta - 1} $ for some $0 < s \leq 1$. Then there exists a constant $C = C(s) > 0$ such that for $k\geq 1$
