{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.403607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_089e85bdd9b9019a674f8afa0e41daf361ea6955f4c24c07191ded9d2c3adfc7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem spin wedge of arXiv:2608.25889, 'Slope Inequalities for the Geography Problem of Spin Symplectic 4-Manifolds'] {\rm (cf.~Theorem~9 in [ap: spin] and Remark~4.2 in [apu])} 
Let\/ $Z$ be a closed spin symplectic\/ $4$-manifold that contains a symplectic torus\/ $T$ of self-intersection\/ $0$.  
Let\/ $\nu (T)$ be a tubular neighborhood of\/ $T$ and\/ $\partial(\nu (T))$ its boundary.  
Suppose that the homomorphism\/ $\pi_1(\partial(\nu (T))) \rightarrow \pi_1(Z\setminus\nu (T))$ induced by the inclusion is trivial.  
Then for any pair of integers\/ $(\chi, c)$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
0\leq c \leq 8\chi  \quad 
\text{and\/} \quad  
c-8\chi \equiv 0 \pmod{16}, 
\end{equation}
there exists a closed spin symplectic\/ $4$-manifold\/ $Y$ with\/ $\pi_1(Y)=\pi_1(Z)$, 
\begin{equation*}
\chi_h(Y)=\chi_h(Z)+\chi  \quad \text{and\/} \quad 
c_1^2(Y)=c_1^2(Z)+c .   
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.758035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08a0e99236cdfaef6b93f4edfa4262c0a71c948120359350983c390dc2eb0fb7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:well-posed of arXiv:2411.02459, 'Existence and higher regularity of statistically steady states for the stochastic Coleman-'] {Assume that \nameref{cond:mu}, \nameref{cond:Q} and \nameref{cond:phi}--\nameref{cond:phi:3} hold}. Then for all $U_0\in\mathcal{H}^0_\mu$, (equation eqn:react-diff:mu of the paper) admits a unique weak solution $U(\,\cdot\,;U_0)$ in the sense of Definition (defn:mild-soln of the paper). Furthermore, the solution $U(t;U_0)$ is continuous in $H$ with respect to $U_0$, for all fixed $t\ge 0$, i.e.,
