{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.478188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08c6b234877c2f1f9d658d0758cc4e94ee6a186b24b76ca9b61afa656acab74b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 98 (Covariance--Gram cut-profile transfer) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Assume the hypotheses of Lemma~\ref{lem:CG-identities}.  Suppose that
$H\ge0$ and $L_q,R_q\ge0$, $0\le q\le m$, satisfy
