{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.609878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08d56951d7d2407d63a182ea4941d3234119074e6a84dceea58d239ba559eec7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop gamma-function of arXiv:2512.13200, 'Martingales on a Euclidean manifold with a boundary and reflected BSDEs in non-convex doma'] {
Consider $\psi \in C^2(\bar{\mathcal{D}})$ and let $U$ be an open subset of $\mathbb{R}^d$ s.t. $ U\cap\bar\mathcal{D} \neq \emptyset$. Assume that $\psi_{|U\cap\bar{\mathcal{D}}}$ is a special $\Gamma$-convex function according to Definition (de spe gamma func of the paper).}

