        \inf_{\{x : |m(x)|<\varepsilon\}} (\lambda_1 - h(x)) - (1-\frac{1}{N}) \frac{1}{\beta} > (\lambda_1-\lambda_2)(\mathsf{m}_{\textsc{e}}^2 - \varepsilon^2)\,.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.886638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08df50f82b66ee97311d33e89b7cca977fb6e378011e513cd73cdd68b3bdb3b3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:PsiPhio of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Whenever $f_0(x)\neq 0$, we have
