{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.647795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08eab43bdbd057f560835735152b2b57acc863bc63d857e8c34d1a591fbb8371","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Q-max-local-time-tail of arXiv:2605.16086, 'Loop pruning and downward deviations for maximum local time of discrete-time simple random'] There exists \(\rho>0\) such that, for all $n$ sufficiently large,
\begin{equation}
