{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.067926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08f44f22dbed20252fce498255f9d13eaddef7bebdae65be6a13b1af7146037e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: main scaling of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $\nu>0$, $R> 0$, $M\ge 1$ and $\theta^n$ time independent satisfying (hyp_noise of the paper). Assume $p \in (4, \infty)$, $-1/2 < r<- 2/p$. Let $\omega^n$ be the solution of (equation main_ito_cutoff of the paper) associated to $\theta^n$ and some initial data $\omega_0\in \mathcal{B}_p(M)$. Let $\omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}}}$ be the solution of 
    \begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
    \partial_t\omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}}} +  \phi_{R}(\|\omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}}}\|_{H^r_g})\mathcal{L}_u \omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}}} + A\omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}}} - \nu\Delta \omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}}}   =0 \\
