    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.687706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08f56d91852d52864328b098ec6f6dd1579a6b0ab3b36b5dfb33f71f3adacd86","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:higher_spatial_moments_ODE_unsimplified of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] Let $n\geq 1$, and let $P_1,\ldots,P_n$ be monomials on $\mathbb R^d$. Then
