{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.799108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08fef05e83b72081b9fd8a6dd2f8b3795103d00e45aab46e7bf6957aa654452a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:trajectory of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Let $g_0 \in L^2(\pi)$ satisfy the centering condition $\langle g_0, \mathbf{1} \rangle_\pi = 0$. The \emph{relaxation trajectory} generated by $g_0$ is the sequence
\begin{equation}
g_k := P^k g_0, \qquad k = 0,1,2,\dots
\end{equation}
The \emph{energy} of the trajectory at step $k$ is
\begin{equation}
E_k := \|g_k\|_\pi^2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.390423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0900e3aec1f6609463619e3b80dfd6b8b10138131adf1fc5d2a1bd1cce59ce7f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p.prob.space of arXiv:2507.16056, 'Conditional GMC within the stochastic heat flow'] Notation as above.
\begin{enumerate}
\item 
The polymer measures $M^{\theta}_{[s,t]}$ for $s<t\in q\mathbb{D}$ can be constructed on $(\Omega,\mathscr{F},\mathbf{P})$ with each $M^{\theta}_{[s,t]}$ being $\mathscr{F}_{[s,t]}$-measurable.
\item 
For $t_1<\cdots<t_{2\ell} \in q\mathbb{D}$, $I_{i}:=[t_{2i-1},t_{2i}]$, and $r_i:=t_{2i+1}-t_{2i}$\ ,
\begin{align}

	\mathbf{E}\big[ 
		M^{\theta}_{[t_1,t_{2\ell}]} 
	\,\big|\,
		\mathscr{F}_{I_1\cup\cdots\cup I_{\ell}}
	\big]
