{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.150880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0905559480c3717db64fc0d086dcd75646931b3d0cfbdf59806b95980db741ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma3.1 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $\Omega \subset \mathbb R^3$ be  a smoothly bounded domain, and supposed that $p>0$ and $1< r<6$. Then for any $\eta>0$ one can find constant $C(\eta,p,r)>0$




such that
