{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.125851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_093bd9e9f077b2be46441646d89e6e16e04aba19867553162f6966d71c74bebb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 (Rohlin--Sinai--Kami\'nski) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Let $T$ be a probability-preserving $\bZ^d$-action on a standard probability
space, and let $\Pi(T)$ denote its Pinsker $\sigma$-algebra. There is a
