{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.851286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0945fa7101b0b995741f882749d9551ee385c13f04d52e1d87e3935c2d7240c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop hepp_3 of arXiv:2607.10105, 'The four-dimensional Anderson model: a case study for critical SPDEs'] For any Hepp tree $\mathcal T$ and marking $(N_\mathfrak n)$, let $\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T)$ be the automorphism group of $\mathcal T$  (preserving the root), and $\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n)$ be the automorphism group of the marked tree $\mathcal T$ (preserving the root and the marks). Then, for any $(m_\mathfrak l)$ and any $(y_j)\leftrightarrow (\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n,m_\mathfrak l)$ we have
\begin{equation}
\#\{(N_\mathfrak n',m_\mathfrak l'):(y_j)\leftrightarrow (\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n',m_\mathfrak l')\}\geq\frac{|\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T)|}{|\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n)|}.
\end{equation}
In addition, for any $z_0,z_1\in\mathbb Z_M^4$ we have
\begin{equation}\frac{|\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n)|}{|\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T)|}\sum_{\substack{Z\leftrightarrow (\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n)\\z_0\in Z}}1\leq C^n\prod_{\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B} N_\mathfrak n^{4(\gamma_\mathfrak n-1)},\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\frac{|\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n)|}{|\mathrm{Aut}(\mathcal T)|}\sum_{\substack{Z\leftrightarrow (\mathcal T,N_\mathfrak n)\\z_0,z_1\in Z}}1\leq C^n\cdot\langle z_0-z_1\rangle^{-4}\cdot\prod_{\mathfrak n\in\mathcal B} N_\mathfrak n^{4(\gamma_\mathfrak n-1)},
\end{equation}
where $\gamma_\mathfrak n$ is the number of children of $\mathfrak n$ as in Definition (def.hepp_2 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.678317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_094844c52cee3620eb94b32c86b771bcf6f976924efa9751d441507e60e67500","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:walk of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Fix $N,l\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$ and $M_{1},\ldots,M_{l}\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$, $M_1+\ldots+M_l=M$. For each sequence of monomials $\{P(s)\}_{s=0}^{M}$, coming form the action $\frac{1}{\mu_{+}(N)^{M}}\left(\frac{\mathcal{D}_{i_{l}}}{N}\right)^{M_{l}}\cdots \left(\frac{\mathcal{D}_{i_{1}}}{N}\right)^{M_{1}}G_{N}(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta)|_{\vec{x}=0}$, let $E(t):[0,M]\rightarrow \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$ be a C\'adl\'ag function defined by 
        \begin{equation}
