        \end{equation} 
        We refer to $E(t)$ as a walk.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.402421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0949ac8dd3a117d78dd739a992e457ef7cded7d744bec9384668a74cad5bbde7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2605.15386, 'The non-central gamma sum and difference distributions: exact distribution and asymptotic '] 1. Suppose that $\alpha_1+\alpha_2<1$. Then, as $x\rightarrow0$,
	\begin{equation}
		f_{X_1-X_2}(x)\sim \frac{1}{\pi}\beta_1^{-\alpha_1}\beta_2^{-\alpha_2}\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda_1-\lambda_2}\sin(\pi a_{0,0}(x))\Gamma(1-\alpha_1-\alpha_2)\,|x|^{\alpha_1+\alpha_2-1},
	\end{equation}
    where $a_{0,0}(x)=\alpha_1$ for $x>0$ and $a_{0,0}(x)=\alpha_2$ for $x<0$.

    \vspace{3mm}

	\noindent 2. Suppose that $\alpha_1+\alpha_2=1$. Then, as $x\rightarrow0$,
	\begin{equation}
	f_{X_1-X_2}(x)\sim-\frac{1}{\pi}\beta_1^{-\alpha_1}\beta_2^{-\alpha_2}\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda_1-\lambda_2}\sin(\pi a_{0,0}(x))\ln|x|.
	\end{equation}
    3. The distribution of $X_1-X_2$ is unimodal with mode 0 if $\alpha_1+\alpha_2\leq 1$.

    \vspace{3mm}

    \noindent
4. Suppose that $\alpha_1+\alpha_2>1$. Then
\begin{align}
f_{X_1-X_2}(0)&=\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda_1-\lambda_2} \beta_1^{-\alpha_1}\beta_2^{-\alpha_2}\bigg(\frac{1}{\beta_1}+\frac{1}{\beta_2}\bigg)^{1-\alpha_1-\alpha_2} \frac{\Gamma(\alpha_1+\alpha_2-1)}{\Gamma(\alpha_1)\Gamma(\alpha_2)}\nonumber\\
&\quad\times  \Psi_2\bigg(\alpha_1+\alpha_2-1,\alpha_1,\alpha_2,\frac{\lambda_1\beta_2}{\beta_1+\beta_2},\frac{\lambda_2\beta_1}{\beta_1+\beta_2}\bigg). 
\end{align}

    \vspace{3mm}

    \noindent
	5. The PDF $f_{X_1-X_2}(x)$ is bounded for all $x\in\mathbb{R}$ if and only if $\alpha_1+\alpha_2>1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.076525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_094e07612f49da9884e7ef11376a8cd770d6203fc1bb412f5990354dfa925011","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sineb_series of arXiv:2509.15446, 'On the pair correlation function of the $\Sineb$ process'] Define $\mathbf{s}_k \in {\mathbb C}^n$ recursively as
