{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.985310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_096d2bf07030061bc80d1f4cf163f2b391c758c1a87c8edcdb208f637d1470bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm d'existence of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] Assume (a1 of the paper)-(a2 of the paper).  Let $\eta_0>0$ and  $\lambda_0>0$ small enough. Let $\eta \in [0,\eta_0]$ and $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ fixed, with $|\lambda|\leqslant \lambda_0$. Then, there is a unique function $M_{\lambda,\eta}$ in $\mathcal{H}_0$, solution to the penalized equation
\begin{equation}
\big[-\Delta_v+ W(v)+  \mathrm{i}  \eta v -\lambda\eta^{\frac{2}{3}}\big]M_{\lambda,\eta}(v)= b(\lambda,\eta)\Phi(v), \qquad v \in \mathbb{R}^d ,
\end{equation} 
where $\displaystyle b(\lambda,\eta):=\langle N_{\lambda,\eta},\Phi \rangle$ with $N_{\lambda,\eta} := M_{\lambda,\eta}-M$. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \| N_{\lambda,\eta} \|_{\mathcal{H}_0} = \| M_{\lambda,\eta} - M \|_{\mathcal{H}_0} \underset{\eta \rightarrow 0}{\longrightarrow}0.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.688986+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09701b3bfc5f773d07c01f14bb23e0f1cf75cff9e1ee1cf7c3a0ed36f69c8be1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Almost-diagonal action of physical cutoffs) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $\varphi\in C_c^\infty(\R^3)$.  For every $L>0$, every
$1\le q\le\infty$, and every two non-comparable dyadic scales $M,N$,
\begin{equation}
 \|P_M\varphi P_N\|_{\mathcal L(L^q,L^q)}
 \lesssim_{L,q,\varphi}
 \left(\frac{\min\{M,N\}}{\max\{M,N\}}\right)^L.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every $r\in\R$,
\begin{align}
 \|\varphi f\|_{H^r}
 &\lesssim_{r,\varphi}\|f\|_{H^r},
 \\
 \|\varphi f\|_{B^r_{2,\infty}}
 &\lesssim_{r,\varphi}\|f\|_{B^r_{2,\infty}}.

\end{align}
In particular, these estimates hold for negative $r$.  Multiplication by
$\varphi$ preserves the little-Besov space $b^r_{2,\infty}$ and, for path
spaces, the uniform little-Besov tail condition
\eqref{eq:uniform-little-besov-tail} introduced below.  The same conclusions
hold for differences of two fixed physical cutoffs.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.764273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_097076332bab0c773f90259b870cf14a72fc8daa0d33aaff761e8f073822380e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 17 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] Let $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ be some fixed sampler and $G$ the Gibbs sampler induced by some partition $(\mathcal{O}_i)_{i=1}^k$, where $n \geq k \geq 2.$. Suppose further that $\pi$ is ordered non-decreasingly, i.e. $\pi(1) \leq \pi(2) \leq \dots \leq \pi(n).$ Then for $\alpha \in [0,1)$, the partition
    \begin{equation}
        (\mathcal{O}_i)_{i=1}^k = \begin{cases}
        \{ i \}, & \mathrm{if}\ 1 \leq i \leq k-1,\\
        \{ k, k+1, \dots, n\}, & \mathrm{if}\ i = k.
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation}
    belongs to the set of minimisers

    \begin{align*}
        \argmin_{\mathcal{O}_1 \neq \emptyset, \mathcal{X},\ldots,\mathcal{O}_k \neq \emptyset, \mathcal{X}} \KL{\widetilde{\pi}_\alpha}(Q_\alpha\ \|\ \widetilde{\Pi}_\alpha) 
        &= \argmin_{\mathcal{O}_1 \neq \emptyset, \mathcal{X},\ldots,\mathcal{O}_k \neq \emptyset, \mathcal{X}} \KL{\pi} (G\| \Pi) \\
        &= \argmin_{\mathcal{O}_1 \neq \emptyset, \mathcal{X},\ldots,\mathcal{O}_k \neq \emptyset, \mathcal{X}} H(\overline{\pi}).
    \end{align*}

    Moreover, the minimiser is unique up to permutation of block labels and ties in the probabilities $\pi(x)$. In particular, any minimising partition may be obtained by choosing $k-1$ states of smallest $\pi$-mass as singleton blocks, with the remaining states grouped into one block.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.982057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09739b07ed846c2cc716513f6349284c6921c48f58a2216a72b75d0f07950405","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem_epsBallSupEstimate of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] Let $\mathcal{M}$ be a homogeneous Riemannian manifold with some fixed point $O\in\mathcal{M}$ on which the fractional L\'evy field exists for a Hurst parameter $H>0$. Then it is a.s.\ continuous and there exists a constant $C_1 > 0$ (depending only on $d$ and $H$), such that for all $\zeta\in\mathcal{M}$ and all $0 < \varepsilon < 1$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        \expec{\sup_{\eta\in\mkern 1.5mu\overline{\mkern-1.5mu\mathcal{B}\mkern-1.5mu}\mkern 1.5mu_{\varepsilon}(\zeta)} X_\eta} \leq \varepsilon^H \sqrt{- C_1 \log \varepsilon} + \mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\varepsilon^H}{\sqrt{-\log \varepsilon}}\right).
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.589433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0973beba7fc947dabfccc1457d7ec512958ea9449d705154593961a2f5047160","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm higher alpha of arXiv:2603.15323, '\Large \bf Small-time heat decay for stable processes on fractal drums'] Let $d\geq 1$, $\alpha\in (d-\mathfrak{b}, 2)$, where $\mathfrak{b}$ is the interior Minkowski
dimension of $\partial G$, and $G$ is a set given as in (equation eqn:SS of the paper).
Assume that Condition (cond:higher alpha of the paper) holds true. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $\{\ln\frac{1}{r_j}\}_{j=1}^{N}$ is non-arithmetic, then we have 
\begin{equation}
Q_{G}^{(\alpha)}(t)=m(G)-C_{1}t^{\frac{d-\mathfrak{b}}{\alpha}} +o(t^{\frac{d-\mathfrak{b}}{\alpha}}) \text{ as } t\downarrow 0,
\end{equation}
where $C_{1}$ is the constant given by 
$$C_{1}=\frac{\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}\mathcal{R}(e^{-z})dz}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}r_{j}^{\mathfrak{b}}\ln\frac{1}{r_{j}^{\alpha}}}=
\frac{\int_{0}^{\infty}\left(m(G_{0})-Q_{G_{0}}^{(\alpha)}(u)-\mathcal{D}(u)\right)u^{-1-\frac{d-\mathfrak{b}}{\alpha}}dt}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}r_{j}^{\mathfrak{b}}\ln\frac{1}{r_{j}^{\alpha}}}.
$$

\item If $\{\ln\frac{1}{r_{j}}\}_{j=1}^{N}$ is arithmetic with span $\rho$, then we have 
\begin{equation}
Q_{G}^{(\alpha)}(t)=m(G)-f(-\ln t)t^{\frac{d-\mathfrak{b}}{\alpha}} +o(t^{\frac{d-\mathfrak{b}}{\alpha}}) \text{ as } t\downarrow 0,
\end{equation}
where 
\[
f(z)=\frac{\alpha\rho}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}r_{j}^{\mathfrak{b}}\ln\frac{1}{r_{j}^{\alpha}}}
\sum_{n=-\infty}^{\infty}\mathcal{R}(e^{-(z-n\alpha\rho)}).
\]
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.663384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0973f6b845a3557c77bb5c8c519f87575e0243e4b72a38874ee5ca1ceb639134","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2607.25645, 'Estimates of the total variation distance between laws of Sobolev mappings on Gaussian spa'] Let $g_1,\ldots,g_k,h_1,\ldots,h_k\in L^p(\gamma)$, where $p>2k-1$. Then
