{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.713773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09782e420517dd7964055329486eddfbff7861c84cec7809e4713ab1fdc125a5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $\widetilde{p}$ be the reference kernel defined in Theorem (prop:alpha_llt of the paper) with $\alpha=2$. In the diffusive regime ($n\lambda \to \infty$), we have
