{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.732363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_098d3a0bfa8951a484e359f300288584105fda47776a7911e237171c42e8b236","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 88 (Continuity of the localized source maps) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Fix $0<T\le T_0$, an adapted localization pair $(\chi,\rho)$, and constants
$A,R\ge1$.  Let $\Xi,\widetilde\Xi$ satisfy Definition~\ref{def:Xi-assumptions} on $[0,T]$ and assume
\[
 M_T(\Xi)+M_T(\widetilde\Xi)\le A,
\]
and let $Z,\widetilde Z\in\mathcal Z_T$ satisfy
$\|Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}+\|\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}\le R$.  To display the dependence on $\Xi$, write
$\mathscr F_{X;\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}$ and
$\mathscr F_{Y;\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}$ for the functionals in
\eqref{eq:localized-X-source}--\eqref{eq:localized-Y-source}.  Then
\begin{align}
 &\bigl\|\mathscr F_{X;\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(Z)
       -\mathscr F_{X;\widetilde\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(\widetilde Z)
  \bigr\|_{\mathfrak R_T^{s_1,\sigma}}
 \notag\\
 &\quad+
 \bigl\|\mathscr F_{Y;\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(Z)
       -\mathscr F_{Y;\widetilde\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(\widetilde Z)
  \bigr\|_{\mathfrak S_T^{s_2,\sigma}}
 \notag\\
 &\qquad\le C_{A,R,\chi,\rho}
 \left(M_T(\Xi-\widetilde\Xi)
       +\|Z-\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}\right).

\end{align}
Consequently, if in addition
$\Theta,\widetilde\Theta\in
 C_T\mathcal C_{\mathrm{loc}}^{-1-\betasum-\kappa}$, then the source triples satisfy
\begin{align}
 &\|\chi(\Theta-\widetilde\Theta)\|_{
       C_T\mathcal C^{-1-\betasum-\kappa}}
 +\bigl\|\mathscr F_{X;\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(Z)
       -\mathscr F_{X;\widetilde\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(\widetilde Z)
  \bigr\|_{\mathfrak R_T^{s_1,\sigma}}
 \notag\\
 &\quad+
 \bigl\|\mathscr F_{Y;\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(Z)
       -\mathscr F_{Y;\widetilde\Xi}^{\chi,\rho}(\widetilde Z)
  \bigr\|_{\mathfrak S_T^{s_2,\sigma}}
 \notag\\
 &\qquad\le C_{A,R,\chi,\rho}
 \left(
 \|\chi(\Theta-\widetilde\Theta)\|_{
       C_T\mathcal C^{-1-\betasum-\kappa}}
 +M_T(\Xi-\widetilde\Xi)
 +\|Z-\widetilde Z\|_{\mathcal Z_T}
 \right).

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.873294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_098fd4cd77ae70bfbeef7b0ae22973c71e3d1fbfba1458c03f0a1615289823fd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:G6local of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] For every fixed $h\le H$,
\begin{align}
  \left|\frac1N\sum_{c=1}^N\mathbb{E}[\theta_{c,h}^3]\right|
  &\le C_Hr_{\gamma,N},                                                     \\
  \frac1N\sum_{c=1}^N\mathbb{E}[\theta_{c,h}^4]
  &\le C_Hv_{\gamma,N}.                                                  
\end{align}
