{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.032885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09a3f47dbd1cea01036575222fd4b9243f79a66cd74966e72220f7d2f742563c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:muckenhoupt_maximal of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] If $\rho\in A_2$, then there exists a constant $C(d)>0$ such that for $u\in L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\rho)$,
