{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.726050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09aca1cb8983d2478967c0715597fd5ea4003716fa9eb0116351dc9a5705883e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2511.13559, 'Asymptotic analysis of rare events in high dimensions'] Let $f$ be a function on $\br^d$ and $h(x) = f(x) -f(0_d)-\nabla f(0_d)^\top x - \frac12x^\top\nabla^2f(0_d)x$. Let $X\sim \mathcal N(0_d, (\la H)^{-1})$ and $\us = \us(R\e)$. Let $f_3 = \|\nabla^3f(0_d)\|_H$ and $f_4=\sup_{x\in\us}\|\nabla^4f(x)\|_H$. Then 
