{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.862898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09ad6918c5ed1472a6731aaf582c87bfda12cdf9009cafe306628123b1879188","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 16 of arXiv:2511.22156, ''] Let $u_n$ be the function attaining \eqref{e:5.1}. Let $Q_1,Q_2\in \mathcal{Q}_0(F_0^n)$ with $\sigma(Q_1\cap Q_2)>0,$ and denote by $\nu_i$ the outer normal to $\partial Q_i$ for $i=1,2$. Then 
