{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.842475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09c7aed248847da4947913e8505ad6587e7d14608103106ece74063aecb3ab89","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:95 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c$ such that for all $n$, all $1\leq \Delta\leq 2\varepsilon n^{1/3}$, all $|j|,|k|\leq 3\varepsilon n^{1/3}$, and all $0\leq i\leq \Delta^3/4$, we have
