{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.579228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09cafe545c864f81688bd0402f5eae4511d169e7dd51e54dafb94a6edceb9875","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:weak_sol_ Robin of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] {Let $\rho_0:[-1,1]\rightarrow [0,1]$ be a measurable function.} We say that  $\rho:[0,T]\times[-1,1] \to [-1,1]$ is a weak solution of the heat equation with Robin boundary conditions 
	\begin{equation}
