{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.316874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09deb76fe1c66e6e931d03a30acbcaa0ef26f6e1e2d2952e1132d71733f93139","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2609.01485, 'On the Ramification of Quadratic Fields where the Torsion of a Rational Elliptic Curve Gro'] Let $E/\mathbb{Q}$ be a rational elliptic curve such that there exists $P\in E(K)[5]\setminus E(\mathbb{Q})$, where $K|\mathbb{Q}$ is a quadratic field. Suppose that $E$ has additive reduction at $5$. Then the following are equivalent
