{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.232066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09e32b51901f86f210bccc06b7644bf7ffc43e60dc19faff4b457f8cd2ac31e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm1:srd of arXiv:2506.17168, '{\bf Scaling limits for sample autocovariance operators of Hilbert space-valued linear pro'] Let $\{X_n\}_{n \in \mathbb Z}$ be an $\mathbb{H}$-valued linear process (equation eq:linear_process of the paper), and consider its autocovariance operators $(\widehat \Gamma_{N,h}, h = 0,\dots,H)$ given in (equation eq:SampleAutoShort of the paper) with $\widehat \Gamma_{N,h} \in \operatorname{HS}(\mathbb{H})$ for all $h$ with a slight abuse of notation. Suppose (equation cond:srd-improved_1 of the paper) and 
