{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.352907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09e4819d6370d342cc6004cef102e6d0303a497e0214f774e2f6d1cada778ea6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_hypercontract of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] ([nourdinpeccatibook])

    Assume $p>1,t>0$ and $q(t)=e^{2t}(p-1)+1$. If $F\in L^p(\Omega)$ then
