{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.977933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09ee03e650cb7f7d6ef23319019729c7173fe53a56ad949da09777e6b8896f5d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.11369, 'Mean-field limits for stochastic particle systems on dense graphs'] Let $(\mu_t)_{t\ge 0}$ be a weak solution of \eqref{eq:weak_limit} such that for every $T>0,$
