{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.989951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09fcba722a4b43aa8dda6f2b4b04c6aa24b1ef84e53e5eca037d93ce2b2e15a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2604.00882, 'On some extensions of generalized counting processes'] The probability generating function $
	{G}_\nu(u, t) = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} u^k {p}_k^\nu(t)$, $|u| \leq 1$, solves the following fractional differential equation
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{\partial^{2\nu} G_\nu(u, t)}{\partial t^{2\nu}} + 2\lambda \frac{\partial^\nu G_\nu(u, t)}{\partial t^\nu} = \Lambda(u - 1)G_\nu(u, t), 
	\end{equation}
	subject to the initial condition $G(u, 0) = 1$, and is given as
	\begin{equation}
		G_\nu(u, t) = \tilde \ell_\nu (\Lambda(u - 1), t), \,\,u < 1,
