{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.316083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a05404c01c9cfd03fe0b72bac409288a659a682acb5ad1ae116314fcc11a34c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:loop-mass-estimates of arXiv:2607.18070, 'The Brownian loop-catcher'] These estimates hold with
constants independent of the mesh.
\begin{enumerate}
\item For every \(\varepsilon>0\),
\begin{align*}
 \lim_{\eta\downarrow0}\limsup_{\delta\downarrow0}
 m_\delta\{\operatorname{dur}(\ell)\geq\varepsilon,\
       \ell\not\subset D_\eta\}=0,\qquad
 \lim_{\eta\downarrow0}
 m_D\{\operatorname{dur}(\ell)\geq\varepsilon,\
       \ell\not\subset D_\eta\}=0.
\end{align*}
\item If two sets \(A_\delta,B_\delta\subset D^\delta\) have distance at
