{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.464445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a1a1020caf8fb4afe39b960799288de9bb9eb45ed8e6dbcbd003da4b9e4c65c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2606.28793, 'Randomized second order Riesz projections on the Hamming cube'] Let $1<p<\infty$ and assume that $X^*$ has Rademacher type $2$.  Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$ be the Pisier holomorphic semigroup exponent, chosen uniformly for the finite Hilbertian sums $\ell_2^M(X)$.  Define
\[
 a_{p,X}=
 \begin{cases}
  (2-\alpha)/p, & 1<p<2,\\
  1-\alpha/2, & 2\leq p<\infty.
 \end{cases}
\]
Then, for every $k\geq1$, every $n,d\geq1$, and every $f\in\mathcal P_d(\Omega_n;X)$,
\[
 \|G^{\mathrm{ord}}_{k,X}f\|_{L^p(\Omega_n)}
 \leq C_{p,X}^k d^{ka_{p,X}}\|f\|_{L^p(\Omega_n;X)}.
\]
In particular,
\[
 \left\|
 \left(
 \sum_{\substack{A\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}\\ |A|=k}}
 \|D_Af\|_X^2
 \right)^{1/2}
 \right\|_{L^p(\Omega_n)}
 \leq C_{p,X}^k d^{ka_{p,X}}\|f\|_{L^p(\Omega_n;X)}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.835135+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a22d4426a7e9639030668a63ad0e8c4ed02515947d98b41ee6e6c5f72086f52","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 5 of arXiv:2506.12755, '{\bf Stochastic intrinsic gradient flows on the Wasserstein space}\footnote{Supported in p'] In addition to $(C_3)$ we assume $W_F\in\D(\EE)$ and $\e^{-W_F}\in\D(\EE)\cap L^\infty(\scr P_p,\Lam)$. Let $(A,\D(A))$ be the generator of $(\EE,\D(\EE))$ in $L^2(\scr P_p,\Lam)$.
	The diffusion $(\Omega, \scr F,(\mu_t)_{t\geq 0},$ $(\P^\mu)_{\mu\in \scr P_p})$ on $\scr P_p $ 
