{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:02:18.047866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a3b94a07c924a4cda169019de7ac0768b34fbb641ab17e89f6d87c1e08657de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:h-basic-chernoff of arXiv:2602.21315, 'The Instability of all Backoff Protocols\thanks{For the purpose of Open Access, the author'] Fix a send sequence $\overline{p}$ with $p_0=1$. Let $\alpha$ be a real number with $0 < \alpha \le 1$, let $j\ge 1$ be an integer, and suppose $j$ is sufficiently large relative to $\alpha$. Fix an integer $\tau \ge 0$, a real number $\nu\ge 0$, and $\overline{a} \in (\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0})^j$. Let $E^+$ be a constant-escape process on $[j]$ with send sequence~$\overline{p}$, start time $\tau$, end-of-step arrival rate $\nu$, and $\overline{\mathrm{arr}}_{[j]}^{E^+}(\tau) = \overline{a}$. Fix $k \in [j]$ and $t \ge \tau$, and let $\mu = h_k^{\nu,\overline{a}}(t-\tau)$. If $\mu \leq \alpha^2j(\log j)^2/6$, then with probability at least $1-j^{-3j}$,
    \begin{equation}
        b_k^{E^+}(t) \le \alpha^2j(\log j)^2.
    \end{equation}
    Otherwise, with probability at least $1-j^{-3j}$,
    \begin{equation}
        b_k^{E^+}(t) \le \Big(1 + \frac{\alpha j^{1/2}\log j}{4\mu^{1/2}}\Big)\mu < 2\mu.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.912139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a3d6abefee0cf9df70be4163711cabec61f7946593e041bcd027e8faa002dbc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:ProbEstimate of arXiv:2608.27828, 'Scaling limit of the 3D abelian Yang--Mills Langevin dynamics'] Let $T>0$, $p \geq 2$, and $0<\kappa<1$ sufficiently small. Then, for any $\tilde\kappa\in (0,\kappa)$,
