{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.687601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a3ee5fd8b02ecdb028da78c35b4db60973105d7e6931643eb7727246170082f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 (Prefix trace of a tree-reduced path) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $E$ be a finite-dimensional real vector space equipped with an auxiliary Euclidean norm, and let $\eta:[0,T]\to E$ satisfy the equivalent conditions of \cref{prop:reducedness}. Then
