{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.102134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a598ccb739284fc22baf90e4a3916d634f7e68ddcabce08d2121730aa0b7718","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 6 of arXiv:2608.28200, '\textbf On the Formality of Configuration Spaces of $\aka$'] A {CDGA} is a graded $\mathbb{C}$-vector space $A = \bigoplus_{p\in\Z} A^p$ equipped with a linear map $d: A^p \to A^{p+1}$ such that $d^2 = 0$, and a multiplication satisfying:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item {Graded commutativity:} For any homogeneous elements $x, y \in A$, $xy = (-1)^{|x||y|}yx$.
    \item {Leibniz rule:} $d(xy) = (dx)y + (-1)^{|x|}x(dy)$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

