{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:21:28.734371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a8d73b59796313546c8488fae87318ca40f53495dd9e001786a5812a4f54eee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:E-m-evol of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] Let $\sigma(x) = \fc{e^x}{1+e^x}$. Let $h\in \mathbb R^n$, $E(t) = \sumo in \sigma(h_i+t)$ and $m(t) = \sumo in \sigma(h_i+t)(1-\sigma(h_i+t))$. Then 
