{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.066914+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a8dc1bd94f2b3cf7a9dbc3fd8f1fc34a926ac752296282a20b436e9b09f7d5e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Duality for the process $X^{(N)}$) of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] Assume that $\Lambda$ is not the zero measure. Then the process $X^{(N)}$ is dual to the process $Y^{(N)}$ with respect to the duality kernel $D^{(N)}:\{0,\ldots,N\}^2\to\rz$ defined via
   \begin{equation} 
      D^{(N)}(n,m)\ :=\ \frac{h_m^{(N)}(n)}{\mu_m^{(N)}}
      \ =\ \frac{(n)_m}{(N)_m\mu_m^{(N)}}
        \ =\ \frac{\binom{n}{m}}{\binom{N}{m}\mu_m^{(N)}},
      \qquad n,m\in\{0,\ldots,N\},
   \end{equation}
   where $Y^{(N)}$ is a death process with state space $\{0,\ldots,N\}$, whose generator $L^{Y^{(N)}}$ acts on functions $f:\{0,\ldots,N\}\to\rz$ via
   \begin{equation} 
      L^{Y^{(N)}}f(m)\ =\ \frac{1}{\mu_m^{(N)}}\sum_{k=1}^m \varphi(k,m)\mu_{m-k}^{(N)}\big(f(m-k)-f(m)\big),
      \qquad m\in\{0,\ldots,N\}.
   \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.334002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a96b2492a86bf046ee859c8340a59b0e00298a7440ac052b10c088f5c15e9f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] Let \(A \subset \{1,\ldots,n\}\) and choose arbitrary \(\epsilon > 0\).
Then, for some \(C_{t,\epsilon}, c_\epsilon > 0\), independent of \(n\) and \(A\), we have
\begin{equation*}
\sup_{\sigma \in \{-1,1\}^{A}}
\E\Big|\sum_{j=1}^nm_{ij}^{[A]}\Big|^{2+\epsilon}
\le C_{t,\epsilon}
\end{equation*}
