{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.528829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0aa452af55997a7aeda6c7abf758f5bfefddfb809ca5dc9a3e368d37e01312fa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:renormalisation_scales of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{def:recursive_tiles}
    Given $\overline{r}_0 \ge r_0 > 0$ and a sequence of positive reals $(m_i)_{i \geq 1}$, we define the \textbf{renormalisation scales} to be the sequence of positive reals $(r_i)_{i \geq 0}$ recursively defined by 

    \begin{equation}

        r_{i + 1} = m_{i + 1} r_i.
    \end{equation}

    We let $(V_i)_{i\geq 0}$ be a sequence of maximal $r_i$-separated nets, where a given net $V_i$ consists of the elements $\{\netvertex{i}{j}\}_{j \geq 0}$, and we let $((\vor{\netvertex{i}{j}})_{j \geq 0})_{i \geq 0}$ be the sequence of Voronoi tilings associated to the nets $(V_i)_{i \geq 0}$. 

    We define a \textbf{level $0$ tile} $\Tile{0}{j} = \tile{0}{\netvertex{0}{j}} = \vor{\netvertex{0}{j}}$ and its associated \textbf{cell} $\Cell{0}{j} = \cell{0}{\netvertex{0}{j}} = B(\netvertex{0}{j}, \overline{r}_0)$. 

    For $i \geq 1$, we define a \textbf{level-$i$ tile} as the union of level-$i-1$ tiles whose centre is contained in $\vor{\netvertex{i}{j}}$,

    \begin{equation}

        \Tile{i}{j}
        =
        \tile{i}{\netvertex{i}{j}}
        =
        \bigcup_{\netvertex{i-1}{k} \in \vor{\netvertex{i}{j}}}
        \tile{i-1}{\netvertex{i-1}{k}},
    \end{equation}

    and its associated \textbf{cell} is similarly defined

    \begin{equation}

        \Cell{i}{j}
        =
        \cell{i}{\netvertex{i}{j}}
        = 
        \bigcup_{\netvertex{i-1}{k} \in \vor{\netvertex{i}{j}}}
        \cell{i-1}{\netvertex{i-1}{k}}.
    \end{equation}

    We say that $\netvertex{i}{j}$ is the \textbf{centre} of $\Tile{i}{j}$ and we call the level $i-1$ tiles in $\Tile{i}{j}$ the \textbf{subtiles} of $T_{i,j}$. 

    Similarly, we say that $\netvertex{i}{j}$ is the \textbf{centre} of $\Cell{i}{j}$ and we call the level $i-1$ cells in $\Cell{i}{j}$ the \textbf{subcells} of $\Cell{i}{j}$.

    We write $\kappa_{i,j}$ for the number of level-$i-1$ net vertices in $\vor{\netvertex{i}{j}}$.

    We define the \textbf{renormalization scheme} associated to the renormalisation scales $(r_i)_{i \geq 0}$ to be the sequence of tilings $((\Tile{i}{j})_{j \geq 0})_{i \geq 0}$ associated to the sequence of nets $(V_i)_{i \geq 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

