{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.535118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ad5afbfe58aa114bd444dd9b3b4908d765deb03b6df517ea391302629eb3487","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2603.28093, 'Random Stability of Random Variables'] Assume $\mathbb E[X] < \infty$. We can define $L$ as a complex-valued function on the half-plane $\mathbb H = \{z \in \mathbb C\mid \mathrm{Re}(z) > 0\}$. This function is analytic on $\mathbb H$, and we have: 
