{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.310824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b1a5e1d8801ccda59930874f9d480dfd2121330c8f7b50ff984b100c620a554","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] Suppose $p \ge 2$ and $d(p-1) < 2p$. Conditioned on the event $\{\alpha([0,t]^p) \ge t^p\}$, $\widetilde{L}_t^{\otimes p}$ satisfies an LDP in the compact metric space $\widetilde{\mathcal{X}}_{\le 1}^{\otimes p}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ with good rate function
