{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.708363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b1bb1fab7fe08dac20bac0fc7c60357b83dedd6bd30b416ed04b43dd2fbe4ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj:1 of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $\operatorname{\bf NG}_{s}$ be a probability measure given by moment generating function
