{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.675325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b258ecd5ab429f74d17a020067a5d6706ee61eb2c50ef9826add4cd088bc963","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2607.11275, 'The limit law of the maximum of discrete partial-sums distribution II'] The distribution functions $F^{(1)}_{\infty},\,F^{(2)}_{\infty},\,\ldots,\,F^{(N)}_{\infty}$ satisfy
