{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.675182+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b35ee2027402f5a4dbc674037e910abd78dd2aea691dbe58ce22840a7af52de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma sto-martingale-limit of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] For every $\varphi_1,\varphi_2\in C^\infty(\mathbb{T}^d)$, let the quadratic variation be given by
		\begin{align*}
			{\,\rm d}\,\<M^N(\varphi_1),M^N(\varphi_2)\>&=\sum_k \big\< \sigma_k^N\cdot\nabla (-\Delta)^{a} \omega^N,\varphi_1\big\>\big\< \sigma_k^N\cdot\nabla (-\Delta)^{a} \omega^N,\varphi_2\big\>\,{\,\rm d} t\\
			&=:I^N_{\varphi_1,\varphi_2}\,{\,\rm d} t.
