{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.747740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b4e8616f5dc8ae81964bf308e0acc892fcf6cc31b67ea1ec3770d96cc6f50f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:conditions_a_b of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let $\{h_n \}_{n \geqslant 1}$ be a sequence of random elements in $\mathcal{H}(\mathbb{D})$ and denote the coefficients of $h_n$ by $(\xi_k^{(n)} )_{k \geqslant 0}$ so that for all $z \in \mathbb{D}$, $h_n(z) = \sum_{k \geqslant 0} \xi_k^{(n)} z^k$. Suppose also that the following conditions hold.
