{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.745438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b7e7980b86411246594a325bdad77f8d1c00a972e1acfdb5ae3068b31d6a403","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:commutatorTruncationEstimates of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Let $0<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}$, let $n\ge1$, and let $v:{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}\to{\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d}$ be globally Lipschitz.  For a differentiable kernel $\phi$, let
