{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.628132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b8cec3d826036bd4a2394a9f3022443cce83f0b9d3816351715e061ba34aeb9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ev_tail_estimate of arXiv:2511.22162, 'Landau Hamiltonian with Gaussian white noise potential and the asymptotics of its bottom o'] Fix $\eta \in (0,1)$ and $z \in \R^2$. There exist constants $x_0>0$, $r > 2$ such that for all couple $(L, x) \in \R_+^2$ verifying $x \ge x_0$ and $\frac{5r}{\sqrt{x}} \leq L \leq x^x$ the following inequalities hold
