{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.679594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bada20de72e3d649d0f40ac261fb14436e461684ec80969c4ff9b8d75c99a69","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] Fix $\rho_0 \in \Pp(\R^2)$, $c_0 \in L^\infty(\R^2)\cap L^1(\R^2)$, as well as $\chi>0$, $\lambda>0$, 
$\theta>0$, $N\geq 2$, $M>0$ and $\e\in (0,1]$. Consider the $(\rho_0,c_0,N,M,\e)$-2SKS system
with all the associated random objects. For all $\varphi \in C^{2}(\R_+\times\R^d)$, all $t\geq 0$,
\begin{align*}
\langle \nu^{1,N,M,\e}_t,\varphi(t,\cdot)\rangle=& \langle \nu^{1,N,M,\e}_0,\varphi(0,\cdot)\rangle
+\frac 1 \theta \int_0^t \langle \mu^{1,N,M,\e}_s,\varphi(s,\cdot)\rangle\dd s\\
&+ \int_0^t \Big\langle  \nu^{1,N,M,\e}_s, \partial_t\varphi(s,\cdot)+\frac1\theta(\Delta \varphi(s,\cdot)
-\lambda \varphi(s,\cdot))\Big\rangle \dd s\\
&+\frac1{(N-1)M}\sum_{a \in \Uu_{N,M},a_1\neq 1}\sqrt{\frac 2 \theta}\int_0^t \1_{\{s\in [\tau_a^{N,M},\zeta_a^{N,M})\}} 
\nabla\varphi(s,Y^{a,N,M,\e}_s) \dd W^a_s\\
&+\frac1{(N-1)M}\sum_{i\in I_N,i\neq 1}\int_0^t\varphi(s,X^{i,N,M,\e}_s) \dd \tilde \pi_s^{i,M}\\
&-\frac1{(N-1)M}\sum_{a \in \Uu_{N,M},a_1\neq 1}\int_0^t \1_{\{s\in (\tau_a^{N,M},\zeta_a^{N,M}]\}}
\varphi(s,Y^{a,N,M,\e}_\sm) \dd \tilde \Lambda^a_s,
\end{align*}
where $\tilde \pi_t^{i,M}=\pi^{i,M}_t-\frac M\theta t$ and $\tilde \Lambda^a_t= \Lambda^a_t- \frac\lambda \theta t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.765493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0baf7436a9b11e9d666c951a98ff233d878ec644f18615c8876ba5f1e5cb5e4b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Exponential decay of hitting times) of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] For any $i,k \ge 1$ and for all $p > 1$, sufficiently close to $1$, we have
