{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.475910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bb4d5088798156214f6556949235dda650ade80e37dae37e06c3696117bdca8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma box-product-bifun-general of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] For any compact Lie groups $G,H$, the box product defines a homotopical left Quillen bifunctor $\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}\times\cat{$\bm H$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}\to\cat{$\bm{(G\times H)}$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}$.
    \begin{proof}
        The pushout-product axiom for cofibrations is verified in [barrero2021]*{Lemma A.6}, while the preservation of weak equivalences is Corollary 3.10 of \emph{op.\ cit.}

        For the pushout product axiom for acyclic cofibrations, we will more generally show that the pushout product of any h-cofibration $i$ (of orthogonal $H$-spaces) with any $G$-global weak equivalence $f$ is a $(G\times H)$-global weak equivalence. As both h-cofibrations and weak equivalences are stable under restriction (see Lemma~(lemma:restr-right-Quillen of the paper)), this follows at once by applying [barrero2021]*{Corollary~A.10} to ${\textup{triv}}_Gi$ and ${\textup{triv}}_Hf$.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.330985+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bb6a1d8ba080ce3220cb9c1dd32ce7f479ba282dee0cb03dc8d6c90df8f0e6c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_chaoticrv of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] ([bourguintaqqu2019])
    An eigenfunction $F$ corresponding to an eigenvalue $-q$ of $L$ is called {\textit{chaotic}} if there is $\eta>1$ such that $-q\eta\in \Lambda$ and 
