		where $C$ is a constant depending only on the density $p_k$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.711756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c1d7bd553deb0e02094b0e2e30dfa5fbf33dd1eecf088a38e169c20e050c337","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Uniform endpoint flows) of arXiv:2609.01143, 'The voter model on the hyperbolic graph'] Fix $\gamma,\zeta>0$.  With high probability, simultaneously for every pair $x,y$ with
\[
h(x),h(y)\geq\gamma R, \qquad \operatorname{dist}_{\mathbb S^1}(\vartheta(x),\vartheta(y))\geq\zeta,
