{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.499793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c1fb889927cc13aff99f92396e0509adc1af2ec7f8ce8827dfc89c12e2b5f88","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $\beta \in (\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{2}]$ and $\alpha \in (0,\beta)$ be arbitrary. Then for each rough path $\mathbf{X} = (X,\bbx) \in \scrc^{\beta}([0,T],V)$ we also have $\mathbf{X} \in \scrc^{\alpha}([0,T],V)$ and the estimate
