{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.496334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c2b3f66152ba48b335a7ddbf1d216c32db3f7b0ebeb6239b495094be04b2388","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Lead-excursion estimate) of arXiv:2605.09641, 'The Ballot Event for Two-Player Coupon Collection: A Renewal--Catalan Asymptotic'] Fix $g_0\ge0$.  Uniformly for integer sequences $s_0=s_0(d)$ satisfying $0\le s_0<d-g_0$ and $s_0=o(d)$, one has
\begin{equation}
        U_d(s_0,g_0)=H(s_0,g_0)
        \left(1+O_{g_0}\left(\frac{s_0}{d}+\frac{\log d}{\sqrt d}\right)\right).
\end{equation}
In particular, if $s_0=O(d^{1/2}\log d)$ and $g_0=1$, then
\[
        U_d(s_0,1)=\frac{2}{d-s_0+1}(1+o(1))=\frac{2}{d}(1+o(1)),
\]
