{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.167806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c2d00f942cde1d45a504165806f22b95c6ce00b35502d46a4b266a10f69e705","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 (Transition semigroup) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let $X(\cdot; t, x)$ denote the $H$-valued Markov process corresponding to the unique mild solution of the semilinear stochastic differential equation \eqref{eq:cauchy_problem}. The two-parameter transition semigroup $\{P_{t,s}\}_{0 \le t \le s \le T}$ acting on the measurable weighted space $\mathcal{B}_m(H)$ is defined pointwise by
