{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.612474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c471612c153ec9fe3faf635c1445d00f76aca3860ef847a03c3883325115bde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:onepointDelta of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For any $\varepsilon>0$, there exists a large constant $C>0$, such that for any $t\in{\mathbb R}$, the following holds with probability at least $1-\varepsilon$: 
