{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.651423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c4c01a09dc9de1a4da9cb1b664dff8dada722c3a742bf88ae3cd3b14fc92069","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 4 (Prior) of arXiv:2605.07050, 'Universality of the fluctuations of the free energy in generalized Sherrington--Kirkpatric'] For a random variable $\bsx = (x_1, \dots, x_N) \in \R^N$ whose distribution is given by a prior $\caX$, we assume that for $i=1, 2, \dots, N$, 
