{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.877459+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c4fe30cb4df2df2e2ee85d84647caea6fc26cef9c3b61ba51c8db05bbb53182","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop multgain1 of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $\gamma$ be a closed curve on $S$ with $m$ pairwise-disjoint segments, each having the coarse itinerary (equation eq:strict-pattern of the paper). Let $A, A_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_n(\mathbb{C})$ be the determinant-one lifts of $\rho(\gamma), \rho_0(\gamma)$ respectively. Then we have 
