{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.685823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c532f952edfa3b60610771c902fb7b8ee11a5fdab8db1ac9af750a49b4ab6af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:caracterizacionTypeIsphericalspaceforms of arXiv:2609.01920, 'Isospectral and not strongly isospectral spherical space forms with non-cyclic fundamental'] Let $\Gamma=\Gamma_d(m,n,r)$ be a Type I group, $p$ a positive integer, and
		\begin{equation*}
			\rho= \bigoplus_{j=1}^{p} \left(\pi_{k_j,\ell_j}\oplus \overline{\pi}_{k_j,\ell_j} \right)
\qquad\text{and}\qquad
			\rho'= \bigoplus_{j=1}^{p} \left(\pi_{k'_j,\ell'_j}\oplus \overline{\pi}_{k'_j,\ell'_j} \right)
		\end{equation*}
two fixed point free real representations of $\Gamma$. Then the spherical space forms $S^{2dp-1}/\rho(\Gamma)$ and $S^{2dp-1}/\rho'(\Gamma)$ are isometric if and only if there exist integers $a$ and $b$ with 
\begin{align}
\gcd(a,m)&=1, &
\gcd(b,n)&=1, &
b&\equiv 1\pmod d,
\end{align}
a permutation $\sigma$ of $\{1,\ldots,p\}$,  $\epsilon_1,\dots,\epsilon_p\in\{-1,1\}$, and $c_1,\dots,c_p\in\{0,\ldots,d-1\}$ such that 
		\begin{align*}
			k_{\sigma(j)}' &\equiv \epsilon_j ak_{j}r^{c_j} \pmod m,&
			\ell_{\sigma(j)}' &\equiv \epsilon_j b\ell_{j} \pmod {n/d},
			\qquad 
			\text{for all $1\leq j\leq p$}.
		\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.732546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c5610c5da35bcc4ca65d236f37b769eb10adb5dcb67654230062ae4f2c2596f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:buser-isoperimetric-bound of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] If the Ricci curvature of $\mathcal M$ is bounded below by $-(N-1)\delta^2$ for some $\delta>0$, then 
