{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.230088+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c5619288e6cc33cde232a74dc96a19c4dbf4cc4d894bd83c9ff490fdc852881","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] There exist $c,C>0$ such that for all $\delta>0$ and $n\in \N$ with $n\geq \delta^{-2}$, 
