{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.101218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c57d2784ee483a91e8b4572ecc515386478f60d82fe6fa8b2740df61cff699b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2608.30059, 'Multihomogeneous Measures and Stochastic Polar Representations'] Let \(Z\) and \(W\) be \(E\)-valued random elements. If  
