{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.601009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c5b4c8fccec84bc8bd19b7d0a0c56f7a098dfa98ff3eadf5a5511d66c09dcd7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Prop2.4 of arXiv:2602.23124, '\textsc{ Necessary and Sufficient Conditions for the Lacunary/Hereditary Laws of Large Num'] On a   probability space $\,(\Omega, \mathcal F, {\mathbb P})$  consider   real-valued, measurable functions $\,f_1, f_2, \cdots$. \\ 
{\bf (i)} Suppose that  the sequence $\,f_1, f_2, \cdots$ is bounded in $\,\mathbb{L}^0$ with ``determining" subsequence  $f_{k_1}, f_{k_2}, \cdots\,,$ whose limiting random distribution $\,\omega \mapsto   {\bm \mu}_\omega\,,$     as in and below  (equation B0 of the paper), satisfies 
  \begin{equation} 

 \mathbb E^{\mathbb P} \int_{\mathbb R} \big| x \big|  \,  {\bm \mu}  (\mathrm{d} x, \cdot)  \,<\,\infty\,.
  \end{equation}

Then  the \textsc{Ces\`aro}  convergence (equation 2 of the paper) holds $\,{\mathbb P}-$a.e.\,\,for the $\,{\mathbb P}-$integrable function   $\, f_* = \int_{\mathbb R}   x   \,     {\bm \mu}  ( \mathrm{d} x, \cdot): \Omega \to \mathbb R\,;$      and there exist a $($further, relabelled$\,)$ subsequence $f_{k_1}, f_{k_2}, \cdots\,,$ as well  as a sequence of sets $\, A_1 \subseteq A_2 \subseteq \cdots \subseteq A_n \subseteq \cdots \,$ in $\,\mathcal F\,$ with $\,\lim_{n \to \infty} {\mathbb P} (A_n ) =1\,,$ such that the sequence
\begin{equation} 

\Big( f_{k_n}  \, \mathbf{1}_{A_{n}} \Big)_{n \in \mathbb N}~~~\text{is bounded in} ~ \,\mathbb{L}^1 ({\mathbb P}) \,.
\end{equation} 
 {\bf (ii)} Conversely, suppose there exist a subsequence $f_{k_1}, f_{k_2}, \cdots\,,$ and a sequence of sets $\, A_1 \subseteq A_2 \subseteq \cdots \subseteq A_n \subseteq \cdots \,$ in $\,\mathcal F\,,$ satisfying $\,\lim_{n \to \infty} {\mathbb P} (A_n ) =1\,$ as well as the property (equation A16 of the paper). 

Then the \textsc{Ces\`aro}-mean     convergence (equation 2 of the paper) holds $\,{\mathbb P}\,-$a.e.\,along a $($relabelled,\,``determining"$\,)$ subsequence,   with a  limiting function $\,f_*$ which is $\,{\mathbb P}\,-$integrable$\,:  \, \mathbb E^{\mathbb P} \big( \big| f_* \big| \big) < \infty\,.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

