{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.059802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c7ec5455501ac72b4e2600fe729f1cf7d126bce50982fa76d8c5b565cc72604","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem precise_bounds of arXiv:2506.10623, 'Polynomial slowdown in an angle-dependent 2d branching Brownian motion'] Let $\alpha \in (0,2)$, $\varrho \geq 1$ and $\xi\in\mathbb{R}$.
	Let $T \in (0,1)$, $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2 \in (0,T/10)$ such that $\varepsilon_2 \leq (1-T)/10$.
