{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.511906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cb4ba46e56386bc1fafada18f3b94fc2e1063a6d77007d3693852cad6dc0613","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma gfsum of arXiv:2601.09537, 'Gene genealogies in haploid populations evolving according to sweepstakes reproduction'] Let $F$ and $G$ be positive and bounded real-valued functions defined on $\{\ell, \ell + 1 \ldots \}$ for  $\ell \in \{0, 1, \ldots, \}$, and write $s(k) := \sum_{i\ge k}F(i)$.   Then, for any $M \in \{0, 1,\ldots \}$, 
