{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.611342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cb574e2606ba83766297b5a35b9361d28411f437854da141fb6e570c5bcd929","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] For every plan $\gamma \in \ov\Gamma(\mu,\nu)$ there exists a Zolotarev projection $\ov\rho \in \Pi_{\succeq_c \mu}(\nu)$ and a martingale plan $\breve\gamma  \in \Gamma_{\mathrm{M}}(\mu,\ov\rho)$ such that,
	\begin{equation*}
		\int_X W_2^2(\gamma_x,\breve\gamma_{x}) \,\mu(dx)  =  \big(1- \alpha_{\succeq_c}(\nu\,|\,\mu) \big) Z_2(\mu,\nu),
	\end{equation*}
	where $\gamma_x,\breve\gamma_{x}$ are the relevant transport kernels with respect to the marginal $\mu$. Moreover, the Zolotarev projection and the martingale plan can be computed as follows: $\breve\gamma = (\pi_1,\ov\zeta) \# \gamma$ and $\ov{\rho} = \ov\zeta \# \gamma$, where $\ov\zeta$ is expressed by \eqref{eq:ovzeta} for any optimal potential $\ov{u}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.291916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cb6fc5c631a131a18d6ded30e5fabef339c3d16955cae84eded4dfba161be26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:2G_randomD of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $X$ satisfy Assumption~(ass:chi of the paper)(i).  Fix a (large) $L>0$ and (small) $c_0,\epsilon,\nu,\xi>0$. Let $\theta>0$ be a (possibly, $N$-dependent) small parameter.  Consider $k_j\in[N]$ and denote $x_j:=k_j/N$, $j=1,2$. There exists a universal constant $d>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\left\vert\left\langle \left(G_1B_1\widetilde{G}_2 - M_{1\widetilde{2}}^{B_1}\right)B_2\right\rangle\right\vert \le C_\theta \frac{N^\xi}{N\eta_1\eta_2},

\end{equation}
uniformly in $\eta_j:=|\Im w_j|\in (N^{-1+\epsilon}, N^L)$, $|\Re w_j|\le \theta^d N^{-\nu}\eta_j$, $z_j\in \mathbf{C}$ such that $\theta\le|z_j-\sqrt{x_j}|\le L$, $x_j\in [c_0,1]$ and in deterministic matrices $B_j\in \{E_\pm^{(k_j)},\big(F^{(k_j)}\big)^{(*)}\}$, $j=1,2$. The constant $C_\theta>0$ in (equation eq:2G_av of the paper) satisfies $C_\theta\le \theta^{-D}$ for some fixed $D>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.258722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cb7ce57b78b1828038cf3890ff3e2d05afe83c23a25cb63021fa8c4a16dd8a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 129 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any $x \in [0, a]$, we have  
