{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.315915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cbb7ad2a1fff782e8fa7acf34628195dcae5b40fc317ae0e1d6d06cc5ec2764","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma AuxiliaryEstimate of arXiv:2411.06089, '{\Large \bf Averaging principle for semilinear slow-fast rough partial differential equati'] For any $T>0$ and $(x,y)\in \mathcal H_\eta \times \mathcal{H}$ with $\eta \in [0,\gamma)$ and $\gamma\in (1/3,\gamma_0)$, there exists a constant $C_{M,T}>0$ such that
