    Moreover, if $(\lambda',u')$ is another pair of such solution, then $\lambda=\lambda'$ and there exists $c>0$ such that $u=cu'$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.907179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ccae21b29c084fe8511a03b792a52f333a27357a402f3107020a596357b2080","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:majorization of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$, let $\mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon}: \R^{d_1 \times d_2}  \to \R$ be the $\varepsilon$-smoothed nuclear norm (eq:smoothedell1:objective of the paper) and $Q_{\varepsilon}(\cdot \mid \mathbf{X}): \R^{d_1 \times d_2} \to \R$ be the quadratic model function of (eq:smoothedell1:IRLSmajorizer of the paper) defined by the harmonic-mean weight operator (eq:W:operator:action of the paper) with core matrix (eq:harmonic:mean of the paper). Then, $Q_{\varepsilon}(\cdot \mid \mathbf{X})$ majorizes $\mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon}$ globally, i.e.,
	\begin{equation} 
	Q_{\varepsilon}(\mathbf{Z} \mid\mathbf{X}) \geq \mathcal{J}_{\varepsilon}(\mathbf{Z})
	\end{equation}
	for each $\mathbf{Z},\mathbf{X} \in \R^{d_1 \times d_2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.026087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cd40d4e52ffe14420a6b6ed5d8c42ea4871dead7d6b24a397b433c54fefb084","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2606.06757, 'Path-Dependent Ergodic Optimal Control \\ and Backward Stochastic Differential Equations'] There exists a sequence $T_n \rightarrow \infty$ and a  function $\overline{v} :\R\times \mathcal{C}_{\theta} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, such that:
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{array}{cc}
         \displaystyle  v^{T_n}(t, \xi) - v^{T_n}(0, \textnormal{\textbf{0}}) \xrightarrow[T_n \rightarrow \infty]{} \overline{v}(t, \xi) \,, & \text{for all } \, t\in\R \, \text{ and } \,  \xi \in \mathcal{C}_{\theta} \, .
    \end{array}
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that, for all $t, t'\in\R$ and $\xi, \xi' \in \mathcal{C}_{\theta}$,
    \begin{equation}
            \begin{array}{l}
                 \displaystyle \big|\overline{v}(t, \xi) - \overline{v}(t, \xi') \big| \leq C | \xi - \xi' |_{\theta} \, , \\[5pt]
                 \displaystyle \big|\overline v(t',\xi)-\overline v(t,\xi)\big|\le C \big(\,(1+|\xi|_{\theta})\,|t'-t|^{1/2}+|t-t'|+\omega_{\theta,\xi}(|t'-t|) \big) \, .
            \end{array}
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.847953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cd6b0c94b3c1e0752f970e7f124d0f586a5271ee6fcc5173dda3a8510ca0070","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: spatial rescaling of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] If $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in \mathcal{S}_{\bar \boldsymbol{y}}[a, b]$, then for all $t \in [a, b]$ and $\varphi \in C_c^1(\mathbbm{R}_+ \times U_g)$, we have:
	\begin{equation}

		L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_t}\left(\varphi_t\right) = L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_a}\left(\varphi_a\right) + \lambda_0 \int_a^t \varphi_s(0, 0)ds + \int_a^t L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_s}\left(\partial_t\varphi_s + \bar \boldsymbol{r}_s \partial_x \varphi_s + \partial_y\varphi_s\right)ds,
	\end{equation}
	where $\bar \boldsymbol{r}_s(y) = \mathbbm{1}_{\left\{y \leq \bar \boldsymbol{y}_s\right\}}$ for all $s \in [a, b]$ and $y \in \mathbbm{R}_+$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.230769+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cd7461307ae193a08a918cc8449993ff531a311bbdd83bec326e014edf1a54f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 45 ($\Psi|_S$) of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] Given $S, M \subset M_0$ such that $S \subset M$. Given $\Phi \in FLOW(S)$ and $\Psi \in FLOW(M)$, where
\begin{align*}
\Phi&=\{\phi_{i} \in TRAJ(S) \ |\ i\in I_S\} \quad (I_S \subset \mathbf{Z}),\\
\Psi&=\{\psi_{j} \in TRAJ(M) \ |\ j \in I_M\} \quad (I_M \subset \mathbf{Z}). 
\end{align*}
$\Phi$ is called the \textit{restriction of $\Psi$ on $S$} if
\begin{equation*}
\text{for }\forall \phi_{i} \in \Phi,\  \exists \psi_{j} \in \Psi \text{ such that }  \phi_{i} \subset \psi_{j}. 
\end{equation*}
Recall that we write $\phi_{i} \subset \psi_{j}$ if $abc \in \psi_{j}$ for $\forall abc \in \phi_{i}$ (Definition \ref{def_traj}).
The restriction of $\Psi$ on $S$ is uniquely determined and denoted by ${\Psi}|_{S}$, i.e.,
\begin{equation*}
 \Phi={\Psi}|_{S} \quad  \text{if $\Phi$ is the restriction of $\Psi$ on $S$}.
 \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.707427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cd89e4de260586012908898ae0e02036c16e4eeaeae53fa86b2ac4d834453a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:asymptotic_threshold of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Consider a family of local memory systems, indexed by $N$, with request processes satisfying Assumptions (ass:renewal of the paper) and (ass:weak_convergence of the paper). Choose the memory size of the $N$-th system as $C_N=cN$ with $0< c \leqslant 1$. If there exists a unique solution to $\theta^*$ satisfying:
\begin{equation*}
  G_\infty(\theta^*) = 1-c
\end{equation*}
then the sequence of thresholds $\theta_N:=\theta_{C_N}$ defined by (equation eq:threshold_n of the paper) satisfies $\theta_{N}\to\theta^*$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.708862+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cd9ca857a82b0599170f3504222fe82b9e53db0ee464856828075d07b00d75c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem magextrapolation of arXiv:2412.00593, 'A new approach to strong convergence II.\\The classical ensembles'] For any $h\in \mathcal{P}_q$ and $K>0$, we have
$$
	|h(x)|   \leq 
	\left(\frac{2|x|}{K}\right)^q  \sobnorm{h}{0}{[-K, K]}
	\quad \text{for all } x\in \mathbb{R} \backslash [-K, K].
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.348026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cda1caf9696d123ed0a9849b28ba8da83d1b94e792f5d96506f89c7e6abc88a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:complete-spectrum of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For every $k \ge 1$ and $f\in {\rm Ker}\,\mathfrak{a}_{\alpha,k-1}^\dagger$, we have
\begin{equation}
\ensuremath{\mathcal E}_{K,\alpha,k}(f) = k \left(|\alpha|+k-1\right) \left\lVertf\right\rVert_{\alpha,k}^2 \; \text{.}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.102508+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cdd8bc36490815e5568102db7062ad23f2fa4bb73240b2ec5720d510db0c79f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Uniform threshold transfer) of arXiv:2608.20101, '\bfseries Largest bulk gap of the complex Ginibre ensemble'] Let \(t_n\ge0\), \(\kappa>0\), and suppose that
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{a\in B}
 \left|K_n(a,a)q_n(a,t_n)-\kappa\right|\longrightarrow0.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\{N_n(t_n;B)=0\}\longrightarrow e^{-\kappa|B|},
\end{equation}
and, for every fixed \(k\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\{N_n(t_n;B)\le k-1\}
 \longrightarrow e^{-\kappa|B|}
 \sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\frac{(\kappa|B|)^j}{j!}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.598091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cde026c6a064bac31fb4027ff4e9ff5a45cada07705677ffdecc681c72f071b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $\Lambda$ be a compact subset of $\Delta_I$ and let $k_t:\Lambda\to\N^d$ satisfy the preceding approximation condition. Then

\begin{equation*}
\sup_{\lambda\in\Lambda}
\left|\frac{\mathfrak N(k_t(\lambda))}{t}-\kappa(\lambda)\right|
\xrightarrow[t\to\infty]{\mathrm{a.s.}}0.
\end{equation*}

If $\Ee_{\mathfrak a}[L_1]<\infty$, then

\begin{equation*}
\sup_{\lambda\in\Lambda}
\left|\frac{N(k_t(\lambda))}{t}-\rho(\lambda)\right|
\xrightarrow[t\to\infty]{\mathrm{a.s.}}0.
\end{equation*}

The same convergences hold in probability under every initial law for which the first entrance time into the split atom and the corresponding entrance displacement are finite almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.960239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ce00c7b31828176026492d81a7f2af41a8f23e4318251b1c6eafa523c6242a6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 ({\cite[Theorem 8.1.6) of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] {RV}}] 
$\xi$ is an non-negative random variable, $l(\cdot)$ is a slowly varying function at $\infty$. Define $F(x)=\P(\xi\le x)$. $\hat F$ is the Laplace transform of $\xi$, i.e., $\hat F(s)=\E[\mathrm{e}^{-s \xi}]$.   If $\mu_n:=\E[\xi^n]<\infty,\, \alpha=n+\beta,\, \beta\in[0,1]$, then the following are equivalent:
\begin{align*}
f_n(s):= (-1)^{n+1}\left\{\hat F(s)-\sum_{i=0}^n \mu_i\frac{(-s)^i}{i!} \right\}\sim s^\alpha l(1/s),\,  s\downarrow 0\\
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle\int_{x}^\infty t^n dF(t)\sim n!l(x)\quad   &\beta=0 \\
1-F(x)\sim \dfrac{(-1)^n}{\Gamma (1-\alpha)}x^{-\alpha}l(x)   &\beta\in(0,1),\quad  x\to \infty,\\ 
\displaystyle\int_{0}^x t^{n+1} dF(t)\sim (n+1)!l(x)\quad   &\beta=1
\end{cases}
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.500073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ce571545d836c182bebae7ebf0cceb5ff43f1b36a307c52bcfa09f2f651798f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] We say that a rough path $\mathbf{X} = (X,\bbx) \in \scrc^{\alpha}([0,T],V)$ is \emph{weakly geometric} if the first order calculus condition
\begin{align}
{\rm Sym}(\bbx_{s,t}) = \frac{1}{2} X_{s,t} \otimes X_{s,t} \quad \text{for all $s,t \in [0,T]$}
\end{align}
is fulfilled.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.322621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ce7ec63fd5ca6bf78a08e728ef2b43972313d9eeba6eb9a7fcd01e68c05a1e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 43 (Explicit upper bounds) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $\sigma, \alpha > 0$ and $d_0 \coloneqq 1 - \log 2$. Then
\begin{align}
    \sigma \vee \alpha \ <\ c^{\SG}(\sigma, \alpha) \ \le\ (\sigma + 2\alpha) \wedge \sigma\,\mathcal{U}(a),

\end{align}
{where $a = \alpha/\sigma$ as in \eqref{eqn:normalize} and}
\begin{align}
    \mathcal{U}(a) \coloneqq \sup_{\ell \ge \log 2} \frac{a\ell + \sqrt{2\ell}}{\ell + d_0},

\end{align}
{a one-variable supremum that Lemma~\ref{lem:sgMeval} evaluates in closed form. Its variable is $\ell = \log(1/p)$, and the constraint $\ell \ge \log 2$ is the range of $\ell$ as the atom weight $p$ runs over $(0,1/2]$.} Consequently
\begin{align}
    \frac{c^{\SG}(\sigma,\alpha)}{\sigma \vee \alpha} \longrightarrow 1
