{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.632747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d05333af191e50c89c08ce0949bba985adbde7719a75174a17d05f280996e6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem local_limit_boundary of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] Fix $\theta \in [0,\frac{1}{2})$, $\displaystyle \frac{g_n}{n} \underset{n \to +\infty}{\longrightarrow}\theta$ and $\mathbf{p}^{n} = (p^n_{1},\cdots,p^n_{\ell_n})$ such that $|\mathbf{p}^{n}| = o(n)$ and $\displaystyle \frac{|\mathbf{p}^{n}|}{\ell_n}  \underset{n \to +\infty}{\longrightarrow}+\infty$. Denote by $e^n$ a uniformly chosen oriented edge on the union $\partial_1\cup \cdots \cup \partial_{\ell_n}$ of the boundaries of $T_{n,g_n,\mathbf{p}^{n}}$. Then, the following convergence holds for the local topology
