{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.545469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d0604ee194831b4f67e2dd81a95dd517d6e3ac09902ed827d59fceeb0f045f4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: Branch overlap of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Let $A\subsetneq \mathbb{Z}_q$ with $|A|\geq 2$. Consider the $A$-localized state $\mu_A$, see Proposition (prop: Bounds A-loc. states of the paper), for the class of models with Hamiltonian of the form (equation def: Hamiltonian of the paper) and a potential defined in (equation eq: Potential ferr n.n. model of the paper) fulfilling the $u,U,d$-bounds in (equation eq: u,U-bounds of the paper). Then, the thinned branch-overlap $\underline{\phi}^\omega$ is $\pi(\cdot|\omega)$-a.s. lower bounded by 
