{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.220649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d12f16bd83e63e04d962f513ba90f8e55719ad348e62e3dd71c552acfbd618d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma2 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] For every $q\in (0,1)$, $t\ge 0$ and $x\in \mathbb{C}\backslash\{0\}$,
\begin{align}
F(x,t;q)=\frac{(q;q)_\infty}{2\pi i}\oint_{\mathcal{C}}\frac{e^{-\log x\log z/\log q}}{(z;q)_\infty}e^{t(1-z)}dz
\end{align}
where ${\mathcal{C}}$ is a clockwise Hankel contour around the positive real axis from $\infty-i0$ to $\infty+i0$
that can be deformed to run along the straight line $(\rho-i\infty,\rho+i\infty)$ for $0<\rho<1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.317346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d1692976f6ade086e943832b99bbb2cb7f9f923f325ff2f1d1656492c61d780","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2608.30232, 'Strong Unique Continuation for Fractional Schr\"odinger Operators'] Let $h\in L_s^1(\R^n)$ satisfy $(-\Delta)^s h=0$ distributionally in $B_{2R}$. Then there exist $\rho_0\in(0,R)$ and $H>0$ such that, for every $m\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
    h=T_{m-1}h+h_m\qquad\text{in }B_{\rho_0},
\end{equation}
where $T_{m-1}h$ is the Taylor polynomial of $h$ at the origin of degree at
most $m-1$, and
with
\begin{equation}
    |h_m(x)|\le H\rho_0^{-m}|x|^m,
    \qquad |x|<\rho_0.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.650140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d1cc2c08c536659ecfe06e59a258a740158a23035484441dd591c299ac622a8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:PWd of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] For $f\in PW_{\Omega}$ the Fourier inversion formula extends $f$ to an
entire function
$$
  F(z):=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{d}}\int_{B_{\Omega}}
