Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
J_g'(\Omega)(V)
=
-\frac{p-1}{p}
\int_{\partial\Omega}
\left|
\frac{\partial u_\Omega}{\partial\nu_g}
\right|^p
g(V,\nu_g)\,dS_g.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.122764+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d2b541b576b79430ee3a2013d4a4100d8915392e52d50805f465783efe88f5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] For every sufficiently small \(\eps>0\), the blow-up
