{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.107786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d45ac4fc5c1108e2b812d6997460845474a65ef07e201c793ff32caed902728","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma intermediate-system of arXiv:2606.21556, 'Mean field limit of non-exchangeable interacting diffusions on co-evolutionary networks'] Consider the following nonlinear system of SDEs for the unknown processes \((\bar{X}_i^N)_{1\leq i\leq N}\):
	\begin{align}
		d\bar X_i^N(t) &= \frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^N\int_{\mathcal{C}^d_t}\int_{-W}^{W}\Phi_t(\bar X_{i,[0,t]}^N,\gamma,w) K(\bar X_i^N(t),\gamma(t)) \, dq_{ij,0}^N(w) \, d\bar \mu^{N,j}_{[0,t]}(\gamma) \, dt + \sqrt{2\nu}\,dW_i^N(t),\quad t\in [0,T], \nonumber\\
		\bar X_i^N(0) &= X_{i,0}^N, \quad \bar \mu^{N,i}_{[0,t]} := \mathrm{Law}(\bar X_{i,[0,t]}^N) \in \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{C}^d_t),
	\end{align}
	where \(q_{ij,0}^N := \mathrm{Law}(Nw_{ij,0}^N) \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R})\). Under Assumptions (assump:interaction-kernel of the paper), (assump:plasticity-function of the paper), and (assump:weights of the paper), consider initial states \((X_{i,0}^N)_{1\leq i\leq N} \subset L^p(\Omega,\mathbb{R}^d)\) for some \(p\in[1,\infty)\). Provided that these initial states are independent of the driving standard Wiener processes \((W_i^N)_{1\leq i\leq N}\), there exists a unique strong solution \((\bar{X}_i^N)_{1\leq i\leq N} \subset L^p(\Omega,\mathcal{C}_T^d)\) to the system (equation eq:multi-agent-discrete-independent-projection-solved-weights of the paper). Furthermore, if the initial states \((X_{i,0}^N)_{1\leq i\leq N}\) are independent, then the resulting solution processes \((\bar{X}_i^N)_{1\leq i\leq N}\) are also independent.","status":"unverified"}

