{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.695997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d4920a59f73860c857bde39f4defab88313bf6a152a5d358416c76350efc661","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] Let $G_i$ be a sequence of Lie groups and  $\phi _i : G_i \to G$ a sequence of good approximations. If $G$ is a Lie group, then its Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}$ admits an ideal $\mathfrak{h} \trianglelefteq \mathfrak{g}$ with $\mathfrak{g}/ \mathfrak{h}$ nilpotent and such that 
