{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.943722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d765356163a6f894043b65b7035bc1096f3ed4ab9790ddfc97084c091b55634","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2608.01860, 'A Variational Characterization of a Gibbs Measure related to the Aviles-Giga Functional'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $X$ and $F:L^\infty(X)\to \R$,  $f\mapsto \log\left(\int_X\exp(f(x))\ \mu(dx)\right)$. Then
    \begin{align*}
        F(f)=F^{**}(f)=\sup_{\gamma\in P_\mu(X)}\left\{\int_X f(x)\ \gamma(dx) -\int_X\log\left(\frac{d\mu}{d\gamma}(x)\right)\ \gamma(dx)\right\},
    \end{align*}
    where $F^{**}$ denotes the Fenchel biconjugate of $F$. 
    In particular, it holds
    \begin{align*}
         -\log\left(\int_X\exp(-f(x))\ \mu(dx)\right) = \inf_{\gamma\in P_\mu(X)} \left\{\int_Xf(x)\ \gamma(dx)+\int_X\log\left(\frac{d\gamma}{d\mu}(x)\right)\ \gamma(dx)\right\}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.638450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d7664a7e541536c02b244d3e26bc482691b4a9085b67ddfc7a56948c0a297ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2605.23461, 'An almost sure invariance principle for the Takagi--van der Waerden class functions'] Suppose that \eqref{Assump2:A_n_to_infinite} and \eqref{Assump2:last_term} hold. We also assume that
