{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.092784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d808c3608fa505e94fe31f91e083147bf1aa344d38466adb8219e8fbfc149e2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Carnot-isotropic-covariance of arXiv:2609.02710, 'Asymptotic Mean Value Laplacian\\ on equiregular sub-Riemannian manifolds'] The covariance operator $\mathbf M:V_1\to V_1$ defined by
\begin{equation}
  \langle\mathbf M u,v\rangle
  :=\int_{\widehat B}
  \langle\xi_H,u\rangle\langle\xi_H,v\rangle\,\,d\xi
\end{equation}
commutes with $K_G$. Moreover, if the representation of $K_G$ on $V_1$ is
irreducible, then $$\mathbf M=m_G I,\qquad m_G = \frac{1}{k} \int_{\widehat B} |\xi_H|^2 \,d\xi, $$ and therefore
