{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.251995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d8241d51f933d51de63d68a920b8e711130eccc4d2e556dc777b836632f10cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_no_same_E of arXiv:2412.09532, 'Percolation on the stationary distributions of the voter model with stirring'] There exist dimension-dependent constants~$a,b>0$ such that the following holds. Fix~$N, \ell,L \in \mathbb{N}$ with~$\ell \ge 6$ and~$q(\ell,L) \in (0,1)$ and a proper embedding~$\mathcal T \in \mathcal P_N$. Then, there exist~$\mathsf v_0 = \mathsf v_0(\ell)$ such that, for all~$\mathsf v \ge \mathsf v_0$, all~$\alpha, \beta \in (0,1)$ with~$\alpha > \beta$, and all families~$\{E_m: m \in T_{(N)} \}$, where each~$E_m \in \mathcal{G}^{(2)}_{B(2L)} $ is either increasing-decreasing or decreasing-increasing, we have
