{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.251600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0da398cfd35e673fab229454fcce16504827d4d604efee6d9d0c4514e3d6b9e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_Psi_incr_decr of arXiv:2412.09532, 'Percolation on the stationary distributions of the voter model with stirring'] There exist dimension-dependent constants~$a,b>0$ such that the following holds. Fix~$\ell,L \in \mathbb{N}$ with~$\ell \ge 6$ and~$q(\ell,L) \in (0,1)$. Then, for all~$\mathsf v \ge \mathsf v_0, \alpha \in (0,1)$, all increasing events~$E$ and decreasing events~$F$ in~$\mathcal G_{B(2L)}$, we have
    \begin{align*}
    & \mathbb{E}[ \pi_\alpha(\zeta: \zeta \vee \eta_2 \in E) \cdot \mathds{1}\{ \eta_1 \equiv 0 \} ] \leq \pi_{\alpha + q-\alpha q}(E) + a \cdot |B(2L)|^2\exp \Big\{ -\frac{b \cdot \ell^{1/4}}{|B(2L)|} \Big\}, \\
