{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.609225+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0db4fa1b95e33e7ae53d6bc765ab00d9be9317abd0a5cfc34828388136e348d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: of arXiv:2608.13559, 'Equi-dependence implying independence'] Take any two nonnegative integers $s$ and $t$. Let 
\begin{equation*}
	\mathcal{P}_{\infty,s,t}:=\Big\{(S,T)\colon S\in\binom\mathbb{N} s,\ T\in\binom\mathbb{N} t,\ S\cap T=\emptyset \Big\}. 
