{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.209003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0dd7391f1a30246a67fa54b3abf1459dad9be2e444429b52c13ad9ca64700861","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 13 (Upper and lower escape probabilities) of arXiv:2512.09136, 'On the Green's functions and Martin boundary structure of a planar diffusion in a disconti'] Let $(a_0, b_0) \in \R^2$. Then: $$\P_{(a_0,b_0)}\bigl(B_t \underset{t\to+\infty}{\longrightarrow} +\infty\bigr) = h_{\alpha_{\mu^+}}(b_0),\quad \textnormal{and}\quad \P_{(a_0,b_0)}\bigl(B_t \underset{t\to+\infty}{\longrightarrow} -\infty\bigr) = h_{\alpha_{\mu^-}}(b_0).$$
