{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.812593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e18289319293a1b58d58ed5ef9a4cad17145e91d6d7d0dbba3102f87cc76b25","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mgf-bounds of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $n \geq n_0$ and $\nu_n$ be the stationary distribution of the $M/M/n$ system with arrival rate $\lambda = n-n^{1-\alpha}$ and unit service rate, we have  $\E_{\nu_n}\sqbr{e^{\theta_n(q-n)}} < \infty$ for $\theta < \log \frac{n}{\lambda}$. Moreover, when $\varepsilon_n = 1-\frac{\lambda}{n}$ and $\theta_n = \frac{1}{1+\delta} \log \br{\frac{n}{\lambda}}$, we have
\begin{align}

    \E_{\nu_n}\sqbr{e^{\frac{\varepsilon_n (q-n)}{1+\delta}}} \leq \frac{\sum_{q=0}^{n-1} \frac{\lambda^q}{q!} e^{\theta_n(q-n)} + \frac{\delta+1}{\delta} \frac{\lambda^n}{n!} n^\alpha}{\sum_{q=0}^{n-1} \frac{\lambda^q}{q!} + \frac{\lambda^n}{n!} n^\alpha} \leq 1+\frac{1}{\delta}.
\end{align}
Moreover, if $\alpha \in (0,1/2)$ then
\begin{align*}
    \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \E_{\nu_n}\sqbr{e^{\frac{\varepsilon_n (q-n)}{1+\delta}}} = 0.
\end{align*}
If $\alpha \in \br{1/2,\infty}$ then
\begin{align*}
    \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \E_{\nu_n}\sqbr{e^{\frac{\varepsilon_n (q-n)}{1+\delta}}} &= 1+\frac{1}{\delta}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.853817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e18ad26c7d248fc4d332213c2c49d8453355943791a97483a8f20ee9c3d7194","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_C of arXiv:2607.11469, 'Breuer-Major-Donsker invariance principle'] Suppose $\varphi\in L^2(\gamma)$ and the  processes $V_n$ 
