{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.821285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e2874300dd78d0c404c264a2609f901b97996f5afffcb257e69796baa0faabc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.04334, 'Fractional counting process at L\'{e}vy times and its applications'] Let  $\mathcal{N}_{\mu, \vartheta }^{\zeta ,\theta}(t),\; t\geq 0$ be the FCP defined in Eq. ((process of the paper)). The time-changed fractional counting process (TCFCP), denoted by $Z(t,\lambda _{\theta }),\;t\geq 0$  is obtained by the subordination of a non-decreasing L\'{e}vy process to an independent FCP and is given by
