{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.411804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e2cf1c66571588134ff316aeda8817c24556064aae004b34d3f341c21840e59","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 26 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] The difference
		\begin{equation}
			\zeta_{\pLie}(s)
			-\frac{C_{G,L}}{\Gamma(s)}
			\sum_{\ell=0}^{\infty}
			\frac{\beta_{G,L}^{\ell}}
			{\ell!\,(s-Q/2+\ell)}
		\end{equation}
		is entire. Hence
		\begin{equation}
			\operatorname*{Res}_{s=Q/2-\ell}\zeta_{\pLie}(s)
			=\frac{C_{G,L}\beta_{G,L}^{\ell}}
			{\ell!\,\Gamma(Q/2-\ell)}
		\end{equation}
		whenever $Q/2-\ell$ is not a nonpositive integer. If $Q/2\in\mathbb N_0$, the only possible poles are the simple poles at
		\[
		s=1,\ldots,Q/2.
		\]
		Some of them may disappear when the corresponding local coefficient vanishes. In this case,
		\begin{align}
			\zeta_{\pLie}(0)
			&=C_{G,L}\frac{\beta_{G,L}^{Q/2}}{(Q/2)!}-1,
			\\
			\zeta_{\pLie}(-j)
			&=(-1)^j j!C_{G,L}
			\frac{\beta_{G,L}^{Q/2+j}}{(Q/2+j)!},
			\qquad j\ge1.

		\end{align}
		If $Q/2\in\frac12+\mathbb N_0$, then
		\begin{equation}
			\zeta_{\pLie}(0)=-1,
			\qquad
			\zeta_{\pLie}(-j)=0\quad(j\ge1).
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.578910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e2eba68390d04ca56b40e1cf384a0bb7b1c4618e023ca035c6f70e9632284e0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:QuasiReg of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] A Dirichlet form~$(\mssE,\msD(\mssE))$ is $\tau$-\emph{quasi-regular} if
\begin{enumerate}[$(\text{\textsc{qr}}_1)$]
\item there exists a $\tau$-compact $\mssE$-nest;
\item there exists an $\mssE^{1/2}_1$-dense subset of~$\msD(\mssE)$ the elements of which all have $\mssE$-quasi-continuous $\mssm$-versions;
\item there exists an $\mssE$-polar set~$N$ and a countable family~$\left(u_n\right)_n$ of functions~$u_n\in\msD(\mssE)$, all having $\mssE$-quasi-continuous $\mssm$-versions~$\tilde{u}_n$ so that~$\seq{\tilde{u}_n}_n$ separates points in~$M\setminus N$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.859177+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e2f2a719076824b4bb69e307267e1c112ca98f5afc0b058d774071c2cbc8860","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 8 (\textit{cf.} {\cite[Chapter V, Proposition 8.8) of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] {IkedaWatanabe}}]
