{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e303e4737630c133d0727b67b6782435221ea2576754f6a13897f19ee41868b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:incrementMn of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] For any $\varphi\in\mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R} )$ and any $0\le s<t\le T$, the martingale term satisfies 
