{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.956224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e425569f19a1bb772d91382b0d1cec60341f6b62763148fcab9985a10f321e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:ci_sample_mean of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Let the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:ci of the paper) hold. Fix a confidence level $1-\alpha$, with
$\alpha \in (0,1)$, and for $n \geq 1$ define
\begin{align}
  r_A(\alpha,n,t)
  =
  \sqrt{\frac{2\tilde\sigma_A^2}{nt}\left(\log\frac{2}{\alpha} 
  + n\log N_\nu\right)}
  +
  \frac{c_A}{nt}\left(\log\frac{2}{\alpha} + n\log N_\nu\right).

\end{align}
Then for every $n \geq 1$ and $t > 0$, it holds that
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left(-r_A(\alpha,n,t) \leq \widehat{A}_{n,t} 
  - \E^\mu[\overline{A}_t]
  \leq r_A(\alpha,n,t)\right)
  \geq 1-\alpha,

\end{align}
that is, with probability of at least $1-\alpha$, under $\mathbb{P}^\nu$, the stationary mean
is found in the confidence interval
\begin{align}
  \E^\mu[\overline{A}_t]
  \in
  \left[\widehat{A}_{n,t} - r_A(\alpha,n,t),
  \widehat{A}_{n,t} + r_A(\alpha,n,t)\right].

\end{align}
Corresponding one-sided guarantees hold with the smaller radius
$r_A^{(1)}(\alpha,n,t)$ obtained by replacing $\log(2/\alpha)$ with $\log(1/\alpha)$
in Eq.~(equation eq:ci_sample_mean of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.345711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e432928baa491652a54dae3802ab72e325122a7b4de6b51bffa013163e04019","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2604.21113, 'Tail Bounds via Southwest Boundary'] Suppose $X \in \mathcal{T}^d(f)$ and $g$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $k$ plus a constant $C$. 
