{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.384068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e499a8444e8646449fc228470a0b64fa7360a95473372f6549c0e05c1026314","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Eproduct of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For any fixed $k$, let $e_1, \dotsc, e_k \in \binom{[n]}{2}$ be distinct potential edges and suppose that
