{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.957898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e49e103ca38ee754350afe7539286600fd4e1cfdfb5ef464c69488f71aca630","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2608.24675, 'Towards Liouville Quantum Gravity on fractals'] We say that	a centered Gaussian random element $h\colon\Omega\to \mathcal S'(K)$ is a \emph{fractal Gaussian free field} (FGFF) on $K$  if its covariance is given by
