{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.587964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e566d8f7af20dfe4deb549b9961a751de1ad6a56d0e4660d26d27a9c909cbcc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:space time correlations of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let $\underline{x}=(x_1,\dots,x_n)\in \Lambda_{N}^{n,\neq}$ and $\underline{y}=(y_1,\dots,y_m)\in \Lambda_{N}^{m,\neq}$ with $n,m\geq 1$. For any initial product measure $\mu^{\epsilon}$ and times $0<s<r$, the space-time correlation $v$-function is given by 
