{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.959542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e5adf59142de6878327ffeeb4b86a3116a5d4e05e50534b222f384799987f46","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Lamperti reduction) of arXiv:2608.08177, 'Uniform-in-Time Smoluchowski--Kramers Approximation\\ in Total Variation for Fractional SD'] Let \Cref{ass:smooth} hold and set
\[
  Z_t^\mu=F(X_t^\mu),\qquad
  U_t^\mu=\frac{Y_t^\mu}{\sigma(X_t^\mu)},
  \qquad z_0=F(x_0),\quad
  u_0=\frac{y_0}{\sigma(x_0)}.
\]
Then \eqref{eq:kinetic-original} is equivalent to
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
 dZ_t^\mu=U_t^\mu\,dt,\\[1mm]
 \mu\,dU_t^\mu
 =\bigl(a(Z_t^\mu)-U_t^\mu
        -\mu c(Z_t^\mu)(U_t^\mu)^2\bigr)dt+dB_t^H,\\[1mm]
 Z_0^\mu=z_0,\qquad U_0^\mu=u_0.
