{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.412528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e80f99bd613b4613a360494a5beada8398d7d57e7ff9d495d71d2f9b59319e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:variance_sensitive_local of arXiv:2608.27313, 'A Finite Sample Analysis for Quantile Temporal Difference Learning in Distributional Reinf'] There exists a universal constant $C_\star$ with the following property. Let $n$ be an $({\mathcal{F}}_t)$-stopping time satisfying $u\le n\le v$ and
