{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.738181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ea1abe9e9dc3d89246cc3b5738ab37aa4468fe309fd5c1173decd01dc2fdf1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma main_lemma_com of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Let $H$ and $\widetilde H$ be two matrices satisfying (main_assm of the paper). Suppose they satisfy the following moment-matching conditions: for $i,j\in \mathcal I$ and integers $l,l'\ge 0$,  

\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E} (H_{ij})^l (H^*_{ij})^{l'} - \mathbb{E} (\widetilde H_{ij})^l (\widetilde H^*_{ij})^{l'}=0 \ \ \text{for} \ \ l+l'\le 3, 
\end{equation}
and there exists a constant $\delta \in (0,1/2)$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\left|\mathbb{E} (H_{ij})^l (H^*_{ij})^{l'} - \mathbb{E} (\widetilde H_{ij})^l (\widetilde H^*_{ij})^{l'}\right| \lesssim N^{-2-\delta}  \ \ \text{for} \ \ l+l'= 4. 
