{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.470993+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0eae3a2e4a150032adf416bfe6519f412c54afacce6d41f79776ec174ff461e2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: reduced X_F_h^omega_Q of arXiv:2608.28278, 'Reduction of symmetric time-dependent Hamiltonian systems I: presymplectic principal $\R$-'] In the hypothesis of Corollary (corollary: reduction corank 2 of the paper), the Hamiltonian vector field $X_{F_h}^{\omega_Q}$ restricts to $J^{-1}(\nu)$, and its restriction is $\pi_\nu$-projectable on a vector field $X_\nu$ on $(T^*Q)_\nu$, that is, 
