As a consequence, (\ref{Av}) holds with $\widehat{\varepsilon }_{N}=\frac{
4d_{0}C_{d_{0}}(f^{\ast })^{2}}{f_{\ast }}N^{-1}.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.889100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0eb86106b3a7b7a9ef4edac49fdbd6f00ef5de674c2b7cfa16b9976afdfc8ab6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teorema 15 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] Let $ T\in S_m(M,M')$ and $ T'\in S_m(M',M'')$ be two stochastic transformations and $ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ be a non-explosive stochastic differential equation such that $ E_{T}(\mu,\sigma)$ and $ E_{T'}(E_{T}(\mu,\sigma))$ are non-explosive.  Given  a weak solution $(X,W)$  to $ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ in the probability space $ (\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$, then in the probability space $\ (\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{Q})$

    it holds that 
    \begin{equation*} P_{T'}\circ P_{T}(X,W) = P_{T' \circ T}(X,W); \ \ \ \ \ \  E_{T'} \circ E_T (\mu,\sigma)= E_{T' \circ T}(\mu,\sigma) \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.654432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0eba56f90788e870a4ee623e58f8b4d27465fb34adeeec15df17c988c7ddc854","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.04631, 'Existence of Martingale Solutions to Stochastic Constrained Heat Equation'] We say that there exists a martingale solution of (equation main prob of the paper) (SCHE) if there exist
\begin{enumerate}
    \item a stochastic basis
