{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:45.011496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0eccc407bb4ed74dcd3e9d76450dda583626aefbde99fa6b9ca9ec104f5a2dcf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (\cite{shuster1968inverse}) of arXiv:2605.11877, 'Fluctuation analysis for a randomly perturbed dynamical system with state-dependent impuls'] \,
Suppose $X$ is a positive random variable with an inverse Gaussian distribution with parameters $\hat{\mu} > 0$, $\lambda > 0$, i.e., $X$ has density
\begin{equation*}
f(x)= \begin{cases}
		\left( \frac{\lambda}{2 \pi x^3} \right)^{\frac{1}{2}} \exp \left[ -\frac{\lambda (x - \hat{\mu})^2}{2 \hat{\mu}^2 x} \right], &\quad x > 0,\\
		0, & \quad x \leq 0.
	\end{cases} 
\end{equation*}
Let $F(c; \hat{\mu}, \lambda) = \BP(X \le c)$ denote the cumulative distribution function of $X$, set
\begin{equation*}
a \triangleq \frac{\lambda (c - \hat{\mu})^2}{\hat{\mu}^2 c} \quad \text{and for $z>0$, let} \quad \quad G(z) \triangleq \int_z^\infty (2 \pi t)^{-\frac{1}{2}} \exp(-t/2) \, dt 
\end{equation*}
be the tail probability of $\chi^2_1$.
Then	
\begin{itemize}
\item[(A)] $F(c; \hat{\mu}, \lambda) = \frac{1}{2} G(a) + \frac{1}{2} \exp(2 \lambda / \hat{\mu}) G(a + 4 \lambda / \hat{\mu}), \quad 0 < c \leq \hat\mu;$
\item[(B)] $F(c; \hat{\mu}, \lambda) = 1 - \frac{1}{2} G(a) + \frac{1}{2} \exp(2 \lambda / \hat{\mu}) G(a + 4 \lambda / \hat{\mu}), \quad\hat{\mu} < c < \infty,$
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

