{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.272623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ee5de58f18bf688d99590866a4ddc0a21a94e456ad38c9b4afec77cb419baf3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm MainThm1 of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] Let $k\in \mathbb{N}, s\in \mathbb{R}_+$, $\beta >0$ such that $2ks^2>\beta$. Then, as $N \to \infty$,
