{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.520510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f0a1f9671835b6e3ce0491a6c6567622505067efc92f40d7a540045251bbb75","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 (Admissible radial denominator) of arXiv:2609.02595, 'Minimal Radial Sub-Gamma Envelopes for Infinitely Divisible Random Vectors'] A function \(q:\R^d\to[0,\infty]\) is admissible for \(X\) if it is positively homogeneous and
