{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.078232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f20eeaa71a14f9a1c5c15b7a2386c65f0eb3a56de19516843a4b810b0a7b9a7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 36 of arXiv:2510.26216, 'A functional Breuer-Major theorem with Poisson noise'] If $k$ is even, then for every $ (u_1,\dots,u_k)\in \ZZ^k$ we have \begin{equation}
             R_k \big( (u_1,\dots,u_k) \big)\lesssim \prod_{j=1}^{\frac{k}{2}}R_2 ((u_{2j-1},u_{2j})).
        \end{equation}
If $k\ge 3$ is odd, for every $ (u_1,\dots,u_k)\in \ZZ^k$ we have \begin{equation}
      \begin{aligned}
            R_k\big( (u_1,\dots,u_k) \big)\lesssim & \big(R_2\big( (u_{2k-2},u_{2k-1})\big)R_2\big( (u_{2k-2},u_{2k})\big) + R_2\big( (u_{2k-2},u_{2k-1})\big) R_2\big( (u_{2k-1},u_{2k})\big)\\
            &+ R_2\big( (u_{2k-2},u_{2k})\big) R_2\big( (u_{2k-1},u_{2k})\big)\big) \prod_{j=1}^{\frac{k-3}{2}}R_2((u_{2j-1},u_{2j})).
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Furthermore, the proportionality constants are independent of $ (u_1,\dots,u_k)$.","status":"unverified"}

