{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.278650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f4467351fc7ec177475c9fe5565b012ce12c64f127bcf2026a8f8a17f0b9b5a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] In the same setting of Theorem \ref{Theo_main1}, we have for $0<\alpha\le 1$ and $t\ge 0$
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{P}\{\vert \xi^\top A\xi-\mathbb{E}\xi^\top A\xi\vert\ge L(\alpha)^{2}t    \}\le 2\exp(-c(\alpha)f(t)),\nonumber
	\end{align}
where  $L(\alpha)=\max_{i}\Vert \zeta_{i}\Vert_{\Psi_{\alpha}}$, $c(\alpha)$ is a positive constant depending only on $\alpha$, and
\begin{align}
	f(t)=\min\Big\{ \frac{t^{2}}{\sum_{k}a_{kk}^{2}p_{k}+\sum_{i\neq j}a_{ij}^{2}p_{i}p_{j}}, 
	& \frac{t}{\Vert (a_{ij}\sqrt{p_{i}p_{j}})_{n\times n}\Vert_{l_{2}\to l_{2}} }, \nonumber\\
	&\Big( \frac{t}{\max_{i}\big( \sum_{j}a_{ij}^{2}p_{j}\big)^{1/2}} \Big)^{\frac{2\alpha}{2+\alpha}}, \Big(\frac{t}{\Vert A\Vert_{\infty}}\Big)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}}\Big\}.\nonumber
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.851678+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f46b752f2d21f137cdfc97c30a60ec9f479371ab9bd586ad2143343227a027e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Bulk case) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] We recall Convention~\ref{conv:inverse-stieltjes-branches}. Fix \(E\in(-2,2)\) and define the anchor \\
\(
i_N(E)\;:=\;\min\bigl\{\,k\in\{1,\dots,N\}\ :\ \lambda^{(N)}_{k}\ \ge E\sqrt{N}\,\bigr\}.
\) Then the overlaps satisfy
\begin{equation}
\Omega^{(N)}_{\,i_N(E)+u,\;i_N(E)+v}
\;\mathrel{\underset{N\to\infty}{\overset{d}{\sim}}}\;
\frac{g_v}{\,S_{\mu,\,g^2}^{-1}(h)_u-\mu_v\,}\,
\sqrt{\bigl(S_{\mu,\,g^2}^{-1}\bigr)'(h)_u},
\qquad h=-\frac{E}{2\sqrt{4-E^2}}.
\end{equation}

\noindent
Here $(\mu_u)_{u\in\mathbb Z}$ follow the sine$_\beta$ point process, and $(g_u)_{u\in\mathbb Z}$ are i.i.d. standard Gaussians $\mathcal{N}_\beta(0,1)$ independent of $(\mu_u)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.637057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f46bb9da508c3861f6a3b3667dd09ccaff0647fff4cd4aae33c1d29d80cfc6d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:root deg of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mu=\mu_n$ be such that $1\ll\mu\ll n^{1/4}$.
    Let $\mathbf{T}_n$ be a tree distributed according to~(equation eq:T dist of the paper).
    Then the asymptotic behavior of the degree of the root $\varnothing$ in $\mathbf{T}_n$ is given by
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\deg_{\mathbf{T}_n}(\varnothing)-2\mu}{\sqrt{6\mu}}\overset d\longrightarrow\mathcal{N}(0,1)\,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.953958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f472c73d0bc832cfde3d13b736f1009f13e4c1054847b1196b1ac92e92c81a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Let $\nu \in \mP(\mC_T^1)$ and $H_\nu^t$ be the operator defined in \eqref{eq: H_mu^t}. Then we have
    \begin{align}
\begin{split}

    K_\nu(s, u)- H^t_\nu(s,u)= \beta^2 \int_0^t K_\nu(s,r)H^t_\nu(r,u)\,dr
    =\beta^2 \int_0^t H^t_\nu(s,r) K_\nu(r,u)\,dr,\end{split}
\end{align}
for almost every $u, s, t \in [0, T]$. Moreover, the kernel $H_\nu^t$ extends to a continuous function on $[0, t]^2$, and we have
\begin{equation}

        \sup_{t \in [0, T]} \sup_{u, s \in [0, t]} H_\nu^t(u, s)  \leq A^2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.497848+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f4a6671cb74b641552c1a1268045d8e97401fa07fcec375f1878f6866202327","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma two point commutation of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] For adjacent growth points $x, y \in \mathbb{R}$ (no marked points $\{z_1,z_2,\ldots,z_n\}$  are between $x$ and $y$). If the system
\begin{equation}
\left\{\begin{array}{l}
\frac{\kappa}{2} \partial_{x x} \psi+\sum_i \cot(\frac{z_i-x}{2})\partial_i \psi+\cot(\frac{y-x}{2})\partial_y \psi+\left( \left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right) \frac{1}{4\sin^2(\frac{y-x}{2})}+h_1(x, z)\right) \psi=0 \\
\frac{\kappa}{2} \partial_{y y} \psi+\sum_i \cot(\frac{z_i-y}{2}) \partial_i \psi+\cot(\frac{x-y}{2}) \partial_x \psi+\left(\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right) \frac{1}{4\sin^2(\frac{x-y}{2})}+h_2(y, z)\right) \psi=0
\end{array}\right.
\end{equation}
admits a non-vanishing solution $\psi$, then: functions $h_1, h_2$ can be written as $h_1(x, z)=h(x, z), h_2(y, z)=h(y, z)$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.724295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f4c5fde20c4ccb217e24f9ce6d4bd5240df76dc4017ae264b3c56822a114674","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:xi-lower-weak-upper-p of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $1 < p < 2$. The following holds for all $\beta$ sufficiently large. Let $h = H+1-n$ for fixed $n\geq 0$.  Then for any $\delta > 0$ and all $1 \leq \ell \leq L^{\frac12-\delta}$, we have
\begin{equation}

 1 - L^{-2\delta + o(1)} \leq \frac{\xi^{(p)}_{\ell,h}}{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_\infty(\phi_o < -h)} \leq 1 + L^{-1+o(1)}\,.
\end{equation}
If $p > 2$ instead, there exists $c(\beta), c_0(\beta)$ such that for $1 \leq \ell \leq \sqrt{L}e^{-c(\beta) \sqrt{\log L}^{\frac{p}{p-1}}}$, we have
\begin{equation}

 1 - e^{-c_0(\beta) \sqrt{\log L}^{\frac{p}{p-1}}} \leq \frac{\xi^{(p)}_{\ell,h}}{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_\infty(\phi_o < -h)} \leq 1 + L^{-1+o(1)}\,.
\end{equation}
Moreover, this holds when replacing $\xi_{\ell,h}$ by $-\frac1{|S|}\log{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_\infty(\phi_x\geq -h,\,\forall x\in S)$ for any set $S\subset \mathbb Z^2$, not necessarily connected, of size at most $\ell^2$. In addition, the upper bound holds for all $\ell \geq 1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.698711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f589da1d522178c9524a2d7a121bf18af70dff1c1fb5e9e1cb7f7c119d5447d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2608.17437, 'Spectral gap for unlabelled Ginibre Interacting Brownian motion'] Let $P_N:\mathcal L_N\to\mathcal H_N$ be the orthogonal projection.  Then, 
\begin{equation}
  \|u-P_Nu\|_{\mathcal L_N}^2
  \le
  \sum_{i=1}^N\|\overline\partial_i u\|_{\mathcal L_N}^2 

\end{equation}
for every $u \in D(q_N):=\{u \in \mathcal L_N: \overline\partial_i u \in \mathcal L_N,\ 1 \le i \le N\}$, where $\overline\partial_i$ is understood as the distributional derivative.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.600408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f59fc6e05df2d64f17fe9dd80d6d523439ad06c22873b17d3ddee8e147ae2bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Td-ad-model-exists of arXiv:2606.10257, 'Downward conditional monotonicity gives survival and extinction for contact processes in r'] Consider an MMPP $(B,X)$ with irreducible, monotone $T$, increasing $\alpha$, eigenvector $v^*$, and which satisfies, for all triples $\ell<i<j$,
	\begin{equation}
		(\alpha_j-\alpha_i)\sum_{\ell\leq s} v^*_s\leq \sum_{\ell\leq s} (T_{is}-T_{js}).
	\end{equation}
	For any $\delta>0$, there exists an MMPP $(B^\delta,X^\delta)$ with strictly monotone $T^\delta=T+\delta E$ (with $E$ an appropriate matrix), the same $\alpha$, eigenvector $v^\delta$, and which satisfies, for all triples $\ell<i<j$,
	\begin{equation}
		(\alpha_j-\alpha_i)\sum_{\ell\leq s} v^\delta_s < \sum_{\ell\leq s} (T^\delta_{is}-T^\delta_{js}).
	\end{equation}
	Furthermore, $(B^\delta,X^\delta)$ weakly converges to $(B,X)$ as $\delta\to0$, and the eigenvectors satisfy $v^*\preceq v^\delta$ for all $\delta>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.606240+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f5babff73c0929edd1010cab6951209df0ff09d6fba7cdc4316c2ed40a5cce7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gyration_derivative2 of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] Let $u\in \mathbb R^d$. The estimate
\begin{multline}
\frac{1}{\beta_c |J'(r)|} \frac{d}{dr} \mathbb E_{\beta_c,r} \left[\sum_{x\in K} \langle x,u\rangle^2 \right]
=  2 |B_r| \mathbb E_{\beta_c,r}|K| \mathbb E_{r} \left[\sum_{x\in K} \langle x,u\rangle^2 \right] + (\mathbb E_{\beta_c,r}|K|)^2 \sum_{y\in B_r} \langle y,u\rangle^2
 \\
 \pm O\left(\|u\|^2_2 r^2 \mathbb E_{\beta_c,r}\left[|K|^2|K\cap B_r|\right]\right) \pm O\left(\mathbb E_{\beta_c,r}\left[|K||K\cap B_r| \sum_{x\in K}\langle x,u \rangle^2\right]\right).

