{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.250201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f6971f757111e2affe489d3eecd50d107a1e4373e1cbf0c1dba19f599e1b4c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 48 (Annuli) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any real numbers $q, u \ge 0$ and integer $\ell \ge 1$, define the following subsets of the liquid region:
	\begin{flalign*}
		\mathcal{A}_{\ell}^{q} = \big\{ z \in \mathfrak{L}_q: 4^{-\ell} \le \mathtt{d}_{z} \mathtt{e}_{z;q} \le 4^{1-\ell} \}; \qquad  \mathcal{B}_{\ell}^q = \big\{ z \in \mathfrak{L}_q : 4^{1/2-\ell} \le \mathtt{d}_z  \mathtt{e}_{z;q} \le 4^{1 - \ell} \big\}.
	\end{flalign*}
as well as
