		\mathcal{A}_{\ell}^{q} (u) = \big\{ z \in \mathcal{A}_{\ell}^q: \mathtt{d}_z^{1/2} \mathtt{e}_{z;q}^{3/2} \ge uN^{-1} \big\}; \qquad \mathcal{B}_{\ell}^q (u) = \big\{ z \in \mathcal{B}_{\ell}^q : \mathtt{d}_z^{1/2} \mathtt{e}_{z;q}^{3/2} \ge uN^{-1} \big\}.
	\end{flalign*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.766413+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f6da556942fec9ac5406322b378479b547408db73a3a974fe5a2f8abc81d274","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] Suppose $\nu^N$ converges weakly towards $\nu^*$ on $(D_{\mathscr{S}^\prime},M_1)$. Then, for every $a > 0$, we have uniformly in $N \ge 1$ and $t \in [0,T]$ that 
	\begin{align}
		\E{\langle\nu_t^N,\nnorm{x}^k\1_{(-\infty,-\lambda]}(x)\rangle} &= o(\lambda^ke^{-a\lambda}), \\
		\E{\int_0^T\langle\nu_t^N,\nnorm{x}^k\1_{(-\infty,-\lambda]}(x)\rangle\diff t} &= o(\lambda^ke^{-a\lambda}), \\
		\E{\int_0^T\langle\nu_t^*,\nnorm{x}^k\1_{(-\infty,-\lambda]}(x)\rangle\diff t} &= o(\lambda^ke^{-a\lambda}). 
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.835020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f70e3beaf667a62493c77362ce105df37b499c345e48e1480cc7363f63a766e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2604.10820, 'A Strict Gap Between Relaxed and Partition-Constrained\\ Spectral Compression in a Six-Sta'] Assume the local-mode-dominated ordering
