{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.680897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f8a6575de465febedda284e8503982feef3eca60346810ea88714d6dee1f571","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:jump_reconstruction of arXiv:2510.18106, 'Law equivalence for Ornstein--Uhlenbeck dynamics\\ driven by L\'evy noise'] There exist Borel maps $\mathcal Z:D_{H,T}\to D_{H,T}$ and, for each Borel set $E\subset H\setminus\{0\}$ bounded away from $0$, maps $Z^1_E:D_{H,T}\to D_{H,T}$ such that:
