{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.741855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fb281969fb4e088a443e24b2377952d7bd8300e09d64c473ac9e2a013240552","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition {Following \cite[Thm.\ B of arXiv:2609.00163, 'Decompositions and diagrams of symplectic surfaces in Weinstein domains'] {gironella2020some}}]
    Let $(W',\omega')$ be a (weak, strong, Weinstein) filling of $(M',\xi')$, and $(W,\omega)$ be a (weak, strong, Weinstein) filling of $(M,\xi)$. A {\it branched cover of (weak, strong, Weinstein) fillings} $f:(W',S')\rightarrow (W,S)$ is a smooth branched cover with branching set $S$, such that
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item $S$ and $S'$ are symplectic surfaces in $(W,\omega)$ and $(W',\omega')$, respectively;
    \item $\partial S$ and $\partial S'$ are transverse links in $(M,\xi)$ and $(M',\xi')$, respectively;
    \item $(M',\xi')$ is a contact branched cover of $(M,\xi)$ along $\partial S$ in the sense of [geiges2008introduction]; and
    \item $\omega'$ is deformation equivalent 
    to the form $\hat{\omega}_\epsilon$ in [gironella2020some] for $\epsilon$ sufficiently small.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.835096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fb628e2270cfe56879a8fd1bce7c676f593893549064ebf0321f32f10e22d46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (\cite{Bog78,Bog80,SS85}) of arXiv:2609.01965, 'A logarithmic Bogomolov--Sommese vanishing theorem on compact K\"ahler manifolds'] Let $X$ be a projective manifold and $L$ a line bundle over $X$. 
