{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.363393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fc3e80b31e169e9615f9469f2e714a1d329946b41befc5c2f468885ebf50532","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 (Total variation bound between two clusters and two bridges) of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] Let \(0<J<U\) satisfy \(\sinh 2J=e^{-2U}\). There exist \(n_0\geq 1, c_0\geq 0, c>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), \(m_n\geq c_0n\), there exists a probability measure \(\MixMeas_n\) on \((\SetRootMarkBackCont\times \SetRootMarkForwCont)^2\) such that the following holds.
