{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.452302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fca33090c4ea66a4928ae418caf29e363f3983ff431dadf9916ff5f0c02ba0e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def : Intro/main_thm/adm_metrics of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $L>0$ and $g$ be a norm on $\mathbb{R}^d$. We define $\RegPD[g]^L$ as the set of all pseudometrics $D$ on $X$ such that
