{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.732593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fcb656865fccb4d554d2e8b984d4cc8f88e210568449ab22e3c0b331b280435","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop decoup of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] For every $k\ge2$ there exists a constant $C_k>0$, depending only on $k$, with the following property.  Let $\{\xi_i\}_{i}$ be a sequence of independent random variables in a measurable space $(S,\mathscr{S})$, let $\{\xi_i^{(j)}\}_{i}$, $1\le j\le k$, be independent copies of $\{\xi_i\}$, and let $f_{i_1\cdots i_k}:S^{k}\to E$ be measurable functions with values in a Banach space $(E,\|\cdot\|)$.  Then, for every $n\ge k$ and every $t>0$,
