{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.925305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fe08b6a4e0c4502add1401247f02d9e98efaa0b0061f1a7d84421493e1a80a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2412.02162, 'Limit theorems for random permutations induced by Chinese restaurant processes'] Suppose there exists $\beta\in[0,\alpha^2/2)$ such that $|a_{i+j}(f) - a_i(f)|\le Cj^\beta$ for all $i,j\in{\mathbb N}$. Then, 
