{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:49:24.962457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10577bc1e4d49ce4bd4239d2844ce3ca04243255f41e712ef641fd5fdc17bc69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Q-existence of arXiv:2609.03428, 'A New Sufficient Condition for Oriented Graphs Determined by Their Generalized Skew Spectr'] Let $\Sigma$ be a controllable oriented graph and let $\Delta$ be an oriented graph. Then $\Sigma$ and $\Delta$ have the same generalized skew spectrum if and only if there exists a unique regular rational orthogonal matrix $Q$ such that
