{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.674519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_105fc30fa1e78e5892eded1f73e4d3f6d8332adbfcc1c48ad7b6711ddb7b2166","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Driscoll:zero of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] Let \( \xi : T \times \Omega \to \mathbb{R} \) be a centered Gaussian process with covariance function \( K \), and suppose that \( (\Omega,\mathcal{A},\mu) \) is complete.
