{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.885128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1068c09ba6e81e89644c8b7034f34aedc662c66e0a09ef5bcfba5070e61c41da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:bounded_second_mom of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] There is a constant $c_3 > 0$ such that for all $N \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t > 0$ with $tN \in \mathbb{N}$, 
