{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.892673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_106a8023bff03f8d999c2817878739b403abdafa1965a108edefb73d81710135","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Conditional Bernstein condition) of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] There exists an absolute constant $H>0$ such that, for every integer $m\ge3$ and every $k\ge1$,
