{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.878086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_106e49f028686ed8e76e8cca192fc19325bba1e713de49cbaa6f53449875810e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] We call a contour ${\mathcal C}$ (of the type defined above) a \emph{good contour}
