{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.447050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1070ca665fb24df307e21380988abd159f6e5680e56dc44b75f667570287028b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn planar-embedded of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a loop $\ell$ and a plaquette assignment $K$ such that the pair $(\ell,K)$ is balanced. We say that an  embedded map $M=(m,\psi)$ with boundary $\ell$ and plaquette assignment $K$ (Definition~(defn:embedded-maps-bound-plaq-ass of the paper)) is \textbf{planar} if $M$ satisfies the two following additional conditions:
