We say that the mild solution of (equation eqFO of the paper) is unique if  $\{X_1(t,x)\}_{t\in [0,T]}$, $\{X_2(t,x)\}_{t\in [0,T]}$ are two mild solutions to (equation eqFO of the paper) defined on the same complete filtered probability space then it satisfy
\[
X_1(t,x)=X_2(t,x),\quad \forall t\in [0,T], \quad \mathbb{P}{\rm-a.s.}
\]","status":"unverified"}

