{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.060174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10903187f5033c6e004a172486bab0258ab999effb0ce27b18a0bcf7a3b09ba7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Two-sided branching process in a random environment) of arXiv:2607.02019, 'Critical branching processes in random environment with immigration and an application to '] A \emph{two-sided branching process in the random environment} $(\mathcal E_k)_{k\in\mathbb Z}$ \emph{with immigration} is a process $(Z_n)_{n\in\mathbb Z}$ with $Z_n\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}$ for all $n\in\mathbb Z$ satisfying
