{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.960710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10e68ebfb9960bfff90f8b191c8a9995e1a019a9b1f050a95a59f4429d25d9ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Independence of the increment map) of arXiv:2608.12225, 'Higher-order variation and\\ pathwise It\^o calculus on manifolds'] Let $e$ and $\widetilde e$ be two admissible increment maps and let
$X\in C([0,T],M)$. Assume that
\[
    \sup_{n\geq n_0}
    \sum_{i=0}^{N_n-1}
    |\Delta_i^{n,e}X|_g^p
    <\infty.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
   \mathop{\sup}_{n\geq n_0}
    \sum_{i=0}^{N_n-1}
    |\Delta_i^{n,\widetilde e}X|_g^p
    <\infty,\qquad \left\|
        \mu_{X,n}^{(p),e}
        -
        \mu_{X,n}^{(p),\widetilde e}
    \right\|_{\mathrm{TV}}
    \longrightarrow0.

\end{equation}
In particular, if
\[
    \mu_{X,n}^{(p),e}
    \stackrel{*}{\rightharpoonup}
    [X]_{\pi}^{(p)},
\quad{\rm then}\quad
    \mu_{X,n}^{(p),\widetilde e}
    \stackrel{*}{\rightharpoonup}
    [X]_{\pi}^{(p)}.
\]
Thus the finite $p$-energy property and the $p$-th variation tensor do not depend on the choice of admissible increment map.","status":"unverified"}

