{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.934418+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10e9aa8a2014ed94cae79457066fef83c8e84c637e0d90f9dc5f3564cfa2330b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm masterthm of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Let $T \in (\mathbb R^d)^{\otimes r}$ be a symmetric random jointly Gaussian tensor with $\mathbb E[T] = 0$ and $2 \leq p < \infty$.
