{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.775096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10f4b6ca69cf33dad055d9d9450efd6192c6cc3320dd6ce5bcce9b6e29193029","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop TP2-fnk of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $A=(A_{i,k})_{i,k\geq0}$ and $F=(F_{n,k})_{n,k\geq0}$ be two arrays

