{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.591273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10f5ec0350fb1a9f8e933d17ac4473eb196c8934a073d0ccd73c423f5edc92e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor prop_2.2 of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Consider a TASEP $(\tilde{x}(t),t\geq 0)$ with a deterministic initial condition $\{x_n^f, n \in \mathbb{Z} \}$ with $x_n^f \leq 0$ for $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $x_n^f > 0$ for $n \in \mathbb{Z}_{\leq 0}$. Let $d > 1$, define $\hat{c}_2$ and $c_1$ as in Assumption~(assumpt:2.9 of the paper) and suppose that
	\begin{equation}  
	y_T(\tau) \coloneqq \frac{x^f_{\hat{c}_2 \tau T^{2/3}}+d\hat{c}_2 \tau T^{2/3}}{c_1 T^{1/3}}, \ \ \tau \in \mathbb{R}, 
	\end{equation}
	fulfils $y_T(\tau) \geq - 2 (1+d)^{-2} \tau^2$ for $\tau \in [-\hat{c}_2^{-1} (1-d^{-2})T^{1/3}, \hat{c}_2^{-1} d^{-2} T^{1/3}]$ and for all $T$ large enough. Further, suppose that $y_T$ converges uniformly on compact sets to a piecewise continuous and càdlàg function $y$. Then, it holds 
	\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned} 
	\lim_{T \to \infty} \mathbb{P}(\tilde{x}_{d^{-2} T}(T) > (1-2d^{-1}) T - S T^{1/3})
	&= \mathbb{P}\left( \sup_{\tau \in \mathbb{R}} \{ \mathcal{A}_2(\tau) - \tau^2 - y(-\tau) \} < c_1^{-1} S \right).
	\end{aligned}  
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10f66fef367d98550074aa9fe0f7376d408efcd023c5b809de7ece6067acf327","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2mmnew of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] For $\alpha > 0$ fixed and $\mathcal{A}_j$ defined as above, let us define the event
