{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.467693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1121a2f9f2f9eab85896331bcb60959de9e3366246835ac27674a656453ae6f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Palm-Lcal-ijn of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] For $r\neq l\in [n], k=1,2$ and for all non-negative measurable functions $f$ on $(\Omega,{\mathcal F })$,
\begin{align}
 \frac{\Lambda^{(k)}_{l,r}}{4\lambda_l\lambda_r v_lv_r} \mathbb{E}^0_{{\mathcal V }^{(k)}_{l,r}} [f ({\mathcal H })]
& = \int_{0}^\infty  \int_{0}^h \int_{t^*}^\infty 
\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal H }\Bigg[ f \Big(\theta_{\hat{s}(0,h,-t',h')}({\mathcal H }^r+\delta_{(0,h)}+ {\mathcal H }^l+\delta_{(-t',h')}+\!\!\!\sum_{ m\neq l,r}{\mathcal H }^m)\Big) {\nonumber}\\

&\hspace{2.5in}\times \prod_{i}{\mathds{1}}_{{\mathcal H }^i\left(E^{\hat{s}_k(0,h,-t',h'),v_i}_{\hat{h}_k(0,h,-t',h')}\right)=0}
