    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.226452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_114c9f079db22feb7791853cf6526d8767410daada6344e91d8d417f82b920ee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma elliptic_sys2 of arXiv:2609.00627, 'Global well-posedness of radially symmetric strong solutions to two-dimensional compressib'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded domain with $C^{k+2}$ boundary.  Given $f \in W^{k,p}(\Omega)$,  if $v$ is the solution to following \textit{Neumann} boundary problem of the elliptic system equation
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{cases}
			\Delta v=f,  \enspace in \enspace \Omega\\
			\frac{\partial v}{\partial n}=0, \enspace on \enspace \partial\Omega
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation}
	satisfies the following elliptic estimates
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{aligned}
			\|\nabla v\|_{W^{k+1,p}(\Omega)} \leq C\| f \|_{W^{k,p}(\Omega)}. 
