{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.623077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_114f417b35bd7e5e91bb2af0d14aa9a6de5b956aca255d3d39a33e339393ef79","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2605.12142, 'Nonlinear filtering with stochastic discontinuities'] Let $\Gamma=\Gamma(\omega;t,y)$ be an $\bbF^Y$-predictable function such that Equation \eqref{positivity condition} hold. The process $\rho(1)$ solves 
