{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.116694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1150bf68229b93ac40d205879a064afcefffe7af7589c790c7c0421991a13fab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: partition procedure in sle of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] There exist a constant $c_2>0$ and a  partition $\mathsf{B}_1,\cdots,\mathsf{B}_n$ of $\Lambda_N$ such that the following holds:
