{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.638923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1155b6277e8045d89de2391a1f200c64cb5692a295769987c05e6f43c6d1b9a0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:complex-Rd of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Let $\mu$ be a sub-exponential distribution on $\RR^d$ and $f\in L^2(\mu)$.  
Let $\varphi(\xi) = \cF[r_D\cdot \mu](\xi)$, where $r_D$ is the residual function after projecting $f$ onto polynomial space of degree at most $D$. 
Then for any $\xi \in \RR^d$, it holds that 

\begin{align}
  |\varphi(\xi)| &\le \norm{r}_\mu \, \tanh\Big( \frac{K\pi \|\xi\|_2}{4}\Big)^{D}. 

\end{align}
In addition, for any $v_1, v_2, \ldots, v_k\in \SS^{d-1}$ with $k \le D$, it holds that 
\begin{align}
\big|  \partial^k \varphi(\xi)[v_1, v_2, \ldots, v_k] \big|&\le \norm{r}_\mu \, \kappa_{4} (v_1,v_2,\ldots, v_k) \,  \tanh \Big( \frac{K\pi \|\xi\|_2}{2}\Big)^{D-k}, 
\end{align}
where $\kappa_{4}(v_1,v_2,\ldots, v_k) = \Big\|{\Big(\prod_{j=1}^k \dotp{v_j}{x}\Big)^2}\Big\|_\mu^{1/2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.133269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1155fe26ba7cf5cfbd6b5c9102d90b97659163ee4553fd51f846039a16346bf3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:covering-packing-4 of arXiv:2606.21556, 'Mean field limit of non-exchangeable interacting diffusions on co-evolutionary networks'] Consider a metric space $(\mathcal{X},d_\mathcal{X})$, and assume that $d'_\mathcal{X}$ is any other metric on $\mathcal{X}$ such that there exist two constants $C_1,C_2>0$ verifying
$$\frac{1}{C_1}d'_\mathcal{X}(x,y)\leq d_\mathcal{X}(x,y)\leq C_2d'_\mathcal{X}(x,y),$$
for any $x,y\in \mathcal{X}$. Then, for any compact set $K\subset \mathcal{X}$ the following relations holds true
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{N}_{\frac{\varepsilon}{C_2}}(K,d_\mathcal{X}')&\leq \mathcal{N}_\varepsilon(K,d_\mathcal{X})\leq \mathcal{N}_{C_1\varepsilon}(K,d_\mathcal{X}')\\
\mathcal{M}_{C_1\varepsilon}(K,d_\mathcal{X}')&\leq \mathcal{M}_\varepsilon(K,d_\mathcal{X})\leq \mathcal{M}_\frac{\varepsilon}{C_2}(K,d_\mathcal{X}'),
\end{align*}
for every $\varepsilon>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.299731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_115696e3b37a590a9819aa8836730b0fd8feb0c2d5b483e49a052dfb94b6bcff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Linear Gaussian smoothed likelihood and force) of arXiv:2608.21709, 'Posterior Information Dynamics of Diffusion Models for Linear Inverse Problems'] Let \(X_0\sim\calN(0,\Sigma)\) and
\(R=AX_0+\varepsilon\), where \(\varepsilon\sim\calN(0,\Gamma)\),
\(\Gamma\succ0\), and \(\varepsilon\) is independent of \(X_0\) and of the
forward noising variable used to form \(X_t\).  Define
\begin{equation}

B_t=a_t^2\Sigma+\Delta_t\Id_d,
\qquad
Q=A\Sigma A^\top+\Gamma.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}

R\mid X_t=x\sim \calN(M_tx,\Sigma_{R\mid t}),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

M_t=a_tA\Sigma B_t^{-1},
\qquad
\Sigma_{R\mid t}=Q-a_t^2A\Sigma B_t^{-1}\Sigma A^\top.
\end{equation}
Consequently, the exact measurement force is
\begin{equation}

g_t(x,r)=M_t^\top\Sigma_{R\mid t}^{-1}(r-M_tx).
\end{equation}
Under the joint law of \((X_t,R)\),
\begin{equation}

\frac1d\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2
=
\frac1d\operatorname{Tr}
\left(M_t^\top\Sigma_{R\mid t}^{-1}M_t\right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, under the VP schedule \eqref{eq:forward-marginal} (so that
\(\Delta_t=1-a_t^2\)), if along a dimension sequence
\(\lambda_{\min}(\Gamma)\ge\gamma_0>0\) and
\(d^{-1}\|A\Sigma\|_F^2\le C_0\), then as \(a_t\to0\),
\begin{equation}

\frac1d\E\|g_t(X_t,R)\|^2=O(a_t^2),
\end{equation}
which is the Gaussian specialization of
Corollary~\ref{cor:general-high-noise-energy}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.694336+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11583c031b137322f9373e4c5e23ffe67c274521c32077e249398d70b01c3dd2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:U_asy of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] For the deformed Gaussian matrix $X$ defined in Definition~(def:inhomo of the paper) under Assumptions~(itm:B1 of the paper)--(itm:B2 of the paper) of Definition~(mixingdef of the paper), with $n = \sum_{j=1}^s n_j$ and $a=\|A_N\|_{\mathrm{op}}$, the following statements hold:
