{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.132055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_115a22b756d30ca3afb8c1aea5ee1c983f290a170ed08d6eb9822598312e32ab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:covariance-bounds of arXiv:2510.11015, 'An interpretable universal bound for multiserver queues via a leave-one-out technique'] Consider the modified $GI/GI/n$\xspace system satisfying Assumptions~(assump:bdd-exp-remain of the paper) and (assump:modified-ggn-stable of the paper), with the load $\rho < 1$. Let $\Gamma_{{s,j}}$ and $\Gamma_{a}$ be the terms defined in (equation eq:gamma-s-def of the paper) and (equation eq:gamma-a-def of the paper), respectively. Then 
