where $x_i^*:=\sum_{j=1}^i p_jx_j$ and $f$ is the $n$-atomic $q$-Bass map with respect to $\nu$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.988503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_115e2a12adc558c43d807df196757ad2093edbcbec20c37fc242cc67dc886a11","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma thm:factor_hl of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] Let $\tau_1,\ldots,\tau_{\binom{n}{k}} \in S_n$ be a set of coset representatives for $S_n/(S_k \times S_{n-k})$, let $\mu \in \Sig_k, \nu \in \Sig_{n-k}$, and define
