{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.350619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_119529981a8cafbd64da62d0914713ddd2d6ac235059c5e81bd6ed626b192f2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 (Universality of persistence on triangulable spaces) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $M \subset \RR^D$ be an admissibly triangulable space, let $f: M \rightarrow \RR_{\ge 0}$ be a good density, and let $\filt$ be either the Vietoris-Rips or \v Cech filtration. Then the following holds independently of $M$ and $f$:
