{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.816150+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_119a6ea5a790a55187be3c5e0de25c3ee7b234d8a7bf422dc713e98d4a71e43f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:mpinformal of arXiv:2411.09516, 'Sharp Matrix Empirical Bernstein Inequalities\footnote{NeurIPS 2025 Poster}'] Let $n$ be even and $ \mathbf{X} _1,\dots ,  \mathbf{X} _n$ be i.i.d.\ symmetric matrices with eigenvalues in $[0,1]$ and mean $ \mathbf{M} $. Let $ \mathbf{V} _n^*$ be the paired sample variance  $n^{-1}(( \mathbf{X} _1 -  \mathbf{X} _2 )^2+ ( \mathbf{X} _3 -  \mathbf{X} _4 )^2+ \dots + ( \mathbf{X} _{n-1} -  \mathbf{X} _n )^2)$. Then,
