{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.304367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11a07a4f1faeb54a1588f92131bec61dbbb052be944039140efdd919703a6169","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 53 (Backwards-time propagation of test functions in $d \geq 3$) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Let $d\ge 3$. Assume $\x_N=(x^1_N,x^2_N)$ is any sequence such that $N^{-1/2}x_N^1 \to x_1$ and $x^1_N-x^2_N$ converges to $y\in I$ (\textit{without} any normalization), and consider the same setting as Assumption \ref{ass:SRI}. 
      Consider smooth bounded functions $\phi_1, ..., \phi_m : \mathbb R^d\to \mathbb R$ with globally bounded and continuous first and second partial derivatives, and consider $f^1,..., f^m : I\to \mathbb R$ continuous of exponential decay at infinity. Then \begin{align} 
