{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.621580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11a343c7218e5849129d4883c016866ecbe0634e109e4eadda7b1e34f461ec69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 (Elementary symmetric functions of the principal curvatures) of arXiv:2605.11995, 'Intrinsic volumes of \(\ell_p\)-balls and a continuum of Maxwell--Poincar\'e--Borel laws f'] Fix a point $x\in \partial K_n$ such that $x_i\neq 0$ for all $i=1,\ldots,n$.
