{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.075033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11b9264a0cc41fd58c4f3a8fdc5477bdf4f0a690001508d511cde9dc152dcd77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2510.26216, 'A functional Breuer-Major theorem with Poisson noise'] Suppose $M\in\NN$. For $i=1,\dots,N$, let $\Upsilon_i$ be a distribution on $\RR$. Fix an even function $\zeta\in \sS(\RR)$ with $\zeta(0)=1$. Then for any $\beta\in(0,1)$, we have
