{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.598395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11c1a31e0cdf6fa82cf007fb052274ff2dd05638bf5f011a44b30ecf9271d9a3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:exp-decay of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] In the same setting as in Theorem~(thm:main of the paper), for every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists a random constant $D_\varepsilon(\omega,u_0)$ satisfying $D_\varepsilon \in (0,1]$, $\mathbb{P}\times \mu$ almost surely, and a closed random subspace $F(\omega,u_0)\subset L^2_{*}$ with $\mathrm{codim}\,F(\omega,u_0) = m \in (0,\infty)$, such that for all $ \varrho_{0} \in L^{2}_{*}$ we have for all $t\geqslant 0$
