{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.479154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_121b9d27231a435b3af758df9f78505e72bce9161744b3b3dcf0be1390248f7c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:properce of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $E_{\mathcal{N}} : \mathcal{M} \to \mathcal{N}$ a conditional expectation with respect to $\sigma$. Then $E_{\mathcal{N}}$ is self-adjoint with respect to the $s$-inner product $\langle \cdot ,\cdot \rangle_{\sigma,s}$ for any $s \in [0,1]$, where the inner product $\langle \cdot ,\cdot \rangle_{\sigma,s}$ is defined as in (equation def:s-inner of the paper). It follows that $E_{\mathcal{N}}$ commutes with the modular automorphism group:
