{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.309414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_121bd1ff4288578cafc0b9d19edbdd1b1b357e3fb469c86e78ec50ec00934259","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2604.07697, 'Stochastic fractional heat equation with general rough noise'] (\cite[Proposition 2.3]{HHLNT2017})
   Let $\Lambda_{H}$ be the space of predictable processes $g$ defined on $\mathbb{R}_{+}\times\mathbb{R}$ such that almost surely $g\in\mathfrak{H}$ and $\mathbb{E}[\|g\|_{\mathfrak{H}}^2]<\infty$.  Then,  the following items hold.
