{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.592820+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_123dbd06f8cd78c05e47651ab68ae41d42313c49842a9d393120ee0b4360368b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-2 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] For each~$b\ge2$ there exists a continuous function $\kappa\colon(0,\ffrac12)\times\mathbb R_+\to\mathbb R_+$ satisfying
