{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.843353+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_124662669c975652585406eb168ad5f428e441b696b67077d8b8383b6ded1a4e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:preliminaries of arXiv:2607.07598, 'Universal Central Limit Theorem for non-exchangeable interacting diffusions'] Suppose Assumption (assum.main of the paper) holds with $k \ge 0$. Then:
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item \emph{(Well-posedness)} For every $n\in{\mathbb{N}}$, the system (equation eq:X of the paper) admits a unique strong solution on $[0,T]$. Moreover, the McKean-Vlasov equation (equation eq:MKV of the paper) admits a unique strong solution $(Y_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$. In particular, the measure flow $(\mu_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ is uniquely determined.


				\item \emph{(Uniform moment bounds)}
				For every $p\in[1,\infty)$, we have
				\begin{align} 
