{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.565286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_125e522bea159b3e70e2d7e48f2c87eb58680fc33a0fa318e3ca5e2fb1214c3a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 35 of arXiv:2608.26068, 'All once-extended 3D TQFTs are Reshetikhin--Turaev theories'] Let $\Gamma$ be a ribbon graph with partial ribbon-colouring $\mathbf{K}$. Let $T$ be a ribbon subtree whose edges are uncoloured. Then $\mathbf{K}$ induces a (partial) ribbon-colouring $\mathbf{K}_{/T}$ of $\Gamma/T$.

