{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.868115+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_127076e046dc7b444474eeb63b6fd63c856ab6a61bcc9bc0399095257be0bcb4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2609.02040, '\Large Quantum Landau Damping with Coulomb Repulsion in the Whole Space'] For any $\h\in[0,1]$, it holds
		\begin{equation}
			\sabs{\hatGr_\h(t,k)} \leq C \, \tfrac{\n{k}^3}{\weight{k}^4} \, e^{-\sigma\n{k}t}
		\end{equation}
		for some $C,\sigma>0$ independent of $k$ and $\h$. Moreover,
		\begin{equation}
			\n{\hatGr_\h(t,k) - \hatGr_0(t,k)} \le C \, \tfrac{\n{k}^3}{\weight{k}^4} \, e^{-\sigma\n{k}t} \min(1, h^2 |k|^2) \, .
		\end{equation}
		In addition, for $t>0$, $k\neq0$, and every multi-index $\n{\alpha}\leq2$,
		\begin{align}
			\n{\partial_k^\alpha\hatGr_\h(t,k)}
