{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.635777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_129e6fde1ceba75cf2fca37ffe90adc1ad05dcd77bc91288481aecc61d40e7a1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l4.1 of arXiv:2603.14447, '\Large \bf Backward doubly stochastic differential equations with and without reflection u'] \sl
		Let the conditions \(\textbf{(A2)}\) and \(\textbf{(G2)}\) be satisfied. Moreover, let \( C >0 \) be a constant, \(a:[0,T] \longmapsto \mathbb{R}_+ \) and \( b: [0,T]\longmapsto \mathbb{R}_+\) be two non-negative functions, such that for all \((t,y,z)\in [0,T]\times\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}^d\), 
		\begin{align*}
			|f(t,y,z)|\leqslant a_t+b_t|y|+C|z|^2.
