{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.936773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12a0a2cceb91099783e0eb83334a0bb2e6dac998e083647dede54d0af0c3790b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Strato of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Let $r\in (0,1]$ and $0\leqslant \theta_1 \leqslant \theta_2 \leqslant 2\pi$. The parallel transport of $A$ along $\theta_1\xrightarrow r \theta_2$ is defined as the strong solution of the Stratonovich SDE 
