{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.165256+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12a759001237b2852956e705901f05913e0c6294ee585bf200da027cf1593a52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:free-energy of arXiv:2608.30829, 'Free energy and phase transition for\\ 2D directed polymers with critical spatial correlat'] Suppose that Assumption~(main-assumption of the paper) holds. 
  Then, as \(\beta\downarrow 0\), we have that
  \[
   \mathtt{F}(\beta) = 
   \begin{cases}
    - \exp\Big( - (1+o(1))\, \mathscr{C}_h \, \beta^{-2}  \Big)  &\quad\text{ if (equation finite-sum of the paper) holds,}\\
