  The constants \(\mathscr{C}_h\) and \(\mathscr{C}_a\) are explicit, given by $\mathscr{C}_h = \frac{\pi}{\Sigma_h}$ and \(\mathscr{C}_a = ((a+2) 2^{(a-1)/2} \,z_a)^{2/(a+2)}\), where \(z_a\) is the first zero of the following Bessel function of the first kind
  \begin{equation}

    J_{\alpha} (z) \coloneqq \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{(-1)^n}{\Gamma(n+\alpha+1) n!}\Big(\frac{z}{2}\Big)^{2n+\alpha} \qquad \text{ with } \alpha \coloneqq \frac{a+1}{a+2} -1 >-1 \,.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.319380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12aa203e208030caea363028535b319fe221a8344b6284d8347122b07a05af56","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 32 (Continuity and endpoint limits) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For fixed $a > 0$, the map $p \mapsto \nu^{\SG}_{\max}(p,a)$ is continuous on $(0, 1/2)$, and
