{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.733028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12ac907dbcdf2df4b3898bca38491b586bb058dd3fdee2f690499ef864cb83a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition realizing-symplectic-surface.prop of arXiv:2609.00163, 'Decompositions and diagrams of symplectic surfaces in Weinstein domains'] There is a realizing symplectic surface $S(U,\nu)$ properly embedded in $(W,\omega)$, constructed from the transverse banded link $(U,\nu)\subset (\Lambda, k)$ via the steps below.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Consider the pair $(B^4, D)$ of a collection of symplectic 2-disks $D$ bounded by the max-$sl$  unlink with $|U|$ connected components in $\partial B^4$; such disks are provided by Proposition~(uniquedisks.prop of the paper).
    \item Attach $k$ Weinstein 1-handles to $B^4$ away from the boundary unlink of to get the pair \mbox{$(\natural^k S^1 \times B^3,   D)$.}  Identify $\partial D$ with $U$ via a transverse isotopy.
    \item Concatenate the surfaces $S_\nu$ in $(\#^k S^1\times S^2)\times [0,1]$ corresponding to the bands $\nu$ to obtain the pair \mbox{$(\natural^k S^1 \times B^3, s(U,\nu))$.}      
    \item Attach Weinstein 2-handles to $\#^k S^1\times S^2$ along the components $\Lambda_i$ of $\Lambda$ away from the boundary $U[\nu]$ of $s(U,\nu)$. Extend the surface into the cobordism by attaching $(\{t\} \times U[\nu])$ to $s(U,\nu)$. This gives the pair $( W, S(U,\nu))$.  
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.344823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12ad9e93cc2a40498977860cd31b377addb877ad7c176c80f74948e80cbb7342","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2604.20631, 'The Ising Model on a Two-Community Stochastic Block Model'] Let $(\alpha_n)_{n\in\N}\in (0,1]$ such that $\lim_{n\to\infty}\alpha_n=0$, and for $\beta>\beta^*(\alpha_n)$, 
