{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.429553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12e62533be1f0dc8178da9b7f90e32fbe7765fa942d1babfb29f096f391c27d8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dual_identity of arXiv:2604.20094, 'Persistence and local extinction for superprocesses in random environments'] Let $X$ solve (equation eq:MP of the paper) with $\mu\in {\mathcal M}_\rho({\mathbb R}^d)$, independent of $Y^{(n)}$. For any $t\geqslant 0$ and $\phi\in \Phi_\rho$,
