{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.852967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_132f4599edc4dd30b850681f255c1add51fb83f2644e3432fb1e687e2d5bab81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:general of arXiv:2509.16694, 'A central limit theorem for two-dimensional directed polymers with critical spatial correl'] Let $\{Z_N\}_{N \in {\mathbb N}}$ and $\{Z_{k,M,N}\}_{1 \le k \le M, \, M , \, N \in {\mathbb N}}$ be respectively a sequence of positive random variables and an array of random variables with mean one and finite variance, satisfying the following conditions:        \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
            \item  \emph{Independence:} for $M,N\in\mathbb N$, $\{Z_{k,M,N}\}_{ 1 \le k\leq M}$ is a collection of independent random variables.    
            \item \emph{Decoupling in $L^2$:} for $M\in\mathbb N$, $Z_N$ admits a multiplicative approximation in $L^2$, i.e.\ \begin{equation}

             Z_N - \prod_{k=1}^{M} Z_{k,M,N} \xrightarrow[N \to \infty]{L^2} 0\,.
            \end{equation}        
    \end{enumerate}
    Moreover, denoting the centered variables $U_{k,M,N}:=Z_{k,M,N}-1$, we assume:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), start=3]
        \item  \emph{Second moment convergence:} there exists $\sigma_M^2>0$ and $\sigma^2>0$ such that
        \begin{equation}

        \lim_{N \to \infty} \sum_{k=1}^M \mathbb{E} \big[ U_{k,M,N}^2 \big] = \sigma_M^2\,, \, \ \text{for }M \in {\mathbb N} \qquad \text{and} \qquad \lim_{M \to \infty} \sigma_M^2 = \sigma^2\,.
        \end{equation}
        \item  \emph{Lyapunov condition:}
        \begin{equation} \exists \, \varepsilon_0>0 : \quad \limsup_{M\to\infty} \,\limsup_{N\to \infty}\, \sum_{k=1}^M \mathbb{E}\big[ \big|U_{k,M,N}\big|^{2+\varepsilon_0} \big]=0\,.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}
Then, $\log Z_N \, \stackrel{{ (d)}}{\longrightarrow} \, \mathcal{N}\left(-\frac{\sigma^2}{2},\sigma^2\right)\,.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.221281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_132f82cc2e76668055ddce5731866738d09cd4ae76d93abac1e72686cc1f10d2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 17 of arXiv:2608.13976, 'Boundary Harnack principle for diffusion with jumps on metric measure spaces'] Suppose that ${\rm \bf (\wh{Jt})}_{\leq, \bar r, \gamma}$ holds  with   $\bar r>0$ and $\gamma>0.$ Then there is a constant $C=C(\bar r, \gamma)\in  (0,\infty)$
