{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.877883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_134afda77ff8f257a52c100212a1cba3bcdb7742af64d7cddab33bc0dc068c1e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm|forComputer of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] The following two implications hold for every $\omega\in\Omega$.
