{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.134396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_135eea98d2ffd700677ef95b049e7c6af8f3f56f162a537d9c53dfec2da36a5a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro:number_of_steps_and_size_of_trace_of_SRW_are_comparable_on_nonamenable_graphs of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Given a nonamenable and transitive graph $G$, for any $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists $c(\varepsilon) > 0$ such that for any $t > 0$ we have
