{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.677446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1362a643354d9e93ef0365724371968286084bc4c5e91a279555461e85e31e21","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $f:X \longrightarrow Y$ be an almost covering map from a closed topological $n$-manifold $X$ to a closed topological $n$-pseudomanifold $Y$. Let $R$ be the fibered set of $f$ and suppose the restriction $f|_{f^{-1}(R)}:f^{-1}(R)\longrightarrow R$ is a fiber bundle with fiber $F$. Set $B:=f^{-1}(R)$. Assume $R$ and $F$ are closed topological manifolds, the normal bundle of $B$ in $X$ exists and is orientable, and the link of every $x\in B$ in $X$ is homeomorphic to a sphere. Let $k:B\hookrightarrow X$ and $i:X\setminus B\hookrightarrow X$ be the inclusion maps. Then the distinguished triangle
