{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.315080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1362fd9c796f24ada853a1e9170f289df0ec9eb36cfe5c863f360590fc634d46","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor graph-diam-giant of arXiv:2606.01627, 'The geometry of the giant component of random geometric graphs'] Let $\lambda_0 > \lambda_c$. There exist constants $C=C(\lambda_0,M), c=c(\lambda,M)>0$ such that
