{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.162199+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_137d7c5553b2dd9a1baed65c09d90cc2e578496c03c4e1f1d40edcd44d71ac78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.17302, 'Elephant random walk with attributed steps and extractions of random sizes'] Consider Scenario~\eqref{Scenario_2}. We consider the following different regimes:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(E\arabic*), ref=E\arabic*]
\item  Suppose that \eqref{thm:C_{n}_a.s.:g_C^{2}} and \eqref{contraction_criterion_g} are satisfied, and, almost surely as $n\rightarrow\infty$, 
\begin{equation}
\text{either }\sum_{i=N}^{n}\E[K_{i}^{-1}]=o(\sqrt{n/\log n}) \quad \text{or} \quad \sum_{i=N}^{n}\E[K_{i}^{-1}](i+1)^{-1/2}=o(\sqrt{\log n}).
