{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.300058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_137fe6fcf83833464f1f55c4c69da0d05060231a0e398afada8ce7e6ea22f06c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:b-geodesics of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] If $b$ is a finite eternal solution, then for $(x,t) \in \mathbb{R}^2$, define the functions $g_{(x,t)}^{b,L},g_{(x,t)}^{b,R}:(-\infty,t] \to \mathbb{R}$ as follows: For $s < t$, let $g_{(x,t)}^{b,L/R}(s)$ be the leftmost/rightmost maximizers of the function
