{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.723760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1382402ae0aff235634c0540c2a553d1fe37fafb0bae5047cefe022cdfb74266","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn triangleW of arXiv:2606.02340, 'Transitivity in Inhomogeneous Random Tournaments'] Given a tournamenton $W$, the 2-point conditional homomorphism density function for the clockwise oriented circular triad $(\cc)$ is defined as: 
For $x, y \in [0, 1]$, 
\begin{align*}
    t_{W}(\cc, x, y) &= \mathbb{E}\left[ W(\eta_1, \eta_2) W(\eta_2, \eta_3) W(\eta_3, \eta_1) \mid \eta_{1}=x, \eta_2 = y \right].     \\ 
&= W(x,\,y)\int_0^1W(y,\,z)W(z,\,x)\mathrm{d}z  .
\end{align*}  
Similarly, the 2-point conditional homomorphism density function for the anti-clockwise oriented circular triad $(\cac)$ is defined as  
\begin{align*}
    t_{W}(\cac, x, y) &= \mathbb{E}\left[ W(\eta_1, \eta_3) W(\eta_3, \eta_2) W(\eta_2, \eta_1) \mid \eta_{1}=x, \eta_2 = y \right].     \\ 
&= W(y,\,x)\int_0^1W(x,\,z)W(z,\,y)\mathrm{d}z  =  t_{W}(\cc, y, x).
\end{align*}  
Finally, define {\it symmetrized $2$-point conditional homomorphism density} as: 
\begin{align}
    \triangle_{W}(x,\,y) :=\frac{t_{W}(\cc, x, y) + t_{W}(\cac, x, y) }{2} . 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.086409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_138268b232fdf0f971fa2345ea6a48f706275271b991d832b1ac3d75ce3cffbd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 17 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] For fixed {$h \in T/{\mathbb N}^*$} and 
