{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.978420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13d7b92f9c70954b41cd57735d3260bad2e046dc576bf67fee822b261f440288","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Exact primitive kernel) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $q\ge2$ and let $k=[f_n]_{\mathcal U}\in\cH_q$.  The following
conditions are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
 \item $k\in\cK_q$.
 \item For every $1\le r<q$ and every $u=[u_n]\in\cH_r$,
 \begin{equation}
  [f_n\otimes_ru_n]_{\mathcal U}=0.

 \end{equation}
 \item For every $1\le r<q$,
 \begin{equation}
  \Ulim\norm{L_{f_n,r}}_{\op}=0.

 \end{equation}
 \item For every $1\le r<q$,
 \begin{equation}
  \Ulim\norm{f_n\otimes_rf_n}=0.

 \end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Equivalently, if $M_{r,u}v=u\wtensor v$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\displaystyle
 \cK_q=\bigcap_{r=1}^{q-1}\ \bigcap_{u\in\cH_r}
 \Ker M_{r,u}^*.}

\end{equation}

Moreover, if $k=[f_n]\in\cK_p$ and $\ell=[g_n]\in\cK_q$, then
\begin{equation}
 \Ulim\norm{f_n\otimes_rg_n}=0

\end{equation}
for every contraction which is not total, that is, except possibly when
$p=q=r$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.990457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13d84a259693c2e585b675060fc20792699abbc53dfeb51b1f9ad14394f3dba3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.04579, 'Solvable Families of Random Block Tridiagonal Matrices'] Suppose that $\mathbf{M}$ is an ${\mathbb{F}}$-Hermitian $rn\times rn$ matrix.
 We define the spectral measure of $\mathbf{M}$ with respect to $\mathbf{e}_{[\![r ]\!]}$ as the $r\times r$ matrix-valued measure
\begin{align*}
 \mu_{[\![r ]\!]}=\sum_{j=1}^{rn} \mathbf{v}_{j,[\![r ]\!]} \cdot \mathbf{v}_{j,[\![r ]\!]}^{\dag} \delta_{\lambda_j}.
\end{align*}
Here $\mathbf{v}_{j}$ is the normalized eigenvector corresponding to $\lambda_j$, and
