{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.090333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13d8eb88edef1c3845c29d345810189669470ef664dd21bbc0f3987a0352f75c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 (Poisson--Dirichlet approximation of the one-step exponents) of arXiv:2604.25877, 'Asymptotic height of Plancherel random trees'] Fix $t>1$. For an integer $k\ge2$, let $(A^{(u)}_i)_{1\le i\le d(u)}$ be the multiset of block sizes in the
$\mathrm{Ewens}(k-1,\theta)$ partition at a node $u$ with $K(u)=k$. We define the 

one-step exponent:
\begin{equation*}
\kappa_k(t):=\log\,
\E\!\left[\sum_{i=1}^{d(u)}\left(\frac{A^{(u)}_i}{k-1}\right)^t\ \Big|\ K(u)=k\right].
\end{equation*}
Then as $k\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
\kappa_k(t)\longrightarrow \kappa(t)=\log\beta_t(\theta).
\end{equation}
More precisely, there exists a constant $C=C(t,\theta)<\infty$,
$\gamma=\gamma(\theta)\in(0,1/2]$, and $m_0\ge 2$ such that for all $m\ge m_0$,
\[
\sup_{k\ge m}\,|\kappa_k(t)-\kappa(t)| \le C\,m^{-\gamma}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

