{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.952915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13ef56f31daa4c263c2358c71820b71ee32eaedaa4ec0d8f10749a0527f33f83","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:SW of arXiv:2608.16915, 'Exact mean--covariance dynamics of the Weber field in the stochastic Lagrangian representa'] Let $u$ be a maximal classical periodic solution on $[0,T_*)$, and let
$\bar F=M^\top N+\mathcal R$ as in (equation eq:decomp of the paper), so that $u=\mathbb{P}\bar F$. For
$1<p\le\infty$, $1<q<\infty$ and any interval $I=(\tau,T_*)$,
\begin{equation}
  C_q^{-1}\,\left\lVert u\right\rVert_{L^p(I;L^q)}
  \ \le\ \Bigl\|\,t\mapsto\left\lVert [\bar F(t)]\right\rVert_{L^q/\nabla W^{1,q}}\Bigr\|_{L^p(I)}
  \ \le\ \left\lVert u\right\rVert_{L^p(I;L^q)} .
\end{equation}
If $q>3$ and $2/p+3/q\le1$, finiteness of the middle quantity implies that $u$ extends
past $T_*$; the same conclusion holds at the endpoint $(p,q)=(\infty,3)$ by the
backward-uniqueness theorem of Escauriaza, Seregin and \v Sver\'ak
[EscauriazaSereginSverak2003], whose localization to the periodic setting is
standard.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.846358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13ef74022ada12ae16f4bac93880bd16975c505e6730b8dc1b0366fb17331053","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 26 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] In the setting of Definition \ref{tech1}, for any monomial $M$ (with coefficient 1) in non-commutative variables $(X_{i,I})_{i\in [1,d],I\in J_n}$ we have
