{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.856946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1400c4b769274eec2e73d4319e4930f36e066856cb733ee88c529658b414ac52","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 15 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] A set $\mathcal Q$ is called a semi-ring if
