{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.589710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_142ae7ddbc42d671b22f0d3be4ea41e09c6e0ac15576b4b7cd3157f570af6d2c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:FJ2 of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] Let $1 \le p \le \infty$  and $\ell_1, \ell_2, m_1, m_2$ be integers such that $\ell_1 \le m_1$ and $\ell_2 \le m_2$. Assume that $g_{\bar{k}}$, $\bar{k} \in \mathbb{Z}^2$, are functions satisfying the following inequality 
\begin{equation}
\forall {\boldsymbol{x}} \in \mathbb{R}^2, \, \vert g_{\bar{k}}(\boldsymbol{x}) \vert \le \frac{C}{\left( 1+2^{\min(\ell_1,m_1)}|x_1 - 2^{-m_1}k_1 \vert \right)^2 \left( 1+2^{\min(\ell_2,m_2)}|x_2 - 2^{-m_2}k_2 \vert \right)^2}.
\end{equation}
for some $C>0$. If one sets  
$$
F = \sum_{\bar{k} \in \mathbb{Z}^2} d_{\bar{k}} g_{\bar{k}},
$$
then
\begin{equation}
\Vert F \Vert_{L^p} \le C \, 2^{-(m_1+m_2)/p} 2^{m_1-\ell_1}2^{m_2 - \ell_2} \left( \sum_{\bar{k} \in \mathbb{Z}^2} \vert d_{\bar{k}} \vert^p \right)^{1/p}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.656327+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_142daae4dc8fada88604a383d50a9bcc157a20d93d3a8f0594c02410cc41567a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:valid of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] A bounded, simply connected domain $D$ is \emph{valid} if
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item $\dim_M(\partial D)<2-\alpha^2/2$, when considering $\field{e^{i\alpha\phi}}$ or $\cos(\alpha\phi)$;
        \item $\mathrm{Leb}(\partial D)=0$, when considering $:\! \sin(\alpha\phi) \!: $.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.644175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_142e5b9a5e21e155af54472d06ed39204a85ccb0f8cb718295aae8a8f6eec709","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop existence of plus state extremal of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\beta_0,h_0\geq 0$. There exist $a_0,b_0>0$ such that the following properties hold for $\beta\leq \beta_0$ and $\mathsf{h}\in (\mathbb R^+)^{\mathbb Z^d}$ such that $\mathsf{h}\leq h_0$. 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[$(i)$] The measures $\nu_{\Lambda, \beta,\mathsf{h}}$ are $(a_0,b_0)$-regular for every finite $\Lambda\subset \mathbb Z^d$. In addition, they converge to a measure $\nu_{\beta,\mathsf{h}}\in \mathcal{G}(\beta,\mathsf{h})$ as $\Lambda\nearrow \mathbb Z^d$. We call $\nu_{\beta,\mathsf h}$ the infinite volume free measure at parameters $(\beta, \mathsf h)$.
    \item[$(ii)$] There exists a measure $\nu^+_{\beta,\mathsf{h}} \in \mathcal{G}(\beta,\mathsf{h})$ which is maximal, extremal, and $(a_0,b_0)$-regular. We call $\nu^+_{\beta,\mathsf{h}}$ the infinite volume plus measure at parameters $(\beta,\mathsf{h})$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.764640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_142efc13ff8b9b0a8abc677a88d1b74e8d72c5ec6548eb072d41d353ea97605f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:8' of arXiv:2508.21658, 'Infinite-dimensional stochastic differential equations for Coulomb random point fields'] For $ \mu $-a.s.\,$ \aaa $ and $ m \in \zN $, the following hold: 
