{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.594826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1438e5596b938dad3909e8a6d66694b7a66860ed0daee28f3a188b39c07e0378","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor-5.3 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Let~$\beta>0$ and~$\alpha\in\mathbb R$ and let $\{w_k\}_{k=1}^{ n+1}$ be defined by (equation Eq:5.2 of the paper) with
\begin{equation}

w_1(q):=
\sqrt{\frac{2\pi\sigma_0^2}\beta}
\,\frac{a(q)}{a_0(0)}\,\theta_0^{(q+\alpha)^2},\quad q\in\mathbb Z,
\end{equation}
where $\{a(q)\}_{q\in\mathbb Z}$  denote the Fourier coefficients of~$\nu$.
Let~$\{f_k\}_{k=1}^{ n+1}$ be defined from $\{w_k\}_{k=1}^{ n+1}$ as in (equation Eq:5.2b of the paper). Then $w_k(\cdot)$ is strictly positive for all~$k=1,\dots,n+1$  and
\begin{equation}

\langle\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{2\pi\text{\rm  i}\mkern0.7mu\alpha(\phi_x-\phi_y)}\rangle_{n,\beta} = E\bigl(\,|f_k(\phi_k)|^2\bigr)
