{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.233139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_148479e5cb882b71408a8016d720b2a0e4a7c2d5b50ac78825e359f4024216de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 57 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\rho$ be a separable unital representation whose support is a perfect subset of $\hat{\A}$ for the Fell topology: that is, it has no isolated points.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[a.] If another separable unital representation $\pi$ weakly contains $\rho$, then $\pi \gtrsim_\rm{a} \rho$.
\item[b.] If another separable unital representation $\pi$ is weakly equivalent to $\rho$, then ${\pi \simeq_\rm{a} \rho}$.
\item[c.] If a sequence $(\pi_n)_{n\ge 1}$ converges to $\rho$ strongly, then $\t{\pi_n}$ sq-converges to $\t{\rho}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

