{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.196730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_148874a4c12a5832bec6f3cbca14794d29169de8a36a195266bc113f99891f6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cpts-length of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $\varepsilon, \delta \in (0, 1)$, and $A, B$ with $B \in \ensuremath{\mathcal Y}_\delta^\blacktriangleleft(A)\setminus \{A\}$. Let $V$ be an $\varepsilon$-nice domain, and $U$ any domain. There exists $\beta_0, v_0, \delta_0, c > 0$ such that uniformly over $n$, $\beta \geq \beta_0$, and $r \geq 1 + 2\varepsilon$, we have
