{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.769011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14b7d6cbdf5bfdeec6694923772b6eeee3f91dd3ab526e1b99d630c9690ae4a6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lA4cor of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] For any $q\in(0,p)$
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\sup_{t\in[t_k, t_{k+1})}\mathbf{E}^{(N)}_{t_1,\dots,t_N}\Big[\|\Delta_t^n\|^q\Big|\mathcal{F}_{t_k-}\Big]
&\leq_C \|\Delta_{t_k-}^n\|^q\\
&+h_n^{\frac{p-q}{\chi}\wedge q}(1+\|X_{t_k-}^{(n)}\|^p)
+ h_n^{\frac{p-q}{\chi}\wedge q}(1+\|X_{t_k-}^n\|^{p})\\
&+ (U^n_{t_k-})^q
+h_n^{1\wedge \frac{q}2}(U_{t_k-}^n)^{(p-q)\wedge (q\chi)}+h_n^{1\wedge \frac{q}2}
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
for $n$ large enough uniformly over
$N\in\mathbb{N}$, partitions $\{t_1,\dots, t_N\}$,  and $k=1, \dots, N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.380741+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14b86924e1f45eee397b1ec07dfef4423f4353ffa8509cba55715dc317b83c04","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 27 (FK-triangulation of a simplex) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $\sigma \subset \RR^D$ be an affine $d$-simplex with an ordering of vertices given by $v^\sigma_\bullet = (v_0^\sigma, \ldots v_d^\sigma)$. The $k$-th FK-triangulation of $(\sigma, v^\sigma_\bullet)$ is defined as follows:
    \begin{align*}
        \FK_k(\sigma, v^\sigma_\bullet) \eqdef \phi_* \big( \mathsf{FK}(\RR^d)|_{k \cdot \ordsimp{d}} \big)
    \end{align*}
    where the FK-triangulation on $k \cdot \ordsimp{d}$ is described by \eqref{eqn:fkt_kfold_simplex}, $\phi$ is the affine linear map defined by setting $\phi(k \cdot (\vecbf e_1 + \cdots + \vecbf e_i)) = v_i^\sigma$ for every $i = 0, 1, \ldots d$, and $\phi_*$ denotes the pushforward. This triangulation is independent of the linear embedding $\sigma \hookrightarrow \RR^D$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.303766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14ba961d4050e5e43c1139b7ed627d88498ac49617dfe0dab3916a2fe85e01e2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma pitdef of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] Suppose $\textup{\texttt{slope}}_m (h)> \textup{\texttt{slope}}_{m+1} (h)$ and recall $\sigma^m$  defined in (equation qmap of the paper).
