{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.639717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14da87172e567e5febb6393faf1ad26e0ef4998534e8ecaa65cc2e3f058ea6bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm THeorem:varphi_hatvarphi solution to Schrodinger system of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Assume that the conditions of Theorem (Theorem:DensityKunita of the paper) are satisfied, and suppose that the Schr\"odinger system (equation Equation:fgSchrodingerSystem of the paper) admits solutions $\mathfrak{f},\mathfrak{g}$ that are non-negative, measurable and bounded functions with compact support. Then the functions $\varphi,\hat\varphi$ given by (equation Equation:phi-definition of the paper), (equation Equation:phihat-definition of the paper) are of class $C^{1,\infty}$ and the pair $(\varphi,\hat\varphi)$ solves the system of PIDEs
