{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.545003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14df95f1cb53383af1f9d7d7b05d2222243a51f1268d4af2a79f334f71185593","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: mu_A reconstruction theorem of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Consider a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-valued nearest-neighbor clock model with Hamiltonian given in (equation def: Hamiltonian of the paper) and a potential defined in (equation eq: Potential ferr n.n. model of the paper) fulfilling the $u,U,d$-bounds in (equation eq: u,U-bounds of the paper). Furthermore, let $A\subsetneq \mathbb{Z}_q$ with $|A|\geq 2$ and $\beta$ be large enough. Then, the $A$-localized state $\mu_A$ for this model, see Proposition (prop: Bounds A-loc. states of the paper), satisfies the following bound
\begin{equation}
    \mu_A\bigg(\big\{\omega:~\pi(\sigma_\rho=a|\omega)< 1-\epsilon_1(\beta)\big\}\bigg| \sigma_\rho=a\bigg) \leq 2|A|\epsilon_2(\beta)
\end{equation}
for any $a\in A$. Here, $\epsilon_1(\beta)\downarrow 0$ and $\epsilon_2(\beta)\downarrow 0$ as $\beta \uparrow \infty$ and both quantities were introduced in Lemma (lem: Key Lemma of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.511306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14e2942a36c66b1758662026df235e57e6edaa2d6688e6fea0bca7b605704158","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (Cumulants and endpoint behavior) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] For every integer $n\geq1$ such that
$\int |x|^{n+2}\nu(\dd x)<\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \E R_X^n=\frac{2\kappa_{n+2}(X)}{(n+1)(n+2)V}.

\end{equation}
In particular, when the third cumulant is finite,
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X)\geq\pos{\frac{\kappa_3}{3V}},
 \qquad
