{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.756210+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14f19d75dd289d33c25379b4da51f142804f9e7cd5c3ba6de577d7c203513e7e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2609.02218, 'Neumaier graphs of coherent rank five'] Let $n\geqslant8$ and $m\geqslant3$. 
Suppose $H$ is a Hadamard matrix of order $n$ with first row $h_1=\one^\transpose$, and let $\bL$ be a family of $m$ MALS of order $n-1$. 
Let $A$ be the adjacency matrix of $\Gamma(H;\bL)$.
Then
\[
 A^2
 =
 \left ((m-1)\frac{n(n-1)}2+n(n-2)\right )A_0+\mu_{A_1}A_1+\lambda_{A_2}A_2
 +\mu_{A_3}A_3+\lambda_{A_4}A_4,
\]
where
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
 \lambda_{A_2}
 &=(m-2)\frac{n^2}{4}+n(n-2),
 &\lambda_{A_4}
 &=(m-1)\frac{n(n-1)}4+n(n-3),\\
 \mu_{A_1}
 &=(m-1)\frac{n(n-2)}4+n(n-2),
 &\mu_{A_3}
 &=(m-2)\frac{n(n-2)}4+n(n-2).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
