{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.570682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15085b78f743f9723e4334b6188b6feff0462619426ccb0afef751c9e784c89c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2605.30869, 'Approximate Transitivity of Young Translation on Rough Paths'] Let $\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y} \in \mathcal{C}^{p\text{-var}}_{\mathbf{1}}$. Then there exists  a sequence of paths $(h^n)\subset  C^{\infty}_0$ such that $(\mathbf X\boxplus h^n)$ converges uniformly to $\mathbf{Y}$ and for any $p'>p$ one has
	 \begin{equation}
\rho_{p'\text{-var}}(\mathbf X\boxplus h^n,\mathbf{Y} )\to 0 \,.
	\end{equation}
	Moreover if $\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}\in \mathcal{C}^{0,p\text{-var}}_{\mathbf{1}}$ the sequence $(h^n) $ can be chosen  such that
	 \begin{equation}
\rho_{p\text{-var}}(\mathbf{X} \boxplus h^n, \mathbf{Y}) \to 0\,.
\end{equation}
If in addition $\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y} \in \mathcal{C}^{\alpha}$, then $(h^n)$ can be chosen such that \eqref{eq:weak_conv_Y} and \eqref{eq:strong_conv_Y} hold with the metrics $\rho_{\alpha'}$ for any $\alpha'<\alpha$, and $\rho_{\alpha}$ in the case $\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y} \in \mathcal{C}^{0;\alpha}_{\mathbf{1}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.609480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1508b49ea6b0cf157ae5c7c98354190cf07757f5806b19763b7f2e30c8710432","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 14 of arXiv:2607.08314, 'Berry-Heisenberg random waves'] Let $G$ be a separable, locally compact group of type I. A function $B: G \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}$ is positive definite if and only if it can be represented as 
    \begin{equation}
        B(g) = \operatorname{Tr} \left( \pi (g)  F(\widehat{G} ) \right),
    \end{equation}
    where $\widehat{G}$ denotes the unitary dual of $G$,  $\pi$ is a unitary representation of $G$ acting on the Hilbert space $H_{\pi}$, and $F$ is a positive operator-valued measure over $\widehat{G}$, whose values are  Hermitian non-negative definite operators on the representation space $H_{\pi}$, such that 
    \begin{align}
       \operatorname{Tr} \left( F(\widehat{G}) \right) = \Vert \xi_0 \Vert_{H_{\pi}}^{2} < \infty,
    \end{align}
    where $\xi_{0} \in H_{\pi}$ is given by \eqref{eqn.pos.def.fun1}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.415291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_150d82d6ed243bc399cff3478e3599d4978af90c956f048a99d3f4834357f844","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma closedness conditions of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] The following are equivalent:
