{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.713323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1527036f739981ffc1a3a054144253135a98f467959165dbc320c28c4dba516a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:clt-upper of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $p_n(x,y)$ and $\widetilde{p}_n(x,y)$ be the $n$-step transition probability given by the Markov chain in Definition (defmodel of the paper), with profile functions $f$ and $\widetilde{f}$  satisfying the assumptions in Definition~(ass:ft of the paper).
