for every $i\in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket$ and every $\alpha,\beta\in \llbracket 1,n \rrbracket$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.209452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_152a04813afc9c2f9319348a9def9425aa922b658274a522ae36d9dbaa0199fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-graded-com of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] For any cochains $\phi \in \mathcal{W}^p(X, \lambda)$ and $\psi \in \mathcal{W}^q(X, \lambda)$, we have 
