{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.303478+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_152ce037eec04776849b0e035c4533ba10d20faad4671afe3be31442bd852f2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:JSQ_random_pool of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] Suppose there exist $(\mu_1, \ldots, \mu_m)$ such that the limiting service rate distribution and the limiting initial distribution can be expressed as $F(\mathbb{A}) = \sum_{j=1}^m \gamma_j \delta_{\mu_j}(\mathbb{A})$, and $\xi_i(0)(\mathbb{A}) = \sum_{j=1}^m X_{j,i}(0) \delta_{\mu_j}(\mathbb{A})$, respectively, for all $\mathbb{A}\in \mathcal{B}$ and $i\geq 2
