{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.191887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15720c0bee26c1df3def9b24db1cb72b52af1401aa44758141b4a65bb2c925cc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 ({\hspace{1pt}\cite[Proposition~1.21) of arXiv:2510.21595, 'One-arm exponents of high-dimensional percolation revisited'] {DewanMuirhead}}] For every $d\geq 2$ and $L\geq 1$, there exists a constant $C_0=C_0(d,L)>0$, such that for every set $\Lambda\subset \mathbb Z^d$ containing $0$, every event $\mathcal{A}$ measurable with respect to $\mathcal C_{\Lambda}(0):=\{x\in \mathbb Z^d:0\connect{\Lambda\:}x\}$, and every $\tfrac{p_c}{2}\leq p'< p\leq \tfrac{p_c+1}{2}$, we have
