{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.725999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_158686f0f855dacca2778c4c9cfe33f74bf8758bd495025897d1dc2a42dd18d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem general_bound of arXiv:2411.04322, 'Bounding Hellinger Distance with Stein's Method'] Let $\mathbf{X}$ be random variable taking values in a Polish-space $\mathcal{X}$ and $g:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a measurable function for which $S\triangleq g(\mathbf{X})$ has convex support $\Omega_S\subseteq\mathbb{R}$, $\mbb{E}[S]=0$, 
$\mrm{Var}(S)=1$, Lebesgue density $f_S\in C^1$, 
and {first and second-order score functions} 
$\score[S],I_S \in\Lp[2](S)$ satisfying $\norm{\score[S](S) S}_2<\infty$.

Fix any $D\in(0,1)$ and any anti-symmetric function $F(\cdot,\cdot):\mathcal{X}^2\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ and, for each $t \geq -\frac{1}{2}\log(1-D)$, 
define $S^t\triangleq g(\mathbf{X}^t)$ where $\mathbf{X}^t$ is an exchangeable copy of $\mathbf{X}$ and
\begin{talign}
\sum_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{e^{-kt}k}{\sqrt{k-1}!\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}^k}\|\mbb{E}[(S^t-S)^{k-1}F(\mathbf{X}^t,\mathbf{X}) \mid S]\|_2< \infty.
\end{talign}

Then, for any $s\in\mathbb{R}$,
we may bound the Hellinger distance

\begin{talign}
 H(S,Z) 
 &\triangleq (\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}}(\sqrt{f_S(x)}-\sqrt{\varphi(x)})^2dx)^{1/2}\\
 &\le\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\int_0^{\infty}\|I_{Z_t}(Z_t)-I_{Z}(Z_t)+Z_t(\score[Z_t](Z_t)-\score[Z](Z_t))\|_2dt
   \\&\le \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}

   \{-\frac{1}{2}\log(1-D)(1+\|\score[S](S)S\|_2)


    +\|\score[S](S)\|_2(\sqrt{\frac{D}{1-D}}-\rm{tan}^{-1}(\sqrt{\frac{D}{1-D}}))\\
&+\frac{D}{1-D}\|I_S(S)\|_2
    + 
\int_{-\frac{1}{2}\log(1-D)}^{\infty}\|\frac{e^{-2t}}{{1-e^{-2t}}}h_2(Z)-\frac{e^{-t}}{\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}}Sh_1(Z)-\tilde\tau_{t,s}\|_2dt\}

\end{talign}
in terms of the Gaussian score functions $\score[Z](z) \triangleq -z$ and $I_Z(z) \triangleq z^2-1$, the interpolants

\begin{talign}
Z_t\triangleq e^{-t}S+\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}Z 
    \ \ \text{with}\ \  
    Z\perp\!\!\!\perp S, 
    \ \ \text{density}\ \ 
f_{Z_t},
    \ \ \text{and}\ \ 
    (\score[Z_t],I_{Z_t}) \triangleq (\frac{\partial_x{f_{Z_t}}}{f_{Z_t}}, 
\frac{\partial_x^2f_{Z_t}}{f_{Z_t}})
\end{talign}
for $t > 0$,  
and the Hermite sum 

\begin{talign}

\tilde\tau_{t,s}
    &\triangleq
\frac{se^{-t}}{\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}}\mbb{E}[F(\mathbf{X}^t,\mathbf{X})\mid S]h_1(Z)+\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{s e^{-kt}}{k!\sqrt{1-e^{-2t}}^k}\mbb{E}[(S^t-S)^{k-1}F(\mathbf{X}^t,\mathbf{X})\mid S]h_k(Z)
\end{talign}
where $h_k(x)\triangleq (-1)^k e^{x^2/2} \frac{\partial^k}{\partial x}e^{-x^2/2}$ designates  the $k$-th Hermite polynomial for $k\in\mathbb{N}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

