{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.100882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_159ae288fe66ce7f4bbe8f1d5d1343ba7511f406eaed4c4b7f31c4b2e5335596","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bounded_metric of arXiv:2608.13716, 'Graph Causal Optimal Transport \\ and Wasserstein Distances'] For a sequence $(\mu^{(m)})_{m \geq 1}$ in $\Gpprobabilities{p}{\mathcal{X}}$, and $\nu \in \Gpprobabilities{p}{\mathcal{X}}$, the following are equivalent:
