{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.647014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15a1281cd6651214b5c9f7ff9442752e2f400a7f824938833453eb59d4951ad7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: solution of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] A random field $\{u(t,x), t\in[0,T], x\in \mathbb R\}$ is called a \emph{mild Skorohod solution} to (equation e:she of the paper), if $\{u(t,\cdot), t\in[0,T]\}$ is adapted to the filtration induced by the noise $\xi$, $u(t,x)$ is $L^1$-integrable for each $(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb R$,  and the following integral equation is satisfied:
