{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.639000+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15afe510153d973e7830d3290e25f755cd1177f60dfdc7edbfd7faf0a2a24a28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2605.31344, 'Subcritical sharpness for real-valued spin models'] Let $\Lambda \subset V$ be finite, and $\beta\geq0$. Let also $\eta_1,\eta_2\in \mathbb R^{V}$ be such that $\eta_1\leq \eta_2$. Then, for any increasing function $F:\mathbb{R}^{\Lambda}\to\mathbb{R}$ we have 
