{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.792301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15b78e48848b95b8bbd425fb2ab919d97e628192c3ce0c7148f482cfda49bd94","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:conv_stopping_time of arXiv:2412.04328, 'The critical Karp--Sipser core of Erdős--Rényi random graphs'] There is $\eta_0>0$ such that the following holds. Let $0<\eta<\eta_0$ and $K>0$, and let $(a_n, b_n, c_n) \in \mathcal{R}^n_{\eta,K}$ for all $n$. Then we have the convergence of conditional distributions
