{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.806120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15c539ec38f190139e0425e48053cb1d5862d2dbcdef29479e4e995279ed573c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition P:Prelimit-2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the process $\theta_t^\varepsilon$ be the solution of (equation E:theta-R-Q of the paper) and the limiting variance $\sigma_t^2$ is defined in equation (equation E:Limiting-Variance of the paper). Then, for any $t \ge 0,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
