{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.197414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15c672ded195b7ef3697b1ed1755b2fa46c1b3f1fe8aaa7ca87b3abd1ae0d4e9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 40 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Fix any probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal F, \P)$ and sub-$\s$-algebra $\mathcal G \subset \mathcal F$. For any $\delta>0$ and  event $A \in \mathcal F$ such that $\mathbb P(A) \geq 1-p_0$, we have 
