{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.840296+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15cb3a365b3be4e212ab4264db7bc523deb269bcd43eb050c9519b3187dbf91e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 (Ultrametric space) of arXiv:2609.03647, 'Extension Problems for the Vladimirov--Taibleson Operator and the Hierarchical Laplacian'] Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space. If the strong triangle inequality
