{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.160591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15cc0c41bf43c143205ef48bdb5d00b5934f169dc9f7378da1706c27699e000c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (The prime $2$ for even parameters) of arXiv:2609.01594, '2609.01594'] Let $A$ be even.  Then $u_n(A)$ is odd exactly when $n$ is odd.  If $n$ is
