{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.427347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15df551167057326745fe01df7331ad16bb9ac60b4c14693e39e5757bafe173a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2508.03577, 'Phase Transitions in a Particle Model\\ for the Self-Adaptive Response to Cancer Dynamics'] Let $\tau$ be the time such that above procedure has selected each row at least once. We then have that for every $\varepsilon_M>\log^{-1/2}(M)$
