{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.665966+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15f22399c937759f6f50af7754be1e82d341c8f087ebfe7d4089b92608ac0b7e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sumovery of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Under the conditions of Theorem (thm:lattice of the paper) there exist numbers $b_\ell^{(h)}$ such that, for every $h=0,1,\dots, r+1,$
