while the deterministic mean-matrix difference converges to a nonzero rank-one perturbation and has a nonvanishing analytic LSS response.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.088959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15fdf047391c03c20cf3a62e7788e1d41e35270233686c08158f372acf8ecec2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Bandeira--Cipolloni--Schr\"oder--van Handel of arXiv:2510.12520, '\Large Strong Convergence: A Short Survey\thanks{Contribution to the Proceedings of the In'] Let $p/2\le\ell<3p/4$ and $d = {\ell\choose p/2}{n-\ell\choose p/2}$.
