for all $z_1,\dotsc,z_q\in\mathcal{Z}$ such that the right-hand side of (equation kerform of the paper) is finite. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.148778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16079874386a01f5e818d10a71da97ddebf1fccd966615971c460be6d9eb7392","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 12 of arXiv:2604.13387, 'Multiradial Schramm-Loewner evolution: \\ Infinite-time large deviations and transience'] The mappings $\tilde \Psi^\kappa_T \colon \Dindpaths[\boldsymbol{nT}] \to [-\infty, \infty)$ defined as 
