	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.326641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1650107460f29125354725ab237d00b41530c179b02ede7994ff5cdde1b912fa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def-bs-topology of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $(M,e)$ and $(\widetilde M , \widetilde e)$ be directed planar maps, each equipped with a (directed) root edge. 
For $r \in \mathbbm N $, define the graph-distance ball $\mathcal B_r(M)$ to be the directed submap of $M$ consisting of the vertices of $M$ which lie at (undirected) graph distance at most $r$ from the initial vertex of $e$, together with the (directed) edges whose vertices both lie in this vertex set and the faces whose boundary vertices all lie in this vertex set. 
Similarly define $\mathcal B_r(\widetilde M)$. The \textbf{Benjamini-Schramm local distance} between $(M,e)$ and $(\widetilde M , \widetilde e)$ is 
\begin{equation*}
D_{\operatorname{loc}}((M,e) , (\widetilde M , \widetilde e)) = \inf\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ 2^{-r} : \mathcal B_r(M) \cong \mathcal B_r(\widetilde M)\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} 
\end{equation*}
where $\cong$ means that the two balls are isomorphic as directed planar maps.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.957550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16503b941834bad9161e34b95161c6f3fb4444777dae6448ca10346d873d2501","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (See Theorems~\ref{thm: transition prob pfaffian kernel} and \ref{thm: transition prob pfaffian kernel initial cond} in the main text) of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $N$ be a fixed even integer and let $x=(x_1,\dots,x_N)$ be the ordered coordinates of half-space TASEP particles. Then the half-line open TASEP has transition probability from an empty state to $x$ is given by the Pfaffian
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}_t(\emptyset\to x) = (-1)^{\binom{N}{2}} \mathrm{e}^{-\alpha t} \Pf \left[\mathsf{Q}\right],
	\end{equation}
    where $\mathsf{Q}$ is a skew-symmetric $N\times N$-dimensional matrix whose entries are given by
    \begin{align*}
        [\mathsf{Q}]_{i,j} := & Q_{i,j}(x_{N-i+1},x_{N-j+1}), 
    \end{align*}
    for all $1\leq i,j\leq N$ and
	\begin{equation}

		Q_{i,j}(x,y) = \alpha^2 \oint_\contour \frac{\dd u}{2\pi\ii} \oint_\contour \frac{\dd w}{2\pi\ii} \frac{u-w}{1-u-w} \frac{w^{i-x}\mathrm{e}^{t(w-1)}}{(w-\alpha)(w-1)^i} \frac{u^{j-y}\mathrm{e}^{t(u-1)}}{(u-\alpha)(u-1)^j},
	\end{equation}
    where the contour $\beta$ surrounds the points $1,0,\alpha$ and $1-\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

