{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.256963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16621e02a2763a1e49c7538b14519aa70f7a1f95bdf3963bc1852e1353d56fb2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition POINT of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] Let \( \overline{\mathcal{A}} = \left\{ \overline{\mathcal{A}}(\omega^-) \right\}_{\omega^- \in \mathcal{B}} \) be defined by
