{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.826051+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16663172ff24a732087d0372bdc66317c695022fda5b08a1f0a3400d678e4001","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:defecttwolattice of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] For every $h\geq2$ and $n\geq1$, the least $D$ for which some
$A\subset[0,D]^n\cap\mathbb Z^n$ with $|A|=4$ satisfies $|hA|=M_h-2$ is
\begin{equation}
 D_h=1+\binom{h+1}{2}.
\end{equation}
Consequently
\begin{equation}
 1+\binom{h+1}{2}
 \leq\nu_n(h,4)\leq\nu_1(h,4)
 \leq\max\{h^2,D_h^{\max}\}.
\end{equation}
In particular, $\nu_n(h,4)=\Theta(h^2)$ with constants uniform in $n$.
Moreover, for every $n\geq2$,
\begin{equation}
 \nu_n(h,4)>\nu_1(h,4)^{1/n}.
\end{equation}
Thus the inequality proposed in [NathansonLattice2026]
fails already for $k=4$, for every $h\geq2$ and every $n\geq2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.666738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1668d05a2793784e0b10ccc49fba3c18190adf1ce153269d2cb1477efe0e4898","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: equal difference of arXiv:2411.01104, 'Gaussian universality of $p$-adic random matrix products via corners'] Suppose $1\le j\le n-1$, $(\lambda_{n-j},\ldots,\lambda_n)\in\Sig_{j+1}$, $A^{(n-j)}\in\GL_{(j+1)\times n}(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ be full rank, and $A^{(n-j+1)}\in\GL_{j\times n}(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ be the submatrix of $A^{(n-j)}$, consisting of the last $j$ rows and all $n$ columns. Suppose we have the inequality

\begin{equation}
\SN(\diag_{(j+1)\times(j+1)}(p^{\lambda_{n-j}},\ldots,p^{\lambda_n})A^{(n-j)})_2<\lambda_{n-j}+\SN(A^{(n-j)})_{j+1}.
\end{equation}
Then we have 
$$\SN(\diag_{(j+1)\times(j+1)}(p^{\lambda_{n-j}},\ldots,p^{\lambda_n})A^{(n-j)})_1-\lambda_{n-j}=|\SN(A^{(n-j)})|-|\SN(A^{(n-j+1)})|.$$","status":"unverified"}

