{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.357276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1682a1c8ac1c42d569d65631ff064671b02b2f342bb093e92be55e5d01ef486f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: strongest result for discrete and bounded time of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $f \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal B}} $. There exists a sequence of (discrete time) Markov chains $((X_t)_{t\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} })_{n\geq 1}$ such that 
