{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.529139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16983e7076703c6df8266509758e486874e060fd579f937194ce3b7e9f6559a7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:configuration_disagree_6 of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:coupling-on-radius}
Let $(G,J)$ be a transitive graph and a transitive kernel, and let $(G_n,J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ be a sequence of transitive graphs and kernels converging locally to $(G,J)$.

Let $\beta \in \mathbf{R}_+$ and let $(\beta_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$.

Let $\omega_n$ be a configuration sampled from $\mathbf{P}_{\beta_n,G_n,J_n}$ and let $\omega$ be a configuration sampled from $\mathbf{P}_{\beta,G,J}$.

Then there exists a coupling $\mathbf{P}$ of $\omega_n$ and $\omega$ on $B(R_n)$ so that for any $R\le R_n$ satisfying (equation eq:coupling-recall of the paper),

\begin{equation}

    \mathbf{P}
    \Big(
    \omega_n\big[B(R)\big]
        \neq 
        \eta\big[B(R)\big]
    \Big)
    \leq
    \beta \varepsilon + |\beta_n-\beta|\sum_{x,y \in B(R)} J(x,y).
\end{equation}

Suppose that $R \in \mathbf{N}$ is fixed and that $\beta_n \to \beta$.

Then for $\xi > 0$ and for any event $\mathcal{A}_{R}$ which is locally determined by $B(R)$, for all $n$ sufficiently large

\begin{equation} 
   \left\vert
       \mathbf{P}_{\beta_n,G_n,J_n}
        \left(
            \mathcal{A}_{R}
        \right)-\mathbf{P}_{\beta,G,J}
        \left(
            \mathcal{A}_{R}
        \right) 
    \right\vert
    \le
    \xi.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.590010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_169cfa2e5dbfd7e4def1f155b37b9d9a04a25d817ff51b8c5e920726bcb0a899","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Main.SVE021 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For any $\beta\in\mathbb{R}$, the stochastic Volterra equation (equation MainThm.SVE of the paper) is equivalent to 
 	\begin{eqnarray}  
 	X_\zeta(t)\!\!\!&=\!\!\!& \zeta \cdot c\cdot W'_\beta(t)  +  \int_0^\zeta\int_0^\infty  \big( W_\beta(t)-W_\beta(t-y) \big) \, N_0(dz, dy)   \cr
 	\!\!\!&\!\!\!&  + \int_0^t (\beta-b)\cdot W'_\beta(t-s) X_\zeta(s)ds + \int_0^t \int_0^{X_\zeta(s)}   W'_\beta(t-s) \, B_c(ds,dz) \cr

 	\!\!\!&\!\!\!& + \int_0^t \int_0^{X_\zeta(s)} \int_0^\infty \big( W_\beta(t-s)-W_\beta(t-s-y) \big) \, \widetilde{N}_\nu(ds,dz,dy) ,\quad t\geq 0 . 
 	\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

