{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.284504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16df76f2627d1aac9816f30b554f9b8d4c5c0a4c55655ba6915860b6288609bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm MainThm2 of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] For all $\beta>0$ and $m\in \mathbb{N}$, we have:
\begin{equation}
\boldsymbol{\rho}^{(m)}_\beta(x_1,\dots,x_m)=\mathfrak{C}_{\beta}^{(m)} \prod_{1\le i<j \le m}\left|x_i-x_j\right|^\beta \mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{j=2}^m \left|\boldsymbol{\xi}^{\beta,m\beta/2}\left(x_j-x_1\right)\right|^\beta\right],
