  \end{equation}

  \medskip\noindent
  \item[\textup{(a)}] (Mollified score at fixed $\varepsilon$; classical Bismut formula.) Suppose, in addition, that at each fixed $\varepsilon > 0$ the regularised equation supports the classical Malliavin framework (in the white-in-time or abstract Gaussian-space form of Remark~(rem:abstract-gaussian of the paper)), i.e., $F^\varepsilon \in \mathbb{D}^{\infty,p}(\Omega)$ for all $p < \infty$, $\sigma_t^{(\varphi,\varepsilon)} > 0$ a.s., and $(\sigma_t^{(\varphi,\varepsilon)})^{-1} \in L^q(\Omega)$ for all $q < \infty$. Then $F^\varepsilon$ admits the intrinsic scalar logarithmic derivative
