{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.688744+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16fd0931eb32a2212db514e6523b07ceabc9d67c3290e9017a1674e60065fbf7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 101 (Dyadic reconstruction of a controlled remainder) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Let $E$ be a separable Banach space.  Let $X:[0,T]\to H$,
$Y':[0,T]\to\mathcal L(H,E)$, and
$R:\Delta_T\to E$ be random continuous fields with $R_{t,t}=0$ and
\begin{equation}
 R_{s,t}-R_{s,u}-R_{u,t}=Y'_{s,u}X_{u,t},
 \qquad s\le u\le t.
\end{equation}
Suppose that for some $q>1$ and all $s<t$,
\begin{align}
 \|X_{s,t}\|_{L^{2q}}&\le C_X|t-s|^{1/2},
 \\
 \|Y'_{s,t}\|_{L^{2q}}&\le C_{Y'}|t-s|^{1/2},
 \\
 \|R_{s,t}\|_{L^q}&\le C_R|t-s|.

\end{align}
If $0<\alpha<1/2$ and
\begin{equation}
 2\alpha<1-\frac1q,
\end{equation}
then, after modification on one null set,
$X$ and $Y'$ are $\alpha$-H\"older and $R$ is $2\alpha$-H\"older.  Moreover
\begin{equation}
 \|[X]_\alpha\|_{L^{2q}}
 +\|[Y']_\alpha\|_{L^{2q}}
 +\|[R]_{2\alpha}\|_{L^q}
 \le C_{\alpha,q,T}
 \bigl(C_X+C_{Y'}+C_R+C_XC_{Y'}\bigr).
