{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.707643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16fdc02499cca4a4792fd15ffbbfae77775fd34cfcf55b38e7bb1340d97cdda7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition tavradiamouleipeisKoulii of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] Let $(\mathcal{A}, \varphi)$ be a non-commutative probability space. The
  multilinear functionals $(\kappa_n : \mathcal{A}^n \rightarrow
  \mathbb{C})_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ uniquely determined by the relation
  \begin{equation}
    \varphi (a_1 \ldots a_k) = \sum_{\pi \in \ensuremath{\operatorname{NC}} (k)} \prod_{\{i_1 <
