{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.194353+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1711ae7cd94a52a5241b54f08e5dfaea25c76245bf56dec5f0d3bfcf637a2ea9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 20 of arXiv:2605.03851, 'The Relay Random Tree:\\A stochastic geometry approach of multihop relay in an urban visib'] \textbf{Blockage in the finite range case.}

For $\landsc$ a landscape, and $(x, y)\in \Half$ a point, the blocking building of $(x, y)$ in $\landsc$ is, when it is well defined, 
\[\tau (x, y, \landsc) = (x_b, y_b) := \underset{\substack{(a, b) \in \landsc \\a\in ]x, x+R]}}{\text{argmax}} \frac{b-y}{a-x}.\]
And $\tau(x, y, \landsc) = (-\infty, -\infty)$ when there is no building in $]x, x+R]$.

We define the blockage angle $\theta$ and its tangent $\mathrm{t}$ similarly to the infinite range case (with the convention that $\mathrm{t} = -\infty$).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.117654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17143331c69c3063a19868f9fee8053557f92c931fb74a9d38c2412f5f6a9f99","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:generator of arXiv:2608.17022, 'Sharp hypocoercive convergence estimates for underdamped Langevin dynamics with specular r'] Let $f\in\mathscr C$ and let $(X,V)$ solve (equation eq:sde-jump of the paper)--(equation eq:jump-term of the paper) on $[0,T]$ with $\mathcal T\cap[0,T]$ finite and $(X_s,V_{s-})\notin\Gamma_0$ for every $s\in\mathcal T$. Then
