{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.585864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17232ce1915c3d7dcb12f675d6d6be2e3c6438fbcff1045817cd2aa89788d904","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm.LaplaceF of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $\sigma$-finite measure $\mu(ds)$ on $\mathbb{R}_+$, 
  	the nonlinear Volterra equation (equation NonlinearVolterra of the paper) has a unique global solution $V_\mu \in D(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+) $ and the Laplace functional of $L^\xi_\zeta$ admits the representation
  	\begin{eqnarray}
  	\mathbf{E}\bigg[ \exp\Big\{- \int_{[0,x]} L^\xi_\zeta(x-s)\,\mu(ds) \Big\} \bigg]
  	= \exp\big\{  -\zeta \cdot \boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}\circ V_\mu(x)   \big\}, 
  	\quad x\geq 0,
  	\end{eqnarray}
  	where $\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}$ is a nonlinear operator acting on a locally bounded
  	function $f$ by
  	\begin{eqnarray}
  	\boldsymbol{\mathcal{F}}\circ f(t)
