{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.335414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17235cd86f285bedba6904072c7edce6fb85c8e2478da73a40c2a716b264beb2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Annealing scheme of arXiv:2411.09075, 'Weak Poincar{\'e} Inequalities, Simulated Annealing, and Sampling from Spherical Spin Glas'] Let $H$ be a Hamiltonian over $\Omega$, and $(\mu_\beta)_{\beta \ge 0}$ the class of distributions over $\Omega$ with $\mu_\beta(\sigma) \propto e^{\beta H(\sigma)}$. For each $\beta \le \beta_0$, let $P = P_\beta$ be a (reversible and ergodic) Markov chain with stationary distribution $\mu_\beta$. 

    An \emph{(inverse) temperature schedule} is any function $\beta: \R_{\ge 0} \to \R_{\ge 0}$. 
    An \emph{annealing scheme} $\calA$ is the time-inhomogeneous Markov chain such that at time $t$, one applies the Markov chain $P_{\beta(t)}$.","status":"unverified"}

