{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.618295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_173c7c8f8585a76bc983aa99b3c003da49ae6c3d5e719e3b25d534c7429f4308","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 75 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist positive constants $C,c,C',c'$ such that for all $\delta>0$, all $n$ and all $0\leq m\leq n/2$, we have
  \begin{align}

