{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.571807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_173ca2847345dafb81c9b406170aa9114aba90f2069969ce0e340461e35e1d48","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 22 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] An \emph{augmented massive (co-polyharmonic) Gaussian field} $\tilde h$ on $(M,g)$ with mass $m>0$ is a centered Gaussian random variable $\tilde h$ on ${\mathfrak D}$ with covariance
	\begin{equation}

		\mathbb{E} \Big[\langle \tilde h|\phi\rangle\cdot \langle \tilde h|\eta\rangle\Big]={\mathcal K}_{m}(\phi,\eta)

		\quad\qquad \forall \phi,\eta\in {\mathfrak D} ,
	\end{equation}
	where
	\begin{align*}
		{\mathcal K}_{m}(\phi,\eta)
		=&\sum_{j=1}^\infty \frac{\scalar{\phi}{\psi_j}\scalar{\eta}{\psi_j}}{\nu_j+m}+\sigma^2\scalar{\phi}{1}\scalar{\eta}{1}.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_173e3dbe47b56847644b319f168d1ce9ca523afd263d7ddbde14cb992d7c8041","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 34 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>6$. There exist $K>0$ and $k_0\geq 1$ such that the following holds. For every $k\geq k_0$, letting $n=2^k$ and $u_n:=\phi_{\beta_c}[0\connect{}\partial \Lambda_n]$, one has
