{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.311234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17577082ab4c0ca05f5d6336734963d2da8767699bcd6ee2bd2f05deffd2cb3a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor-speciallineargroup of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Let $L=(L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) and let $X=(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ denote its stochastic exponential. Then $X_t\in \operatorname{SL}(\mathbb{R},d)$ for all $t\geq 0$ if and only if
