{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.471744+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17673cbd1e19b284a76ba00896025d26b34c85cca38367bc5a3173e7aa414267","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq: F_h^nu o pi_nu = F_h o i_nu of arXiv:2608.28278, 'Reduction of symmetric time-dependent Hamiltonian systems I: presymplectic principal $\R$-'] Let $h_\nu: (V^*\Pi)_\nu \to (T^*Q)_\nu$ the section of $\mu_\nu$ induced by the Hamiltonian section $h$ of $\mu$. Then, there exists a unique function $F_h^\nu:(T^*Q)_\nu\to\mathbb{R}$ characterized by
