{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.647437+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_177c84408c484ce0474eff84c5622f4a19d90ef4eda9afd9601784a174229d1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.29878, 'Discontinuous phase transitions \\ in the one-dimensional \\ pair and triplet creation pro'] Let $v :\RR \to [0,1]$ be Lipschitz continuous, i.e., $|f(x)-f(y)| \le K|x-y|$ for all $x,y$. Suppose that the initial configuration has a density $v$ in the sense of \eqref{densdef}. If $t$ is fixed and $-m_\ep \le m < m_\ep$ then
