{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.875402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17877afa404735b043fe4f23ebcdc903a647c8ecbb74e55b2ce5cd8d920450a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dist_as_dplus of arXiv:2605.10911, 'The stochastic block model has the overlap graph property for modularity'] Suppose that $n$ is divisible by $k$. 
Let $\mathcal{A}$ be any partition of $[n]$ with $k$ parts, and let $\mathcal{P}$ be the planted partition.
Let $X=X(\mathcal{A})=(x_{ij})_{1\leq i \leq j \leq k}$ be the signature of $\mathcal{A}$. Then,
\begin{equation}
d(\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{P}) = 1-\tfrac{1}{k}\max_{\sigma} \sum_{i=1}^k x_{\sigma(i) i}, 
\end{equation}
where the maximum is taken over all permutations of $[k]$. 

Moreover, $d(\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{P}) \leq 1 -1/k$ and this upper bound is sharp, that is, there exists a partition~$\mathcal{A}$ such that $d(\mathcal{A}, \mathcal{P}) = 1 -1/k$, provided that $n$ is divisible by $k^2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.020909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1788247357649ef52055254b803ca0b9e80f78bdad4d114bc6b799b0c9069b53","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 42 of arXiv:2609.02878, '2609.02878'] Let $(\hat X,\hat g_s)$ be the underlying metric flow of a tangent space
at a fixed limiting point whose base lies in $Y^{\rm prod}$, in the
relative-dimension-one setting.  For every $A>1$,
\begin{equation}
