{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.402837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17a71c27a954f98468b1a70129f2b92d0fa2785c8f07966bb637ed8e3c5850c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.03185, 'Uniqueness of tangent flows in free boundary flow'] Let $N\subset \mathbb{R}^{n+1}$ be a hypersurface satisfying $|\langle x,n_N(x)\rangle|\leq C_0$. Suppose that $M$ be a normal graph over $N$ on $B_R(0)$ given by a function $u$ with sufficiently small $C^2$ norm. Then, for every $f\in C^1(\mathbb{R}^{n+1})$, there exists a constant $C$ such that
