where all $L^2$ and $H^2$ norms are taken over $N\cap B_R(0)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.041860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17a8a4e651d42d5ee2c75b04ca3e656eb57b311eb187001bf7f9ffc5e85cca82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 51 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let   $\lambda\geq 0$, $\rho\in (0,\rho_{b}]$, and let $y$ be 
