{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.281626+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17ed81b6867d23d7ab267a9bb06e1b4d9a6163ef83b42238136a9dfa6322e1f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 (Almost sure sign-balance) of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] Recall that for $u \in \R$, the level-imbalance $\Bc_{T,u}(r)$ of the random waves is defined in \eqref{eq:sign-imbal def waves}. Assume that either (a) $\eta(T)\rightarrow \infty$ or (b) $\Mcc=\Sc^{d}$, and let $\bar{r}_T$ be given by \eqref{eq:rT crit rad rand wav}. Then if $\mu > 0$ is sufficiently large, as $T \to \infty$, one has 
