{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.765066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17fd0dce8dc771b4dfbc3ed9ca293c3e9c2d026c773ed9d04a023ab7701d2026","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t41 of arXiv:2411.19433, 'Singular mean-field backward stochastic Volterra integral equations in infinite dimensiona'] Let condition $(A_{3})$ satisfy. Then, for every \( \varphi(\cdot) \in L^2_{\mathcal{F}}(0, b; H) \), the equation (equation 63 of the paper) admits a unique solution \( Y(\cdot) \in L^2_{\mathcal{F}}(0, b; H) \). Moreover, the subsequent estimate holds:
