{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.401293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_180c48a99a6544e883bedb481c151fd2dd81ee5a2ab4a8b527665e00b7ba686c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t: main theorem displacement of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $p\in[-d,\infty)$. Suppose that $Z$ is an invariant $\R^d$-valued random field on $\R^d$, that $\Phi$ is an invariant locally square-integrable random measure, and that $\Psi$ is defined as in~(equation e: definition Psi displacement of the paper). Either assume that for some $\vartheta>0$ and strongly log-dominating function $\rho$,
