{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.783964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18a678b949faacbd9cddf1bd2eda08f0d430867d8055879b03ddb97b0f96a3d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2604.00474, 'Trap behaviors for Brownian motions'] Let $L$ be the inverse of the $\alpha$-stable subordinator $H$. 
\begin{itemize}
\item[i)] Assume $0 < \beta < 1/\alpha$, then
\begin{align}
    \mathbf{E}_0[(L_t)^\beta] = \frac{\Gamma(\beta + 1)}{\Gamma(\beta \alpha + 1)} t^{\alpha \beta}, \quad t>0.

