{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.321269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18cb05f3eeb89596aea64d8f73ad056ff9d0088e19d46470fb9276948e1ab339","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.Holder_coefficients of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Fix $\alpha \in (0,1)$ and let $\alpha' = \nicefrac{2\alpha}{3}$.  Suppose that $\left\langle v \right\rangle^m g \in C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}$ for some $m\neq 3$.  Then, if $m > 2 + \nicefrac\alpha3$,
