    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.297644+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18ce2ee1581c17750ee9397bff98ba000787a89ae7cd78fdeadd128904feab21","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Cor2 of arXiv:2608.30212, 'A Painlev\'e equation for the H\"ormander-Bernhardsson constant'] Let $n=2k\in \mathbb{N}$ with $k\ge 2$. Assume $\varphi_j=\varphi_j(c)$ and $\psi_j=\psi_j(c)$, $1\le j\le k$ are continuous in $c$ such that
