holds. Define $I_k = \{c\in\mathbb{R}:\text{ condition (equation Phi-interlace of the paper) holds}\}$, let $I_{k,0}$ be the connected component  of $I_k$ that contains $0$, and let $H=H_c$ be the corresponding $\pm1$ function on $(0,\pi)$ with $H_c(0+)=(-1)^{k+1}$. If $\sup I_{k,0}<\infty$, then $ C_{2k-2} = \sup I_{k,0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.317518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18cf673367ab07ab7f9d0529ed675b627e4f625ed9d368a0c209a62ed8ead011","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 19 (Optimal scale of a fixed two-point member) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For every $p \in (0, 1/2]$ and $\nu > 0$, the infimum
