{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.274972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18d5d33ed6fc71c1476431736a679bb092c7b65c742c6a8bc8dd9e402c08b696","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_fineteness_moments_plusBC of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$ be a bounded, open and simply connected domain such that $\partial D$ has Hausdorff dimension strictly smaller than $7/4$. Then, for any $k \geq 1$,
