{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.772134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18dfd883698452a63c55cc3a2928efeddb33041496ff7353b1066bb75a232448","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 52 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation from Definition \ref{Def.ParametersEdge}. There exist constants $\delta_0 \in (0,1)$ and $C_0 > 0$, depending on $q, \kappa$ and $c$, such that the function $\SFb(z;\kappa)$ is analytic in the disk $\{|z-\zc(\kappa)| < 2\delta_0\}$, the functions $\SFt(z;\kappa), \GFt(z)$ are analytic in the disk $\{|z- c| < 2\delta_0\}$, and the following statements hold. 
If $|z-\zc(\kappa)| \leq \delta_0$, then
\begin{equation}
\left| \SFb(z;\kappa) - \SFb(\zc(\kappa);\kappa)  \right| \leq C_0 |z - \zc(\kappa)|^3.
