    where $n_0=0$, $x_0=x$ and $\sigma_N^2>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.796796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18e4965ea99145335cdfc7e684e141fae89ad4db79fa92f7e368419c21d86b0f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 66 of arXiv:2608.30549, '\vspace{-1cm}Maximally Spread Out Measures and Implications\\{} for Phase Transitions in A'] Let $\emptyset \ne \Omega \subset \RR^d$ be an open and bounded subset.
Let $A_1,A_2\in \{B,F\}$.
Let $s_1,s_2\in \RR$ and let $0<p_1,q_1,p_2,q_2 \le \infty$ (with $p_i<\infty$ if $A_i=F$).
Assume that 
\begin{equation*}
   s_1 > s_2 
   \quad \text{and} \quad
    s_1 - \frac{d}{p_1} > s_2 -\frac{d}{p_2}.
\end{equation*}
Then the embedding $\iota \colon (A_1)^{s_1}_{p_1,q_1}(\Omega) \embeds (A_2)^{s_2}_{p_2,q_2}(\Omega)$
is compact and there exist constants $C_1, C_2>0$ such that the dyadic entropy numbers of $\iota$ satisfy
    \begin{equation*}
        C_1 \cdot k^{-\frac{s_1-s_2}{d}} 
        \le \en_k(\iota) 
        \le C_2 \cdot k^{-\frac{s_1-s_2}{d}} 
        \quad 
        \text{ for all $k\in \NN$}.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.309477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18e7ca68b505f9c5d64e3ac2010abb3c2b2434aad5e36716513cca70820877af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2606.24485, 'On the convex hull of a planar Brownian bridge with a random Gaussian endpoint'] For $0<\sigma\le 1$, the maximizing time $\tau_\sigma$ has density
	\begin{equation}
		f_{\tau_\si}(t)
		=
		\frac{\sigma}{\pi\sqrt{t(1-t)}}
		+
		(1-\sigma^2)\ug{
			1-\frac{1}{\pi}
			\arctan \ob{
				\frac{\sigma}{(1-\sigma^2)\sqrt{t(1-t)}}
			}
		},
		\qquad 0<t<1.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.595306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18e83f354bddd6d8a920b71a648f3d8e0e0c6a37e230cfaf2f5722c3d7b6acd6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] Let $t_0:=k\lceil \ln(2k)\rceil.$ Then, for every $x \in Q_k$ and every $A \subseteq Q_k,$
    \begin{equation}
        (K^{\star})^{t_0}(x,A) \geq \frac{1}{2}\pi(A), \qquad x\in Q_k ,\quad A\subseteq Q_k.
    \end{equation}
    Consequently, for every probability measure $\mu$ on $Q_k,$ 
    \begin{equation}
        ||\mu (K^{\star})^{mt_0}- \pi||_{\TV} \leq 2^{-m}, \qquad m\geq0.
    \end{equation}
    In particular, for every bounded $g:Q_k\to\R,$
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{x\in Q_k} \left|((K^{\star})^{mt_0}g)(x)-\pi(g) \right| \leq ||g||_{\infty}2^{-(m-1)}, \qquad m\geq 0.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.652916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18e885316079d04e0196937730d48794bdca8e9d6e28b61ba7748e7319f58d6d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 of arXiv:2607.24533, 'Colored Markov-Modulated Brownian Motion for Preemptive Workload Stacks'] {Suppose that the hypotheses of Lemma~\ref{lem:green} hold.} Then, for every $x>0$,
\begin{equation}

