{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:34.002455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18e9f02e24316aad7748339d2a05ba9e15c00d7a969f9a0ba3c3b1bd0d2096a6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 63 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] Let $0\le T\le I_m$, and let $F$ be a $\mathbb C^{m\times m}$-valued function analytic in $\mathbb C_r$. The kernel
\[
  K_{T,1}(z,w)=\frac{F(z)+F(w)^*+T-F(z)TF(w)^*}{z+\overline{w}}
\]
is positive definite in $\mathbb C_r$ if and only if there exists a (non-uniquely determined in general) $\mathbb C^{m\times 2m}$ bounded function
$S=\begin{pmatrix} S_1&S_2\end{pmatrix}$ such that
\begin{equation}

      \begin{split}
        (F(z)+I_m)S_1(z)&=F(z)\sqrt{I_m+T}\\
        (F(z)+I_m)S_2(z)&=\sqrt{I_m-T}.
      \end{split}
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.576999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18ea5ab129e425d6c24d545443cfa678c5a3c4a120060c9910ba3bd4b120cac3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:2F1-Log of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] For all $H \in (1/2, 1)$ and $t > 0$, the following holds:
    \begin{align*}
      \int_0^t (t-s)^{2H-2} \log\left(\frac{t+s}{t-s}\right) \ensuremath{\mathrm{d} } s =
    t^{2H-1} \left(\frac{\Gamma(2H-1)}{\Gamma(1+2H)} \lMr{2}{F}{1}(1,1;1+2H;-1) + \frac{1}{(2H-1)^2}\right).
  \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.093253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18edb97cbb563a7ebd93c9a3a19d8226598f58f57d2f01502e4a8de37bd0c02c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:first-moment-condition of arXiv:2609.02710, 'Asymptotic Mean Value Laplacian\\ on equiregular sub-Riemannian manifolds'] The first-kind coordinates at $x$ satisfy the \emph{first-moment condition}
with respect to $\mu$ if the limits
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma_i(x):=\lim_{h\downarrow0}\frac1h
  \int_{B_{x,h}}\xi_iJ_x(\delta_h\xi)\,\,d\xi,
  \qquad i=1,\ldots,k,
\end{equation}
exist. We call the $\Gamma_i(x)$ the first-moment coefficients in the
chosen chart.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.450339+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18ef884aa464150fa49eec8440ba971929e2c29d2ffa5510eeb4b65608840f81","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop theorem:lowerboundLp of arXiv:2504.19942, 'The edge-averaging process on graphs \\ with random initial opinions'] Consider the edge-averaging process on $G=(V,E)$ where $G$ is either the $n$-cycle or the infinite path $\mathbb Z$. For every $p\in[1,\infty)$ and $\delta>0$, there are i.i.d.\ random variables $\{f_0(v)\}_{v \in V}$ in $L^p$, such that if $t^*=\min (t,n^2)>30^4$, then  
\begin{equation}
\|f_t(o)-\mu\|_p\geq 

\begin{cases}
    t_*^{\frac{1-p}{2p}-\delta}&p\in [1,2)\,,\\
    t_*^{-1/4}&p \ge 2\,.
