{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.287293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_18f8ef990b23f609ae99094ff2da330159fefd0ac739bc373fcddb033829bfbc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm MainBound of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] Let $\beta,\delta>0$, $\ell \in \mathbb{N}$ and $(x_1,\dots,x_\ell) \in \mathbb{R}^\ell$. Suppose $r_1,\dots,r_\ell \in \mathbb{R}_+$ are such that $\sum_{j=1}^\ell r_j\le2\delta$. Then,
