{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.017508+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1900123a638dab3e46292de012dba2b623d4b61a6d149cc4e2922c4b99bc4c4f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Suppose~\cref{ass:oracle} holds, $\Gamma>0$, and $\lVert G_s\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq G_{\mathrm{op}}$ almost surely for every~$s$, fix $\rho>0$ and $\epsilon>0$, and let $B_{\mathrm{NS}}\coloneqq\sqrt r((1+2A)\Gamma+\sigma)$.
Running~\cref{alg:generic-o2nc} using \cref{alg:momentum-muon} as its online learner $\mathcal A$ with $1-\beta=\min\{1/9,(\epsilon/3B_{\mathrm{NS}})^2\}$, $D=(1-\beta)\rho/(4\beta)$, and depth $q=\left\lceil\log_A\max\left\{1,\ 3B_{\mathrm{NS}}G_{\mathrm{op}}\sqrt r / (\Gamma\epsilon)\right\}\right\rceil$ gives
