{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.135276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_190da2869f9fee091a6fed53d89b05881581adf629b2df949d3f333c92050f3c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:FerreStoltz of arXiv:2603.00773, 'Long-time $L^p$ Wasserstein contraction for diffusion processes without global dissipativi'] Under Assumptions~(assum:Ferre of the paper) and~(Assum:PointwiseContractInfty of the paper), assume furthermore that $\eta$ is bounded\footnote{This assumption could be weakened to $\eta(x) \ll |x|^2$, cf. [FerreStoltz]} and $\mathcal C^\infty$ with all derivatives growing at most polynomially. Then:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For all $R_0>0$ and $p\geqslant 1$, there exists $C_{R_0}>0$ such that for all $t\geqslant 0$,
\begin{equation}
\sup_{x\in \mathcal B(0,R_0)} \left| \frac1t \ln G_p(x,t) - \mathcal J(p\eta)\right| \leqslant \frac{C_{R_0}}{t}\,,
\end{equation}
where, for $f\in L^\infty(\mathbb R^d)$, 
\begin{equation}

\mathcal J(f) = \sup_{\nu\in\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)}\left\{\int_{\mathbb R^d} f \text{d} \nu - \mathcal I(\nu)\right\}\,,
\end{equation}
with the rate function 
\[\mathcal I(\nu) = \sup_{u\in \mathcal D_+(\mathcal L)}\left\{ -\int_{\mathbb R^d} \frac{\mathcal L u}{u} \text{d} \nu \right\}\,,\]
 where, denoting by $\mathcal D(\mathcal L)$ the extended domain of the generator $\mathcal L$ (cf. [FerreStoltz]) and $\mathcal C(\mathbb R^d)$ the space of continuous functions,
 \[\mathcal D_+(\mathcal L) = \left\{ u \in \mathcal D(\mathcal L) \cap \mathcal C(\mathbb R^d), \ u>0,\ \frac{\mathcal L u}{u} \in L^\infty(\mathbb R^d)\right\}\,.\]
\item For all $p\geqslant 1$, there exists $C>0$ such that for all $t\geqslant 0$,
\begin{equation}

  G_p^*(t)  \leqslant C e^{ t \max\left( -\rho, \mathcal J(p\eta)\right)}  \,.
\end{equation}
If, moreover, there exists $K>0$ such that $|b(x)|\leqslant K|x|+K$ for all $x\in\mathbb R^d$, then for all $p\geqslant 1$, there exists $c>0$ such that for all $t\geqslant 0$,
\begin{equation}

   G_p^*(t) \geqslant c  e^{ t \max\left( -\rho', \mathcal J(p\eta)\right)}\,,
\end{equation}
with $\rho' = -\liminf_{|x|\rightarrow \infty}\eta(x) \in[\rho,\infty]$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

