{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.402836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1915f43b8b12ff87ab356f6313dd195f14d1de8d1d435c868846f2be94ed22ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 of arXiv:2605.15386, 'The non-central gamma sum and difference distributions: exact distribution and asymptotic '] 1. Suppose that $r_X+r_Y\not=0$. Then, as $x\rightarrow\infty$,
\begin{align}f_{S_n}(x)&\sim C(r_X,r_Y,\rho,n)\,x^{(n-3)/4}\exp\bigg(\frac{|r_X+r_Y|}{1+\rho}\sqrt{\frac{nx}{s}}-\frac{x}{s(1+\rho)}\bigg)\sum_{l=0}^\infty c_l(r_X,r_Y,\rho,n)\frac{s^{l/2}}{x^{l/2}}, 
