{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.161532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_194ecfb28e0c9b9fb40da725075377a2b95f4a090b4cf5bac0eafd726363cfc4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2607.02477, 'Mixing times of spin systems on dynamical percolation'] Let $(\Phi^{(N)})_{N\geq 1}$ be such that $\Phi^{(N)}$ is a collection of potentials on $\T_N^d$ as above, and assume that for each $\kappa\in(0,1/2)$ and $a>0$,  we have $h_\kappa(a)<\infty$. Then, for any $d\geq 1$, $\kappa\in(0,1/2)$ and $p<p_c(d)$, there exist $C_\star>0$, $\lambda_0>0$ and $N_0\in\N$, so that for each $\lambda<\lambda_0$ and $N>N_0$,
