{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.633753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19648386e8f9cb3135f44c5c37ea594949839f6771bb2aed57f553c50437bc58","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2506.17094, 'Nonlinear random perturbations of Reaction Diffusion Equations'] Under Hypotheses \ref{H1}, \ref{H2} and \ref{H3}, for all $T>0$ and $p\geq 1$ we can find $\e_{T,p}>0$ such that for all  $x\in E$  and $0\leq \lambda<t \leq T$ and all $\e\leq \e_{T,p}$ 
