{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.658529+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1975c0ce65173b7ec151cf4bef99c12c2e6ded58a2726cc3af153f3da060eec9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 (Theorem 2.1 of \cite{nutz2021introduction}) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Suppose that $\mathcal{R} \sim \mu_0 \otimes \mu_1$ and that $D_{\textup{KL}}(\mu_{0} \otimes \mu_{1} || \mathcal{R}) < \infty$. Then the following hold.
