{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.861467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19a7d3c530f80954afe47c8a5003269f1462d3d38e7f5a4c17dc47ec77cdaf2f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop late-catch-up of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that Equation~(equation eq:persistent of the paper) is satisfied for $\alpha > 0$ and $K \in \mathbb{N}$. Then, for any $u \in \mathcal{U}$,  
