{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.727435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19cab084f4ed1fa033610147b87b144cf5f546fd4a443d2dbcd20572657dddfa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:5.3 of arXiv:2604.19294, 'On the maxima of Littlewood polynomials on $[-1,1]$'] There exists an absolute constant $C>0$ such that the following holds. Let $N$ be sufficiently large and $\Delta\in[N^{-1},e^{-1}]$. Then
