{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.385153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19cbd20481faf984da489f3b56e8cde34749fdf9b5db588db503270de74efb61","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 20 of arXiv:2609.03248, 'Connections between colored restricted $b$-ary and ordinary partitions'] Let $b\geq 2$. The sequence $\left(C_b^1(n)\right)_{n\geq 0}$, which gives the
numbers of $b$-ary partitions of $n$, satisfies the recurrence relations
\begin{equation}
C_b^1(bn+j)=\sum_{k=0}^n C_b^1(n-k) \qquad (j=0, 1,\ldots b-1),
\end{equation}
and consequently
\begin{align}
&C_b^1(bn) = C_b^1(bn+1) = \dots = C_b^1(bn+b-1),\\
&C_b^1(bn) - C_b^1(bn-1) = C_b^1(n).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

