{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.518719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19ea4982806c879cbd185737a2f8e4fdf7e0d07235fa50b9360e5a8d80814d19","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:truncated_kernel of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{thm:truncation_problem}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with dimension $d \geq 2$ and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel satisfying $J(x,y) = \Omega (d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha \in (1,2)$. 

