{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.035370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19f9d437708a88d9b2109de2a2068bdd8b28a8940c908495c5c2c4454510a509","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture 44 of arXiv:2506.09609, 'Schramm-Loewner evolution contains a topological Sierpi\'nski carpet when $\kappa$ is clos'] For each $\underline{\kappa} \in (0,4)$, there exists $\rho_c = \rho_c(\kappa) \in (-2-\underline{\kappa}/2,-2) \cap [\underline{\kappa}/2-4,-2) $ such that the following holds. Let $\eta$ be an SLE$_{\underline{\kappa}}(\rho)$ curve from $0$ to $\infty$ on $\mathbb{H}$ with force point always located to the right of the tip.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item For $\rho \in (\rho_c, -2)$, almost surely, the range of $\eta$ is conformally removable and the adjacency graph of $\mathbb{H} \setminus \eta$ is connected.

        \item For $\rho \in (-2-\underline{\kappa}/2,\rho_c) \cap [\underline{\kappa}/2-4,\rho_c)$, the range of $\eta$ is conformally non-removable, the adjacency graph of $\mathbb{H} \setminus \eta$ is disconnected, and the range of $\eta$ contains a topological Sierpi\'nski carpet.
