{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.965162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a0882b3af7b2ca2af11033ae00a7801e43e4586aa0d9ad091fa2886b0453dea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop quadrisk of arXiv:2412.03560, 'Non-asymptotic entropic bounds for non-linear kinetic Langevin sampler with second-order s'] Let $f:\mathbb R^d\rightarrow \mathbb R$ be a bounded measurable function and, for $N,n\in\mathbb N$. Then,
