{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.671801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a1ec7ee7c829e06534d301026eb73c2001a820ec75e7dcf82e5a9a624da4381","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.10725, 'From the Airy line ensemble to the Gaussian free field'] The random measure $M^{\mathsf{S}; \mathcal{A}}$ in \eqref{Eq.RMS1} is a determinantal point process with reference measure $\mu_{\mathsf{S}} \times \mathrm{Leb}$ as in Definition \ref{Def.Measures}, and with correlation kernel given by 
