{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.319420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a2476520c2abccc64e73f7dc7d701a02d79fa77ffc03344eb523388760f0b59","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 (Annulus BPZ) of arXiv:2607.27786, 'Gaussian free field in annulus: \\BPZ equations and crossing probabilities for level lines'] Recall that $\Theta_1, \Theta_3$ are rescaled Jacobi theta functions in~\eqref{eqn::JacobiTheta_productexpansion}. Define
\begin{align} 
	H_1(r;z) := 2 \partial_z \log \Theta_1(r;z), \qquad
	H_3(r;z) := 2 \partial_z \log \Theta_3(r;z).
\end{align}
The partition functions $\LZann{n}$ and $\LZcro{n}^{(\ell)}$ in~\eqref{eqn::LZann_def} and~\eqref{eqn::LZcroell_def} satisfy the following system of annulus BPZ equations: for all $j\in\{1, \ldots, n\}$, 
\begin{align} 
	\begin{split}
		\frac{\partial_r \LZ}{\LZ}=2\frac{\partial_{\alpha_j}^2 \LZ}{\LZ} & +   \sum_{\ell\neq j} \left( H_1(r; \alpha_\ell-\alpha_j) \frac{\partial_{\alpha_\ell} \LZ}{\LZ} + \frac{1}{4} \partial_z H_1(r; \alpha_\ell-\alpha_j) \right) \\
		& +  \sum_{\ell=1}^n \left( H_3(r; \beta_\ell-\alpha_j) \frac{\partial_{\beta_\ell} \LZ}{\LZ} + \frac{1}{4} \partial_z H_3(r; \beta_\ell-\alpha_j) \right) + \frac{1}{2r} + \frac{3}{4} \LE(r) + \frac{n}{4}; 
	\end{split} \\

	\begin{split}
		\frac{\partial_r \LZ}{\LZ}= 2\frac{\partial_{\beta_j}^2 \LZ}{\LZ} &+  \sum_{\ell\neq j} \left( H_1(r; \beta_\ell-\beta_j) \frac{\partial_{\beta_\ell} \LZ}{\LZ} + \frac{1}{4} \partial_z H_1(r; \beta_\ell-\beta_j) \right) \\
		& +  \sum_{\ell=1}^n \left( H_3(r; \alpha_\ell-\beta_j) \frac{\partial_{\alpha_\ell} \LZ}{\LZ} + \frac{1}{4} \partial_z H_3(r; \alpha_\ell-\beta_j) \right) + \frac{1}{2r} + \frac{3}{4} \LE(r) + \frac{n}{4}; 
	\end{split}
\end{align}
where \begin{equation} 
	\LE(r) := -\frac{1}{6} + \sum_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{\sinh^2(kr)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.749349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a275711ee1907a7f836bc77ec803b7dbfe6177f768c29b36187cfeabd9f35ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma inclusion_exclusion_degree of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and $k,\ell\in[n]$. Fix integers $d_{a_1},\ldots ,d_{a_k}$ and $d_{f_1},\ldots, d_{f_\ell}$. Then,
\begin{equation} \begin{aligned} 
\mathbb P{}&\big(\deg_n(a_v)=d_{a_v} \text{ for all }v\in[k], \deg_n(f_w)=d_{f_w}\text{ for all }w\in[\ell]\big)\\
&= \sum_{R\subseteq [k]}\sum_{S\subseteq[\ell]}\!\!(-1)^{|R|+|S|}\P{\deg_n(a_v)\geq d_{a_v}+\mathbbm{1}_{\{v\in R\}},v\in[k], \deg_n(f_w)\geq d_{f_w}+\mathbbm{1}_{\{w\in S\}},w\in[\ell]}.
\end{aligned} \end{equation} 
In particular, for integers  $k\geq k'\geq 1$ and $\ell\geq\ell'\geq 1$  and $d_{a_1},\ldots, d_{a_{k}}$ and $d_{f_1},\ldots, d_{f_{\ell}}$, 
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\mathbb P({}&\deg_n(a_o)=d_{a_o}, \deg_n(a_v)\geq d_{a_v} \text{ for } 1\leq o\leq k'<v\leq k,\\
&\deg_n(f_u)=d_{f_u}, \deg_n(f_w)\geq d_{f_w}\text{ for }1\leq u\leq \ell'<w\leq \ell)\\
={}&\sum_{R\subseteq [k']}\sum_{S\subseteq[\ell']}\!\!(-1)^{|R|+|S|}\mathbb P(\deg_n(a_v)\geq d_{a_v}+\mathbbm{1}_{\{v\in R\}},v\in[k], \deg_n(f_w)\geq d_{f_w}+\mathbbm{1}_{\{w\in S\}},w\in[\ell]).
\end{aligned}\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.240742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a27ba827264acd891b213273933f9da143c4f0948b68a85a3c60895fb8c9310","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:log_price_sig_repr of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] The log-price $X_t = \log S_t$ for $t \in [0, T]$ is given by
