{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.185136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a55bb204d74a1c9b7309538630f60697b1cd283a7e312880f650c1a7bc165ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:TimeCoM of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Consider the chain $\mathbf{X} = (X_{t})_{t \geqslant 0}$. Then for all $\varepsilon, C, \theta > 0$, there exists some $C^\prime = C^\prime(\varepsilon, C, \theta) > 0$ such that for all $n$ sufficiently large,
