{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.291252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a6dad2ae6adf4db8e2fa5ce8d5a2871647697c291d94b841b0a2123234c1ffc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem hls of arXiv:2411.05204, '\Large\bf Sample Path Properties of the Fractional Wiener--Weierstrass Bridge'] Let $H\in(0,1),\,k\in\mathbb N,\,\alpha\in(0,1),\,b=\alpha^{-1/H}$, and $\{I_m\}_{m\in\mathbb N_0}$ be a collection of $k$-intervals with $|I_m|=b^m$. Define
