\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.462755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a82a154c888892c27cd61f949820b0c2b9d8ae16d28498133bdcc6eb7ffddd7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Censored random walk, \cite{ding2014mixing} of arXiv:2505.02685, 'On the Spectral Expansion of Monotone Subsets of the Hypercube'] Given $A \subseteq \{0,1\}^n$, the \emph{random walk on $\{0,1\}^n$ censored to}
    $A$ is defined as follows. On state $x \in A$, sample $i \in [n]$ uniformly
    at random and let $y$ be the vertex obtained by flipping the $i$-th bit of
    $x$. Then
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If $y \in A$, flip a coin and either stay at $x$ or move to $y$ (each with probability $1/2$).
        \item If $y \not\in A$, stay at $x$ (in which case we call this a \emph{censored} step).
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.053388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a832bdf63f58338dd81142572e769640867a8e0a7ead71a891ddb12a8548b1f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 40 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $0<T\le1$, $0<\sigma<1$, and suppose that $H$ satisfies the parabolic tail condition \eqref{eq:parabolic-tail-bound}.  Then the heat spectral splitting satisfies
\begin{equation}

\max\{\norm{Q_{cb}}_{H^\alpha},\norm{Q_{ba}}_{H^\alpha}\}\le \left(\frac12+C L^\eta\right)\norm{Q_{ca}}_{H^\alpha} +C\bigl(\norm{H}_{\gamma,\alpha}+K\bigr)L^\gamma,
\end{equation}
where $\eta:=\min\{1-\sigma,\rho\}>0$ and $\rho=\frac{\sigma\beta}{2}$.
In particular, at $\gamma=1$ this is a critical admissible scale splitting.  If $0<\gamma<1$, then after restricting to a sufficiently small time horizon $T_0$, it is a subcritical admissible scale splitting, because $1/2+C T_0^\eta<2^{-\gamma}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.765479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a83450c75029c10dae027ae4a6abf5fcd86f37df2348af90a4e9dfa7132cb0c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz thm:necessity-bernoulli of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d\in\mathds{N}$, $s,\alpha,\beta,\gamma \in\mathds{R}$, $p,q\in (0,\infty]$, and $\mu,\nu \in [-d,0]$.
