{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.479780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a8696a17a001c3a9bb534307c7b28c05ef3c17fcbaf5630f8ca0a2aff87d5dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Thm_MakNikPal of arXiv:2606.22183, 'Expected loss of quasi-arithmetic means of exchangeable random variables'] Let $I\subseteq \mathbb{R}$ be a nonempty open interval, $\alpha:(I-I)\to\mathbb{R}_+$ be an even error function, and $L:I\to \mathbb{R}$ be a function.
