{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.354340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a9eb3a931ce5143b25bb9c5f68f2ecc70f460f419e63e7d02503a4e7ef3f2af","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm of arXiv:2608.10215, 'The variance of the Pitman--Yor process: a Cifarelli--Regazzini identity and inversion for'] Let $n, k, N \in \mathbb{N}$, with $\max\{n, k\} \leq N$.
Given $(N_1, \dots, N_k) \in \mathcal{P}^{\downarrow}(N; k)$ and $z_1, z_2, \dots, z_k \in \mathbb{R}$, the following identity holds:
\[
\sum_{(\ast)} \prod_{i=1}^k \binom{N_i}{\nu_i} z_i^{\nu_i} = \frac{1}{n!} \frac{\mathrm{d}^n}{\mathrm{d} t^n} 
\left[ \prod_{i=1}^k (1 + t z_i)^{N_i} \right]_{t=0} 
\]
where $(\ast)$ indicates summation over all $k$-tuples $(\nu_1, \dots, \nu_k) \in \mathbb{N}_0^k$ satisfying $\nu_i \le N_i$ for $i=1, \dots, k$ and $\sum_{i=1}^k \nu_i = n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.877857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a9fe3daa5c473abd32de4caf34e67510acf7f482dc176e81e6ef599b6b431c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] For $0<\eps\le1$, constants $A_0,L_0,D_{\cX},D_{\cY}<\infty$, $\gamma_{\mathrm{osc}},q\ge0$, and metric dimensions $\mathfrak d_{\cX},\mathfrak d_{\cY}\ge1$, let $\mathfrak M_\eps$ contain all models $(\cX,\cY,\mu,\nu,c_\eps)$ where the supports $\cX,\cY$ have covering numbers bounded by $(1+D_{\cX}/t)^{\mathfrak d_{\cX}}$ and $(1+D_{\cY}/t)^{\mathfrak d_{\cY}}$, respectively.
The cost takes the form $c_\eps(x,y) = a_\eps(x)+b_\eps(y)+\eps\ell_\eps(x,y)$.
The interaction $\ell_\eps$ must satisfy the oscillation bound $\osc_{\cX\times\cY}(\ell_\eps) \le A_0+\gamma_{\mathrm{osc}}\log(1/\eps)$ and feature Lipschitz conditions bounded globally as:
\begin{equation}
 \sup_y\operatorname{Lip}_x(\ell_\eps(\cdot,y)) \vee \sup_x\operatorname{Lip}_y(\ell_\eps(x,\cdot)) \le L_0\eps^{-q}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

