{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.904764+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ab3b9200838ded868ae30b3b2f58204a539ca6872bdd0a510928d416eecbbf5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma separability of arXiv:2411.11425, 'Non-equilibrium steady states with a spatial Markov structure'] Let $\{\Lambda^n\}_{n \geq 1}$ be a symmetric two-sided Markov family. For arbitrary $n\geq 1$ and $y\in \mathbb{R}^+$, there exist $y$-dependent functions $f_n,g_n$ and $h_n$ on $(\mathbb{R}^+)^2$ such that 

    \begin{equation}
        \Lambda_{a,b}^{n,1}(x) = f_n(a,b) \cdot g_n(b,x) \cdot h_n(x,a) \cdot \mathds{1}(x \in I_{a,b})
    \end{equation}

    for all $a,x,b \in \mathbb{R}^+$ such that $x \in I_{a,b}$ and $b \in I_{a,y}$. If a density is of this form we will refer to it as factorizable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.631944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ab42a75d545e89850347ece0feca01b95da51ceea2e02f765d3404d4aa9490a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ldp of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mu=\mu_n$ be such that $1/\sqrt{n}\ll\mu\ll n$.
    Let $\mathbf{T}_n$ be a $\mu$-height-biased tree of size $n$.
    Then the sequence of random variables $(h(\mathbf T_n)/(2\pi^2n/\mu)^{1/3})_{n \geq 1}$ satisfies a large deviation principle at speed $(\mu^2 n)^{1/3}$ and with good rate function given by
    \begin{align*}
        \Lambda^*(x)=\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
            \left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)^{2/3}\frac{(x-1)^2(2x+1)}{x^2} & \textrm{if $x>0$} \\
            \infty & \textrm{otherwise.}
        \end{array}\right.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.778371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ab705c85d16b34aa8fcccefd71498337872b598a92aa855e6cdb33cc2e35fa9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor eigencor of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] Assume in addition that $g,\mu$ and $W$ are such that the operator 
    \begin{equation}
