{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.441687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af107896f1d6211dc4189a8eb74149b79c038c58e1e9567291fc473aaa3fd01","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 30 (Maximal local solution and blow-up criterion) of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] Assume the conditions of Theorem \ref{thm:localexistence}. Then there exists a unique maximal local solution $(z,\tau_{\max})$ of \eqref{eq:FullNoiseSPDE} in the following sense:
