{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:27.977238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af2c5820169df6546af84454f0d5b2255a6b8f0a9a65c99d31bf3352497ead0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:VolumeCn of arXiv:2608.04162, 'Correlation Matrices in High Dimensions:\\ The Elliptope as a Sample-Correlation Ensemble'] The Lebesgue volume of $\mathcal{E}_n$ satisfies the recursion
$$
\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal{E}_{n+1})
=\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal{E}_{n})\times
\left[B(\tfrac{n+1}{2},\tfrac{1}{2})\right]^{n},\qquad n\geq1,
$$
with $\operatorname{Vol}({\mathcal{E}_{1}})\equiv 1$; consequently,
\begin{equation}
\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal{E}_n)
=\pi^{\frac{n(n-1)}{4}}
\prod_{j=1}^{n}\frac{\Gamma\big(\tfrac{j+1}{2}\big)}{\Gamma\big(\tfrac{n+1}{2}\big)},
\qquad\text{for }n\geq 1.
\end{equation}
For large $n$, $\log\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal{E}_n)=-\tfrac{n^2}{4}\log \frac{n}{2\pi\sqrt{e}}+O(n\log n)$ and in terms of $d=\tfrac{n(n-1)}{2}$ we have
\begin{equation}
\log\operatorname{Vol}(\mathcal{E}_n)
=-\tfrac{d}{4}\log(\tfrac{d}{2e\pi^2})-\tfrac{1}{2\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{d}-\tfrac{1}{48}\log d + \kappa
+O\big(\tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}\big), 
\end{equation}
where $\kappa=\tfrac{1}{4}\left[(1+\zeta(-1))\log 2-\zeta(-1)+2\zeta^\prime(-1)\right]\approx 0.097$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.375351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af43cb3d48f1b5fe338fd3adb40fd4b39539b0d20d35f015c08d89a70a7df67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor:moments of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $\beta\in\mathbb{R}$, $N\in\mathbb{N}$, $k\in\mathbb{N}$, and
	$\mathbf x=(x_1,\ldots,x_k)\in\mathbb{Z}^k$. Recall $\mathscr E_{\beta,k}$ from (equation eq:G-beta-k of the paper). Then, for every $t\ge0$ and every
