{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.597242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af468e31eab090f26b6e0fde5f97264190a1767491f635dddcc5ef7dbb04ee0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma2.0 of arXiv:2411.15724, 'Wasserstein Convergence Rates for Empirical Measures of Random Subsequence of $\{nα\}$'] For any $1 \leq p \leq \infty$ and $\nu \in \mathscr{P} (\mathbb{T})$,
\begin{align*}
\mathbb W_p(\nu, \mu) = \inf_{y \in \mathbb R} \| F_\nu - y \|_p \leq \| F_\nu - \widehat{F_\nu}(0) \|_p,
\end{align*}
where $F_\nu$ is the antiderivative of $\nu - \mu$ given by (equation def of anti of the paper). In the particular case $p = 2$,
\begin{align*}
\mathbb W_2^2(\nu, \mu) = \inf_{y \in \mathbb R} \| F_\nu - y \|_2^2 = \sum_{m \ne 0} \frac{|\widehat{\nu}(m)|^2}{4 \pi^2 m^2}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.004736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af64a1170a06a91cde408b4d732cc1600d774778958644bcf5e7435666c643c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corol:HHgenerale of arXiv:2606.27549, 'On Analytically Tractable Multidimensional Diffusions via Doob $h$-Transforms, with Resett'] For any  initial state ${\bf y}\in {\cal D}$, let us define the set 

\begin{equation}
    H_{\bf y}=\{{\bf x} \in {\cal D}:\;h({\bf x})=h({\bf y})\}.

\end{equation}

From Eq.\ ((2.1 of the paper)), for $\bf{y}\in  {\cal D}$ and $t>\tau\geq 0$, one has

\begin{equation*}
f({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)=\widehat{f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau),\qquad \forall \,{\bf x} \in H_{\bf y}. 
\end{equation*}

In addition, by defining the regions  

\begin{equation}
{\cal H}^-_{\bf y}=\left\{ {\bf x} \in {\cal D}:\;h({\bf x})<h({\bf y}) \right\} \quad \text{and} 
\quad 
{\cal H}^+_{\bf y}=\left\{{\bf x} \in {\cal D}:\;h({\bf x})>h({\bf y})\right\},

\end{equation}

we have

\begin{equation} 
f({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)<    (>)\, \widehat{f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau),
\qquad \forall \, {\bf x} \in {\cal H}^-_{\bf y}\; ({\bf x} \in {\cal H}^+_{\bf y}), 

\end{equation}

and thus  

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{l}
  {F}({\cal H}^-_{\bf y},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)
 = \widehat{F}({\cal H}^-_{\bf y},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)- \Pi (t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau),
\\
 {F}({\cal H}^+_{\bf y},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)
 =\widehat{F}({\cal H}^+_{\bf y},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)+ \Pi (t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau),
\end{array}

\end{equation}

where ${F}$ is defined similarly as 
$\widehat{F}$ in ((1.1 of the paper)), and  
$$
 \Pi(t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau):=\int_{{\cal H}^-_{\bf y}} 
 \left|\widehat{f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)- {f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau) \right|
    \,{\rm d}{\bf x}
    =\int_{{\cal H}^+_{\bf y}} 
 \left|\widehat{f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau)- {f}({\bf x},t\,|\,{\bf y},\tau) \right|
    \,{\rm d}{\bf x}.
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.846720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af691cda11b86a80fc10a04ea3ccda00d8baf58a33d0fad3617a9c1df051c65","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lemma-expression-U of arXiv:2607.08187, 'Asymptotic behaviours of critical branching random walk in $\mathbb{R}^d$'] For any $x>1$ and $\mathbf{y}\in \overline{D}_1$, we have 
	\begin{align}
		U_{(\gamma,\theta)}(\mathbf{y};x)  = G^x (\mathbf{y})
		-x^{-2} \mathbb{E}_{x\mathbf{y}}\bigg(\sum_{i=1}^{\tau_x-1}e^{-\gamma i x^{-\frac{2\alpha}{\alpha-1}}} \phi^{(x)}\Big(U_{(\gamma, \theta)}\Big(\frac{\mathbf{S}_{i}}{x};x\Big)\Big)\bigg),
	\end{align}
	here we used the convension that $\sum_{i=1}^0 =0$ on the set $\{\tau_x=1\}$. 
	Moreover, for any $\theta, \gamma\geq 0 $,
	\begin{align}
		\sup_{\mathbf{y}\in \overline{D}_1, x>1} U_{(\gamma, \theta)}(\mathbf{y};x)  \leq  C_\tau \gamma 
		+\theta=: \Gamma_{(\gamma, \theta)}<\infty.
