{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.650473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b3d1a6dcea8fe4ab642e9e756db3ed8b480c056b9557bd0178d8859d64654ea","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.04590, 'Singular stochastic delay equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: Dynamics, longti'] Assume $\frac{1}{3}<\alpha\leq\frac{1}{2}$ and  $X \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}^d$ be a locally $\alpha$-H\"older path and $r > 0$. For $r_1\in\lbrace 0,r\rbrace$ , a \emph{delayed L\'evy area} for $X$ is a continuous function
			\begin{align*}
				\mathbb{X}(-r_1) \colon \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}^d \otimes \mathbb{R}^d
			\end{align*}
			for which the algebraic identity
			\begin{align*}
				\mathbb{X}_{s,t}(-r_1)=\mathbb{X}_{s,u}(-r_1) + \mathbb{X}_{u,t}(-r_1)+X_{s-r_1,u-r_1}\otimes X_{u,t} 
			\end{align*}
			holds for every $s,u,t \in \mathbb{R}$ and for which $\| \mathbb{X}(-r_1) \|_{2\gamma ; I} < \infty$



			holds on every compact interval $I \subset \mathbb{R}$. If $\gamma \in (1/3,1/2]$ and $X$ admits L\'evy- and delayed L\'evy area $\mathbb{X}$ and $\mathbb{X}(-r)$, we call $ \mathbf{X}= \big{(}X, \mathbb{X}, \mathbb{X}(-r)\big{)}$ a \emph{delayed $\gamma$-rough path with delay $r > 0$}. We use $\mathscr{C}^{\gamma}_2(\mathbb{R}^d)$, to denote the space of (delayed) L\'evy areas.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.857248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b3ee1719db2431e1b028b16e43a30837e3125e7ee8052f0578487a478754d94","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2608.21063, '\textbf{Non-bijective scaling limits and phase transitions of planar maps}'] As $n \to \infty$,
