{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.236361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b40a05e3612011c5024214521db2dee46e527faf9248b164fcca7c2fd7445b5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2604.14427, 'A criterion for proving entropy chaos on path space'] Given $\mu, \nu \in \mathcal{P}(E), $ the relative entropy between the two measures is defined, when $\mu$ is absolutely continuous with respect to $\nu$ as
