{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.650782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b7f0b50a28a22188f6a1c059250bbd712ee9df3ad7ff844aaa61539a8a74b0c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:approx_strat_delay_f of arXiv:2411.04590, 'Singular stochastic delay equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: Dynamics, longti'] Let \(B^{\epsilon}\) be the regularized path in Definition (REGU of the paper) and 	
			\begin{align*}
