{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.309519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b97ec86ec4b28143d56caae22ee6a6688755f9bd4468ed9dbb480c9051689a0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2609.02392, 'Large values of cubic and quartic Dirichlet $L$-functions of prime moduli'] Suppose $\chi$ be a primitive Dirichlet character modulo $q$. Let $A$ and $B$ be positive real numbers with $AB = q$.  Then we have
\begin{align*}

L \left( \frac{1}{2} , \chi \right) = \sum_{m=1}^{\infty} \frac{\chi(m)}{m^{1/2 }} V_{\af}\left(\frac{m}{A}\right)
+ \epsilon(\chi) \sum_{m=1}^{\infty} \frac{\overline{\chi}(m)}{m^{1/2}} V_{\af}\left(\frac{m}{B}\right),
\end{align*}
  where
\begin{align*}
\epsilon(\chi) = i^{-\af} q^{-1/2} \tau(\chi), \quad V_{\af}(x) = \frac{1}{2\pi i} \int\limits_{(2)} \frac{G(s)}{s} \gamma_{\af}(s) x^{-s} \dif s,  \quad \gamma_{\af}(s) = \pi^{-s/2} \frac{\Gamma\left(\tfrac{1/2 + \af+ s}{2}\right)}{\Gamma\left(\tfrac{1/2 + \af}{2}\right)}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.483074+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b99cda9bd91d5e60a8d71b77b0cb00d7eba177953ec8d1d09539bdaa6f719de","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 121 (Optimal normalized constants across chaos order) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] For $\mathbb K\in\{\mathbb R,\mathbb C\}$ and $m\ge1$, let
