{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.592529+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ba4a74c49c070136ce377afc4220985814a1289e1de92009b304090cf695fa2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Satz: LR-Zerleg. superkrit. Reg. of arXiv:2509.15790, 'Covariance matrices of volume power functionals of random simplicial complexes -- an asymp'] For $n\geq2$ let $\Sigma_n$ be defined as in ((Eq: Kov.matrix Laengen Potenz Funktional of the paper)) in the supercritical regime. The following statements then hold.
\begin{enumerate}
\item 
An LU decomposition $\Sigma_n =LU$ of $\Sigma_n$ is given by the matrices $L= (l_{ij})\in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ and $U=(u_{ij})\in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ which have the entries
\begin{align*} 
l_{ij} = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
1&\text{ for }\,i=j,\\
\frac{a_1}{a_i} & \text{ for }\,i >1  \text{ and }  j=1,\\
0& \text{ else}.\\
\end{array}
\right.\, \text{ and }\,
u_{ij} = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\frac{1}{a_1a_j} & \text{ for }\,i=1,\\
0& \text{ else}.\\
\end{array}
\right.
\end{align*}
