{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.405497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bba415216f79d9d823f6784a932fd1845b42cef0649471dfcaa1db43b7e2832","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:xBhatproc of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] For each ${\widehat B}\in \widehat{\mathcal{K}}$, the process ${\boldsymbol{\pi}}^{{\widehat B},u,{\raisebox{1.3pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}}$  satisfies the following properties: 
