{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.161465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bf1b1e80e5bb1c63ad6009b542ee0e06b95c9939ab727885eb3d9468a39d352","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.17302, 'Elephant random walk with attributed steps and extractions of random sizes'] Assume that we are in Scenario~\eqref{Scenario_2}, and that each sample is drawn with replacement. Assume that $g$, defined in \eqref{g_defn}, satisfies one of the following criteria:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(B\arabic*), ref=B\arabic*]
\item  that $g$ is Lipschitz on $\mathcal{S}$, and that the series 
\begin{equation}
\sum_{n\geqslant N}(n+1)^{-1}\E\left[K_{n}^{-1/2}\right] \text{ converges};
\end{equation}
\item } that $g\in\mathcal{C}^{(1)}(\mathcal{S})$, and that the series 
\begin{equation}_series_convergence}
\sum_{n\geqslant N}\frac{1}{n+1}\min\left\{\omega\left(\nabla g;\sqrt{\E\left[K_{n}^{-1}\right]}\right)\sqrt{\E\left[K_{n}^{-1}\right]},\omega\left(\nabla g;\frac{\E\left[K_{n}^{-1}\right]}{\E\left[K_{n}^{-1/2}\right]}\right)\E\left[K_{n}^{-1/2}\right]\right\} \text{ converges};
\end{equation}
\item } that $g\in\mathcal{C}^{(2)}(\mathcal{S})$, and that the series 
\begin{equation}_series_convergence}
\sum_{n\geqslant N}(n+1)^{-1}\E\left[K_{n}^{-1}\right]\text{ converges}.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Then the sequence $\left\{\left(n^{-1}A_{n},n^{-1}B_{n}\right)\right\}$ converges almost surely to a (possibly sample path dependent) compact connected internally chain transitive invariant set, contained in $\mathcal{S}$, corresponding to the autonomous ODE:
\begin{equation}
\left(\dot{x}(t),\dot{y}(t)\right)=\hat{h}\left(x(t),y(t)\right) \text{ for }t\geqslant 0, \quad \text{with} \quad \left(x(0),y(0)\right)\in\mathcal{S},
\end{equation}
where the function $\hat{h}$ is as defined in \eqref{hat{H}_hat{h}_defn}, and $\mathcal{S}$ is as defined in \eqref{domain_defn}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.312720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bf5ed58f76b69ad088adb5f59745b0d576dc3b1b60b4978f8c696557284b398","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cltholder of arXiv:2411.08848, 'Stationary random measures: Covariance asymptotics, variance bounds and central limit theo'] (CLT for H\"{o}lder continuous statistics)

Let $\alpha \in [0,1]$. Let ${\mathcal X}$ be a simple  stationary point process on $\mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying Assumption (asmpt:integrationofrhokT of the paper). Assume that for all $m \geq 2$ and for all $l_i \in \mathbb{Z}_+, \sum_{i=1}^{m-1} l_i= m$, 

\begin{equation}

 \int_{(\mathbb{R}^d)^{m-1}}  \prod\limits_{i=1}^{m-1} |z_{i}|^{\alpha l_i}\; |\kappa_{m-1}|(z_1,\ldots ,z_{m-1}) \, \mathrm{d} z_1\ldots \mathrm{d} z_{m-1} < \infty.
 \end{equation}

Suppose that $f \in C_0^{\alpha}$ and ${\rm Var}[{\mathcal X}_L(f)] \geq CL^{-2\alpha + \varepsilon}$ for some $\varepsilon,C > 0$.  Then CLT holds for ${\mathcal X}_L(f)$, i.e.,

\[  \frac{{\mathcal X}_L(f) - \mathbb {E} [{\mathcal X}_L(f)]}{\sqrt{{\rm Var}[{\mathcal X}_L(f)]}} \stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N(0,1).\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.351061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bf7ba8a211c3045055732da74d1efb078312d8eb35c8314ff6f83e36bbebcd7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_steinmethod_gendif of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Let $X$ be a centered random variable in $L^2\autobracket*{E,\mu}$ and $F=X+m$.  Choose any $x\in \mathbb{R}$. Assume   the following moments  
conditions:
