{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.958953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bfac2a3c232e6cd8f694e1d31e0825a73b5af8a7531b5d00b39cdf52923a170","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2412.05764, 'A method of solution for the inverse problem for $h$-functions of planar Brownian motion'] The periodic Poisson integral takes the form
    \begin{align*}
        (P_y\ast f)(x) = \frac{1}{2}\int_T \frac{\sinh\pi y}{\cosh\pi y - \cos\pi(x-t)} f(t) dt.
    \end{align*}
	for $(x, y) \in T\times \mathbb{R}^+$. In the limit we have,
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{y\to\infty} (P_y\ast f) = \frac{1}{2}\int_T f(t)dt.
    \end{align*}
    This exists for $f\in L^p(T)$, and furthermore the Poisson integral is bounded on $L^p(T)$ and $P_y\ast f$ is harmonic on 
    $T\times \mathbb{R}^+$ with $\lim_{y\to 0} (P_y\ast f) = f$ almost everywhere.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.662784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bfbad6c26d6b03edc6f0ee0ae85a1dc773e3237f62aafa04c21484e39244b71","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn $L^r$-quantization error induced by a quantizer of arXiv:2506.01746, '\bf Optimal Bregman quantization: existence and uniqueness of optimal quantizers revisited'] Let  $r>0$ and let $\|\cdot\|$ denote any norm on $\mathbb{R}^d$.  Assume that the distribution $P$ has a finite $r$th moment i.e. $\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}\|\xi\|^rP(\mathrm{d}\xi)<+\infty$. Let $\Gamma  \subset \mathbb{R}^d$ be a  {\em quantizer}. We define the $L^r$-mean quantization error of the distribution $P$ induced by $\Gamma$ by 

\begin{equation*}
    e_r(\Gamma,P,\|.\|) = \left[\int_{\mathbb{R^d}}\min_{a\in\Gamma} \|\xi-a\|^rP(\mathrm{d}\xi)\right]^{\frac{1}{r}}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.833633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1bff8bec0d87f225f26d4f933dae8c89e930bd48afbbce98e01721dd21432045","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2609.03830, 'Parabolic Poincar\'e inequalities and maximal function estimates for systems of partial di'] Let $|F|\in L^2_{\loc}(\Om_T)$and assume that $u\in L^2_{\loc}(0,T;W^{1,2}_{\loc}(\Om;\mathbb{R}^N))$ is a weak solution to \eqref{eq}.
