{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.621303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c15f9f6409a991fe2254d723274af83c3848e9a1f9133bc426420bb0b199af6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma semigroup of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] Let $h\in L^2([0, 1])$. For each $\theta\ge0$, the semigroup $(P_t^\theta h)(u)$ can be written as
\begin{equation}
    (P_t^\theta h)(u)=\sum_{n=1}^\infty a_n e^{-\gamma_n t} \psi_n(u),
\end{equation}
for $(t, u)\in[0, \infty)\times[0, 1]$, where:
\begin{enumerate}[i)]

    \item $\{\psi_n\}_n$ is a complete, orthonormal basis of the $\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta)^{-1}$-weighted Hilbert space $L^2([0, 1], \Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta(u))^{-1}\de u)$, defined in (equation def:weighted_hilbert of the paper);

    \item $\{a_n\}_n$ are the coefficients of $h$ in that basis, namely $a_n=\langle h, \psi_n\rangle_{L^2([0, 1], \Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta)^{-1})}$;

    \item the sequence $\{\gamma_n\}_n$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \kappa_1((n-2)\pi)^2\le \gamma_n\le \kappa_2((n+1)\pi)^2
    \end{equation}
    for each $n\ge 2$, where
    \begin{equation}
        0<\kappa_1:=\myinf_{u\in[0,1]}\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta(u))\le \mysup_{u\in[0,1]}\Phi'(\bar\rho_\theta(u))=:\kappa_2<\infty.
    \end{equation}

\end{enumerate}
Consequently, the series (equation eq:explicit_semigroup of the paper) converges exponentially fast for $t>0$, and thus $(P_t^\theta h)(u)$ is smooth $(0, \infty)\times[0, 1]$. Moreover, if $h\in\mathcal{S}_\theta$, then $(P_t^\theta h)(u)$ is smooth $[0, \infty)\times[0, 1]$.","status":"unverified"}

