{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.351266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c1ed182d6ae234e5b49056a18515cfae8d975cbbd830d31ef106e0cc3f94d5a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] Let $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ be a $\Lambda$-coalescent with death according to $D(dz)$ where $D(\{0\}) = 0$. Similarly, let $(\widehat{X}(t))_{t \geq 0}$ be a $\Lambda_*$-coalescent where $\Lambda_*(dz) = 2\Lambda(dz) + D(dz)$. If $X(0) = \widehat{X}(0)$, then there exists a coupling of $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ and $(\widehat{X}(t))_{t \geq 0}$ and a random time $t^* > 0$ a.s. such that

