{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.139023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c26924263c227b19d324d61112d372a6a8a195ecd35ccc39722481b7c66ddc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.27569, 'Laplace and Dolbeault operators on Sasakian manifolds'] On the $\left( 2n+1\right) $-dimensional
Sasakian manifold with Lefschetz operator $L$ and adjoint $\Lambda $ and operator $H$, we have for all positive integers $b$, 
\begin{align*}
[L^{b},H] &= 2bL^{b}, \\
[L^{b},\Lambda] &= (-bH-b(b-1))L^{b-1}.
\end{align*}
As a consequence, the map $L^b:\Omega^m\to \Omega^{m+2}$ is injective for $m\leq n-b$ and $\Lambda^b:\Omega^m\to \Omega^{m-2}$, for $m\geq n+2b$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.027450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c287f715fca61bfbedcfbfa3dcf4996374b138c827aee58bdb2d0eef5335954","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma global_existence of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Under the conditions of Theorem (theo:tied-SGD of the paper), let $C_*$ be the uniform spectral bound in Lemma (lemma:bound-tied-SGD of the paper). For every finite $T>0$ and every pair $C_*^2<\rho_-<\rho_+$, there exists a unique admissible trajectory $\bar\mu\in C([0,T];X_{\rho_-}^0)$ such that
\begin{equation}
\bar\mu(t)=\bar\mu(0)+\int_0^tV(\bar\mu(s))\,ds,
\qquad t\in[0,T],

\end{equation}
where the identity is understood in \(X_{\rho_+}^0\). Moreover,
\begin{equation}
q(\bar\mu(t))\succeq0,
\qquad t\in[0,T],
\end{equation}
and $|\bar\mu_\alpha(t)|\le C_*^{2|\alpha|}$
for every multi-index $\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

