{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.535452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c29aa8cb9a51e60aebf5ded2882e547e61cbf412a371d1d78a5d10d5002d5da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.decom_DF_j of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Let $F_*, F_\circ$ follow the decomposition (equation eq.def_WIP_new of the paper), and $v_{m}$ follow the canonical grain extension in Definition~(def.ConstantExtension_canonical of the paper). Given ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m \in  \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{k}$ and ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \in \mathcal{P}^{(N,k)}_{h}$, we have the identity
