{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.236761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c36138eb74a7506b05e274c05d73785137d9631d01c68153620af5f12a596e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 33 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let $f \colon Y \to X$ be a qcqs morphism of qcqs $\F_p$-schemes.
