{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.236093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c3a8b382e26f31c4d846f6190738928833842ff6d8d3619a39cff2ae893059d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2512.10536, 'Large deviations for invariant measure of the stochastic Allen-Cahn equation with inhomoge'] For every $t>0$, $r >0$ and $x \in E$, there exists $\bar{R}_r$ such that
