{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.461395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cc7fe19b8528a3da4700222ab958558bfec92290bca4f029a79db2c6f1ee5fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma local control of arXiv:2505.11721, 'Variational principles for Hausdorff and packing dimensions of fractal percolation on self'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm-2.4 of the paper)(1), if $\log(m)=o(\ell_m)$ and with probability~1, conditional on $\nu\neq 0$, for $\nu$-almost every $\boldsymbol{i}$, one has 
