{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.306106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ccaf1b6b56c822dc0da8039b2dca1261d5cfce9558d4fc9b06052b15b11f837","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (LSE Hessian Lipschitzness) of arXiv:2608.21995, '2608.21995'] For any fixed $\tau>0$, $\nabla^2\operatorname{LSE}_\tau$ is Lipschitz on any compact convex domain $D\subset\mathbb{R}^K$. More explicitly, there exists $L_{\tau,K}<\infty$ such that, for all $x,y\in D$,
