{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.897772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cd639bd276b8ab57f81d4f4a0334383aadde3fce09b0dd896f5eae4e17cdc18","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:nonzero of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let $(M,g)$ be a compact Riemannian manifold of dimension $n\ge 2$ without conjugate points. Let us consider the monochromatic case: $\phi_\ell:=\phi_I^M$, with $I=[\ell-\eta_\ell, \ell]$, where $\eta_\ell=\mathrm{o}(\ell)$. Assume in addition that: if the dimension is $n=2$, then $\eta_\ell\log\ell=\mathrm{O}(\ell)$. Then, we have
      \begin{equation}
{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left( \frac{\mathrm{Vol}^{n-1}(\{x:\phi_\ell(x)=t\sigma_\ell(x)\})[2]}{\lambda_\ell}\right)\ge\Theta\left( \frac{1}{N^M_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}}\right),
    \end{equation}
where $\sigma_\ell(x)^2:={\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}(\phi_I^M(x))$ and $\lambda_\ell:=\lambda\left( \phi_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}^M\right)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.077584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cd64d4212b843fde1281e990f1adaeaf6d98bc68c1677abbdb95a32f70e5f0b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 29 of arXiv:2510.26216, 'A functional Breuer-Major theorem with Poisson noise'] For every $\eps>0$ and every $m\ge d$, we have
        \begin{equation}
            \lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathbf{E}(\widetilde{Y}^{\eps,m}_n)^{2p} =(2p-1) !!  \bigg( \var \sum_{j=1}^{N} b_j B_{t_j} \bigg)^p  \mu_{\eps,m}^{2p},
        \end{equation}
    and
        \begin{equation}
            \lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathbf{E} ( \widetilde{Y}^{\eps,m}_n)^{2p-1} =0,
        \end{equation}
    where $\mu_{\eps,m}^2=\big\langle\widehat{\phi}_\eps^{\otimes 2},\widetilde{\bB}_{2,m}\big\rangle$. As a consequence of the moment method, $\widetilde{Y}^{\eps,m}_n$ converges in law to $\mu_{\eps,m} \sum_{j=1}^N b_j B_{t_j}$, where $(B_t)_{t \in [0,1]}$ is a standard Brownian motion.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.840953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cdbc5bf66abd25f593612267576b3521050bb9215c8efb07c600c11d7c709a8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 (Hierarchical Laplacian) of arXiv:2609.03647, 'Extension Problems for the Vladimirov--Taibleson Operator and the Hierarchical Laplacian'] Let $C:\mathcal{B}\to(0,+\infty)$ be a strictly positive choice function
    such that, for every $B\in\mathcal{B}$,
    \begin{align*}
        \sum_{\substack{D\in\mathcal{B}\\D\supseteq B}}C(D)<+\infty,
    \end{align*}
    and, for every $x\in X$, along the descending chain
    $B_k(x)\ni x$ described above,
    \begin{align*}
        \sum_{\substack{D\in\mathcal{B}\\D\supseteq B_k}}C(D)
        \longrightarrow+\infty
        \qquad(k\to+\infty).
    \end{align*}

    For $f\in \mathcal{S}(X)$, the hierarchical Laplacian $L_Cf(x)$ is
    defined pointwise by the series
    \begin{align*}
        L_Cf(x)
        =\sum_{\substack{B\in\mathcal{B}\\B\ni x}}
        C(B)\left(f(x)-\frac{1}{m(B)}
        \int_Bf(y)dm(y)\right).
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.482829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cdd3dee86c8fb2dce009f7acd004170f88c717e268875eb5b5eeaacf290de63","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 27 of arXiv:2607.28238, 'Well-posedness and large deviations for the obstacle problem of first-order stochastic con'] The kinetic solution $u^{h}_{\alpha}$ of \eqref{eq:skeleton-obstacle-problem-viscous} converges to the kinetic solution $u^{h}$ of \eqref{eq:skeleton-obstacle-problem} uniformly on $h\in S_M$. That is,
