{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.942816+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ce5e096c40a9455a0c60019f6313d8eac670069086b442354ced5ac3133838e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 (Conditionally sub-Gaussian vector) of arXiv:2608.24426, 'Sequential operator learning under dependent data'] Let $\outH$ be a Hilbert space, $\{\filtration_\iteridx\}_{\iteridx=0}^\infty$ a filtration, and let $\{\vnoise_\iteridx\}_{\iteridx\in\N}$ denote a sequence of $\outH$-valued random variables adapted to $\{\filtration_\iteridx\}_{\iteridx=1}^\infty$. Then $\vnoise_\iteridx$ is said to be conditionally $\vncov$-sub-Gaussian, given a bounded positive-semidefinite linear operator $\vncov$ on $\outH$, if:
    \begin{equation}
        \forall \iteridx\geq 1, \quad \forall \outfun \in \outH, \quad \expectation[\exp(\inner{\outfun, \vnoise_\iteridx}) \mid \filtration_{\iteridx-1}] \leq \exp\left(\frac{1}{2}\inner{\outfun, \vncov \outfun} \right) \as.

    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

