{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.655651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ce99e75d037265e5dcc5fa5709c624d615ae8ae932592daa1ce2fcd838d9568","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_exit_exp of arXiv:2603.29442, 'A compact support property for infinite-dimensional SDEs with Hölder continuous coefficien'] There are constants $c_3>0$ and $C_2 \geq 1$ such that for all $\delta \in (0,1]$ and all $\zeta >0$ satisfying $2\delta \zeta^{1-2\gamma} \leq 1$, for all $n \in \mathbb{N}_0$ and $\mathbb{P} \in \mathscr{M}_{\gamma,\delta}(I_n)$, 
