{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.580371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cf1934119c36621036eb9d34a591d20ebca30cfb58db55f1915e504e372c30b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:longEdges of arXiv:2411.10333, 'Subcritical annulus crossing in spatial random graphs'] We define for all \(r>0\) and \(c>0\) the \emph{presence of long edges} event as
		\begin{equation}
			\mathcal{L}(r,c):=\big\{\exists\ \boldsymbol{x}\sim \boldsymbol{y}\colon |x|<r, |x-y|>cr \big\}.
		\end{equation} 
		That is, we can find an edge of length at least \(cr\) in \(\mathscr{G}\) with one endpoint being located in \(B(r)\). We say that \(\mathscr{G}\) has 
		\begin{equation*}\tag{\(\mathscr{L}\)}
			\text{Property } \mathscr{L}_\lambda \quad \text{ if } \quad \limsup_{r\to\infty}\mathbb{P}_\lambda(\mathcal{L}(r,c))=0 \quad \text{ for all }c>0.  
		\end{equation*}
		If Property \(\mathscr{L}_{\lambda'}\) is \emph{uniformly} fulfilled for all \(\lambda'\leq \lambda\), we say that the graph has Property \(\overline{\mathscr{L}}_\lambda\). More precisely, \(\mathscr{G}\) has 
		\begin{equation*}\tag{\(\overline{\mathscr{L}}\)} 
			\text{Property } \overline{\mathscr{L}}_\lambda \quad \text{ if }\quad \limsup_{r\to\infty}\sup_{\lambda'\leq \lambda}\mathbb{P}_{\lambda'}(\mathcal{L}(r,c))=0 \quad \text{ for all }c>0.
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.490897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cf660ad60a18afeed5789e29695cd79c77c3f75fe6d90c9dfdf13ee94f7ffd1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2607.04012, 'Hölder regularity for backward stochastic Volterra integral equations and applications to '] Suppose that $\Psi^\pi \in L^{p}\big(\Omega; L^2(0,T) \big)$, that $G^{\pi,0} \in \mathcal{H}_{\Delta}^{p}(0,T)$, and that $G^\pi$ is uniformly Lipschitz in $(y,z)$, with Lipschitz constant $[G^\pi]_{L}$. Then the BSDE system \eqref{def:BSDE-app-BSVIE} admits a unique solution $(Y^\pi, Z^\pi )$ with
    \begin{gather*}
         \big(Y^\pi(t_k, \cdot), Z^\pi(t_k, \cdot) \big) \in \mathcal{H}^{p}(t_k,T) \times \mathcal{H}^p(t_k, T)
    \end{gather*}
    for each $k\in\{0,\dots,N-1\}$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C>0$, depending only on $p$, $T$ and $[G^\pi]_L$, such that 
    \begin{flalign*}
       \mathbb{E}\Bigg[ 
        \sup_{s\in[0,T]}
        \bigg(
        \sum_{k:t_k\leq s}
        \Delta_k &
        |Y^\pi(t_k,s)|^2
        \bigg)^{\frac p2} + 
        \bigg(  
        \int_{0}^{T}
        |Y^\pi(\tau(r),r)|^2\,dr
        \bigg)^{\frac p2}
         \\ &+
        \bigg(
        \sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \Delta_k
        \int_{t_{k+1}}^T
        |Z^\pi(t_k,s)|^2\,ds 
        \bigg)^{\frac p2}
        \Bigg]
        \leq
        C\bigg(
        \norm{\Psi^\pi}_{2,p}^p
        +
  \norm{G^{\pi,0}}_{\mathcal{H}_{\Delta}^p}^{p}
        \bigg).
    \end{flalign*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.367958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cf7bae81b6e47a2b23049177ad4a4822c96fa115e77a81d0ba3e2f12989d383","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2606.03122, 'Propagation of support for super-Brownian motion with general branching mechanism'] Suppose that $\Psi$ satisfies Condition \ref{con_localize}. Then, for $\theta>0$, $t\geq 0, R>0$ and $x\in B(0,R)$, we have
