{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.654904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d050f49b1aa689130851ee59e21b209a50038eef8434bb242f88e75d10772bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition State of detachment vs. detachment time of arXiv:2512.05896, 'T\'oth's buses and the ``detachment process'''] When $L_k=n$, we say the process is in a \emph{state of detachment}. But $k$ is called a \emph{detachment time} only when $L_{k-1}<n$ and $L_k=n.$

