where $ \ell(r) $ is defined in (equation def: s(r) of the paper) and $f(r)$ is defined as in Lemma~(lemma: range_estimates_main_text of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.810173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d0c40983f2f38b199d27a63dde9dd8babece4421df911e3c9adb3f9995412cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:stoch_int_bd of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $s\in (0,d/2)$. For every $(\mathcal{F}_t)_t$-progressively measurable process $M$ with paths in $L^2_t(H^{-s}_{\div})$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s., the stochastic integral
	\begin{align*}
		N_t:= \int_0^t B[M_r] \,\mathrm{d} W^\mathcal{K}_r
	\end{align*}
	is a well-defined local martingale with values in $\dot{H}^{-s-1}_{\div}$ and the following bound holds for its quadratic variation $[N]$:
	\begin{align} 
		\trace_{\dot{H}^{-s-1}_{\div}}[N]_t  = \int_0^t \| B(M_r) \|^2_{\operatorname{HS}(H^{d/2 + \alpha}_{\div}; \dot{H}^{-s-1})} \,\mathrm{d} r \lesssim \int_0^t \|M_r\|_{H^{-s}}^2 \,\mathrm{d} r.
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.413566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d0c7fcd1e990588378ef02e77b6ef4a4e579db606c063ba229012805a063c76","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:complement_r_connected}
