{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.576563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d1d5ce3b8ece9f115a0347864a3a0b8519eff42362b3a5ea607cff9212035f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:one-to-one of arXiv:2605.16086, 'Loop pruning and downward deviations for maximum local time of discrete-time simple random'] Let $E$ be a finite set of loops and let $s'$ be an \(E\)-pruned finite path. Define
