{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.948254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d42329f4281a262af615aa892d2f1039820e0761b858301c33113d1a8bf1614","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:soft_ogp of arXiv:2412.03511, 'Near-optimal shattering in the Ising pure $p$-spin and \\ rarity of solutions returned by '] If $\beta \in (\bar{\beta}_{d}, \beta_c)$, there exists $\varepsilon>0$, $c>0$ and $0\le \underline{q}<\overline{q} \le 1$ depending on $\beta$ and $\xi$ such that for all $\tau \in [0,1]$, 
  \begin{equation}
     \operatorname{\mathbb{E}} \mu_{\beta,\bm{G}}\Big(\Big\{\bm{\sigma} : \exists\, \bm{\sigma}' \in S_{(1-\varepsilon)\beta}(\bm{G}_\tau),\,\,\textup{s.t.}\,\,  \underline{q} \le \langle \bm{\sigma},\bm{\sigma}'\rangle/N  \le \overline{q} \Big\}\Big) \le e^{-cN}\,.
\end{equation}

In the case $\tau = 1$, if $\beta \in (\bar{\beta}_{d}, \beta_c)$ then for any $\bm{\sigma} \in \{-1,+1\}^N$,
\begin{equation}
