\end{equation} 

Finally in the case of the pure $p$-spin $\xi(x)=x^p$, for $\varepsilon'>0$, if $\beta \in \big((1+\varepsilon')\sqrt{(2\log p)/p},\\ \sqrt{2\log 2} \big)$, there exists $p_0$, $\delta>0$ and $c'>0$ all depending only on $\varepsilon'$ such that for all $p \ge p_0$, the bounds~(equation eq:soft_ogp of the paper) and~(equation eq:tauequal1 of the paper) hold with $\underline{q} = 1 - \delta/p$, $\overline{q} = 1- 1/p^{1+\delta}$ and $\varepsilon = c'\sqrt{(\log p)/ p}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.385040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d4313a04a1b2d412c38272f826d01042171427770595ab2a78486df5031be72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.03248, 'Connections between colored restricted $b$-ary and ordinary partitions'] For integers $\rho\geq 1$ and $n\geq 1$,the number $Y_n$ defined in \eqref{6.1}
