{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.169429+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d49ebbb409ab9180365ed164523217156498317d91adeb152c6e4fd44584ab6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.01774, 'Hypoellipticity on time-periodic space-times'] Let $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$ be an irrational number which is not a Liouville number.  Let $\nu>\mu(\alpha)$. Then there exists $C>0$ such that 
