    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.925284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d70cd0d0623b2f36e488d5800b94e049092ff3ee0079110a22d8f31fffaaeee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 17 of arXiv:2603.27433, 'The $k$-cycle shuffling with repeated cards'] Let $P_{n,k}$ be the random permutation in $\S_n$ given by
\begin{equation}
P_{n,k}:=\begin{cases}
(i_1\ldots i_k) & \text{with probability }\frac{k}{n(n-1)\cdots(n-k+1)}\\
\text{otherwise} & \text{with probability zero}\end{cases}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $t\ge 1$, let $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ be the $t$-fold convolution of $P_{n,k}$. If $k$ is even and $t$ is odd, we view $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ as a random variable in $\A_n^c$; otherwise, we view $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ as a random variable in $\A_n$. Given $n=ml$ with $l\ge 2$, the random variable $\sim_l\backslash P_{n,k}^{*t}\in\sim_l\backslash\S_n$ is induced from \Cref{defi: quotient of space} in the obvious way.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.581996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d71a830ffa38cb6ca1247800f71692b6121a2d21843c58cbaddfb68e203e037","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 61 (Trace-normalized nuclear minimizers are PSD) of arXiv:2608.27372, 'Universality and sharp thresholds for ellipsoid fitting'] Assume the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:phase-transition} and
