{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.379942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d733c29bdf3dc62f1cb866c273e33e468e068575411ba22fd81a86e62769a37","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 23 of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Suppose $\vecbf n \in \ZZ^d$, $\permelt \in \permgrp_d$, and $I = \{u(0), \ldots u(m)\} \subseteq \indexset{0, d}$ with $u(0) < \cdots < u(m)$. Then $(t_1, \ldots t_d) \in \vecbf n + \permelt (\partial_I \simp_d)$ holds iff the following hold:
    \begin{align} 
        1 & = t_{\permelt(1)} = \cdots = t_{\permelt(u(0))} \ge t_{\permelt(u(0)+1)} = \cdots = t_{\permelt(u(1))} \ge \cdots \nonumber \\
        & \cdots \ge t_{\permelt(u(m-1)+1)} = \cdots = t_{\permelt(u(m))} \ge t_{\permelt(u(m)+1)} = \cdots = t_{\permelt(d)} = 0
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.858300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d736838681dfcba5cc1d29c82fab30ca97874f014804c1b8c3575f49fac2651","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:supp_lmeasx of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The set $\mathcal{G}_0 \coloneqq \{z \in \mathrm{HC} \mid z_a=0\}$ is a measurable set of full measure w.r.t.\ $\mu^{(a)}$ and $\var{\sigma^{(a)}}$, (where we identify $\mathcal{G}_0$ with its canonical embedding into $[C_0]$,) but it is not closed as a subset of $(C_0, \| \cdot \|_{\infty})$. Identifying the considered measures with their restrictions to $\mathcal{B}(L)\cap [C_0]$ or $\mathcal{B}(C_0,\|\cdot\|_{\infty})$ (see Remark (rem:embeddings_and_measurability of the paper)), it holds that
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathrm{supp} \, \mu^{(a)} = \mathrm{supp} \var{\sigma^{(a)}} = \{z \in C_0 \mid z_a=0\},
    \end{equation*}
    where the support is defined w.r.t.\ the topology on $C_0$ induced by $\| \cdot \|_{\infty}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.385748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d746bd2d89af3dfacacbbb177670933b2f9c2bc1e036e78dbcb5cd3d43c9b5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:global_clt_intro of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Define
\begin{equation}

    \sigma_n^2 = 
    \mleft( 1 - 2 p (1-p) \sum_{j=1}^K \beta_j \mathsf{e}_j (\mathsf{e}_j-1) p^{\mathsf{e}_j-2} \mright)^{-1}
    \times p(1-p) \binom{n}{2}.
\end{equation}
Then for any $\varepsilon > 0$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{d} \mleft( \frac{\mathsf{E}(X) - \mathbb{E}[\mathsf{E}(X)]}{\sigma_n}, Z \mright) \lesssim n^{-\frac{1}{2} + \varepsilon},
\end{equation}
for both $\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Was}$ and $\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Kol}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.240151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d74c8ee11db77c1c880c76e9af997a616fd38ac4bb66773230205abba2bbf3f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:diamond_def of arXiv:2604.22528, 'Malliavin calculus for signatures with applications to finance'] Fix three words ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_1}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_2}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{w}}} \in V$. For two words ${\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v'}}}$, define $\diamond^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_1}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_2}}}}_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{w}}}}: \TA\times\TA\to\TA$ by
    \begin{equation}
        {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}} \diamond^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_1}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{u_2}}}}_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{w}}}}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v'}}} 
        = \sum_{\substack{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_2}}}:\\{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1u_1v_2}}} = {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v}}}}}
          \sum_{\substack{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1'}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_2'}}}:\\{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1'u_2v_2'}}} = {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v'}}}}}
          ({\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1}}}\mathrel{\sqcup \mkern -3mu \sqcup}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_1'}}})\otimes{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{w}}}\otimes({\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_2}}}\mathrel{\sqcup \mkern -3mu \sqcup}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{v_2'}}}).
    \end{equation}
    For two tensor sequences $\bm{\ell}, \bm{\ell}' \in \TA$, the operator is extended by bilinearity. We also define $\diamond := \sum_{i = 1}^d \diamond^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i}}}, {\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{i}}}}_{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{0}}}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.730935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d75739c3a292a066084cf1cedd399ac3ff0c145544ffc41d8a70552fbe7d472","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem poisson_convergence of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $m\in\mathbb{N}$ and a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$ is satisfied for some $\varepsilon<1-1/((m+1)\log\theta)$ in Part~(item:hI of the paper) and some $\eta<1-1/((m+1)\log\theta)$ in Part~(item:Jn of the paper). Fix $\varepsilon^\mathrm{a},\varepsilon^\mathrm{f}\in[0,1]$ and let $\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{a}\overset \mathrm{d}=\mathcal{P}^{\varepsilon^\mathrm{a}}$ and $\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{f}\overset \mathrm{d}= \mathcal{P}^{\varepsilon^\mathrm{f}}$ be independent point processes. Let $(n_\ell)_{\ell\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a subsequence of integers such that $n_\ell\to\infty$ and $\varepsilon_{n_\ell}^\square\to\varepsilon^\square$ as $\ell\to\infty$ for $\square\in\{\mathrm{a},\mathrm{f}\}$. Then, $\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{a}^{(n_\ell)}$ and $\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{f}^{(n_\ell)}$ jointly converge weakly to $\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{a}$ and $\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{f}$ as $\ell\to\infty$  in $\mathcal{M}^\#_{\mathbb{Z}^*}$, respectively. Equivalently, for any $i<i^\prime\in\mathbb{Z}$ and $j<j'\in\mathbb{Z}$, jointly as $\ell\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
({}&X_i^{(n_\ell)},\ldots,X_{i^\prime-1}^{(n_\ell)},X_{\geq i^\prime}^{(n_\ell)},Y_j^{(n_\ell)},\ldots,Y_{j^\prime-1}^{(n_\ell)},Y_{\geq j^\prime}^{(n_\ell)})\\ 
&\buildrel {\mathrm{d}}\over{\longrightarrow}(\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{a}}\{i\},\ldots,\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{a}}\{i^\prime -1\},\mathcal{P}_\mathrm{a}[i^\prime,\infty),\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{f}}\{j\},\ldots,\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{f}}\{j^\prime -1\},\mathcal{P}_{\mathrm{f}}[j^\prime,\infty)).
\end{aligned}\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.659172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d771ca4da6727674a8e8a8325aebffd68d36a20fe5f1cd1a300c3d67ea4c872","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:walk-overshoot of arXiv:2411.10113, 'Long-range one-dimensional\\ internal diffusion-limited aggregation'] Suppose that~(equation ass:irreducible of the paper) and~(equation ass:moments of the paper) hold. 
