 are finite and equal.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.304387+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1da49c2d58345d65cf03fd34cb23f95fc389e1ac559d45caeb1b46b5ed70ee5e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem DistribXrho of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<1$, there exists $ {\mathbf{c_{_0}}}>0$ such that for $x$ large if $\overline{y}>x$. There exists a function ${\bf c} : \mathbb{N}^2 \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, such that for any  $\overline{y}-x \leq A x^{\alpha} $, 
