{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.348950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dc1aa6fbd6d4d72eace8674879ad1b38294d77b37f68a2721b1917f08aee73f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:interpolation of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $N \ge 1$, let $W_1, \dots, W_N$ be independent copies of $(x x^\top - I_d)/\sqrt d$, and let $G_1, \dots, G_N$ be independent copies of (equation eq:G-def of the paper), independent of the $W_i$'s.  Suppose $F : (\mathsf{S}^d)^N \to \mathbb{R}$ is $C^3$ with bounded first three Fr\'echet derivatives, and put
\[
M_3(F) = \sup_{A \in (\mathsf{S}^d)^N} \sum_{i=1}^N \|D_i^3 F(A)\|_{\pi,\mathrm{op}},
\qquad
R_{N,d} = \mathbb{E} \max_{1 \le i \le N} \|x_i\|_2^2 .
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
\bigl| \mathbb{E} F( \{W_i \}) - \mathbb{E} F(\{G_i \}) \bigr|
\;\le\; \frac{4 R_{N,d}}{3\, d^{3/2}}\, M_3(F) .
\end{equation}
Moreover
\begin{equation}
R_{N,d} \;\le\; d + 2\sqrt{d \log N} + 2 \log N ,
\end{equation}
so that for every fixed $C_{\mathrm{row}} < \infty$, if $N \le C_{\mathrm{row}} d^2$, then for all sufficiently large $d$,
\begin{equation}
\bigl| \mathbb{E} F(\{W_i \}) - \mathbb{E} F(\{G_i \}) \bigr| \;\le\; \frac{C}{\sqrt d}\, M_3(F),
\end{equation}
with $C$ an absolute constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.997162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dc4e525a2fea5567ffbc376056c0596bac6c642ead9eaaafa2792d017ea2791","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 51 of arXiv:2604.01685, 'Probability with Measure\footnote{Lecture notes. University of Ljubljana.}'] Let  $(\Omega,\FF,\mu)$ be a measure space and $(f_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence in $\FF/\mathcal{B}_{[0,\infty]}$. Then 
