{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dd340bcac303a9fd29b337941d5a33bd12687bb6b5a3cddfd8f543095138fad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr:decay_1 of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] If $\alpha_0$ is sufficiently small, then there exist constants $0 < \rho < 1$ and $C > 0$ such that for any $u[0]$ with $V_{\alpha_0}(u[0]) < \infty$, we have 
