{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.936185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ddad8de98a416f193014b0cffce6ea2fce909bfaa25e1fec24bdbb82f363505","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For any $\beta>0$, there is a unique family of time-dependent (stationary) continuous random processes --- denoted by $\{\mathcal{A}^\beta_i(\boldsymbol{\tau})\}_{i=1}^\infty$ --- such that they are ordered $\mathcal{A}^\beta_1\ge \mathcal{A}^\beta_2\ge \dots$; and for any $m\in \mathbb N$, $\vec \mathbf k \in \mathbb R^m_+ $, and $\vec \boldsymbol{\tau}\in \mathbb R^m$ such that $\boldsymbol{\tau}_1\le \cdots \le \boldsymbol{\tau}_m$, the joint moment for the Laplace transforms
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb E\left[ \prod_{\ell=1}^m \left(\sum_{i=1}^\infty
\exp(\mathbf k_\ell \mathcal{A}^\beta_i(\boldsymbol{\tau}_\ell)/2) \right) \right]
\end{equation}
equals $\mathbf L_\beta(\vec\mathbf k,\vec\boldsymbol{\tau})$, which is defined below in (defn:core of the paper)\footnote{The factor of dividing by $2$ in (equation eq_expected_Laplace of the paper) is to simply the expressions in (defn:core of the paper), avoiding various extra factors there. It also comes up naturally in the edge scaling limits.}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.654626+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ddb2beb20a7d1eab1ffc9aafeecf7afa01df53ad714caf7c2d84492f18dfca9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.04631, 'Existence of Martingale Solutions to Stochastic Constrained Heat Equation'] Let $Y_k$ satisfies \textbf{[T]}. Assume $\mathbb{P}_k$ be the distribution/law of $Y_k$ on $C ([0,T],\mathcal{S})$, $k \in \mathbb{N}$. Then 
