{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.495218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dfe512e4dc00f1354e77a5111ac0cfafe8bc9d897e8c7e49e50d459251d0bab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 (Moments of the corrected large side) of arXiv:2607.04138, 'Hives from deformed GUE minor processes'] \lab{prop:large-side-moments}
Let
\[
Q_n=\frac{\E|L_n|^2}{n^2}.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}\lab{eq:large-side-Q}
Q_n=n^{21}+O(n^{20}).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{align}
\frac{\E|\lambda_n|^2}{n^2}&=a^2n,&
\frac{\E|\lambda'_n|^2}{n^2}&=b^2n,\lab{eq:large-side-spectral-moments}\\
\frac{\E\langle L_n,\diag(X_n)\rangle}{n^2}
&=un^{11}+O(n^{10}),&
\frac{\E\langle L_n,\diag(Y_n)\rangle}{n^2}
&=u'n^{11}+O(n^{10}),\lab{eq:large-side-mixed-moments}\\
\frac{\E|\diag(X_n)|^2}{n^2}&=w^2+u^2n,&
\frac{\E|\diag(Y_n)|^2}{n^2}&=(w')^2+(u')^2n.\lab{eq:large-side-diagonal-moments}
\end{align}
Consequently, for
\[
N_n=L_n+\diag(X_n),\qquad P_n=L_n-\diag(Y_n),
\]
one has
\begin{equation}\lab{eq:large-side-exterior-moments}
\frac{\E|N_n|^2}{n^2}
=Q_n+2un^{11}+O(n^{10}),\qquad
\frac{\E|P_n|^2}{n^2}
=Q_n-2u'n^{11}+O(n^{10}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.297947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dff18290b653b86d9429bc8aad4223194ebf75a43eb5f0167e1649eaeb84f02","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 (Lemma~A.2 in \cite{forien_stepping_2019}) of arXiv:2606.23242, 'Correction to ``The stepping stone model in a random environment'' - limit theorems for th'] There exists a constant $ C > 0 $ such that, for $ \mu $-almost every $ \omega \in \Omega $,
		\begin{align*}
			\sup_{t \geq 0} \sup_{x, y, z \in \Z} t^{3/4} \frac{\abs{h^\omega_t(x,y) - h^\omega_t(x,z)}}{\abs{y-z}^{1/2}} \leq C.
		\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.760291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dffe3b55658052c1eca998812f02b579041631c1f95200024d6dde10f3c3f74","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:A^(n)phi(u) of arXiv:2411.02459, 'Existence and higher regularity of statistically steady states for the stochastic Coleman-'] Suppose for $n\ge 1$, $\varphi\in C^{2n}(\mathbb{R})$ and $u\in H^{2n}$. Then,
\begin{align} 
\Delta^n\varphi(u)& = \varphi'(u)\Delta^n u+ c_n\varphi''(u)\nabla u\cdot \nabla \Delta^{n-1}u +\varphi^{(2n)}(u)|\nabla u|^{2n} \notag \\
&\quad\ +\sum_{i=2}^{2n-1}\varphi^{(i)}(u)\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}I_{ij}(u),
\end{align}
where $c_n>0$, $I_{ij}(u)=c_{ij}\prod_{k=1}^{m_{ij}}(D^{\alpha_{ijk}}u)^{n_{ijk}}$ with $c_{ij}>0$, $|\alpha_{ijk}|\le 2n-2$, and $\alpha_{ijk}\in \mathbb{Z}^+$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.467415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e00330afb02ed69fa2b75d146b82a248e277732077e5d6e1dbe948ab3794e45","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 30 (directional mass retracts) of arXiv:2604.04267, 'On Sharpest Tail Bounds for Functions \\ of Tail Bounded Random Variables'] Let $W \subset [0,\infty)^n$ be closed. For $k=1,...,n$, $\forall x = (x_1,...,x_n) \in \mathbb{R}^n$, denote
\begin{equation}
h_k(x) = \inf \Big\{y \in \mathbb{R} \ \big| \ (x_1,...,x_{k-1},y,x_{k+1},...,x_n) \in W  \Big\}
\end{equation}
from which we define
\begin{equation} 
\Gamma_k(x) := 
\begin{cases} 
\big(x_1,..,x_{k-1},h_k(x),x_{k+1},...,x_n\big) & \text{if } x_k \geq h_k(x) \\ 
x & \text{otherwise} 
\end{cases} 
\end{equation} 
Lastly, define $\Gamma := \Gamma_n \circ \cdots \circ \Gamma_1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.611842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e00630dca51f923627a02daa0fc8882c58d321141d7bf9f0b256bf5bbac9b65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:integrals of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d>8$ and $L \ge L_0$.
There is a constant $C>0$ such that for all $r \ge 2L+1$, $p \in [p_c - \delta_L, p_c)$, and $x\in \mathbb{T}_r^d$,
