{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.025662+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0536cef1e713466761be3f1cf669b5b95da6e653a8d716c269bc8c091bc656","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary lm:ds of arXiv:2608.09465, 'Balancing fractional Brownian motion'] Let $F:\mathbb R^m\to C([0,1])$ be linear and define
\begin{equation}
C_F\coloneqq\mathbb E_{z\sim N(0,I_m)}\bigl[\|F(z)\|_\infty\bigr].

\end{equation}
For any $u_1,\ldots,u_n\in\mathbb R^m$ with $\|u_i\|_2\leq\zeta$, there is a randomized polynomial-time algorithm returning $\sigma\in\{\pm1\}^n$ such that, with probability at least $1/2$,
\[
\left\|F\left(\sum_{i=1}^n\sigma_i u_i\right)\right\|_\infty
\leq (c\zeta)\cdot C_F
\]
for an absolute constant $c>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e06381bd8754576cd7020b6150e7efbb589e71c56a726d6b0975826401b74ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 78 ({\cite[Theorem 2.7.1) of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] {VWJ96}}]
  Let $I\subseteq \R$ be a bounded interval with Lebesgue measure $|I|>0$ and $\kappa\in (0,1]$.
  Then there exists a constant $C=C(\kappa)$ such that
  \begin{align*}
    \log N(C^{\kappa}_1(I),\|\cdot\|_{\sup},\varepsilon)\leq C(|I|+2)\varepsilon^{-\frac{1}{\kappa}},\qquad\varepsilon>0,
  \end{align*} 
  where 
  \begin{align*}
    C^{\kappa}_1(I)=\{f:I\to\R:\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}}\le 1\}.
  \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.515604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0abc50384b722468c60977a171a95d24f2f561aa0bffd25877daa2a0379b7b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 ({\cite[Theorem 1.4.1) of arXiv:2608.28528, 'Strong solutions of SDEs with critical discontinuities in diffusion coefficients'] {Ku}}]
Let $X(x)$, $x\in D$, be a random field with values in a Banach space $B$, where $D$ is a domain in $\mathbb R^d$.
Assume that there exist positive constants
$\gamma$, $C$, and $\alpha_i$, $i=1,\ldots,d$ with $ \sum_{i=1}^{d}\alpha_i^{-1}<1$ satisfying 
\begin{equation*}
\mathbf{E}\!\left[ \left\|X(x)-X(y)\right\|^\gamma \right] \leq C\left(   \sum_{i=1}^{d}  |x^i-y^i|^{\alpha_i}\right),
\quad x,y\in D.
\end{equation*}
where, $\|\cdot\|$ stands for the norm of the Banach space and $ x=(x^1,\ldots,x^d)$, $y=(y^1,\ldots,y^d)$.Then $X$ has a continuous modification. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.583715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0ac03fec30be87f95d8554506a1be2e3c802e77c8f999759b0c38a3df6ed7a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem scfg2 of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] If the conditions of (lem.scfg1 of the paper) hold, then the limiting measures in~(thm:criterion2:F of the paper) and~(thm:criterion2:Fsphere of the paper) are identical, namely $\nu_0$. In addition, letting $p\coloneqq e^b$,  one has $\lim_{n\to \infty} \lambda_{n} F(n)= p^{\xi}$ for some $\xi\in\mathbb R$ and the limiting measure can be decomposed as
		\begin{equation}

			\nu^{(\xi)}\coloneqq \lim_{n} \lambda_n \iota_n^*\mu = \nu_0\otimes \beta^{(\xi)},
		\end{equation}
		where $\beta^{(\xi)}$ is the measure on $\mathbb Z$ defined by $\beta^{(\xi)}(i)\coloneqq(p-1)p^{i-1+\xi}$ for $i\in \mathbb Z$. In particular, one has
		\begin{equation*}

			\iota_i^*\nu^{(\xi)} = p^{i} \nu^{(\xi)},\quad \forall i\in\mathbb Z.
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.471658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0b085e6040974d2d898e84b65feabf483fbbfe98f01b42889fd86ff1720a4d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: section h_nu of arXiv:2608.28278, 'Reduction of symmetric time-dependent Hamiltonian systems I: presymplectic principal $\R$-'] The section $h: V^*\Pi \to T^*Q$ restricts to a $G_\nu$-equivariant map $h_{\vert (J^V)^{-1}(\nu)}:(J^V)^{-1}(\nu) \to J^{-1}(\nu)$. Then, 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[(i)] The restriction $h_{|(J^V)^{-1}(\nu)}$ induces a section 
    $$h_\nu: (V^*\Pi)_\nu = (J^V)^{-1}(\nu)/G_\nu \longrightarrow (T^*Q)_\nu = J^{-1}(\nu)/G_\nu$$ characterized by 
    \begin{equation}
        h_\nu \circ \pi_\nu^V = \pi_\nu \circ h.
    \end{equation}

        \item[(ii)] $h_\nu^*\omega_h^\nu = \Omega_h^\nu$.
        \item[(iii)] The vector field $R_h^\nu$ on $(V^*\Pi)_\nu$, given in ((eq: ker Omega_h^nu = R_h^nu of the paper)), is $h_\nu$-projectable over the vector field $X_\nu$ on $(T^*Q)_\nu$, characterized by ((eq: X_F_h^omega_Q is pi_nu projectable over widetilde X_nu of the paper)), i.e.,
        $$T_{\pi_\nu^V(\beta_q)}h_\nu(R_h^\nu(\pi_\nu^V(\beta_q))) = X_\nu(h_\nu(\pi_\nu^V(\beta_q))), \quad \text{for all} \quad \beta_q \in (J^V)^{-1}(\nu).$$
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.480233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0b3eb3d208cd16692ad673bbcb58e11b1874e0750768aeddcfe6e5dd7bd61e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 43 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] With notation as above, let $g:S' \rightarrow S$ be either an open immersion satisfying $c_{X}(v)\in S'$ or a localization $S'=\Spec \sO_{S,\xi} \rightarrow S$ at a point $\xi \in c_{X}(v)$. Then
\begin{equation*}
\begin{gathered}
v_{\num}(D/S) = v_{\num}({g'}^{*}D/S'), \\
{g'}^{-1}(\NNef(D/S))= \NNef({g'}^{*}D/S'),
\end{gathered}
\end{equation*}
where $g':X \times_{S} S' \rightarrow X$ is the natural morphism.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.831628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e0c5ccfbd5352bc3943c3daf1438deb80ed38e4519b71f3a9ec34ab4fcc706d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:monotonicity of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] If $\mathbf{x}_- \preceq \mathbf{x}_+$, $\mathbf{y}_- \preceq \mathbf{y}_+$, $\bm{\lambda}_- \succeq \bm{\lambda}_+$,
$\mathbf{f}_- \preceq \mathbf{f}_+$, and $\mathbf{g}_- \preceq \mathbf{g}_+$, then
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x}_-,\mathbf{y}_-,\bm{\lambda}_-}_{n,\ell,r,\mathbf{f}_-,\mathbf{g}_-}
    \preceq
    \mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x}_+,\mathbf{y}_+,\bm{\lambda}_+}_{n,\ell,r,\mathbf{f}_+,\mathbf{g}_+}.
