{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.535742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e2c5d5374aca894dc9ff1a1474d8c180d3d6ed2d0f0a1fdf29b7fb431bf1c8a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2603.28212, 'Limit Laws for the Distance to Fr\'echet Means of Random Graphs'] For any graph $G \in \mathcal{G}_n$ with vertex degrees $D_1, D_2, \dots, D_n$, we have that
