{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.962253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e3f95a283ab0cc2d9052ae7741db71573a5bf354efa9412f15322650a8e8138","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] For the random variables given in~\eqref{eq:XYU}, some universal constant $C>0$, and all $1<t<t'$, we have 
 \begin{align*}
