{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.387682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e49dc082d312028ebd8aeae088d4602660cf2d4804fd661878d468e87bdf1ad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:gaussianZ of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] Under the additional assumption that $p_n\;\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\; p\in[0,1)$, we have
    \[
        \mu_{G_n+\frac{{Z}_n^\circ}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}}-\mu_{G_n+\sqrt{1-p}B_n}\;\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\;0\qquad\mbox{ weakly in probability},
    \]where $B_n$ is an $n\times n$ symmetric random matrix independent of $G_n$ and whose upper-triangular entries are independent and verify, for all $i\le j$,
    \[
        (B_n)_{ij}=\begin{cases}
            \mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{1}{{K_n}}\right) & \mbox{if }\quad 0 < \min\big(|i-j|,\, n - |i-j|\big) \le \frac{K_n}{2}, \\
            0 & \mbox{otherwise,}
        \end{cases}
    \]
    with $\mathcal{N}\left(0,1\right)$ the standard normal distribution.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.460548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e4a5e16d165c1bc05d0eba18c9a663e268207e69d63e562d65dd1111d1dba40","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.28307, 'Rigidity of closed $\lambda$-self-expanders'] \cite{okumura1974hypersurfaces}
Let $\lambda_1, \lambda_2, \cdots, \lambda_n, n\geq 3$, be real numbers such that $\sum_i\lambda_i=0$ and $\sum_i\lambda_i^2=\mu^2$. Then
$$\frac{-(n-2)\mu^3}{\sqrt{n(n-1)}}\leq \sum_i\lambda_i^3\leq \frac{(n-2)\mu^3}{\sqrt{n(n-1)}},$$
and equality holds if and only if at least $(n-1)$ of $\lambda_i$ are equal. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

