{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.277115+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e4fddd1284deae41c6d4286e9990f5b859145c9a3676cf6f3cbd9aef7f9de71","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 44 (Theorem 2.1 in \cite{G1990}) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Let $\mu, \nu \in \cP_2(\mathbb{R}^n)$. Let $(a, A) \in \bR^n \times \mathscr{S}_+(n)$ be the mean and covariance of $\mu$ and similarly let $(b, B) \in \bR^n \times \mathscr{S}_+(n)$ be those of $\nu$. Then
