{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.275715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e7d93e6bb4d50d119f00a674431345529cc0a616675389e269977b5ed1f0fa1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 (Projection) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Suppose that $\mathscr{K} \subset \mathscr{L}(N, d)$ is nonempty and satisfies Assumption \ref{ass:projection}. Then, for any $L \in \mathscr{L}(N, d)$ there exists $\hat{L} \in \mathscr{K}$ such that
