{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.894339+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e826cf40b0161967b2b5e353133630634d44ef45596bbeeee608979ea3e68f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 (\cite{Ber21}) of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Specializing the objects defined in this section to the setting of Definition~\ref{def:2_l_weights}, we have 
\begin{multline}
  K^{-1}( w_{\ell x'+i',ky'+j'},  b_{\ell x+i,ky+j}) 
