{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.317545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1e9743cb32e8eb9ba0b282a17a31829a1a2875bbf979bdc2d7522f0a5e0d67ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2608.30232, 'Strong Unique Continuation for Fractional Schr\"odinger Operators'] There exists a constant $C_0=C_0(n,\alpha) >0 $ such that, for every $m\ge1$ and every compactly supported $F$ satisfying
