{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.644107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1eb449b9855028e70d6f5ef31f24965cfffe0d885b2df972aca4f41d52bbde16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma EHI:l:234 of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $Z \sim N(0, I_d)$ be a standard $d$-dimensional Gaussian. There exist positive constants $C$ and $c$ (which may depend on $d$) such that for all $r \geq 1$,
