{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.488623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ec1a6409dd7b867c8256b39299934988fe1fde03432656011915651336840bd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Normalized Coulomb gas correlations for a divisor on the Riemann sphere of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] Let the divisor
$$
\boldsymbol{\sigma}=\sum \sigma_j \cdot z_j,
$$
where $\left\{z_j\right\}_{j=1}^n$ is a finite set of distinct points on $\widehat{\mathbb{C}}$.
The normalized Coulomb gas correlation $C[\boldsymbol{\sigma}]$ is a differential of conformal dimension $\lambda_j$ at $z_j$ by

Let $\lambda(\sigma)=\sigma^2+2\sigma  \quad(\sigma \in \mathbb{R})$.
\begin{equation}
\lambda_j=\lambda_b\left(\sigma_j\right) \equiv \sigma_j^2+2\sigma_j  ,
\end{equation}

whose value is given by

\begin{equation}
C[\boldsymbol{\sigma}] =\prod_{j<k}\left(z_j-z_k\right)^{2\sigma_j \sigma_k} ,
\end{equation}
where the product is taken over all finite $z_j$ and $z_k$.","status":"unverified"}

