{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.523168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ef1531d2c9c690ac7a526fa4a28384317f321d10bd19b343130c82b45ffa08f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: sizes-of-maximum-matching of arXiv:2601.13426, 'A uniformity principle for spatial matching'] Let $\nu_n(r, b, p)$, $\nu_n^{\mathrm{NF}}(r, b, p)$, $\nu_n^{\mathrm{F}}(r, b, p)$ respectively denote the expected number of matched supply, inflexible supply, and flexible supply nodes in the dual service range model. Then, 
