{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.976838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ef2ad80b2aa39a469c1b6a2e81859d500cc69123f2b3ae469d90e393e3f6517","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem paths agree of arXiv:2508.13827, 'Surface sums in two-dimensional large-$N$ lattice Yang--Mills: Cancellations and explicit '] Let $\mathbb{T}^*=\mathbb{T}^*_{p,q,M}(\mathfrak{p})= \{T_1^*,T_2^*\}$ be a spanning pair of trees avoiding $p$ and $q$ generated from $\mathfrak{p}$ of size $M\geq 1$. Fix $e\in E^{\times}(\mathbb{T}^*)$. Then, for any $\mathfrak{p}^e=\{p^e_i\}_{i=1}^{\infty}\in \mathfrak{P}_{\mathbb{T}^*}(e)$ and $\mathfrak{q}^e=\{q^e_i\}_{i=1}^{\infty}\in \mathfrak{P}_{\mathbb{T}^*}(e)$,
