{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.710356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1efdc916a42c7702275e3fe3880eda33bf44a4ffd81c37d4970e37b7b632466a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop mdp y_t of arXiv:2604.10509, 'Nonequilibrium fluctuations and moderate deviations for the occupation time of the SSEP wi'] The sequence of processes $\{\mathcal{Y}_t / a_n, 0 \leq t \leq T\}_{n \geq 1}$ satisfies the large deviation principle with decay rate $a_n^2 $ and with rate function $\mathcal{Q}_T$. Precisely speaking, for any closed set $C$ and any open set $O$ in $D([0,T], \mathcal{D}^\prime (\mathbb T^d))$,
	\begin{align*}
		\limsup_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{a_n^2} \log \mathbb P^n_{\rho_*} \Big( \{\mathcal{Y}_t/a_n, 0 \leq t \leq T\} \in C\Big) \leq - \inf_{\mu \in C} \mathcal{Q}_T (\mu),\\
		\liminf_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{a_n^2} \log \mathbb P^n_{\rho_*} \Big( \{\mathcal{Y}_t/a_n, 0 \leq t \leq T\} \in O\Big) \geq - \inf_{\mu \in O} \mathcal{Q}_T (\mu).
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.739089+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1eff73bd755ce9755fde0464cc8e6c0d512b0e32bfea2b50556e6e685ddf89fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2506.10494, 'Geometric Jensen-Shannon Divergence Between Gaussian Measures On Hilbert Space'] [\cite{Minh:LogDet2016}]

			Let 

			{$A \in \Sym(\H) \cap \Tr(\H)$}
			and {$\gamma > 0$, $\gamma \in \R$}, be such that {$(A + \gamma I) > 0$}. 

			Then {$\log(A+\gamma I) \in \Tr(\H)$} and {$\trace[\log(A+\gamma I)]$} is finite if and only if {$\gamma = 1$}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.072117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1eff930866b46faa2f6211a3d437ae666add13323e2b797c476473434010f80e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thm:unif-rsw of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Fix $m>0$, a proper $s$-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{\delta}$ of a graph $(S, (x_e)_{e\in E})$ satisfying {\mbox{\textsc{Unif(}$\delta,r_0,\theta_0$\textsc{)}}}\,, and a collection of masses $(m_{e})_{e\in E}$ all bounded by $m$. Fix a square $\Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$  of width $\rho>0$ drawn over $\mathcal{S}^{\delta}$. Consider the FK-Ising model on $\Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$, where the coupling constant on the edge $e\in \Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$ is $x^{(\delta)}_e=x_e + \delta m_e$, and denote by $\mathbb{P}^{\textnormal{free}}_{\textnormal{FK}}$ the measure with $\textnormal{free}$ boundary conditions on the annulus $\Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$. Then, there exists $c(m,r_0,\theta_0)>0$, only depending on $m,r_0,\theta_0$, such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}^{\textnormal{free}}_{\textnormal{FK}} \big( \textnormal{There exist an open circuit in } \mathrm{A}_{\frac{\rho}{2},\rho} \big) > c(m,r_0,\theta_0).		
\end{equation}
A similar estimate holds for the dual model. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.963379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f01212deaf094b39b82d86edfe6d38e931b2b4a50bec66b516cc029fd7a9263","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] For every $\mathcal{I}=[t_1,t_2]\subset[0,\infty)$ and $\mathcal{J}=[\underline{a},\overline{a}]\subset(0,1)$ it holds that
    \begin{equation*}
