{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.727188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f182fe605e0448b7761d2e475e0b1ca828c800aeebb8a91ad55130536e9766f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmas3.1 of arXiv:2608.01279, 'Stochastic heat equation with nondegenerate Hölder diffusion coefficient: uniqueness below'] For every fixed \(\delta>0\),

\begin{equation}
D\to K_\delta(D)-I,
\qquad
D\to S_\delta(D)

\end{equation}
are globally Lipschitz maps from \(H\) to the Hilbert--Schmidt
operators on \(H\).  More precisely,

\begin{equation}
\|K_\delta(D)-K_\delta(E)\|_{\mathrm{HS}}
+\|S_\delta(D)-S_\delta(E)\|_{\mathrm{HS}}
\le C_{K_0}\delta^{-1}\|D-E\|_H,

\end{equation}
where $C_{K_0}>0$ only depends on $K_0$.
Furthermore,

\begin{equation}
\|K_\delta(D)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\le1,
\qquad
\|S_\delta(D)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\le1,
\qquad
K_\delta K_\delta^*+S_\delta S_\delta^*=I.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.704569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f215bfea39fa68850827eb99e41df5bc961471481fd4f3976c82f0ce512b66d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 30 of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Assume \textnormal{(A1)-(A4)}. Then the pullback random attractors obtained in Theorem~\ref{The2} are upper semicontinuous at $\epsilon=0$: for every $\omega\in\Omega_0$,
