{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.141350+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f28288b67e9e37007853430d50814ef5dbf77004d59b07470037b94775db6ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Majorizing Measure Theorem) of arXiv:2608.11031, 'A Bayesian Proof of the Bernoulli Theorem'] There are universal constants $c,C>0$ such that every finite
