{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.894247+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f2d28b490f99e1ac4215cbc28979de95d3e93ba6fb8fcd1cbcb15e0e7b4acbf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 21 of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Specializing the objects defined in this section to the setting of Definition~\ref{def:1_l_weights}, we have 
\begin{equation*}
\Phi(z)=\prod_{m=1}^\ell\frac{\gamma_m+\alpha_m z^{-1}}{1-\beta_m z^{-1}},
\end{equation*}
and since~$\Phi$ is scalar, the equation~$P(z,w)=0$ becomes~$w=\Phi(z)$. Moreover, the fact that~$\Phi$ is a scalar rational function means that the Wiener--Hopf factorization simply reads
\begin{equation*}
\widetilde \phi_+(z)=\prod_{m=1}^\ell (\gamma_mz+\alpha_m)^N \quad \text{and} \quad \widetilde \phi_-(z)=\prod_{m=1}^\ell(z-\beta_m)^{-N}.
\end{equation*}
The inverse Kasteleyn matrix given in Theorem~\ref{thm:inverse_kasteleyn_general} becomes
\begin{multline}
  K^{-1}(w_{\ell x'+i',y'},b_{\ell x+i,y})
  =-\frac{\mathbf{1} \{\ell x+i \geq \ell x'+i'+1\}}{2\pi\i}\int_\Gamma \left(\frac{\prod_{m=1}^{i'+1}(\gamma_m+\alpha_m z^{-1})}{\prod_{m=1}^{i'}(1-\beta_m z^{-1})}\right)^{-1} \\
  \times \prod_{m=1}^{i}\frac{\gamma_m+\alpha_m z^{-1}}{1-\beta_m z^{-1}}w^{x-x'}z^{y'-y}\frac{\d z}{z}
  +\frac{1}{(2\pi\i)^2}\int_{\Gamma_s}\int_{\Gamma_l}\left(\frac{\prod_{m=1}^{i'+1}(\gamma_m+\alpha_m z_1^{-1})}{\prod_{m=1}^{i'}(1-\beta_m z_1^{-1})}\right)^{-1} \\
  \times \frac{\prod_{m=1}^\ell(z_2-\beta_m)^{N}}{\prod_{m=1}^\ell(z_1-\beta_m)^{N}}
  \prod_{m=1}^{i}\frac{\gamma_m+\alpha_m z_2^{-1}}{1-\beta_m z_2^{-1}}\frac{w_2^{x}}{w_1^{x'}}\frac{z_1^{y'}}{z_2^y}\frac{\d z_2\d z_1}{z_2(z_2-z_1)}.
\end{multline}
Where~$\Gamma_s = \{|z_1| = r_s\}$ and~$\Gamma_l = \{|z_2| = r_l\}$ for~$r_s < 1 < r_l$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.738206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f35c5d16dd56baf27cc9c1a5350071464e6cfabcbe2961bf7f907d56e6e5efc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq: satake of arXiv:2609.01990, 'Jacquet-Zagier treatment of the beyond endoscopy trace formula for \(\GL_2\)'] Consider the normalized basis 
    \[
    \left\{f_{m,n} = q^{-(m-n)/2} \mathbf{1}_{K\left( \begin{matrix}
