{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.505202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f373e24cb86f02aadc38ba0d944a8277ad17c888ec23a69c9a6124b971ec386","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def.split-function of arXiv:2505.15283, 'Quantization of Probability Distributions via Divide-and-Conquer: Convergence and Error Pr'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on the measure space $({\mathbb{R}}, {\mathcal{B}}({\mathbb{R}}))$. We say that any function
