{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.555962+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f489a5bd5db4997057865007e4bb5f866907cd964f9f54f222b2f0db7fcd4b5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 42 of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] There is a constant $C = C( g_0, T )$ such that
