{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.039696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f54c47a3f9d1dd8305d08e66cf5eb4c266584e761555197e70b3751b998b93e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main_theorem of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any $\mu_{g} \xrightarrow[g \to \infty]{}\mu_c$ such that $\mu_c -\mu_g = o(g^{-2})$, we have
