{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.897035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f6a6dce2805bcf49cbb1f30d8a9b2c14acfc738697447417216dac085f15d98","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary strict monochromatic of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let $n\ge 2$. 
When $\alpha=1$, if $\beta_\ell$ and $\frac{1}{\beta_\ell}$ are bounded, the scaling bound in (equation eq:scalimRW of the paper) becomes
\begin{equation} 
