{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.794378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fb31fdd17a167fa4cd3160a8e9a5c30e45155ad7c6aaf882c734322423f9520","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2609.03152 (conj environment labelled conj: rigidity).] [BS24:refGW]
 Suppose $(X\times \Aaff{2},\gpT)$ is equivariantly Calabi--Yau and $\beta$ is a curve class in $\CYth$ for which $\Mbar_g(X,\beta)$ is proper for all $g\geq 0$. Then
 \begin{equation*}
