{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.047725+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_201f5093b583bb46db8598e1674d97a2d801a651d7ce4fd186b7add37b625f00","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition asymptotics_of_coefficients of arXiv:2506.02611, '\textbf{The tight length spectrum of large-genus random hyperbolic surfaces with many cusp'] For any $\mu_g \underset{g \to +\infty}{\rightarrow}\mu_c$ such that $\mu_c - \mu_g = o(g^{-2})$ and any $p_1,\cdots,p_k \ge 1$, $n\ge0$ and $q_1,\cdots,q_n \ge 0$, we have
    \begin{align}        \alpha_{n,g,\mathbf{p},\mathbf{q}}(\mathbf{M})\underset{g \to +\infty}{\sim} \varphi(n,g,\mathbf{p}) \prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{1}{(2q_i+1)!}.
    \end{align}
Furthermore, for $g$ large enough we have
\begin{align}
        \forall \mathbf{p}\in (\mathbb{N}^{*})^{k},\hspace{0.2cm}\forall \mathbf{q}\in \mathbb{N}^n,\hspace{0.3cm}\big|\alpha_{n,g,\mathbf{p},\mathbf{q}}(\mathbf{M}) \big|\le C_n  \bigg(-\frac{M_1}{M_0}\bigg)^{n-|\mathbf{p}|}g^{n+k}A^k\varphi(g)\prod_{i=1}^{n}\frac{1}{q_i!},
