{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.748562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20409091fade7477b8c387be569368b2fa41ff6d55f240ba4f50c80a893334d5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 18 of arXiv:2607.28865, 'First-Passage Percolation on Spread-out line graphs: Microscopic Regime'] Let $\rho_1<\rho_2<\cdots$ be the sequence of pivot nodes. For any non-negative measurable function $f:\dR^{\cE^{(\ell)}}\to\dR_+$ defined on the edge environment $\mvgo$, we have
