{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.006680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2044a45df754283b4cd0a1e376ec8fc021a2d2eb4634669b4ea02c9349069715","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma neigh_asymp of arXiv:2606.27844, 'Critical percolation on preferential attachment graphs with infinite variance'] Let  $f(x)=\tfrac{1}{\gamma}x^{-\gamma}$.
Then
\begin{align}
     \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{n\beta(n)^{\alpha/2}}\#\big\{x\in\{1,\dots,n\}\,:\, x \sim C_1(\mathcal G_{n,\mu}^{(2)}) \}  = 
     \mu^{1-\gamma} \int_0^1 f(x) \rho(\kappa_\mu , x)\,\text{d}x\,,
\end{align}
in probability, where $\rho(\kappa_\mu , x)$ is the survival probability of the multitype Galton-Watson tree started in $x$ associated with the kernel $$\kappa_\mu(x,y)= \mu^{1-2\gamma}(2\gamma-1)^{-1}x^{-\gamma}y^{-\gamma}\,.$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.763237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2048482c2ebe248551a9e16c6c2d1d537ff1cf496177015cb09c78ebd28bfd87","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] Take any $A_\alpha = \alpha P + (1-\alpha)G$ with $G$ as the Gibbs kernel, and $P$ a $\pi$-reversible kernel. Then for any positive integer $l \geq 2$ and $\alpha \in (0,1)$,
