{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.898928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20ad8510dc915d7a2885b2532ee8bf1166fd8b4261c8bb67958b16697c122cd2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:contourintegral of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] Given a symmetric matrix $M$ with eigenvalues $\lambda_1\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_N$, the partition function $Z_N$ with the corresponding Hamiltonian $H(\sigma) =\frac12\sigma^TM\sigma$ can be expressed as
 \begin{equation} 
Z_N=C_N\int_{\gamma-\mathrm{i}\infty}^{\gamma+\mathrm{i}\infty}e^{\frac{N}{2}\mathcal{G}(z)}\mathrm{d} z
 \end{equation} 
where the contour is a vertical line crossing the real axis at any $\gamma>\lambda_1$ and
 \begin{equation} 
\mathcal{G}(z)=\beta z-\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N\log(z-\lambda_i),\qquad C_N=\frac{\Gamma(N/2)}{2\pi\mathrm{i}(N\beta/2)^{N/2-1}}.
 \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.096396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20b294eae4c5e288645f0c37268f1a050b37758afa8b04e728f15f8821eeb183","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 (\cite{marshall2011}, Theorem~3.A.4) of arXiv:2604.26026, 'Stochastic Ordering of Dependent Systems under Transformation Models and Archimedean Copul'] Suppose $J \subset \mathbb{R}$ is an open interval and $h: J^{n} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ is continuously differentiable. Then, $h$ is Schur-convex (Schur-concave) on $J^{n}$ if and only if
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $h$ is symmetric on $J^{n}$, and
		\item for all $i \neq j$ and all $\boldsymbol{\alpha} \in J^{n}$,
		\begin{equation}

        \left(\alpha_{i}-\alpha_{j}\right)\left(\frac{\partial h(\boldsymbol{\alpha})}{\partial \alpha_{i}}-\frac{\partial h(\boldsymbol{\alpha})}{\partial \alpha_{j}}\right) \geq (\leq)\,0,
		\end{equation}
		where $\frac{\partial h(\boldsymbol{\alpha})}{\partial \alpha_{i}}$ represents the partial derivative of $h$ with respect to its $i$-th argument.
	\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.286841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20b385b3e39b39b62b8e44e50583704e3cefe8eac1758b6b7ac155b40b646c05","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop CbetaECorr of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] Let $\boldsymbol{\rho}_{N,\beta}^{(m)}$ be the $m$-th correlation function of $\textnormal{C}\beta \textnormal{E}_N$. Then, for $N > m$, 
