{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.988210+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20c12fdc53fe548affc33c40f29d238ffcbf1926f30349293f0782d9cb09eaa7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 63 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $\theta_1, \ldots, \theta_m$ be unit flows from $u$ to $v$ that are supported on disjoint edges, that is for each edge $e$ we have $\theta_i(e) > 0$ for at most one $i \in \{1, \ldots, m\}$. Then, for any $\alpha_1, \ldots, \alpha_m \geq 0$
