{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.120088+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20d50681a7d3b2eca6eb28b47175c6e87e3ce0d4eb041570822e169a29f5abf0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2604.04840, 'Bounding the Gap Between Zeros of the Variable-\\Parameter Confluent Hypergeometric Functi'] Let $b$ and $z$ be positive real numbers and $-\infty < \cdots < \nu_{k+1}^* < \nu_k^* < \cdots < 0$ be the sequence of zeros of $\Phi(\nu,b,z)$. Given a bound $\Delta$ such that $\nu_k^* - \nu_{k+1}^* \geq \Delta$ for $k>N$, an upper bound on $\varepsilon_N$ is

