{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.315857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20d614465c7201ae0d8681367bd5da41899ab1fcb1bab2d95c8c7debd65d966c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Polya schur and multiplicative groups of arXiv:2605.31356, 'P\'olya--Schur problems and free probability'] Let $\{f_n\}\subset\mathcal{LP}$ be a sequence of functions with only negative roots and which satisfies  Assumption (assump:main assumption of the paper). If $t\geq 0$ and $\{p_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ is a sequence of positively-rooted polynomials indexed by their degree such that $\llbracket p_n\rrbracket\Rightarrow\mu$ as $n\rightarrow\infty$, then \begin{equation}
		\left\llbracket f_{\lfloor tn\rfloor}(tz\partial_{z})p_n(z)\right\rrbracket\Rightarrow \mu\boxtimes \tilde{\mu}_{c,\Sigma}^{\boxtimes t},
