{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.723838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20d61648e65e23c50c75cc3fdb26a624a374007343d905e668c4fbe2531a5e88","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm eq:irreg of arXiv:2606.02340, 'Transitivity in Inhomogeneous Random Tournaments'] Fix a tournamenton $W$ with $\zeta(W) \in [0, 1)$ and consider the $W$-random tournament $T_n \sim T(n, W)$. Then for $N_{\triangle}(T_n)$ as defined in (equation eq:N of the paper) the following hold: 
