{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.203260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20dd95738eeb7f5beecaddc4ff6fd42b397fe0f2d877f13cfc7b886a754a0a18","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2604.26898, '\bf Stochastic Scaling Limits and Synchronization \\by Noise in Deep Transformer Models'] There exists a constant $\mathsf c_T>0$, independent of $N$, $m$, and $L$, such that
