{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354753+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_20f8a32e24ec6b0a3dd23ad3859b386237a24dfb5e974b590e2dae279a604747","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nu-remask of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Consider the remasking process with parameter \(p_M\) and let \(\rho = \sqrt{1 - p_M}\). Recall \(\nu(t, c)\) from~(eq:def-nu of the paper). We have
