{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.302682+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_212d5f657faa5d6fbdd5ee7a18a16b7db0d2c38c340a730b3e5289c75fbb7aea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:monotone of arXiv:2605.26869, 'Law of Large Numbers for a random walk on dynamic environments with drift'] \emph{[CKKR24]}
If $\eta,\widetilde{\eta} \in \Sigma$ and $K\subseteq \mathbb{Z}\times\mathbb{Z}^+_0$ are such that 
