then for every $w,w'\in K$ with $\pi_1(w')\le \pi_1(w)$ and $\pi_2(w)= \pi_2(w')$, and for every $n \geq 0$ such that $[\pi_1(w)-k,  \pi_1(w')+k]\times [\pi_2(w), \pi_2(w)+k] \subseteq K $ for all $0 \leq k \leq n$\color{black}, one has that
