{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.990968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_212f17dffb2d6214b667f92832acbe4a5e2fa3ed8bc91e575ea396e73f96aaae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 102 (Critical) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $p= \frac{1 + \epsilon}{n}$ with $\epsilon = \lambda n^{-1/3}$, $\lambda \in \R$. Then for all $\delta < 1$
