{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.417760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21350ac66660072f22262184e12ba7f8107fef155be154072f4a0064bb849a43","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 108 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] We denote $\mathcal{D}^+$ the set of $(\theta,\hat{n},\hat{A}_1,\hat{A}_2,\hat{B}_1,\hat{B}_2) \in \amsmathbb{R}_{> 0}^2 \times \amsmathbb{R}^4$ cut out by the inequalities
