{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.146857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2137c24c5b2f29aafa4de65030abf18473e93f616208416faec4f66aa45865fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $b>0$ and let $\mathsf{S}^{(N)}:= (\sfU^{(N)} \sfV^{(N)})$ be a random walk on $\bbR^2$ such that 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\sfS^{(N)}_0 = (0, \lfloor b\sqrt{N} \rfloor )$;
        \item $\sfS_{n+1}^{(N)}-\sfS_n^{(N)}$ is i.i.d.~with mean $0$, and its norm is bounded by some constant independent of $N$; 
        \item $\mathbb{E}[(\sfU^{(N)}_{n+1}-\sfU^{(N)}_{n})^2] = \mathbb{E}[(\sfV^{(N)}_{n+1}-\sfV^{(N)}_{n})^2] = a_{11} $ and $\mathbb{E}[(\sfU_{n+1}^{(N)} -\sfU_{n}^{(N)})(\sfV_{n+1}^{(N)} - \sfV_{n}^{(N)})] = a_{12}$ for some constants $a_{11}$ and $a_{12}$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Let $\tau_N = \inf \{ t:\sfV_{t}^{(N)} \leq 0\}$ and let $B_t = (U_t, V_t)$ be a two-dimensional Brownian motion started from $(0,b)$ with covariance matrix $\begin{pmatrix}
        a_{11} & a_{12}\\
        a_{12} & a_{11}
        \end{pmatrix}$.
        Then as $N\to \infty$,  $(\frac{\sfS_{\lfloor Nt\rfloor}}{\sqrt{N}})_{0\leq t\leq \tau_N} $ converges in distribution to $ (B_t)_{0\leq t\leq \tau} $ where $\tau: = \inf\{t: \sfV_t  \leq 0 \}$ with respect to the metric~\eqref{eq:curve-metric}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.302267+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21407ca4bd00296d6907e6838d7476b006f4e2fdc1ed5a16d44e2633b0e8931c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 24 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Fix $k\in \mathbb N$. There exists $C=C(k)>0$ such that the following bounds hold uniformly over $   \beta_1,...,   \beta_k \in \ak$ and $\x\in I^k$ 
    \begin{align*}\bigg|
    \mathcal K(\x,\boldsymbol\beta; k) - \sum_{i<j} \sum_{\substack{r_1+...+r_d=p\\s_1+...+s_d=p}} \frac{   \beta_i^{\;   r}   \beta_j^{\;   s}}{   r!    s!} \boldsymbol \eta_{   r,   s}(   x_i-   x_j)
    \bigg|&
    \leq 
C  \min\bigg\{ \bigg(\sum_{i=1}^k|   \beta_i|\bigg)^{2p+1
    } ,\Fd\big(\min_{i<j}|   x_i-   x_j|\big)^{1/2}\bigg\},
       \end{align*} 
    where $   r = (r_1,...,r_d)$ and $   x^{\;   r} = x_1^{r_1}\cdots x_d^{r_d}$ and $   r! = r_1!\cdots r_d!.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.062226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21438c14215f06cc2921a0dc5e0292a6a8b7f28b01aba5e310bb6617d789d6d2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem equalfnbootstrap of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] Let $\Omega$ be an open subset of ${\mathbb R}^2$. 
Let $\{Z_n(x,y)\}_{(x,y)\in \Omega}$, $n\in {\mathbb N}$, and $\{Z(x,y)\}_{(x,y)\in \Omega}$ be random fields.  
Let $m\in{\mathbb N}$. 
Let $\mathcal S$ be an open subset of $\Omega^m \subset {\mathbb R}^{2m}$. 
Let $g: \Omega \to {\mathbb R}$ be a continuously differentiable function satisfying $\frac{\partial g}{\partial y}(x,y) \ne 0$ for every $(x,y) \in \Omega$. 
Suppose that the following two conditions hold:
\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
\item If $(x_1,y_1,\cdots, x_m,y_m) \in \mathcal S$ and $g(x_i,y_i) \ne g(x_{i+1},y_{i+1})$ for all $i$, then 
\begin{equation} 
    \{Z_n(x_i,y_i)\}_{i=1,\dots,m} \xrightarrow{d} \{Z(x_i,y_i)\}_{i=1,\dots,m}
    \qquad \textnormal{as $n\to \infty$.}
\end{equation}
\item For every $x_1, \cdots, x_m \in \pi_x(\Omega)$ and $r_1,\cdots,r_m \in {\mathbb R}$ 
\begin{equation*}
    	(y_1, \cdots, y_m) \mapsto \mathbb{P} (Z(x_i, y_i) \leq r_i, i =1, \cdots, m)
\end{equation*}
is jointly continuous in $(y_1, \cdots, y_m)\in \prod_{i=1}^m \pi_y(\Omega \cap (\{x_i\} \times {\mathbb R}))$
\end{enumerate}
Then (equation eq:convergenced2 of the paper) holds for all $(x_1,y_1,\cdots,x_m,y_m) \in \mathcal S$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2143ab4bcd0f97b532d3a6322a010fadc329c13ba42009ad7ef0c56ead2ba19f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:wt-score of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Fix \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\) and let \(u = T - t_{k+1},\ \ell = T - t_k\). For \(t \in [u, \ell]\), define
