{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.474365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_214b6c600f7d5673a86781c6c7b4f9e6e022dd9011703b24b443be98d69e327e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 61 (Finite-overlap reconstruction) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Fix $1\le r\le\infty$ and put $s_r:=\min\{r,2\}$, with
