{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.842687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21a24f84f5c17ccd9c4b0880bcde08de5077c63a4325e0a7918b85cc025e7335","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:136 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There exist constants $C,c_1,c_2$ such that for all $n$ and all $j,k,i,\Delta\in [\![-2\varepsilon n^{1/3},2\varepsilon n^{1/3}]\!]$ additionally satisfying $\Delta\geq 0$ and $i\geq 1$,
