{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.325231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21c426bf71f7eaadc6ffd5a7a3814f28c544b7640c654e7403f51f5240c1023e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-gf-pos of arXiv:2411.06301, 'Inverting the operation of conditioning a branching process on extinction'] Let $X = \{X(n)\}_{n\in\mathbbm N_0}$ be a $d$-type branching process which is positive regular and non-singular (Definition~(def-bp-basic of the paper)). There exists $N\in\mathbbm N$ such that for each $k,j  \in \{1,\dots,d\}$, 
