{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.353034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21dbb83feb37a33a87f44cd6688e1a4906905561a328b078bfdd1e49cf834425","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:bernton31mod of arXiv:2506.03999, 'Large deviations for scaled families of Schr\"odinger bridges with reflection'] For $\delta, \delta' \in [0, \infty]$ with $\delta \leq \delta'$, let $A_k(\delta, \delta') \coloneq \{(x_i, y_i)_{i=1}^k \in (\calX \times \calY)^k: \sum_{i=1}^k c(x_i, y_i) - \sum_{i=1}^k c(x_i, y_{i + 1}) \in [\delta, \delta']\}$, where $y_{k+1}$ is interpreted as $y_1$. 
    Then, for any Borel set $A \subseteq A_k(\delta, \delta')$,
    \begin{equation}
        \limsup_{\eta \downarrow 0} \eta \log \pi_\eta^k(A) \leq -\delta,
    \end{equation}
    and if $\overrightarrow{A} \coloneq \{(x_i, y_{i+1})_{i=1}^k: (x_i, y_{i})_{i=1}^k \in A\}$ satisfies $\liminf_{\eta \downarrow 0} \eta \log \pi_\eta^k(\overrightarrow{A}) = 0$, then also,
    \begin{equation}
