{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.527532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2202784962b7cc828164df1626fdbf12a8e89ee467e95bf3ae7e0d4ef83b9347","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop partition of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given a random set of good cubes $\mathcal{G}\subseteq \mathcal{T}$ satisfying (equation e:local_dependence of the paper), then for any cube ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \in \mathcal{G}$, there exists its local partition of good cubes denoted by $\mathcal{S}^{loc}_{\mathcal{G}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}) \subseteq \mathcal{G}$, such that the following properties hold:
