{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.435146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_221234388f639a52891f01588e12c38ecadacc1943011a61cac32f498b5de7b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:train_test_equivalents_vanishing_kappa of arXiv:2608.23938, 'Generalization, memorization, and overfitting \\for diffusion models trained in the lazy h'] Suppose that Assumptions~(ass:high_dim of the paper),~(ass:input_dist of the paper), and~(ass:kernel_func_vanishing_kappa of the paper) hold. Suppose further that there exists an $\epsilon\in(0,k_0-2)$ such that $d^{-k_0+2} \lesssim \kappa \lesssim d^{-\epsilon}$, where $k_0$ is given in Assumption~(ass:kernel_func_vanishing_kappa of the paper). Then, \(|{\mathcal L}(\widehat{{\boldsymbol f}}_{\kappa};0)| \prec  \kappa\). Furthermore, for every constant $c \in (0, (\epsilon \wedge 1)/2)$ and $\zeta >0$ given in Assumption~(ass:kernel_func_vanishing_kappa of the paper),
