{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.771060+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_221cd057d6770d0d81a2b1e8bdacfdc2f9f8aae7a257f618f614f5c22fd8eb09","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tail of arXiv:2608.04900, 'A Sharper Hoeffding Bound for Weighted Sums of Exchangeable Random Variables'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:main of the paper), if $P_{\mathbf{1}^\perp}\widetilde w\ne0$, then for any $\delta\in(0,1)$,
