{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.076823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_221cf569fca57478a15268aeac0370d4206fceff4ad3922706ad746ee3e92b94","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 (Polarized identity and weighted-Poincar\'e deficit) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] In the regular moment-map model,
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
