{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.309113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22340e9679556b4d0d9a6b86a3d3a5b23636ea7c29f33d00a6a12e72a06ea78a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.02392, 'Large values of cubic and quartic Dirichlet $L$-functions of prime moduli'] With the notation as above and the truth of GRH, we have, for sufficiently large $X$, 
