{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.325598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_223b177fab3b9b4e9324350c79a83ad4152f7cdc3da9407c00ed1334ad467f6c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:Neumann of arXiv:2606.01866, 'Phase Transition of a Semiflexible Membrane in Two Dimensions'] In (equation eq:beforeNeumann of the paper), the $L^2$ matrix norm of $\Gamma_N\Delta_N$ is less than $1$, if $N$ is large enough. In particular, the series
