{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.646308+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2240cc13341fe24b4ecaf1cf556f2f710d7092f5599471391c0f54a6d7b88745","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Nn_small of arXiv:2605.16086, 'Loop pruning and downward deviations for maximum local time of discrete-time simple random'] Fix a finite loop set \(E\) satisfying (equation eq:E-assumption-for-Nn-small of the paper) below. Then there exists a constant \(b<1-\beta\), depending only on \(E\), such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{Q}\bigl(\mathcal{N}_n\le n^b,\,
\xi^*(S'[0,u_n])\le \Lambda_n\bigr)=1-o(1).
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\bigl(\mathcal{N}_n\le n^b,\,
\xi^*(S'[0,u_n])\le \Lambda_n\bigr)
