{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.579140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2258022c5f4337641182b812c0f0a90c11d3cf75a8871ebdecbb6e18ee7c4eb4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:Capacity1 of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] For every~$\mssE^i$-capacitale~$A_i\subset M_i$ and every~$\mssE^i$-quasi-open~$U^i\subset M^i$,
\[
\mathrm{cap}_{\mssE}(A_1\times A_2, U_1\times U_2)\leq \mathrm{cap}_{\mssE^1}(A_1,U_1) \left\lVerte_2\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_2)}^2+  \mathrm{cap}_{\mssE^2}(A_2,U_2) \left\lVerte_1\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_1)}^2 \,\mathrm{,}\;\,
\]
where~$e_i$ is the equilibrium $\mssE^i$-potential for the pair~$(A_i, U_i)$.
\begin{proof} It suffices to estimate
\begin{align*}
\mathrm{cap}_\mssE&(A_1\times A_2,U_1\times U_2) 
\\
=&\ \inf \set{\mssE_1(u) : u\in\dom{\mssE^{U_1\times U_2}} \,\mathrm{,}\;\, \car_{A_1\times A_2}\leq u\leq \car \ \mssE\text{-q.e.}}
\\
\leq&\ \inf\set{ \mssE_1(u_1\otimes u_2) : u_i\in\dom{\mssE^{i,U^i}}\,\mathrm{,}\;\, \car_{A_i} \leq u_i \leq \car \ \mssE^i\text{-q.e.}\,\mathrm{,}\;\, i=1,2}
\\
\leq&\ \inf\set{\begin{gathered}\mssE^1 (u_1)\left\lVertu_2\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_2)}^2+\mssE^2 (u_2) \left\lVertu_1\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_1)}^2+ \left\lVertu_1\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_1)}^2\left\lVertu_2\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_2)}^2 :\\ u_i\in\dom{\mssE^{i,U^i}}\,\mathrm{,}\;\, \car_{A_i}\leq u_i \leq \car\ \mssE^i\text{-q.e.}\,\mathrm{,}\;\, i=1,2 \end{gathered}}
\\
\leq&\ \inf\set{\begin{gathered}\mssE^1_1(u_1)\left\lVertu_2\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_2)}^2+\mssE^2_1(u_2) \left\lVertu_1\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_1)}^2 :\\ u_i\in\dom{\mssE^{i,U^i}}\,\mathrm{,}\;\, \car_{A_i}\leq u_i \leq \car\ \mssE^i\text{-q.e.}\,\mathrm{,}\;\, i=1,2 \end{gathered}}
\\
\leq&\ \mssE^1_1(e_1)\left\lVerte_2\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_2)}^2+\mssE^2_1(e_2) \left\lVerte_1\right\rVert_{L^2(\nu_1)}^2 \,\mathrm{.} \qedhere
\end{align*}
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.187661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_226224ea0d70b3076b8e537f7d4a72e0e7b112ae344ddcd683a08c8833d9a999","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 7$ and $\epsilon>0$, there exist $\Cl(d,\epsilon),\cl(d,\epsilon)>0$ such that for any $n\ge  \Cref{const_highd_avoid_box_twopoint1}$, $N\ge \Cref{const_highd_avoid_box_twopoint1}n$, $\psi\in \Psi(n,N)$, $i\in \{ 1,2\}$, and any $x\in \mathfrak{B}_{m_{\diamond},100}^{\diamond}$ satisfying $|z_i^{\diamond}- x | \ge \frac{m_\diamond}{100}$,  
