{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.943194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_226827a98a6cfbaa015f5e0ae841e15125828236352d1971f0c16bcc88a7acd3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:approx_dual of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}_{tem}^+)$, $p>2$, such that (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper) holds and let $a$ be defined as in (equation eq:def_d of the paper). Let $Y^n$ be as above, independent of $X$. Then there exists a time $T_0>0$ depending only on $\langle \mu,1\rangle$ and $a$ such that for all $t \leq T \leq T_0$  we have
