{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.771897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22746914c4c816a1e6f52c9f78168bff188f04497d340bfa63a8835e5c96a9e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2608.31168, 'The anisotropic Michael-Simon inequality for surfaces in every codimension'] Let $S,T$ be finite vector-valued measures on $\bR^2$ with measure-valued divergence.
    For every non-negative compactly supported Borel function $\chi$, it holds that
    \begin{align*}
