{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.858640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22a3bec8bdd3eae059eb4db2bd7674b485b6dc17f4303daa13d03505fdaa53d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] Let $\{F_n\}_{n \in \N}$ be a sequence of random variables belonging to the $m$th Wiener chaos with $m \geq 2$ such that $\E[F_n^2] = 1$. 
Assume that there exists a sequence $\{\varphi(n)\}_{n \in \N}$ such that $\varphi(n) > 0$ for all sufficiently large $n$, $\dis \lim_{n \to \infty}\varphi(n) = 0$, and 
\begin{equation}
    \left(F_n, \frac{1- \abra{DF_n, -DL^{-1}F_n}_{\fH}}{\varphi(n)}\right) \xrightarrow[n \to \infty]{d} \cN\left(0, \begin{pmatrix} 1 & \zeta \\\zeta & \eta \\\end{pmatrix}\right), \qquad \eta \in (0, \infty). 

\end{equation}
Then, for every $k \in \N_0$ and $r \in [1,\infty]$, we have $\rho_{F_n} \in C_{\mathrm{b}}^k(\R) \cap W^{k,r}(\R)$ for all sufficiently large $n$ and 
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{n \to \infty}  \left\lVert \frac{\rho_{F_n}^{} - \rho_{\cN}^{}}{\varphi(n)} - \frac{\zeta}{3}\rho_{\cN}^{(3)} \right\rVert = 0, 
\end{equation}
 where $\norm{\cdot} \in \{\norm{\cdot}_{C_{\mathrm{b}}^k(\R)}, \norm{\cdot}_{W^{k,r}(\R)}\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.033431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22a4687cf1d9382dc925cebf64821beb23cfc74a59801aab7a246834d7a44377","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2606.07839, 'Bounds on Spectral Gaps for Non-Reversible Markov Chains with Applications to Temporal Dif'] Let $P$ be a Markov kernel with invariant probability distribution $\mu$. 
   Let $\phi_i\in L^2(\mu)$ for $i=1,\ldots,n$ and define the matrices $A$ and $S\in\bbC^{n\times n}$ by:
  \begin{align*}
    A_{ij}&=\langle \phi_i,(P^{(\lambda)}-I)\phi_j\rangle.
  \end{align*}


