{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.237696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22a50f1b2074a0ff22e81b074f894ea03383b4bf95300cd242e04405a9f4a911","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma N_properties of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] For all $\phi\in C^\infty(\mathcal{D})\cap V,$ and $\psi, z \in C^\infty(\mathcal{D})$,  $\mathcal{N}$ is anti-symmetric i.e. $\mathcal{N}(\phi, \psi) = - \mathcal{N}(\psi, \phi)$, moreover it holds 
   \begin{align}
   &\int_\mathcal{D} \mathcal{N}(\phi, \psi) z = - \int \mathcal{N}(\phi, z) \psi,    \\
   & \int_\mathcal{D} \mathcal{N}(\phi, \psi) \phi  =0,  \\
     &\int_\mathcal{D} \mathcal{N}(\phi, \Delta \phi) z = \int_D \nabla^\perp \phi \otimes \nabla^\perp \phi : \nabla \nabla^\perp z. 
    \end{align}
    By density, the bilinear operator $\mathcal{N}$ can be extended as an operator $\mathcal{N}:(W^{1,4}\cap V)\times L^4 \rightarrow V'$ so that (equation N-properties 3 of the paper) holds for all $\psi\in L^4, \phi \in W^{1,4}$. 
