{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.209787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22b0d096fd37142f7d3deee08fed4c387ccbfb61ba34dbfa4bbb664a6ec0a912","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-MCG lens spaces of arXiv:2609.00233, 'A survey on mapping class groups of 3-manifolds'] The group $\pi_{0}\Diff(L(p,q))$ for $p\geq 2$ is isomorphic to:
    \begin{enumerate}[(a)]
        \item $\mathbb{Z}/2$, generated by $\tau$, if $q^{2} \not\equiv \pm 1 \mod{p}$;
        \item $\mathbb{Z}/2 \oplus \mathbb{Z}/2$, generated by $\tau$ and $\sigma_{+}$, if $q^{2} \equiv 1 \mod{p}$ and $q \not\equiv \pm 1 \mod{p}$;
        \item $\mathbb{Z}/2$, generated by $\tau$, if $q \equiv \pm 1 \mod{p}$ and $p\neq 2$;
        \item $\mathbb{Z}/4$, generated by $\sigma_{-}$, if $q^{2} \equiv -1 \mod{p}$ and $p \neq 2$;
        \item $\mathbb{Z}/2$, generated by $\sigma_{-}$, if $p=2$.
    \end{enumerate}
    In each case the orientation-preserving subgroup $\pi_{0}\Diff^+(L(p,q))$ is the subgroup generated by $\tau$ and $\sigma_+$.  Thus
    $\pi_{0}\Diff^+(L(p,q)) = \pi_{0}\Diff(L(p,q))$ in cases (equation lens-space-case-a of the paper), (equation lens-space-case-b of the paper), and (equation lens-space-case-c of the paper), while $\pi_{0}\Diff^+(L(p,q)) \cong \mathbb Z/2$ in case (equation lens-space-case-d of the paper) and $\pi_{0}\Diff^+(L(2,1)) \cong \pi_{0}\Diff^+(\mathbb{RP}^3) = \{0\}$ in case (equation lens-space-case-e of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

