{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.301243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22e94d5d82c1621e40006e60e7e1c036df168f120b9926a98e9af837aecfb115","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:free-energy-random-ferro of arXiv:2608.06500, 'Free energy of Ising models under a spectral condition'] Let $G_N^{(r)}=(\text{\boldmath $A$}_N^{(r)},{\boldsymbol 0})$ be a sequence of random
