If $\beta\ge0$, then we may take $\eta=1/(4\sqrt{k-1})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.418696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22ea2a13b8d895a38bd6a4f04eb5ebf7dacb84e9e9a70202ddd39985a272c56e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2605.16560, 'Seasonal Statistics of Shannon Rate in a Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Cellular Network'] The marginal pdf of  $R_{\sst \Ical}$ is given by

