{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.738984+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22f3e600fe87bf47d6e935e21510e1085b7104ec67c291a035ddd32767534a6c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Proposition-KMP-SFK of arXiv:2507.19222, 'Convergence of the KMP model to the KPZ equation'] Let $\left(\eta(t,x)_{x\in \mathbb{Z}}\right)_{t\geqslant 0}$
be the KMP process with initial condition $\left(\eta(x,0)\right)_{x\in \mathbb{Z}}$.
	Let $\left(K_{t}(y,x)_{x,y\in \mathbb{Z}}\right)_{t\geqslant 0}$ be the stochastic flow of kernels defined in (equation definition-kernel of the paper). For any bounded function $\varrho_0:\mathbb{Z}\to \mathbb{R}_{+}$, let 
    \begin{equation}
 \varrho_{t}(x):=\sum_{y\in \mathbb{Z}}\varrho_{0}(y)K_{t}(y,x).
    \end{equation}
	Then, if $\varrho_{0}=\eta(0, \cdot)$ we have that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\eta(t,x)\overset{(d)}{=}\varrho_{t}(x), 
