{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.984471+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22f8999573abee4732183908af77a16e511a31673533c2d4734e62a6c89a52ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] \item Assume (a1 of the paper)-(a2 of the paper).  Let  $\alpha := (\beta-d+2)/3$,  and let $\eta_0>0$ and  $\lambda_0>0$ small enough.  Then, for all $\eta\in [0,\eta_0]$,  there exists a unique eigen-couple $\big(\mu(\eta),M_\eta\big)$ in $\{\mu\in \mathbb C, |\mu|\leqslant \eta^{\frac{2}{3}}\lambda_0\}\times L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{C})$, solution to the spectral problem 
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}_\eta(M_{\mu,\eta})(v)=\big[-\Delta_v +W(v) + \mathrm{i} \eta v_1 \big] M_{\mu,\eta} (v)= \mu M_{\mu,\eta}(v) , \quad  v\in \mathbb{R}^d .
