{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.023581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23128ab1af3307237d02fa201fbf0cd9616ea589b3d8b453eee36ae8ce40bab4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2609.03848, 'The mean-field limit of the Schr\"{o}dinger-Lohe model\\ and emergent dynamics'] \label{L-B.1}
Let $t\mapsto X(t,\cdot)$ be a continuous and bounded, time-dependent vector field on $(\mathbf{S}\mathfrak{H})^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N$ that is Lipschitz continuous on $\mathfrak{H}^N\times C(\mathbb T^d)^N$ uniformly in $t\in \mathbb R$, and let
