{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.857688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2346f53564498f89ceccf6d7893079a34838b5f5778caa25a6fe2dc98fdc72fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (K, Nourdin, Peccati, Speicher, \cite{1529a405-f4b1-33eb-aeac-05c9f76e60d3}) of arXiv:2511.20875, 'Double $q$-Wigner Chaos and the Fourth Moment'] Let $f_k$ be a sequence of mirror symmetric functions in $L^2(\mathbb{R}^n_+)$ (i.e.\ $f(t_1,\ldots,t_n) = \overline{f(t_n,\ldots,t_1)}$) with $\|f_k\|_2\to 1$ as $k\to\infty$.  Then the following three conditions are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\displaystyle{\lim_{k\to\infty}\tau_0[I_0(f_k)^4] = 2}$.
    \item $\displaystyle{\lim_{k\to\infty} f_k \overset{p}{\frown} f_k = 0}$ in $L^2(\mathbb{R}_+^{2(n-p)})$ for $p=1,\ldots,n-1$.
    \item The sequence $(I_0(f_k))_{k\in\N}$ converges in distribution to a standard semicircular random variable.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.579948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_234856fd6537a19c9226484b50e198b1554ac43669311d3d5e29d088cc8931cc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to \Rbb$, $q\in [1,2)$ and $t\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
    \Vop^k(\Pop_t f) \leq \upe^{-2kt} \Vop^k(f)^{1-\vartheta} \min\left\{\Vop^k(f),\,\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^q}^{2},\, \sum_{J\subseteq[n]:|J|=k}\left\|\Dop_J f\right\|_{\Leb^q}^2\right\}^{\vartheta},
\end{equation}
and similarly, for all $J\subseteq [n]$,
\begin{equation}
    \Vop_J(\Pop_t f) \leq \upe^{-2t |J|} \Vop_J(f)^{1-\vartheta} \min\left\{\Vop_J(f),\,\left\|\Dop_J f\right\|_{\Leb^q}^2\right\}^{\vartheta},
\end{equation}
where $\vartheta=\vartheta(q,t) \triangleq \min\left\{\frac{q}{2-q}\tanh(t), 1\right\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.358554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2349535a679bd6bc7f8991ac4fd8e7402fd821e29411bd5b9ccc4993efc39957","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm area min of arXiv:2512.12796, 'Symmetrization and the Planar Skorokhod Embedding Problem'] Let $\mu\in\mathfrak{M}$. Then for every $s\in(0,1)$
