{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.524494+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_234b32d28dff6603d6dae9c6735626acdd62a7a45f277d2af115c5e631649dc7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.30638, 'On compact steady pluriclosed soliton surfaces'] Let $M$ be a Hopf surface, then $\pi_1(M)$ contains a cyclic subgroup $\langle \gamma\rangle$ with finite index. The action of $\gamma$ on $\mathbb C^2\setminus\{(0,0)\}$ under some holomorphic coordinate can be written as 
