{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.620851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_238f9b61dc8342fbaaca5f02ee69e1b00c6f107968515089e639ea3876211c02","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:G0 of arXiv:2412.05503, 'Critical scaling profile for trees and connected subgraphs \\ on the complete graph'] For both trees and connected subgraphs, for all $s \ge 0$, and for all sequences
$p_V$ with $p_V \le 1+sV^{-1/2}$ and $\lim_{V\to\infty}p_V=p\in [0,1]$,
\begin{align}

    \lim_{V\to\infty} G_{V,0}(p_V)
    &=
