{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.487096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23908f1757236678914fb5620d46fdfc88a212f4bee1b85a4febea519ae118d3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 6 of arXiv:2607.03360, 'Smoluchowski-Kramers Approximation Meets Khasminskii Averaging Principles in Nonequilibriu'] Fix $R>0$. For each $x\in \rr^{d_1}$ and $y \in \rr^{d_2}$, let $M_{R,n}(x,y)$ and $\Dl_{R,n}(x,y)$ be defined in \eqref{M-mat} and \eqref{Dl-xy}, respectively. Then 
