{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.399680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23a44470546bc21146fb58e2b4f80d032ec8c824ba72fa71a924df4ea6866d17","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:decorrelation setting of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $p\in[-d, 2]$. Suppose that $\Phi$ is a locally absolutely square-integrable invariant random measure, and suppose that $K$ is an invariant transport kernel. Assume that Condition~(c:condition square-integrable general with p of the paper) or Condition~(c:condition square-integrable Markov with p of the paper) is fulfilled. Further, assume that 
