{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.765357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23be126fc2671a287aa5d7936c9cf2137911a4519e6f52aa8281eda069426534","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Radon-Nikodym Estimate) of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] Let $\mathcal{E}_t$ be the stochastic exponential defined as in \cref{prop: NOVIKOV CONDITION FOR THE STOCHASTIC EXPONENTIAL}. Then, for all $p > 1$ close enough to $1$,
