{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.406367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23bf15a4cd0358ffe2c53b5e45f322a338db0f79f31db3daa39e0a3e8c716b86","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L: squeeze lemma of arXiv:2511.11036, 'Analysis of a class of Recursive Distributional Equations Including the Resistance of the '] Assume that $\mathcal{F}$ and $Q$ satisfy assumptions (equation A: elliptic of the paper) and (equation A: lipschitz of the paper) and fix $F_{\text{in}} \in CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$.  Suppose that $\{F^{(N),+}_{\text{in}}\}$ and $\{F^{(N),-}_{\text{in}}\}$ are two sequences of continuous functions in $CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$ such that
