{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.710712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23c0423bd6da306b5a7482b35d49857c7e540927b2fc7330cb8084616b8da855","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:prelim-ll-bounds of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Recall that $\lambda$ satisfies $L = \frac{\lambda\beta}{{\widehat\pi}_\infty(\phi_o = H+1)}$. For $\beta$ large, there exists $\varepsilon_\beta^\square \downarrow 0$ such that the following holds w.h.p.:
