{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.636025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23e6c1b2c6367be5c7c5dbd085073bfaa9a6c33bd1e07c92100c9b600f674c65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:semi-good2 of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] Let $a,\delta>0, n \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $J : \mathbb{H}_L \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ be a kernel such that $J\left(L^j\right) \geq \frac{(a+\delta)L \log (j)}{L^{2j}}$ for every $j\geq n$. Then, for all $k\in \mathbb{N}$ for which $(a+\delta)( 1 - L^{-k} ) \geq a$ and for all subsets $A\subset \Lambda_{n,n+k}$ of size $|A|=\gamma L^k$ one has
