{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.702056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23fdf06b8f15e220fbf70584ed0cfd049a399ca89ffec9e0a3aff3ad39736cd4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem cancellation2 of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Fix a tuple $(i_{1},\ldots,i_{l})$ that is not composed of mutually distinct indices, and define the set $J$ from $(i_{1},\ldots,i_{l})$ as before. Then there exists a constant $C>1$ that depends on $\mathbf{k}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{k}_{l}$ and $\sigma$, and is uniform in $N$, such that for all $N\ge 100$, 
