\end{enumerate}
Then, in addition to all the conclusions of Theorem~(t:BendikovSaloffCoste of the paper),
\begin{enumerate}[$(i)$]
\item if~(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:A of the paper) holds, then~$\left(\boldsymbol\mssE,\msD(\boldsymbol\mssE)\right)$ is strongly local;
\item if~(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:B of the paper) holds, then~$\left(\boldsymbol\mssE,\msD(\boldsymbol\mssE)\right)$ admits carr\'e du champ operator~$\tparen{\boldsymbol{\mathsf{\Gamma}},\dom{\boldsymbol{\mathsf{\Gamma}}}}$ the closure of~$(\boldsymbol{\mathsf{\Gamma}},\Cyl{}{})$;

\item if~(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:A of the paper) and~(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:B of the paper) hold, then the martingale~$M^{\class{u}}_\bullet$ in~(equation eq:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:1 of the paper) has quadratic variation~$\tquadvar{M^{\class{u}}}_\bullet=\tsharpb{M^{\class{u}}}_\bullet$ given by the right-hand side of~(equation eq:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:2 of the paper) for every~$u\in\Cyl{}{}$.
\end{enumerate}
\begin{proof}
(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:1 of the paper) Strong locality (in the generalized sense) is invariant under quasi-homeo\-morphisms by (the proof of)~[Kuw98].
Thus, applying the quasi-homeo\-morphism~${\boldsymbol\upalpha}$ constructed in the proof of Theorem~(t:BendikovSaloffCoste of the paper), it suffices to prove the assertion in the case when~$M_k$ is compact for every~$k$.
In this case, the form~$\big({\boldsymbol\mssE,\msD(\boldsymbol\mssE)}\big)$ is additionally regular, and \emph{strong locality} in the sense of~[FukOshTak11] coincides with \emph{locality} in the sense of~[BouHir91], as noted, e.g., in~[tElRobSikZhu06].
Thus, the assertion holds by~[BouHir91] in light of Remark~(r:BHTensor of the paper).

(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:2 of the paper) holds by~[BouHir91] in light of Remark~(r:BHTensor of the paper).

(i:c:BSCStronglyLocal:3 of the paper) is standard, cf.\ e.g.~[FukOshTak11].
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

