{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.123134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24331037da37d2ae66c30f105fbdeeb1882a09965465d1c71ab2c9fd9dfd4153","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2605.27713, 'Lower path regularity in all dimensions'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ be a centered Gaussian process $X=(X^1,...,X^d)$ with values in $\mathbb{R}^d$ and with real valued components $X^\ell=(X^\ell_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ satisfying
		\begin{equation}

			C_- \lvert t-s\rvert^{2H} \leq \mathbb{E}(X^\ell_t - X^\ell_s)^2 \leq C_+\lvert t-s\rvert^{2H},\qquad 0\leq s<t\leq T,
		\end{equation}
		for fixed constants $H \in (0,1)$ and $C_+\geq C_->0$. Suppose that the local non-determinism property
		\begin{equation}

			\E \left| \sum_{k=1}^m \langle \xi_k,X_{t_k}-X_{t_{k-1}}\rangle\right|^2 \geq C \prod_{\ell=1}^d \sum_{k=1}^m \xi_{k,\ell}^2 \E (X^\ell_{t_k}-X^\ell_{t_{k-1}})^2
		\end{equation}
		holds with a constant $C>0$ and for all $m\in \mathbb{N}$, $\xi_k \in \mathbb{R}^d$ and all $0=t_0<t_1<\ldots<t_m\leq T$. Then 
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(i)] Assumption \ref{a1} (i) and (ii) hold with $\theta=0$ respectively $\iota = \frac12$.
			\item[(ii)] For any $t \in (0,T)$  there is a constant $c_4(t)>0$ such that
			\[\liminf _{r \to 0} \sup_{s \in (t-r,t+r)} \frac{\|X_t - X_s \| }{r^H(\log\log r^{-1})^{-H}} \geq c_4(t)\qquad \text{$\mathbb{P}$-a.s.}\]
			\item[(iii)] There is a constant $c_5>0$ such that		
			\[\liminf _{r \to 0} \inf_{t\in (0,T)} \sup_{s \in (t-r,t+r)} \frac{\|X_t - X_s \| }{r^{H} ( \log r^{-1})^{-H}} \geq c_5\qquad \text{$\mathbb{P}$-a.s.}\]
		\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.331709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2434646c545e8c4ad0d14f4fd418e5aef1dc63acec60c39c2a1045bfcf9bb04b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:Ito_Lie_series of arXiv:2411.06827, 'The Exponential Lie Series and a Chen--Strichartz Formula for L{\'e}vy Processes'] In terms of the It{\^o} integrals $I_w$ the Chen--Strichartz series is given by
