{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.339245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_243b260acb8c06a5737e81117a04134f34ce46ab994c34333b845073eafa1a82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 18 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] Assume $V''\ge -\a$ for some $\a>0$ and $\int_\R e^{-V(\eta)} d\eta<\infty$.
