{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.766730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2460c023e1939c362f53174d26a349159bf2a52b76dd869f4fe643dc97522cc1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2608.26803, 'On bubbling of Fueter maps'] Let $X$ be a reduced complex space. The \textbf{Barlet space} of compact $n$--cycles is defined to be the following set of formal sums of analytic subsets of $X$
  \begin{align*}
  \mathcal C_n(X)\coloneq \Bigg\{ \sum_{j=1}^{r} m_j Z_j\ \Bigg|\
  \begin{array}{l}
    Z_j \subset X \text{ are distinct irreducible compact analytic} \\
    \text{subsets of pure dimension } n \, \text{with } m_j \in \mathbb Z_{>0}
  \end{array}
  \Bigg\}.
\end{align*}
  If $Z  =\sum_{j=1}^{r} m_j Z_j \in \cC_n(X)$ is an analytic cycle, we denote by 
  \begin{equation*}
    |Z| \coloneq  \bigcup_{j = 1}^r Z_j
  \end{equation*}
  its \textbf{support}. The cycle $Z$ is called \textbf{reduced} if all $m_j = 1$.

  More generally, if $S$ is a set parametrizing a family of cycles $(Z_s)_{s \in S}$ of $n$--cycles in $X$, we define its \textbf{set-theoretic graph} to be 
  \begin{equation*} 
    |\Gamma_S| \coloneq \{(s,x) \in S \times X \mid x \in |Z_s|\}. 
  \end{equation*} 
  In particular, the \textbf{tautological family} over $\cC_n(X)$ is the family whose member over a point $Z \in \cC_n(X)$ is precisely the cycle $Z$ itself.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.043112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2463809ce7d9e6b7c9ef9a1adab2acc7984382129b5df85525c389cb461734aa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2606.31936, 'Coupling and Maximal Inequalities for Graph-Dependent Empirical Processes'] Suppose $(N_{n},V_{n})$ is a uniform doubling with polynomial growth graph with dimension $d$.	Then, for any $n \in \mathbb{N}$, any $a,b >0$, any $p \in [1,\infty]$, and any $d \geq 1$, there exists a partition \(\mathcal P_n(q_n)=\{B_1,\ldots,B_{M_n}\}\)  satisfying $\max_{m\in[M_n]}|B_m|\lesssim q_n $ with $q_{n} \in [n] $, such that
	\begin{align*}
		\left \| \sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}  \mathbb G_{n}(f)   \right\|_{L^{1}(\mathbb P)} \lesssim 	\Lambda_{p,d}(q_{n})  \gamma_{2,a}(\mathcal F ,   \max_{i \in N_{n}}   || \cdot ||_{L^{2p}(P_{Z_{i}}) } )   + \left(   \frac{q_{n}}{\sqrt{n}}  + \sqrt{n} 	\bar{\tau}_{\operatorname{cone} \mathcal F,G_n}
		\left( 	\mathcal P_{n}(q_{n}), 	\mathcal C_{q_{n}^{1/d}}[\mathcal P_{n}(q_{n}) ] \right)  \right)  \gamma_{1,b}(\mathcal F ,   ||\cdot||_{\infty}).
	\end{align*}
where 
\begin{align*}
	\Lambda_{p,d}(q_{n}) : = 	\left\{  
	\begin{array}{ll}
	\max_{m \in [M_{n}]} 	\sqrt{  q^{(1-1/d)}_{n}   \sum_{\rho=0}^{	\lfloor 2 q^{1/d}_{n} \rfloor+1}   \left(  \alpha_{ \mathcal{F} , B_{m} }(\rho)   \right)^{1-\frac{1}{p} } }  & if~p \in (1,\infty] \\
		\sqrt{ 	q_{n}  } & if~p = 1
	\end{array}
\right.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.688223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2466449edfddf96f78ded7d63068ed6e034c0739093a981783481838eb39b396","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thmLowerTailAsymp of arXiv:2411.18563, 'Lower tails for triangles inside the critical window'] Fix $c>0$ and $\eta\in [0,1)$ satisfying $c< \overline c(\eta)$.
If $p=(1+o(1))c/\sqrt{n}$ then 
\begin{equation}

  \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{n^{3/2}}\log \mathbb{P}_p(X\leq \eta \mathbb{E} X)=\frac{1}{2} \cdot\left[  \frac{W(2 \zeta c^2)^{3/2} +3W(2\zeta c^2)^{1/2}}{3\sqrt{2\zeta}}-\frac{\log(1-\zeta) \eta c^3}{3}-c\right]
\end{equation}
where $\zeta$ is the unique solution in $[0,1]$ to the equation
 \begin{equation}

    (1-\zeta)\left( \frac{ W(2 \zeta c^2)}{2 \zeta c^2} \right)^{3/2}= \eta\, . 
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.289451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2466a45b852422ecf13645986fe8a911a9a4b001fd5af7605bd2f9b5d0c6f033","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:genPI of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] Let $M\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|\times |\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}$ be an irreducible generator. A strictly positive probability measure $\zeta\in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$ satisfies the
\begin{itemize}
\item \emph{generalised Poincar\'e inequality (gPI)} if there exists a constant $\alpha > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\forall f\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}  : \ \ \operatorname{var}_\zeta(f)\leq \frac{1}{\alpha} \mathscr{E}_\zeta(f);
\end{equation}
\item \emph{generalised log-Sobolev inequality (gLSI)} if there exists a constant $\alpha > 0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\forall \varphi\in \mathcal D_\zeta(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}): \ \ \mathscr{H}_\zeta(\varphi)\leq  \frac{1}{\alpha} \mathscr{R}_\zeta(\varphi).
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal D_\zeta(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$ is the space of densities with respect to $\zeta$ (defined in~(equation def:SpaceDen of the paper)).
\end{itemize}
The suprema over all possible choices of $\alpha$ are called respectively the \emph{generalised Poincar\'e} and the \emph{generalised log-Sobolev constants}. We denote them by $\alpha_{\gPI}(\cdot, M), \alpha_{\gLSI}(\cdot, M) :\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})\to [0,\infty)$ and they are given by
\begin{align}
    \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta, M) \coloneqq \inf_{\substack{ f\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|} \\ f\notin \langle\1\rangle }} \frac{\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f, M)}{\operatorname{var}_\zeta(f)}, \quad\text{and}\quad \alpha_{\gLSI}(\zeta, M) \coloneqq \inf_{\substack{\varphi\in\mathcal D_\zeta(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}) \\ \varphi\neq \1}} \frac{\mathscr{R}_\zeta(\varphi, M)}{\mathscr{H}_\zeta(\varphi)}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.762145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24690acff7d5902037402d02e0aca3ef9c41b0e79e9fe081fba6e50e11c4d1fb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (Approximate functional equation) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $A\gg1$ be a large number, and $G(u)=\left(\cos{\frac{\pi u}{4A}}\right)^{-5A}$. We have, 
		\begin{equation}
			L\left(\frac{1}{2},\; \sym^2\pi\right)=\sum_{n\geq 1}\frac{\lambda_\pi(n^2)}{\sqrt{n}}V_{1/2}\left(\frac{n}{\sqrt{\mathcal Q}}\right)+\eps(\pi, \sym^2)\sum_{n\geq 1}\frac{\lambda_{\bar \pi}(n^2)}{\sqrt{n}}\tilde{V}_{1/2}\left(\frac{n}{\sqrt{\mathcal Q}}\right).
		\end{equation}
		where $\mathcal Q=Q(\sym^2\pi)$, and the weight functions are given by,
		\begin{equation*}
			\begin{split}
				&V_{1/2}(y)=\sum_{d|p^\infty}\frac{\lambda_{\sym^2\pi}(d)}{\sqrt{d}}W(dy)\\
				&W(y)=\frac{1}{2\pi i}\int_{(2)}\frac{L_\infty(1/2+u, \sym^2\pi)}{L_\infty(1/2, \sym^2\pi)}L(1+2u, \chi_\pi^2)G(u)y^{-u}\frac{du}{u}.
			\end{split}
		\end{equation*}
		$\tilde V_{1/2}$ is defined in a similar way as $V$ except $\lambda_{\sym^2\pi}$(resp. $\chi_\pi$) is replaced by $\lambda_{\sym^2\bar \pi}$ (resp. $\bar\chi_\pi$). Set $q_\infty=q_\infty(1/2, \sym^2\pi)$, for any $j\geq0$ we have, 
		$$
		y^j V_{1/2}^{(j)}(y)\ll_{j, A} \left(1+\frac{y}{\sqrt{q_\infty}}\right)^{-A}.
		$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.441772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_246bd7f423eb4f2416bb8f820bb996414da8e4999d4937c019f9d1e2a953e5f8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 31 of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] It almost surely holds that for all ${\bm u} \in H^{1,2} \cap L^{\frac{q}{q-2}}$ and $t \in [0,T]$ and $n \in \mathbb N$
