{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.303526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2480098c4397e13296dcf20205b43e52921ae96939ca3bda7e2e896457155274","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 41 (Diffusive scale estimate for differences of coordinates) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Fix $q\ge 2$, $M>0$, and some $F:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ that is decreasing and $\sum_{k=0}^\infty k^{d-1} F(k)<\infty$. 
