{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24846bce218a0b5424fe6e5dda2813431db305b1c187d773d6a04b8ee55c3b53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: LLN for subsequence of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Assume that $\{X_t\}_{t\geq 0}$ (resp. $\{X_k\}_{k\geq 0}$) is a d-dimensional $\alpha$-mixing identical process (resp. sequence) on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$ for some $\alpha>0$ with $\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_0|^{2}]<\infty$. Let $\{t_k\}_{k\geq 1}$ (resp. $\{m_k\}_{k\geq 1}$) be a $(\gamma,\delta)$-admissible subsequence for some $0<\gamma<1, \delta>0$. Let
		\begin{equation}
			S_n:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n X_{t_i} \ (resp. \ S_n:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n X_{m_i}), \ \text{ and } \ X_0\sim \Gamma.
