{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.569373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2487ae2e76490795365a6145bfad30252bcd4afd2644035b764232d1abfb148e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.14170, 'Uniform-in-time error estimates for McKean-Vlasov SDEs with common noise and stochastic al'] Suppose that Assumptions \ref{A1}, \ref{A2}, \ref{S1}, \ref{N1} hold with $\lambda_1>2\lambda_2$ and that $\sigma_0\sigma_1\neq 0$. Let 
