{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.455532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_248e54937206e0e17a8f451ae492bf309d094eaa72c901a4e74747e001984b6a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 6 (Time evolution of a plateau before breaking time) of arXiv:2609.02523, '\bf Strong Ill-Posedness in critical and subcritical regimes for the Hunter--Saxton equati'] Assume that the initial data $u_0$ is given such that $q_0 =-A$ on some space interval $R$, for some $A>0$, where 
