{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.307573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_248fffbd2a7dd5f3527b1e49bba2bd5e4752a4c6fdcac8dbb4df0de426e22222","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:dec of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] For any $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$, $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$ and $n \in {\mathbb{Z}}_{\ge 0}$, we have 
                \begin{align}
