{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.722397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24b9727d2b664bb8234b981a51092ef2e06b3091da615744472381f228c07780","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main of arXiv:2609.02769, 'Divergence-Free Approximation in Sobolev and Lebesgue Spaces on general unbounded domains '] Let $\Omega=\mathbb{R}^d$, $d\in\{2,3\}$  and $r\in[1,\infty).$ Let $\boldsymbol{u}_0\in \mathbb{H}$ and $\boldsymbol{f}\in \mathrm{L}^{2}(0,T;\mathbb{V}')$  be given.  Then  there exists a Leray-Hopf weak solution to the system ((abstract-CBF of the paper))  
		\begin{align} 
			\boldsymbol{u}\in \mathrm{L}^{\infty}(0,T;\mathbb{H})\cap \mathrm{L}^2(0,T;\mathbb{V})\cap \mathrm{L}^{r+1}(0,T; \mathbb{L}_{\sigma}^{r+1}), \ \frac{\/\mathrm{d}\/\boldsymbol{u}}{\/\mathrm{d}\/ t} \in \mathrm{L}^{p_d}(0,T;\mathbb{V}')+ \mathrm{L}^{\frac{r+1}{r}}(0,T;\mathbb{L}_{\sigma}^{\frac{r+1}{r}}),
