{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.848748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24bbb3243d96934b1dfad9c3834894649866ee66149a3545e4c9dcefb206c429","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm stat_conv of arXiv:2607.08869, 'Inequalities for convex functions of random points inside and on the boundary of convex bo'] For $X, Y \in \mathbb{R}^d$, one has $X \preceq_{cx} Y$ if and only if for every unit vector $u \in S^{d-1}$ and every convex $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$,
