    \end{equation}
    Then, with probability at least $1-\iota$, 
    \begin{equation}
    \mbox{all connected components of } \cup_w \overline{B(w, 1)} \mbox{ have } |\cdot|_\infty \mbox{-diameter at most } \iota R,
    \end{equation}
    where the union is over those $w \in \mathscr{L}_R$ for which $\mathcal{E}_w$ does not occur, and two boxes that share exactly one point are also viewed as connected. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

