{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.344191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24d7ebcd03729a4175ca56be15a025db807a16e97f22c1c9b8f02bd2c557fcdc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 23 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] \normalfont
Let $M,N\in(\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{loc}})^\mathbb{B}$, and $M^c$ and $N^c$ be their continuous martingale parts. Define
\begin{equation}
[M,N]=M_0N_0\mathfrak{I}_\mathbb{B}+\langle M^c,N^c\rangle+\Sigma (\Delta M\Delta N).
