{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.788055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24ec998c301b33f3ae404d0896560552af0d48a5ac6e5a357ade9d697def1749","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:fluctuation-identities of arXiv:2608.22910, 'A Commutator Framework for Selective Spectral Alignment in Deep Neural Networks'] Let \(x,x'\) be independent with law \(\mu\). Then
\begin{align}
\mathcal V_{\ell+1}
&=
\mathbb E_\mu\|S_{\ell+1}\|_F^2
-\|\mathcal S_{\ell+1}\|_F^2\\
&=
\frac12\mathbb E_{\mu\otimes\mu}
\|S_{\ell+1}(x)-S_{\ell+1}(x')\|_F^2.

\end{align}
If \(g_{\ell+1}=\nabla_{a_{\ell+1}}F\), so that
\(S_{\ell+1}=g_{\ell+1}g_{\ell+1}^\top\), then
\begin{align}
\mathcal V_{\ell+1}
&=
\mathbb E_\mu\|g_{\ell+1}\|^4
-\left\|
\mathbb E_\mu[g_{\ell+1}g_{\ell+1}^\top]
\right\|_F^2
\\
&=
\frac12\mathbb E_{\mu\otimes\mu}
\bigl[
\|g_{\ell+1}(x)\|^4+\|g_{\ell+1}(x')\|^4
-2\langle g_{\ell+1}(x),g_{\ell+1}(x')\rangle^2
\bigr].

\end{align}
In particular, \(\mathcal V_{\ell+1}=0\) if and only if
\(S_{\ell+1}(x)=\mathcal S_{\ell+1}\) for \(\mu\)-almost every \(x\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.377333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24f2567a0a424194dfceaa989af4384db9b38832b8284a3c5b8e21dbb261ba69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma vprocess of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix  $k \geq 2$, a finite-support function $h:\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{R}$, and a sequence $\beta=\beta_N\to 0$ as $N\to \infty$. Consider $\mathbf x^N\in \mathbb{Z}^k$ such that $N^{-1/2}\mathbf x^N\to \mathbf z \in \mathbb{R}^k$ as $N\to \infty$. Then, for all $1\le i,j\le k$, $i\neq j$, the pair
     \begin{equation}
      \tonde{N^{-1/2}\tttonde{R^i_{tN} - R^j_{tN}},N^{-1/2} \textstyle{\int_0^{tN}} h(R^i_s - R^j_s)\,{\rm d} s }_{t\ge 0}\; \text{,}\;\;\quad\text{under}\ \mathbf P_{\mathbf x^N}^{(\beta_N,k)}\; \text{,}\;\;
