    \begin{equation}
    (W_t, \gamma^2(h)\, L_t^W )_{t\ge 0}\; \text{,}\;\;\quad \text{with}\ \gamma^2(h)\coloneqq \textstyle{\sum_{x\in \mathbb{Z}}}\, h(x)\; \text{,}\;\;
    \end{equation}where $W$ is a Brownian motion with $W_0=z_i-z_j\in \mathbb{R}$, and $L^W$ is its local time at zero. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

