{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.321168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2511346c7de7f979ec18512a92453fef6e6cc03bc5c1a5d7f0facc5e83ffcf3b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 of arXiv:2506.21087, 'Quasi-Stationary Distributions of Interacting Dynamical Systems and their approximation'] Assume \ref{condhzero}, \ref{condhun} and \ref{condhdeux}. 

\begin{itemize} 

\item[(i)] For any $\mu_0\in{\cal P}(\MM)$, the differential equation

