{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.777375+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_251c165f7e9f6a387d3c721ff3fd9bfa9eebc1a2a787f3f911237d3a10bb419e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_modification_of_shift of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] For any $1\le k\le DN/2$, suppose that $\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}$ satisfies the condition (equation eq:condA2 of the paper). Defined $z_1$ and $\Delta_{\text{\rm{ev}}}$ as in (equation eq:z1 of the paper) and (equation definition_shift_eigenvector of the paper) for a constant $\varepsilon\in\left({0,1}\right)$.

