{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.795001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25490a70f29ee7587962225aa359a8d3465cda350b03c4b0c4eacc8f2cc4f58b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma scaling_plambda of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] Fix $p\in(0,1)$ and let $E$ be a finite-crossing event associated with some $(k,A)$. Then, for any decay exponent $1<\delta\le\infty$, we have
