{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.827501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_255358de8d65402cbf54748480248639c8569168fea04754532a3e0432351b10","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: closeness_of_solutions_time of arXiv:2609.00257, 'Stability estimates for the initial-to-final-state inverse problem'] Let $V_j\in L^1((0, T); L^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n))$ with $n\geq 2$ be such that $\| V_j \|_{w}< \infty$ with weight $w:\mathbb{R}^n \to (0,1]$ and satisfying the smallness condition $\|  \mathop\mathrm{Im} V_j \|_{w} \leq \frac{1}{4T} $, for $j\in\{1,2,3\}$.
For $f,g\in L^2(\mathbb{R}^n)$, let $u_j, \, v_j \in C([0, T]; L^2(\mathbb{R}^n))$ be solutions of the corresponding initial and final value problems for the Schr\"odinger equation

\[
\begin{dcases}
(i\partial_t+\Delta - V_j)u_j = 0, \quad &\textup{in}\,\, \Sigma, \\
u_j(0, \centerdot) = f \in L^2(\mathbb{R}^n), &\textup{in}\,\, \mathbb{R}^n
