{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.105919+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2559c083e7a2cb46a8802865033383d48ee495982c790a037a34950dd32a4350","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem workload-optimality of arXiv:2505.04942, '\textbf{Randomized Routing to Remote Queues}'] Assume the conditions of Theorem~(theorem:load-balancing of the paper) hold for a sequence of GBC systems where the customers' origins are known. Then for $T > 0$, $ \sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} \tilde{\Gamma}^{\dagger}_{n}(t) \Rightarrow 0 $ as $ n \to \infty $. If conditions~(equation eq:fourth-moments of the paper) and (equation eq:log-log-n-bound of the paper) also hold, then there exist two positive numbers $ C^{\dagger} $ and $ C^{\ddagger} $ such that with probability 1,
	\[
	\sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} \tilde{\Gamma}^{\dagger}_{n}(t) < \max \Big\{ C^{\dagger} \chi_{n}, C^{\ddagger} \frac{\log \log n + \log (n \chi_{n}^{2})}{\sqrt{n} \chi_{n}} \Big\} \quad \mbox{for $n$ sufficiently large.}
