{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.306217+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_258a6f4a69d43d4ee7750a5c5761aa33436dd00a0c86c6a66b85519a78630a74","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: main 1 of arXiv:2607.20097, 'Phase transition for the asymptotic entropy of branching random walks on groups'] Let $G$ be a countable group and let $\textsf{BRW}(G,\pi,\mu)$ be a branching random walk with step distribution $\mu$ on $G$ and offspring distribution $\pi$ with mean $\mathbb{E}[\pi]=\rho>1$. If $\mu$ has finite entropy, $\pi(0)=0$, and $\pi$ has a finite second moment, then the following holds for the entropy $H(\widehat{M}_n)$ of the empirical distribution $\widehat{M}_n$ of $\textsf{BRW}(G,\pi,\mu)$\textcolor{blue}{:}
\begin{enumerate}[label = (\roman*)]
\setlength\itemsep{0em}
    \item \textbf{Small-$\rho$ regime.} If $\rho\leq \mathsf{e}^{\textsf{h}(\mu)}$, then almost surely
    $$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{H(\widehat{M}_n)}{n}=\log\rho.$$
    \item \textbf{Large-$\rho$ regime.} If $\rho > \mathsf{e}^{\textsf{h}(\mu)}$, then almost surely
    $$\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{H(\widehat{M}_n)}{n} = \textsf{h}(\mu),$$
    where $\textsf{h}(\mu)$ is the asymptotic entropy of the random walk $(G,\mu)$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

