{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.441136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25b31f244b739ae06eee00c3dbce1451724d68505972b3ca229cef2ff5476060","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 154 (Scaled response germs) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] A \emph{scale system} at $z$ is a family
\[
 r_\beta:(0,1]\to(0,\infty),
 \qquad r_\beta(\eps)\downarrow0,
 \quad \beta\in\mathfrak B.
\]
A pointed curve $\gamma=(\gamma_\eps)_{\eps\downarrow0}$ in
$\mathsf Z_{\mathfrak R}$ is an \emph{$r$-controlled response germ at $z$} if
$\gamma_\eps\to z$ in the response-generated uniformity and
\begin{equation}
 \limsup_{\eps\downarrow0}
 \frac{\delta_\beta(\gamma_\eps,z)}{r_\beta(\eps)}<\infty
 \qquad\text{for every }\beta.
\end{equation}
For two controlled germs set
\begin{equation}
 \gamma\sim_{z,r}^{(1)}\eta
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 \frac{\delta_\beta(\gamma_\eps,\eta_\eps)}{r_\beta(\eps)}\longrightarrow0
 \quad\text{for every }\beta.
\end{equation}
The quotient
\begin{equation}
 T_{z,r}^{\rm resp}\mathsf Z_{\mathfrak R}
 :=\operatorname{Germ}_{z,r}(\mathsf Z_{\mathfrak R})/
      \!\sim_{z,r}^{(1)}
\end{equation}
is the \emph{scaled response tangent set}.  At this level it is a pointed set.
Linear, graded, or Lie structure descends from short-experiment operations
that are asymptotically congruent.","status":"unverified"}

