{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.149050+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25e6381f191d542e2eece4f05f3983385a6baaacdc28010b9164aa9ec84fac91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.13387, 'Multiradial Schramm-Loewner evolution: \\ Infinite-time large deviations and transience'] There exists a constant $\kappa_0 = \kappa_0(n) > 0$ depending only on $n$ such that the following holds.
