{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.822813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25e722da778d8c3f5aeb825fc27343e00e57635290f5b24ee64aa39a2f3d839f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: negative part vanishes of arXiv:2504.04792, 'Uniqueness and Longtime Behavior of the Completely Positively Correlated Symbiotic Branchi'] Let $u$ and $M$ as above. Assume that $M \geq 0$. Then,

