{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.477540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25ef620a7489ad49e4c24052a3460322e2e4c75253b29cd1c509817a9e9b1603","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 91 (Chronological Gaussian realization of the tensor--Pfaffian mechanism) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $H_0$ be a separable real Hilbert space, let $W$ be cylindrical Wiener
noise on $H_0$, and let
$K:[s,t]\to\Sch_2(H_0,E)$ be deterministic and strongly measurable.  Set
\[
 M_u:=\int_s^uK_v\,dW_v,
 \qquad
 R:=\int_s^t\|K_v\|_{\Sch_2}^2\,dv<\infty.
\]
Let $\Xi_k^{s,t}$ be the chronological alternating It\^o tower of $M$ and
$A^M_{s,t}$ its skew L\'evy area.  Then the same-field branch of
Theorem~\ref{thm:tensor-pfaffian-transfer} applies with $\rho=1$ and
$\sigma=2$.  More precisely, there are symmetric kernels
$\mathbf L_k\in\mathfrak W_{k,2}$ such that
\begin{equation}

 \Xi_k^{s,t}=I_k(\mathbf L_k),
 \qquad
 \|\mathbf L_k\|_{\mathfrak W_{k,2}}
 \le \frac{R^{k/2}}{k!}.
\end{equation}
Consequently
\begin{equation}

 \mathcal G^{\rm W}_{1,2}
 \le \frac{e^2}{4}R,
\end{equation}
and for every finite $p\ge1$,
\begin{equation}

 \bigl\|\|A^M_{s,t}\|_{\Sch_{1,\infty}}\bigr\|_{L^p}
 \le C_pR.
\end{equation}
Thus, in the deterministic Gaussian martingale sector, the weak-trace endpoint
is obtained through the explicit composition
\[
 \text{ordered It\^o kernel}
 \longrightarrow \text{Wick/oriented tensor estimate}
 \longrightarrow \text{Pfaffian spectral extraction}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.417660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25f227a358143e0f90499b52f49db100f442145c0e1fbf3284af5ce4d85ebcfe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma limit_of_operator_U_coefficients_a_0_a_1 of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] The coefficients of the operator $\mathfrak{U}_t$ (equation eq:operator_U of the paper)
