{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25f3d5a119bd285e7ce072415ba271b78d1f145d65984b1b63037fb39429d59e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem nhprob of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] There exists a constant $C=C(\mathrm{D})>0$ such that, for all $x \in {\rm D}_n$, $t>0$,
