{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.776934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_25fd94339c2acf7946aeea2f1fa7dccbc68fd25ee1c35974ee2ac9cb97373147","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma apx_lemma: random_walk_expected_hitting_size_lower_bound of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$ for some $\alpha, K > 0$. Fix $K_0 \ge 1$ and $\varepsilon \in (0, 1)$.
