{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.785834+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_266c172e9a74aba1eb91fbf36dcfae53083bd0277a2891237a8383a422fce66a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 19 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $g(s,p)$ be a polynomial with real coefficients. Then $g(s,p)$ is without roots in ${\mathbb G}$ if and only if there exists a real contraction \begin{equation} \begin{pmatrix} A_1 & A_2\cr A_2 & A_1\end{pmatrix} \end{equation} such that 

