{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.609407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2693e5339f4ad3789f119c730c35ee827e8aa58724d4c9c358a109c85080ec9e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 13 of arXiv:2607.08314, 'Berry-Heisenberg random waves'] Let $G$ be a separable, locally compact group of type I. A function $B: G \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}$ is positive-definite if and only if it can be represented as 
