{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.468567+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26d4c7df7660345c09dd6aeb759c4aba04c93158a5ae7a17ad1a9ce2e3fa75cd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 66 of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Given intervals $I,J \subset \R$ and real numbers $\ubar,u \in \R$, we define:
