{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.553012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_272f94c3f3deda52342e8d0242a2f99307803f62909eeb22959611355efabd94","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2605.30055, 'The Wasserstein cost of importance sampling'] Let $f,g$ be two probability densities on $(0,1)^d$ satisfying Hypothesis \ref{hyp:W} and let $\hat{g}_n$ be the self-normalized importance sampling measure for $g$ based on $n$ iid samples from $f$.
