{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.219801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_273e875d3263bcbc54ef1b02fd45eb7cbedd7ec46daacca63c485b1efc996835","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: 96 of arXiv:2607.05848, 'Mesoscopic eigenvalue statistics for correlated random matrices'] Consider $H=A+W\in\mathbb{C}^{N\times N}$ satisfying Assumptions (assump: 118 of the paper)--(assump: 176 of the paper). 
Let $g\in C_{\textnormal{c}}^{2}(\mathbb{R})$. Fix a small constant $\epsilon_{0}\in(0,1/2)$, independent of $N$. Consider $\eta_{0}=\eta_{0}(N)\in(N^{-1+\epsilon_{0}},N^{-\epsilon_{0}})$.
Take a fixed reference energy $E_{0}>0$ in the bulk, i.e.\,$\rho(E_{0})\ge\epsilon_{0}$ where $\rho$ is defined in (equation eq: 180 of the paper).
We define the mesoscopically scaled test function $f$ by setting
\begin{equation}
	f(x) \coloneqq g\Big(\frac{x-E_{0}}{\eta_{0}}\Big).
\end{equation}
Let $\mathsf{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})$ denote a Gaussian random variable of mean $\mu$ and variance $\sigma^{2}$.
Then we have the following convergence in distribution:
\begin{equation}
	\Tr f(H) - \mathbb{E}[\Tr f(H)] \overset{\text{d}}{\longrightarrow} \mathsf{N}\Big(0,\frac{1}{2\beta\pi^{2}}\lVert g\rVert_{\dot{H}^{1/2}}^{2}\Big),
\end{equation}
where $\beta=1$ and $\beta=2$ corresponds to real symmetric and complex Hermitian $H$, respectively, and
the norm $\lVert g\rVert_{\dot{H}^{1/2}}$ is  defined in (equation eq: 186c of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.344149+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_273eaf4702401b4075f54a4906962fc3d9ca2fa4668570ff3d365394a9a82ca5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem chessboard-estimate of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] Let $R$ be a block of $\Lambda$, let $A \subset T_{\Lambda}^R$ and let $(f_{\tau})_{\tau \in A}$ be  
