{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.396319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_274820f1c9b1eb87932b518a79d0f484c8c58e0afc1e1aabf3d032cb9ee2b520","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary theorem1.69 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Let $A_n$ be a random symmetric matrix with entry distribution $\zeta$ having mean 0, variance 1 and a finite log-Sobolev constant. Then for any $\kappa>0$, with probability $1-e^{-cn}$, singular values of $A_n$ in $[\kappa n^{1/2},(2-\kappa)n^{1/2}]$ are distinct. Moreover, for any $\epsilon>0$,
    $$
\mathbb{P}(\text{Minimal gap of singular values of $A_n$ in $[\kappa n^{1/2},(2-\kappa)n^{1/2}]$}\leq \epsilon n^{-3/2})\leq C\epsilon+e^{-cn}
    $$ for some $C,c>0$ depending only on $\zeta$ and $\kappa$.

    More generally, fix some $\sigma\in(0,1]$ (and no longer assume that $\zeta$ satisfies LSI). Then we have the following estimate: for the random matrix $A_n$ and any $\epsilon>0$, \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}_{A_n}(\text{Minimal gap of singular values in $[\kappa n^{-1/2+\sigma},(2-\kappa)n^{1/2}]$}\leq \epsilon n^{-3/2})\leq C\epsilon+e^{-cn^{\sigma/2}}
    \end{equation} for some $C,c>0$ depending only on $\zeta$ and $\kappa$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.088525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_274dbc9874b213fc310e32f883f7be749e6b95f7302e76b262aaa599ad2c33b4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 ($\mathrm{Ewens}(m,\theta)$ distribution) of arXiv:2604.25877, 'Asymptotic height of Plancherel random trees'] The $\mathrm{Ewens}(m,\theta)$ distribution on integer partitions of $m$ is the probability
measure on feasible count vectors
$(C_1,\dots,C_m)$ given by
\begin{equation}
\Pp\left((C_j)_{1\le j\le m}=(c_j)_{1\le j\le m}\right)
=\frac{m!}{\theta^{(m)}}\prod_{j=1}^m \frac{\theta^{c_j}}{j^{c_j}c_j!}~,
\end{equation}
for all $(c_j)_{1\le j\le m}$ such that $\sum_{j=1}^m j c_j=m$~.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.488064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_274e3dfd46d970e164742d96299ca49bf6a1a2fbb0aaa4c5996f531e36c2ff34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:feebee-auc of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] For any noise level $\nu \in [0, 1)$, 
