{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.220214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_277ae4ab25b0cd6d211bf9deab15d9f3f33c11bf532aa9631ea7230477fb2ee1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: 369 of arXiv:2607.05848, 'Mesoscopic eigenvalue statistics for correlated random matrices'] {EHR25} and [MR3941370]}]
Consider an $N\times N$ matrix $H=A+W$ satisfying Assumptions (assump: 118 of the paper)--(assump: 176 of the paper).
Let $\epsilon_{0}$ as in Theorem (thm: 96 of the paper).
Let $\rho$ be as in (equation eq: 180 of the paper).
Define $$\mathcal{I}(\epsilon)\coloneqq\{E\in\mathbb{R}: \rho(E)\ge\epsilon\}, \quad \epsilon>0.$$
Let $M(z)$ be the solution of (equation eq: 197 of the paper).
Then, uniformly for all $z=E+\mathrm{i}\eta$ with $E\in\mathcal{I}(\epsilon_{0}/2)$ and $\eta\in[N^{-1+(\epsilon_{0}/100)},100]$ (where the number $100$ can be replaced with any large positive real), the resolvent $G(z)\coloneqq (H-z)^{-1}$ satisfies the isotropic local law,
\begin{equation}
	|\mathbf{u}^{*}(G(z)-M(z))\mathbf{v}| \prec \lVert\mathbf{u}\rVert \lVert\mathbf{v}\rVert (N\eta)^{-1/2},
\end{equation}
for any deterministic vectors $\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{C}^{N}$, and the average local law,
\begin{equation}
	|\langle (G(z)-M(z)) B \rangle| \prec \frac{\lVert B\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}}{N\eta} ,
\end{equation}
for any deterministic matrix $B\in\mathbb{C}^{N\times N}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

