{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.357569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27839d9102cff7c5d7dc7c068583e60cf97099fd2d8f29d4f151e551700583f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2609.03098, 'Standing waves for Schr\"odinger equations with Kato class potentials and $L^\infty$-bound'] Let $u_n:[t_0,t_1]\to H^1(\mathbb{R}^N)$, $n\ge 1$, be a solution of equation \eqref{A-Fn-eqn}, where the family $\{F_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ satisfies the condition \eqref{k-set-for-seq}. Suppose that there exists $R>0$ such that
