{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.735323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_279bc5bbb28b14181bc947fd65ff84895e844f514a76ff1b7778172243089b97","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 15 of arXiv:2609.02197, '2609.02197'] Let $\left(\alpha,\gamma,r\right)\in \mathbb{R}\times \left[1,+\infty\right[^2,$
\begin{align*} 
\left\Vert\cdot\right\Vert_{\mathscr{C}^\alpha}: \mathscr{S}' &\longrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{R}}_+ \\ f & \longmapsto \left\Vert f\right\Vert_{\mathscr{C}^\alpha}=\sup_{q \in \mathbb{N}}2^{\alpha\left(q-1\right)}\Vert \delta_{q-1}f\Vert_{L^{\infty}\left(\mathbb{T}^d\right)}
