{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.270986+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27bf0c8b97912ec9753a81c97999154031f26f28046f558d160728f44dd71c08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pc of arXiv:2412.09535, 'Local limit theorem for joint subgraph counts'] Suppose $p = a/b$ where $a$ and $b$ are relatively prime positive integers. Then a positive integer $n \geq 3$ is $p$-PC if and only if
\begin{cond}
