{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.573423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27d97e09eded583922a3fe5ab43f60eee9b09d784b5d91156e4fb4e3c2824080","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 15 of arXiv:2606.14564, 'Upper tails for irregular graphs \\ beyond the mean-field regime'] For every $J \in \cJ$, all graphs $G$ with $v_G \ge v_J$ and $e_G \ge e_J$, and every $uv \in G$,
