    for any $\rho\geq 0$, where $\hat s=\frac{h_1^2-t_2^2-h_2^2}{2t_2}, \hat h^2=\frac{1}{4}\left[t_2^2+2(h_1^2+h_2^2)+\frac{(h_2^2-h_1^2)^2}{t_2^2}\right]$, 
    $\hat s_1=\frac{t_3^2+h_3^2-h_1^2}{2t_3}$ and $\hat h_1^2=\frac{1}{4}\left[t_3^2+2(h_1^2+h_3^2)+\frac{(h_3^2-h_1^2)^2}{t_3^2}\right]$ and $\vert U^{\hat s}_{\hat h}\cup U^{\hat s_1}_{\hat h_1}\vert $ is evaluated in Lemma~(lemma:UcupU of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.256762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2803e53f88f3b1fde78baf715d3ec9f2c5bedd73c70f5a13beb84117464d9f7f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 54 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $A,A_n,$ and $B$ be compact subsets of a metric space
  $(X,d^X)$ consisting of at least two elements.
  \begin{itemize}
    \item [$\mathrm{(i)}$]There exist $a_1,a_2\in A$ and $b_1,b_2\in B$ satisfying the following.
    \begin{itemize}
      \item $a_1\neq a_2,b_1\neq b_2$
