{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.935714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_281238971e327d492b91c38ef04def4b061eb3ce3ff2cf9f5272a6c7a82a8742","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm|BoundFourierLevel2Torus of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] If $a$ is an integer multiple of $b-a$, then there exists a constant $C$, depending only on $a$, $b$, $p$, and $d$, such that the level-$1$ and level-$2$ Fourier sums of $f^{\tau}$ satisfy
