      c^{-1}t \le D(t)&\le ct.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.833541+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2830276ce37a0488643d3c8ebd6f9605bb37a51d0b90fe6e9d8be09689670e52","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2506.12632, 'Point process convergence of extremes in $K$-symmetric exclusion'] For $A, B \in \sB_\R$, 
