{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.887179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2897e9465cd11120107decfa65a6f556bbc2d5f577872905d3197b8b7016299c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 (Long-range order threshold) of arXiv:2504.02435, 'Poisson-Voronoi percolation in higher rank'] Let $G$ be a lcsc group acting continuously and transitively by isometries on a geodesic lcsc metric space $(M,d)$ and fix some $o\in M$. Suppose that $G$ has property (T). Then for every $R>0$, there exists $p^*<1$ such that every $G$-invariant normal random closed subset $\mathcal Z$ of $M$ with $\mathbb P(o \in \partial \mathcal Z)=0$ satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
        \inf_{x,y\in \mathcal B_R(o)} \mathbb P \big( x\overset{\mathcal Z}{\longleftrightarrow} y \big)>p^* \quad \Rightarrow \quad \inf_{x,y\in M} \mathbb P \big( x\overset{\mathcal Z}{\longleftrightarrow} y \big)>0.
