{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.101831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28affd3fcbda98835f7bce32615ea4cd4b28edf3d85964afef12965dd5dd9aca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem THM33 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $M\in \text{MF}(X)$ and $m^*:=m|_{E_M}$.   Then, the subprocess $X^M$ is a nearly $m^*$-symmetric right process on $E_M$, which is properly associated with the Dirichlet form $({\mathscr E}^M,{\mathscr F}^M)$ {on $L^2(E_M, m^*)$} given by
\begin{equation}
	\begin{aligned}
		&{\mathscr F}^M={\mathscr F}^{E_M}\cap L^2(E_M, \rho_M+\lambda_M), \\
		&{\mathscr E}^M(f,g)={\mathscr E}(f,g)+\nu_M(\tilde{f}\otimes \tilde{g}),\quad f,g\in {\mathscr F}^M,
	\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where ${\mathscr F}^{E_M}$ is defined as in (equation eq:31 of the paper) with $G=E_M$.
 Furthermore,  $X^M$ is $m^*$-tight,  and $({\mathscr E}^M,{\mathscr F}^M)$ is quasi-regular on $L^2(E_M,m^*)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.646439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28b3c2d392196d7299aeb3edc0abdccd85b8e4e9f8d180d39d56cb4fef946f0d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop reg_plus half-space of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] {PV26}}] 
Let $\beta,h \geq 0$. There exists $r\geq 0$ such that, for every $\Lambda'\subset \Lambda \subset \mathbb H$ finite satisfying $\mathrm{d}(\partial^{\textup{ext},+} \Lambda,\Lambda')\geq r$,
\begin{equation}
\nu_{\Lambda,\beta}^{+,h} \preccurlyeq \nu_{\Lambda',\beta}^{+,h} \quad \text{and} \quad \nu_{\Lambda,\beta}^{+,h}(|\cdot|) \preccurlyeq \nu_{\Lambda',\beta}^{+,h}(|\cdot|).
