{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.264005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28b947f4e27afad5e6284f156e908e174a77bd004e87f73d4272a9cfad3e04db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma concentration of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] For any $z\in\CC^+$, $\Gamma\in\mathsf{Sym}_L(\RR)$, and any $A\in\CC^{nL\times nL}$ with $\nbr{A}=1$, the normalized trace $\frac{1}{n}\tr\sbr{ A G(z;\Gamma) }$ concentrates around its mean. Namely, for any $\delta>0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \PP\rbr{ \abr{ \frac{1}{n}\tr\sbr{ A G(z;\Gamma) } - \EE \cbr{ \frac{1}{n}\tr\sbr{ A G(z;\Gamma) } } } \ge \delta } \le 2 \exp\rbr{- C \rbr{\Im z}^4 n^2 \delta^2}.
    \end{equation}
