{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.946071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28bf6d14572447ad32081b6fd7c448e9150b39879a21ab18e274fb3d3e224070","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop bicausaltptplansinducedbybicausalmongemapswienermeasures of arXiv:2412.02948, 'Causal transport on path space'] Let $\pi \in \Pi_{bc}\deln{\mathbb{W}^d, \mathbb{W}^d}$ and $\rho : \sbr{0,1} \times \mathcal{W}^d \times \mathcal{W}^d \rightarrow \mathcal{C}^d$ be the $\deln{\deln{\mathcal{\mathcal{H}}_t \otimes \mathcal{\mathcal{H}}_t}^\pi}_{t+ \in \sbr{0,1}}$-progressively measurable correlation process of the marginal processes $X,Y$ under $\pi$: 
