{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.067194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28d4f2f3c1120d9ec83b7af17be143a63486616591d7de003215e56a97f3445d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2606.27520, 'Critical curve of loop percolation on the $d$-regular tree'] There exists a real number $z_0 \in (1, 1/\tau^{2})$ such that $Z_{\widetilde{Q}} = \{z_0\}$. Furthermore, $z_0$ is a simple zero of $\widetilde{Q}(z)$ and it is given as the unique solution of $z \in D$ to
