{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.429826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28d7f2c92b9069a387480d9bd6ca3d315abf91b44fd00c0869d321e24e5f3fe3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 200 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Let $C > 0$. Consider the defining data for a master problem such that
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\boldsymbol{\Theta}$ is positive semi-definite;
\item $\forall h \in [H] \quad \theta_{h,h} \geq \frac{1}{C}$;
\item $H \leq C$ and $|\!|\boldsymbol{\Theta}|\!|_{\infty} \leq C$;
\item the distance between any pair of points in $\bigcup_{h = 1}^{H} \big\{\hat{a}_h^{\mathfrak{m}},\alpha_h,\beta_h,\hat{b}^{\mathfrak{m}}_h\big\}$ is larger than $\frac{1}{C}$ and the absolute value of all these points is smaller than $C$.
\end{enumerate}
Then, the master problem of Definition~\ref{def:master} has a unique solution
 \begin{equation}

 \forall h \in [H]\qquad \forall z \in \amsmathbb{C} \setminus \amsmathbb{A}_h^{\mathfrak{m}}  \qquad F_h(z) = \Op_h\big[\boldsymbol{E}\,;\,\boldsymbol{\kappa}\big](z).
 \end{equation}
For any $h \in [H]$, the solution operator $\Op_h$ is linear in the arguments $(\boldsymbol{E},\boldsymbol{\kappa}$), depends smoothly on the parameters $\boldsymbol{\Theta}$ and $\boldsymbol{\alpha},\boldsymbol{\beta}$ (\textit{i.e.}, for each $z$ the dependence on these parameters is infinitely differentiable, locally uniformly in $z$), depends on the segments $(\amsmathbb{A}_g^{\mathfrak{m}})_{g = 1}^{H}$ and the domains $(\amsmathbb{M}_g)_{g = 1}^{H}$ only through the domain of definition --- the precise meaning of this statement is explained below --- and is continuous in the following sense. Consider any $H$--tuple of contours $(\gamma_h)_{h=1}^H$, with each $\gamma_h\subset \amsmathbb{M}_h$ being a simple loop surrounding $\amsmathbb{A}_h^{\mathfrak{m}}$, and partitioning $\amsmathbb C$ into bounded interior of $\gamma_h$ and unbounded exterior. For any $H$-tuple of compact subsets $(\amsmathbb{K}_h)_{h=1}^H$, with each $\amsmathbb K_h$ being in the exterior of $\gamma_h$ (\textit{cf.} Figure~\ref{Fig:Kdomain})
 there exists a constant $C' > 0$ depending only on these contours, compacts, and on the constant $C$ --- in particular, independent of $\boldsymbol{E},\boldsymbol{\kappa},h$ --- such that for any $\boldsymbol{E},\boldsymbol{\kappa}$ we have
 \begin{equation}
\max_{h \in [H]} \sup_{z \in \amsmathbb{K}_h} \big|\Op_h\big[\boldsymbol{E}\,;\,\boldsymbol{\kappa}\big](z)\big| \leq C' \cdot \Big( \max_{h \in [H]} \sup_{z \in \gamma_h} |E_h(z)| + |\!|\boldsymbol{\kappa}|\!|_{\infty}\Big).
\end{equation}
Besides, if $E_h(z)$ is holomorphic in $\amsmathbb{M}_h$ for each $h \in [H]$, then
\begin{equation}

\forall h \in [H]\qquad \Upsilon_h[\boldsymbol{E}\,;\,\boldsymbol{0}] = 0.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.642709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28d96cc355e98b1501ea92279d46c707b679b7722163e9c92668fd911a169dd7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] The free cumulants have the following properties:
