{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.049328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28ea92528b8c0d3ddf782cb71915a81eb5d57d76d3eec111a0104c4969fafb25","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2606.16083, 'Eyring--Kramers asymptotics for infinite-dimensional stochastic gradient systems'] Let $x,c_x,B_{r_x}(x)$ and $\eta:=\zeta_x$ be as in \eqref{Eq:Open_Saddle}. Then, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for all $\Psi\in \mathrm{Lip}_b(B)$ with $\mathrm{supp}(\Psi)\subseteq B_{r_x}(x)$
