{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.238549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28eec02842d3f7dce88c778776e4229b050f42c0274ee798c567b690766bf749","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 43 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix initial data $\hfix_0 \in \UC$ and $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$ such that
\begin{equation}
\hfix_0(x) = \hfixp_0(x)
\end{equation} for all $x\in \R$, where with a slight abuse of notation, we extend $\hfixp$ periodically from $\mathbb{T}$ to $\R$. 
Fix some $a\in \R$. 

Then there exist constants $c,C>0$, and a coupling $\mathbf{P}$ between the periodic KPZ fixed point $\hfixp$ and the KPZ fixed point $\hfix$, started from $\hfixp_0$ and $\hfix_0$, respectively, such that 
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{A}_{\varepsilon} := \left\{ \hfixp\big(\hfixp_0;y,\varepsilon\big) = \hfix(\hfix_0;y,\varepsilon) \ \forall y \in \Big[a-\frac{1}{4},a+\frac{1}{4}\Big] \cap  \textup{ext}_{\varepsilon}(\hfix_0)\right\}
\end{equation}
satisfies for all $\varepsilon>0$
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{P}\left( \mathcal{A}_{\varepsilon} \right) \geq 1- C\exp(-c\varepsilon^{-1/2}) .
\end{equation} Moreover, we get that for all $y\in \mathbb{T}\setminus\textup{supp}(\hfix_0)$ 
\begin{equation}
   \lim_{\varepsilon \rightarrow 0} \hfix\big(\hfix_0;y,\varepsilon\big) =  \lim_{\varepsilon \rightarrow 0} \hfixp\big(\hfixp_0;y,\varepsilon\big) = -\infty ,
\end{equation} in the sense of almost sure convergence in supremum-norm of the function in $y$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.302380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28f1fd683cf25cbb920f132b842fca542d38373120efa4787fb73ca0d8a9ea2e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:boundary2 of arXiv:2601.05361, 'Noise sensitivity in last-passage percolation'] For every $p\in(0,1)$, $0<\lambda<\lambda'<1$ and $u\in{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, we have for every $x\in u+{\mathbb{Z}}_{\ge0}^2$ that
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
    \item (stationarity) $\{(T(\lambda;x,x+y),T(\lambda';x,x+y)):y\in{\mathbb{Z}}_{\ge0}^2\}\stackrel{d}{=}\{(T(\lambda;u,u+y),T(\lambda';u,u+y)):y\in{\mathbb{Z}}_{\ge0}^2\}$;
    \item (monotonicity) $\omega_x\le\omega^H_x(\lambda')\le\omega^H_x(\lambda)$ and $\omega_x\leq\omega^V_x(\lambda)\le\omega^V_x(\lambda')$;
    \item (independence) $\{\omega^V_{x+j\mathbf{e}_2}(\lambda):j>0\}$ and $\{\omega^V_{x+j\mathbf{e}_2}(\lambda'):u_2-x_2<j\le0\}$ are independent; the same holds for $\{\omega^H_{x+i\mathbf{e}_1}(\lambda):i>0\}$ and $\{\omega^V_{x+i\mathbf{e}_1}(\lambda'):u_1-x_1<i\le0\}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.315836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28f33b8d5e8b3c1c364e59c92fa63e5d69268257ee346c78fff73712782f93d3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-cell-ldp-lower of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] For each $n\in\mathbbm N$ and $A> 1$, 
\begin{equation} 
