{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.975327+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2922e66207bfcbe0f84484e7dba557d8b68f066f9441bb0ee87e71cff39145be","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] (Exercise 3.16 from \cite{RevuzYor1999}). Let $M = (M_t)_{t \ge 0}$ be a continuous local martingale vanishing at zero. If there exists a constant $c > 0$ such that $\langle M \rangle_t \le ct$ for all $t \ge 0$, then for any $a$, it follows that:
