{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.658618+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2944dbd4cc755856c4db4b9cd7184005ff4f537d132ed09ad9b9fa2539c85a34","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma: Dimension bound under proper factor condition of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] Let $X$ be an ergodic $\mathbb{Z}^{d'}$-system, $f \in L^\infty(X)$, and $\delta > 0$. Let $D \geq 0$ and let $(N_n)_{n \geq 0}$ be nilfactors of $X$, each of dimension at most $D$, satisfying:
    \begin{equation}
        \|\mathbb{E}[f \mid N_n] - \mathbb{E}[f \mid N_n']\|_2 > \delta
    \end{equation}
    for every $n \geq 0$ and every strict nilfactor $N_n' \to N_n$ (i.e.\ of dimension strictly smaller than $\dim N_n$). Then for every finite $I \subset \mathbb{N}$, the joining of $\{N_n\}_{n \in I}$ inside $X$ is a nilsystem of dimension at most $D \|f\|_2^2 \delta^{-2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.994086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2944f9acdfabd485e98854042cc5716acc2a0e6f75918a1c7895b28273904162","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-entridentshreds of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] For any box $W\Subset \mathbb{R}^d$ and any $\xi\in{\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal S }_W)$, 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
H_{{\mathcal S }_{W}}\big(\xi\,\big|\, \partial\Pi_{W}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(\xi)\otimes{\tt K}_W\big)
&=\int_{{\mathcal T }_W}\partial\Pi_{W}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(\xi)({\rm d} \mu)\, H_{{\mathcal S }_W}\Big(\xi(\mu,\cdot)\,\Big|\,\bigotimes_{i\in I}\Pi_i(\xi(\mu,\cdot))\Big)\\
&\quad +\int_{{\mathcal T }_W}\partial\Pi_{W}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(\xi)({\rm d} \mu)\, \sum_{i\in I}H_{{\mathcal C }_{l_i}}\big( \Pi_i(\xi(\mu,\cdot))\,\big|\, q_{x_i,y_i}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({l_i,W}})}}}\big),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where we wrote $\mu=\sum_{i\in I}\delta_{(x_i,l_i,y_i)}$ and $\Pi_i\colon {\mathcal C }^I\to {\mathcal C }$ for the canonical projection on the $i$-th factor and $\xi(\mu,\cdot)$ for the kernel $(\xi)_{{\mathcal T }_W\to{\mathcal S }_W}(\mu,\cdot)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.725755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29450bc7d0b20f3976da48c5b89ad8beb77a0a04f153fc40660ba2e62c4a42d6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] There exists a constant $C_0>0$ such that 
