    for any path $u\in  {\mathcal{D}}_{\mathcal{E}}([0,T],{\mathcalboondox M}_{ac})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.355331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2946418e2d60b04f06de166d88586fcafd8ea3765d0b70a1afe5067f0615d271","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: discrete time profiles intro of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $(t_n)$ be a sequence of positive integers and $(w_n)$ be a sequence of positive real numbers such that $w_n = o(t_n)$ as $n\to \infty$. Let $p{\ensuremath{\;:\;}} {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}}  \to [0,1]$ be a weakly decreasing function (but not necessarily continuous) such that $p(x) \xrightarrow[x\to -\infty]{} 1$ and  $p(x) \xrightarrow[x\to +\infty]{} 0$. There exists a sequence of discrete time Markov chains $((X_t^{(n)})_{t\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} })_{n\geq 1}$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{c\in {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}}  {\ensuremath{\;:\;}} t_n + cw_n \in {\ensuremath{\mathbb N}} } \left| \mathrm{d}^{(n)}(t_n + c w_n) - p(c) \right| \xrightarrow[n\to \infty]{} 0.
