{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.297163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29467dd081f67588194b11bee57932373c3f94196af19a75d9d4aaae5264f915","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2DHD-lem4.1 of arXiv:2604.21591, '\bf Long-time dynamics of stochastic 2D hydrodynamic-type evolution equations driven by mu'] Let Hypotheses $(2DHD-Ass2.0 of the paper)$, $(2DHD-Ass2.1 of the paper)$ and $(2DHD-Ass2.4 of the paper)$ hold. Assume that (equation LSWs4.1 of the paper) and (equation LSWs4.5 of the paper) are satisfied. Then, there exists $
	\varepsilon_0=\sqrt{\frac{\mu \lambda_1}{2L_g}}$ such that for any $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2 \in (0,\varepsilon_0]$,
	$ \tau \in \mathbb{R} $ and $ B=\{ B(t) \}_{t\in \mathbb{R}}\in \mathfrak{D} $, there exists $ T:=T(\tau,B)>0 $ such that for all $ t\ge T $, the solution $ u$ of system ((2DHD-1.1 of the paper)) satisfies
