{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.243161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_294a58f2938004c9168f4a65bb28d3177d689f5af47309291b37ec77aceff10e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tmpAc of arXiv:2607.00753, 'Threatening excursions in large population\\ quasi-stationary birth and death systems.\\ O'] If
$A$  is an open subset of $\mathds R_{+}^{d}$ satisfying Assumption ${\bf (HS)}$, there exists a constant $C_{3}(A)$ such that  for any $L$ with $\lambda_{{\scriptscriptstyle K}}^{-1}>L> \,\delta_{{\scriptscriptstyle K}}$ and
