{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.337979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29521ba0805a6ffb3c5163ccfaa9deefe650688c3440f32f89a9bbb6b1902c72","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:TAL of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] Let $\mu\in\mathcal{P}(H^{-s}(\Lambda_{L} ))$ be a Gaussian measure $\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)$ with covariance operator $\Sigma$ which is a strictly positive, self-adjoint, compact operator in $L^2(\Lambda_{L})$ that admits a smooth diagonalizing basis $\{e_k\}\subset H^s(\Lambda_{L} )$. Then, for any $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(H^{-s}(\Lambda_{L}))$, we have the inequality
