{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.908172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2955effa1019e7c4c2e66d5b7a08b29213315078e6e45b1e30ba05d8f6cf4d08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop energy-est of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] Let $B$ be a finite subset of $\mathbb{Z}^d$. 
Consider a function $\eta: \mathbb{Z}^d\to \mathbb{R}$ with 
\begin{align*}
    \supp \eta \subset B, \quad 0\leq \eta \leq 1, \quad \eta \equiv 0  \text{ on } \partial B.
\end{align*}
Suppose $u: \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{Z}^d \to \mathbb{R}$ is either non-negative $L^\omega$-subharmonic $(-L^\omega u\leq 0)$,  or $L^\omega$-harmonic $(L^\omega u = 0)$ on $B$. Then we have for $p \in [1,\infty]$, there exists a constant $C_{\mathrm{En}} $ such that for all $t\in I $, 
\begin{align}


  \frac{\mathcal{E}_\Gamma^\omega(\eta u)}{\abs{B}}\leq C_{\mathrm{En}} \norm{\mu^{(2), \omega}}_{p, B} \, \norm{\nabla \eta}^2_{\ell_\infty(E)}  \norm{u^2}_{p_*,B}, 
\end{align}
with $p_*= p/(p-1)$ being the H\"{o}lder conjugate of $p$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.656007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2959cfef8c42cddca4838d84e79ca1d3530905c2e862f483cda80bf795f49825","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2605.07411, '\bf {A note on the equivalence of super-Poincar\'e inequality}'] The following statements hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item [(1)] Suppose that SPI \eqref{e1-1} holds with associated rate function $\beta_{{\rm SP}}(\cdot)$ and
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n \to \infty}n\xi_1(\delta^{-n+1})=0,
\end{equation}
where $\xi_1(\cdot)$ is defined by \eqref{t1-2-1}.
Then the SLSI \eqref{e1-2} holds
with rate function $\beta_{{\rm SL}}(s)$ defined by
\begin{equation}
\beta_{{\rm SL}}(s):=
\begin{cases}
(\log \delta)(1+N_0(s)),\ &\ s\in (0,s_0],\\
\beta_{{\rm SL}}(s_0),\ &\ s\in (s_0,+\infty),
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
N_0(s):=\sup\left\{n\ge n_0; C_4n\xi_1\left(\delta^{-n+1}\right)> s\right\},
\end{equation}
$C_4$, $s_0$, $\delta>2$ are some positive constants.
\medskip
\item [(2)] Suppose that SLSI \eqref{e1-2} holds with associated rate function $\beta_{{\rm SL}}(\cdot)$, then
the SPI \eqref{e1-1} holds with the rate function $\beta_{{\rm SP}}(\cdot)$ as follows
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\beta_{{\rm SP}}(s):=&
C_5\inf\Bigg\{\delta^{k};k\ge n_0,\ {\rm such\ that}\
\xi_2(k \log \delta)\le C_6s\Bigg\},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where $C_5$, $C_6$, $\delta>2$, $\gamma\in (0,1)$, $n_0\ge 2$ are some positive constants,
\begin{equation}
\xi_2(t):=\inf\left\{\frac{r}{t-\beta_{{\rm SL}}(r)};r>0\ {\rm such\ that}\ t-\beta_{{\rm SL}}(r)>0\right\},
\end{equation}
and we use the convention that $\inf \emptyset=-\infty$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.075803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_295ad32fe541873b4bdffa3dc4c0dcf93712c76900bc2f8feef0e873b00b3f36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 3 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] Let $X_t$ be the solution to \eqref{0.1} in the sense of Definition \ref{Defi 0.1}. Then, we have
