{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.203752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29631fe79673d92fa51b5a55080df7835d856942bab9d5e0b01a4f6c4a1035a0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 18 ($q$-labeling of $\lambda$) of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Given a partition $\lambda$, we will assign a number to each cell $(i,j)$ in $\lambda$. For each $k \in \Z$, we will label the cells in the $k$th diagonal according to the following rules:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item If $\lambda^k = \lambda$, we fill the $k$th diagonal with ones.
    \item If $\lambda^k > \lambda$, then we fill the $k$th diagonal with the values $(1-q)^{-1}, (1-q^2)^{-1},\dots$ starting with the box touching the bottom boundary.
    \item If $\lambda^k < \lambda$, we fill the $k$th diagonal with the values $(1-q),(1-q^2),\dots$, again starting with the box touching the bottom boundary.
\end{enumerate}
Let $w_\lambda(i,j)$ denote the value assigned to box $(i,j)$ by this labeling. See Figure \ref{fig:tiling} for an illustration of this labeling.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.921830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29643e0a1072cbb4e303f456ca4d82e00e56272d439d31e423ff5216600e210d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:geod of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] The following holds on the event $\Omega_1$: For all $\xi \in \mathbb{R},(x_0,s) \in \mathbb{R}^2$ and $t>s$, if $f = f_{(x_0,s)}^\xi$, then any $(f,s)$-to-$(x,t)$ geodesic $g$ satisfying $g(s) \le x_0$ is a $\xi-$ geodesic rooted at $(x_0,s)$, restricted to $[s,t]$, and any $(f,s)$-to-$(x,t)$ geodesic $g$ satisfying $g(s) \ge x_0$ is a $\xi+$ geodesic rooted at $(x_0,s)$, restricted to $[s,t]$. In addition, if we set
    \begin{equation} 
    \tau_t^{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}} = \tau_{(x_0,s)}^{\xi,{\scaleobj{0.8}{\boxempty}}}(t),
    \end{equation}
     where the right-hand side is as defined in (equation eq:Buse_interface of the paper), then 
    the following holds: 
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), font=\normalfont]
        \item  If $x<\tau_t^-$ then $\pi$ is an $(f,s)$-to-$(x,t)$ geodesic if and only if it is a restriction to $[s,t]$, of a $\xi-$ geodesic rooted at $(x,t)$. Moreover, in this case,
        \begin{equation}
            \chi^{R}(f,s;x,t)<x_0
        \end{equation}
        \item  If $x > \tau_t^+$ then any $\pi$ is an   $(f,s)$-to-$(x,t)$ geodesic if and only if it is a restriction to $[s,t]$, of a $\xi+$ geodesic rooted at $(x,t)$. Moreover, in this case,
        \begin{equation}
            \chi^{L}(f,s;x,t)>x_0
        \end{equation}
        \item  
        If $\tau_t^-\leq x \leq \tau_t^+$, then the restriction to $[s,t]$ of any $\xi -$ or $\xi +$ geodesic started from $(x,t)$ is an $(f,s)$-to-$(x,t)$ geodesic. Moreover, in this case,
        \begin{equation}

            \chi^{L}(f,s;x,t)\leq x_0,\,\, \text{ and }\,\, \chi^{R}(f,s;x,t)\geq x_0.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.071162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2967a830d2146f083073f5c6cfe54c82ff7bcf8618cae5e27669faf2057468b8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2606.01832, 'MA(1) processes with uniform innovations conditioned to stay positive in the non-expanding'] In the green region, we have

