{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.284916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_297003ae7bceda997d5fbc2b9c7a99a6b7e4fbbc3d47e7959e5f7c9b066c4537","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop holderproper of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] We work under the assumptions of Theorem~(theo:convergence of the paper). Then, the following convergence in law in the space $\mathbb{D}([0,T], \mathbb{R})$ holds true
