{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.263225+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29822d7ce30869901e3775224d2c8110b46b726bc587bcc4f0bba3c176005e26","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma minimizer-to-valid-mde-branch of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] Suppose that for every $\sigma\ge1$ there exists $\chi^\ast(\sigma)\in[-1,0)^L$ such that
