{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.358989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29b9b77db598d02f3e6765908f52104adedddab24af269cefea988be86720a51","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Single-scale estimate) of arXiv:2604.21143, 'Quantitative homogenization for the critical long-range random conductance model'] There exists $C = C(d) < \infty$ such that for every bounded Lipschitz domain $U \subset \Rd$, every $\eps \in (0,1)$, every integer $k \ge 0$ with $\eps 3^k \le \operatorname{diam}(U)$, and every $h \colon \eps\Zd \to \R$ with $h = 0$ on $\eps\Zd \setminus U$,
