{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.759305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29d31da294bece8993db7cc8a6258d32345866e8dc739ce57231fa3e342933fc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:quasi of arXiv:2604.24389, '``True" self-avoiding walks on general trees'] A bond percolation $\mathbf{Q}$ is \textbf{quasi-independent} if there exists a  constant $M\in (0,\infty)$ such that \begin{align}

