{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.399002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a342a5bafb23ec8810b05510225edb242955b90b8eda9444867d90d8d84b152","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:main theorem of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Suppose that $\Phi$ is a locally absolutely square-integrable invariant random complex measure, and let $K$ be an invariant transport kernel. We distinguish the following two cases. 
