    \begin{equation}
        K\Phi(f) = \sum_{q=0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{q!} \Psi_q\big(f^{(q)}\big).
    \end{equation}
    Note that the Paley-Wiener theorem ensures that $f\in\cC^\infty$. Now Theorem~(t: stealthy characterization of the paper) implies that the RHS of~(equation e:stealthy taylor of the paper) is deterministic, as we assumed that $\Psi_q$ is $\infty$-uniform with radius $\varepsilon$ for every $q\in\N_0$, and that $\hat{f}$, and therefore also $\widehat{f^{(q)}}$ has support in $B_\varepsilon$ for every $q\in\N_0$. Hence, the LHS (left-hand side) must also be deterministic, which implies that $K\Phi$ is $\infty$-uniform with radius $\varepsilon-\vartheta$ by Theorem~(t: stealthy characterization of the paper), as $\hat{f}(k)\neq 0, k\in B_{\ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

