{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.916688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a38355aa47c487bc920ae1bda2b179e9deac377362238f17f4e4e3475604c3d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:equ of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] [Busa-Sepp-Sore-22a] 
    On a single event of full probability, for every $\xi\in\Xi$ and $t\in\mathbb{R}$,
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            \mathfrak S^L_{t,\xi}&=\{x\in\mathbb{R}:D^\xi_t(x-\varepsilon) < D^\xi_t(x), \,\, \forall \varepsilon>0\}\\
