{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.995736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a40c3e808e51fb37658f9158c14354d4ea3b3d7a9ac6a994951e0bc708ab8ab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 35 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let $N\geq M\geq 1$ be fixed integers and let $w=(w_1,\dots,w_N)$ be a fixed alphabet and let $y_1,\dots,y_M\in\mathbb{Z}$ be fixed so that $y=(y_1,\dots,y_M)$  is a collection of integers\footnote{Typically we consider the case where $y_1\geq \cdots\geq y_M\geq 1$ so that $y$ is a half-space configuration. However we will need the more general statement in the proof of Lemma \ref{lm: F-eigenvector property} later on.}. The function \eqref{eq:F initial coord function} satisfies the following recursion relation for all $k\in\{1,\dots,N\}$:
