{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.847439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a4241254b70c42aee1b3e8fe79b2ed8a8eeb76f80d4cd350e888c3b9aa0822e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Diffusion matrix at equilibrium) of arXiv:2609.03847, 'A counterexample to McKean's conjecture for the Landau-Coulomb equation'] There exist constants $c,C>0$ such that,
