{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.749578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a448c8e452daf03dd98398ca6ca2da941e83cbaa9ec729c9a69895c948142c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] For every fixed $k\in \N_0$ there exists a unique $C^\infty$-function $g_k:[0,\infty) \to \mathbb{C}$ such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty} \sup_{s\in [0, An]\cap \Z} \left|\eta_{k;n}(s)-g_k(s/n)\right| = 0,
\end{equation}
for every $A>0$.
Moreover,  the functions  $g_k(\gamma)$, $k\in \N_0$,  are  uniquely characterized by the triangular ODE system
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
g_k'(\gamma)
&=
\Phi_k \left(g_1(\gamma), \ldots, g_{k-1}(\gamma); \alpha\right)
=
\alpha \sum_{j=1}^{k-1} j  g_j(\gamma)
\widehat{B}_{ k-j} \left(g_1(\gamma), \ldots, g_{k-j}(\gamma); \alpha\right),
\quad k\in \N,\ \gamma\geq 0,
\\
g_{0}(\gamma) &=  1 \quad (\text{for all } \gamma\geq 0), \qquad g_{k}(0) = 1 \quad (\text{for all } k\in  \mathbb N).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.574052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a44f8b7e14fac281be2b9caa15f798b670f280ffb0d0f670a5b89ec71fe8ce7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem THm-scal-eps of arXiv:2605.15742, 'Turbulent stretching of FENE dumbbell polymer model via special stochastic scaling and sin'] (Stochastic scaling limit)
   Let  $f_0\in H.$       For any $\varepsilon>0,$ there exists a unique $f_\varepsilon$ such that
    \begin{itemize}
        \item a.s.  $f_\varepsilon \in L^2(0, T;V) \cap C([0, T];H),$
        \item   $f_\varepsilon$ satisfies:  $f_\varepsilon(0)=f_0$ and a.s. for any $\Phi \in V$ it holds
        \begin{align}
    \langle\dfrac{\partial f_\varepsilon}{\partial t},\Phi\rangle_{V^\prime,V}=-\int_{\mathbb{T}^2}\int_D\big ( \dfrac{\kappa}{\beta} f_\varepsilon F(r)r+\dfrac{1}{\beta}\nabla_rf_\varepsilon+ \dfrac{1}{2}\varphi_\varepsilon^2 A(r) \nabla_rf_\varepsilon\big)\cdot \nabla_r\left(\dfrac{\Phi}{\mathbf{M}}\right) drdx.
\end{align}
    \end{itemize}
      Moreover, the following convergence holds, as $N\to +\infty$
    \begin{align}
        f^\varepsilon_N(t) \rightharpoonup f_\varepsilon(t) \text{ in } L^2(\Omega,H) \text{ for any } t\in [0,T],
    \end{align}
  where $(f^\varepsilon_N)_{N}$ is unique quasi-regular weak solution (in the sense of (Def-sol-QR-* of the paper)) to       (equation Ito-FP_eps-V2 of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.561612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a4b94e517309ec0bddd08393940b9e98b5d297925b7ba2011a340b5e6a15328","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:trace-derivative-1 of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:trace-derivatives}
