{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.644980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a4ead079dfa1bc10190a48b9a6e6e7a4345dd7713c39b866d69d364421746e5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro cor: ES correlations of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $\Lambda\subset \mathbb Z^d$ be finite, $\beta\geq 0$ and $\mathsf h \in (\mathbb R^+)^\Lambda$. For every $x,y\in \Lambda$, 
\begin{align}

\langle \tau_x \rangle_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}
&=
\Psi^0_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}[\mathsf{a}_x \mathds{1}\{x\longleftrightarrow \mathfrak{g}\}], 
\\

\langle \textup{sgn}(\tau_x) \rangle_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}
&=
\Psi^0_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}[x\longleftrightarrow \mathfrak{g}], 
\\ 
\langle \tau_x \tau_y \rangle_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}
&=
\Psi^0_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}[\mathsf{a}_x \mathsf{a}_y \mathds{1}\{x\longleftrightarrow y\}], 
\\ 
\langle \textup{sgn}(\tau_x) \textup{sgn}(\tau_y) \rangle_{\Lambda,\beta,\mathsf{h}}
