{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.394879+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a4f8d6b98d8a396dd09188efb17f3dde7218839e5b0a0e26e765c9a09d99545","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:aux of arXiv:2507.19554, 'Full extremal process in four-dimensional membrane model'] Set $b_K:=c\log\log K$ for some $c>0$ sufficiently small. For any $m\geq 1$, let $d^{(m)}$ denote the Levy metric on probability measures on $\mbR^m$. Then, for any $m\geq 1$ and any collection
