{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.711484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a4fab5dcd0514c6524e2dbc7a80697a30a9421501c5786e63b1d1eaf45e8e82","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 (Critical learning rate of SGD) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] There exists a unique critical learning rate satisfying
\[
0<\eta_{\sgd}^{\crit}<\frac{2B}{(B+1)\lambda_{\max}}
\]
and
\begin{equation}

\sum_{i\geq1}
\frac{
\eta_{\sgd}^{\crit}\lambda_i
}{
2B-(B+1)\eta_{\sgd}^{\crit}\lambda_i
}
=1.
\end{equation}
The SGD iteration is risk stable if and only if
\[
0<\eta<\eta_{\sgd}^{\crit}.
\]
Moreover,
\begin{equation}

\frac{2B}{(B+1)\lambda_{\max}+\Tr(\bH)}
\leq
\eta_{\sgd}^{\crit}
\leq
\min\left\{
\frac{2B}{(B+1)\lambda_{\max}},
\frac{2B}{\Tr(\bH)}
\right\}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, under the fixed-exponent power-law assumptions
\(
\lambda_i\eqsim i^{-\beta},
\beta>1
\), we have
\[
\eta_{\sgd}^{\crit}\eqsim1.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.780399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a54619634992d1222f9eae752b2a813fbe42a8e8f195cd2dc9b3aa5b7c6b66c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:harmonic of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Fix an input $x$ and a parameter $\theta$.
