{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.814520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a5c37ce140411f948653132296c43e3616270e37d1bb44f2d87bd077bf63863","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:energy-level-set of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] There exists a deterministic sequence $\{n_k\}_{k\geqslant 1}\subset \mathbb{Z}_{\geqslant 1}$ with $n_k\uparrow\infty$ such that for any $\beta\geqslant 0$, it holds almost surely that
