{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.202689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a700c255d539d0421997beda0f48c084ae18151228c50c7bff563131d12ff37","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Fisher Chaos of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Fix $h\in\G_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$, and let $\mu:=\mu_{J,h}$. Suppose  $f\in\ensuremath{\mathcal S}_h$ is such that the  measure \(\nu := f \mu \in \mathcal{P}(\Omega)\) is irreducible. 
