{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.321472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a70c1a6e5ee8f882a6deea4fe12acee3af50f81f344877bcd66c61d6845ee74","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:Jack-Plancherel-measure of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] For $N\geq1$ and $s\geq0$, the Jack--Plancherel measure considered in
this paper is the Jack measure corresponding to
$(1^N,\mathrm{Pl}_s)$:
\begin{align}
  \mathbb P_{N,s}^{(\theta)}(\lambda)
  &:=e^{-\theta sN}
    \frac{J_\lambda(1^N;\theta)
          J_\lambda(\mathrm{Pl}_s;\theta)}
         {j_\lambda(\theta)}
  \notag\\
  &=e^{-\theta sN}(s\theta)^{|\lambda|}
    \prod_{\square\in\lambda}
    \frac{N\theta+a'(\square)-\theta l'(\square)}
    {\bigl(a(\square)+\theta l(\square)+\theta\bigr)
     \bigl(a(\square)+\theta l(\square)+1\bigr)}.

\end{align}
It is supported on partitions with at most $N$ rows.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.416659+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a70c334af6309184de0c4318d311c1bc56d54e77d0ee68440ac05efb5c487d9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:2d_kernel_operator_interpretation of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] {borodin-gr2009q}}]

