{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.831355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a78911437dc76cd92cfefcbab2acae71c812b3edf6a781a9073aed9cdc61934","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:norm<N of arXiv:2510.00214, 'On the local well-posedness of randomly forced reaction-diffusion equations with $\bm{L^2}'] Choose and fix real numbers $\alpha>0$, $\beta\ge1$, $\tau,\mu\in(0\,,1)$, and 
	let $\{X(t\,,x)\}_{(t,x)\in \mathscr{D}(\infty)}$ denote a space-time random field
	such that, for some $k \ge 4(\tau^{-1}+\mu^{-1})$,
	\begin{equation}
		C = \adjustlimits\sup_{\varepsilon\in(0,1)}\sup_{t>0}\sup_{0\le x<y\le1}\left(
		\frac{t^\alpha\mathrm{e}^{- \beta t}\|X(t+\varepsilon\,,x) - X(t\,,y)\|_k}{
		\varepsilon^\tau \vee |x-y|^\mu}\right)<\infty.
	\end{equation}
	Then, $\E( \|X\|_{\mathscr{C}_\infty(\bar\alpha,\bar\beta)}^k)
	\le (1280L)^k[ \mathcal{N}_{k,\alpha,\beta,\infty}(X)+C]^k$
	for all $\bar\alpha>\alpha$ and $\bar\beta > \beta$,
	where
	\begin{equation}\begin{split}	
		L = L(\alpha\,,\bar\alpha\,,\beta\,,\bar\beta) =
		\max\left( \frac{2^{\bar\alpha}}{2^{\bar\alpha-\alpha} - 1}
		~, \sum_{n=0}^\infty (n+1)^{\bar\alpha+\alpha}\
		\mathrm{e}^{-n(\bar\beta-\beta)/\beta}\right).
	\end{split}\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

