{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.590161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a7cc9489601c0d6eddf3c96634bf1b922c1d81efe6a0bf6cffdcf73c702cde5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main of arXiv:2608.30575, 'A Counterexample to Belinsky's Conjecture on Ces\`aro Means at Lebesgue Points'] There exist a strictly convex increasing sequence $(a_m)$ of positive
