\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.082183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a7f9ffcd3caab377591f9935d120b6e2870c660eb3333aa377cfd5c4f3d38d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Main of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] For any $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3\backslash\{0\}$ and $t>0$, there exist a function $G_t^\alpha(x)$ and a probability measure $\mu_{t,x}^\alpha $  on the Wiener space $\left(\Omega=C([0,\infty),{\mathbb{R}}^3), \mathcal{B}(C([0,\infty),{\mathbb{R}}^3))\right)$ such that  \begin{align*}
