for $u_0\in C_b({\mathbb{R}}^3)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.782304+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a842966fd051911b4146b1cfc2f0a4af9aec4dc8188bcd79d66a089a8cb616c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm Supremum Lemma of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For some constants $C,c(T)>0$. We have the following sub-Gaussianity estimates. For any $u,\epsilon>0$ we have
