{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:20:30.593539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a877df52c72ee03f8d62468079aaa34fef1ea95265ac24b5e56ef4f99f26b76","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2609.01851, 'Minimum Weakly Saturated Graphs and Bootstrap Percolation in General Host Graphs'] Let $H=K_{n_1,n_2,...,n_r}$ be a complete $r$-partite graph (where $r> 2$). The graph $H$ will self-percolate to $K_n$ if and only if the following conditions hold: 

\begin{enumerate}
