{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.836642+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2aabb66d96e57ae8bda570e7ab190585f98166ce55c16c10893658b33f788cff","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2511.09726, 'The non-covered set in Dvoretzky covering is a set of multiplicity'] Let $(f_n(\omega,t))_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of random functions. Suppose that there exists $\alpha \in (0,1)$ such that 
