{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.571036+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2acbab211b160331c413d1f12ed6051a345300fcc755c649877d71ce0a5546b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2605.30869, 'Approximate Transitivity of Young Translation on Rough Paths'] Fix $\frac 1 3 < \alpha < H \leq \frac 1 2$, a fractional Brownian motion $B^H$ and $\fX$ in $\mathcal{C}^{0;\alpha}_{\mathbf{1}}$. Let $B_n^H$ be piecewise linear approximations of $B^H$ and $x_n$  $C^1$ paths with $S^2(x_n) \to \fX$ in $\cC^{0;\alpha}_{\mathbf 1})$. Then there exists a random ($\alpha$-H\"older) geometric rough path $\fB^H \widehat{\boxplus}\;  \fX$ such that
