{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.830537+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ad8ddd31dbe91a0b657201845ecdc549d82b655a71d813181e3c21e52c451c4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm self-adjBS of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] For $\mu > -\frac12$ and ${\boldsymbol{\kappa}} \in {\mathbb R}^{d_2-1}$ with ${\kappa}_i > -1$, $1 \le i \le d_2-1$,
\begin{align*} 
  {\mathfrak D}_{\mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} & = \frac{1}{|{\bm y}|} \left[ \frac{1}{{\bm W}_{\mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} ({\bm x},{\bm y})}
    \sum_{i=1}^{d_1} \partial_{x_i} \left({\bm W}_{\mu+1,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} ({\bm x},{\bm y}) \partial_{x_i} \right)  
     + \sum_{1 \le i < j \le d_1} \big( D_{i,j}^{({\bm x})} \big)^2 \right]\\
   & +  \frac{1}{{\bm W}_{\mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} ({\bm x},{\bm y})} \sum_{i=1}^{d_2-1} (\partial_{y_i} - \partial_{y_{d_2}})
       y_i  {\bm W}_{\mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} ({\bm x},{\bm y}) (\partial_{y_i} - \partial_{y_{d_2}}) \notag \\
  & +  \frac{1}{|{\bm y}|^{d_1+1} {\bm W}_{\mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} ({\bm x},{\bm y})} 
         \big(|{\bm y}| \partial_{y_{d_2}} +{\langle} {\bm x}, \nabla_{{\bm x}}{\rangle} \big) |{\bm y}|^{d_1}
              {\bm W}_{\mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb B}\rtimes \Sigma} ({\bm x},{\bm y}) \big(|{\bm y}| \partial_{y_{d_2}} + {\langle} {\bm x}, \nabla_{{\bm x}}{\rangle} \big). \notag
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.582922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2adb269bd931d469c0632ed44e6e051b96cb3014f918197b2803f911104137b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 60 (Vu's concentration inequality) of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Let $t_1,\ldots,t_n$ be independent random variables in $[0,1]$. Let $Y(t_1,\ldots,t_n)$ be a multivariate polynomial of degree $d$ with coefficients in $[0,U]$ for some $U>0$ and with no variables raised to a power higher than $1$.

		For any multiset of variables $A$, let $\partial_A$ denote the partial derivative with respect to the variables in $A$. For $j\leq d$, define $\mathbb{E}_j(Y):=\max_{|A|=j}\mathbb{E}(\partial_AY)$. Let $\lambda>1$ be a parameter, and let $\mathcal{E}_0>\ldots>\mathcal{E}_d=1$ be a sequence satisfying $\mathcal{E}_j/\mathcal{E}_{j+1}\geq\lambda+4j\log n$ and $U\mathcal{E}_j\geq\mathbb{E}_j(Y)$.

		Finally, define recursively $c_1=1$, $c_j=2j^{\sfrac12}(c_{j-1}+1)$, and $c'_1=2$, $c'_j=2(c'_{j-1}+1)$. Then $$\mathbb{P}\left(|Y-\mathbb{E}(Y)|\geq Uc_d\sqrt{\lambda\mathcal{E}_0\mathcal{E}_1}\right)\leq c'_de^{-\lambda/4}.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.469383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2adbaf988e6b1cdbcc348b126441639a18814e874845f5590cdaf234eb6c8633","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 76 (Pointwise norms) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] If $\upxi$ is a type $\binom{m}{n}$ tensorfield, then we define $|\upxi|_{\gnulltori} \geq 0$ by:
