{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.235736+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2af256a20752d822805d6aa99749fb51ab6bfbd959eac4e9be1a078ba7e1b72d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: less naive Lp estimate of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
	There exist a constant $C_2$ such that for every $p\in (1,2]$ and $p\leq q\leq 2$, for every $k \, \geqslant\, 1$, $N \, \geqslant\, 1$ and $I \subset \intg{1}{k}$, for any tetrahedral function $f \in {\ensuremath{\mathcal T}} _N^k$,
	\begin{equation}
		{}
		\begin{split}
		\left\|X_N(f; \omega^{(1)}, \dots,\omega^{(k)})\right\|_p & \\
		\, \leqslant\, \Big( \frac{C_2}{p-1} \Big)^k & \Bigg( \sum\limits_{n_i, i \in I} \prod\limits_{i \in I} \| \omega_{n_i}^{(i)} \|_p^p \bigg(  \!\!\!\sumtwo{n_i, i \notin I}{1 \, \leqslant\, n_1 < \dots <n_k \, \leqslant\, N} \!\!\!  |f(n_1,\dots,n_k)|^q \prod\limits_{i \notin I} \| \omega_{n_i}^{(i)} \|_q^q \bigg)^{p/q}\Bigg)^{1/p}.
		\end{split}
	\end{equation}
	Additionally, applying Jensen's inequality (to the first sum) shows that the above is bounded by
	\begin{equation}
