{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.481311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b0445db55053bd11c57ea92e5094008f9f17e8dbde2c5245ad3ef0f814dbb45","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 117 (Finite-grade Schatten--Fock equivalence and Cauchy criterion) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Fix an integer $Q\ge0$, $1\le r<\infty$, and $1\le p<\infty$.  Let
\[
 H^{(0)}\in\Sch_r(\cC,\cE),
 \qquad H^{(q)}\in\Coeff_{q,r}
 \quad(1\le q\le Q),
\]
with all grades realized over the same isonormal process, and put
\[
 Z:=\sum_{q=0}^{Q}I_q(H^{(q)}).
\]
Set $R_{0,p,r}:=1$ and, for $Q\ge1$,
\begin{equation}

 R_{Q,p,r}:=\max\left\{1,
  \max_{1\le q\le Q}\lambda_{q,p,r}^{-1}\right\}.
\end{equation}
With the convention
$\norm{H^{(0)}}_{\Coeff_{0,r}}:=\norm{H^{(0)}}_{\Sch_r}$,
\begin{align}

 \frac1{\kappa_QR_{Q,p,r}}
 \max_{0\le q\le Q}\norm{H^{(q)}}_{\Coeff_{q,r}}
 &\le\norm Z_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \notag\\
 &\le\norm{H^{(0)}}_{\Sch_r}
 +\sum_{q=1}^{Q}\Lambda_{q,p,r}
  \norm{H^{(q)}}_{\Coeff_{q,r}}.
\end{align}
For $r\ge2$, one may use
$\lambda_{q,p,r}^{-1}\le d_{q,p}q^{q/2}/q!$ and
$\Lambda_{q,p,r}\le A_q(p+r)^{q/2}$.
Consequently, for a sequence of Gaussian polynomials of degree at most $Q$
whose members and grades are defined relative to one fixed isonormal process,
$L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)$ Cauchy convergence is equivalent to Cauchy convergence
of every canonical symmetric order-$q$ coefficient in $\Coeff_{q,r}$.  Equipping
\[
 \Sch_r\times\prod_{q=1}^{Q}\Coeff_{q,r}
\]
with the maximum coefficient norm, the finite graded evaluation is a
Banach-space isomorphism onto a closed image.","status":"unverified"}

