{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.044550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b1bbf5f81a1fa494db9fe0cd191449f94339073cc81dacaa0413dddd152ff0f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:GTD of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Let $\kappa>1$, let $(s,\beta)\in(0,\infty)\times(0,1)$ satisfy the numerical stability condition (equation eq:HBstability of the paper), and fix an integer $m\ge3$. With the notation introduced above:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(i)] There exists a $C^1$ function $f:\mathbb R^2\to\mathbb R$ that is $1$-strongly convex and has $\kappa$-Lipschitz gradient such that
\begin{equation*}
 x_{t+1}^\circ=(1+\beta)x_t^\circ-\beta x_{t-1}^\circ-s\nabla f(x_t^\circ)
 \qquad\text{for every }t
\end{equation*}
if and only if $P_m(s,\beta;\kappa)\le0$. When this condition holds, the potential function $\psi$ defined in (equation eq:GTDpsi of the paper) is one such function and is piecewise quadratic.
\item[\rm(ii)] Suppose $P_m(s,\beta;\kappa)<0$, and let $\psi$ be the potential function in (equation eq:GTDpsi of the paper). Then there is a radius $r_{\max}=r_{\max}(m,s,\beta,\kappa)>0$, given explicitly in the proof, such that $\psi$ is quadratic with Hessian $\mathrm{Id}_2$ on each ball $B(x_t^\circ,r_{\max})$, that is,
\begin{equation}
 \nabla\psi(x_t^\circ+u)=\nabla\psi(x_t^\circ)+u,
 \qquad\lvert u\rvert\le r_{\max}.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.707335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b1c0e6b17b056b7e1f95f611a80f09e536388428a3a2092e7371550be287c57","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:zerosZak of arXiv:2609.00481, 'The frameset of the second-order B-spline along $ab=1/q$'] Let $b\geq\frac{3}{2}$, $N=R(b)$, and $\varepsilon=F(b)$. For $(x,\gamma)\in[0,1)^2$, $(Z_{1/b}Q_2)(x,\gamma)=0$ only if $x\in[|\varepsilon|,1-|\varepsilon|]$, and moreover only if either
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item $\gamma=k/N$ for some $k\not\equiv0\pmod N$, in which case 
    \begin{align}
        (Z_{1/b}Q_2)(x,k/N)=0 \text{ for every } x\in[|\varepsilon|,1-|\varepsilon|]; 
    \end{align}
 or
    \item $\gamma$ satisfies
    \begin{align}
        \tfrac12\cot(\pi\gamma) + (b-N)\cot(N\pi\gamma) = 0, 
    \end{align}
    in which case $x=\tfrac12$ is the unique zero.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.561760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b1d700c468fbd45508b21d7141f6f7a366ebcb690ca0e8218a3df06e65722a2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2605.30560, 'Projected McKean--Vlasov Dynamics for Entropic Weak Optimal Transport'] For any $\pi \in \Pi(\mu,\nu)$, we formally identify the tangent space as
