{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.143629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b57a031f69a77efa92c507e665435e9397677c1ebee97d2b2b436a04ef6268b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lbthm1 of arXiv:2608.18990, 'Proving Lehner's formulas via RDT -- indefinite and asymmetric scenarios'] Let $k_1=k_2=k,l\in{\mathbb N}$ be fixed and let $m=n\in{\mathbb N}$ be large such that. Let $G_{i}\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times n}$, $G_{i}^{(1)}\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times n}$, and $G_{i}^{(2)}\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times n},i=1,\dots,l$ be independent  standard normal matrices. For deterministic symmetric $A_i\in{\mathbb R}^{k\times k}$ and fixed $R_X\in{\mathbb R}^{k\times k}$ such that $\mbox{Tr}(R_X^TR_X)=1$, let $F_{i}$ and $|F_{i}|$  be as in 
((eq:lbinteq1ab0b0 of the paper)) and ((eq:lbinteq1ab0b0a0 of the paper)). Set
\begin{eqnarray}

 L & = &  
 \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\max_{X\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times k}, X^TX =I} \sum_{i=1}^{l} \left (  \mbox{Tr}( X^T G_i^{(1)} X R_XU_i | D_i| U_i^T R_X^T) +\mbox{Tr}(  X^T G_i^{(2)} X R_XU_i | D_i | U_i^T R_X^T)\right ) 
