{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.727066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b6d3fef6ebd18f569406bbc807bd2ed2d5b1605722c9ac1faa8ef6a5840167b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition LLN_perturbed_process of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Fix $G \in C^{0,1}(\Omega_T)$. A function  {$\rho \in L^2([0,T],H^1([0,1]))$} such that $0\leq \rho \leq 1$ a.e. in $\Omega_T$ is called a weak solution of 
\begin{align} 
    \begin{cases}
    \partial_t \rho = \Delta \rho-2\nabla\{\sigma(\rho)\nabla G\}\\
    \nabla \rho_t(0) -2\sigma(\rho_t(0))\nabla G_t(0) = -\mathfrak{p}^-(\rho_t(0),G_t(0))\\
    \nabla \rho_t(1) -2\sigma(\rho_t(1))\nabla G_t(1)= \mathfrak{p}^+(\rho_t(1),G_t(1))\\
    \rho(0,x) = \gamma(x)
    \end{cases} 
\end{align} if 
\begin{align*}
    \int_0^1 \left[\rho_t H_t -\gamma H_0 -\int_0^t \rho_s\partial_s H_s\;ds \right] dx &=\int_0^t\int_0^1\{-\nabla\rho_s\nabla H_s+ 2\sigma(\rho_s)\nabla G_s\nabla H_s\}\;dx\;ds\\
    &+ \int_0^t \{\mathfrak{p}^-(\rho_s(0),G_s(0))H_s(0)+\mathfrak{p}^+(\rho_s(1),G_s(1))H_s(1)\} ds,
\end{align*}
for all $t\in [0,T]$ and all test functions $H\in C^{1,2}( {\Omega_T})$.","status":"unverified"}

