{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.116847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b70ca62569c4e053abd2ded158c979a76cade60acdb2d88a0101e603d3f1a65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: upper-bound for the sum of squares of k point function of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Recall the convention that ${\operatorname{dist}}(A,B)=1$ if $A\cap B\neq\emptyset$.
    For any subset $I,S \subset\Lambda_N$, let \begin{equation}
        F(S, I)=\prod_{x\in I}\frac{1}{\big[{\operatorname{dist}}(x,S\cup (I\setminus\{x\}))\big]^{\frac{1}{{8}}}}.
    \end{equation}
For any \(s\in(0,1)\), there exists a constant \(c_4=c_4(s)>0\) such that the following holds. Let \(t>0\), and let \(S,\Lambda\subset\Lambda_N\) satisfy
$
