{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.653800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b72fcb189af289b4dbdf61d4fcc03c25c8b6a9a77f9dfcdc7a1e6e9b1d80298","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Downward jumps are not admissible) of arXiv:2608.30859, 'Conservation Laws with Discontinuous Flux:\\ A First Application to Traffic Flow'] Let the flux functions $f,g$ satisfy the Assumption \ref{assump}. Let $(u^-,\theta^-)$ and $(u^+,\theta^+)$ denote the left and right state of a jump. Then, any downward jump ($u^->u^+$) violates the Lax admissibility condition
