{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.300581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b856ab3751b16f058327a3841bc4e03a442c435090b954719c15a2112defac0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:s3 of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $b$ be an eternal solution, and assume there exists $s \in \mathbb{R}$ such that $\pmb{\xi}^{b,s}$ contains at least two colors. Then, for all $x \in \mathbb{R}$,
  \begin{equation}

  \begin{aligned}
         &\quad \;b(x,s)-b(\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_0},s) \\
         &=
         \begin{cases}
            \sum_{j=0}^{i-1}W^{\xi_j}\left(\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_j},s;\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{j+1}},s \right)+W^{\xi_{i}}\left({\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{i}},s;x,s}\right) & x\in[\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_i},\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{i+1}}), i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}\\
             -\sum_{j=i+1}^{-1}W^{\xi_j}\left(\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{j}},s;\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{j+1}},s\right)+W^{\xi_i}(\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{i+1}},s;x,s) & x\in(\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_i},\mathfrak{a}_{\xi_{i+1}}], i \in \mathbb{Z}_{< 0},
         \end{cases}
         \end{aligned}
     \end{equation}
     where we have used the shorthand notation $\xi_i = \xi_i^s$ and $\mathfrak{a}_\xi = \mathfrak{a}_\xi^s$ for our particular choice of $s$. Here, in the $i = 0$ and $i = -1$ cases, we interpret the empty sum $\sum_{j = 0}^{-1}$ as $0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.831552+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b874720ecc5f9c3c951d17300f2107ac286dbb2be56ef7ee1fa9ce260d1628b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:extFLE of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] For $\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{y} \in \mathbb{A}_+^n$ and functions
$\mathbf{f}, \mathbf{g}: (\ell,r) \to \mathbb{A}_+^n$ with $\mathbf{f} \prec \mathbf{g}$ and $\bm{\lambda} : (\ell,r) \to \mathbb{R}^n$,
let  $\mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\bm{\lambda}}_{n,\ell,r,\mathbf{f},\mathbf{g}}$ denote the probability measure
with the following Radon--Nikodym derivative relative to the
Brownian bridge measure $\mathcal{B}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}}_{n,\ell,r}$:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d\mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\bm{\lambda}}_{n,\ell,r,\mathbf{f},\mathbf{g}}}{d\mathcal{B}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}}_{n,\ell,r}}(\mathbf{X}_n)
    \propto \Exp{-2 \sum_{i=1}^n \int_\ell^r \lambda^i(t) X^i_n(t) \,dt}
    \ind{\mathbf{X}_n(t) \in \mathbb{A}_+^n \text{ for all } t \in [\ell,r]}
    \mathbf{1}_{\{\mathbf{f} \prec \mathbf{X}_n \prec \mathbf{g}\}}.
\end{equation}
Note that to recover the geometrically increasing area tilts, we should
take $\bm{\lambda}(t) \equiv (1,\lambda,\lambda^2,\dotsb,\lambda^{n-1})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.872232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b8aabfe8dc3de1ec77358860eda3eaa06a6ae912ec1ccf51f0463f0a3e2e910","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:phi_i of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] Let $\bar\gamma$ be a Borel measure on $\reals^d\times\reals^d$. The left and right marginals, zero-marginals of $\bar\gamma$ are defined as the measures $\phi_1 \bar\gamma, \phi_2 \bar\gamma$ and $\varphi_1 \bar\gamma, \varphi_2 \bar\gamma$ respectively where
    \begin{align*}
        \phi_1 \bar\gamma(A) = \bar\gamma(A \times \mathbb{R}^d)
        \quad &\text{and} \quad
        \phi_2 \bar\gamma(A) = \bar\gamma(\mathbb{R}^d \times A) 
        \quad \text{for $A \in \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d)$,}
        \\
        \varphi_1 \bar\gamma(A) = \bar\gamma(A \times \mathbb{R}^d)
        \quad &\text{and} \quad
        \varphi_2 \bar\gamma(A) = \bar\gamma(\mathbb{R}^d \times A) 
        \quad \text{for $A \in \mathcal{B}(\reals^d_{\smallsetminus 0})$.}
    \end{align*}
    For a Borel measure $\gamma$ on $(\reals^d\times\reals^d)\setminus\{0\}$ we define $\phi_i\gamma=\phi_i\tilde\gamma$ for $i=1,2$ where $\tilde\gamma$ is the extension of $\gamma$ with $\tilde\gamma\rbr{\left\{0\right\}}=0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.279088+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b8ca9da5796df078534339d8c0121dac0032ee4773170358c77cbbb674505de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Let $\xi$ be a random variable such that for $r\ge r_{0}$
	\begin{align}
		\Vert \xi\Vert_{L_r}\le \sum_{k=1}^{m}C_{k}r^{\beta_{k}}+C_{m+1},\nonumber
	\end{align}
	where $C_{1},\cdots, C_{m+1}> 0$ and $\beta_{1},\cdots, \beta_{m}>0$. Then for $t>0$,
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{P}\big\{ \vert \xi\vert>e(mt+C_{m+1}) \big\}\le e^{r_{0}}\exp\Big(-\min\big\{\big(\frac{t}{C_{1}}\big)^{1/\beta_{1}},\cdots, \big(\frac{t}{C_{m}}\big)^{1/\beta_{m}}\big\}\Big).\nonumber
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.471485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b8f86bdd55f52b14aa1147dc05148c55d50f45502bbf24fb1dc2508798a6fff","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 101 (The key identity verified by $\upmu \Ricfour_{\Lunit \Lunit}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Assume that the entries of $\wavearray = (v^1,v^2, v^2,v^3,\LogDensity,\Ent)$ solve the geometric wave equations \eqref{E:VELOCITYWAVEEQUATION}--\eqref{E:ENTROPYWAVEEQUATION}. Then the following identity holds:
	\begin{align}  
		\upmu \Ricfour_{\Lunit \Lunit} = & L \left\lbrace - \vec{G}_{\Lunit \Lunit} \diamond \muX \wavearray - \frac{1}{2} \upmu \mytr_{\gtorus} \angG \diamond \Lunit \wavearray - \frac{1}{2} \upmu \vec{G}_{\Lunit \Lunit} \diamond \Lunit \wavearray + \upmu \angG_{\Lunit}^{\#} \diamond \cdot \angrmD \wavearray \right\rbrace \notag \\
		& \ \ + \mathfrak{A},
