{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.316166+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c0245ee405432bedb05fd520853bac1fcad28e311077122d210a9481c7085a5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2506.20411, 'Maximal Counts in the Stopped Occupancy Problem'] For every $K\in{\mathbb Z}_{>0}$, as $n\to\infty$ locally uniformly in  $s\in {\mathbb R}$
\begin{equation}
