where $\xi_i\stackrel{\rm d}{=}{\rm Gumbel}(i)$ is the decreasing sequence of  atoms of\/ $\Xi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.259728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c047fa41cb1069b58890c74d33ca039d3b543dbddb85f6c4d1a7828a20f15b7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.19738, 'Phase Transitions in the Fluctuations of Functionals of Random Neural Networks \\'] Under \Cref{ass::CRI} and $\kappa'(1)<1$, for every $x\in [-1,1]$, we have
