\end{equation}
where $\beta$ is continuous  function with $\beta(x)<0$ for $x\in(-1,1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.590154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c051035a62f9cf14d89d6688d96108ed43a9d7062f12d68542c7d7bbb7e1fa2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm th:finite_time_identity_non_random_IC of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] For any $n \in \mathbb{N}$, it holds
	\begin{equation}  \begin{aligned} 
	&\mathbb{P} (x^f_n(T) > s) \\  &= \mathbb{P} ( x_n(t) > s - f(T-t) \ \forall t \in [0,T], \ x_{n-j}(T) > s - x_{1+j}^f \ \forall j \in [n-1]),
	\end{aligned} \end{equation}
	where $[n-1] = \{0, \dots, n-1\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.089548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c0aa6bd425cf4c975d72bad86854391db6a23caf13ccb00f58062fb650cabf5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Same-block probability under Ewens) of arXiv:2604.25877, 'Asymptotic height of Plancherel random trees'] Let $\Pi_m$ be an $\mathrm{Ewens}(m,\theta)$ random partition of $\{1,\dots,m\}$. Pick $s\ge 2$ distinct labels $U_1,\dots,U_s$ uniformly without replacement from $\{1,\dots,m\}$, then
\begin{equation}
\Pp\left(U_1,\dots,U_s \text{ are in the same block of }\Pi_m\right)
=
\frac{(s-1)!}{(\theta+1)^{(s-1)}}
=
\frac{\Gamma(s)\,\Gamma(\theta+1)}{\Gamma(\theta+s)}=: \beta_s(\theta),
\end{equation}
for all $m\ge s$.","status":"unverified"}

