{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.852496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c0d3e49970b70e8975ee805e0ea80844a8421180da02261e3cdaf5fe1b0a8e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:harris of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Suppose $\alpha >0$ and let  define
\begin{equation}
\varphi_n(t)=\int\exp(t\,\ell(n,z))\,dG(z).
\end{equation}
Suppose that there exists a bounded function $r:\mathbb N\cup\{0\} \to \mathbb R$ that does not change sign and  is bounded away from $0$, and satisfies

\begin{equation} 
\begin{split}
\varphi_{n+1}(r(n+1))\geq 1+ \alpha r(n), \quad \forall n\geq 0, \quad \mbox{if } r(0)>0;\\
\varphi_{n+1}(r(n+1))\leq 1+ \alpha r(n), \quad \forall n\geq 0, \quad \mbox{if } r(0)<0.
\end{split}

\end{equation}
Then,
if $\sup_n \varphi_n(r(n))<\infty$ and $\sup_n r(n)<\infty$, $\mathbb E^{\alpha,x}[T_A]<\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.657615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c0f7fa13f5461008c048838dd860e4cec6d803ac27c1140159806565881c61f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ptoinf of arXiv:2609.01885, 'The Order of the Non-universal Tree of a Hilbert Space with Respect to the Haar Basis'] Let $\mathcal F\subseteq\mathcal P([0..m-1])$ be nonempty and define $T_\mathcal{F}\in B(\ell_m^p,\ell_{b_m}^\infty)$ by 
\begin{equation*}
T_\mathcal{F}(a_0,\ldots, a_{m-1}) = \bigg(\sum_{n\in F_0} a_n, \ldots, \sum_{n\in F_{b_m}} a_n\bigg)
\end{equation*} 
Let $k = \sup_{F\in\mathcal{F}}\{|F|\}$ and $q$ be the Holder conjugate of $p$. Then $||T_\mathcal{F}|| = k^\frac{1}{q}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.987778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c0f8b52a31537ae466624d9ec0d81f9820640a9cc54b4b1c7ca27040c927339","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 57 (Local weak convergence) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $(G,v)$ be a (random) rooted graph, and consider a random graph sequence $(G_n)_{n \in \N}$ with corresponding laws $(\mu_n)_{n \in \N}$, and let $(v_n)_{n \in \N}$ be vertices drawn uniformly from the vertex sets of $(V(G_n))_{n \in \N}$. We say that the sequence $(G_n)_{n \in \N}$ converges locally to $(G,v)$ if, for all $r \geq 1$ and every finite rooted graph $(H,o)$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \limn \mu_n \Big( \big(B_{G_n}(v_n,r), v_n \big) \simeq (H,o) \Big) = \mu \Big( \big(B_G(v,r), v \big) \simeq (H,o) \Big).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.366721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c12ad63131bcf84b6f34b3db541b1e20366cee85a3d0aee66325a96ddea64f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:SPDE:reg of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Fix a compact rectangle $I \times J \subset (0\,,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}^d$.
    Then, under (equation ns:cond:sol of the paper), we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \|u(t\,,x)-u(s\,,y)\|_2 \asymp \phi((t\,,x)\,,(s\,,y)) := \phi_1(|t-s|) \vee \phi_2(|x-y|),
    \end{align*}
    uniformly for all $(t\,,x),(s\,,y) \in I\times J$, where
    \begin{align*}
        &\phi_1(|t-s|) := |t-s|^{\theta_1} \quad \text{and}\\
        &\phi_2(|x-y|) := \begin{cases}
            |x-y|^{\theta_2}, & 0<\theta_2<1,\\
            |x-y|\sqrt{\log_+(1/|x-y|)},& \theta_2 = 1,\\
            |x-y|, & \theta_2>1.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    Moreover, $t \mapsto u(t\,,x)$ is a.s.~H\"older continuous on $I$ of order $\theta_1^-$; $x \mapsto u(t\,,x)$ is a.s.~H\"older continuous on $J$ of order $\theta_2^-$ when $0<\theta_2<1$, and a.s.~continuously differentiable when $\theta_2>1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.166279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c176938f53e982a234a1e18157d9a62f3eedb08beece49ee9177150e8ff16ef","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition U delta density of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] Let $s_0\in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$ be such that $|\mathcal B_{s_0}|<g$. Let $\delta \in \operatorname{Hom}_{\breve{Z}_p}(\Lambda_0,\Lambda_{s_0})$. Then, if $[\delta]_{s_0+1}\notin [p^{\lceil\frac{s_0}{n}\rceil}\breve{\mathbb{Z}}_p]_{s_0+1}$, the set
\begin{equation}
	U_\delta=\{\underline{a}\in U(\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p) \mid \delta(v(\underline{a}))\notin \mathcal{D}\cdot v(\underline{a})\}
\end{equation} is non-empty.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.505100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c181c6c1e16eb59ffc94761b0dc9a7b832d42f2a14a96ee404ab523087a974b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Covariance under constant channel mixing) of arXiv:2608.30589, 'Vector-Valued Wavelet Bases as Hilbert $\mathbb{M}_m(\mathbb{R})$-Module Bases: A Construc'] Let $U\in \mathbb{M}_m(\mathbb{R})$ be constant and define $(Uf)(x):=U\,f(x)$ for $f\in L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{R}^m)$.
