{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.471384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c219e2d9589dadfd11677d6b4fbdbb2542e47e74feff5afcdb2e7c2e0306927","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: lowerbound of arXiv:2606.19583, 'Power-law hypothesis and (un)fairness of PageRank on undirected multi-type PAMs'] Fix $k \in S$. Then, for any $\tilde{t}>2/\varphi_k^{\boldsymbol{m}}$, choose $\tilde{p}_{k,\tilde{t}} \in (0,1)$ as in Lemma (lem: exclusiveFraction of the paper). Next set $p \in (\tilde{p}_{k,\tilde{t}},1)$ and arbitrarily choose $t>0$ and $\varepsilon \in (0,p-\tilde{p})$. Finally, choose
$\alpha:=\bar{F}_{D_{k,\tilde{t}+t}}^{\leftarrow}(p-\tilde{p}-\varepsilon):=\min\{s \in \mathbb{N} \mid \mathbb{P}(D_{k,\tilde{t}+t} \geq s) \leq p-\tilde{p}-\varepsilon\}$ where $D_{k,\tilde{t}+t} \sim Poisson(m_k\varphi_k (\tilde{t}+t)).$  Then the assumption (equation eq: LowerBoundMainAssumtion of the paper) is fulfilled for any of the above choices of $p$ and $\alpha$.
In particular, for any $\beta>\frac{2(m_k+\alpha)}{(1-p)c(1-c)}$, 
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{P}_k^{\mathcal{T}}(R_\phi^{1,\textup{dirTr}}>r) \geq (1+o(1))\mathbb{P}_k^{\mathcal{T}}(d_\phi^->\beta r) \quad \text{as }r \rightarrow \infty.  
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.106944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c29e602790382293953ab3a38be365266f28ca477ddae1324197adae45fe611","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 52 of arXiv:2608.28200, '\textbf On the Formality of Configuration Spaces of $\aka$'] The Dolbeault cohomology of a polydisk with $k$ punctures is \\
