{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.701287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c2cf27f9d7ae9901b07932aa29b9984c55b9991d73ccbd19d5ba31c48f75a54","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop location of the components of the lemniscate: lemma of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] For every $A>0$ there exists $\kappa=\kappa(A)>0$ such that, with $r_n:=\kappa\sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}$, we have
