{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.700207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c30412cb583494cee9a60a44b90645129d196a280c7222f771eb3c7949cf518","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eqn:asymptotics_T_mapsto_g_k1(T) of arXiv:2604.09509, 'An Improved Bipartition Cover Bound for the Multispecies Coalescent Model'] The function $T \mapsto g_{k,1}(T)$ has asymptotics
\begin{equation}
     \begin{cases} 1 - g_{k,1}(T) \sim \frac{3(k-1)}{k+1} \exp(-T), & T \uparrow \infty, \\ 
 g_{k,1}(T) \sim \frac{k!}{2^{k-1}} T_k^{k-1}, &  k^2T_k = o(1).
\end{cases}

\end{equation}
\noindent Moreover, for fixed $T$, we have $g_{k,1}(T) \downarrow \mathbb{P}(S_\infty \leqslant T) =: s(T)$ where $S_\infty := \sum_{i=2}^\infty \tau_i$ for $\tau_i \sim \mathrm{Exp}\left({i \choose 2}\right)$ independent. Furthermore, the gap $\Delta_k(T) := g_{k,1}(T) - s(T)$ satisfies

\[\Delta_k(T) = \frac{2f_{S_\infty}(T)}{k} + o\left(\frac{1}{k}\right) \sim \frac{2f_{S_\infty}(T)}{k}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.560596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c31533fea13ec1838281c3ea4b34278334b21540de6be9ada14ed3142a7ad80","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defs 54 (Quasi-Gibbs measures, {\cite[Dfn.~2.2) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] {OsaTan20}}]
We say that a Borel probability~$\QP$ on~$\U$ is a \emph{$(\Phi,\Psi)$-quasi-Gibbs measure} if, for $\QP$-a.e.~$\eta\in\dUpsilon$, every~$r>0$ and every~$k\in \mathcal K_r^\eta$, there exists a constant~$c_{r,\eta,k} \in (0, \infty)$ such that
\begin{align}
c_{r,\eta,k}^{-1}\, e^{-\msH_r} \cdot \mssm_r^{\odot k} \ \leq \QP_r^{\eta, k} \ \leq \ c_{r,\eta,k}\, e^{-\msH_r} \cdot \mssm_r^{\odot k}\fstop
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.592197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c34cce339be6a9a794cb8fda8f77cd3896e489e9dc36b9f6d30cde9875f9b4f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 4 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $\phi\in\mathcal{S}([G_n])$. Then
