{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.703851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c4f1b24d0d191abab282e77d02963d868f66eb31dea689a55f0d54abc33795e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 (Law attractor and pathwise fibers) of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Assume \textnormal{(A1)-(A4)}. For every $\epsilon\in[0,\epsilon_0]$, the law semiflow $\varphi_P^\epsilon$ possesses a unique $\mathfrak D_P$-global attractor
	\begin{align}
