{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:26:47.149573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c62098c97e0f2c8e6f0f31bc9096f092fd0ce81a491f0c94328ed0a881a27df","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.29361, 'Convergence of the subcritical $\gamma$-LQG metric to the critical $2$-LQG metric as $\gam'] Fix a bounded open set $U \subseteq \CC$ and $\alpha , A \in (0,\infty)$. Suppose that we have chosen the functions $b,M$ such that $b(\xi) \sqrt{M(\xi)} > 2A$. Then, there exist constants $c_0,c_1 \in (0,\infty)$ depending only on $U,\alpha,$ and $A$ such that for all $t\geq 1$, it holds with probability at least 
