{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.634862+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c6870556c4c763e40dab5234798379f701c46d6cd471e2bcf3d0a6d3faf44ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: character estimate many fixed points with error term of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $r\geq 1$. As $n\to \infty$, uniformly over all diagrams $\lambda \vdash n$ with $n-\lambda_1 = r$, and all permutations $\sigma \in {\ensuremath{\mathfrak{S}}} _n$ with $f_1(\sigma) \geq \sqrt{n}$, we have, denoting $f = f_1(\sigma)$ and $k=n-f$,
