{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.060072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c8a88ec8997a00ad861dff0379a112eb19c4178787909e357f343b4c36fb0ae","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Branching process started at time $n$) of arXiv:2607.02019, 'Critical branching processes in random environment with immigration and an application to '] A \emph{branching process in the random environment} $(\mathcal E_k)_{k\in\mathbb Z}$ \emph{with immigration} started at time $n\in\mathbb Z$ is a process $(Z^{(n)}_{n+k})_{k\ge0}$, with  $Z^{(n)}_n\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}$ and defined recursively by
\begin{equation}
	Z^{(n)}_{n+k+1}=\sum_{i=1}^{Z^{(n)}_{n+k}} \xi_{n+k,i}+M_{n+k+1},\qquad k\ge0.
\end{equation}
A \emph{branching process in the random environment} $(\mathcal E_k)_{k\in\mathbb Z}$ is defined using \eqref{eq:BP1}  but with $M_{n+k+1}=0$ a.s. for all $k\ge 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.357833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c8d7da49961bafad7ac03d2ac59046307394d41ab4560f8961ff7235b888550","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.vn.1lip of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $n \in {\mathbb N}$ and $k \in \{0,1,\dots,n\}$, $\mathcal{V}^n(k,\cdot)$ is $1$-Lipschitz with respect to $|\cdot|_{\infty}$, i.e., for all $\bm{x},\bm{y}\in{\mathbb R}^n$
