{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.076909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cbc5631fc64d3c8ab87e3fd836fb97c859aaff84188b090c4e3e61a8326c9d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lifted of arXiv:2608.13716, 'Graph Causal Optimal Transport \\ and Wasserstein Distances'] Suppose $G$ is a transitively closed DAG and $\mu \in \Gprobabilities{\mathcal{X}}$, $\nu \in \Gprobabilities{\mathcal{Y}}$. Then
