{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.670297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ccea11ecf5b798eb7bcd6db928c08455dd319aa12b06577fe8c26778bcc5253","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_phi of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] For each $\sigma \in \{-,0,+\}$, we define the maps $\phi^{\sigma}$ by setting,
\begin{equation*}
\begin{array}{cccc}
