{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.302612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ccfbf4431dc3bc1d88f78ecf94003659ef5e2deb95f4208f8e9b16dccb44581","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2606.24056, 'Decorated stable $p$-adic self-similar processes with stationary increments'] Let \(0<\alpha\le2\) and \(H>0\). In the above setting, suppose that \(f_t\in L^\alpha(E,\mu)\) for each \(t\in\Q_p\), and
define
\begin{align}
    X(t)=\int_E f_t(x)\,M_\alpha(dx).
\end{align}
Then
\begin{equation}
  \E \left[\exp\left(i\sum_{j=1}^r\theta_jX(t_j)\right)\right]
  =
  \exp\left(-\int_E
  \bigg|\sum_{j=1}^r\theta_jf_{t_j}(x)\bigg|^\alpha\mu(dx)\right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, \(X\) is \(p\)-adic \(H\)-sssi if and only if the following two identities
hold for every \(r\ge1\), \(t_1,\ldots,t_r\in\Q_p\),
\(\theta_1,\ldots,\theta_r\in\R\), \(h\in\Q_p\), and \(a\in\Q_p^\times\):
\begin{equation}
  \int_E\bigg|\sum_{j=1}^r\theta_j(f_{t_j+h}-f_h)\bigg|^\alpha d\mu
  =
  \int_E\bigg|\sum_{j=1}^r\theta_jf_{t_j}\bigg|^\alpha d\mu
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  \int_E\bigg|\sum_{j=1}^r\theta_jf_{a t_j}\bigg|^\alpha d\mu
  =
  \abs{a}_p^{\alpha H}
  \int_E\bigg|\sum_{j=1}^r\theta_jf_{t_j}\bigg|^\alpha d\mu .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

