{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.749419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cd8fc70d62f13866d0045a0860d50bc716a2c13086ce57a76c394fa89cd03e7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] Let $m_k(s)=\frac{1}{k} [u^{k-1}] ((1+u)^k \eee^{sku})$, $k\in \N$, $s\in \R$. Then,
