{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.299449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cec64cf1c9cc8b5f32c7b0b2a25c7af1129f198b374a3b5b1d7d83e49834b36","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:dominating of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] For $\varphi \in \Phi$, we call a point $\xi\in\operatorname{supp}(\varphi)$ a (left) dominating color if there exists $\varepsilon_0>0$ such that for every $\varepsilon<\varepsilon_0$
