{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.120024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d0d117f6d8fe5bf7efb07cb8b34a5eae5c94245459a8ad54c22c0c4a4f32995","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma criterion_survival of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] [maillard2025generalisedprincipaleigenvaluesglobal]
    Suppose there exists a bounded measurable function $q:\mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R}$, $\delta \in (0,1)$, and $\rho\geq 1$ such that, for every $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$,
