{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.500417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d1186cb8fb0c9fb2955090c0fb1cca349711ae2e109c378a1aa45eb39b2f217","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop : FdTmon/LowerBound of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $D\in \RegPD$ and $\p{\gamma_k : \intervalleff{0}{T_k} \rightarrow X}_{1\le k \le K}$ be a finite family of $1$-Lipschitz, injective and pairwise disjoint paths. Then
