{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.475274+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d14e31ffa41b22460d7f3fe595ff9bf7901f5acd0aa36a7ca6f4ac6be596c32","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Main theorem) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] For every $0 < \alpha \leq 2$ and $0 < a < 1$,
\begin{equation}

0 < \Lambda(a,\alpha) \leq \min\Bigl\{\log{2},\frac{\alpha}{2}\log{(1/a)}\Bigr\}.
\end{equation}
For every fixed $a_{0}\in(0,1)$ and every $a\in[a_{0},1)$, one has the subsampling bound
\begin{equation}

\Lambda(a,\alpha) \geq
\frac{\Lambda(a_{0},\alpha)}{\bigl\lceil \log{(1/a_{0})}/\log{(1/a)} \bigr\rceil}.
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}

\frac{\Lambda(a_{0},\alpha)}{\log{(1/a_{0})}+\log{(1/a)}}\log{(1/a)}
\leq \Lambda(a,\alpha) \leq \frac{\alpha}{2}\log{(1/a)}.
\end{equation}
Therefore,
\begin{equation}

\Lambda(a,\alpha) \asymp \log{(1/a)}, \quad a \uparrow 1,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

\lim_{a \uparrow 1}G_{\alpha}(a) = G_{\alpha}^{*} \in (0,\alpha/2].
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.359091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d1777bf12c8e43ea056e5609eafc03f019e57cc5f4f124e35a73fea9c084dd4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor one-environment-transience of arXiv:2507.09421, 'Stability of randomly switching stochastic reaction networks with asymptotically linear tr'] Suppose that $M$ is a $d\times d$ matrix which is associated to a CRN in the sense of equation (equation eq:associated CRN of the paper); suppose further that the CRN is endowed with mass-action kinetics and has at-most-monomolecular reactions. Suppose that there exists a vector $v\in\mathbb R_{\ge0}^d$ such that $(vM)_m>0$ for each $m$ such that $v_m>0$, where as above $(vM)_m$ is the $m$-th entry of the vector $vM$. Then $x$ is a evanescent state for the CRN for each $x\in\mathbb Z^d_{\ge0}$ such that $\operatorname{supp}(v)\cap\operatorname{supp}(x)\ne\varnothing$.
\begin{proof}
    Fix $x\in\mathbb Z^d_{\ge0}$ such that $\operatorname{supp}(v)\cap\operatorname{supp}(x)\ne\varnothing$. We can view the CRN as a mixed process in one environment with $M_1=M$ and switching matrix $Q=(0)$. So if we consider the mixed process with matrix $\kappa Q$, then Theorem (thm:slow-switching-transience of the paper) says that $x$ is evanescent for the process if $\kappa$ is small enough and Theorem (thm:fast-switching-transience of the paper) says that $x$ is evanescent for the process if $\kappa$ is large enough. But $\kappa Q=Q$ in this case, so either theorem is enough to conclude the claimed result.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.239701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d1afba9eac58bd25af9f843af09ea7b11beb626986784507cd803aad45b4fbd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 1 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] Let Assumptions~\ref{ass:fLip},~\ref{ass:noise} and~\ref{ass:init-strong} be satisfied.

