{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.597703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d232909379339f3c282af2cc0050f41c274ca57d89fefd817562efa10739411","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lyap-sns of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] There exists a $ c_{\star} > 0 $, as used in (equation e:lyap-sns of the paper), such that
