{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.184230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d23320ae818f4718fe81796d7dac9f70985f8ab9536479bf9033cf37729b50a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2608.26974, 'Why not to use the Gaussian kernel'] Let $d \geq 1$ and $\sigma \geq 0$.
