{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.161224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d2382aefb65a170a1c4b11f08ad9500fc4f28bd2f1ce12c0cff612a42345d00","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_SlicesAreTameFrechetSubmanifolds of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] For every $(Z_0,[{\mathfrak l}_0]) \in \mathbf{Ram}$, normal data $(N,h,I)$ for $Z_0$, and $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}]) \in \mathbf{Sl}$ the tangent space $T_{{\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}]}\mathbf{Sl}$ decomposes into three tame Fréchet space subspaces
  \begin{align*}
