{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.012192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d55d04c8641502cef567a0e1d9c440d68c18a50d505e4a95d70b3874b2ad5f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ske-lem of arXiv:2605.13479, '\LARGE Dean-Kawasaki Equation with Biot-Savart and Keller-Segel Interactions: Existence an'] Let $\mathcal{V}[\cdot]$ be defined by (equation ker-V of the paper), and $\rho$ be a nonnegative function satisfying $\mathcal{I}(\rho)<+\infty$, then there
exists a function $\Psi^{\rho}$, such that $\sqrt{\rho}\nabla\Psi^{\rho} \in L^2_{[0,T]}L^2_{\mathbb{T}^2}$, and $\rho$ is a weak solution of 
\begin{equation}
\partial_t\rho+\nabla\cdot(\rho \mathcal{V}[\rho])=\Delta\rho-\nabla\cdot(\rho\nabla\Psi^{\rho}),
\end{equation}
and the rate function $\mathcal{I}$ defined in (equation I0-intro of the paper) has an equivalent representation
\begin{align}
\mathcal{I}(\rho)=\frac{1}{2}\|\sqrt{\rho}\nabla\Psi^{\rho}\|_{L_{[0,T]}^2L^2_{\mathbb{T}^2}}^2.
\end{align}
If we further assume that $\rho \in L^\infty_{[0,T]}L^\infty_{\mathbb{T}^2}$,  then $\rho$ is also a renormalized kinetic solution of the skeleton equation (equation ske of the paper) with control $g=\sqrt{\rho}\nabla\Psi^{\rho}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.547545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d58d122e06232ce2bae584316fe9a228ab2b98cba4120cac665bd0ec5bd3d4f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 30 (The support of a measure and the range of a measure-valued process) of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F(\mathbb{R}^d)$. Then $\mathbb{R}^d$ has a largest open subset $U_\mu$ such that $\mu(U_\mu)=0$ -- this is the union of all open subsets $U$ such that $\mu(U)=0$. The \emph{support} of $\mu$ is defined to be $\text{supp}(\mu) \coloneqq \mathbb{R}^d \backslash U_\mu$.
    \par
    For a measure-valued c\`adl\`ag process $\mathcal{W}=(\mathcal{W}_s)_{s \geq 0}$ we define the \emph{range} to be 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathcal{R}(\mathcal{W}) = \bigcup_{\delta > 0} \overline{\bigcup_{y \geq \delta} \text{supp}(\mathcal{W}_y)}.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

