{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.635026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d5cc3557f9dad9442ad7e76b6d399b2f7b91d99e0f4e691866c35ec97afecec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2605.31088, 'On couplings for kinetic Langevin diffusions'] Assume that $\gamma^2>4\alpha>0$ and let $\mu$ be a Markovian coupling of $(Z_t,\tilde Z_t)_{t\geq 0}$ of two solutions to \eqref{eq: kinetic Langevin with quadratic potential} with initial values such that $\Delta z\neq0$. Then there exist constants $t_\mu\geq0$, $c_\mu>0$ such that for all $t\geq t_{\mu}$ we have 
