   \item[\rm (ii)] For any finite-dimensional Borel-measurable function $\sigma(x_1,\ldots,x_d)$ taking values in $[\underline{\sigma},\overline{\sigma}]$, there exists $P\in\text{core}(\widehat{\mathbb E})$ such that ((eq:thLIL2:1 of the paper)) and ((eq:thLIL2:2 of the paper)) hold for $\sigma(x_1,x_2,\ldots)=\sigma(x_1,\ldots,x_d)$.
