{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.560594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d73d498a6abd0a5b64de2b3a4b0aa851ca2baf19e541a9df6519f251ff7d64c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:repeat_time of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] For any $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists $r(\varepsilon), n_0(\varepsilon) > 0$ such that for $n \geq n_0$
