{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.403119+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2da31e31ad1d223230711fda411192a4f40ed4ba350f00e6d1b2e80fe9afe4f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Lemma 5.2 of \cite{gz25}) of arXiv:2605.15386, 'The non-central gamma sum and difference distributions: exact distribution and asymptotic '] Fix $a,A,z>0$ and $b,m\in\mathbb{R}$, and Let $g:(0,\infty)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be such that $g(x)=O(x^{-1/2})$ as $x\rightarrow\infty$.  Then the equation
