	When $b=0$ and $g(x)=O(x^{-1})$ as $x\rightarrow\infty$, the error in  (\ref{l5.22}) is of order $O(1/\ln(1/z))$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.249124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2da52c77edb4744e386f227ea6bfd828c0cacba5e96dad8fc42d648b0d6f77b8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ferrestimate of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Consider the function {\small$\mathfrak{f}_{\mathrm{err}}$} from (equation eq:msheIIfa of the paper)-(equation eq:msheIIfe of the paper). We have the identity 

\begin{align}
[\mathscr{S}^{N}\star(\mathfrak{f}_{\mathrm{err}}[\tau_{\cdot}\bphi_{\t}]\mathbf{Z}^{N}_{\t,\cdot})]_{\x}&=[\mathscr{S}^{N}\star(\mathfrak{f}_{\mathrm{err}}[\tau_{\cdot}\bphi_{\t}]\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathbf{S}^{N}_{\t,\cdot})]_{\x}.
\end{align}

Also, the operator {\small$\mathsf{f}_{\cdot}\mapsto\mathscr{S}^{N}\star(\mathfrak{f}_{\mathrm{err}}[\tau_{\cdot}\bphi_{\t}]\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathsf{f}_{\cdot})$}, which acts on functions {\small$\mathsf{f}:\Z\to\R$}, satisfies the following pointwise estimate (in which {\small$\delta_{\mathbf{S}}$} is a small parameter from Definition (definition:zsmooth of the paper) and {\small$\mathrm{C}=\mathrm{O}(1)$}):

\begin{align}
|[\mathscr{S}^{N}\star(\mathfrak{f}_{\mathrm{err}}[\tau_{\cdot}\bphi_{\t}]\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathsf{f}_{\cdot})]_{\x}|\lesssim N^{-\frac12+\mathrm{C}\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}\cdot N^{-1+\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}\sum_{|\w|\lesssim N^{1-\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}}\Big(1+\sum_{|\z|\lesssim1}|\bphi_{\t,\x+\w+\z}|^{\mathrm{C}}\Big)\cdot|\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\x+\w}|\cdot|\mathsf{f}_{\x+\w}|.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

