{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.017939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2dbd581e0b223983229727e66ee391b73d60a208649eddcbed1f2cb2d060afae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:xiphi of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d\ge 1$ and $\delta >0$.
Suppose that Assumptions~(ass:Omega of the paper) and~(ass:J of the paper) hold for $S_z$ for each $z\in [z_c-\delta,z_c)$, suppose that $m_z \to 0$ as $z \to z_c$,
