{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.056973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2dcc077377e2cfd906d281a04e7c30dbbdbc451aab6248b509dc853b25ad689d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Step3+odd of arXiv:2607.14062, 'Gilbert's disc model conditioned on the square lattice'] Let $p\in[1,\infty)$, $R<\min\{1/2,R(p)\}$. We consider the sequence $u=(u_k)_{0\leq k\leq9}$ defined by
	$$\begin{array}{llll}
	u_0 = (0,0), & u_1 = (1,0), & u_2 = (1,1), & u_3 = (2,1),\\
	u_4 = (2,2), & u_5 = (1,2), & u_6 = (1,3), & u_7 = (0,3),\\
	u_8 = (0,2), & u_9 = (-1,2), &&
	\end{array}
	$$
	see Figure~(fig:Step3+odd of the paper). 
	Then, there exists $c_2>0$ such that for any $P\in\mathcal{P}$ such that $u$ is a path of $\Gamma_{p,R}^{\texttt{NN}}(P)$, we have 
