\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.055971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2df4f5aa93814fa43d072b06f84402b695ff62501f933b4528797570bfc241af","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 (Replacement) of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] There exists $\gamma>0$ such that for every test function $f$ and every $t > 0$
