{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.845294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2df5c5d8e5ca12b8f9e7d229556d2619641385ebd23d9d37264e579ccc2af61c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: hazard rate terms of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Consider the following events:
	\begin{align*}
		&A_i^\alpha(s) \vcentcolon= \left\{a_i \leq s < d_i, r\left(\boldsymbol{\mu}_s, \boldsymbol{y}_i(s)\right) = \alpha\right\}, \\
		&B_i(s, t) \vcentcolon= \left\{a_j, d_k \notin (s, t]\ \text{for all}\ j \geq 1\ \text{and}\ 1 - M \leq k \neq i\right\},
	\end{align*}
	defined for all $i \in \mathbbm{Z}$, $\alpha \in \{0, 1\}$ and $0 \leq s < t$. The former event corresponds to task $i$ being present at time $s$ with service rate $\alpha$, and the latter event corresponds to no tasks arriving in $(s, t]$ and no tasks leaving with the possible exception of task $i$. Let $I_i^\alpha(s)$ and $J_i(s, t)$ denote the indicator functions of the above events, respectively, and define the random variable
	\begin{equation}

		H_i^\alpha(s, t) \vcentcolon= \frac{S_g\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(s), \boldsymbol{y}_i(s)\right) - S_g\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(s) + \alpha(t - s), \boldsymbol{y}_i(s) + t - s\right)}{S_g\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(s), \boldsymbol{y}_i(s)\right)}.
	\end{equation}
	Consider the $\sigma$-algebra $\mathcal{G}_i(s, t) \vcentcolon= \sigma\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(s), \boldsymbol{y}_i(s), I_i^0(s), I_i^1(s), J_i(s, t)\right)$. Then
	\begin{equation}

		P\probarg*{d_i \leq t | \mathcal{G}_i(s, t)}I_i^\alpha(s)J_i(s, t) = H_i^\alpha(s, t) I_i^\alpha(s) J_i(s, t)
	\end{equation}
	with probability one for all $\alpha \in \{0, 1\}$ and $0 \leq s < t$. Furthermore,
	\begin{equation}

		\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{H_i^\alpha(s_n, t_n)}{t_n - s_n} = \alpha h_g^x\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(t), \boldsymbol{y}_i(t)\right) + h_g^y\left(\boldsymbol{x}_i(t), \boldsymbol{y}_i(t)\right)
	\end{equation}
	surely for all $t \geq 0$ and any two sequences such that $s_n \uparrow t$ and $t_n \downarrow t$ as $n \to \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.368100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2df7ff9f9ee13632e66d346c86d3e109859721a8dcd57f3e6a10df2a6b484d1e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:LSI:uvn of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:invMeasure of the paper). Fix $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$. Define the family of functions
\begin{equation}
    U^n_v(x):= \begin{cases}
    U(x) &\quad v  \in \{-n+1,\ldots, n-1\}, \\
    \frac{1}{2}U(x) &\quad v \in \{-n, n\}.
    \end{cases}, \quad x \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d,

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    H_n\big(\mathbf{x}^{(n)}\big) := - \sum_{v = -n}^n \bigg(U^n_v(x_v) + \sum_{u \sim v} \frac{1}{2}W(x_v - x_u) \bigg), \quad \mathbf{x}^{(n)} \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n}.

\end{equation}
Let $\theta^n$ be the Gibbs measure of Definition (def:results:gibbs of the paper). We have the following alternative representation of $\theta^n$:
\begin{equation}
    \theta^{n}(d\mathbf{x}^{(n)}) = \frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}^n} e^{-H_n(\mathbf{x}^{(n)})} d\mathbf{x}^{(n)},

\end{equation}
where $Z^{n}$ was defined in (equation eq:results:gibbsPFN of the paper). Moreover $\theta^n$ is a 1-MRF, and for each $v \in \mathbb{T}_2^n$ and $x_{\partial v} \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{N_v(\mathbb{T}_2^n)}$, the conditional distributions $\theta^n_v$ take the following form:
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
    \theta_v^n\big(dx_v|x_{\partial v}\big) &= \frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}^n_v\big(x_{\partial v}\big)} \exp\bigg( - U^n_v(x_v) - \sum_{u \sim v} W(x_v - x_u) \bigg) dx_v, \\
{\mathcal{Z}^n_v\big(x_{\partial v}\big)} &:= \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d} \exp\bigg( - U^n_v(x) - \sum_{u \sim v} W(x - x_u) \bigg) dx.
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
Moreover for each $v$ and $x_{\partial v} \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{N_v(\mathbb{T}_2^n)}$, $\theta^n_v(\cdot | x_{\partial v})$ has finite moments of all orders.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2df8c1946b5a69fbfd6bef2d42b81f72e2cd684eab8d61ca139e02e50fa36833","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral_heat of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega\subset \mathbb G$ be bounded, open set satisfying the volume density condition (see Definition~(def:VDC of the paper)). Then for all $0<\alpha<1$, 
        \begin{align}
