\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.501114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e0b8b5ea06532fc83911389d036e0f43129a70c5d56e30fde8fefeeaaa3e260","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:squarefree-profile-error of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:squarefree-rank-one}
Let \(S\subset[N]\) have cardinality \(k\ge p\), put
\[
 v_S=k^{-1/2}\sum_{i\in S}e_i,\qquad
 P_{k,S}(x)=\frac{p!}{k^{p/2}}
 \sum_{\substack{A\subset S\\ |A|=p}}\prod_{i\in A}x_i.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1)}
 \abs{P_{k,S}(x)-\ip{x}{v_S}^p}
 \le\frac{\binom p2}{k}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.341602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e0db41af3a83212fd065f7d18eb05454e2faeb124dd49c16885c3ecb69296b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] The functions $f_+$ and $f_-$ are strictly convex, satisfying
\begin{equation}
 f_+(0)=f_-(0)=0,\qquad f_-(1)=0,\qquad
 f_+(1)=-\log R.
