{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.821692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ea6e879f7debe5dd52530742d6a709ccb56e057ee28b5a9146ff7054df722fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:tail_bounds of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] For any relative deviation $\varepsilon \in (0, 1)$, the following upper and lower tail bounds hold:
  \begin{equation}
    \begin{gathered}
    \mathbb{P}\big(\bar{X} \ge \rho(1+\varepsilon)\big) \le \exp\braces*{-n \frac{\rho \varepsilon^2}{3\Gamma}},\\
     \mathbb{P}\big(\bar{X} \le \rho(1-\varepsilon)\big) \le \exp\braces*{ -n \frac{\rho \varepsilon^2}{2\Gamma}}.
