{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.712495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2eb8f70419d2ec269041a9b6dda6f8928f0204d35fd20304cba08d32c7a7a18a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Maintheorem 3 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] There is a probability law \(\mu_H\) on
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal Y
  :=\mathbb R_+^2\times C_{\mathrm{loc}}(\mathbb R_+)^2

\end{equation}
equipped with its product topology, with local uniform convergence in each
path coordinate,
such that
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal L_{\widehat{\PP}_a}
  (U_a,V_a,\overline L_a,\overline R_a)
  \Longrightarrow \mu_H.

\end{equation}
Let \((U,V,\overline L,R)\) denote the coordinate random element under
\(\mu_H\).
The left horizon \(U\) is finite almost surely, whereas \(R\) is defined on
the whole half-line.  The path \(\overline L\) is constant on
\([U,\infty)\) almost surely.  Write \(L\) for the restriction of the
constant-extended path \(\overline L\) to \([0,U]\).  Moreover,
\begin{equation}
  J_\infty
  :=\int_0^Ue^{-L(s)}\,\mathrm ds
    +\int_0^\infty e^{-R(s)}\,\mathrm ds

\end{equation}
satisfies \(0<J_\infty<\infty\) almost surely and
\begin{equation}
  J_a\Longrightarrow J_\infty,
  \qquad
  \widehat{\EE}_a[J_a^{-1}]
  \longrightarrow
  D_H:=\EE_{\mu_H}[J_\infty^{-1}]\in(0,\infty).

\end{equation}
Finally, the persistence probability satisfies
\begin{equation}
  \lim_{T\to\infty}{T^{1-H}}{\PP\bigl(B_t\leq1\text{ for every }0\leq t\leq T\bigr)} = \mathsf C_H,

\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  \mathsf C_H
  =\frac{H\,\EE[M]}{\Gamma(1/H)D_H}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.602573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ec19cc915839d6dd9e39afe7e2632caa49f9aa78b0b8942f3234ecb9b01d9cb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 39 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $d=2$ and fix $x\in\X$. Assume that $\overline H_x(\zerod)=1$ and that

