{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.248843+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ee893bd2a441c5e0809b63f5b2cb9a287e4c7936e0869127997b9d20f247584","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2604.15191, 'Quantitative Stability of Many-Marginal Schr\"odinger Bridge'] Suppose a probability density function $\rho(x)$ satisfies $0<m_\rho\leq \rho(x) \leq M_\rho < \infty$ for all $x\in\mb T^d$. Then, $\rho\in\ms P_{ac}(\mb T^d)$ satisfies the Boman chain condition with constants $A, B, C > 1$ only depending on $d, m_\rho, M_\rho$. Moreover, there exists a constant $\kappa = \kappa(m_\rho, M_\rho, d) > 0$, such that
