{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.331321+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2eec86b09a9c360088e9f327d428abe61817aeaa107a8c49f39b252778c79cb7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:partitionFunction of arXiv:2601.19630, 'Mass generation for the two dimensional O(N) Linear Sigma Model in the large N limit'] Let $\Lambda \subset (-\frac{L}{2},\frac{L}{2}]^{2}$. There exist a constant $C(\lambda,m,|\Lambda| ) \geq 1$ independent of $L$ and $N$ such that 
