{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.358823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f19cbdf106c173ce234ba67da09f6cc9f018d9d5015006649f8717b437620d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2609.03098, 'Standing waves for Schr\"odinger equations with Kato class potentials and $L^\infty$-bound'] Assume that one of the conditions $(LL)_{\pm}$ holds. Then the maximal invariant set $K_\infty$ for the semiflow $\Phi$ determined by $(P)_\lambda$ is isolated in $H^{1}(\R^{N})$, and its Conley index is given by 
