{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.265402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f2304f4d3ee821efc2400c3ef68540755c0a729e894b9161dcdd02961048286","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2603.14906, 'Four Levels of Thermodynamic Convergence of Singularly Perturbed Markov Semigroups'] In the sense of (def:thermo-conv of the paper), for every $t>0$ the family $(P_t^\varepsilon,\pi^\varepsilon)$ converges thermodynamically to $(\bar P_t,\bar\pi)$ as follows:
