{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f29fe51aef644c290d7862eea9620cb77eff27d071d2ba3a3735aa64ccf15cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr:wick_renormalization of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $X_{N} := \mathcal{L}_{N} X$. Then there exist a stochastic process $\Wick{X^{\otimes 2}}$ such that for any $T>0, \kappa>0$,
    \begin{equ}

        \big(\Wick{X_N^{\otimes 2}}\big) := X_N^{\otimes 2} - \mathbb{E} X_N^{\otimes 2} \rightarrow \Wick{X^{\otimes 2}} \quad\text{in}\quad C([0,T]; \mathcal{C}^{-\kappa})\;.
    \end{equ}
    Since $X_N$ is stationary in space, we have in particular 
        $\div(X_N^{\otimes 2}) \rightarrow \div(\Wick{X^{\otimes 2}})$ in $C([0,T]; \mathcal{C}^{-1-\kappa})$.
    Moreover, for any $0<\eta<\frac{1}{2}$, $p\geq 1$ and small $\kappa'>0$, we have 
    \begin{equs}

        \mathbb{E} \sup_{s \leq t}\|X[s]\|_{\mathcal{C}^{-2\eta}}^p &\leq C(p,\eta, \kappa') \alpha_0^p t^{p(\eta-\kappa')}\;, \\

        \mathbb{E} \sup_{s \leq t}\|\div(\Wick{X^{\otimes 2}[s]})\|_{\mathcal{C}^{-1-2\eta}}^p &\leq C(p,\eta,\kappa')\alpha_0^{2p} t^{p(\eta-\kappa')}\;.
    \end{equs} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.505895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f2e2719eeb0ee369302fcd8bf95c88cb218252c6096ff6939cef922f5a51abc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c.recursive-identity of arXiv:2505.15283, 'Quantization of Probability Distributions via Divide-and-Conquer: Convergence and Error Pr'] Let $\mu \in {\mathcal{M}}_1$ then for $n \geq 1$ we have
