{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.541234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f4367a3d179e8c274e374edf64b1b8d6f82094e1129834b119d3e74fc894103","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.smallClusters of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For any cube ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \in \mathcal{T}$ which admits local partition $\mathcal{P}$ of very-well-connected cube defined in Definition~(def:well_connected of the paper), we call the non-maximal boundary-connecting clusters $\mathscr{C}_{\operatorname{bc}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}) \setminus \mathscr{C}_{*}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}})$ \emph{small clusters} and they satisfy
