{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.682704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f446fb4590d1dc6fd15e35f52acd879e0aad4df2517c5f65d65eee9ea2606c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma hit_rate_process_intensity of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Let $\mathcal{C}(t)$ be a causal policy. The stochastic intensity of its associated hit process $\Psi_\mathcal{C}(t)$ defined by (equation eq:hit_process of the paper) is
