Then $H^{\tau}=(H^{\tau}_i)_{i\ge 0}$ is a sequence of non-anticipative functions. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.844114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f4c3eaddb48c808b05ab7966ac3c3a77a25417c1f6913483c95dd6de012d4a8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:slope of arXiv:2608.23742, 'Second-order fusion asymptotics for $\Sine_\beta$ correlation functions'] Let $\delta>1/2$. Then, for every $0<p<2\delta+1$,
