{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.882321+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f4f13cbd7ad29da4f615d6c447311fe07bb9fb4bee618c7789b6bca28039f26","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] The \emph{covariance function} of $\mathcal{X}$ is the function $\mathrm{K}:M\times M\to \mathbb{R}$ given by 
  \begin{equation}
