	\phi_{G, \beta}^0[0 \connect{} B] \leq \sum_{\substack{u\in S\\ v\notin S\\ u\sim v}} \phi_{S, \beta}^0[0 \connect{} u]\beta\phi_{G, \beta}^0[v \connect{} B]. 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.224205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f59c349be844d30b1a1db58cc7b0bef1cbad92c1c3cdd931c06d566201c9729","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2607.17943, 'Coadjoint averaging and cross-scale fluxes in a fast-slow stochastic Euler-Arnold system o'] For any $z$ in the interior of \emph{$\mathcal{A}_{\text{regular}}$}, as $dm_z(\Omega)=dm_{\mathrm{KKS},z}(\Omega)$, the fast coadjoint leafwise averaged fluxes \emph{(\ref{Def:FluxZeitlin:LeafwiseAveragedFluxEnergyEnstropy:Eq})} for energy and enstrophy both vanish, i.e.
