{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.580468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f60695968b0c4fe0ea31c8842cc24f2cac8423ba973b47ad65a433fdc0808a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor xi-examples of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] The following graphs satisfy the independence on $\xi$ mentioned in (thm.ioxi of the paper):
			\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
				\item The Diestel--Leader graph ${\rm DL}(p,q)$, which in the case $p=q$, is a Cayley graph of the lamplighter group $\mathbb{Z}_{p} \wr \mathbb{Z}$.
				\item The direct product $\mathcal{T}^{(p)}\times \mathcal{T}^{(p)}$, which is a Cayley graph of the product of two free groups if $p$ is even.\footnote{Note that if $p$ is odd, $\mathcal{T}^{(p)}\times \mathcal{T}^{(p)}$ is the Cayley graph of $(\mathbb{Z}_2 * \cdots * \mathbb{Z}_2)^2$ where duplicated edges are removed.}
			\end{enumerate}
			In contrast, $\mathcal{T}^{(p)}\times \mathcal{T}^{(q)}$, when $p>q\geq 1$, does not satisfy independence on $\xi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.635992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f60721d786fde3fe1b70ca2ebe3d87ebae7449ce286bbf200793cf332ea7b44","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $G = (V,E)$ be a finite graph and $S \subset V$. If $P \in \Ec$, then
