{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.956393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f738f588c89ba5a292ebc656033288c41691432ca098a5113ba85abf9800bc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:peaks of arXiv:2508.12464, 'On the Fitness Landscape in the $\NK$ Model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1].$ For any $0<\varepsilon<\beta_c,$ there exist two absolute constants $C_1,C_2>0$ independent of $N$ such that with probability at least $1-C_1e^{-N/C_1}$, there exists a set $S_N(\varepsilon)\subset \Sigma_{N}$ with the following properties
