{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.013331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2faf687f401debf156258efe85a9d1d5592a60557d172beb602d798a8b0fddc6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:covering-stability of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] Let $X^{(n)}$ be a sequence of variational solutions to (equation eq:SPDE of the paper) with coefficients $(\mathcal{A}^{(n)}, \mathcal{B}^{(n)})$ satisfying Assumptions (ass:LR of the paper), (ass:diff2 of the paper), (ass:SC of the paper), and (ass:nondeg of the paper) uniformly in $n$. Let $Y^{(n)}$, $\gamma_t^{(n)}$, and $v_h^{(n)}$ denote the associated first variation, Malliavin covariance, and covering field, and write $\Phi_r^{(n)} := Y^{(n)}(t,r)\mathcal{B}^{(n)}(r, X^{(n)}(r))$ and $\Phi_r := Y(t,r)\mathcal{B}(r, X(r))$. Fix $q \in (2,\infty)$ from clause~\textup{(iii)} below, and set $k := q/(q-2)$. Suppose:
