{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.310389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2fc18efc50bd8253503204475375aceeea7499ee6c675be5f04157addfd5ec6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2609.01485, 'On the Ramification of Quadratic Fields where the Torsion of a Rational Elliptic Curve Gro'] Let $E/\mathbb{Q}$ be a rational elliptic curve and $\ell$ a prime such that there exists a point $P\in E(K)[\ell]\setminus E(\mathbb{Q})$, where $K = \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{d})$ and $\ell\geq 3$. Let us consider another prime integer $0<p\in \mathbb{Z}$, we have
