{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.897598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2fd0c8f393c6f0f1cf8c7af9cee956dedf07313c4be970ba4fa102422d3ce698","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition GPpointdef of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] For $i\! \in \!  \{ 1, 2\}$, let $(E_i, d_i, \rho_i, \mu_i )$ be Polish metric spaces where 
$\rho_i \! \in \! E_i$ and $\mu_i \! \in \! \mathcal{M}_{\! f} (E_i)$. We define their 
\textit{Gromov--Prokhorov pseudo-distance} by 
\begin{equation}

{\boldsymbol{\delta}}_{\mathtt{GP}} (\mu_1, \mu_2) = \inf \big\{ \delta ( \phi_1(\rho_1), \phi_2 (\rho_2)) \vee \delta_{\mathtt{Pro}}(  
\mu_1 \! \circ \! \phi_1^{-1}\! ,  \mu_2\!  \circ \! \phi_2^{-1} )  \big\} , 
\end{equation}
and if the $E_i$ are compact, their \textit{Gromov--Hausdorff and  Gromov--Hausdorf--Prokhorov distances} by
\begin{eqnarray*}
 {\boldsymbol{\delta}}_{\mathtt{GH}} (E_1 , E_2) \!\!\! \!\! &=&\!\!\! \!\! \inf \! \big\{ \delta \big( \phi_1 (\rho_1), \phi_2 (\rho_2) \big) \vee \delta_{\mathtt{Haus}} (
 \phi_1 (E_1), \phi_2(E_2) )  \big\} \quad \textrm{and} 
 \\
{\boldsymbol{\delta}}_{\mathtt{GHP}}\!  \big(\!(E_1, \mu_1), \! (E_2 , \mu_2)\!\big) 
   \!\!\!\! \!&=&   \!\!\!\!  \!   \inf \! \big\{\!  \delta \big( \phi_1 (\rho_1), \phi_2 (\rho_2) \big) \! \vee\!  \delta_{\mathtt{Haus}} (
 \phi_1 (E_1), \phi_2(E_2) ) \! \vee \!  \delta_{\mathtt{Pro}}(  
\mu_1 \! \circ \! \phi_1^{-1}\! ,  \mu_2\!   \circ \! \phi_2^{-1} )\! \}
\end{eqnarray*}
where infima are taken on all Polish metric spaces $(X, \delta)$ and all isometrical embeddings $\phi_i \! : \! 
E_i \! \rightarrow \! X$, $i\! \in \!  \{ 1,2\}$; 
here, $ \delta_{\mathtt{Haus}}$ stands for the Hausdorff distance on the space of compact subsets of $X$ and $ \delta_{\mathtt{Pro}}$ stands for the Prokhorov distance on $\mathcal{M}_{\! f} (X)$. $\hfill \square$","status":"unverified"}

