{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.828236+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2fe1b73f93be35e17e5b45ea8820cd757758656d47f848b39780c617897b65eb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ito-defect of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $X$ be a finite-variation c\`adl\`ag{} path in $\mathbb{R}^d$, and let $\mathrm{Sig}^I$ denote its forward lift. For all letters $i,j$,
\begin{equation}
