{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.357364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2fed7e9e1c6195c06002597dc6300715d18437b3f97e7d7bb3c8ac340040b992","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(p\geq 1\). Let \(S\) be the random walk with i.i.d.\ steps of law \(\calN(0,\beta)\). Then, for any \(\lambda \geq 0\),
