{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.593182+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3004f2c38cf4b3f1291f99da03e30ca801cc25564037e9794fab365ebe60568b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-shift of point function of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Suppose that $X $ is a non-empty set and $p$ is  a point function on $X$.  Given $t \geq 0$ we define $\theta_tp$ by
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Dom}(\theta_tp)&:=\bigl\{s \in (0,\infty): s+t \in \mathrm{Dom}(p) \bigr\}=(\mathrm{Dom}(p)-t)\cap (0,\infty), \\
\theta_tp(s)&:= p(s+t), \;\; s \in \mathrm{Dom}(\theta_tp).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
In other words, if $\mathrm{Dom}(p)=\{ s_i\}$, then $\mathrm{Dom}(\theta_tp)=\{ s_i-t: s_i>t\}$ and $\theta_tp(s_i-t)=p(s_i)$.","status":"unverified"}

