{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.901980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_300b98597894784b393b514569805dbff22bb7431bfeab3d8c3bebc67fcce275","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.20908, 'On It\^o-Stratonovich formula for rough sheets'] Let $\ga_1,\ga_2>0$ and recall that the spaces $\cp_{1,1}^{\ga_1,\ga_2}$ are defined by \eqref{c3}. We consider a field $x$ in $\cp_{1,1}^{\ga_1,\ga_2}$ and a function $\varphi\in \mathcal{C}_{b}^2(\RR)$. We set $y=\vp(x)$. Then $y \in \cp_{1,1}^{\ga_1,\ga_2}$ and there exists a constant $c_{\varphi}>0$ such that 
