{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.834737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30177890ad9200f04a7f7e2769212dd72571cef7801f525f404b8bdcca532602","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:exp-log-differentials-app of arXiv:2609.00556, 'Higgs--Demailly System and Positivity of Higgs Bundles'] For a Hermitian endomorphism $u$ and an endomorphism-valued one-form $X$,
\begin{align}
 e^{-u}\mathcal D(\exp)_u(X)
 &=\int_0^1e^{-su}Xe^{su}\,ds,
 \\
 \mathcal D(\log)_G(B)
 &=\int_0^\infty(G+\rho\operatorname{Id}_E)^{-1}B(G+\rho\operatorname{Id}_E)^{-1}\,d\rho.

\end{align}
If $u=\operatorname{diag}(\ell_1,\ldots,\ell_r)$ at a point, then
