{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.631941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_301a00907820c1692fecf484f6c04952d85eee31b0f34e490bfb86b8c54fa92a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:capacity of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let $W$ be a simple random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ for $d\geq 3$ and denote by $\mathbb{P}_y$ the law of $W$ with $W(0)=y\in\mathbb{Z}^d$. For a set $A\subset\mathbb{Z}^d$, the capacity of $A$ is defined as
\begin{equation}
    \Ca(A):=\lim_{\|y\|\rightarrow\infty}\frac{\mathbb{P}_y(W[0,\infty)\cap A\neq\varnothing)}{G(0,y)}=\sum_{a\in A}\mathbb{P}_a(W[1,\infty)\cap A=\varnothing),
\end{equation}
where $G$ is the SRW Green's function on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ and $\|y\|$ denotes the Euclidean norm of $y$.","status":"unverified"}

