{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:02.098872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3043bfeb722c68ad1420794c063075c50452496faa6fb9a6f5ce8d9164049d3b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Proposition~3 in \cite{shi2020power}) of arXiv:2604.26396, '\LARGE Limiting spectral distributions of large consistent rank correlation matrices'] Let $\mZ=(Z_1,Z_2)^\tp\in\R^2$ be Lebesgue absolutely continuous, and let $\mZ_1,\mZ_2,\ldots$ be independent copies of $\mZ$. Then the following four statements are equivalent:

