{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.286015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3052b96cd48987a36dc27db15495e61a7da71583c67b79e51763f96a11de01ae","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $p\geq 1$. There exists a map
    \begin{equation*}
        S(\cdot)_T:C_o^{\textup{$p$-var}}([0,T],G^{\lfloor p\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k))\rightarrow (T(\mathbb{R}^k)):=\prod_{\ell=0}^\infty (\mathbb{R}^k)^{\otimes \ell};\quad S(\mathbf{x})_T=\left(1,S(\mathbf{x})^{(1)}_T,S(\mathbf{x})^{(2)}_T,\dots\right)
