{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.356484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3065e550ccb290fb3dd7ca8e947ddf691f94f43e286ae4782b326ece3b787902","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Generic-gn of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] (Properties of $\gamma$)\\
	For $\nu > 2, \kappa \in (0, 1/2 - 1/\nu), C \geq 0$ and $R,J: (0,\infty) \to [0,\infty)$ let
	\begin{equation}
		\gamma(m, \delta) = C m \left(R(\delta) + J(\delta) m^{-\kappa} \right)^2, ~ m \in \mathbb N, \delta > 0.
	\end{equation}

	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] For any $\delta > 0$, the pair $(\nu/2, \gamma(.,\delta))$ fulfills condition (equation MSS-ConditionM of the paper) with index $Q = 2^{2\kappa} \in [1,2^{1-2/\nu}).$

		\item[(ii)] For any $\delta > 0$, $\gamma(., \delta)$ fulfills condition (item:Uniform_FCLT_Cond4 of the paper) of Theorem (UniformFCLT-general of the paper).		

		\item[(iii)] If $\lim_{\delta \downarrow 0} R(\delta) = 0$, then $\gamma$ fulfills condition (item:Uniform_FCLT_Cond3 of the paper) of Theorem (UniformFCLT-general of the paper). 
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.816328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3068b65acd18d2393fbac90daafecabeca78dfa2e1b27e56821405281c915d13","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2607.17048, 'Concentration Inequalities for Incomplete U-statistics over Arbitrary Sampling Graphs'] Suppose for every $e\in E$, there exists $\sigma_e>0$ such that 
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb{E}\Bigl[e^{\lambda \{h_e(X_i, X_j)-\mathbb{E}h_e(X_i, X_j)\}}\Bigr]\leq e^{\lambda^2\sigma_e^2/2}, \qquad\mbox{for all $\lambda>0$}. 
\end{equation} 
If there exists a proper $K$-edge-coloring of $G$, then for all $t>0$, 
