\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.737055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_306902b603be40a1e2d1bb1f6f1def94e3fcb2e3b3e0cb62a60869430f05ebf2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmain of arXiv:2605.01878, '\Large Random trade timing and power-law tails in realized prices'] Let $(X_t, t\geq 0)$ be a Markov-modulated L\'{e}vy process with the matrix Laplace exponent $A(z)$, described in Section (smain1a of the paper). Let $1_N$ denote the $N \times 1$ vector of ones, and let $w_0=(w_{01},w_{02},\ldots,w_{0N})'$ denote the initial distribution of $J$, i.e., $w_{0,j}=\mathbb{P}(J_0 = j)$ for $j = 1,\ldots,N$. Then
