{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.556740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3072c26d9500114b909a22e02c6e0b6f3ed77ef2540c7df1712d48c7cfafadc8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:cdbm-def of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] The \emph{constrained Dyson Brownian motion} (CDBM) is the solution to the stochastic differential equation
