{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.446439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_309e4cb08b6ef2768acf52911cd21f3c7dd0b922f5c277256930d1c0be70e048","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollaire EstimatesVolumeBalls of arXiv:2411.16541, 'The Hausdorff measure of the boundary of the Brownian disk'] Let $h(s)=s^2\log\log \frac 1 s$, and let $\alpha,\gamma$ be given as in Proposition (TheoBessel of the paper). There exists a constant $K>0$ such that for all $n\geq 1$, we have:
