{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.585773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30ca04c72df8ccab39d69e6c7c782e620c42a6448fa1c1371c9e9e534fa81101","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Progress-aware exploitation score) of arXiv:2608.25116, '\method: Gradient Refinement and Progress-Aware Exploitation for Query-Efficient High-Dime'] Let $\gamma_\bv=\mu_\bv/\sigma_\bv$ denote the standardized directional
mean. The progress-aware exploitation score of direction $\bv$ at $\bx$ is
\begin{align}
\mathcal{P}(\bv) &:= \mathbb{E}\bigl[-\nabla_\bv f(\bx)\mid \nabla_\bv f(\bx)<0\bigr] \notag \\
