{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.761026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30cfa1e75265e5c45869a476ef0deadcb55bae945ef1197e993cbac7d6c0a744","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2609.00448, 'Equivariant formality and representation theory'] \textnormal{(\cite[Theorem 1.3]{F2}).} Let $G$ act on a finite CW-complex $X$. Then the following are equivalent. 
\begin{enumerate}
	\item $X$ is an equivariantly formal $G$-space.
	\item The forgetful map $f: K_G^*(X; \mathbb{Q})\to K^*(X; \mathbb{Q})$ is surjective. 
	\item The forgetful map $f$ induces an isomorphism $K_G^*(X; \mathbb{Q})\otimes_{R(G; \mathbb{Q})}\mathbb{Q}\to K^*(X; \mathbb{Q})$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.752851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30d224eeed4835375026e9ce27d7d2e1638d5627a08a194bc5a48819d89dd52d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 of arXiv:2605.14206, 'The clumsy coupon collector's problem'] For any $r > 0$, the tail event $\{ T_{m, p} \geq r \}$ has the following
  upper bound:
  \begin{align*}
      \PP(T_{m, p} \geq r)
      &\leq 2 - 2 
      \binom{m\exp(1/r)}{m}^{-1}
      (1-p)^m\\
      &\phantom{{} \leq 2 - 2} \times
      \left[
      1 - \int_0^1 p \, m
      \left(1-x\right)^{m\exp(1/r)-m}
      \left(1-p\,x\right)^{m-1} dx
      \right]^{-1}.
  \end{align*}
  \begin{proof}
    Since $T_{m, p}$ is non-negative,
    we can invoke a common bound from \cite[p.~126]{kallenberg2021probability},
    namely $\PP(T_{m,p} \geq r) \leq 2\left(1 - M_{T_{m,p}}(-1/r)\right)$.
    Substitute Lemma \ref{thm:factored mgf}.
  \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

