{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.359866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30db0b75dbc9cec4cb1fde0281f170d907302feb70b72536321c1bcda1fbbae7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2506.19008, 'Sprinkled Decoupling for Hammersley's Process'] Let $\upsilon\in(0,1/2)$. There exists $k_0\in\bN$ such that, for each $k\geq k_0$, there exists $M_k\subseteq \ZZ^2$ satisfying: 
