{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.965227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30ef7cca3f13a103091cf3685afdbfccd67f569bf6d54943ba44ace1e4305a58","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma judge the singular numbers of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] Let $D\in\Alt_{2k-1}(F)$, and $\alpha_1=(c_{1,1},\ldots,c_{(2k-1),1})^t,\alpha_2=(c_{1,2},\ldots,c_{(2k-1),2})^t\in M_{(2k-1)\times 1}(F)$. Also, let 

$$D_1=\begin{pmatrix}0 & \alpha_1^t\\ -\alpha_1 & D\end{pmatrix},D_2=\begin{pmatrix}0 & \alpha_2^t\\ -\alpha_2 & D\end{pmatrix},D_{12}=\begin{pmatrix}0 & \alpha_1^t+\alpha_2^t\\ -\alpha_1-\alpha_2 & D\end{pmatrix}$$

Then $\det (D_{12})=\det D_1+\det D_2\pm2\sqrt{\det D_1\det D_2}$. Here $\pm\sqrt{\det D_1\det D_2}$ is one of two elements in $F$ such that its square equals $\det D_1\det D_2$.","status":"unverified"}

