{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414969+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30f58ef7a36950c818eea0f5be9d04c1f6e2c04da028e530ff7bfd6fb404d489","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma two Killing vector fields of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $k$ be a solution to (equation eq:EL for k of the paper) for $C^2> 0$ on $[0,L]$. By (equation eq:EL for k and tau of the paper), set $\tau =C k^{2-2p}$. Let $\gamma:[0,L]\to \R^3$ be an associated curve with tangent $T$, normal $N$ and binormal $B$. 
