{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.898889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30f9947dcaf62fba0795c441d366c564011db34e8624cfa25f16c847b1302c0d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Hunibound of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] Fix $0<q<1$ and $\theta_{0}\in\left(0,\pi\right)$. Then there exists a constant $C=C\left(q,\theta_{0}\right)>0$ such that for all $n\geq 0$ and all $\theta\in[0,\theta_{0}]$ (equivalently, $x=\cos\theta\in[\cos\theta_{0},1]$) one has
