{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.962335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31190a37b084fdd7282accd7d2c8177cc4bdcd2fd4bba670d331cbb9f1ebefa3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Structure of the continuation region) of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] There exists a lower semicontinuous boundary $b_T:[0,T)\to(1/2,1)$
