for every $\eta \in \mathcal{T}$ in cases (item:1 of the paper),(item:2 of the paper),(item:4 of the paper), or for every radial $\eta \in \mathcal{T}$ in case~(item:3 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.654611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31285005d891a13667a9bfcd8e0cd401eaec3a743961444b0d5f0fc81ffb01e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:countable-dense-regular-families of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] There exists a countable collection $\mathscr D$ of finite regular based loop families with the following property. For every finite regular based loop family $L=(\ell_1,\ldots,\ell_r)$ and every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $L'=(\ell'_1,\ldots,\ell'_r)\in\mathscr D$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $L'$ has the same marked ambient ribbon type as $L$;
\item $\max_i d_1(\ell'_i,\ell_i)<\varepsilon;$
\item the marked ambient equivalence can be realized by an ambient isotopy fixing $o$ and $\partial\Sigma$ pointwise and supported in an open set of area smaller than $\varepsilon$.
\end{enumerate}
Hence, corresponding complementary components have areas differing by less than $\varepsilon$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.236473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_312c4f473615e0a6d9307cc01769d629ede87ba5dff0eb0ad90d759ea3e286ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l4.1 of arXiv:2604.22510, 'Asymptotics of Multi-Scale McKean--Vlasov Diffusions with Super-Linear Kernels: a Lifted S'] Fix $t\in[0,T]$.	The following limit holds in distribution:
