{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.791955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3140568cea82d7f33b7750114924b2f35f07a64eb7d511f34c21f7d9b6e39e2c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:linearization of arXiv:2606.10973, 'Quasisymmetric rigidity of the Brownian sphere'] There exists $\delta = \delta(A, a) > 0$ such that the following is true: Let $f^{-1} \colon B_\rr(\zz) \to \BC$ be an embedding. Suppose that there exists $J \in \mathop{\mathrm{GL}}(2, \BR)$ with $\lVert J - A\rVert \le \delta$ and $\lVert\yy - \zz\rVert \le \delta\rr$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \lVert f^{-1}(y) - J^{-1}(y - \yy) - f^{-1}(\yy)\rVert \le \delta\lVert y - \yy\rVert, \quad \forall y \in B_\rr(\zz). 
    \end{equation}
    Then 
    \begin{equation*}
        A^{-1}(y_{\zz,\rr}^{j,\bullet} - \zz) + f^{-1}(\yy) \in f^{-1}(B_{\zz,\rr}^{j,\bullet}), \quad \forall j \in [1, a^{-1}]_\BZ, \ \forall \bullet \in \{0, 1, 2\}. 
    \end{equation*}
    (Here, we note that $y_{\zz,\rr}^{j,\bullet} - \zz = y_{0,\rr}^{j,\bullet}$ does not depend on $\zz$.)","status":"unverified"}

