{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.593787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31592ccf8b195adf2d9ec8d96c83a09413ded5eb3beb3eac2a66f3a76d5939d3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] Suppose $Y_i$ are independent and identically distributed random variables with $P(Y_i = 1) = \frac{1}{2}$ and $P(Y_i = -1) = \frac{1}{2}$. For each $t$, let
    \begin{equation*}
        X_t = \sum_{i=1}^{t}Y_i, \quad X_0 = 0.
    \end{equation*}
    $X_0$, $X_1$, $X_2$, $X_3$, ... is called \textit{simple random walk}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.586713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_315c06829939552ca143176158644a83ff3b2a3568d617c8ef78fd0e05c5bcfd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:soliton-symmetries of arXiv:2609.00840, 'Kählerity of complete almost-Kähler gradient shrinking Ricci solitons'] Let $(M^{2m},g,J,\omega,f)$, $m\geq2$, be a complete almost-K\"ahler gradient shrinking Ricci soliton. Then, for $V=\nabla f$ and $W=JV$, we have
	\begin{equation}
		\beta=2\lambda\omega-2\rho,
		\qquad
		\mathrm d\rho=0,
	\end{equation}
	where $\beta=\mathcal L_V\omega$ and $\rho$ is the Ricci form. Moreover,
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathcal L_VJ=0,
		\qquad
