{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.936965+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3182aaea67c521761840f335932b21658df8a095ca8c0dd0c11b9ff28ca042f4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm|dLanes of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] The number $D(m_1,m_2;\beta_1,\beta_2)$ is $0$ if $\beta_1-\beta_2\geq m_2$ or $\beta_2-\beta_1\geq m_1$. 
