{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.637113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31b497ddc6a26697608a4d3224c96ae771fc6bafc7836269d3739afaa434991d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Theorem:fg-existence of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] [leonard2013survey]
Assume that $\mathbf{R},\rho_0,\rho_T$ are such that the static SBP (equation Definition:StaticSBP of the paper) with reference measure $R=\mathbf{R}_{0T}$ and target marginals $\rho_0,\rho_T$ admits a unique solution $\hat\pi$. If $\mathbf{R}$ is Markov and satisfies $\mathbf{R}_{0T}\ll \mathbf{R}_0\otimes \mathbf{R}_T$, then there exist non-negative measurable functions $\mathfrak{f}, \mathfrak{g} : \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}$ such that\\
1. $\hat\pi$ takes the following form:
\begin{equation}
    \hat{\pi} = \mathfrak{f}(X_0)\mathfrak{g}(X_T)\mathbf{R}_{0T};
\end{equation}\\
2. the unique solution to the dynamic SBP (equation Definition:DynamicSBP of the paper) with reference path measure $\mathbf{R}$ and target endpoint distributions $\rho_0,\rho_T$ is given by
\begin{equation}
    \hat{\mathbf{P}}=\mathfrak{f}(X_0)\mathfrak{g}(X_T)\mathbf{R};
\end{equation}\\
3. the pair $(\mathfrak{f},\mathfrak{g})$ satisfies the \textup{Schr\"odinger system}
\begin{equation}
    \begin{cases}
    \vspace{0.2cm}\displaystyle \mathfrak{f}(x)\Esub{\mathbf{R}}{\mathfrak{g}(X_T)|X_0=x} = \frac{d\rho_0}{d\mathbf{R}_0}(x)& \text{ for $\mathbf{R}_0$-a.e. $x$},\\
    \displaystyle \mathfrak{g}(y)\Esub{\mathbf{R}}{\mathfrak{f}(X_0)|X_T=y} = \frac{d\rho_T}{d\mathbf{R}_T}(y)& \text{ for $\mathbf{R}_T$-a.e. $y$}.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.247501+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31b4d1ce0651aed9b9d7163ec26af553203b509a56790f3b8b6da4ccac59ca95","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 33 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] There exist constants $\varepsilon > 0$ and $C>1$ such that the following holds for any $q,q' \in [-\varepsilon, \varepsilon]$, with $q \ge q'$, and $z \in \mathfrak{X}$. For each $\mathfrak{e}_z \in \{ \mathfrak{e}_{z;q}, \mathfrak{e}_{z;q'} \}$, we have 
