{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.781929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31cee0b8b43bcdfb00868b4e7be37a06f31369c40717289b2df2df4ffb76f6ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 35 (Multiplication between $n$th and $m$th chaos) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Assume $f\in\H^{\otimes n}$ and $g\in\H^{\otimes m}$. Then 
\begin{equation}

 \hat I_n(f)\hat I_m(g) 
 = \sum_{p=0}^{n\wedge m} \hat I_{n+m-2p}(f\star_p g)
\end{equation} 
where $\star_0 = \otimes$ and 
the contraction $\star_p$ is defined 
for $\mathbf{i} = (i_1,\dots,i_{n-p})$ 
and $\mathbf{j} = (j_1,\dots,j_{m-p})$ 
by  
\begin{equation}

 (f\star_pg)(\mathbf{i},\mathbf{j}) 
 = \sum_{\substack{\Sigma\in\frakS(p,n)\\ \bar\Sigma\in\frakS(p,m)}}
 \sum_{\sigma\in\frakS(p)}
 \sum_{\mathbf{k}\in\intset{1,N}^p} f(\Sigma(\mathbf{k},\mathbf{i}))g(\bar\Sigma(\mathbf{k},\sigma(\mathbf{j})))\;. 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.580713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31d144451fed30cc6fbcd07e6150db75eae51a19ea680944b687326c0526b35b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 2 of arXiv:2606.14917, 'The Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process on $\scr P_2$ \\with a volatility operator'] The symmetric, non-negative bilinear form
