{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.839348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31dd6a7494e21ead300ecb0b1e1343ab6f62636ccd4081d11557d8ca2d65d2a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] Let $p \geq 1$ and $1 \leq k < d$, let $\mu \in \cP_p(\R^d)$, and let $\nu$ be a probability measure supported on a countable closed set $\cY$.
