{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.357869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31e645d25a2a23d92e2fdf42f550e525b92670d1ad06620963f0b17f7325b36d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Union of diagrammatic graphs of arXiv:2506.06559, 'Bi-infinite incipient cluster in high dimensions'] Let ${\bf G}=(G,S,\ell)$ be a diagrammatic graph and $x,y\in \mathbb{Z}^d$. We will denote ${\bf G}\uplus \{x,y\}$ the diagrammatic graph $(G’,S’,\ell’)$ defined as follows
\begin{enumerate}
\item if $x,y\in \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$, then 
\begin{itemize}
 \item $V(G’)=V(G)$ 
 \item $E(G’)=E(G)\cup e_{\{x,y\}}$ where an edge $e_{\{x,y\}}$ is added between the vertices $s,s’\in S$ such that $x=\ell(s)$ and $y=\ell(s’)$ 
  \item $S=S’$ and $\ell=\ell’$.
\end{itemize}
\item if $x\in \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$ and $y\notin  \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$,
\begin{itemize}
 \item $V(G’)=V(G)\cup\{y_*\}$ 
 \item $E(G’)=E(G)\cup e_{\{x,y\}}$ where an edge $e_{\{x,y\}}$ is added between $y_*$ and the vertex $s\in S$ such that $x=\ell(s)$
  \item $S’=S \cup \{y_*\}$, $\ell(s)=\ell’(s)$ if $s\in S$ and $\ell’(y_*)=y$.
\end{itemize}
\item if $x,y\notin \{\ell(s), s\in S\}$
\begin{itemize}
 \item $V(G’)=V(G)\cup\{x_*,y_*\}$ 
 \item $E(G’)=E(G)\cup e_{\{x,y\}}$ where an edge $e_{\{x,y\}}$ is added between $x_*$ and $y_*$.
  \item $S’=S \cup \{x_*,y_*\}$, $\ell(s)=\ell’(s)$ if $s\in S$, $\ell’(x_*)=x$ and $\ell’(y_*)=y$.
\end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

We will extend this notation to ${\bf G}\uplus {\bf G}'$ when ${\bf G}$ is a diagrammatic graph and ${\bf G}'$ a fully labeled graph simply, by successively adding to ${\bf G}$ the finite number of labeled edges composing ${\bf G}'$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.186340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31e8ad26f7685bdfb0e0dfe37a13ef2e5736f12d3d567a4b3f05cd9de504a711","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:first-failure-short of arXiv:2608.05123, 'A central limit theorem for the random assignment problem'] Conditional on \(U\) under either reference law,
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb P(D_i\ge d\mid U)=
 \frac{S_{i,U}(d)-S_{i,U}(n-)}
      {S_{i,U}(0)-S_{i,U}(n-)},\qquad 0\le d<n.
\end{equation}
Equivalently, if independently for \(j\ne i\),
\[
 \Xi_{ij}\sim{\rm Unif}[-U_j,n-U_j],\qquad
 M_i=\min_{j\ne i}\Xi_{ij},
\]
then
\begin{equation}
 A_i\stackrel d=M_i\mid\{-U_i\le M_i<n-U_i\}.
\end{equation}

If \(J_i\) is the almost surely unique index attaining this minimum,
then, for almost every \(d\) with positive row density,
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb P(J_i=j\mid U,D_i=d)
 =\frac{\omega_n(d+U_j-U_i)}
 {\sum_{k\ne i}\omega_n(d+U_k-U_i)}.
\end{equation}
The row variables are independent conditional on \(U\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.547905+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31e8e8c4f5ea0f2b9e53319986b777dab2db8536aa29601b56c0eb71756ba881","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 (The dimension of the support and the range of SBM) of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be a non-zero finite measure, let $\gamma > 0$ and let $(\mathcal{X}_s, s \geq 0)$ be an $\text{SBM}(\gamma)$ started from $\mu$. Then we have that for $y>0$, that
\begin{equation*}
    \text{dim}(\text{supp}(\mathcal{X}_y)) = 2 \wedge d \hspace{0.5cm} \text{ 
  on   } \{\mathcal{X}_y \neq 0\} \text{    a.s.}
\end{equation*}
Furthermore, for $\delta>0$ we have that
\begin{equation*}
    \text{dim}\Big(\overline{\bigcup_{y \geq \delta}\text{supp}(\mathcal{X}_y)}\Big) = 4 \wedge d \hspace{0.5cm} \text{ 
  on   } \{\mathcal{X}_{\delta} \neq 0\} \text{    a.s.}
\end{equation*}
Finally we have that
\begin{equation*}
    \text{dim}(\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{X})) = 4 \wedge d \hspace{0.5cm} \text{a.s.}
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.337213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31eab0c0ef675ce6bfb41cdb386c06964b7976904d23321bf078ed4dc78ecc67","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 53 ({\cite[Theorem 1.1) of arXiv:2512.05466, 'Stochastic Flows and Marked Stable Processes'] {ShiWinkel-2}}] Let $\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $\theta \ge 0$. 
	For $n\in \bN$, let  $(C^{(n)}(t),\, t\ge 0)$ be a $\mathrm{PCRP}^{(\alpha)}(\theta)$ starting from $C^{(n)}(0)= \gamma^{(n)}$.
	Suppose that  the initial interval partitions $ \frac{1}{n}  \gamma^{(n)}$ converge in distribution to 
	$\gamma\in \mathcal{I}_H$ as $n\to \infty$, under $d_H$.
	Then there exists an $\mathcal{I}_H$-valued path-continuous Hunt process $(\beta(t), t\ge 0)$ starting from $\beta(0)= \gamma$, such that 
	\begin{equation}
	\Big(\frac{1}{n}  C^{(n)}(2 n t),\, t\ge 0 \Big)
	\underset{n\to \infty}{\longrightarrow}  (\beta(t),\, t\ge 0) , \quad \text{in distribution}, 
	\end{equation}
in the space of $(\mathcal{I}_H,d_H)$-valued c\`adl\`ag functions under the Skorokhod $J_1$-topology (see e.g.\@ \cite{Billingsley}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.038571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31eec346d001180a0289858f43abb4b1668c30342d5b96665c5bd2895f4d052f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] Assume that Assumption \ref{assumption:ass1} holds. Let $T_M^{(n)}$ be the stopping time given in \eqref{eq:stopping-time}. Then we have 
