{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.644685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31f5d429b48a154a4f339976bc2275868a972c9d71e28c00ef5202c09e60596c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma EHI:l:YZlemma of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $Y$ have distribution (equation EHI:e:Ydef of the paper), and let $Z$ be a standard Gaussian in $\mathbb{R}^d$, independent of $Y$. Then there exists a constant $C$ such that for all $a \in (0, 1)$,
    \begin{equation*}
