{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.157094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_31f6da03863b202e2b7b0ff6cd5aa2f45c8f96aec8e2ca144e0bc632b8928207","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.01574, 'A linear bound for Fujita's freeness conjecture'] For every positive integer $n$, there exists $\delta_n>0$ with the following property. Let $k$ be a positive integer with $k\leq n$, and let $n=b_0\geq b_1\geq\cdots\geq b_k=0$ be real numbers. For every $0\leq i<k$, let $d_i>0$, set $a_i:=(d_i-b_i)/2\geq0$, and let $0\leq c_i\leq n-d_i$. Then
