{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.225329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32085f6e3c9cf05514932bd82285d3bdad49736da3f028e0e3447445d11928b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop macroscopic coupling of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] {prevost2023phase}, [CT16]}]

    Let $\delta \in (0,1)$. For every $u>0$, $\rho \in (0,1)$ and $N \in \mathbb{N}$, there exists a coupling $\widetilde{\mathsf{P}}$ between the random walk under $\mathsf{P}$ and the random interlacements $\mathcal{I}^{u(1\pm\rho)}$ such that
