    \mathcal{G}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}) \triangleq \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})/\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E}),
\end{equation*}
with $\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{Y}, \mathcal{E})$ introduced in Definition~(definition:anti-shift-functions of the paper)
    and ${\mathfrak{s}}$-normalization follows from  Definition~(definition:s-normalization of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.218547+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3260d71d74a9a2ae321863f0e26d642991ef5050c9fa3d5762aa2e402cc1454b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.13732, '\textbf{On the First Hitting Time Problems \\ for Diffusion Processes: \\ Local Time-Space'] The cumulative distribution function $G(t,x)$ of the first-hitting time of the lower boundary $b(t)$ is given by
