{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.346410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32695a06f8d710b7497c3f0dfe2c73edb46753ac35cb443dc8d6e3dce3af6a15","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition sec5-prop.2 of arXiv:2602.04303, '\Large\textbf{Strong solutions to SDEs with singular drifts driven by fractional Brownian '] Assume (equation cond1 of the paper) and (equation cond2 of the paper). Let $p_1\geq1$ an integer and $X_{s,t}^{x}$ be the unique strong solution to the SDE (equation sec1-eq.2 of the paper). Then, there exists a constant  $C=C(H,d,p,q,T,p_1,$ $\Vert b\Vert_{L^p_xL^q_t})$ such that
