{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.421075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_326d5f6bd33c6e2bfeed0aa0439bf5a81155bde5a3e3bd75b541c666c62eb502","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2607.28215, 'Almost stochastic dominance via optimal transport'] For all $\gamma \in [0,1]$ and all $X,Y\in \mathcal{L}_{c,g}(E)$ we have
