{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.201731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32a13771de3c5cc2645606ab7084d911cda716765aad2c40cbeebd6a861c7295","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nmlsi of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] For all $h\in\G_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$, let $\ensuremath{\mathcal S}_h$ be the set of $f:\O\to {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+$ such that $\mu_{J,h}[f] = 1$ and such that $f\mu_{J,h}\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}(\O)$ has the same magnetization vector of $\mu_{J,h}$, that is \[m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\mu_{J,h})=m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(f\mu_{J,h}).\]  The system is said to satisfy the {\em Nonlinear MLSI} with rate function \(\ensuremath{\mathcal I}:\G_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}\to {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+\) if for all $h\in\G_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$, 
