{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.730071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32af912580e169ef3abf797a04278a2dac66be5de1889b6ea281c06a04fe9741","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor equilibriumFreeEnergyCorrection of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Fix $\beta>0$, and let $\mu_\beta$ be an absolutely continuous thermal equilibrium measure satisfying
\begin{align}
 \mathop{}\!\mathrm d\mu_\beta=Z_{\mu_\beta}^{-1}e^{-\beta(V+h_{\mu_\beta})}\,\mathop{}\!\mathrm d x
\end{align}
and the hypotheses of (thm:partitionFunctionBound of the paper)(ii).  Then the canonical partition function satisfies the exact identity
\begin{align}
 Z_{N,\beta}
 =e^{-\beta N\mathcal F_{\beta,V}(\mu_\beta)}
 {\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu_\beta),
\end{align}
and consequently
\begin{align}
\log Z_{N,\beta}
={}&-\beta N\mathcal F_{\beta,V}(\mu_\beta)
+\beta I_{\mu_\beta}
-\frac12\log\mathrm{det}_2(\mathrm{Id}+\beta T_{\mu_\beta})
+O_{\beta,\mu_\beta}(r_{N,\mathsf{s}}),
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}
 r_{N,\mathsf{s}}
 \coloneqq
 \begin{cases}
 (\log(e+N))^{-\frac{\mathsf{d}-2\mathsf{s}}{2\mathsf{s}}},&0<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2,\\[0.3em]
 (e+N)^{-c_{\log}(\beta,\mu_\beta)},&\mathsf{s}=0.
 \end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.283227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32b12ed9baa6756129e7ff9566eff15b35f19aef9714faa96d20b0a224a9a6eb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 19 of arXiv:2606.21778, 'Pontryagin Maximum Principle in Free Probability Theory'] Let $t\in[0,T]$ and $Z\in \mathbb{B}_2^a$. Consider the Hamiltonian $H$ given in \eqref{eq:genHamilton_inA} and the derivative $H_x$ in  \eqref{eq:genHamilton_deriv_inA}. For each $U\in\mathcal{U}$, the backward SDE (BSDE)
