{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.041442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32b210495486d4b7ae25b266b07881d07ddfcb5bd35aead39f945fb9b9500e9d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Bernstein-bound of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $\mathcal{H}_m$ be a Euclidean class with exponent $V$ consisting of measurable permutation-symmetric functions. There exist absolute constants $c,C>0$ with the following properties. If $\max(V,t)\frac{m^2}{N}\leq c$, then for all $0<\varepsilon\leq 1$

    \begin{multline*}
    \sup_{h\in \mathcal H_m} \left| U_{N,m}(h) - \mathbb E U_{N,m}(h) \right| 
    \leq (1+\varepsilon)\mathbb E\sup_{h\in \mathcal H_m}\left|\frac{m}{N} \sum_{i=1}^N h^{(1)}\left(X_i\right)\right| 
