{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.752320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32e4d88662b66ada1a6a127a383a8e846c990135697fc9b4422c1d5b1e3214d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2607.08696, 'Spectrum of Directed Inhomogeneous Random Graphs'] There exists a constant $K_2>0$ such that, if  $1\ll m \ll \scaling^{1/4}$, 
