{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.049931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32e8838de2d37757946e7ea3f7e50629dfd36c4a4f7a9aaa254e64ad2441245c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mydef 10 of arXiv:2607.00495, 'Rank deficiency of Bernoulli random matrices for growing corank'] For $p \in (0,1/2]$, $L \ge 1$, and $x \in \mathbb{R}^{n}$, let $b_{1},\dots,b_{n}$ be independent Bernoulli($p$) random variables and we define 
