{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.888558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32f32c724df7a1ba37be227aec101df6379b0d6803151f3c30445a96a3962c31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition tara of arXiv:2607.02742, 'Gaussian fluctuations for the parabolic Anderson model with L\'evy white noise'] Let $F\in {\rm dom}(D)$ with $\mathbb{E}[F]=0$ and  ${\rm Var}(F)=\sigma^2 > 0$. Then, 
for any $p,q\in [1,2]$,
\begin{align*}
d_{\rm FM}\left( \frac{F}{\sigma}, Z\right) & \leq d_{\rm W}\left(\frac{F}{\sigma}, Z\right)  \leq    \gamma_1 +  \gamma_2 +  \gamma_3\\
  d_{\rm K}\left(\frac{F}{\sigma}, Z\right) & \leq  \sqrt{ \frac{\pi}{2}} (  \gamma_1 +  \gamma_2)   +  \gamma_4 +  \gamma_5+  \gamma_6 +  \gamma_7,
\end{align*}
where  $Z\sim N(0,1)$ and the seven quantities $ \gamma_1, \ldots,  \gamma_7$ are given as follows:
\begin{align}
\begin{aligned}
 \gamma_1&:=  \frac{2^{\frac2p + \frac12} }{\sqrt{\pi}}
 \sigma^{-2} \bigg( \int_{Z}  \bigg[ \int_{\bf Z}  \| D_{\xi_2}F \|_{2p}  \| D^2_{\xi_1,\xi_2}F\|_{2p} 
  \,  \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_2) \bigg]^p
  \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_1) \bigg)^{\frac1p}
\\
 \gamma_2&:=\frac{2^{\frac2p - \frac12} }{\sqrt{\pi}}
\sigma^{-2} \bigg( \int_{Z}  \bigg[ \int_{\bf Z}   \| D^2_{\xi_1,\xi_2}F\|^2_{2p}  \,  \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_2) \bigg]^p
  \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_1) \bigg)^{\frac1p}
\\
 \gamma_3&:= 2 \sigma^{-(q+1)}\int_{\bf Z} \| D_\xi F \|_{q+1}^{q+1}  \, \mathfrak{m}(d\xi)
\\
 \gamma_4&:= 2^{\frac{2}{p}} \sigma^{-2} \bigg( \int_{\bf Z} \| D_\xi F \|_{2p}^{2p}  \, \mathfrak{m}(d\xi) \bigg)^{\frac1p}
\\
 \gamma_5&:= (4p)^{\frac1p} \sigma^{-2} \bigg( \int_{Z^2} \| D^2_{\xi_1,\xi_2}  F \|_{2p}^{2p}
\, \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_1)\mathfrak{m}(d\xi_2)  \bigg)^{\frac1p}
\\
 \gamma_6&:=(2^{2+p}p)^{\frac1p} \sigma^{-2} \bigg( \int_{Z^2} \| D^2_{\xi_1,\xi_2}  F \|_{2p}^{p}
 \| D_{\xi_1}F \|_{2p}^p
\, \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_1)\mathfrak{m}(d\xi_2)  \bigg)^{\frac1p}\\
 \gamma_7&:=  \frac{  (8p)^{\frac1p} }{\sigma^2}
 \bigg( \int_{Z^2} \| D^2_{\xi_1,\xi_2}  F \|_{2p}
 \| D_{\xi_1}F \|_{2p}  \| D_{\xi_2}F \|_{2p}^{2(p-1)}
\, \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_1) \mathfrak{m}(d\xi_2)  \bigg)^{\frac1p}.
\end{aligned}

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:56.997072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32f4a54c29640b2c15954c85c3ab2820808008b54bc8c59d3748bd638cc504f4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.02785, 'Characterization of Stanley-Reisner varieties by their automorphism group'] The following are equivalent:
