{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.876241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3310e9f5b9f7a4a9c8e51e7bb9b8ffa2e7c5b4cd0deb6660846dce6662e86703","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2608.29501, 'Disorder Thresholds and Free Energy of Brownian Directed Polymers with\\ Product and Radia'] Assume \eqref{eq:product-tail}.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
  \item If \(\kappa>2\), then
  \begin{equation}
    0<\beta_c\le\bar\beta_c<\infty.

  \end{equation}
  \item If \(\kappa<2\), then there exist \(0<c<C<\infty\) and
  \(\beta_0>0\) such that
  \begin{equation}
    c\,\beta^{4/(2-\kappa)}
    \le -p(\beta)\le C\,\beta^{4/(2-\kappa)},
    \qquad 0<\beta\le\beta_0.

  \end{equation}
  In particular, \(\beta_c=\bar\beta_c=0\).

  \item If \(\kappa=2\), then
  \begin{equation}
    \beta_c=0<\bar\beta_c<\infty.

  \end{equation}
  More explicitly, strong disorder holds for every \(\beta>0\), while
  there exists \(\beta_0>0\) such that
  \begin{equation}
    p(\beta)=0,
    \qquad 0\le\beta\le\beta_0.

  \end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
All constants may depend on \(d,\bm\alpha,c_Q,C_Q\), but not on
\(\beta\). In particular, the critical case is possible only when \(d\ge3\), since every
\(\alpha_j<1\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

