{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.364720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_334967a4fa2e2c8cae202682636a551ce5e1031587d6e5c21c9767afa796db15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:covariances of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Recall the random variables $S_j^X(n), S_j^Y(n)$, and $S_j^Z(n)$, $j=0,1,\ldots,\ell$ just defined, and assume they satisfy~(equation eq:gdcondvars of the paper). Then  there is an $m\in \N$ depending only on  $\ell, N, (K_j)_{j=0}^\ell$, and $\alpha$, such that for 
