{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.289263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33948e8f38aa5969901ac53ba4a2e3fd3c283b103811177ba836f7fd20320e93","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2411.04988, '{\bf A relation between isoperimetry and total variation decay with applications to graphs'] Let $M<\infty$ and let $G$ be a graph with degrees bounded by $M$ and non-negative Ollivier-Ricci curvature. Then the isoperimetric profile $\Phi$ of $G$ satisfies
