Then $\mathcal{X}_n$ converges in law to a Poisson-Dirichlet distribution. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.559625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33a20b254c10c0c1fd250b6e2672095c71f1eb773ee616f51f5cc4c4bba3af90","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:union_of_largest of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Fix $\varepsilon>0$. There is $n_0=n_0(\varepsilon)\in \mathbb{N}$ such that, if $k\coloneqq \lceil (\log n)^3 \rceil$ and $n\geq n_0$, then
