{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.965780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33a8be9a5c9e666cf609d894439c1cbd0625f24a073e08df0448cebe679039d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 20 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {ATE for Well-Conditioned Measures (Theorem 3.1, \cite{ascolani:lavenant:zanella2026})}


    Let the probability measure $\nu$ on $\R^n$ have density $\nu(x) \propto \exp(-V(x))$ where $V : \R^n \to \R$ fulfills Assumption \ref{ass:strongcondition}. Then, with $X \sim \nu$ we have
