{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:21:28.715717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33bae12f92089a87ad240bbd4ca2b754140f6dfd11235d38a7c9cf4871e548a9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:rs-lc of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] The following implications hold for a polynomial $p\in \mathbb R[z_1,\ldots, z_n]$:
