{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.359443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33c8518385e10f2899df5e9ca2f3ed5bffcf3ab4d38da1c4264d3517ec465b9f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2604.21143, 'Quantitative homogenization for the critical long-range random conductance model'] Let $\alpha \in [0,\infty)$. Then there exists a constant $C \coloneqq C(\alpha, d) < \infty$ such that, for every $\eps \in (0,1)$,
		\begin{equation}

			\eps^d \sum_{\substack{z \in \eps \Zd \setminus \{0\} \\ |z| \leq 1 }} \frac{1}{|z|^\alpha} \leq
			\left\{ \begin{aligned}
				C  &\quad\text{if }\alpha < d\,, \\
				C (1 + \left| \ln \eps \right|) &\quad\text{if }\alpha = d\,, \\
				C \eps^{d - \alpha} &\quad\text{if }\alpha > d\,.
			\end{aligned} \right.
		\end{equation}
		and for every $\alpha > d$,
		\begin{equation} 
			\eps^d \sum_{\substack{z \in \eps \Zd \\ |z| \geq 1 }} \frac{1}{|z|^\alpha} \leq C
		\end{equation} 
		Additionally, for every $\eps \in (0,1/2]$ and every integer $1 \le i \le d$,
		\begin{equation}

			\frac{\eps^d}{\left| \ln \eps \right|} \sum_{\substack{z \in \eps \Zd \setminus \{0\} \\ |z| \leq 1}} J(z)  z_i^2 = \frac{\eps^d}{d \left| \ln \eps \right|} \sum_{\substack{z \in \eps \Zd \setminus \{0\} \\ |z| \leq 1}} J(z)  |z|^2 =  V_d + O\left(\frac{1}{\left| \ln \eps \right|}\right)\,,
		\end{equation}
		and for every pair of distinct integers $1 \le i, j \le d$ with $i \ne j$,
		\begin{equation}

			\frac{\eps^d}{\left| \ln \eps \right|} \sum_{\substack{z \in \eps \Zd \setminus \{0\} \\ |z| \leq 1}} J(z) z_i z_j = 0\,.
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.962921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33c87d8e9267a0ddc8893fe2718b53f1af938b818583ab1741befdbcbd03d1cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:wlln of arXiv:2509.11384, 'The Horton-Strahler number of butterfly trees'] \[
