{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.338911+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_345113a6f5b7447168ed65b9b523d04340899a4947c1c07987b9cd261425c7b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] (One-block estimate, cf.\ Lemma 5.4 of \cite{BFS})
Let $f=f(\eta)$ be a local $L^{p'}(\mu_{N,m})$ function on $\mathcal{X}_{N,m}$
with $p'>p$ depending 
only on $\eta_{\La_{\ell_0}} = (\eta(x))_{x\in \La_{\ell_0}}$.  
Then, there exists $C>0$, uniform in $N, m, \ell$ and $\ga$,
such that, for $\ell\ge \ell_0$ and $p\ge 2$, we have
\begin{align}  
E_{\mu_{N,m}} & \Bigg[ \sup_{0\le t \le T} \Big| \int_0^t \sum_{x\in \T_N}
h(s,x) \Big\{ f(\t_x \eta_s^N)- E_{\mu_{N,m}} [f(\t_x\eta_s^N)|\eta_s^{N,(\ell)}(x)]\Big\} ds
