{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.882994+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3479afd332b7a04ed23e362999df2d3fdda045616a853e463a035fc694221d2e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:dragoverkill of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] There exists a smooth function $\mathrm{O}(t)>-1$, defined for $t\in [0,1)$ such that $\mathrm{O}(0)=0$, and such that the following holds.
Let $(M,g)$ be a compact smooth Riemannian manifold of dimension $n$, possibly with boundary. Let $\phi$ be a Gaussian field of class $\mathcal{C}^3(M)$ with covariance function $E$ and parameters $\lambda=\lambda(\phi)>0,\sigma=\sigma(\phi)>0,\varepsilon=\varepsilon(\phi)$ defined as in [cgv2025StecconiTodino] (see also (def:three of the paper)), and let $\tau:=\tau(\phi)$ be as in (eq:defe03 of the paper).
Assume that there exist positive numbers: $ \frac{c} {\lambda} \le r\le \rho$, $\delta$ and $B$, satisfying the following assumptions.
\begin{enumerate}
\item The eccentricity is less than one:
\begin{equation} 
\varepsilon=\varepsilon(\phi)<1, \quad \text{and} \quad \tau=\tau(\phi)<1.
\end{equation}
\item The pull-back field satisfies: 
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{\substack{x,y\in M,
\\
 \mathrm{dist}(x,y)\le r}
}
\sigma^{-2}\|j^{3,3}_{x,y}E\|_{g^{\lambda}}

\le B
\end{equation}
\item The field satisfies:
    \begin{equation} 
\sup_{\substack{x,y\in M,
\\
r
\le \mathrm{dist}(x,y)\le \rho
}}

\sigma^{-2}\|j^{1,1}_{x,y}E\|_{g^{\lambda}}
\le \delta  <\frac{(1-\varepsilon)^2}{2\left(1+\mathrm{O}(\tau)\right)} 

\end{equation}

\end{enumerate}
Then, we have the following quantitative Law Of Large Numbers:
\begin{gather}

{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left\{ \frac{\mathcal{L}_f(M)}{\lambda}\right\}\le

{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left\{ \frac{\mathcal{L}_f(M)[2]}{\lambda}\right\}

+\mathfrak{C}\rho^{-n}\cdot  \Bigg(\mathfrak{D}r^{n}+
\\

+

\frac{(1+\mathrm{O}(\tau))(1+\mathrm{O}(\varepsilon))}{1-\delta\frac{2 (1+\mathrm{O}(\tau))}{(1-\varepsilon)^2}}
\frac{2^4}{n}\int_{\substack{x,y\in M,
\\
r
\le \mathrm{dist}(x,y)\le \rho}}\|\sigma^{-2}j^{1,1}_{x,y}E\|^4_{g^{\lambda}} \dd x \dd y 
\Bigg).
\end{gather}
where $\mathfrak{D}=\mathfrak{D}(n,M,g;B,c)$ is a constant depending only on $n,M,g$ and on the constants $B,c$; $\mathfrak{C}=\mathfrak{C}(n,M,g)$ depends only on the geometry.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.025745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_347c8188d9f8c9e7a18b09ee95357a55ee366a07aa503a8652c3d22cb639cc12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thm:fBm-loc-ord of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] Let $ B^H$ be a fractional Brownian motion with Hurst parameter   $ H \in ( 0 ,1)$  and let $W^H$ be the probability law of $B^H$. Then  $W^H$-almost surely the local order  of the standard Wiener measure $W$ (for the uniform norm) at $ B^H$ is given by
        \begin{equation*}
            \mathsf{ord}_{ \mathrm{loc}  } W ( B^H) =
            \begin{dcases}
                2 ( H^{-1} - 1) & \qquad  \text{ if } \, 0 < H < 1/2 \\
                2 & \qquad \text{ if } \, 1/2  \le  H <  1  \, .
