{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.303554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34a46fefb964d12ce12f983f76bbe82bd28627de6e86743db6587b30ac424382","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Heat Kernel of arXiv:2605.26869, 'Law of Large Numbers for a random walk on dynamic environments with drift'] Let $(a_n)_{n\geq 0}$ be an arbitrary positive sequence converging to 0. For $n\geq 0$ and $z\in \mathbb{Z}$, let $w = z - (2q-1)n$. As $n\rightarrow \infty$, we have that uniformly in $z\in [(2q-1)n-na_n,(2q-1)n+na_n]$:
