\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Then $f$ is Borel measurable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.204006+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34a78d5348aedec2bdc093a8ff14dcee6dde83a1c1b149c47fa96296c7713025","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ProLiu of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Let $\{L(t)\}_{t\geq 0}$ be defined by (equation Alphastabile of the paper) with $\alpha\in (0,2)$ and let $\gamma\geq 0$. Then the following assertions are equivalent.
