{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.759385+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34a8e183687e06b50fac5d183b92f23855c0bbe4913445d2b7904314dd07ac11","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 60 of arXiv:2511.20322, 'Dissertation'] Assume \assref{assum:H}, $\bar f \in \Lip^{6+1}([0,T]\times \R^d)$ and $\sqrt \Si\in \Lip^{6+1}([0,T]\times \R^{d\times d})$. Suppose $X$ is the solution to the family of \tSDE{}
