{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.220804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34d6d27af881135b5e5f3ebcac8a2104f1f69bf744d26c0079d8d594f4a97e7b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: 523 of arXiv:2607.05848, 'Mesoscopic eigenvalue statistics for correlated random matrices'] {AEK20}}]
Let $\beta_{*}$ and $\epsilon_{*}$ be as in Lemma (lem: 792 of the paper). Consider $(z_{0},w_{0}),(z_{1},w_{1})\in\mathbb{C}$ satisfying $|z_{i}-w_{i}|\le\beta_{*}$, $\mathrm{Re}\, z_{i}, \mathrm{Re}\, w_{i}\in\mathcal{I}(\epsilon_{0}/2)$, and $\mathrm{Im}\, z_{i}\cdot\mathrm{Im}\, w_{i}<0$ for each $i=0,1$.
Denote the stability operator $\mathcal{B}_{i}\coloneqq \mathcal{B}_{z_{i},w_{i}}$ and
the single eigenvalue $\beta_{i}\coloneqq\beta_{z_{i},w_{i}}$ of $\mathcal{B}_{i}$ for each $i=0,1$.
Let $R_{0}$ be the normalized right eigenvector of $\mathcal{B}_{0}$ corresponding $\beta_{0}$;
i.e.\,$\mathcal{B}_{0}[R_{0}]=\beta_{0}R_{0}$ and $\lVert R_{0}\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}=1$.
Similarly, let $L_{0}$ be the corresponding left eigenvector, that is, $\mathcal{B}_{0}^{*}[L_{0}]=\bar{\beta}_{0}L_{0}$  and $\lVert L_{0}\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}=1$.
Let $\Pi_{i}$ be the rank-one spectral projection corresponding to $\beta_{i}$ (as in Lemma (lem: 792 of the paper)) for each $i=0,1$.
Define $R_{1}\coloneqq \Pi_{1}[R_{0}]$ and $L_{1}\coloneqq \Pi_{1}^{*}[L_{0}]$.

Then $R_{1}$ and $L_{1}$ are (unnormalized) eigenvectors of $\mathcal{B}_{1}$ and $\mathcal{B}_{1}^{*}$ corresponding to $\beta_{1}$ and $\bar{\beta}_{1}$, respectively.
Write $\Delta\mathcal{B}\coloneqq \mathcal{B}_{1}-\mathcal{B}_{0}$. Then, we have
\begin{equation*}
	R_{1} = R_{0} + O(\lVert \Delta\mathcal{B}\rVert_{\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}\to\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}}), \quad
	L_{1} = L_{0} + O(\lVert \Delta\mathcal{B}\rVert_{\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}\to\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}}),
\end{equation*}
\begin{equation*}
	\beta_{1}\langle L_{1}, R_{1} \rangle 
	= \beta_{0} \langle L_{0}, R_{0}\rangle + \langle L_{0}, \Delta\mathcal{B}[R_{0}]\rangle + O(\lVert  \Delta\mathcal{B}\rVert_{\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}\to\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}}^{2}),
\end{equation*}
where the implicit constants in the error terms $O(\lVert \Delta\mathcal{B}\rVert_{\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}\to\lVert\cdot\rVert_{\textnormal{hs}}})$ depend only on $\epsilon_{*}$ and $\beta_{*}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.552083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34da29146cfe0c4e17650d99ce13b5539c77fe4821e5a697ef606eb90163ce23","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] For $\mu$ as in Assumption \ref{ass:low-temperature},
