{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.486817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35062cbba679e9b796a58685b15e057cf1493739c346f103d96543d3d5f5d433","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Closing conditions for a nut-type collapse) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] In case (2) of Lemma \ref{lem:bolt-nut-dichotomy}, a smooth closing at $s = 0$ requires:

