{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.956747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_351f27872ae6f5235c8759a268b3692d1e161118c355f3ebc72806c7ddd64a69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Knowntheorem 40 (\cite{BorJanVol2013}) of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Suppose $Y=Y_1+iY_2$ is a conformal martingale and $X=X_1+iX_2$ is an arbitrary martingale. Then 
