{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.811999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35222c76c47caa2efa6dd03fd0075d00da667737e8ced2cdded6b1fb1aa0db10","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Full statement of Lemma \ref{lemma: roughly-uniform} of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\lambda_n = n-n^{1-\alpha}, K = \{\lfloor 2\lambda_n \rfloor - n,...,n-1\}$ and $\nu_K(x) = \frac{\nu(x)}{\sum_{x \in K} \nu(x)} \forall x \in K$ and $\nu_K(x) = 0$ otherwise. For $\alpha \in (1/2,1)$ and $n \geq 110$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \underbrace{\frac{\br{1-\frac{1}{(n^\alpha-2)^2}}^n \sqrt{1-2n^{-\alpha}-n^{-1}}}{e^{\frac{1}{12\lfloor n-2n^{1-\alpha}\rfloor}} \br{2+n^{\alpha-1}}}}_{L_K(n)} \times n^{\alpha-1} \leq \nu_K(x) \leq \underbrace{\frac{e^{\frac{1}{12\lfloor n-2n^{1-\alpha}\rfloor}} \sqrt{1-2n^{-\alpha}-n^{-1}}}{2 \br{1-\frac{1}{(n^\alpha-2)^2}}^n}}_{U_K(n)} \times n^{\alpha-1}.
