{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.332477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3530a199cee0554d2e399321333e4a3c1e8f865fca446bc0e3aa26897c735688","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 12 of arXiv:2608.30380, 'Morita Induction and Geometric Ideals in $\ell^p$ Roe-Type Algebras'] Let $I\triangleleft B$ and set $J=\Ind_B^A(I)$.  With
\[
 X=E_I^{>},\qquad Y={}_I E^{<},
\]
