{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.655801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_354a72ee96048caae1f3f6b72c5ebb41ded58b739edd96f3fd3d4917bda82be5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2609.03556, 'An Effective SPDE Model for a Schr\"odinger Equation with a Fluctuating Magnetic Potential'] \label[proposition]{prop:well_posed_averaging_limit}
   Assume \cref{hp:noise}. For each $\epsilon\in [-5,5]$ and
