{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.254551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355429b02903a6098c4f066f9df8996ed772e37fa5d30c270be36d6ac2aa12f0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 20 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For $\calX=(X,d^X,\mu_X),\;\calY=(Y,d^Y,\mu_Y)\in\frK(\tau)$, we define
