 m_i \, = \, \Big( \kappa \tfrac{a_i^\rho}{a_i^\rho + b_i^\rho} +  \tfrac{1-\kappa}{2} \Big) m_{i+1} + \Big( \kappa \tfrac{b_i^\rho}{a_i^\rho + b_i^\rho} +  \tfrac{1-\kappa}{2} \Big) m_{i-1} \, - \, a_i \, .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.892592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355a538dfce69991e8263c21f99ee8577c9099922469b792f7141617632f3625","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] There exist absolute constants $c_0,C_0,C_1,C_2>0$ such that, for every $n\ge1$,
\begin{align}
 |V_n^2-n|&\le C_0(1+A_\infty)\quad\text{a.s.},\\
 |s_n^2-n|&\le C_1,\\
