 \quad\text{a.s. for every }k\ge1.
\end{align}
In particular, $s_n^2\asymp n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.993358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355c185b524ae0d582154164650f4395d26b1289201fe9bf2e68fa02be62ba12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main-1 of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded Lipchitz domain   in $\mathbb{R}^3$.
