{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.327996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355e8c603463bd30b5540b0c73bce9c478059c4ced1ad290b65edb637162190f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Piecewise-linear approximation of time-Haar atoms) of arXiv:2607.14361, 'NeuralChaos: Optimal Adapted Approximation of Square Integrable Predictable Processes'] Let $p \in \mathbb{N}_{+}$ and let $q \in \{0,\ldots,2^{p}-1\}$. If $0<\eta_t<2^{-(p+2)}$, then 
