{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.185473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_358d09d9423aaa910ad15394047b6db3d20ea349b3fc33e433d9dd527156c5d5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2606.30364, 'Distributional comparison for non-commutative infinitely divisible probability measures'] Let $\circledast \in \{ \ast, \boxplus ,\uplus, \rhd \}$. 
