{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.908241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3598c5041759d665bb4aa159a9b8606d0c9ff80c5eec2eabc74a638c48cd4db6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2608.01081, 'The Optimal Rate in the Averaged Random-Marginal Central Limit Theorem for Log-Concave Mea'] There is a universal constant $c>0$ such that, for every sufficiently large
