{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.746892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3614ca4679e5a27f49f5a1760d4bfef4fe4eec0f88eb769f0319b99d54e708f4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:alpha_family of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let $\alpha \in (0, 2)$ and let 
    $\left(N_q^{(\alpha)}\right)_{q \geqslant 1}$ be independent $q$-Poisson processes defined in Definition (def:q_poisson_process of the paper). Then, for $q \geqslant 1$ and $m \geqslant 2$, let us set 
\begin{equation}

    V_{q, m}^{(\alpha)} \coloneqq  q \int f_m(u)  N_q^{(\alpha)}(\,\mathrm{d} u) = q \sum_{i \geqslant 1} f_m \left(\xi_{q,i}^{(\alpha)} \right) \,.
\end{equation}
For $m=1$, since $f_1 \notin \mathrm{L}^1(\nu_q^{(\alpha)})$ but $f_1 \in \mathrm{L}^2(\nu_q^{(\alpha)})$, we define $V_{q, 1}^{(\alpha)}$ as a compensated Poisson integral
\begin{equation*}
    V_{q, 1}^{(\alpha)} \coloneqq  q \int f_1(u)  \tilde{N}_q^{(\alpha)}(\,\mathrm{d} u) \in \mathrm{L}^2({\mathbb P})  \,,
\end{equation*}
where $\tilde N_q^{(\alpha)}(\,\mathrm{d} u)
    =N_q^{(\alpha)}(\,\mathrm{d} u)-\nu_q^{(\alpha)}(\,\mathrm{d} u)$.
 We call an \textit{$\alpha$-Poisson family} the family $\left(Z_k^{(\alpha)} \right)_{k \geqslant 1}$ given by 
\begin{equation}

    Z_k^{(\alpha)} \coloneqq  \sum_{q | k} V_{q, k/q}^{(\alpha)} \, , \qquad k \geqslant 1 \,,
\end{equation}
where the summation in (equation eq:family_alpha of the paper) is over all divisors of $k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.851047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3616756f04aa8a42f1afebd4676a1a24f6d6d66a2e85a05bf79be4ddd877d52d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:continuous-comparator-bound of arXiv:2608.25182, 'Minimax Alternating Regret \\for the Experts Problem and Online Convex Optimization'] For every $u\in\mathcal{X}$ and every $\delta\in(0,1)$,
