{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.608408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3636c6df38b1a18328a60f908b667ac3b0af049c327cb12f8c36853d0ae61ad1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2607.08314, 'Berry-Heisenberg random waves'] \cite[Theorem 5.4.2]{AdlerTaylor07}
    Let $f=\{ f(t), \, t\in \R^{n}\}$ be a mean-square continuous, centered (Gaussian) stationary random fields on $\R^{n}$ with covariance function \eqref{eqn.cov.Rn}. Then there exists a complex (Gaussian) $\nu$-noise $W$ on $\R^{n}$ such that 
    \begin{align}
        f(t) = \int_{\R^{n}} e^{i  t\cdot \lambda}  dW(\lambda),
    \end{align}
    where the equality holds in mean-square for each $t\in \R^{n}$.

    Conversely, the random field $f$ defined by \eqref{e.spectral.rep.real} has covariance function given by 
    \begin{align*}
        C(t,s) = \int_{\R^{n}} e^{i ( t-s) \cdot \lambda } d \nu (\lambda),
    \end{align*}
    and so is stationary. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.362885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363746bfe35c2bb53dd9d072a1e690553ec0be03abb993e4451952af2cda38d3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 72 (Size of $k_i$ at the $\sqrt{n}$ threshold) of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Let $i_* := \inf \{1 \le i \le S : k_i > \sqrt{n}\}$. Then there exists $c=c(\varepsilon)>0$ such that for all $n\ge 1$,
    \begin{align}
\widetilde{\p}_n\bigg( k_{i_*}> \sqrt{n}\Big( 1+ \frac{2}{(\log n)^\alpha}\Big) \,\bigg|\, i_*\le S\bigg) \le \exp\Big(-\frac{c \sqrt{n}}{(\log n)^{2\alpha}}\Big).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.749926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363a6e7d6e71e932274bfc2bec8fd2159abb2a4efa572e9b975509591e6ec2bc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ladder-estimate-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Fix \(q\in(1,2)\) with \(\rho(q)<1\), let
\(0<\beta<\beta_X(q)\), and fix \(\alpha_{\mathrm{gr}}>1\).  Then there exist
constants
\[
    C_{\mathrm{lad}}<\infty,\qquad
    \tau_{\mathrm{lad}}<\infty,\qquad
    n_0\ge1,
\]
depending on \(q,\beta,\alpha_{\mathrm{gr}}\) and on the law of the cascade,
such that, for every \(n\ge n_0\) and every \(0\le k\le n\),
\begin{equation}
    A^{(q,\alpha_{\mathrm{gr}})}_{k,n}
    \le
    C_{\mathrm{lad}} n^{\tau_{\mathrm{lad}}}2^{-q\beta k}.
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
    A^{(q,\alpha_{\mathrm{gr}})}_{n,n}
    \le
    C_{\mathrm{lad}} n^{\tau_{\mathrm{lad}}}2^{-q\beta n}
    \qquad(n\ge n_0).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.713942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363bd5b3948303c63fa52fcb52c440210dd1c413a5eaf2dd4060da3309641288","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 45 (Hermitian dilation and the rectangular inequality) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $A_{\nu}:\mathcal H_0\to\mathcal H_1$ be a finite family of operators between
