{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.144261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363d7d66c918dc807606bc721add400c051902bab6e79b05be5bbbac36dff41d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:thm1a0 of arXiv:2608.18990, 'Proving Lehner's formulas via RDT -- indefinite and asymmetric scenarios'] Assume the setup of Theorem (thm:thm1 of the paper) with $A_0=0$. For $m,n\in{\mathbb N}$ such that $\alpha=\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{m}{n}$, let $G_{i}^{(4)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k_1\times m}$ and $G_{i}^{(5)}\in{\mathbb R}^{k_2\times n},i=1,\dots,l$ be two matrices comprised of independent standard normals. Moreover, let $G_{i}^{(4)}$ and $G_{i}^{(5)}$ be independent of all other randomness. Set
\begin{eqnarray}

 L_{l,Y} & = &  
   \max_{Y\in{\mathbb R}^{m\times k_1}, Y^TY =I} \sum_{i=1}^{l}  \mbox{Tr}\left ( G_i^{(4)} Y F_{i,Y}F_{i,Y}^T \right )   \nonumber \\
    L_{l,X} & = &  
   \max_{X\in{\mathbb R}^{n\times k_2}, X^TX =I} \sum_{i=1}^{l}  \mbox{Tr}\left ( G_i^{(5)} X F_{i,X}F_{i,X}^T \right )      .
\end{eqnarray}
Let $\xi_{l,Y}$ and $\xi_{l,X}$ be as in ((eq:hrd0a0a0 of the paper)).  One then has  
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_a  
 \geq 
 \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_{l,Y}
+
 \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty}  \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}  {\mathbb E} \xi_{l,X}
  = \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\mathbb E} L_{l,Y}
  +
  \lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}} {\mathbb E} L_{l,X}.
\end{eqnarray}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.481381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363e2063b91bc546424fbf689750e62583d0473b9503503535797fdacfda62fe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 16 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] For every $D\subsetneq \C$ open simply connected domain and
