{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.110441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3640ac269a63cf9cb2755014f9c3acf295e976ab5cd5994c93830bec388e470b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.27398, 'Strict Stability and Strict Minimality of Regular Area-Minimizing Hypercones: A Quantitati'] There exists a constant $c_{\C}>0$ such that, for every $R>0$ and every set
