{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.896610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_366deb51e46be51cc77959cf7b4155c35b6fafe8626e7adb0e3ab5ab82fc4390","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition erasedmassdef of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] Let $(T, d, \rho, \mu)$ be a rooted finitely measured Polish $\mathbb{R}$-tree and let $h \! \in \!  \mathbb{R}^*_+$. Then 
$\nu \! := \! \mathtt{P}_{T_{\! \mu, h}} \mu + h \varpi_{T_{\! \mu, h}}$ is the unique positive Borel measure on $T$ such that 
