{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.732931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36a6d1688ee43ac422c6c00e3dc931db13e0c37ac990d59a3bcd9d9fb0ac6e21","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Upward and downward two-sided exit problem) of arXiv:2605.18136, 'L\'evy processes with partially stochastic resetting'] For $a, b \in \mathbb{R}$ and $x \in[b, a]$, the following limits hold
