{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.437504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36c2b6174cea33ffe8d2839fc40bec5dbeb031d243c1453ff6ed364d10d63c31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2604.07275, 'Some probabilistic properties and time-changed versions of a renewal process based on Mitt'] Consider two independent inverse subordinators  $\{Y_{f_1}(t)\}_{t\ge 0}$ and $\{Y_{f_2}(t)\}_{t\ge 0}$ with associated  Bern\v{s}tein functions $f_1(s)$ and $f_2(s)$, respectively. Then
		\begin{equation}
			Y_{f_1}(Y_{f_2}(t)) \overset{d}{=} Y_{f_1 \circ f_2}(t), \ t \ge 0,
		\end{equation}
		where $(f_1 \circ f_2)(s) = f_1(f_2(s))$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.770629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36c542024060db2d2825de0bed456c7e6b18c126dc080522db36d66980ae2ad7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop MRSC satisfies the side condition of arXiv:2605.03151, 'Giants through Higher-Order paths in Random Simplicial Complexes'] Assume that $d = 2$ with $p_1$ and $p_2$ parametrized by $p_1 = \Theta(n^{-\alpha_1})$ and $p_2 = \Theta(n^{-\alpha_2})$ satisfying $2\alpha_1 + \alpha_2 = 1$. Assume further that $0 \leq \alpha_1 < \frac{2 \log 2}{\log \lambda + 2 \log 2}$. Then, $X_n \sim \MRSC_2(n; p_1, p_2)$ satisfies the condition ((eq: 4.1.1 of the paper)) (equivalently, the condition ((eq: 2.2.3 of the paper)). More precisely,
\[  \tag{4.1.3}
\lim_{r \to \infty} \limsup_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P} \left( \sigma_1 \centernot\longleftrightarrow \sigma_2,  s_{1} \left( \partial B_{X_n} (\sigma_1; r) \right),  s_{1} \left( \partial B_{X_n}(\sigma_2; r) \right) \geq r \right) = 0.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.425707+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36c68283c3286913e3d983ab4fc3276edbd32ea6b2975df1bc450b707621a6d2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2606.09691, '\textsc{Degenerate Diffusions on Continuum Percolation and Hamilton-Jacobi-Bellman Equatio'] Under Assumptions \ref{f1} and \ref{f2}--\ref{f4}, for every $T>0$ there exists a constant $\bar C_{T,f}$ such that
