{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.481191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36cbdcfe7fe56488474514cd5380208abb951c2e044db513157764d39be868db","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Chordal Loewner chain of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] Let $g_t$ satisfies the chordal Loewner equation

\begin{equation}
\partial_t g_t(z)= \frac{2}{g_t(z)-\xi(t)}, \quad g_0(z)=z,
\end{equation}

where $t \mapsto \xi_t$ is continuous and called the driving function. 
Let $K_t$ be the set of points $z$ in $\mathbb{H}$ such that the solution $g_s(z)$ blows up before or at time $t$.  $K_t$ is called the chordal SLE hull driven by $\xi_t$

Chordal Loewner chain in arbitrary simply connected domain $\Omega \subsetneq \mathbb{C}$ from $a$ to $b$, is defined via a uniformizing conformal map from $\Omega$ onto $\mathbb{H}$ sending $a$ to $0$ and $b$ to $\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.223983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36cd0a579729f84bb65c1bff153a7078644c08fc3d17a34f06b69d242de9a40d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theoremletter Thm:Neumayer of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $(M,g)$ be a closed Riemannian manifold of dimension $n\geq 3$ that is not conformally equivalent to the round sphere. Then, there exist constants $C>0$ and $\theta\geq 0$, depending on $(M,g)$, such that
    \begin{align*}
        Q(u)-Y(M,[g]) \geq C d(u,\mathcal{M})^{2+\theta} \quad \forall u \in H^1 (M,\mathbb{R}_+ ),
    \end{align*}
    where $d(-,\mathcal{M})$ is a suitable distance to the set of minimizers $\mathcal{M}$. Moreover, there exists an open dense subset $\mathcal{G}$ in the $C^2$ topology on the space of smooth conformal classes of metrics on $M$ such that if $[g]\in \mathcal{G}$ then $\theta = 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.224015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36cfcf314511e102d2d5ca7446e18b4a6580b1d09bf49cf18633d983aee82273","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma est of arXiv:2412.09471, 'On the moderate deviation principles in the sparse multi-type Erd\H{o}s R\'enyi random gra'] For any $n\in{\mathbb N}$ and $k\in {\mathbb N}^d$,
