{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.974347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36f713e6f0f60535d5170dc6eea7282977dca4587801dfd531f60afed30812b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.13648, 'Stochastic dominations for FK percolation and sharp thinning thresholds for the Ising ener'] For any parameters $p,\tilde{p}\in [0,1]^{E}$ and real numbers $q,\tilde{q}\ge1$, we have the following stochastic domination:
