{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.165147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36fd9c3a59cf8fb51f467a57771a2f660407b73427762923b3b11d63b2a28179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: boundary of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] For every $f \in C^\infty(\mathbb T^2
)$, there exists $\mathcal{Z}^0(f) > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{T \rightarrow \infty}\mathcal{Z}_T^0(f) = \mathcal{Z}^0(f). 	
\end{equation}
Consequently, there exists a unique probability measure$\nu^0$ on $S'(\mathbb T^2)$ such that the measures $\nu^0_T$ converge weakly to $\nu^0$ as $T \rightarrow \infty$.  

Furthermore, there exists random variables $W^0_\infty$ and $Z^0_\infty$ defined on the probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb P)$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
	\item[(i)] $\nu^0 = {\rm Law}_{\mathbb P}(W^0_\infty+Z^0_\infty)$,
	\item[(ii)] ${\rm Law}_{\mathbb P}(W^0_\infty) = \mu^0$,
	\item[(iii)] $Z^0_\infty \in H^{1/2-\kappa}_z$ almost  surely,
	\item[(iv)] $\mathbb E[\|Z^0_\infty\|_{H^{1/2-\kappa}_z}^2]\leq C$. 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.059409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36feb0a08d0775c8fb0ab0de3896851f5f18e87bec6cde0cbfa94a0b31bde816","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Key1 of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $r_k=r_k(X)$ for a random variable $X$. Let $\alpha=(\alpha_1, \alpha_2, \ldots )$ be a weak partition of $q$ with at least two nonzero parts. The following bounds hold.

\begin{enumerate}
\item If $(r_k)$ is log-concave, then $\prod_ir_{\alpha_i}\geq r_1r_{q-1}\geq r_q$;\\

