{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.869474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_370697eb502ad4d068d4d54e5747409b535ba31643e9709852d7ae977ab2bd28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:expr_zcmcoup of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] Let $\mu,\nu\in\mathrm{M}_{0}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_{0,\mathrm{cm}}(\mu,\nu)$, and assume that $\mu$ vanishes on sets of Hausdorff dimension at most $d-1$. Then for any closed convex function $\psi: \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathbb{R} \cup \left\{\infty\right\}$ satisfying $\operatorname{spt}\gamma\subset \partial\psi$, we have $\mu(\reals^d_{\smallsetminus 0} \setminus \operatorname{dom} \nabla\psi) = 0$. The measure $\nu$ can be written as the push-forward of $\mu$ by $\nabla\psi$, up to a residual term: for every Borel set $B\subset\reals^d_{\smallsetminus 0}$,
    \[
        \nu(B) = (\nabla\psi)_{\#} \mu(B) + \gamma(\left\{0\right\} \times B). 
    \]
    In addition, $\gamma$ is uniquely determined by $\nabla \psi, \mu, \nu$ through the identities
    \begin{align*}
        \gamma(A \times B) 
        &= (\operatorname{Id} \times \nabla\psi)_{\#}\mu(A\times B)
        = \mu \rbr{A \cap (\nabla\psi)^{-1}(B)}, &&
        A \in \mathcal{B}(\reals^d_{\smallsetminus 0}), \, B \in \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d), \\
        \gamma(\left\{0\right\} \times B)
        &= \nu(B) - (\nabla\psi)_{\#} \mu(B), &&
        B \in \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d), \, 0 \not\in \operatorname{cl}(B).
    \end{align*}





















    Finally, if $\gamma$ is proper, i.e., $\gamma\in\Gamma_{0,\mathrm{cm}}^{\mathrm{p}}(\mu,\nu)$, then we have the \emph{proper representation} 
    \begin{equation}

        \gamma = \operatorname{res} \rbr{ (\operatorname{Id} \times \nabla\psi)_{\#}\mu }
        \quad \text{and} \quad
        \nu = \operatorname{res} \rbr{(\nabla \psi)_{\#}\mu}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

