{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.369164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_370f4a8e670cd4cbfb250200c2ff80d80c32e45ba7e8652378c84e3f6cc22633","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] Let \( (u_t)_{0 \leqslant t \leqslant T} \) be a stochastic process satisfying assumptions $\mathbf{(A1)}$ and $\mathbf{(A2)}$. Let \( 0 < a < b \leqslant T \) and \( M > 0 \) be given fixed. Then for any \( \eta \in (0, Q - \alpha) \) (if \( \alpha < 0 \), we further require \( \alpha + \eta < 0 \)), there exists a positive constant \( C = C(a, b, T, M, \alpha, \eta, V) \) such that
