{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.416858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_371ee9391566089bd3d6b3b9b57c0286769e5b93b7b41772f32d1976f9d5179a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (Energy theorem for the \(b\)-adic cube cascade) of arXiv:2606.08703, '2606.08703'] Let \(b\ge2\), \(d\ge1\), and let \(W\) satisfy \eqref{eq:badic-KP}.  Let
\(\mu\) be the associated canonical \(b\)-adic Mandelbrot cascade on
\([0,1]^d\).  Then, almost surely on \(\{\mu\ne0\}\),
