{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.943893+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_373e33a1d4f94bfe5073e68cdc03d8e3ed8e34507fcc5f27a9d346e7b487db15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.24599, '\bf Perron--Frobenius theorem for a general tree-valued growth-fragmentation-isolation pro'] Under Assumption~\ref{assum}, there exists a unique triplet $(\lambda, \pi, h)$ where $\pi, h : \TT \rightarrow  (0,\infty)$ and $\lambda \in \R$, such that for all $s\geq 0$,
