{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.814019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37587e3133e28a6dc961ab09b9f0dc8bca45223e25733390d56bb21ed48c42a6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:limit_uniq of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Assume $d\ge 2$, $s\in (0,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$, let $M_0$ be in $\dot{H}^{-s}$. Let $M$ be a solution to (equation eq:KK of the paper) (in the sense of (def:sol of the paper)) which is also in $L^2_{t,\omega}(H^{-s}))$. For every $\delta>0$ and $R>0$, we have
    \begin{align}
