{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.608640+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_375fac4e41321b209b8d1cc035940c17e88f7ff7a69018458c7fc9b04cfc406c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2607.08314, 'Berry-Heisenberg random waves'] For any $g_{1}, g_{2} \in \Hei$, the Carnot-Carath\'eodory distance is defined by 
    \begin{align*}
         d_{cc} (g_{1}  , g_{2} ) := \inf \left\{ \int_{0}^{1} \Vert \gamma^{\prime}(t) \Vert_{\gamma (s)} ,  \gamma: [0,1] \longrightarrow \Hei , \gamma(0) = g_{1} , \gamma(1) = g_{2} ,  \gamma \text{ is horizontal }\right\}
    \end{align*}
    where $\Vert \cdot \Vert_{g}$ denotes the norm in $\mathcal{H}_{g}$ induced by the sub-Riemannian structure.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.612240+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_376060a7fdfa85b719d3548e5fa6cf065d83b47667ad394e9c1b7c3c68698989","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:CAT(0) of arXiv:2512.13200, 'Martingales on a Euclidean manifold with a boundary and reflected BSDEs in non-convex doma'] Consider a metric space $(\mathcal{X},d_{\mathcal{X}})$. Then, $\mathcal{X}$ is a $CAT(0)$ space, a.k.a. Alexandrov non-positively curved space (shortly, NPC space), if, for all $(x,y,p,q) \in \mathcal{X}^4$ that admit minimizing geodesics $\gamma^{x,y}$, $\gamma^{x,p}$, $\gamma^{p,y}$, $\gamma^{x,q}$ and $\gamma^{q,y}$, we have, for all $z \in \gamma^{x,y}_{[0,1]}$,
\begin{align*} 
d_{\mathcal{X}}(p,q) \leqslant  d_{\mathbb{R}^2}(\tilde{p},\tilde{z}) + d_{\mathbb{R}^2}(\tilde{q},\tilde{z}),
\end{align*}
where $(\tilde{x},\tilde{y},\tilde{p})$ (resp., $(\tilde{x},\tilde{y},\tilde{q})$) is a triangle in $\mathbb{R}^2$ whose edges have Euclidean lengths equal to $d_{\mathcal{X}}(x,y)$, $d_{\mathcal{X}}(x,p)$, $d_{\mathcal{X}}(y,p)$ (resp., $d_{\mathcal{X}}(x,y)$, $d_{\mathcal{X}}(x,q)$, $d_{\mathcal{X}}(y,q)$), and $\tilde{z} \in [\tilde{x},\tilde{y}]$ is such that $d_{\mathbb{R}^2}(\tilde{x},\tilde{z})=d_{\mathcal{X}}(x,z)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.055448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_376102cbaa403130ff042d5708b01f6d735d31e881d3f5e4706fd38da996ecc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] For every test function $f$, we have the following moment estimates for the remainder term $\mathcal R_1^N$:
