{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.553154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_377196f8d2f9618b3ebf5df61b8513619b4111c3557d693c29c7fa3f5ece0869","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2608.27156, 'Traveling Waves in Equity Markets with\\Rank-Based Entry and Exit'] If the drift and volatility are constant, $b \equiv \mu$ and $\sigma(\cdot) \equiv \sigma$, then $u(t,x) := w(t, \log x)$ solves, in the original capitalization variable,
