{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.416571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_379128c8717584de9b20a0e5991d0d3e83af3a05ab230a62742d1f4cee57c24f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:2d_kernel_BGR of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] {borodin-gr2009q}}]

	The two-dimensional correlation kernel $\widetilde{K}(s,x;t,y)$
	of the $q$-Racah nonintersecting path ensemble is given by
	\begin{equation}

		\widetilde{K}(s,x;t,y)=
		\begin{cases}
			\displaystyle
			\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}
			(\widetilde{\mathscr{C}}_n^{t} \widetilde{\mathscr{C}}_n^{t+1}\ldots \widetilde{\mathscr{C}}_n^{s-1})^{-1}\hspace{1pt}
			f_n^s(x)\hspace{1pt} f_n^t(y),&\qquad  s\ge t;\\[12pt]
			\displaystyle
			-\sum_{n\ge N}
			(\widetilde{\mathscr{C}}_n^s \widetilde{\mathscr{C}}_n^{s+1}\ldots \widetilde{\mathscr{C}}_n^{t-1})\hspace{1pt}
			f_n^s(x)\hspace{1pt} f_n^t(y)
			,&\qquad  s<t.
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

