{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.979087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_379727237ed569c6029ec2d0623081b6200893ece31ec468fbb816d9f6c14b50","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj|introducingEAtCost of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] There exists a constant $C$ that depends only on $a$, $b$, $p$, $d$, and $m$ such that for every 
