{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.408745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37a5efe39c24146f737f391ab53671e3f0cd7257dd11af5b0471e9321ef8b450","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2604.06823, 'On spectrum of sample correlation matrices from large fold tensor vectors'] Let the limiting conditions \eqref{eq-def-ratio}, \eqref{eq-def-tau} and \eqref{eq-lim-k} hold. Assume that the base random vector $\y$ is uniformly distributed on the unit sphere $S^{2n-1}$ of $\bC^n$. We set $Y' = (Y_1,\ldots,Y_m)$ and define
\begin{align*}
    M_{n,k,m}' = Y' \Lambda_m Y'^* = \sum_{\alpha=1}^m \tau_\alpha Y_\alpha Y_\alpha^*.
\end{align*}
Then there exists a probability distribution function $F_c$, such that
\begin{align*}
    \lim_{n \to \infty} F^{M_{n,k,m}'} = F_c
\end{align*}
in probability.
Moreover, in the case that $\tau_\alpha \equiv 1$, the limiting distribution function $F_c$ is exactly the Mar\v{c}enko-Pastur law with density function \eqref{eq-MP law}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.450517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37a609db1be639022749b853744fac44ed075cc148a4d19c24d2eeda7bcb4d24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-kk of arXiv:2412.03067, 'Geodesic Trees and Exceptional Directions in FPP on Hyperbolic Groups'] [kapovich-kleiner]
