{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.992955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37abb4da066bd19a2a7b22f96806dcc6a425a6a4cda74a93dca8312313410ab0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-AbstractLDP of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Let ${\mathcal X }, {\mathcal Y }$ be two Polish spaces and pick $\rho\in{\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal X })$ and let $(x_i^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({n}})}}})_{i\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence in ${\mathcal X }$ such that $\frac 1n \sum_{i=1}^n\delta_{x_i^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({n}})}}}}$ converges weakly towards $\rho$ as $n\to\infty$. Let $\zeta\colon {\mathcal X }\times \sigma({\mathcal Y })\to[0,1]$ be a continuous Markov kernel from ${\mathcal X }$ to $ {\mathcal Y }$, where $\sigma({\mathcal Y })$ denotes the Borel sigma field on ${\mathcal Y }$. Furthermore, let $(Y_i^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({n}})}}})_{i\in[n]}$ have the distribution $\bigotimes_{i\in [n]} \zeta(x_i^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({n}})}}},\cdot)$. Then the empirical pair measure $\frac 1n\sum_{i=1}^n \delta_{(x_i^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({n}})}}},Y_i^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({n}})}}})}$ satisfies an LDP with rate function
\begin{equation}
{\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal X }\times{\mathcal Y })\ni q\mapsto \begin{cases} H_{{\mathcal X }\times{\mathcal Y }}(q\,|\,\rho\otimes \zeta)&\mbox{if }\pi_1(q)=\rho,\\
+\infty&\mbox{otherwise,}
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where $\pi_1$ is the canonical projection ${\mathcal X }\times{\mathcal Y }\to{\mathcal X }$, and $\pi_1(q)$ is the corresponding image measure. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

