{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.313693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37cf6b3b9072678838fbdcc7d1e9480a78ce336da84341e682808eb8e9dc41a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:p_moments of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] Let $\phi_0 \in L^p_{\mathcal{F}_0}(\Omega;  V)$. The unique solution of (eq:main of the paper) in the sense of (def-sol-H1 of the paper) satisfies, for every $p\ge 1$ 
