{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.321812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37df0ab31a7a538357ae38b8fe820fa81d37290e5d12e763f8fd720437fe8017","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-maximum-core-level-properties of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Suppose $\lambda = \omega(1)$ and $X_1 \,, \ldots \,, X_m \sim \mathsf{Pois(\lambda)}$ are $i.i.d.$ random variables, where $\exp\left(2\exp(\sqrt{\log \lambda})\right) < m < \exp(\lambda^{1-\epsilon})$ for some constant $\epsilon \in (0,1)$. Define
    \begin{align}{}
        S(\lambda,m) = \frac{ \sqrt{\lambda} \exp(\sqrt{\log\lambda}) }{ \sqrt{\log m} } \,,
    \end{align}
    then we have the following facts:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(1)] There exists $h_*(\lambda , m) \in [\lambda + \sqrt{1.9\lambda\log m}, \lambda + \sqrt{2.1\lambda\log m}]$ such that
        \begin{align}{}
            \mathbb P\left( |\max_{1\leq j \leq m}X_j - h_*(\lambda,m)| > S(\lambda,m) \right) \leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{\exp(\sqrt{\log \lambda})}{2}\right) \,.
        \end{align}
        \item[(2)] For all $v \in \mathbb Z_{\geq 0}$, we have
        \begin{align}
            \mathbb P\left( \#\{i:X_i=\max_{1\leq j \leq m}X_j - v\} \geq \exp\left( 10\max\left\{ v\sqrt{ \log m/\lambda}, \exp(\sqrt{\log \lambda}) \right\} \right) \right) \nonumber \\
            \leq 2\exp \left(-\frac{\exp(\sqrt{\log \lambda})}{2} \right) \,.  
        \end{align}
        \item[(3)] For all $v \in \mathbb Z$ such that $4S(\lambda,m) \leq v \leq \frac{1}{10} \sqrt{\lambda\log m}$, we have
        \begin{align}{}
            \mathbb P\left( \#\{i:X_i=\max_{1\leq j \leq m}X_j - v\} \leq \exp\left(\frac{v\sqrt{\log m}}{4\sqrt{\lambda}}\right) \right) \leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{\exp(\sqrt{\log \lambda})}{2}\right)\,.
        \end{align}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.228918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37df13a38ef162ef060ddca696fc36b5115500baf7e446670f528fa6eb4b9609","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $\varepsilon>0$. For all $s<t$, consider the set of points
