{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.787361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37f700b9029b944d104a9049ad7b856a04ead045373f71599b7fb6d9111ae588","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:master_equation_formal_revised of arXiv:2507.22577, 'A Mean-Field Theory of $\Theta$-Expectations'] The value function $u: [0,T] \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^k) \to \mathbb{R}$ is conjectured to formally solve the terminal-value problem:
\begin{multline} 
    \partial_t u(t,\mu) - \mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}\sim\mu}\left[ \scpr{ G\big(t, \tilde{y}, \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y}), \mu\big) }{ \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y}) } \right] \\
    + \frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{y}\sim\mu}\left[ \mathrm{Tr}\left( \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y}) \partial_\mu u(t,\mu,\tilde{y})^T D_y\big(\partial_\mu u(t, \mu, \tilde{y})\big) \right) \right] = 0,
\end{multline}
for $(t,\mu) \in [0,T) \times \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R}^k)$, with the terminal condition $u(T,\mu) = \int_{\mathbb{R}^k} \xi(y) \mathrm{d}\mu(y)$. The driver $G$ is given by $G(t,y,z,\mu) = \sup_{a \in \mathcal{U}_{g(\mu)}} F(t,y,z,a,\mu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.158415+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37fbc195a1a3c651099e87fcbe484b431b421c83cbc36c5939281e752a6c1b49","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Electric cancellation at zeroth order) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Assume the bootstrap bounds of \cref{sec:high-order}.  The electric work in
