{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.408369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37fd690500425fe38d943d87633963d26ca14b87526715a84c868eb11a60aef1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Pointwise Gaussian majorizing-measure bound) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] Assume \(0<R_\ast<\infty\) and \(\Phi_{\mu,\ast}<\infty\). There exists an absolute constant \(C>0\) such that, for every ambient prior \(\mu\in\Delta(T)\), every \(r_0>0\), every \(s_0\in(0,R_\ast]\), and every \(\delta\in(0,1)\), with probability at least \(1-\delta\),
