 \begin{equation}
  \cS_s(\Gamma(U)F)=U_s\cS_s(F).

 \end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Thus $\cS(F)$ is the unique minimal graded one-particle support of the
represented packet.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.260882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_381fd2d87cc64056c2db399459aca8a5d972be6f097703f48aaf6cfacedc20f2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: inherit local information of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] Suppose $\omega \in \mathcal{A}$ and $\overline{\omega} \in \overline{\Psi}(\omega)$. 
