{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.588676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3828352bf53bf715d56a3c2f85def48677a87c57080093298e4e34c748f0009c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] [AGS08]
    Let $(S,d)$ be a metric space and $F:S\to (-\infty,\infty]$ measurable. Let $D(F):=\{s\in S\mid F(s)<\infty\}$ be the domain of $F$. The local slope $ \left\lvert\partial  F\right\rvert$ of $F$ is defined by \begin{align*}
