{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.368180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3833e2ea854e16455567d7445def845727858eb7c8d24119fe20bc7e5cfc5677","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 8 of arXiv:2606.03122, 'Propagation of support for super-Brownian motion with general branching mechanism'] Suppose that $X$ is a super-Brownian motion with branching mechanism $\Psi$ satisfying Condition \ref{con_localize}. Let $x_0\in\mathbb R^d$, $R>0$, and let $L>0$ be such that
$$
\overline{B(x_0,R)}\subset \overline{B(0,L)}.
$$
Then there exists a positive constant $C(d)$ which depends only on the dimension $d$, such that for any $0\leq\rho_{x_0}(\mu)<R_1 < R$ and $t\in\left(0,\dfrac{(R_1-\rho_{x_0}(\mu))^2}{d}\right)$, we have
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\mathbb{P}_{\mu}\{\exists s\leq t,X_s(\overline{B(x_0,R)}^c)>0\}\\
&\quad\leq \mu(1)\cdot u_{R,\Phi_L}(R_1)\cdot C(d) \left(\dfrac{R_1-\rho_{x_0}(\mu)}{\sqrt{t}}\right)^{d-2}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(R_1-\rho_{x_0}(\mu))^2}{2t}\right)\\
&\quad\leq \mu(1)\cdot G_{\Phi_L}^{-1}(R-R_1)\cdot C(d) \left(\dfrac{R_1-\rho_{x_0}(\mu)}{\sqrt{t}}\right)^{d-2}\exp\left(-\dfrac{(R_1-\rho_{x_0}(\mu))^2}{2t}\right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
In particular, if $\mu=a\cdot\delta_{x_0}$ and $L$ satisfies $\overline{B(x_0,R)}\subset \overline{B(0,L)}$, then the same estimate holds with $\rho_{x_0}(\mu)=0$ and $\mu(1)=a$.","status":"unverified"}

