{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.802141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_383d6ea97ef6eea413ca8dc4084f6ddeeb138b09011418676763925bd000b36f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition P:CQCLT of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] [bour_spilio_2025]
Let $T>0$ be fixed, $\theta_t^\varepsilon \triangleq \frac{X_t^\varepsilon-\bar{X}_t}{\sqrt{\varepsilon}}$ and $N \sim \mathscr{N}(0, \sigma_t^2).$ For sufficiently small $\varepsilon$ and $\eta,$ and $0<\xi < \frac{1}{2},$ there exists a time-dependent positive constant $C$ such that
