{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.994565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3868e944a53a26887add4a3c67a34ad318bcbf9c9656b76b06d80d992ea01a23","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma local-w of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Suppose  $d\ge 3$ and    $q>1$ satisfies the condition (equation q of the paper).
Let $(u, \phi )\in W_0^{1, 2} (E_1; \mathbb{C}^d) \times L^2(E_1; \mathbb{C})$ be a weak solution of
\begin{equation}
\left\{
\aligned
-\Delta u +\nabla \phi  & =F +\text{\rm div} (f) & \quad & \text{ in } E_1,\\
\text{\rm div}(u) & = 0 & \quad & \text{ in } E_1,\\
u & =0 & \quad  & \text{ on } \partial E_1.
\endaligned
\right.
\end{equation}
 Then
\begin{equation}
\| \nabla u \|_{L^q(E_1)} + \| u \|_{L^q(E_1)}
\le C \left\{ \| F \|_{L^q(E_1)} + \| f\|_{L^q(E_1)} \right\}.
\end{equation}
Moreover,  for any  $0<\rho <1/2$, 
\begin{equation}
\aligned
\left(\fint_{E_\rho } |\nabla u|^q \right)^{1/q}
 & \le \frac{C}{\rho}
\left(\fint_{E_{2\rho} } |u|^q\right)^{1/q}
+ C \rho  \left(\fint_{E_{2\rho} } |F|^q\right)^{1/q}
+ C \left(\fint_{E_{2\rho} } |f|^q\right)^{1/q}.
\endaligned
\end{equation}
The constant  $C>0$ depends only on $d$, $q$ and $M$.","status":"unverified"}

