{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.582190+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_387f185cd18b131b117cf71267df304b870fc9c801de2b436c68609093173990","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm intro1 of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1$ be the laws of two stationary point processes with unit intensity and $\mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_i)<\infty$ for $i=0,1.$ Then, there is an interpolation $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{t\in[0,1]}$ between $\mathsf{P}_0$ and $\mathsf{P}_1$ and a coupling $ \mathsf{Q}^0$ between the Palm measures of $\mathsf{P}_0$ and $\mathsf{P}_1$ such that 
\begin{align}  
    \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t})\leq  (1-t)\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{0})+t\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{1})-\frac{(1-t)t\beta}{2}\int \sum_{(0,0)\neq (x,y)\in \bar\xi} (x-y)^2\inf_{z\in [x,y]}f(\left\lvertz\right\rvert) \mathsf{Q}^0(d\bar\xi),
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.383874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_387f69f733044dbda43b3015208cb76650c75caa959262fa0dd977119d770d9e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 27 of arXiv:2609.03243, 'Weighted Ces\`aro type operators on the weighted Bergman spaces in the unit ball'] Let $\alpha>-1$, $\beta>0$ and $\mu$ be a positive Borel measure on $[0,1)$. Then $\mathcal C_{\mu,\beta}^{\xi}: A_{\alpha}^1(\mathbb{B}_n)\to H^{\infty}(\mathbb{B}_n)$ is bounded if and only if $\mu$ is a $(\beta+n+1+\alpha)$-Carleson measure on $[0,1)$, that is
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{r\in [0,1)}\frac{\hat{\mu}(r)}{(1-r)^{\beta+n+1+\alpha}}<\infty.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.408218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_388062a52899ddb8990aab19df81ad9135f94455a9907aa57a01b34db7df4761","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Lemma 3.4 in \cite{pierre2010global}) of arXiv:2604.06645, '2604.06645'] Let $v_1,v_2$ be regular functions in the sense of \eqref{eq: system classical solution} satisfying
\begin{equation}
\partial_t v_1 - d_1 \Delta v_1 + \theta_1 v_1 
\le \theta_2 \partial_t v_2 - d_2 \Delta v_2 + \theta_3 v_2 + H
\end{equation}
together with the same constant Neumann or Dirichlet boundary conditions for $v_1,v_2$, where $\theta_i \in \mathbb{R}$ and $H \in L^p(Q_T)$, $H \ge 0$. Then, there exists $C>0$ depending on $p,d_1,d_2$ and the domain $D$ such that, for all $1<p<\infty$, $t\in (0,T]$, 
and with bounded initial data,
\begin{equation}
\|v_1^+\|_{L^p(Q_t)} \leq C \left( \|v_2\|_{L^p(Q_t)} + \|v_1(0)\|_{L^p(D)} + |\theta_2|  \|v_2(0)\|_{L^p(D)} + \int_0^t \|H(s)\|_{L^p(D)} ds \right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.041307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3881b32eb4e6bbcad867ad6da8f6a51f3cc0d324fe6be8534ccdbb64f3e2a6ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 1 of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $\mathcal H_m$ be a Euclidean class with exponent $V$. Then for any $p \geq 2$ and $1 \leq j \leq m$,   
    \begin{align*}
    \left(\mathbb E \sup_{h \in \mathcal{H}_m} \lvert V_{N,j}(h) \rvert^p \right)^{1/p}  \leq C^j\max\left\{B_1(p,j), B_2(p,j)\right\} 
\end{align*}
where 
    \begin{align*}
    B_1(p,j) &= p^{j/2}\left(\frac{m}{j}\right)^{j/2} D(p,j)\,,
    \\
    B_2(p,j) &= 
    \left(C_1V \left[j\log\left(\frac{C_2m}{j}\right) \bigvee \log\left( \frac{e}{\Sigma_{\mathcal H_m}}\right)\right]\right)^{j/2} D(p,j).
    \end{align*}
    Moreover, if $p\geq 4V$, then $B_2(p,j)$ can be chosen as
    \[
    B_2(p,j) = ( pj)^{j/2} e^{-pj/V}.
    \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.891141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3883d235ef3c1dc376abd1d209caa39e4a9987fda907a4ea130ed5b67ee202f6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition ABGSymp of arXiv:2607.19037, 'Semiclassical analysis for Yang--Mills \\ random connections on compact surfaces'] Given two tangent vectors 
  \[v=(v_a)_{a\in  \mathsf{Crit}(f)_1}, w=(w_a)_{a\in  \mathsf{Crit}(f)_1} \in T_{(g_a)_{a\in  \mathsf{Crit}(f)_1}}\mathcal{M}_g,\] 
  the symplectic form writes
\begin{equation}
\omega\left(v,w\right)=\sum_{a,b\in \mathsf{Crit}(f)_1} \mathrm{Tr}\Big(  \mathrm{d}\log\left(g_a \right)\left(v_ag_a \right)\  \mathrm{d}\log\left(g_b \right)(v_bg_b)   \Big)  \Big( [W^u(a)]\cap [W^u(b)] \Big),
\end{equation}
where $[W^u(a)]\cap [W^u(b)] \in \mathbb{Z} $ denotes the oriented intersection numbers of the two cycles $[W^u(a)]$,  $ [W^u(b)]$ viewed as elements in $H_1(\Sigma,\mathbb{Z})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.841723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3883fcf9be7232ebc17667b49290acc46c7bef483f2a8b42fb430ee6ff233a19","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:35 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There exists a constant $C$ such that for all $n$ and all $j,k,i,\Delta\in [\![-2\varepsilon n^{1/3},2\varepsilon n^{1/3}]\!]$ additionally satisfying $i\in A_{\Delta}$, we have 
