  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.950734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38862cbcfaf2043db834936f3c9e72de69956ef8147796c188c4e1c7941c6325","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:rescaling of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $a,b,c>0$ and let $X$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper). Then 
	\begin{equation*}
		\tilde{X}_t(x) = cX_{at}(bx), \quad t \geq 0, \quad x\in \mathbb{R}, 
	\end{equation*}
	is a solution to 
	\begin{equation*}
	\begin{split}
		d_t \tilde{X}_t(x) &= \frac{a}{2b^2}\Delta\tilde{X}_t(x) + ach_c(\tilde{X}_t(x)) + \frac{c^{1/2}a^{1/2}}{b^{1/2}}\sqrt{\tilde{X}_t(x)} \dot{W}(t,x),\quad x\in \mathbb{R} ,t\geq 0,\\
	\tilde{X}_0(x) &= cX_0(bx), \quad x\in \mathbb{R} ,
		\end{split}
	\end{equation*}
	where $h_c(x) = h(c^{-1}x)$ for $x\in \mathbb{R}$.","status":"unverified"}

