{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.577660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_388f8d6a1a63c4e5089a8f36799299af657b0fbac04020ca65e393ac0b3f8123","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 39 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $\beta\geq 0$. Then, for every $x,y,z,t\in \mathbb Z^d$, one has
