{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.361276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3897d6a41a19b38f14ac8ab61c53654454d8d16fcfac96bbaaec8e8e9dc3f4bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Change of variables) of arXiv:2604.21389, 'Existence and uniqueness for \\ singular stochastic differential equations \\ with piecewi'] Let Hypothesis~\hypref{hyp:nu} and assume that $b$ and $\sigma$ are measurable and locally bounded.

For every $(X,B)$, weak non-explosive solution to~\eqref{eqn:SDE_general}, let $I$ denote the smallest interval such that~$X_t\in I$ for all $t\geq 0$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.. Then $(\Phi_\nu(X),B)$ is a weak non-explosive solution to the classical SDE
\begin{equation}
Y_t=\Phi_\nu(x_0)+\int_0^t \widetilde b(Y_s)\,\vd s+\int_0^t \widetilde\sigma(Y_s)\,\vd B_s,
\qquad t\ge 0.
\end{equation}
Moreover $\Phi_\nu(X)\in J$ for all $t\geq 0$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s..

Conversely, if $(Y,B)$ is a weak non-explosive solution to~\eqref{eq:SDE_no_nu} and $Y_t\in J$ for all $t\geq 0$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s., then $(\Psi_\nu(Y),B)$ is a weak non-explosive solution to~\eqref{eqn:SDE_general} and $\Psi_\nu(Y_t)\in I$ for all $t\geq 0$ $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.029133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3899d7e7e43fed52c93d1c33ea019f4427222d7b624305aa8712621f00c1d04c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (Shifted SSL) of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] Let $(A_{s,t}: (s,t)\in \overline{[S,T]}^2_\leq)$ be a family of random variables in $L^2(\Omega)$ such that $A_{s,t}$ is $\cF_t$-measurable. Suppose that there exist positive constants $C_1$, $C_2$, $\eps_1$, $\eps_2$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \| A_{s,t}\|_{L^2(\Omega)} & \leq C_1 |t-s|^{\frac{1}{2}+\eps_1} & \forall\, (s,t)\in \overline{[S,T]}^2_\leq, \\
        \| \E_{s-(t-s)} (A_{s,t}-A_{s,u}-A_{u,v})\|_{L^2(\Omega)} & \leq C_2 |t-s|^{1+\eps_2} & \forall\, (s,u,t)\in \overline{[S,T]}^3_\leq.
    \end{align}
    Then there exist finite constants $K_1$, $K_2$, only depending on $\eps_1$, $\eps_2$, and a unique (up to modification) $(\cF_t)_t$-adapted process $\mathcal{A}$ such that $\mathcal{A}_S=0$ and the following bounds hold:
    \begin{align}
        \| \mathcal{A}_t-\mathcal{A}_s- A_{s,t}\|_{L^2(\Omega)} & \leq K_1 C_1 |t-s|^{\frac{1}{2}+\eps_1} + K_2 C_2 |t-s|^{1+\eps_2} & \forall\, (s,t)\in \overline{[S,T]}^2_\leq, \\
        \| \E_{s-(t-s)} (\mathcal{A}_t-\mathcal{A}_s- A_{s,t})\|_{L^2(\Omega)} & \leq K_2 C_2 |t-s|^{1+\eps_2} & \forall\, (s,u,t)\in \overline{[S,T]}^2_\leq,\\
        \| \mathcal{A}_t-\mathcal{A}_s\|_{L^2(\Omega)} & \leq K_1 C_1 |t-s|^{\frac{1}{2}+\eps_1} + K_2 C_2 |t-s|^{1+\eps_2} & \forall\, (s,t)\in [S,T]^2_\leq .
    \end{align}
    Moreover the increments $\mathcal{A}_t-\mathcal{A}_s$ are the unique limits in $L^2(\Omega)$ of Riemann sums over dyadic partition of $A_{s,t}$ (see~\cite[eq. (2.9)]{GalGer2025} for the exact definition). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

