{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.464357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38b5ca2ccb1c6252d790a061b15e372f14a7e680a32b838c32ec23b7b439ae2b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2606.28793, 'Randomized second order Riesz projections on the Hamming cube'] Fix $1<p<\infty$, $a\geq0$, and $C<\infty$.  Let $X$ be a Banach space.  Assume that, for every $M,n,d\geq1$ and every
$F\in\mathcal P_d(\Omega_n;\ell_2^M(X))$,
\begin{equation}

 \|G^{\mathrm{ord}}_{1,\ell_2^M(X)}F\|_{L^p(\Omega_n)}
 \leq Cd^a\|F\|_{L^p(\Omega_n;\ell_2^M(X))}.
\end{equation}
Then, for every integer $k\geq1$, every $n,d\geq1$, and every $f\in\mathcal P_d(\Omega_n;X)$,
\[
