{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.106843+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38be283534d3ef0d22d0513d00bb6765313a4e9504479b74ac049812011b038d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LM32 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $X$ be a Borel right process properly associated with the quasi-regular Dirichlet form $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ on $L^2(E,m)$.  Then the following statements hold:
