{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.474234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38f3ee0a671c794a339957c6156f00d9ef9229f1c1db317546b676b16b419872","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma4 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A7 of the paper) hold and let $\varphi$ be an $h$-dependent descendant characteristic, for some $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, satisfying (C1 of the paper)-(C2 of the paper). Then, we have the following:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\textbf{\roman*})]
