{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.598953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38f57975cc288b491f13b8c91fc3b671f9beeb3254d562301e8cd837f0da84b7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 28 of arXiv:2608.16144, 'Central limit theorem in R\'enyi divergence for lattice random variables'] Let $X_{1},\cdots,X_{n}$ be independent copies of a lattice random variable $X$ with mean zero, variance one and maximal span $h>0$. Let $S_n=(X_{1}+\cdots+X_{n})/\sqrt{n}$ the normalized sum.
Let $\alpha >1$ and $\beta=\alpha/(\alpha-1)$. Then $D_{\alpha}(S_{n}||Z_{n})\to 0$ as $n \to \infty$ if and only if 
