{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.718629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_38ff7f527c566de1cf56355b34019e4afac3097a687399f6367fd58e71c24440","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:theRGthm of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $\eta \in [0,1/2)$,  $d\ge d_{c,u}$ and $g >0$ be sufficiently small,  $(\vec{\textbf{a}}_{c,k})_{k \in \N \cup \{\infty\}}$ be as in Theorem~(thm:theStableManifold of the paper) and $\nu_c$ be as in Definition~(defi:nuc of the paper).
There exist convergent sequences $(\epsilon_k, \epsilon'_k )_{k \in \N \cup \{\infty \}}$ such that $\epsilon_k \rightarrow 0$,  $\epsilon'_k \downarrow 0$ and satisfy the following.
On $\Lambda = \Lambda_N$,  consider $\vec{\textbf{a}}$ given by $\textbf{a}^{(\km)} = \textbf{a}_{c,k}^{(\km)}$ for each $\km \in \kA_1$,  $\textbf{a}^{(\emptyset)} = \epsilon'_k$ and
\begin{align}
	Z_{N,\varnothing} (\varphi) = \E_{w_N} \theta \big[ \exp (-V_{0,\varnothing} (\Lambda,\varphi)) \big] 
\end{align}
where $V_0$ is defined using $\nu_0^{(\emptyset)} = \nu_c + \epsilon_k$, 
$\nu_0^{(\km_1)} = - \textbf{a}^{(\km_1)}_{c,k}$ for $\km_1 \in \ko_{2,\nabla}$,
$g^{(\emptyset)}_0 = g$ and $g^{(\km_2)} = 0$ for $\km_2 \in \ko_{4,\nabla}$.  Then
\begin{align}
	Z_{N,\varnothing} (\varphi) = e^{-u_{N,\varnothing} ( \Lambda_N )} \left( I_{N,\varnothing} (\varphi) + K_{N,\varnothing} \right) 
\end{align}
for some $u_{N,\varnothing} (\Lambda_N) \in \R$,  $V_{N,\varnothing} \in \tilde\cD_N^{(0)}$ and $K_{N,\varnothing} \in M \cK_N$ where $I_{N,\varnothing} = \cI_N (V_{N,\varnothing})$ is as in Section~(sec:WIcoords of the paper) and $M >0$ is a (possibly $L$-dependent) constant.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.046585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_390326869779e2fe89e36a091bc986b753586c9510c85ccb7e03885a2cce4d34","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 (Proper graph coloring) of arXiv:2606.31936, 'Coupling and Maximal Inequalities for Graph-Dependent Empirical Processes'] A proper $(r,K)$-coloring of
	$\mathcal P_{N_n,M}$, denoted by
	$\mathcal C_{r,K}[\mathcal P_{N_n,M}]$, is a partition $\left\{
		C_1,\ldots, C_K
		\right\}$  	of $[M]$ such that, for every $k\in[K]$,
	\begin{align}
		m,m'\in C_k,
		\qquad
		m\neq m'
		\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
		d_n(B_m,B_{m'})
		>
		r.

	\end{align}


	The minimal number of colors is
	\begin{align}
		K_{r} : = K\left(
		r,
		\mathcal P_{N_n,M}
		\right)
		:=
		\min\left\{
		K\in\mathbb N:
		\mathcal P_{N_n,M}
		\text{ admits a proper }(r,K)\text{-coloring}
		\right\}.

	\end{align}
	We refer to
	$K(r,\mathcal P_{N_n,M})$ as the
	$r$-chromatic number of the block partition. Under this choice, we use 	$\mathcal C_{r}[\mathcal P_{N_n,M}]$ to denote the proper coloring.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.915053+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3904756fb4e5846538334a0f57d100482822f94cdd93185be5dafb6c77acd320","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.01419, 'A model of opinion dynamics evolving via a preferential attachment mechanism involving mul'] For the model described in \S\ref{subsec:model_fixed_sample_size}, the sequence $\{(n^{-1}A_{n},n^{-1}B_{n},n^{-1}C_{n})\}$ converges almost surely to a compact, connected, internally chain transitive invariant set, contained in $\mathcal{S}$, corresponding to the autonomous ODE
