= \frac1{c_\lambda}\varphi(y)
= g_\lambda(0,y). 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.500503+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_390d6733f3461f6ab50ca091482418c160759869e2ce4971780448d0d3e7b59d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 12 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] For \(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_N\in\C\), the Vandermonde determinant is
