{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.586222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3933eaecd268cbe11b2f0f2c39d386861e7b891036a5e9362679d701f48a3a07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem general of arXiv:2602.18784, 'A note on the cooperative two-type SIR processes on Galton-Watson trees'] Consider the two-type SIR process on $GW (p)$ with parameters $\alpha_i$, $\beta_i$, $\mu_i$, $i=1,2$. At time $0$, the root is infected with both disease $A$ and disease $B$. All other vertices are susceptible to both $A$ and $B$. Let $m$ be the mean of $p$. If
