{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.334253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3935f1a9a523b6a4828ba4ddb65289a3ecccf5a01aea3e894c72fb6af0b6f31f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a locally finite weighted graph and let $\psi\in C^{1}(0,+\infty)$. Then for any function $0<f\in\mathbb{R}^{V}$, 
