{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.965019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_393aa2a62c9ff4ad286a9b7628c65769cb55e88e8f47528c520e6853f5caa4c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2607.28614, 'Tampered Memory Elephant Random Walk on one-dimensional integer lattice'] Let $S_n$ be a TMERW. Let the collection of sets $\DD$ be a nested sequence generated according to an arithmetic progression, i.e for some fixed $\mu, k \in \bN$, $\PP \left(\tau =k\right)=\PP \left(\sigma =\mu-k\right)=1$. 
Write $ s^*=\frac{(2\lambda-1)(\mu-k)}{\mu - (2p-1)k}$. Let $\Sigma$ and $\widetilde{\Sigma}$ be two positive constants that depend on the parameters. Then,
\begin{enumerate}[i.]
\item If $k> \frac{\mu}{2}$, then there exists a phase transition into a diffusive, critical and superdiffusive behaviour characterised below:
\begin{enumerate}[a.]
\item When $p<\frac{1}{2}+\frac{\mu}{4k}$, then 
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n -n s^*}{\sqrt{n}}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N (0, \Sigma),
\end{equation}
\item When $p= \frac{1}{2}+\frac{\mu}{4k}$, then 
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n- n s^* }{\sqrt{n \log n}}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N (0,\widetilde \Sigma),
\end{equation}
\item When $\frac{1}{2}+\frac{\mu}{4k} <p \le 1$, then there exists a random variable $\xi$, such that, 
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n- n s^* }{n^{1-\rho^*}} \longrightarrow \xi, \text{ a.s.},
\end{equation}
where $\rho^*= 1- (2p-1)\frac{k}{\mu}$. 
\end{enumerate}
\item For $k =\frac{\mu}{2}$, if  $0 \le p <1$, 
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n -n s^*}{\sqrt{n}}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N (0, \Sigma),
\end{equation}
And when $p=1$,
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n -n s^*}{\sqrt{n \log n}}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N (0, \widetilde\Sigma),
\end{equation}
\item If $k < \frac{\mu}{2}$, and $0 \le p \le 1$, then 
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n -n s^*}{\sqrt{n}}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N (0, \Sigma).
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.743469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_393f5d25eeb60f1d2f7a60a5d68c28198901aeab6f176b1a13c212c17dd13d00","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 (Quasi-geodesics) of arXiv:2607.08632, 'Uncountably many extremal Series--Sinai states for the Ising model on Lobachevsky lattices'] Let \(k \ge 1\) and \(c \ge 0\) and let \(I\) be a \emph{closed} interval of \(\mathbb{R}\).
    A \emph{\((k, c)\)-quasigeodesic curve} \(f\) of \(X\) is an application \(f:I\to X\) such that for all \(s,\,t \in I\), we have
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{k} \abs{t-s} - c
        \le 
        \distance{f(s)}{f(t)}
        \le 
        k \abs{t-s} + c.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, if \(I\) is \emph{bounded} (\resp~\(I = \mathbb{R}\)), we say that \(f\) is a \emph{\((k, c)\)-quasigeodesic segment} (\resp~\emph{complete \((k, c)\)-quasi-geodesic}).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.327472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_394252fd5e1935c1e02a3fcf221915ede21a80b9323865617cda704b037fe949","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:intersection of arXiv:2606.16259, 'Super-Arrhenius relaxation of the triangular plaquette model in any dimension'] \leavevmode
