\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.027362+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3956f4fa945343ce5e6874a549afebdc3d30a2056a94a9aa8f4455b9ecd2a23b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor  t LIL of arXiv:2607.28167, 'Temporal properties of the stochastic fractional heat equation with rough dependence in sp'] Assume  Condition (cond A of the paper) holds.
    Choose and fix $t>0$ and $x\in \mathbb R$.  Then with probability one,
    \begin{itemize}
    \item[(a).] (Khinchin's law of the iterated logarithm)
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
    \limsup_{\varepsilon \to 0}\frac{|u(t+\varepsilon, x)-u(t, x)|}{\varepsilon^{\widetilde{H}/2}\sqrt{2 \log\log(1/\varepsilon)}}= \kappa |\sigma(u(t, x))|,
    \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    where $\widetilde{H}=\frac{\alpha+2H-2}{\alpha}$.
        \item[(b).]  (Chung's law  of the iterated logarithm)
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
    \liminf_{\varepsilon \to 0}\sup_{0\le r\le \varepsilon}\frac{|u(t+r, x)-u(t, x)|}{(\varepsilon/  \log\log(1/\varepsilon))^{\widetilde{H}/2}}=  \kappa\lambda_{\widetilde{H}}^{\widetilde{H}/2} |\sigma(u(t, x))|,
    \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    where $\lambda_{\widetilde{H}}$ is the small ball  constant of a fBm with index $\widetilde{H}/2$ (see, e.g., [LS01*]).
  \end{itemize}
  If   $ \beta_0>\frac{\alpha+2H-2}{\alpha}$ in Condition (cond A of the paper), then both results also hold at $t=0$ with $\kappa$ in (equation eq constant 1 of the paper) replaced by   \begin{align}
             \widetilde\kappa= \left( \frac{ \Gamma(2\widetilde{H}) }{2^{1-\widetilde{H}} \Gamma(\widetilde{H})}\right)^{1/2}.
             \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

