{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.239417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3963626c33799d25cc138ac9f4bece78afadd78631b84b28c5bcf7d6180cf692","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: good paths prop of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For $F \subset \mathbb{T}_N$, we say a path collection $\mathcal{A} \subset \Omega_{T_3}$ is $(F,\varepsilon,M_0)$-good if for all $\omega \in \mathcal{A}$,
    \begin{subequations}

        \begin{gather}

            \mathbb{T}_N \setminus F \subset \omega[0,T_3];\\

            \boldsymbol{r}_{x}(\omega) \leq l_N \text{ for all } x \in  \mathcal{L}_{F}^{\beta_N}(\omega);\\

            2d\cdot\mathsf{Mdist}\big(\mathcal{L}_{F}^{\beta_N}(\omega)\big)\leq J(F,M_0),
        \end{gather}
    \end{subequations}
    where 
\begin{equation}

        J(F,M_0)\overset{\rm def.}{=} 2d M_0\cdot|F|N^{-d\gamma}.
    \end{equation}
    For an event $A\in \mathcal{F}_{T_3}$, we also say $A$ is $(F,\varepsilon,M_0)$-good if the path collection $\mathcal{A}=\pi_{T_3}(A)$ (see (equation eq: paths correspond to event of the paper) for definition) is $(F,\varepsilon,M_0)$-good.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.353974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39648128fe4e31cb3c99946053df7230d0872bf20348a1569560b4e1a64d856a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm eq:variance-CR-introduction of arXiv:2608.10215, 'The variance of the Pitman--Yor process: a Cifarelli--Regazzini identity and inversion for'] Let $\alpha \in (0,1)$ and $\theta > 1/2$ be fixed constants. Let $\mathsf{G}$ be a probability measure on $[0, +\infty)$ such that $\int_0^{+\infty} x^{2\alpha} \mathsf{G}(\mathrm{d} x) < +\infty$. 
Then, for any $t \ge 0$, there holds
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}_{(\alpha, \theta)}\left[ \left(\frac{1}{1 + t\mathfrak{V}}\right)^{\theta - 1/2} \right] &= \int_0^1 {\mathcal B eta}(\mathrm{d}\rho; 1/2, \theta - 1/2) \times \nonumber \\
& \times \frac 12 \left\{ \Psi_+(\sqrt{t \rho (1 - \rho)}, t(1 - \rho)) + \Psi_-(\sqrt{t \rho (1 -\rho)}, t(1 - \rho)) \right\} \mathrm{d} \rho 
\end{align}
with
\[
\Psi_{\pm}(u, v) := \left\{ \int_0^{+\infty} [1 \pm 2ux + vx^2]^{\alpha} \mathsf{G}(\mathrm{d} x) \right\}^{-\theta/\alpha} \ .
\]
Moreover, if $\theta > 3/2$, one has
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}_{(\alpha, \theta)}\left[\frac{1}{z + \mathfrak{V}}\right] &= \int_0^{+\infty} \frac{f_{\mathfrak{V}}(x)}{z + x} \mathrm{d} x \nonumber \\
&= z^{\theta - 1} \int_{\Delta_2} {\mathcal D ir}(\mathrm{d}\xi \mathrm{d}\eta; 1/2, 1, \theta - 3/2) 
\left[\frac{\Psi_+(z; \xi, \eta) + \Phi_-(z; \xi, \eta) }{2} \right] 
\end{align}
with
\begin{displaymath}
\Phi_{\pm}(z; \xi, \eta) := \left\{\int_0^{+\infty}  [z \pm 2\sqrt{z \xi\eta} x + \eta x^2]^{\alpha} \mathsf{G}(\mathrm{d} x) \right\}^{-\theta/\alpha}\ . 
\end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

