{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.820325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_398c4766e87e84e34346cae6e4690c4264014de826453442689afa2f182c3edd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop approx Identity Limit of arXiv:2607.17393, 'Optimal Covariance Estimates for Schr\"odinger Semigroups with White Noise in $d=1,2$'] Fix $d\in\{1,2\}$, $x,y\in\mathbb{R}^d$ and $s,t>0$. Then, 
