{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.803267+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39932dd6cf6fc3cc819e680b6557c5bb81b4d468feb9b71debcbb7ed48a237e6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:Second-der-X-W1-W2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the process $D_{r_1,r_2}^{W_1 W_2} X_t^\varepsilon$ be the solution of equation (equation E:Second-der-X-W1-W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2$, there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
