{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.605798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39bd9a38c0d2d086f45e3f8f7d129bce07598908c2e6a3740de331fe4d415c74","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theoremi thm_main_directed of arXiv:2604.04672, 'Connected components and topological ends of stationary planar forests'] Assume additionally that with probability one, $G$ is oriented with out-degree $1$, non-empty and all directed infinite path $(\pi_n)_{n\geq0}$ in $G$ satisfies $\lim_{n\to\infty}\pi_n\cdot e_2=+\infty$, where $e_2\coloneqq (0,1)\in\mathbb{R}^2$ and $\cdot$ denotes the standard scalar product. Then, exactly one of the following holds almost surely:
