{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.712221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39e1071f23992c703e3826b0e1118f9ee70f1b02a1770f46bca9b45735ca97b5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Random normal is non-almost-constant of arXiv:2604.11761, 'The smallest singular value of signed random combinatorial matrices'] Let $\delta, \rho \in \left(0, \frac{1}{12}\right)$. Assume that $n$ is sufficiently large.
