{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.048841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39e42d6003878ca7963402494dae03ad252f64fcf794e3798642677bd27a7745","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mypropo 5 of arXiv:2607.00495, 'Rank deficiency of Bernoulli random matrices for growing corank'] For any $p \in (0,1/2]$ and $\varepsilon >0$, there exist $n_{\ref{Compressible subspace}}$ and $\tau_{\ref{Compressible subspace}}$ depending only on $p$ and $\varepsilon$ such that for all $n \ge n_{\ref{Compressible subspace}}$ and $\log{n} \ge k \ge 1$. Define an event $\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{comp}}$ as the event that there exist orthonormal vectors $x_{1},\dots,x_{k} \subset \ker{B}$ satisfying $x_{1},\dots,x_{k} \in  \mathrm{Comp}_{n}(\tau_{\ref{Compressible subspace}}^{2},\tau_{\ref{Compressible subspace}}^{4})$. Then
