{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.321715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a07e4b582ae7416ad9270d222a77ca7bf6fae61970845d8dc7383e54c1d4e9a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:weak-solutions of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] We say that $f$ is a weak solution to~(equation e.LFD of the paper) on $(0,T)\times\mathbb T^3\times\mathbb R^3$ for $0 < T \le \infty$ if, for some $m>2$,
