{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.893729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a262d3c49704dba7eacca56a1820aee9531961545bdb88135faf700d0db309b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 ($(2\times\ell)$-periodic weights) of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let $\{\alpha_i\}^\ell_{i=1}$ and $\{\beta_i\}^\ell_{i=1}$ be two sets of positive real numbers satisfying
