{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.168039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a4e0343f9d5b8649eb22cd70a5b2f412f5140dd49d3c7fc3b892c652709e38f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 ($\pi$-Infinitesimal Generator) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let $\{R_{t,s}\}_{(t,s) \in \Delta}$ be a $\pi$-continuous evolution family. For any $t \in [0,T)$, the $\pi$-infinitesimal generator $\mathcal{L}_t \colon \mathrm{Dom}(\mathcal{L}_t) \subset \mathcal{B}_m(H) \to \mathcal{B}_m(H)$ is defined by:
