{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.935852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a64e26b2c3932faef6ed3174c273ac0d5bbd9b9bc6fc4ad3532373d14c773d2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 (cf.\ {\cite[Proposition 3.5) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {MSS23}}] 
    Let
    \begin{align*}
        a_1 &:= a_1(\Delta, b) = F^{-1}_\mu \big(\frac{1}{\Delta -1} - \frac{p^*}{2} \big), \\
        a_2 &:= a_2(\Delta, b) = F^{-1}_\mu(1 - p^*).
    \end{align*}
