{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.252272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a6f4b93657b63dddd2b932adab748dfe03c667921e2b981b977f7bd0376e57f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.04080, 'On radicals in differential invariants: \\ global theory vs moving frames'] For algebraic subgroup $\Gamma\subset G$, an unmixed\footnote{That means, all componenets have the same dimensions.} 
