{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.019854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a7ea0930144a24ddd666c342de2524b7d8010c4bd9a301db1bbfa5bf041402e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Problem Problem1 of arXiv:2609.03762, '\vspace*{-2cm} Projected Riemannian Gradient Descent for the Bures--Wasserstein Barycenter'] Let $(R_i)_{i \in [n]} \subseteq \mathrm{PD}(d)$ be a collection of $d \times d$ positive definite matrices and $w := (w_1, \ldots, w_n)$ an associated probability vector.
    Compute the \textit{BW barycenter} of the distribution $(R_i, w_i)_{i \in [n]}$:
    \begin{equation}
        S_\star := \argmin_{S \in \mathrm{PD}(d)} \frac12 \sum_{i=1}^n w_i \mathrm{B}(R_i, S) \equiv \argmin_{S \in \mathrm{PD}(d)} f_1(S).
    \end{equation}
    Throughout, the ensemble is contained in a \textit{spectral interval}: $\alpha I \leq R_i \leq \beta I$ for all ${i \in [n]}$, for some $0 < \alpha \leq \beta < \infty$, and the ratio $\kappa := \beta/\alpha$ is the ensemble's condition number. For a finite ensemble one may take $\alpha = \min_{{i \in [n]}} \lambda_{\min}(R_i)$ and $\beta = \max_{{i \in [n]}} \lambda_{\max}(R_i)$, and the same containment covers distributions of infinite support. (Stated as a problem by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.651212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a8079e8d61ebb4cf36a4daf6fb2fec14229afc54b8295ceae9cb24e1469afa2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop bdy-expect of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$. Let $D$ be a bounded, simply connected domain. Fix any $A\subseteq \partial D$ to be a (deterministic) closed subset of the boundary such that $\dim_M(A)<2-\alpha^2/2$. 
    For any continuous, bounded  function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$,
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n\to\infty}\mathbb E[(\field{e^{i\alpha\phi}}, f\1_{[A]_n})]=0.
    \end{equation}
    As a consequence,
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n\to\infty}(\field{e^{i\alpha\phi}}, f\1_{[A]_n})=0,
    \end{equation}
    where the limit is almost sure and in $L^2(\mathbb P)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.724594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a80aba54e28cec7adeac9db0d1f7d0b7f7a55f5d340a7efedbf95c6c7a16858","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:vd-l2-separated-side-collars of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] The constants $c_{\mathrm{fs}},\ell_{\mathrm{nor}}>0$ can be chosen, depending only on $\Omega$, so that for every side $E_j$ the one-sided collar
