{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.403310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a94c795b6e1e657b9e075154477790e841dae3fbc80f0ba2ac1e7ed1a5c1997","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] If $G$ is simply connected, then $G$ is semisimple, $\Lambda_G=2\pi Q_G^\vee$, where $Q_G^\vee$ is the coroot lattice, and $\varepsilon_G\equiv1$. Consequently
