Then there exists $\hat \alpha  \in \mathbb{R}^{n_N}$ such that $\forall i \in \Iintv*{1, N }, (\alpha^i)^* \in \mathscr{S}(\hat \alpha)$. Moreover, $\alpha^{**}$ the solution of the associated SOP, verifies: $$\forall (i,j) \in \Iintv*{1, N }^2, \alpha^{**}_{i,j} = (\alpha^{\max{\{i,j\}}})^*_{\min{\{i,j\}}}$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.867180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ab1bbb39ed5dc04eb1ffb09b9615d71048b39041fb5b74c56e3d8dea250e8bd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 40 of arXiv:2512.00213, 'On strong sharp phase transition in the random connection model'] Assume that $\|d_\varphi\|_{1,1}>0$.  We have the following:
