{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.250572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ad31754e7d96be96f2008281ab96a336f9f1d6f84662c30186fb5ae5129218b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] A function $u\in L^\infty([0,T],\CD_\mu^1)$ is called an energy solution to \eqref{GeneralEquation} if
\begin{equation}
