{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.640181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b047231ec5ded35fbb5debe2109ca49d2c6b3c05ffa4ab747bafd4018ad1253","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] For a given collection of independent one-dimensional Brownian motions
$(B_1,\ldots,B_N)$ we define $U=(U_1,\ldots,U_N)$ as a solution to the system
