{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.472092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b054a4f801b4fc5c36b4a566b8de2aec9138d9a8a8b51412f1828805a94b75e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:generallift of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $P_t$ and $P_{t,O}$ be contraction $C_0$-semigroups on $\mathcal{H}$ and $\mathcal{H}_O$ with generators $\mathsf{L}$ and $\mathsf{L}_O$, respectively.

 $P_t$ is a second-order \emph{lifted semigroup} of $P_{t,O}$ if
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
     \item 
        The domain relation holds
        \begin{align*}
            \dom(\mathsf{L}_O) \subset \dom(\mathsf{L})\,.
        \end{align*}








        \item   There holds, for any $x \in \mathcal{H}_O$, $y \in \dom(\mathsf{L}) \cap \mathcal{H}_O$, 
        \begin{align} 
            \langle x, \mathsf{L} y \rangle_{\mathcal{H}} = 0 \,. \tag{L1}
        \end{align}
        \item  There exists a positive  bounded operator $\mathsf{S}: \mathcal{H}_O^\perp \to  \mathcal{H}_O^\perp$ such that
        \begin{align} 
            \langle \mathsf{L} x,  \mathsf{S} \mathsf{L} y \rangle_{\mathcal{H}} = - \langle x, \mathsf{L}_O y \rangle_{\mathcal{H}_O}\,,\quad  \forall x \in \dom(\mathsf{L}) \cap \mathcal{H}_O,\, y \in \dom(\mathsf{L}_O)\,. \tag{L2}
        \end{align}
        \end{enumerate}
    In this case, we also say that $P_{t,O}$ is a \emph{collapsed semigroup} of $P_t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.178738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b0a4dc4b3186fefb27f48ae3ab5c6e78ba1f18bf193a900f1250ba04ec1f548","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Amag of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Given a partition $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$ of $[n]$, and $p \in \mathcal{P}(\Omega)$, we define the $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$-\emph{magnetization profile} as the  vector
\begin{equation}
m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p) = (m(p,A)\,,\, A\in \ensuremath{\mathcal A})\,,\qquad  m(p,A) = \frac1{|A|}\sum_{\ell\in A}p[\si_\ell]\,,
            \end{equation}
            where $p[\si_\ell]$ is the expected value of the spin at site $\ell$ according to $p$.
            The vector $m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p) $ is in  $[-1,1]^\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$, and we say that $p$ is $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$-{\em regular} if $m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p)\in(-1,1)^\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$, that is if $|m(p,A)|\neq 1 $ for all $A\in \ensuremath{\mathcal A}$. We write $\mathcal{P}_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\Omega)$ for the set of $p \in \mathcal{P}(\Omega)$ that are $\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$-regular.","status":"unverified"}

