{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.203064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b3c4ade5f0f4283f435e84181a8e130b4c180d608033140d434867a0baeee3f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi defi-dissi of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] A map $f:{\rm Dom}(f)\subseteq \mathcal{K}{\rightarrow}\mathcal{K}$ is said to be dissipative if, for every $\alpha>0$ and $x,y\in {\rm Dom}(f)$, we have
\begin{equation}
{\left\|x-y-\alpha(f(x)-f(y))\right\|}_{\mathcal{K}}\geq {\left\|x-y\right\|}_{\mathcal{K}}.
\end{equation}
If $f=A$ with $A\in\mathcal{L}(\mathcal{K})$, then (equation disban1 of the paper) reads as
\[
\norm{(\lambda{\operatorname{I}}-A)x}_{\mathcal{K}}\geq \lambda {\left\|x\right\|}_{\mathcal{K}}, \quad \forall \lambda>0,\; x\in{\rm Dom}(A)
\]
We say that $f$ is m-dissipative if the range of $\lambda{\operatorname{I}}-f$ is the whole space $\mathcal{K}$ for some $\lambda>0$ (and so for all $\lambda>0$).\\
If $\mathcal{K}$ is a Hilbert space $f$ is dissipative if and only if for every $x,y\in {\rm Dom}(f)$, we have
\begin{equation}
\scal{f(x)-f(y)}{x-y}_{\mathcal{K}}\leq 0.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.226243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b3eda04b67a267e5ff941fdbefdc64de29f823e3eedd8009739131fc449aa2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Poincare-in of arXiv:2609.00627, 'Global well-posedness of radially symmetric strong solutions to two-dimensional compressib'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain. If $\boldsymbol{v}\in H^1(\Omega)$ and $\rho$ is a non-negative function such that
	$$0<c\leq \int_\Omega\rho dx,\quad\int_\Omega\rho^\gamma\leq E_0$$
	with $\gamma>1$. Then, there exists a constant $C$ depending only on $\Omega, c, E_0$ and $\gamma$ such that
