{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.474530+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b4b5678e8cf5581603615df67036161024d18d09e2cbbd9e36e65707fa9a00c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 63 (Gap-diagonal reconstruction) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $1\le r<\infty$, let $I\subset\Lambda\times\cM$, and let
$\mathscr D=(I_\theta)_{\theta\in\Theta}$ be a countable partition of
$I$ such that every $I_\theta$ is a matching: both coordinate maps
\[
 I_\theta\longrightarrow\Lambda,
 \qquad
 I_\theta\longrightarrow\cM
\]
are injective.  For a scalar sequence $x=(x_i)_{i\in I}$, set
\begin{equation}

 \norm{x}_{\mathsf M_r(\mathscr D)}
 :=
 \sum_{\theta\in\Theta}
 \left(\sum_{i\in I_\theta}|x_i|^r\right)^{1/r}.
\end{equation}
Then $\mathsf M_r(\mathscr D)$ is a solid, order-continuous Banach
sequence lattice.  Moreover, every finite block kernel family
$(K_i)_{i\in I}$ satisfies
\begin{equation}

 \Prof_{m,r}\left(\sum_{i\in I}K_i\right)
 \le
 \norm{\bigl(\Prof_{m,r}(K_i)\bigr)_{i\in I}}
       _{\mathsf M_r(\mathscr D)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, $\mathsf M_r(\mathscr D)$ is an
$r$-reconstruction lattice with constant one.

If the output support spaces admit an orthogonality coloring with
$\chi_+$ colors and the input support spaces admit one with $\chi_-$
colors, then
\begin{equation}

 \Prof_{m,r}\left(\sum_{i\in I}K_i\right)
 \le
 (\chi_+\chi_-)^{1-1/r}
 \norm{\bigl(\Prof_{m,r}(K_i)\bigr)_{i\in I}}
       _{\mathsf M_r(\mathscr D)}.
\end{equation}

In particular, for $I=\N_0^2$ and
\[
 I_h:=\{(j,k)\in\N_0^2:j-k=h\},
 \qquad h\in\mathbb Z,
\]
the gap-diagonal norm
\begin{equation}

 \norm{x}_{\mathsf{Gap}_r}
 :=
 \sum_{h\in\mathbb Z}
 \left(
  \sum_{\substack{j,k\ge0\\j-k=h}}|x_{j,k}|^r
 \right)^{1/r}
\end{equation}
defines an order-continuous $r$-reconstruction lattice for dyadic
two-sided blocks.","status":"unverified"}

