\end{aligned}

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.370144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ba1e413015e19c5fd9a6879e5a9c903fa01f95226dd3beff56dddbc37fe2416","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] When $\ell_t$ is a Brownian motion absorbed at $\ell=0$, the test functions $D$ form a subset of the domain $\mathcal{D}(A)$. More specifically, for all $F \in D$ we have the limit
