{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.325985+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3badae2ab6f9d21630d2e50e753fe4bba711a4d8e3cfbc60d94d94884aa4ec9e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop sigma-oo-pres-refl-equiv-cc of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The symmetric monoidal functor $\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty\colon\ul{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_*^\otimes\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes$ is equivariantly cocontinuous. Moreover, if ${\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$ is equivariantly presentably symmetric monoidal, then a fiberwise cocontinuous symmetric monoidal functor $F\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes\to{\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$ is equivariantly cocontinuous if and only if $F\circ\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty_+\colon\ul{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_*^\otimes\to{\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$ is so.
    \begin{proof}
        To see that $\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty$ is equivariantly cocontinuous, we observe that each $\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty\colon{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{G,*}\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is cocontinuous (being the left derived functor of a left Quillen functor), while the Beck--Chevalley condition for left adjoints to restrictions along injective homomorphisms is the content of Lemma~(lemma:Sigma-oo-equiv-left-adjointable of the paper). This completes the proof of the first statement and the `only if' part of the second one.

        To prove the remaining direction, we left $F\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes\to{\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$ be a fiberwise cocontinuous symmetric monoidal functor such that $F\circ\textbf{\textup{L}}\Sigma^\infty$ is equivariantly cocontinuous; we have to show that  the Beck--Chevalley map $i_!F\to Fi_!$ is invertible for every injective $i\colon G\to G'$. Note that the presentably symmetric monoidal $\infty$-categories ${\mathcal{C}}(G)$ and ${\mathcal{C}}(G')$ are stable as they receive symmetric monoidal left adjoints from presentably symmetric monoidal stable $\infty$-categories (namely, $F_G$ and $F_G'$); thus, the Beck--Chevalley condition follows by exactly the same reduction argument as in the proof of the previous proposition.
    \end{proof}","status":"unverified"}

