{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.273727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3bc3a58ba6bdfa581b6d624ef5d626c63f863c09be458aa3bded99c7eaf0c232","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Adapted $2$-Wasserstein distance) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] The adapted $2$-Wasserstein distance $\AW_2(\bX, \bY)$ between filtered processes $\bX, \bY \in \cFP_2$ is defined by
\begin{equation} 
