{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.855424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c2f2cdee9aca466848ade3bf2a6c98ba2fe1472a37b169ff4324ac04d4771ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:fluid of arXiv:2607.12061, 'Models for species evolution with random deaths'] Suppose $f > f^\dagger_c$. If $\mathbf{X}^n(0) \to (m_0,\ell_0)^\top$, where $m_0 \geq \ell_0>0$, then for every $\delta,t>0$ 
