{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.281406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c3c202ee83af5beee1fdefa489bfdd7a9772259193908daae4a5009a68c8c04","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Volume-bias concentration upper bound) of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] There exists a number $C=C(\Mcc)>0$ sufficiently large, and for every $\eps >0$ a number $c=c(\Mcc,\eps) > 0$ sufficiently small, such that the following holds. For all $T \ge 1$ and $r \ge 1/T$ such that either (a) $\eta \in [C,T]$ or (b) $\Mcc = \Sc^{d}$ and $\eta \in [1,T]$, 
