{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.666248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c3cb00324e98331b6232f3665f8f5071b269e08411ff7afed05c77d7ba139ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:2s5c-taylor of arXiv:2411.00930, '\bf \Large Asymptotic Product-form Steady-state for Multiclass Queueing Networks: A Reentr'] Let $\theta(r)\in\mathbb{R}^5$ be given for each $r\in(0,1)$, satisfying $|\theta(r)|\leq cr$. Denoting $\theta=\theta(r)$, as $r\to0$, we have
