{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.856425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c404b0f6ced3c0786f055f6ec4fdbf04c6620ad3d761a6c6a987668b60651f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] If $-\alpha<u<0$ and $v>u$ then,   as $N\to\infty$, we have
 \begin{equation}

     \GG_N(\alpha,u,v)\sim \Gamma(\alpha-u)^{N}\Gamma(\alpha+u)^N \tfrac{\Gamma(\alpha+v)}{\Gamma(\alpha-u)}\EE[R^{-u-v}],
 \end{equation}
 where $R$ is  given by \eqref{Rseries}.

If $-\alpha<v<0$ and $u>v$, then, as $N\to\infty$, we have
\begin{equation}
