{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.686213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c4528808e85955ca1a33c1b33799e0422558ae9be3a81ed07115533befe7c0c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 85 (Uniform spatial trace-tightness profile) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Let $\varnothing\ne\mathcal P_{\rm sp}\subset
\mathfrak S_{\Lambda,0}^{0,T}(H)$.  A sequence of finite-rank orthogonal
projections $P_m\uparrow I_H$, together with numbers
$\vartheta_m\downarrow0$, is a \emph{uniform spatial trace-tightness profile}
if, with $R_m:=I-P_m$,
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{P\in\mathcal P_{\rm sp}}
 \left\|\Tr(R_ma_t^PR_m)\right\|_{L^\infty(\dd t\otimes P)}
 \le\vartheta_m,
 \qquad m\ge0.
\end{equation}
After passing to a subsequence and relabeling, one may assume
$\vartheta_m\le2^{-8m}$.  Writing $r_m=\operatorname{rank}P_m$, define
\begin{equation}
 \omega_{\boldsymbol\vartheta}(\eps)
 :=\inf_{m\ge0}\left(\sqrt{r_m\eps}+\sqrt{\vartheta_m}\right).
\end{equation}
Then $\omega_{\boldsymbol\vartheta}(\eps)\downarrow0$ as $\eps\downarrow0$.","status":"unverified"}

