{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.683363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c75a16d13843ed9671b78e37b16273f3bc703c48f5f984418f0f4569326148d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 63 (Common weak-geometric H\"older locus) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] For $\alpha\in(1/3,1/2)$ define
\begin{equation}
 G_\alpha^{\rm wg}
 :=\left\{x\in G_J:
 \|X(x)\|_{\alpha\text{-H\"ol}}
 +\|\mathbb X^S(x)\|_{2\alpha\text{-H\"ol}}^{1/2}<\infty\right\}.
\end{equation}
Then $G_\alpha^{\rm wg}$ is Borel, invariant under deterministic stopping,
and has full $\Smax$-capacity.  On this set
$\mathbf X^S=(1,X,\mathbb X^S)$ is a weakly geometric
$\alpha$-H\"older rough path in the Hilbert--Schmidt tensor norm.  For every
$\eta\in(1/3,\alpha)$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathbf X^S(x)\in G\Omega^2_\eta(H;\mathcal S_2),
 \qquad x\in G_\alpha^{\rm wg}.
\end{equation}
Consequently
\begin{equation}
 G_{\rm geo}:=
 \bigcap_{\alpha\in\mathbb Q\cap(1/3,1/2)}G_\alpha^{\rm wg}
\end{equation}
is Borel, stopping-stable, has full capacity, and satisfies
\eqref{eq:weak-to-geometric-tuning} for every $1/3<\eta<1/2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.301038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c77d205f445959bcf521a2cfecfc7869639a41134a0695acc104c0f69564885","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Buse_global of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Fix $s \in \mathbb{R}$. Then, on an $s$-dependent event of probability one, there exist continuous functions $C(x,s,t)$ defined for $t > s$ and $x \in \mathbb{R}$ and $a(s,t)$ defined for $t > s$ so that, for all $x,y \in \mathbb{R}$, $\xi \in \mathfrak{X}$, and $t > s$,
   \[
   L(x,s,t,\xi) 
       \le W^\xi(0,s;x,t) \le R(x,s,t,\xi),
   \] 
   where
    \begin{align*}
        L(x,s,t,\xi) &= -|\mathcal P(\xi)| - C(x,s,t)   \\
        & +  \begin{cases}
            (2\mathcal P(\xi) -a(s,t))x + (t-s)\left(\mathcal P(\xi) - \frac{a(s,t)}{2}\right)^2  &x + (t-s)\mathcal P(\xi) > \frac{a(s,t)}{2}(t-s) \\
            -\frac{x^2}{t-s} &|x + (t-s)\mathcal P(\xi)| \le \frac{a(s,t)}{2}(t-s) \\
            (2\mathcal P(\xi) + a(s,t))x + (t-s)\Bigl(\mathcal P(\xi) + \frac{a(s,t)}{2}\Bigr)^2 &x+ (t-s)\mathcal P(\xi) < -\frac{a(s,t)}{2}(t-s),
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    and 
    \begin{align*}
     R(x,s,t,\xi) &= |\mathcal P(\xi)| + C(x,s,t) \\
     &+\begin{cases}
            (2\mathcal P(\xi) + a(s,t))x + t\left(\mathcal P(\xi) + \frac{a(s,t)}{2}\right)^2  &x + (t-s)\mathcal P(\xi) \ge 0 \\
            (2\mathcal P(\xi) - a(s,t))x + (t-s)\Bigl(\mathcal P(\xi) + \frac{a(s,t)}{2}\Bigr)^2 &x+ (t-s)\mathcal P(\xi) \le 0.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

