{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.724887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cb0c930b708ca164016d31f92f7d877796abc298844550994b9b674cfe20211","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma-Interior-Decay of arXiv:2609.01964, 'The critical exponent for the two-dimensional semilinear wave equation with strong damping'] Let $0<a<b<1$ and $u_0,u_1\in\mathcal C_0^\infty$. There exist $C,T_0>0$ such that
