{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.301320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cd396baa4269bc7bce913f8219b429c61b5f9b9d205948357f81cae686b9eeb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: estimating mu, delta, sigma of arXiv:2601.05361, 'Noise sensitivity in last-passage percolation'] There exist constants $0<c,C<\infty$ such that the following holds. For every $n\ge1$, $v\in R_{0,n\mathbf{e}_+}$ and $1\le s\le \frac{1}{18}|v|_1^{1/3}$ such that $|v|_1\le n$ we have that
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item $(Y_j)_{j=1,\ldots,k}$ and $(Z_j)_{j=-k+1\ldots,0}$ are i.i.d.\ sequences;
\item $(Y_j)_{j=1,\ldots,k}$ and $(Z_j)_{j=-k+1\ldots,0}$ are mutually independent;
\item ${\mathbb{P}}(Y_j\ge1)\ge c$ and ${\mathbb{P}}(Z_j\ge1)\ge c$, and $\textup{Var}(Y_j)\ge c$ and $\textup{Var}(Z_j)\ge c$;
\item $0\le{\mathbb{E}}[Y_j]\le Cs|v|_1^{-1/3}$ and $0\le{\mathbb{E}}[Z_j]\le Cs|v|_1^{-1/3}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.664978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cd3b1039b9c6a5a56da52f495c2d5b30dd7ba7072cc693fba4e8937e3571787","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-thm-limit-shape of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $\beta>0$ large enough and consider $\phi\sim \pi^0_\Lambda$, the $(2+1)$\textsc{d}  \ensuremath{\mathbb Z\textsc{gff}}\xspace on $\Lambda=\llbracket 1,L\rrbracket^2$ with a floor and zero boundary conditions. Set $H(L)$ and $N_n$ per (eq:H-def,eq:Nn-def of the paper). Fix $m\geq 1$, and let ${\ensuremath{\mathscr L}}_n$ ($n=0,\ldots,m$) be obtained by placing the 4 quadrants of the Wulff shape $\ensuremath{\mathcal W}$ defined above, rescaled by $N_n$, in the 4 corners of $\Lambda$, and joining them via straight lines along  $\partial \Lambda$. Let $\mathfrak{L}_n$ be the \texttt{large} $(H+1-n)$ level line loop(s) of $\phi$.
Then, with probability $1-O(L^{-10})$:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item{} For each $1\leq n\leq m$, $\mathfrak{L}_n$ is a single loop that satisfies $d_\ensuremath{\mathcal H}(\mathfrak{L}_n,{\ensuremath{\mathscr L}}_n)< N_n e^{-\sqrt{\log L}}$.

\item{} For $n=0$, either $\mathfrak{L}_0$ is empty (no \texttt{large} $(H+1$) level-line loops), or it is a single loop that satisfies $d_\ensuremath{\mathcal H}(\mathfrak{L}_0, {\ensuremath{\mathscr L}}_0) < N_0 e^{-\sqrt{\log L}}$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.889806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cd5fd2caaea969af50c3c953e0ee7e1371a29170ed1355dc81952e44058f05c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2607.11608, '2607.11608'] Let $f$ be a strictly increasing function on $\R_+$
