{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.165654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cd6c9c48d7ea52570b133d088c5891c0175fb304c05734c8bfe36a3e2e6c2ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:coarse-graining of arXiv:2608.30829, 'Free energy and phase transition for\\ 2D directed polymers with critical spatial correlat'] There exists a (small) constant \(\eta = \eta(d)\) such that, if there exists \(L \in \mathbb{N}\) and \(\beta>0\) such that 
