{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.889422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ce511aef9adc57c0767b9115a21c7e8f52a73aaf7fdcd83aecb483db6900d75","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: dth Ar power of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $A\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ be a finite set and let $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{>0}^A$. For every admissible random field $\mathcal{X}\randin C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^m,\mathbb{R}^{m-1})$ independent of $\mathcal{E}_\alpha$, every positive integer $d$ and every $U\subset \mathbb{R}^m$, we have 
