{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.283463+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ce5ffd05b3542fc32e655b445fdc47fe45fff4ae8546c2979527cc97fe4ce2d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Let $(U, V)$ be Banach spaces and suppose $f \in C^\alpha([0, T], V)$, $B \in C^\beta([0, T], U)$ for some 
$(\beta \in (\frac{1}{2}, 1])$, $(0 < \alpha \le \gamma < 1)$ and $(\alpha + \beta > 1)$. Also suppose that \(A \in C^\gamma([0,T],L(V,(U,V)))\) and \(\hat A\in C^\gamma([0,T],L(V,V))\) for \(\alpha<\gamma<1\).
Then, if \(X : [0, T] \to V\)
satisfies the controlled Young differential equation
\begin{equation}
Z_t = Z_0 + \int_0^t \hat A_sZ_s \dd s + \int_0^t A_s Z_s\dd B_s+ f_t.
\end{equation}
Then, 
\begin{equation}
\|Z\|_{\infty,[0,T]} \le C_1 e^{C_2 (\|A\|_{\gamma}^{\frac{1}{\gamma}}+\|\hat A\|_{\gamma}^{\frac{1}{\gamma}}+\|B\|_{\beta}^{\frac{1}{\beta}})} (\|Z_0\|+\|f\|_{\alpha})
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
\|Z\|_{\alpha,[0,T]} \le C_3 \|B\|_{\beta}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}((\|B\|_{\beta}+\|A\|_{\gamma}+\|\hat A\|_{\gamma})\|Z\|_\alpha+\|f\|_{\alpha})
\end{equation}
for some constants \(C_1, C_2, C_3 > 0\) depending on \(\alpha, \beta, \gamma, T\) and \(\|f\|_{BC^2}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

