{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.838012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cee5b048d0a4813bb1ab2a2bb5b199da93c86d00a8ca3be90c792cae38eb9d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2604.11489, '2604.11489'] \cite{G-Z}
If $\beta \in (0,1]$, then
\beq
\ee[|\hat p_{n,i}-p_{n,i}|^{\beta+1}]\leq 4p_{n,i} n^{-\beta}
\deq
and there is a constant $C>0$ depending only on $\beta$ with
\beq
\ee[|\hat p_{n,i}-p_{n,i}|^{\beta+1}]\leq C p_{n,i}^{(\beta+1)/2} n^{-(\beta+1)/2}.
