{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.446578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d140bb375baeb6ddb86dc14d9ccbc68b9906bf8c591006cc5f062c5f3e23a60","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:k-lift-TW-max of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] For any given integer  $k\ge1$, define iteratively $G_N^{(i)}$ as a random 2-lift of $G_N^{(i-1)}$ for $i=1,\dots,k$, where    $G_N^{(0)}$ is a uniformly random $d$-regular graph.   If $d\gg N^{2/3+\tau}$, then
