     \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.889112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d23e45b94885bcaf4caaede45aa9ae8ce34ad4bb0e57f2af84cd3a6427ace16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:conc:I:minus of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] Suppose $x_0 = \Theta(1)$ and $K = o(\sqrt{\log m})$. Then for any $\epsilon > 0$,
