{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.619674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d2e808890195fec333b2e2efa683139f9558d35a70be94cc8f5bf0b176cad88","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 32 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Recall the choices of $\phi_0$ and $\Eis(f)$ from \S \ref{sec:choices} and $x$ from \eqref{eq:def-x}. Then there exists a constant $\mu_1$ depending only on $n$ such that
