{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.211791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d3a160311480d26c097bd3ed04e10d1aab25a9ad738740ea05a7e40bce61e9f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop soldt of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Assume that Hypotheses (EU2 of the paper) hold true. For every small $\theta,\delta\geq 0$ and\\ $x\in E$, the PDE (equation eqdt of the paper) has a unique mild solution $y_{\delta,\theta}(\cdot,x)\in C([0,T],E)$ and it is \\left-differentiable. Moreover for every small enough $\tau,\delta, \theta>0$, for every $x,z\in E$ and \\$t\in [0,T]$ we have
