{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.954469+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d57fbba0ef36eb3f70f6d8ebdca67869fb8d2c91408bbc20b3a8379f59af898","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2604.09365, 'Cotlar martingale transforms and related singular integrals'] Suppose $d=2n$ is even and A is a Cotlar matrix. Then,  
