{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.849456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d61cf47168834eb8b9a1677b6fae93cc6467d7cfcb4b8f8dd36e8542e55e4e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:g:taylor of arXiv:2607.09841, 'Mixing and cutoff for the systematic scan dynamics of the mean-field ferromagnetic Potts m'] For any $\ell \in Q$ and $s,\tilde s \in \mathcal S_q$,
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item  there exists an $R : \mathcal{S}_q \to \mathbb{R}$ such that $g_\beta^\ell(s) = \frac{1}{q} + \frac{\beta}{q} \Big(s_\ell - \frac{1}{q}\Big) + R(s)$  and $\lvert R(s) \rvert \leq 3q\beta^2 \lVert s-\hat e\rVert_2^2$ ;
    \item  $\big\lVert g_\beta(s) - g_\beta(\tilde{s}) \big\lVert_1
    = \frac{\beta}{q} \big\lVert s - \tilde{s} \big \rVert_1 +  \lVert s - \tilde{s} \rVert_1 \Big\{ O\big(\lVert s - \hat{e} \rVert_1 + \lVert \tilde{s} - \hat{e} \rVert_1\big) \Big\}$;
    \item  $\big\lVert g_\beta(s) - g_\beta(\tilde{s}) \big\lVert_2^2
