 where $b^*$ is the unique solution for $b$ in the equation\footnote{The equation $2b\theta_1(b)=1$ simplifies to $\ln(1-b)=-\frac{3}{2}b$.  } $2b\theta_1(b)=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.334982+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d7327072b080b0b6819263e57bfb41c124efc7182e7b095922b15d008622b46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma local_law of arXiv:2606.17425, 'Order statistics for edge eigenvectors of Wigner matrices'] Fix a small $\omega > 0$, and define the domain,
