{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.501546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d8ef12a97ba603a0a5b7f8a41ad714d144802c7daf5d4928f655dd7d9acec13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gaussian-domination of arXiv:2601.05798, '{I}mry-{M}a phenomenon for the hard-core model on $\mathbb{Z}^{2}$'] Fix $\lambda>0$.
	For all $ t \ge 0 $, we have that
	\begin{equation}
		\liminf_{j \uparrow \infty}
		\mathbb{E}\left[
			\exp\left( \frac{t F_{\Lambda_j,\lambda}(X)}{ \sqrt{|\Lambda_j|}}\right)
			\right]
		\ge
		\exp(t^2 b^2/2),
	\end{equation}
	where
	\begin{equation}
		b^2
		\ge
		\frac{1}{2} \mathbb{E}[\mathbb{E}[F_{\Lambda_j,\lambda}(X) \mid X_{\mathsf{o}}]^2]
		+
		\frac{1}{2} \mathbb{E}[\mathbb{E}[F_{\Lambda_j,\lambda}(X) \mid X_{\mathsf{o}'}]^2].
	\end{equation}
	for $\mathsf{o}=(0,0), \mathsf{o}'=(0,1)$ and for and any $j \ge 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:56.995482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d94b402ca77f3b3712e6cb84789fbfd717adc0c79931aea25f0fd9e888175ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Cluster-sum expansion at the square) of arXiv:2609.02784, 'Maximizing the fundamental Laplace--Neumann \\ eigenvalue on quadrilaterals'] For every $\e \in S^3$ we have $\tr\bigl(\widetilde B_1|_{V_0}\bigr) = 0$ and, as $t \to 0$,
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{\lambda_1(t\e)} + \frac{1}{\lambda_2(t\e)}
\;=\; \frac{2}{\pi^2} \;+\; \bigl(\Pi_0(\e) + \Sigma_\perp(\e)\bigr)\, t^2 \;+\; O(t^3),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align*}
\pi^6\, \Pi_0(\e) &:= \tr\bigl((\widetilde K_1|_{V_0})^2\bigr) \;-\; \pi^2\, \tr\bigl(\widetilde K_1|_{V_0}\, \widetilde M_1|_{V_0}\bigr) \;-\; \pi^2\, \tr\bigl(\widetilde K_2|_{V_0}\bigr) \;+\; \pi^4\, \tr\bigl(\widetilde M_2|_{V_0}\bigr), \\
\pi^6\, \Sigma_\perp(\e) &:= \sum_{k \in V_0} \sum_{m \in V_0^\perp} \frac{\pi^2}{\kappa_m - \pi^2}\, \bigl(\widetilde B_1\bigr)_{k, m}^2 \;\;\ge\;\; 0,
\end{align*}
and the remainder in \eqref{e:cluster-sum} is uniform for $\e \in S^3$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.290159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d94be0ea6cf3ff7ccf436a887152426b6bb76406a510517131fd586c8bae16c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_conditional_convergence_in_probability of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] We say that the sequence of random variables $(X_{n})_{n\ge 1} $ converges to the random variable $X_{0}$ in probability, conditionally on the event $\mathcal H $ with positive probability, 
