{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.467621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d98ff122ac18f350947d040d40402918516c793b10c2d867c574f33e89c2da3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Oriented-cut duality and the Hilbert fixed point) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $m\ge1$, $1<r<\infty$, and $r'=r/(r-1)$.  The coefficient pairing,
which is linear in its first variable, induces conjugate-linear isometric
isomorphisms
\begin{equation}

 \begin{aligned}
  \CutCoeff_{m,r'}&\longrightarrow(\CutCoeff_{m,r})^*,
  &L&\longmapsto\bigl[K\longmapsto\ip{K}{L}\bigr],\\
  \Coeff_{m,r'}&\longrightarrow(\Coeff_{m,r})^*,
  &L&\longmapsto\bigl[K\longmapsto\ip{K}{L}\bigr].
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Every coefficient space in this range is reflexive.  In particular, the
quotient-sum and intersection branches are conjugate, while
\begin{equation}

 \CutCoeff_{m,2}=\mathscr K_m,
 \qquad
 \Coeff_{m,2}
 =\cH^{\odot m}\otimes\conj{\cC}\otimes\cE
\end{equation}
are Hilbert spaces with their kernel norms and are conjugate-self-dual
under the same pairing. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.864927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d9bf2d434a5db79a9ab6c0371387412c018493859563d5cfc9a20ea43fc7374","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2509.21253, '\bf Capacity in high dimensional percolation'] \rm{
			For $r>0$ we define the number of pioneer points $X_r$ as follows

			\[
			X_r=\left|\left\{x\in \partial \ball{0}{r}: 0\stackrel{ \ball{0}{r}}{\longleftrightarrow}   x    \right\}  \right|=|\mathcal C(0;B(0,r))\cap \partial B(0,r)|.	
			\]	
			For $x\in \partial \ball{0}{r}$ we define global and local density conditions. For $s>0$ we write
			\begin{align*}
				\mathcal{T}_s(x) = & \{ |\mathcal{C}(x;\ball{0}{r})\cap \ball{x}{s}
				| \leq s^4 (\log s)^7\} \\ &\cap \{|\mathcal{C}(x;\ball{0}{r})\cap \ball{x}{s}\cap \partial \ball{0}{r} |\leq s^2 (\log s)^7  \}.
			\end{align*}
			We now define a local density condition as follows
			\begin{align*}
				\mathcal{T}_s^\textrm{loc}(x) =&\bigcap_{y\in \ball{x}{s}} \{|\mathcal{C}(y; \ball{x}{s^d}\cap \ball{0}{r})\cap \ball{x}{s}|\leq s^4 (\log s)^4\} \\
				&\bigcap \bigcap_{y\in \ball{x}{s}\cap \partial \ball{0}{r}} \{|\mathcal{C}(y;\ball{x}{s^d}\cap \ball{0}{r}) \cap \ball{x}{s}\cap \partial \ball{0}{r}|\leq s^2 (\log s)^4 \} \\
				&\bigcap \{ \exists \ \text{ at most }  (\log s)^3 \text{ disjoint paths from }\ball{x}{s} \text{ to } \partial \ball{x}{s^d} \text{ in } \ball{0}{r} \}.
			\end{align*}
		}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.549032+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d9c22c44eb5fe31f5aec7c7b068c9fb8c12993df466a71c1b811ade8c518e70","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th1 of arXiv:2411.17104, 'Two-barriers-reflected BSDE with Rank-based Data'] With assumptions (\textbf{A1})-(\textbf{A3}), there is a unique quadruplet $(Y^{t,x}(\cdot),Z^{t,x}(\cdot),K^{t,x,+}(\cdot),K^{t,x,-}(\cdot))$ satisfies the properties:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\setlength{\parsep}{0ex} 
\setlength{\itemsep}{0ex}
