{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.834623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3db72404859c148585714383f4a6498468781dabff68a5175a1e11fc6d305200","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Partition-constrained compression) of arXiv:2604.10820, 'A Strict Gap Between Relaxed and Partition-Constrained\\ Spectral Compression in a Six-Sta'] Let $\mathcal A=\{A_1,A_2,A_3\}$ be an unordered partition of the six-state space into three nonempty cells. Choose any ordering of the three cells and define
\begin{equation*}
h_\alpha:=\frac{\mathbf 1_{A_\alpha}}{\sqrt{|A_\alpha|}},
\qquad
H_{\mathcal A}:=[h_1,h_2,h_3],
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
Q_{\mathcal A}(T):=H_{\mathcal A}^*TH_{\mathcal A}.
\end{equation*}
If a different ordering is chosen, then $Q_{\mathcal A}(T)$ is conjugated by a $3\times 3$ permutation matrix, so its determinant is unchanged. Hence $\det Q_{\mathcal A}(T)$ depends only on the underlying unordered partition.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354466+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dbb287a8a9f223c8e4b6e8ebf9cf6bc2b7f56b985baa66ac39a9f8dff3ee417","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-discr of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Fix \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\), let \(u = T - t_{k+1}\) and \(\ell = T - t_k\), and recall \(\cL_{\mathrm{discr}}^{(k)}\) from~(eq:def-discr of the paper).
