for every $(s,t)\in\Delta[U,V]$ satisfying $\omega(s,t)<\delta$. Both constants $\delta$ and $L$ depend only on $C, \widetilde{C}$, $m$, $\|f\|_3$, $\|X\|$, and $p$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.158608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dc67397aeaa43b0584fca496f86e53d5c05aa6b65d0d9cb1437c179931a700c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 (Top-order electric compensation) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] For every spatial multi-index $1\le\abs\alpha\le s$, the leading electric work
in the $\pa^\alpha$ momentum energy satisfies
\begin{equation}
