{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.732918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e01419b0cd62bfef823b24ce09a1d1ef521e5a84e9c16864ba1cf7a5294c49a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thmintro slippery of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Suppose $\Phi$ is LBSF and $\bm{s}$ is a strongly $\aleph$-unobstructed slippery point of $\overline{\mathcal{Z}(\Phi)}$. Then at least one of the following happens:
