{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.033996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e0adaa29ee0badfa50b50e6729f76cdd31493660bada605789a2ed0adbee7da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2605.03057, 'Uniform-in-time quantitative fluctuations of large scale interacting particle systems'] Assume Assumption~\ref{ass:smooth}. Let $\left(\mu_s\right)_{0\le s\le t}$ be the law flow of the McKean--Vlasov SDE~\eqref{eq:MV}.
Let $\varphi\in C_b^5\left(\R^d\right)$ and let $\left(\psi_s\right)_{0\le s\le t}$ be a classical solution to the backward equation
\begin{equation}

\partial_s\psi_s+\mathcal L_{\mu_s}\psi_s+\mathcal A_{\mu_s}\psi_s=0,\qquad s\in\left[0,t\right),\qquad \psi_t=\varphi.
\end{equation}
Then, the limiting variance in Definition \ref{def:uniform-time-limiting-variance-abs-assump} can be written as
\begin{equation}

\sigma_t^2\left(\varphi\right)
=
\Var\left(\psi_0\left(X_0\right)\right)
+\int_0^t \E\left(\norm{\sigma\left(X_s,\mu_s\right)^\top\nabla\psi_s\left(X_s\right)}^2\right) ds,
\end{equation}
where $X$ solves \eqref{eq:MV}. In particular, $\sigma_t^2\left(\varphi\right)=\lim_{N\to\infty}\sigma_{N,t}^2\left(\varphi\right)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.953793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e0b3f21ab9b06983216da6ac9e6709301ea7ecd560ebd581cc1426950357499","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] Let $\bfJ$ be a $N \times N$ matrix of i.i.d. standard Gaussian random variables. Then for all $k, l \in \bbN$ we have
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\bbE\big[\big(J^k(J^\top)^l\big)_{11}\big]}{N^{(k+l)/2}} = \left \{ \begin{aligned}&\delta_{k, l} + \frac{1}{N}\eps_{k, l}  &\quad & k+ l \text{ even,} 
        \\ &0 &\quad & k+l \text{ odd},\end{aligned}\right.

    \end{equation}
    where $\delta_{k,l}$ denotes the Kronecker delta and $|\eps_{k, l}| \leq (k+l)!!$. Additionally for all $k, l, n, m \in \bbN$,
\begin{equation}\frac{\textup{Cov}\big[\big(J^k(J^\top)^l\big)_{11},\big(J^n(J^\top)^m\big)_{11}\big]}{N^{(k+l+m+n)/2}} =
\left \{ \begin{aligned}& \frac{1}{N}\eps_{k,l,n,m}  &\quad & k+ l+n+m \text{ even,} 
        \\ &0 &\quad & k+l+n+m \text{ odd},\end{aligned}\right.
         \end{equation}
         where $|\eps_{k,l,m,n}| \leq (k+l+m+n)!!$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.794677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e0ec67ec7643e8485b7b1d0df6ab80516cced40781811abbe8011b4ea4a57e7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:prob:tail of arXiv:2411.09381, 'On the well-posedness of SPDEs with locally Lipschitz coefficients'] If $L_{\sigma}>0$, then
