{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:12.368967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e113a547db8918a8d5438f207a7228ab14068616ece42698c96697ddf5f090d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2601.16580, 'Coin flipping and waiting times paradoxes: Why fair coins are exceptional' (openquestion environment labelled oq:reversal-amplitude).] Fix a tie convention. Among all pairs with $\mathbb{E}[\tau_U]\ge \mathbb{E}[\tau_V]$, how large can the head‑to‑head advantage of $U$ over $V$ be? Define the \emph{reversal gap}
