{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.252988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e1bf7ddaebbd3ae76f65eb2e1ac7a3997f23693bb271ba56e020c90a6f92b81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main_diagonal of arXiv:2609.04092, 'Short character sums of inhomogeneous polynomials'] Fix a prime $p$ and let  $n\geq1, k\geq 5$ be integers. Let $F=G_1(X_1)+\cdots + G_{n}(X_{n})$, where each $G_i\in \mathbb{F}_p[X_i]$ is of degree $k$.
