{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.771381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e377721ec3cb6ffd0213dea20510a8ca350e5ddb34d2f8b5ce7b72d2692ee84","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:three-point of arXiv:2608.04900, 'A Sharper Hoeffding Bound for Weighted Sums of Exchangeable Random Variables'] Let $A,B\ge0$ with $A+B>0$. Fix $s,q\in\mathbb{R}$ with $q\ge s^2/3$. On
\begin{align*}
C_{s,q}=\{(u,v,z):u+v+z=s,\ u^2+v^2+z^2=q\},
\end{align*}
the function $G(u,v,z)=A(e^u+e^v+e^z)+B(e^{-u}+e^{-v}+e^{-z})$ is maximized at a point where at least two of $u,v,z$ are equal. If $q>s^2/3$, no point with three distinct coordinates can be a maximizer.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.303657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e399df13d20e9677fc3abbfb11e3ea74998ab6d9b4a2c22399769e10cfa6af8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:JFIQ of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] For the JFIQ system, $\eta^{\mathrm{JFIQ}, n}\stackrel{f}{\rightarrow} \eta^{\mathrm{JFSQ}}$ as given in Proposition~(prop:priority_idleness of the paper) and $\hat{\alpha}_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}, n}(n^{1/2}\cdot)\Rightarrow \iota(\cdot)\times F$. Consequently, $(X_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}, n},\boldsymbol{\xi}^{\mathrm{JFIQ}, n})\Rightarrow (X_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}, \boldsymbol{\xi}^{\mathrm{JFIQ}})$, where $(X_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}, \boldsymbol{\xi}^{\mathrm{JFIQ}})$ is the unique solution of 
    \begin{align}

    \nonumber
    X_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(t) & = X_1(0) - (\varsigma+ \nu) t + \sqrt{2}W(t) \\
    &\qquad\qquad\qquad- \mu_{\min}\int_0^t X_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)ds + \int_0^t \langle \iota, \xi_2^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)\rangle ds - U_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(t),\\

    \nonumber \langle f, \xi_2^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(t)\rangle & = \langle f, \xi_2(0)\rangle + \langle f, F\rangle U_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(t) \\
    &\qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad- \int_0^t\langle f\times \iota, \xi_2^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)\rangle ds + \int_0^t \langle f\times\iota, \xi_3^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)\rangle ds ,\\
     \langle f, \xi_i^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(t)\rangle & = \langle f, \xi_i(0)\rangle - \int_0^t\langle f\times \iota, \xi_i^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)\rangle ds +  \int_0^t \langle f\times\iota, \xi_{i+1}^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)\rangle ds,\mbox{ for all }i\geq 3, 
\end{align}
for any fixed $L>0$ and all $f\in \Lipbar{\mathbb{R}, L}(\mathbb{S})$. Moreover $U_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}\in \mathbb{D}_{\mathbb{R}_+}[0,\infty)$ is a non-decreasing function with $U_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(0)=0$ and satisfies
\begin{align*}
    \int_0^\infty \mathbb{I}(X_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s)<0)\,dU_1^{\mathrm{JFIQ}}(s) = 0.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.238407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e3a16758cd61f70231df28dd41d11b819cbd95796c1b40c80f167d311236aaa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:intro-main of arXiv:2608.29561, 'Ball codes: A coding characterization of Hausdorff and packing dimensions'] For every nonempty \(E\subseteq\mathbb R^n\),
