{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.818615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e53d3b60dced5deaa8b3832a4ceaee167c5cc834825dab5655887f8cc61ef6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma r:whitenoise-multiplication of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] Let $\psi,\widetilde{\psi}\in L^\infty(\Sigma)$. For every sequence $(\widetilde{\psi}_n)_{n\geq 1}\in \mathcal{C}^\infty(\Sigma)$ that converges to $\widetilde{\psi}$ in $L^p$ (for every $p<\infty$), $(\xi_\psi\widetilde{\psi}_n)_{n\geq 1}$ also converges to $\xi_{\psi\widetilde{\psi}}$. In particular, the $\sigma$-algebra $\sigma(\xi_{\psi\widetilde{\psi}})$ generated by
