is contained in $\sigma(\xi_{\psi})$, i.e. the same $\sigma$-algebra with $\psi$ replacing $\psi\widetilde{\psi}$ in the definition.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.853799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e53ed3b2ae183eac4319222396f39029b2679764a8f542ec18cb3514ce3f990","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lem:recursiveLemmaFormula of arXiv:2509.16694, 'A central limit theorem for two-dimensional directed polymers with critical spatial correl'] For all $a>-1$, $z\in \big[\,0,\,(a+2)z_a/2\,\big)$ and $x\in [0,1]$,
