{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:46:12.275980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e67a89a55e32c7f80de2db829be7b77272ca03a485bdead815cc5e08aec2390","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 30 (Adapted Brenier coupling between elements of $\mathcal{P}_2(\R^{Nd})$) of arXiv:2604.22159, 'Adapted optimal transport between filtered Gaussian processes'] Let $\mu, \nu \in \cP_2(\bR^{Nd})$ be laws of $d$-dimensional stochastic processes. We say that $\pi \in \Cpl(\mu, \nu)$ is an adapted Brenier coupling of $(\mu, \nu)$ if for all $t \in [N]$ and ($\pi$-almost) all $x_{1:(t-1)}, y_{1:(t-1)} \in \bR^{(t-1)d}$ (empty when $t = 1$), the conditional distribution
\begin{equation} 
\pi_{t}(\dd x_{t}, \dd y_{t} \mid x_{1:(t-1)}, y_{1:(t-1)})
\end{equation}
is a Brenier coupling between the conditional marginals $\mu_{t}(\dd x_{t} \mid x_{1:(t-1)})$ and $\nu_{t}(\dd y_{t} \mid y_{1:(t-1)})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.873574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e6b2bbff8a732fbddd33ced61e5af694461bce1983b7a98d548728cdb895fd1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:G3 of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] For $h\in\{0,\ldots,H\}$ define
\[
  \bar U_h:=\frac1N\sum_{c=1}^N\left(\mathbb{E}[\theta_{c,h}^2]-M_2\right).
\]
Then
\begin{equation}

  \bar U_h
  =\gamma^2\left(h^2Q_{\gamma,N,H}+h\sigma^2\right)+O_H(r_{\gamma,N}),
\end{equation}
and, using (lem:QH-uniform of the paper),
\begin{equation}

  \bar U_h
  =\gamma^2\sigma^2\left(h+\frac{h^2}{H}\right)
   +O_H\left(\frac{\gamma^2}{N}+\gamma^3\right).
\end{equation}
The remainder is uniform in $N$ and $\gamma$ for fixed $H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.413199+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e6c471591cf7b709ce875afe2d2343fd8a5a3f1b935c387961d49d115a05f94","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 65 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Under Assumption~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, there exists $C>0$ depending only on constants in the assumption, such that for any $\boldsymbol{X} \in \amsmathbb{R}^H$ satisfying
