{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.283746+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e81d81d5b7aa67b29c1699d545860f8eef3073860e2f5c7dfd0f6917d22214b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.22044, 'Degenerate Stochastic Delay Modified Equation: Approximation of Stochastic Variance Reduce'] For $0\leq t\leq m\eta,$ denote $v_{t}(y)=\E g(Y^y_{t})$, thus for $\eta\in(0,1)$, we have
