{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.322601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e9a7841f392955a8e71f156545fc2e6d1df8024003e922553395f9ff07a0847","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:linear_existence of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Suppose that $\mathcal A$ is a measurable matrix field satisfying
    \begin{equation*}
        \lambda\, \mathrm{Id} \le \mathcal A(t,x,v)\le \Lambda\, \mathrm{Id} \qquad \text{for each }(t,x,v)\in [0,T]\times \mathbb T^3 \times \mathbb R^3.
