{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.212025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ed22e64d1021b7aedc58a194ad9bfe171e6f6e6f28161df521a34e4baf618fa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma exponential_bound_Nt of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $S \subset V$ be a finite set containing the origin. For $x \in S$ define $D_x := d_{\vec{G}}(x, S^c).$ We have that for any $t > 0$ and $x\in S:$
