{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.484118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ef3e9fa4ebf43a4e3a7d8571b159051d155e89f08cc323d4b2b6b1be6ef8b2b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 125 (Fixed-order sharpness of the uniform $(p,r)$-growth) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $K_{\boldsymbol 1,N}$ be the equal-weight diagonal kernel from
Definition~\ref{def:equal-weight-diagonal}.
Realize its chaos operator with either standard real Gaussian families or
standard circular complex Gaussian families, and let $g$ denote a
one-dimensional standard Gaussian of the chosen type.  For every
$2\le r<\infty$,
\begin{equation}

  \lim_{N\to\infty}
  \frac{\|\cT_{K_{\boldsymbol 1,N}}^{(m)}\|_{L^2(\Omega;\Sch_r)}}
       {\Prof_{m,r}(K_{\boldsymbol 1,N})}
  =\|g\|_{L^r}^m
  \asymp_m r^{m/2}.
\end{equation}
Let
\[
  K_{\mathrm{rk1}}
  :=1\in\C^{\otimes m}\otimes\conj{\C}\otimes\C.
\]
Then, for every $p\ge2$ and $2\le r<\infty$,
\begin{equation}

  \frac{\|\cT_{K_{\mathrm{rk1}}}^{(m)}\|_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}}
       {\Prof_{m,r}(K_{\mathrm{rk1}})}
  =\|g\|_{L^p}^m
  \asymp_m p^{m/2}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, in either fixed Gaussian model, if a function $B_m(p,r)$
satisfies
\[
  \|\cT_K^{(m)}\|_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
  \le B_m(p,r)\,\Prof_{m,r}(K)
\]
uniformly over all finite dimensions and all nonzero coefficient kernels in
that model, then
\begin{equation}

  B_m(p,r)\ge c_m(p+r)^{m/2},
  \qquad p\ge2,\quad 2\le r<\infty.
\end{equation}
Thus, for each fixed $m$, the best constant uniform over all finite
dimensions and coefficient kernels has two-parameter order
$(p+r)^{m/2}$, up to constants depending only on $m$.  The diagonal argument alone does not determine those comparison constants
as $m$ varies; their all-order scale was determined in
Subsection~\ref{subsec:chaos-order-growth}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.982077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ef5ae6fe961df97122506bd4cabdf7617ac8314a53bd31f90b130a77139280d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 2.2 of arXiv:2412.00708, 'Stochastic PDE approach to fluctuating interfaces'] Consider the SPDE (equation eq:2.3-1 of the paper) with $n=1$ and independent space-time
Gaussian white noises $\dot{{\mathbb W}}$ and $\dot{W}$.
Then, $\widetilde{\Psi} = \widetilde{\Psi}^{N,K}$ 
defined by (equation eq:2.stretch of the paper)
satisfies the following SPDE in law
\begin{align}  
\partial_t \widetilde{\Psi}(t,z,\underline{x}) =(- & K \mathcal{A}^K_z + \Delta_{\underline{x}})
\widetilde{\Psi}(t,z,\underline{x})  
 \\
&+ K^{3/4}\partial_z \big(g_1(\bar v^K(z))\dot{W}^1(t,z,\underline{x})\big) + K^{1/4}
g_1(\bar v^K(z)) \nabla_{\underline{x}} \cdot \dot{{\mathbb W}}^2(t,z,\underline{x})  \notag \\
& + K^{3/4} g_2(\bar v^K(z)) \dot{W}(t,z,\underline{x}),  
\notag
\end{align}
for $(z,\underline{x}) \in \sqrt{K}{\mathbb{T}} \times {\mathbb{T}}^{d-1}$, where
\begin{align} 
&\mathcal{A}^K \equiv \mathcal{A}_z^K
= - \partial_z^2 -f'(\bar v^K(z)), \quad z\in \sqrt{K}{\mathbb{T}} = [-\sqrt{K}/2,\sqrt{K}/2),
\intertext{and}  
& \Delta_{\underline{x}} = \sum_{i=2}^d \partial_{x_i}^2, \quad \underline{x}=(x_2,\ldots,x_d) \in {\mathbb{T}}^{d-1},
\end{align}
and $\dot{W}^1(t,z,\underline{x})$, 
$\dot{{\mathbb W}}^2(t,z,\underline{x}) := \{\dot{W}^i(t,z,\underline{x})\}_{i=2}^d$ and
$\dot{W}(t,z,\underline{x})$ are $d+1$ independent space-time
Gaussian white noises on $[0,\infty)\times \sqrt{K}{\mathbb{T}}\times{\mathbb{T}}^{d-1}$.

In view of the SPDE (equation eq:2.2-2 of the paper), we introduce a further scaling
\begin{align}  
\Psi(t,z,\underline{x}) \equiv \Psi^{N,K}(t,z,\underline{x}) 
:= K^{-3/4} \widetilde{\Psi}^{N,K}(t,z,\underline{x}).
\end{align}
Then, $\Psi$ satisfies the SPDE 
\begin{align}  
\partial_t \Psi = & (- K \mathcal{A}_z^K + \Delta_{\underline{x}})\Psi 
\\
& +  \partial_z \big( g_1(\bar v^K(z))\dot{W}^1(t,z,\underline{x})) + K^{-1/2}
g_1(\bar v^K(z))\nabla_{\underline{x}} \cdot \dot{{\mathbb W}}^2(t,z,\underline{x})  \notag  \\
&  + g_2(\bar v^K(z)) \dot{W}(t,z,\underline{x}),  \notag
\end{align}
for $(z,\underline{x})\in \sqrt{K}{\mathbb{T}}\times{\mathbb{T}}^{d-1}$.
Note that the noise terms for $\Psi$ behave as $O(1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

