{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.612573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f0162d49b38fef7d984f318d7b38d212e38126128d63edb966846d851c55cb1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] Assume a continuous cost ${c} \in C((\Rd)^2)$, bounded from below and satisfying the $p$-growth condition \eqref{eq:quad_bound_cost} for $p<2$, and probabilities $\mu,\nu \in \mathcal{P}^\ba_2(\Rd)$  (not necessarily in convex order).

