{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.678473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f3146a44fb28c82f041f5197f38c2244bb9d8e6bd44a61fa58515cec3cd0805","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 (Rigidity under the principal orthogonal response laws) of arXiv:2608.04993, '2608.04993'] Every orthogonally natural quadratic coefficient architecture is unique.  For
every finite-dimensional real Hilbert space $E$,
\begin{equation}
 \kappa_A^E(K)=\|K\|_{\mathcal S_2},\qquad
