\end{equation}
Consequently its dual response gauges on finite-rank state coordinates are
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{\kappa_A(K)\le1}|\operatorname{Tr}(K^*a)|=\|a\|_2,
 \qquad
 \sup_{\kappa_Q(S)\le1}|\operatorname{Tr}(Sq)|=\|q\|_1.
\end{equation}
For a separable Hilbert space $H$, compatible finite-dimensional exhaustion
therefore produces the principal response completion
\begin{equation}
 H\times\mathcal S_2(H)_{\rm sk}\times\mathcal S_1(H)_{\rm sa}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.706206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f31832b04084e59ba405bb7bcf39e1d527e860383438764ad596ceabcabba68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:hamilton_heatkernel of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let $(M,\mathfrak{g})$ be a compact smooth Riemannian manifold. Then there is a constant $C$ depending on the Ricci curvature and on the dimension of $M$ only such that 
