{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.731051+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f5cae595f1a72224dbba9805deae8bab49e29626956fab2926758d00fb85d3c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem maximum_degree of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Fix $m\in\mathbb{N}$, $c\in(0,m+1)$, and a choice sequence $\mathbf x$ such that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$ is satisfied for some $\varepsilon<1-c/(m+1)$ in Part~(item:hI of the paper) and some $\eta<1-c/(m+1)$ in Part~(item:Jn of the paper). Let $(i_n^\mathrm{a})_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ and $(i_n^\mathrm{f})_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be sequences such that $i_n^\mathrm{a}+\log_\theta A_n >0$ and $i_n^\mathrm{f}+\log_\theta F_n >0$ for all $n$, and 
