{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.675934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f63f71013a3df6c8e37fa2307397581119c7f8f682466b7e56d6707cbc70a94","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 (Side-layer committor mismatch) of arXiv:2607.20882, 'An Eyring--Kramers Law for the Hypoelliptic Third-Order\\ Langevin Diffusion'] For $N\ge0$ and $k\in\{0,1,2\}$, define
\[
\begin{aligned}
M_{\eps,\vartheta}^{-,N,k}
&:=\frac{\eps^{-N}(\vartheta\sqrt\eps)^{-k}}{Z_\eps}
\int_{\mathcal A_{\eps,\vartheta}^-}
(1-h_\eps^*)(1-j_\eps)e^{-H/\eps}\,dz,\\
M_{\eps,\vartheta}^{+,N,k}
&:=\frac{\eps^{-N}(\vartheta\sqrt\eps)^{-k}}{Z_\eps}
\int_{\mathcal A_{\eps,\vartheta}^+}
h_\eps^*j_\eps e^{-H/\eps}\,dz,\\
D_{\eps,\vartheta}^{-,N,k}
&:=\frac{\eps^{-N}(\vartheta\sqrt\eps)^{-k}}{Z_\eps}
\int_{\mathcal A_{\eps,\vartheta}^-}
(1-h_\eps^*)
\left|\Phi_\sigma'(\Lambda_\sigma/\sqrt\eps)\right|
e^{-H/\eps}\,dz,\\
D_{\eps,\vartheta}^{+,N,k}
&:=\frac{\eps^{-N}(\vartheta\sqrt\eps)^{-k}}{Z_\eps}
\int_{\mathcal A_{\eps,\vartheta}^+}
h_\eps^*
\left|\Phi_\sigma'(\Lambda_\sigma/\sqrt\eps)\right|
e^{-H/\eps}\,dz.
\end{aligned}
\]
There exists some $K_0=K_0(N,k)$, independent of $\vartheta$, such that for
$K\ge K_0$ and every fixed $\vartheta>0$,
\[
\lim_{\eps\downarrow0}
\frac{M_{\eps,\vartheta}^{-,N,k}+M_{\eps,\vartheta}^{+,N,k}
+D_{\eps,\vartheta}^{-,N,k}+D_{\eps,\vartheta}^{+,N,k}}
{\mathfrak K_{\sigma,\eps}}=0.
\]
In particular,
\[
\lim_{\vartheta\downarrow0}\limsup_{\eps\downarrow0}
\frac{M_{\eps,\vartheta}^{-,N,k}+M_{\eps,\vartheta}^{+,N,k}
+D_{\eps,\vartheta}^{-,N,k}+D_{\eps,\vartheta}^{+,N,k}}
{\mathfrak K_{\sigma,\eps}}=0.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.472101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f64a706fbb479d903a2a3626bb77edc99c1446dc1efbd82a7d5965ccf6f390d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LSI-strongly-log-concave of arXiv:2606.19763, 'Optimal Sparsification of Gaussian Processes'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure on $\R^n$ with density proportional to $e^{-V}$, where $V\in C^2(\R^n)$ satisfies $\nabla^2 V \succeq I$.
