{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.586268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f6d5858d9346f4cfd0a1049c626cc7f37f27f591a734cfb63f3cbb2c0c8293a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:SDE of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For probability measures $\Pi$ on $[0,\infty)^I$, $I\subset \IZ$, we let $\mathsf{S}_t^{gap}\Pi:=\mathsf{law}(X_t)$, where $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is  the unique weak  solution (cf.\ [pilipenko]) of the SDE \begin{align}
        dX^i_t=-dt+l^i_t+\sqrt{2}dB^i_t,\quad i\in I,
    \end{align}
    with $\mathsf{law}(X_0)=\Pi$ where
  $(B^i)_{i\in I}$ are independent standard Brownian motions and $(l^i_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is the local time of $X^i$ in $0$ for $i\in I$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.932396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f731d6d9f03e329ca20df540181cd37a8d2988bd6c21b18fc839826d8bfe2e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:wasserstein_bound_from_local of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] {3Ddimers}}]
	Suppose that $\mu$ and $\nu$ are component measures and are supported on a common compact set $R$ of dimension $d$. Suppose there is a partition of $R$ into sets $\mathcal{B} = \{B_1,...,B_K\}$ of diameter at most $\varepsilon$ such that $\bigg|\mu(B)-\nu(B) \bigg| < \delta$ for all $B\in \mathcal{B}$. If one of the measures corresponds to a discrete flow on $\frac{1}{n} \Lambda$, we {additionally} require that $1/n<\varepsilon$. Then 
	\begin{align*}
		\mathbb{W}^{1,1}_1(\mu,\nu) \leq K(10\varepsilon^{d+1} +\delta).
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.209525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f7445380ae8ce58ba9b671f8a66de9a73673617a71f39c9e0a0f3c91505b6cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] Let $(X, \lambda)$ be a descending type weighted polyhedron. 
