{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.954353+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f7c0e0d754a55c50d501ec69d58414029edd8bc6728376497e65055a522eb26","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:crossing_rectangles of arXiv:2608.17073, 'Near-critical percolation with sparse reinforcements'] For any $L \in \mathbb{Z}_+$, we define the \textbf{horizontal rectangle} $R_L^h$ and the \textbf{vertical rectangle} $R_L^v$ as the following subsets of $\mathbb{Z}^2$:
\begin{align*}
    R_L^h &= [0, 2L] \times [0, L], \\
