{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.530760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f935e5009b3c4b68a69da2001350fb054cc6ce9b7def9aad006dec5b47665f9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Deff reac-diff-domain-avg-lyap-exp of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Let $\epsilon > 0$ be arbitrary and $P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_0)$ denote the set of all invariant measures of the process $v_t \coloneqq u_t/\|u_t\|_{L^1}$ on $\mathcal{M}_0 \coloneqq \{v \in C(\overline D)_+ \mid \|v\|_{L^1} = 1\}$, where $u_t$ solves (equation reac-diff-domain-linearized of the paper). We define \begin{equation}
