{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.270277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f9d755f9ba793bf607e59b89198c4acf322cef2bb4bf41021473137ae5274c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:mtp-lindeberg-clt of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $\{X_n, \mathcal{F}_n\}_{n \geq 0}$ be a square-integrable martingale with $X_0 = 0$, and let $\{Y_n = X_n - X_{n-1}, \mathcal{F}_n\}_{n \geq 1}$ be the martingale differences. Let the cumulative variance be given by
  \(
  V_n = \sum_{i=1}^n \mathbb{E}[Y_i^2 | \mathcal{F}_{i-1}]~.
  \)
  Suppose $V_n \to \infty$ a.s., and
  for all $\delta > 0$,
  \begin{equation}

    \frac{1}{V_n} \sum_{i=1}^n \mathbb{E}\left[Y_i^2 \mathds{1}\{|Y_i| > \delta \sqrt{V_n}\} \, \middle| \, \mathcal{F}_{i-1}\right] \xrightarrow{P} 0 \quad \text{as} \ n \to \infty~.    
  \end{equation}
  Then
  \(
  \dfrac{X_n}{\sqrt{V_n}} \xrightarrow{D} N(0, 1)
  \). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.576555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f9dcd6535ed43b01ecad5384c745d87bdb4978a9e2290a161a95eedab1482b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 of arXiv:2606.14812, 'Joint convergence in Wiener chaos via transport hierarchy and Malliavin covariances'] Let $p \geq 2$ and let $(X_N = I_p(f_N), N \geq 1)$ with $f_N \in H^{\odot p}$ 
