{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.302912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3faf607850811a4edf26603d2208b93d05dc06a00b82ba0cc18d2ec595155f15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: liminf limsup of arXiv:2605.26869, 'Law of Large Numbers for a random walk on dynamic environments with drift'] Let $\eta$ be an environment satisfying~(pe:markov of the paper)-(pe:density of the paper),  (pe:drift of the paper) and (pe:couplings of the paper).  Then, for all $\rho \in J, \varepsilon > 0$, 
