{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.986114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3fc8c454c9b0e4e1e259b5276f6f100fb56012cd9f397dbe199efb95c6824557","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 52 ({\cite[Theorem 1.1) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {Mak24}}] 
    Let $\cT^\omega_{n, \beta}$ be the RSTRE as in Assumption \ref{As:K_n_U}. If $0 < \beta = \beta(n) \ll n/\log n$, then with high probability
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathcal{O}(\beta) = (1 + o(1)) \beta \frac{1 - e^{-2\beta}}{(1 -e^{-\beta})^2}.
    \end{equation}
    If on the other hand $\beta \gg n (\log n)^2$, then with high probability
