 for  $2< q< 3+\varepsilon$ and  $2< p< 2+\varepsilon$, where  $C$ depends only on $ p, q$ and $\Omega$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.239763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ffb7b707ab4cec0ce8ebab8f43e76c0f6f757e5abc344364b5c167b95fe91cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: upsilon2 of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Let $\mathbb P^0$ be a law on admissible boundary conditions $\varphi^0:=(W^0,Z^0)$. Then for every $\alpha \in (0,1)$, there exists $C>0$ such that, for every $T>0$,
