{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.067838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_400ba4c99bc0d3319357c49bef231d421cea5fb97ed1ca39f22f62fb4cb97ab0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: H-1 estimate_local_nonlinear of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $\omega$ be the global solution provided by (prop:global_well_cutoff of the paper) and $T>0$. For every $p\ge1$ there exists a constant $K(T, \nu, p)$ such that it holds
