{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.430033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_400c35cbcb8ebe61b95361e3b7e6cada43111205a6dc8ae5ba0a7881c696f925","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma thm:gaussian.mc.characterization of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] Let $\mathbb{X}^1, \ldots, \mathbb{X}^K \in \mathcal{FG}(T, d)$ be filtered Gaussian processes. 
Let \(\pi = \mathcal{L}(\widebar{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}) = \mathcal{N}_{KTd}(\mathbf{0}, \mathbf{P})\) be a jointly Gaussian coupling of $\mathbb{X}^1,\ldots,\mathbb{X}^K$, where $\mathbf{P}$ satisfies (equation eqn:P.block.condition of the paper). The following are equivalent:
