{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.019642+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4015bffd1899ba3193eed31398f91422e31207bcc4e68cf8ecc2b36ee04941b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t02 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a function $G\colon {\mathbb T}^d_N \to {\mathbb R}$, and a finite subset $A$
of ${\mathbb Z}^d$ with at least two elements. Assume that
