{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.695924+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4059f3d49bfd6bb56fc11bceddab01b2f4f213d1eaa21102a4ad45f24d7b6290","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:homogeneous_theorem of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] For the $\alpha$-stable random band  matrices   in Definition (defmodel of the paper), but with Gaussian entries and  $\alpha>d=1$, assuming that $\sum_{i=1}^s n_i$ is even   and   $t_i\in (0,\infty)$ with   $i=1,\ldots,s$,   for any given {typical} connected diagram $\Gamma\in \mathcal{T}_s$ the following hold:
