{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.332850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_407ae014aa52a0a0c2ffa8055fa4062245b70fb3d4137690371fabd6a5ca21e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:elf of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] There exists $n_0 = n_0(\varepsilon,\delta,k)$ such that for all $n \in \{n_0,n_0+1,\dots\} \setminus (U\cup V)$ we have 
