{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.255319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40a21e2c09eee5d0f23145d437eab0a0e41e0c2dacd41fe49ac5cb2b00d8f435","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: ample_Ban of arXiv:2412.07690, 'A law of large numbers concerning the distribution of critical points of random Fourier se'] An \emph{ample Banach space of sections} of $E$  is  a Banach space   ${\boldsymbol{U}}\subset   C^0(E)$   continuously embedded in $C^0(E)$  such that  \index{Banach space! ample}
\[
\forall t \in {\boldsymbol{T}},\;\;\spa\big\{\,u(t),\;\;u\in {\boldsymbol{U}}\,\big\}= E_t.
\]
Let $k\in {{\mathbb N}}$. We say that the Banach space ${\boldsymbol{U}}$ is \emph{$k$-ample} \index{Banach space! $k$-ample}  if for any \emph{distinct } points $t_1,\dotsc, t_k\in {\boldsymbol{T}}$ the map
\[
{\boldsymbol{U}}\ni u\mapsto  u(t_1)\oplus \cdots \oplus u(t_k)\in E_{t_1}\oplus \cdots \oplus E_{t_k}
\]
is onto.  \nobreak\hfill\penalty250 \hbox{}\nobreak\hfill$\rlap{$\sqcap$}\sqcup$\vskip\aline","status":"unverified"}

