{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.063436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40b254c32ab811300606595ac9590705dd97f34afc28c3e6fc12323905c1e5a1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 of arXiv:2608.19744, 'Conditioned Brownian motion and local equivalence of path ensembles'] Let $z\in\mathbb C$ satisfy $\Re z>0$.  For every
$f\in L^2(\mathbb R^d)$ and $t>0$,
\begin{equation}
  (\mathrm e^{-tH_z}f)(x)
