{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.746238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40f60d44b6df785ab4ca0ae9629bff9f47edb9e1ce205628b39e454ddd20afbe","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 17 (Frankenstein property) of arXiv:2605.02499, '2605.02499'] Let $\mathrm{P}_n$ be the set of permutations of $[n]$. A set $\mathcal{C}=\{C^{(1)},\ldots, C^{(m)}\} \subseteq \varSigma_n$ of cylinders has the \emph{Frankenstein property} if either $\mathcal{C}\subseteq \varSigma_n^R$ or there are distinct indices $\tilde{l}_1,\hat{l}_1, \tilde{l}_2,\hat{l}_2,\ldots,\tilde{l}_p,\hat{l}_p\in[m]$ such that: 
\begin{itemize}
    \item For $j \in [m]\setminus\{\tilde{l}_1,\hat{l}_1,\, \tilde{l}_2,\hat{l}_2,...,\tilde{l}_p,\hat{l}_p\}$, we have $C^{(j)} \in \varSigma_n^R$.
    \item For every $i\in[p]$, there is $\sigma_i\in \mathrm{P}_n$ such that $\big(\sigma_i(C^{(\tilde{l}_i)})\big) \cup C^{(\hat{l}_i)})\in \varSigma_n^R $.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.488912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40f6f7a7df34f0f546e2e919c5fc48a4ec4e1c378c4d4eb56ced5f503e100582","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] Under the neutrality condition $\int \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{+}+ \int \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{-}=-2$ , the value of the differential $C_{\mathbb{H}}\left[\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{+}, \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{-}\right]$ in the identity chart of $\mathbb{H}$ (and the chart $z \mapsto-1 / z$ at infinity) is given by

