{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.422424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40ff53160606babcc9f192bf87d84b45bbc66be2aa9f41086f02df13fd5d5132","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2606.09121, 'Truncated Signature Information for Mixed Fractional Brownian Paths'] Let $U\subset\R^p$ be open, let $\mu:U\to\R^d$ be continuously differentiable, and let $\theta_0\in U$.  If $J_0=D\mu(\theta_0)$ has full column rank, then there exist $r>0$ and $c>0$ such that $\overline{B}(\theta_0,r)\subset U$ and
