{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.165484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4131bdc4b4951da81c1408ed1338702ad621ea0060795f6523605daf8b672ebd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_UniformFredholmMapsAreStableUnderTransverseBaseChange of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let ${\mathbf{X}}$, ${\mathbf{Y}}$, and ${\mathbf{Z}}$ be tame Fréchet manifolds,
  $f \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace {\mathbf{X}} \to {\mathbf{Y}}$ uniformly Fredholm and
  $g \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace {\mathbf{Z}} \to {\mathbf{Y}}$ tame smooth.
  If $f$ and $g$ are \defined{transverse};
  that is: for every $(x,z) \in {\mathbf{X}} \times {\mathbf{Z}}$ with $f(x) = g(z) \eqcolon y$
  the map $T_xf + T_zg \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace T_x{\mathbf{X}} \oplus T_z{\mathbf{Z}} \to T_y{\mathbf{Y}}$ is surjective;
  then:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item
    the fibre product
    \begin{equation*}
      g^*{\mathbf{X}} \coloneq \set[\big]{ (x,z) \in {\mathbf{X}} \times {\mathbf{Z}} : f(x) = g(z) }
    \end{equation*}
    is a tame Fréchet submanifold, and
  \item
    the map $g^*f \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace g^*{\mathbf{X}} \to {\mathbf{Z}}$ is uniformly Fredholm and $\ind g^*f = \paren{\ind f} \circ f^*g$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.623934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4132001d86676b63908f39b640146e61a346d520cf8d87a19df5930263094285","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2605.12269, 'It\^o integral for a two-sided L\'evy process'] Let $p\geq 2$ be an even integer such that $m_p<\infty$. For any $\varphi \in L^2(\bR)$,
