{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.241455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_414e8e8fe60474760b1450e75dbc2785e597fd3264f5e80e0facf67b141b69c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop estimateZ of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] For any $\beta > 0,$ we have 

\begin{align}
	\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{n} \log (Z_n^{\beta,231}) &= 2 \log \left( 1+ \textup{e}^\beta \right) -\beta  - \frac{1}{\beta} \int_{\textup{e}^{-\beta}}^{\textup{e}^\beta} \frac{\log y}{1+y} \textup{d} y;\\
	\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{n} \log (Z_n^{\beta,321}) &= \frac{2}{\beta} \int_{\textup{e}^{-\beta/2}}^{\textup{e}^{\beta/2}} \frac{\log(1+y)}{y} \textup{d} y.
