{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.345484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41601b043aff52528ad91aab9991ccd4b2610450c35e50021c42127ade56866f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem heightoffset0 of arXiv:2609.01499, 'On the rigidity of sloped height functions in $d\ge 3$ \\ and non-crossing surfaces'] Consider any measure $\mu_{\mathfrak{s},a}$ in the extremal decomposition of $\mu_\mathfrak{s}$. Then, there exists some point $(x_{3},\ldots,x_{d})$ such that
