Then, there exists a coupling between {\small$\mathbf{Z}^{N}$} and the solution $\mathbf{Z}$ to (equation eq:she of the paper) with initial data {\small$\mathbf{Z}_{0,\cdot}$} from bullet point (2) above such that {\small$\mathbf{Z}^{N}_{\t,N\X}-\mathbf{Z}_{\t,\X}\to0$} locally uniformly on $[0,1]\times\R$ in probability in the large-$N$ limit. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.305740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_416bcf47bd135f88475fa3cb2a84a653fd8abdab03ed6ed8f30d77ad0677141f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.24167, '\bf On the stability of rarefaction for stochastic viscous conservation law'] Let $\phi\in X_1(T)$ be the solution of \eqref{perturbation}. Then for any $T>0$ we have the following $L^p$ estimates.
		\begin{enumerate}
		    \item [\rm{1.}] {\noindent If $p=2$, then  \text { {\rm{a.s.}}}
            \begin{equation}
			\begin{aligned}
				& \|\phi(t)\|^2 + \int_0^t \|\phi_x\|^2 ds + \int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{R}}\phi^2  \bar{u}_{x} d x ds\\
                \leq&   \| \phi_0 \|^2 +C \ln (1+t)+ 2 \int_0^t \int_ \mathbb R \sum_{i=1}^{\infty} \partial_x \sigma_i (\phi +\bar u) |\phi|^{p-2}  \dif x~\dif B_i(s),
