{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.564652+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_417859174cf1db08b6bade45be353296493bca80ecff64ef70f7e87a8b16a682","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2608.27249, 'Torus actions, almost non-negative curvature and fundamental groups'] For all \(m\in \mathbb{N}\), there is a constant \(0<C(m)<\infty\), such that the fundamental group of every almost non-negatively curved closed manifold \(M\) of dimension \(m\), which is homotopy equivalent to a closed manifold \(N\) such that \(N\) admits an action of a torus \(T\) which has a minimal stratum consisting of a single orbit, contains a abelian subgroup of index \(<C(m)\).

