{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.693107+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41953bad0d32346e74fb273b7f0c4fa0a950c3b37f97f269a8b9d4a136d5188a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 18 of arXiv:2607.29534, 'Expected signatures via partial integration, coordinate change and symmetrization'] Let $p>2$ and let $q\geq 1$ be such that $1/p+1/q>1$. For any pair $(A,\RP{X})\in C^{q\text{-var}}([0,T];\R^m)\times \mathscr{C}^{p\text{-var},0}_g([0,T];\R^d)$, we define now the $T((\mathbb{R}^d))$-valued path $\{\mathbf{S}(Y)_{s,t}:(s,t)\in \Delta_{0,T}^2\}$ in $\Psi$-coordinates  \begin{equation}
