{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.303127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41a5fb1d690763d406b4e9cce8f06d51fac8ca352d4075b64393bc61651ea11a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2608.21787, 'Stability of extremal hyperplane projections of balls in $\ell_p^n(\R)$'] There exists a positive constant $c_{\infty}'$ such that for every $n \ge 1$ and every vector $a = (a_1, \ldots, a_n) \in \R^n$ with $\sum_{i=1}^na_i^2 = 1$ and $a_1 \ge a_2 \ge \ldots \ge a_n \ge 0$ we have
