{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.654446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41b9302bbbdb4dcf08231b79ed230bd91920eb00ce5ac7ab6d7ae8477a5ed548","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Z_n-partition of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] Let $Z_n$ be given by (equation e:unt of the paper) and $\mathcal{P}_n$ be the projection to the first $n$ coordinates. Then for any $F \in \mathcal{F}$ with $\mathbb E|Z_n F| < \infty$ or $F \geq 0$, we have that
