{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.790224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41d06d972284a47bc5cdc17b7a68e4e19e40a3334867134fd305f50136998254","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:z_smooth of arXiv:2412.04328, 'The critical Karp--Sipser core of Erdős--Rényi random graphs'] There is a smooth function $\widetilde{z} : [0,+\infty) \to [0,+\infty)$ such that for all $v>0$ and $s \geqslant 0$, we have $z(v,s)=\widetilde{z} \left( \frac{s}{v} \right)$. Moreover, we have
