{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.994915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_41e630385dbf3cf05aacd997fc3b61f8af8f570241da558b97e94b5f1db4dc00","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 (Gaussian-rate super-Poincar\'e inequality) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There are $A_{\gamma,Q},B_{\gamma,Q}<\infty$ such that, for all $s>0$,
