{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.857756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_423914cb61c85e447693abb8538b3b21a8de21b4d321dd0e0e9a22436f31f9d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 (Deya, Norredine, Nourdin, \cite{MR3089666}) of arXiv:2511.20875, 'Double $q$-Wigner Chaos and the Fourth Moment'] Let $f_k$ be a sequence of {\bf fully} symmetric functions in $L^2(\mathbb{R}^n_+)$ with $\|f_k\|_2\to 1$ as $k\to\infty$.  Then the following three conditions are equivalent.
