{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.774981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42627ee48546a321df0076f29d60a22a243961110c3920bd13010931a9c2fea9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] Let $h>0$. There is a coupling such that the clusters of loops and excursions (in the union of $\wt\Lc^{1/2}_N$ and $\Xi^h_N$) correspond to the sign clusters of $\mphi_{N}+h$ in the following way. 
