{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.055073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_426d966594d9f9e1a0373493d4aba30f48207ebb954c940c54720a0e34a739ce","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition DO noise def of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] Let $H\in (0,1)$. The Dobri\'c-Ojeda noise is a centered Gaussian noise with covariance function given by 
\begin{align*}
        E[\dot{W}(s,x)\dot{W}(t,y)] = s^{H-1/2}t^{H-1/2}\delta_0(t-s)f(x-y),
\end{align*} 
where $t,s > 0$, $x,y \in {\mathbb R}^d$. More rigorously, the Dobri\'c-Ojeda noise is defined similarly as $W_0$, but where the inner product $\langle \cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}$ is replaced by
\begin{equation} 
 \langle \varphi , \psi \rangle_{\mathcal{H}}:=
\int_{[0,\infty)} \int_{{\mathbb R}^{2d}}
\varphi(s,y)\psi(s,z) s^{2H-1} f(y-z) \, dy dz ds.   
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.358294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42714b3de9f734a2b8c0982f3a1ebeddae2dd0cab8a374d0a866c824305f4e08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:frontier-ledger of arXiv:2608.23860, 'Revelation Control'] Writing $\Delta_{\rm rev}=V_B(\mathscr G)-V_B(\mathscr H)$,
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
V_P(\hat\pi_A)-V_R(\hat\pi_F)
=
\Delta_{\rm rev}+P_A+R_F-R_A.
}

\end{equation}
If resources $K_A,K_F$ are priced by $\lambda$, then net value satisfies
\begin{equation}
N_A-N_F
=
\Delta_{\rm rev}+P_A+R_F-R_A
+\lambda^\top(K_F-K_A).
\end{equation}
At equal resource cost, a sufficient condition for active victory is $\Delta_{\rm rev}+P_A>R_A-R_F$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

