{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.501096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4279436cc0a1dbc0d567e536edaf4cd9cc5cd414ddf39158c9a62b31fa1ad49b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Contribution of loops of given diameter) of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] There exist~$C,c\in(0,\infty)$ such that for every~$\lambda>0$,~$0<\eta<1$, and~$0<\delta<\eps$,
