{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.402649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_427bc48d95df7eb3ea81fccb491968ac67bd3282f16852ee02b1d92bab276f68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] For every compact connected two-step pair there are $c>0$ and $N\ge0$ such that, as $t\downarrow0$,
		\[
		p_t(e)=C_{G,L}t^{-Q/2}e^{\beta_{G,L}t}
		+O(t^{-N}e^{-c/t}).
		\]
		Moreover, with the orthonormal bases $Y_a$ of $\lLie$ and $X_i$ of $\pLie$ fixed in \Cref{sec:preliminaries}, and with all norms induced by the fixed invariant inner product,
		\[
		\beta_{G,L}
		=\frac{\operatorname{Scal}_G-\operatorname{Scal}_L}{6}
		=\frac1{12}\sum_{a,i}|[Y_a,X_i]|^2
		+\frac1{24}\sum_{i,j}|[X_i,X_j]|^2,
		\]
		and $C_{G,L}$ admits the root-theoretic integral and the absolutely convergent positive multiple Dirichlet series of \Cref{zeta:complete-local-constants}. Consequently the formulas determine every local heat coefficient, every zeta residue, and every nonpositive zeta value. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_427e699bf0a7fee4714c8b362d2e834a2e4410ebbccf2f88a0465c152e24ca5d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defi2.3 of arXiv:2608.22945, 'A Momentum-Based Variance-Reduced Algorithm for Federated Multiobjective Optimization'] An iterate $x^t$ generated by a stochastic algorithm is said to be an \emph{$\epsilon$-Pareto stationary solution in expectation} if
\begin{equation*}
	\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{G}(x^t)\right] \leq \epsilon,
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation*}
	\mathcal{G}(x):=\min_{\lambda\in\mathcal{C}}
	\left\|\sum_{s=1}^{S}\lambda_s\nabla f_s(x)\right\|^2.
\end{equation*}
The expectation is taken with respect to all the randomness generated by the algorithm up to iteration $t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.794926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_427fb22d99cb79988ff20fbee99373f454cb61bdc47a938502048db4b7aba5b4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop CG1P3.1 of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] Consider $u_{\varepsilon, y}(x,t)=\mathbb E[\Psi_{\varepsilon}(y)\Psi_{\varepsilon}(x,t)]$. Then, there are $c<C\in \mathbb R$, such that
    \begin{equation*}
        c+ \ln\left (\frac{1}{|x-y|\lor \sqrt{|t|}\lor \varepsilon}\right ) 
        \leq 
        u_{\varepsilon, y}(x,t)
        \leq 
        C+ \ln\left(\frac{1}{|x-y|\lor \sqrt{|t|}\lor \varepsilon}\right).
    \end{equation*}
