{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.188643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42b18ccf2a6bbbc7f457fb295ee0b1d6f46d7c48df7f32c9d2136ef8971b12e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2606.30938, 'Poissonian potential measures for refracted-reflected L\'evy processes'] Let $q \geq 0$. Then, for  $\lambda,\gamma > 0$, $x,b \in [0,a]$ and $u \in [0,\infty)$,
			\begin{align}
