{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.881991+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42b7789b36390219906845ab4bc3fe679616c84c6848b6b955ee93106cd6544d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:mainZKROK of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $\mathcal{X}_1\randin C^\infty\left(M,\mathbb{R}^{k_1}\right),\ldots,\mathcal{X}_n\randin C^\infty\left(M,\mathbb{R}^{k_n}\right)$ be independent admissible random fields such that $k_1+\cdots+k_n=m$ and let $U\subset M$ be an open set, we have:
