{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.657371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42d2c285f5a92496ba1632c7b1ac3aba986715f7f9e359ec62472736cc62c1db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma bounded_ratio_vertices of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$. There exists a constant $C_{\varepsilon} > 0$ such that for all $g \ge 0$ and $n \ge 2g-1$ with $\frac{g}{n} \le \frac{1}{2} - 4\varepsilon$ and for all $p_1,\dots,p_{\ell} \ge 1$ with $|\mathbf{p}| \le \varepsilon n$,
