{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.852282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42eaa6e92444e6194379d7aeb2d9091ed5c35b5f7b477feabf3c3641489844dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Secular equation for the eigenvalues) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] If $g_j=0$ for some $j$, then $\lambda^{(N)}_j$ remains an eigenvalue of $H_{N+1}$ with eigenvector
