{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.301380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4313134e151945e67dd1e8d9eb727bf4e622d08446be427d707228c2ba1e1e9f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:resultunknownmask of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Consider any fixed $p \in (0,1)$. Then, the following holds whenever $d \gg \log(n)^3$.

