{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.501723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43186e3a28fa262e7ce60ab2c013ca7761270986cb3a3b0de1ac445401bbaf3e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 4 of arXiv:2607.04730, 'Variance gamma approximation to sums of triplewise independent random variables'] The VG distribution with parameters $r>0$, $\theta\in\mathbb{R}$, $\sigma>0$, $\mu\in\mathbb{R}$ has probability density function
\begin{equation}
p(x)=\frac{1}{\sigma\sqrt{\pi}\,\Gamma\!\left(\frac{r}{2}\right)}
e^{\frac{\theta}{\sigma^{2}}(x-\mu)}
\left(\frac{|x-\mu|}{2\sqrt{\theta^{2}+\sigma^{2}}}\right)^{\frac{r-1}{2}}
K_{\frac{r-1}{2}}
\left(
\frac{\sqrt{\theta^{2}+\sigma^{2}}}{\sigma^{2}}|x-\mu|
\right),
\end{equation}
with support $\mathbb{R}$. Here $K_{\nu}(x)$ is a modified Bessel function of the second kind, defined by $K_{\nu}(x)=\int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-x\cosh(t)}\cosh(\nu t)\,dt.$ For a rv $Z$ with density \eqref{den:VG}, we write $Z\sim \mathrm{VG}(r,\theta,\sigma,\mu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.142932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_431922dc09ad7fcb2d59a1eac7c47121516be62f6936c11cba116b91ba77bb47","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Scalar Cauchy information-estimation identity) of arXiv:2608.11031, 'A Bayesian Proof of the Bernoulli Theorem'] Let $U$ be a finitely supported real random variable, let $S$ be an arbitrarily distributed random variable, and let $Z$ be standard Cauchy and independent of
$(U,S)$.  Define
\begin{equation}
  F(t):=I(U;U+tZ\mid S).

\end{equation}
Then $F$ is decreasing and convex on $(0,\infty)$, with
$\lim_{t\to\infty}F(t)=0$.
Moreover, let $U_t^{(1)},U_t^{(2)}$ be i.i.d.\ draws from the
posterior of $U$ given $(S,U+tZ)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  F''(t)
  \le
  \frac{2}{t^2}
  \E\left[
    1\wedge
    \frac{|U_t^{(1)}-U_t^{(2)}|^2}{t^2}
  \right].

\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
  -F'(t)
  \le
  2\int_t^\infty
  \frac{1}{s^2}
  \E\left[
    1\wedge
    \frac{|U_s^{(1)}-U_s^{(2)}|^2}{s^2}
  \right]ds.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.484424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4319423a3b420bcaca1e4b6451377c49415913ce992ba2ccd84d15a9eefde6e3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 19 (Gaussian dense-sampling limit) of arXiv:2608.17927, 'Near-unit-root persistence of symmetric stable \\ autoregressive sequences'] For $\alpha = 2$,
