{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.876553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43196956d0875a24c953a38e797b136c3dbef427c9abbd3006b840d03ddb4921","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:chain of arXiv:2608.09368, 'A proof of Ross's conjecture for two-site moving-target search'] Let $H,L\in\{1,2\}^n$ be a height-one pair.  Then $L$ can be
transformed into $H$ by a finite sequence of adjacent moves
