{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.354387+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_431bf7fb221473a09d24e8b00eb6491aaaedc16eb8836deb750acec66e396daf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:main-err-decomp of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Let \(0 = t_0 < t_1 < \ldots < t_N \leq T\) be the time discretization. Recall \(s_t\), \(\widehat s_t\) from~(eq:score-func,eq:our-shat of the paper), and \(\widetilde s_t\) from~(def:wt-score of the paper). Then,
    \begin{equation*}
       \mathsf{KL}(q_{T - t_N} \| p_{\mathrm{output}}) \leq \mathsf{KL}(q_T \| q_{\mathrm{noise}}) + \sum_{k=0}^{N -1}\cL_{\mathrm{approx}}^{(k)} + \sum_{k=0}^{N - 1}\cL_{\mathrm{discr}}^{(k)}, 
    \end{equation*}
    where, for \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\), \(u = T - t_{k+1}\), and \(\ell = T - t_k\),
    \begin{equation}

    \cL_{\mathrm{approx}}^{(k)} \coloneqq \int_u^{\ell} \bE_{x_t, x_\ell \sim q_{t, \ell}} \left[ \sum_{y \neq x_t} Q_t(y, x_t) \widetilde s_t(y, x_t) D(\widehat s_t(y, x_t), \widetilde s_t(y, x_t))\right] \mathrm{d} t
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}

    \cL_{\mathrm{discr}}^{(k)} \coloneqq \int_u^{\ell} \bE_{x_t, x_\ell \sim q_{t, \ell}} \left[ \sum_{y \neq x_t} Q_t(y, x_t)  s_t(y, x_t) D(\widetilde s_t(y, x_t), s_t(y, x_t))\right] \mathrm{d} t.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

