{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.389672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_435db68f22ea586c33ed4ba54d29335b4c88e476c9ddc18b40235d847a9fd92c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-rw-coupling of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] For each $z\in\mathcal V\mathcal G$, there is a coupling of $\{Y^n\}_{n \geq n_z}$, each started from $Y^n_0 = z$, such that
