{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.505573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4381f397afc2f339c2b1e76591f6b5ba021d7566be776e5b9fe6d7179a676e65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] Let $\theta$ be an almost surely finite stopping time with
$u_\theta\in C^\gamma$, and let $M\ge M_\bullet$ be an
$\mathcal F_\theta$ measurable integer with $m(\rho_\theta)\le M$.  Define
\begin{align*}
 d_{\theta,M}
 &=\inf\{t\ge0:m(\rho_{\theta+t})\le L_M\},\notag\\
 e_{\theta,M}
 &=\inf\{t\ge0:m_2(\rho_{\theta+t})>M\},\notag\\
 c_{\theta,M}&=e_{\theta,M}\wedge H_M.
\end{align*}
For every $N<\infty$ there are $C_N,R_N<\infty$ such that
\begin{align}
 \mathbf P_\theta\{d_{\theta,M}>H_M\}
 +\mathbf P_\theta\{e_{\theta,M}\le H_M\}
 \le C_NM^{-N}U_\theta^{R_N},
 \qquad U_\theta=1+\|u_\theta\|_{C^\gamma}.

\end{align}
For every $q<\infty$ there are $C_q,R_q<\infty$ such that
\begin{align}
 \mathbf E_\theta
 \|\mathsf p_{\theta+c_{\theta,M}}\|_{H^1}^q
 \le C_qM^qU_\theta^{R_q}.

\end{align}

Starting at an arbitrary finite stopping time $S$ with
$u_S\in C^\gamma$, there is an adapted geometrically descending
construction and a terminal time $\eta_S$ such that
\begin{align*}
 0<\eta_S-S\le T_{\rm it}
\end{align*}
and, for every $r<\infty$,
\begin{align}
 \mathbf E_S\|\mathsf p_{\eta_S}\|_{H^1}^{2r}
 \le C_rU_S^{R_r}.

\end{align}
The deterministic horizon is independent of $S$, of the initial fibre
direction, and of the requested moment order.","status":"unverified"}

