{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.404009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_440810154b1f114a44405b90adac872116464cfb3c951e98d269b276e526148f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:hitting_prob of arXiv:2607.25428, 'The local weak limit of the minimum spanning arborescence in the complete graph'] Fix $k>{\sf T}_{\mathsf{stg1}}$ and let $A \subset V_k \setminus X_k$. Let $H_A$ be the event that the local CLEB process hits $\cont(A)$ in step $k+1$. Then 
