{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.775629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44087ef4273e4c515d0a893c2a8a52df4da59888867854b5d851c829ac965700","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LB_lemma_3 of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $s := \alpha + d$. For each $p > \frac{s + 1}{2d - s}$ and each $C_4 > 0$ there is $C_3 = C_3(C_4, p) \in (0, \infty)$ such that for each $C' \ge C_4$ the quantity 
