Equivalently, $\mathrm{trans}(\widetilde{g}) \equiv 1 \mod 2 \iff \tr(A) < 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.435601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_440b8b19a0dfb91f9f97047b9f6cdaaaece2e705eab199546cc12f6c84e3c00f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:moment_bound_empirical of arXiv:2608.23938, 'Generalization, memorization, and overfitting \\for diffusion models trained in the lazy h'] Suppose that Assumptions~(ass:high_dim of the paper) and~(ass:input_dist of the paper) hold. Then, for every \(\zeta\in (0,1)\),
