{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.673629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_440c455fff9453aac82485e78eb53cbb867bb7a1d0514c87aad79b5334d54d0a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:kernel of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] Let \( K : T \times T \to \mathbb{R} \) be a positive definite function.
