{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.139094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_443f8467926af2398aa5e73ef23f4fc45b540505fcaad19536326d28c7c3d93e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:je-wt-disc of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] Fix a stepsize $h>0$ and let $t^-=h\left\lfloor\frac th\right\rfloor$.
    Consider a discrete-time process
    \[
\widetilde{y}_{t+h} = \widetilde{y}_t + h\widehat{f}(\widetilde{y}_t) + \sqrt h \xi_t , \quad \xi_t\sim \mathcal N(0,I_n), \quad \text{for }t=kh, \,k\in \mathbb N_0.
