{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.906895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_445d56fdda54855371f1654088ac3ac08ba0d773890e8930e57c5b06e5184abd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:hyp-expo of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let $ \mathsf{S}$ the spectral measure of a $ L^{ 2}_{ loc}$ weakly stationary random measure~ $ \mathsf{M}.$
Assume $ \mathsf{S}$ admits exponent $ \alpha>0 $. Let $ f$ an $ \mathsf{S}-$admissible function  {of $   \mathscr  F_{ \gamma }^{ *}(\mathbb{R}^{ d})$. Then} 
\begin{align*}
 \textrm{Var}\left(\mathsf{M}(f_{R})\right) =   
 \begin{cases} 
 O(R^{d-\min(\alpha ,\gamma )  })$  id $\alpha \neq \gamma  .\\
 O(R^{ d-\alpha }\ln(R)))$  if $\alpha  =  \gamma . 
  \end{cases}
