In this case we say that $ \mathsf{M}$ is  {\it  $ \alpha $-hyperuniform.}

If conversely $  \textrm{Var}\left(\mathsf{P}(f_{ R})\right) = O(R^{ d-\alpha })$ holds for some $ \mathsf{S}$-admissible function $ f$ with $ \int_{}f\neq 0$, then $ \mathsf{S}$ admits exponent $ \alpha $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

