{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.703996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4476d87e8eb84d38c0a83c7718df5584bf0cbd2f4072a5ace8fcd2f6e0c067e8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 25 of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Assume \textnormal{(A1)-(A5)}. For every $\epsilon\in[0,\epsilon_0]$, the invariant law $\mu_\epsilon^*$ from Corollary~\ref{Cor1} belongs to $\mathcal P_q(H)$, and $\{\mu_\epsilon^*\}$ is the $\mathfrak D_P$-global attractor of $\varphi_P^\epsilon$. Define
	\begin{align}
		\Psi^\epsilon(t,\omega)x
		=\varphi_H^\epsilon(t,\omega,x,\mu_\epsilon^*),
	\end{align}
	let $\Pi_H(x,\mu)=x$, and set $\mathcal A_H^\epsilon=\Pi_H\mathcal A^\epsilon$. Then $\Psi^\epsilon$ is a continuous random dynamical system on $H$, $\mathcal A_H^\epsilon$ is its unique $\mathfrak D_H$-pullback random attractor, and there exists a measurable random equilibrium $\xi_\epsilon:\Omega_0\to H$ such that
	\begin{align}
		\mathcal A_H^\epsilon(\omega)
		&=\{\xi_\epsilon(\omega)\},\\
		\mathcal A^\epsilon(\omega)
