		&=\mu_\epsilon^*.
	\end{align}
	Consequently, $u_\epsilon(t,\omega)=\xi_\epsilon(\theta_t\omega)$ is a stationary variational solution of \eqref{Eq3} with one-time law $\mu_\epsilon^*$.","status":"unverified"}

