{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.568383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4486db02720cbf0ce5822373dbd0c008a339ceb33e36fca6430b94fb461e3713","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thme 57 (the two-nut case; Theorems \ref{thm:twonut_typeI} and \ref{thm:twonut_models}) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Let $\widehat{M}$ be a compact two-nut closing of $I \times P$ with the circle-bundle ansatz \eqref{eq:ansatz}, and let $g(t)$, $t \in [0, T)$, be a K\"ahler-Ricci flow of ansatz metrics with maximal existence time $T < \infty$. Then, the singularity at $T$ is of Type I, and the blow-up limit splits as $(\Sigma, g_\Sigma(t)) \times (\mathbb{C}^k, \textrm{flat})$, where $(\Sigma, g_\Sigma(t))$ is one of the following:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\mathbb{CP}^{m_0+m_\ell+1}$ with the shrinking Fubini--Study metric, when the fibers collapse;
