{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.231674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44ae0e94c63f2e995799ccd7c02966fb3d090741d52f1b5dc2fe10fd00783cbb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 37 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\phi \in \B(\A,\rmM_k)_+$ be $\l$-normal, and form this $k$-tuple in $H_\l^{\oplus k}$:
	\begin{equation}
	\xi_i = [0,\dots,0,\xi,0,\dots,0]^\rm{T} \qquad (i=1,2,\dots,k),
	\end{equation}
	where only the $i^\rm{th}$ coordinate of $\xi_i$ is nonzero. Then there is a unique non-negative operator $T$ affiliated to $\l^{\oplus k}(\A)'$ such that $\xi_i \in \rm{dom}\,T$ for each $i$ and $\phi$ is associated to $\l^{\oplus k}$ by $T\xi_1$, \dots, $T\xi_k$. \qed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.804257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44af46ddcd44bb2f3cd7bfbb6ea6d2f477c482757ce04fa998f05d70c232c1e2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:hypercube-entropy of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] As $n \to \infty$ with $k = \frac{n}{4}\log n + \alpha n$, the spectral entropy satisfies
\[
S_{\mathrm{spec}}(k) =
\begin{cases}
\Omega(\log n), & \alpha \to -\infty, \\[2pt]
e^{-4\alpha} + O(e^{-8\alpha}), & \alpha = O(1), \\[2pt]
e^{-4\alpha} + o(1) \to 0, & \alpha \to +\infty.
\end{cases}
\]
The collapse from $\Omega(\log n)$ to $0$ occurs continuously over the window $\alpha = O(1)$, corresponding to $\Delta k = O(n)$ steps---precisely the cutoff phenomenon.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.118425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44b080cb3fdfcd13697e967a200c77847d70e408eb1996d52f6d80b1d1f25f0a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2604.04823, '2604.04823'] Make the Assumptions~\ref{a:criticalpts} and~\ref{a: nondegeneracy} on~$U$.
Define a signed distance function~$d:\T^d \to [0,\infty)$ as
\begin{equation}
