{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.738390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44d950680a2928a1997071e0e11b3c1c296de1f80f11403378dd46a225aa6618","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:monotonecurve of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a $C^0$-foliation on $\mathbb{T}^2$, and $\gamma : S^1 \rightarrow \mathbb{T}^2$ be a piecewise $C^1$ closed embedded curve on $\mathbb{T}^2$. We say that $\gamma$ is \textbf{positively (resp.~negatively) monotone} with respect to $\mathcal{G}$ if $\gamma$ decomposes into finitely many $C^1$ subarcs, each of which is either
\begin{itemize}
    \item Contained in a leaf of $\mathcal{G}$, or
