{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.728373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_450509705aa4ccced9646a18a7a645b019f42fa940728d1dbba7b6835baeb222","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem-energy-equality of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] Assume further that $ \beta=\alpha/2.$	Let $\mathcal{C}_0\subset \mathbb{X}_{\alpha,\alpha/2}$ be a weak-strong uniqueness class of (equation PDE-SQG of the paper) such that $\mathcal{C}=\overline{\mathcal{C}_0}^{\mathcal{I}}$ contains non-empty time-reversible subsets. Let $\mathcal{R} \subset \mathcal{C}$ satisfy  $\mathcal{R}=\mathfrak{T}_T \mathcal{R}.$  Suppose that $ \theta\in \mathcal{R} $ is  a weak solution of (equation PDE-SQG of the paper) for some $g \in L^2([0, T];H)$ in the sense of Definition (def-weak-solution-skeleton-equation of the paper). Then the kinetic energy equality holds:
