{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.911549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4547e7767f0b7f43c8d3ee3126782072986f435ce7949bb5fd1a3b48a3b8acd7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ItoWentzel of arXiv:2511.12692, 'A stochastic flow approach to De Giorgi--Nash--Moser estimates for SPDE\lowercase{s} with '] Let $u\colon \Omega\times (0,T]\to H^1_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d) $, $f\colon \Omega\times [0,T] \to H^{-1}_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d)$ and $g\colon \Omega\times [0,T] \to L^2_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d;\ell^2)$ be progressively measurable with $u\in L^2(0,T; H^1_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d))$, $f\in L^1(0,T; H^{-1}_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d) )$ and $g\in L^2(0,T; L^2_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d;\ell^2) )$,  almost surely. We assume that almost surely
	\begin{equation*}
		u_t \,=\, u_0 \,+\, \int_0^t f_s\,\mathrm{d} s\,+\, \sum_{n\geq 1}\int_0^t g_{n,s}\, \mathrm{d} w_s^n
	\end{equation*}
	for all $t\in [0,T]$
	for an ${\mathscr F}_0$-measurable $u_0\colon \Omega \to L^2_{{\rm loc}}({\mathbb R}^d)$.
	Additionally, let $\mu:[0,\infty)\times\Omega\times{\mathbb R}^d\to {\mathbb R}^d$ and $\sigma:[0,\infty)\times\Omega\times{\mathbb R}^d\to \ell^2({\mathbb R}^d)$ be $\mathcal{P}\otimes \mathcal{B}({\mathbb R}^d)$-measurable coefficient functions satisfying Assumption (Ass:Ck_alpha of the paper) for $k=2$ and some $\alpha\in (0,1]$  and $\xi$ be the associated stochastic flow of $C^2$-diffeomorphisms satisfying  (equation eq:SDE_2 of the paper) provided by Theorem (Thm:Ck of the paper). Then it holds almost surely,  for all $t\in [0,T]$
		\begin{align}
		\begin{split}
			u_t\circ \xi_t &= u_0 + \int_0^t f_s\circ \xi_s\, \mathrm{d} s + \sum_{n\geq 1}\int_0^t g_{n,s}\circ \xi_s\, \mathrm{d} w_s^n\\ & \quad +
			\sum_{j=1}^d  \int_0^t [(\partial_j u_s)\circ \xi_s]  \mu^j_s(\xi_s)  \,\mathrm{d} s + \sum_{n\geq 1}\sum_{j=1}^d \int_0^t [(\partial_j u_s)\circ \xi_s] \, \sigma^j_{n,s}(\xi_s)  \,\mathrm{d} w_s^n
			\\ &\quad + \sum_{n\geq 1} \sum_{j=1}^d  \int_0^t [(\partial_j g_{n,s})\circ \xi_s]\sigma_{n,s}^j(\xi_s) \,\mathrm{d} s
			\, + \frac12 \sum_{n\geq 1} \sum_{i,j=1}^d  \int_0^t [(\partial_i \partial_j u_s)\circ \xi_s] \sigma_{n,s}^i(\xi_s)\sigma_{n,s}^j(\xi_s) \,\mathrm{d} s,
		\end{split}
	\end{align}
	as continuous, $H_{{\rm loc}}^{-1}({\mathbb R}^d)$-valued processes. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

