		U_{h;M,Q}'({\hat x}_0)=U_{h;0,0}'({\hat x}_1)
	\end{align*}
	(suppressing from the notation the dependence of $\hat{x}_1$ on $\hat{x}_0$ and $Q$.)
		The choice $M=-2{\hat x}_0-\eta$, for sufficiently small $\eta>0$, has the following property: for each fixed $h'\in(0,h]$, there is a constant
		$c=c(h',h,{\hat x}_0)>0$, such that
		\begin{align}
			\partial_hU_{h';M,Q}({\hat x}_0)-\partial_hU_{h';0,0}({\hat x}_1^{[-2 {\hat x}_0-\eta]})
			\ge cQ\eta.

		\end{align}
                For $0<\varepsilon<h$ one has $\inf\{ c(h',h,{\hat x}_0):h'\in [\varepsilon,h]\}>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

