{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.368690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45ad20f56fd7ad4b9136040c430cffe2d006026f8335cc5a69c4fa60d42a1003","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] The following definition is taken from \cite[Section 3.4]{ethier2009markov}. A set of functions $D \subset B(X)$ over a space $X$ is \textit{separating} if for any measures $\mu$ and $\nu$ on $X$, if 
