{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.125954+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45c8ce28afd994e960510f6851c4ba4777f599a63582ad603e787bb2b338ecd7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2510.01838, 'Shadow and percolation I: discrete landscapes with independence'] Let $A\subset \mathbb{Z}$ be a finite subset, $A=\{a_1,a_2,\dots,a_n\}$ with $a_1<a_2<\dots<a_n$.
