 \mathsf M_u'(t)
    =
    -\sum_{x\in X}\kappa(x)\,\phi(u(t,x))
\end{equation}
for almost every $t\in(0,T)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:54.905458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45cc1810a2cfcb35f4e35034c8a22e040936393bbbbb02519c84cbb8d331da12","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ck-cube of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] \leavevmode
