    \end{center}
    \begin{center}
      \AxiomC{$ $}
      \ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.461122+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45cd723b37be34cb1e3fcda6cd22d1b90076f5d620eb7c8c4375c6a4bd527de0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 (The almost Riemann invariants) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] We define the \emph{almost Riemann invariants away from symmetry} $\almostRiemann_{(\pm)}$ as follows:
