{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.334332+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45de4bf9f559527f50602ff493410fe2b591a29b698c94276e2e085583e5936a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] Let \(A \subset \{1,\ldots,n\}\) and choose arbitrary \(\epsilon > 0\). Then, for some \(C_{t,\epsilon}, c_\epsilon > 0\), independent of \(n\), we have
