{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.976889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45e614f2f522ecb466dbd5bfcc6c8393803c2ca62e12defe511f50683ec86431","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2606.15203, 'The existence of invariant sublinear expectations for $G\text{-}$SDEs'] Let $ X_T=x+\int^T_0 b(X_s)ds+B_T$, where $X_0=x \in \mathbb{R}^d$ is the initial value, $b$ is a Lipschitz continuous function, $B$ is a d-dimensional $G\text{-}$Brownian motion. Then for each $\varphi \in C_{b,lip}(\mathbb{R}^{d })$, for fixed $0 \leq T < \infty$, the G-expectation can be equivalently defined by
