{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.193963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46006f26b1e068d2eb2310bccdd882404505103936664ee8bf94aaeeb3d47f18","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] For fixed $\mu$ such that $\mu(V_k)<1$ and for fixed $\varepsilon$, there exists $\chi=\chi(\mu,\varepsilon),\rho=\rho(\mu,\varepsilon),\varphi=\varphi(\mu,\varepsilon)>0$ such that the following holds. For any sequence of $(\chi,\rho,\varphi)$-almost-$\mu$-like shuffles with deterministic pile sizes $\bn^{(t)}=(n_0^{(t)},\cdots,n_{k-1}^{(t)})$,
		\begin{align}

			\lim_{N\to\infty} d_{\TV}
            \big(\bP(\vec\bn,\lfloor(1-\varepsilon)\overline{C}_{\mu}\log(N)\rfloor),\nu_{\Unif}\big)
            &=
