{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4615ae867cac6245fa91832bf1cc366268bfd90d262991739dfa19aec73030e0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 45 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite graph and $\beta\geq 0$. If $\mathsf{h},\mathsf{h}'\in (\mathbb R^+)^V$ satisfy $\mathsf{h}\leq \mathsf{h}'$ and $v\in V$, then
