{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.764734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_461748aa93c243108b85ec01c12287a819758568508b62bacdbe1105ffcefc80","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem descents technical of arXiv:2603.09008, 'On the statistics of random-to-top shuffles'] Let $K_n$ be a sequence of random variables satisfying the following assumptions.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $K_n/n\to a\in (0,1)$ in probability.
        \item $n^{-1/2}(K_n-\mathbb{E} K_n)\Rightarrow_d\mathcal{N}(0,\tau^2)$ for some fixed $\tau\in[0,\infty)$.
        \item $\operatorname{Var} K_n=O(n)$ and $\mathbb{E}[K_n]=an+o(\sqrt{n})$.
    \end{enumerate} 
    Let $U_i$ be iid continuous uniform on $(0,1)$. Set $T_n=\sum_{i=1}^{\lfloor K_n\rfloor -1}\, \1(U_i>U_{i+1})$. We have
    \[\frac{T_n-\mathbb{E} [T_n]}{\sqrt{n}}\Rightarrow_d\,\mathcal{N}\left(0,\frac{a}{12}+\frac{\tau^2}{4}\right).\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.400708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4617edc57c9b965849abd78860272c24f5f4ea788baacc12ac5f0224254dbec5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Fair STIT of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Suppose that $F$ is a splitting distribution and $P_F$ the corresponding probability kernel from $\cF^d_1$ to $\cF_1^d$ constructed in Remark~(r: fair STIT of the paper). Then we call a random fair partition $(\Phi,\tau)$ a \textit{fair STIT with splitting distribution} $F$ if it is invariant with respect to the probability kernel $P_F$.  To allow for the possibility of a unique invariant distribution, we also formally assume that
    \begin{equation}
        x = \int_{C(x)} z\, dz,\quad x\in\Phi.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.653561+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_461bdb606d41c6d710440896ff5a5d4fe806ec4d388b69379f83097299a40798","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2605.07184, 'Convergence of Stochastic Gradient Descent with mini-batching and infinite variance'] \Cref{assumption:function_H} holds if and only if there exists $p\geq1$ and $\delta,L>0$
