{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.686802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_461fb534f56e665fb5650ea74c85af469202e3ecd2e5d7238068933705124ba7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:F=tildeF of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Suppose that $\| A_N\|_{\mathrm{op}} \le 1+\tau n^{-1}$, where $n = \sum_{j=1}^s n_j$ and $\tau > 0$ is a fixed constant. Under Assumptions (itm:B1 of the paper)--(itm:B2 of the paper) of Definition~(mixingdef of the paper), for any fixed diagram $\Gamma$ the diagram functions in Definition~(defsDF of the paper) satisfy the following asymptotic equivalence:

