{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.847222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_462e8787599ac7bd9fef6f2d696ab63ba5bfd3b8bf1ec64be7187c419653c256","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: limit of partial derivatives term of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] The following property holds in the set $\Gamma$ of probability one:
