{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.992454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46305bd8007a4617f43213820bc46ffd630aef0f68340d95c0e503934e035a1a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.01257, '2604.01257'] Let Basic Axioms hold with $\gamma<0$ and let $\mu:=2\delta-\nu>0$. If ${C_{\textsf{L}}}=|\gamma|$
    in {(\ref{IIB4.3})}, then
\begin{equation}                
    {{e}^{\mathcal{T}(t)}}\mathcal{P}(t;s)=\mathcal{U}(s)\cdot\left(1+\zeta(t;s)\right),
\end{equation}
    where the limiting GF $\mathcal{U}(s)$ has the form
\begin{equation}                
    \mathcal{U}(s)=\exp\left\{\frac{1}{{(1-s)}^{|\gamma|}}+
    \int_{{1}/{(1-s)}}^{\infty}{\frac{|\gamma|-\textsf{L}(u)}{{u^{1-|\gamma|}}}du}\right\}
\end{equation}
    and
\[
    \zeta(t;s)=\frac{|\gamma|}{\delta\mu}\frac{{{\mathcal{N}}^{\mu}}(t)}{{(\nu{t})}^{{\mu}/{\nu}}}\left(1+\sigma(t;s)\right),
\]
    where $\mathcal{N}(\cdot)\in{{\mathcal{SV}}_{\infty}}$ is defined with the property {\eqref{IIB3.2}}
    and $\sigma(t;s)=\mathcal{O}\left({\ln{t}}/{t}\right)$ as $t\to\infty$ uniformly in $s\in[0,d],\;d<1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.065778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46329bfdffac7474dace475d45eb95ddb1de23e3e0f9f926161f4111bb03e7b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2606.00648, 'Asymptotic estimates for multiple point ranges of transient random walks on graphs'] For every $\epsilon > 0$, there exist $C(\epsilon) > 0$  and $N_1 (\epsilon) \in \mathbb{N}$ such that 
