{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.784044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_464a04141c78277687c6886b7004ef24913a86d41a5b47831bf2f77a155888cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:resolvent of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] Let $\alpha \in (0,2)$, $\lambda >0$ and $f\in C_b(\mathbb{R}_*)$. Then, $u = U_\lambda f$ is the solution of the following Neumann problem for the fractional Laplacian
