{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.127837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_465f999525605991fbef1d6f7f4eee793a8c4656a77799317190d9a97bdef319","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: NCMST of arXiv:2605.01444, 'From second moments to pairwise negative correlation: \\applications to minimal and unifor'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for all $n\;\geqslant\; C$, the p-NC property holds for any pair of non-adjacent edges of $K_n$ under the MST measure ${\ensuremath{\mathbb P}} _\mathrm{MST}^{(K_n)}$. That is, if $e$ and $f$ are non-adjacent edges of $K_n$ with $n\;\geqslant\; C$, then 
