{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.038222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4662318104d29904d00d2bc5e87ac8a4d118694ecb55756d490bbd57bf246c8d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop bdsumblo of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] Take $C_1, C_2>0$.
Assume that $|k_\ell-N^{2/3}\mathbf k_\ell|<C_1$ and $|N_\ell-N+\boldsymbol{\tau}_\ell N^{2/3}|<C_1$ for each $N$ and $\ell\in\llbracket 1, m\rrbracket$.
Then there exists $C_3=C_3(C_1, C_2)$ such that
\begin{multline}   
\Bigg| 2^{-m}N^m \sum_{\vec\mathfrak b\in \{0,1\}^m} \prod_{\ell=1}^m (2\sqrt{N_\ell N})^{-k_\ell-\mathfrak b_\ell} \sum_{\substack{(\vec p,\vec\upsilon,\mathcal H)\in \mathscr L_\epsilon[\vec \mathfrak b]:\\ p^0,\mathcal H<C_2 N^{1/3},\delta<C_2}} \sum_{\vec r \in \mathcal L^{-1}(\vec p, \vec\upsilon, \mathcal H)}  w(\vec r) \\ - \int_{\substack{(\vec\mathbf p,  \vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H)\in\mathscr K_\epsilon[\vec\mathbf k]:  \\ \mathbf p^0, \mathbf H, \boldsymbol{\delta} < C_2 }} \exp\left(\sum_{\ell=1}^{m-1}
(\boldsymbol{\tau}_\ell-\boldsymbol{\tau}_{\ell+1}) \mathbf H(\mathbf Q_\ell)/2 \right)\mathbf I_{\beta,\vec\mathbf k}[\vec \mathbf p, \vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H] \mathrm d(\vec\mathbf p,  \vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H)\Bigg| <
C_3\epsilon^{-m/2}N^{-1/40}.
\end{multline}
The same bound holds in absolute values, i.e., if we simultaneously replace $w(r)$ with $|w(r)|$ and $\mathbf I_{\beta,\vec\mathbf k}[\vec\mathbf p,\vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H]$ with $|\mathbf I_{\beta,\vec\mathbf k}[\vec\mathbf p,\vec\boldsymbol{\upsilon},\mathbf H]|$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.797317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46640afe00c57fea6f39af3629fb95edfe4c0bd9cfa631ea333bceac1fac806a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2608.30551, 'Critical Discrete Hardy Inequalities in $L^p$'] Let $p>1$. If $u(0)=0$ and $u\in\ell^p(\N,x^{-2})$, then
