{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.788178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46706b20f7c31c9cf3ad37f68b9c8d9028e5fdd6bf47da84c338ce1ac9b8afac","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.05105, 'Cluster-Cluster model in $\mathbb{Z}^d$'] Let $\mathcal{S}^{(p)}$ denote the class of all stationary and ergodic initial configurations for the Cluster-Cluster model with density parameter $p$. We define
  \begin{equation}
      \begin{split}
          \alpha_{c,p}^+&:=\sup_{\mathfs{A}_0 \in \mathcal{S}^{(p)}}\sup\{\alpha \in {\mathbb{R}}:\mathfs{A}^{\alpha}_t\text{ blows up for some finite }t \text{ almost surely}\}  \\
