{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.985035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4679abe52e10560483c2fe00de653062a4aabfe238dfc79baf3cab2751bfdd30","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_2 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $m\geq 1$ be an integer. For every $\frac{m+1}{m+2}< a<1$, the inequality 
