{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.870357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_469b3800857355664b58b7165607497e073a295144e15d291046d6a4be8b931d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:alternating2Necce of arXiv:2608.24731, 'Optimal Alternating Regret for Online Learning and Games\thanks{Authors are alphabetically'] Suppose that in the above alternating learning dynamics,  the $x$-player and the $y$-player use OCO algorithms with alternating regret bound $\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(x)$ and $\operatorname{Reg}_{\mathrm{Alt}}^T(y)$, respectively. Then 
