{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.379376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46ba6a8aad1c443d7114e5dec5fd7d6cc4ad71c04c20485fd8924394acba0fb5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2609.03962, '$L^p$ isomorphisms for the fractional Laplacian on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and their application'] Let $n\ge2$ and $s\in(0,1)$.
