{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.902174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46e60fd851f6d3cad3c6129c9b8a729d480836c5016aa81e3c3e039b5f789f52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm stabilityforRSDEs_compendium of arXiv:2412.05698, 'Controlled rough SDEs, pathwise stochastic control and dynamic programming principles'] {FHL21}}] 

    In the setting of (thm:wellposed of the paper), let \(\bar{\mathbf{X}} = (\bar{X}, \bar{\mathbb{X}}) \in \mathscr{C}^\alpha([0,T]; \mathbb{R}^{d_X})\), let \(\bar{b}\) and \(\bar{\sigma}\) be two random bounded continuous vector fields 
