{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.683609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4731fb1c699b7e25c6ca5898bb4609a09f140fd84fe94d70b5916c6ddb2b59b7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor C2 of arXiv:2411.03712, '{\bf Probability Versions of Li-Yau Type Inequalities and Applications }\footnote{Supporte'] Assume that $\partial M$ is either convex or empty. Let $x\in M$ and $t>0$.    Then the following assertions hold.
