{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.843479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4741f3ede027761c8fed8f65d5c3c924abbfd0fcf796c50c4100df7e6ed559ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.23742, 'Second-order fusion asymptotics for $\Sine_\beta$ correlation functions'] Let $\beta>0$, $m\ge2$, and suppose $m\beta>1$. For pairwise distinct $a_1,\ldots,a_m\in\mathbb R$, as $\varepsilon\to0$,
