{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.369091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_476964595bdc4516a0f072f971fd9fd2f56931b92de6e66be596d59b0e749f17","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] Recall that $\gamma_s^\ell(dp, dq)$ is the joint distribution of the pair $(p,q)=(\inf_{0\leq r \leq s} \ell_r, \ell_s)$ at time $s$ for a length process started at $\ell$. When the length process $\ell_t$ is a Brownian motion absorbed at $\ell=0$ we have, 
