{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.763304+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4773aa971da84929cdfe5abc9ee13ac7cad12252ceabc891aed29bdc1244e013","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Covariance decomposition) of arXiv:2512.04646, '\textbf{Canonical Rough Path over Tempered Fractional Brownian Motion: Existence, Construc'] Let $R_{H,\lambda}$ denote the covariance of tfBm and $R_H$ that of
standard fBm. For any $s,t \ge 0$,
\begin{equation}

R_{H,\lambda}(s,t)
= R_H(s,t) + E^{(1)}_{H,\lambda}(s,t) + E^{(2)}_{H,\lambda}(s,t),
\end{equation}
where the error terms satisfy the pointwise estimates
\begin{align}
\bigl|E^{(1)}_{H,\lambda}(s,t)\bigr|
  &\le \frac{C_1(H)}{\Gamma(2H)} \, \lambda^{2H} \, |t-s|^2,
   \\[4pt]
\bigl|E^{(2)}_{H,\lambda}(s,t)\bigr|
  &\le \frac{C_2(H)}{\Gamma(2H)\,\lambda^{2H}} \;
       e^{-c(H)\lambda\,d(s,t)},

