{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.027904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47c44d6a5379519148e5eaa64d609996db94c4d6eb811e72809084c4066ce4be","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2609.00736, 'Modalities in non-classical variations of S4'] A \emph{(modal) logic} is a set of formulas closed under necessitation and \emph{modus ponens}:
        \[
            \ax{Nec}:=\frac{\varphi}{\Box\varphi} \text{ and } \ax{MP} :=\frac{\varphi \;\;\; \varphi\to\psi}{\psi}.
        \]
    We write $\Lambda\vdash\varphi$ for $\varphi\in\Lambda$.
    $\csf$ is the least logic containing all intuitionistic tautologies, and the axioms:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item ${\ax K} := (\Box(\varphi\to\psi) \to (\Box\varphi \to \Box \psi)) \land (\Box(\varphi\to\psi) \to (\Diamond\varphi \to \Diamond \psi))$;
        \item ${\ax 4} := (\Box\varphi \to \Box\Box\varphi) \land (\Diamond\Diamond\varphi \to \Diamond \varphi)$;
        \item ${\ax T} := (\Box\varphi \to \varphi) \land (\varphi \to \Diamond \varphi)$.
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.840490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47c5d3a5a9b49cffeb01d80cf527b33284a26f0b158fec6b30a8a4acb8f92ab0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition stat_ergodic of arXiv:2504.04860, 'Stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: dependence on the '] Assume that $\mu  \in C^1(\mathbb{R}^d;\mathbb{R}^d)$ satisfies (equation lip of the paper) and (equation dissip of the paper). Then, there exists a stochastic process $\overline{X}_t^H, t \geq 0$, such that 
