{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.440365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47d00481a61d303f84777a845508bf2f91c499ff9fe938b09d05fe45aa38d21f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:prop3.6 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, any triplet of inverse temperatures $\beta, \beta_1 , \beta_2 \in (0 , \infty)$, any percolation configuration $r \in \{0 , 1 \}^{\Lambda_L}$, and any pair of vertices $x , y \in \Lambda_L$, one has the convergences: 
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, n, \beta, r}^{\mathrm{XY}} =  \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, \beta,r}^{\mathrm{Vil}}
    \end{equation*}
    and
    \begin{equation*}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, n, \beta_1 , \beta_2, r}^{\mathrm{XY}} =  \left\langle \cos \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right)  \right\rangle_{L, \beta_1 , \beta_2, r}^{\mathrm{XY/Vil}}.
