{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.237194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47d3a372ed93dc7d8c2777449055556df9e4727d0f68e33cd6ed8297ff4fd793","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma pos_principle of arXiv:2507.06522, 'Balanced multi-species spin glasses'] Assume (equation converging_ratios of the paper) and (equation delta_decay of the paper).
There is a collection of random variables 
\eeq{ 
(\vc\delta_N)_{N\geqslant1} = (\delta_{s_1,\dots,s_p,N})_{s_1,\dots,s_p\in\mathscr{S},\, p\geqslant1,\, N\geqslant1}
}
such that the following statements hold with $\vc\Delta_N$ defined by $\Delta^2_{s_1,\dots,s_p,N} \coloneqq \Delta^2_{s_1,\dots,s_p} + \delta^2_{s_1,\dots,s_p,N}$.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\alph*)}]

