\item  For either ${\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}\in\{\mathsf{Ising},\mathsf{spherical}\}$ and any $\varepsilon>0$, we have 
\eeq{ 
\lim_{N\to\infty}\sup_{H}\mathbb{E}_{\vc\delta} \mathbb{E}_g G_{N,H+H_{N,\vc\delta_N}}^{\otimes 2}\Big(\bigcup_{s\in\mathscr{S}}\{R_s(\sigma^1,\sigma^2)\leqslant -\varepsilon\}\Big)=0,
}
where $\mathbb{E}_{\vc\delta}$ denotes expectation over $\vc\delta_N$, $\mathbb{E}_g$ denotes expectation over the disorder, and the supremum is over
measurable functions $H\colon \Sigma_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}\to\mathbb{R}$ satisfying
\eq{ 
\int_{\Sigma_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}}\exp |H(\sigma)|\ \mu_N(\mathrm{d}\sigma) < \infty.
}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.856321+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47d4917e5be72a02ad50a568b81c593f5f49595b73a6eda8f84bc3819500ef82","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2608.21014, 'The stochastic Cahn--Hilliard equation in critical spaces'] Let $d=4$ and suppose that the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:localWP_weakened} hold. Moreover, let $u_0\in L^0_{\F_0}(\Omega;H^1(\sO))$ and $T>0$. Let $(u,\sigma)$ be the unique maximal solution to \eqref{eq:SCHtorus}. Then we have
