{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:26:47.188024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47e1961254ec9231b469967f1b98509ec99065b40934a0699440e640d5e2fcfd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 98 (occupation density under ideal smoothing) of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] Let
$\hvY(t) = \vY(t-\sss)+\xxx$
where $(\sss,\xxx)\sim\varphi$ is sampled independently of $\vY$. If $\vY$ has occupation measure $\rho_{\vY}$ as given by Definition~\ref{d:intro.cts.occ}, then $\hvY$ has occupation measure
$\rho_{\vY}*\varphi$ (the convolution of $\rho_{\vY}$ with $\varphi$).\footnote{Note that at times close to $1$ or $q_0$, $\hvY$ may not in general be well defined, since $t-\sss$ can can lie outside the time interval $[q_0,1]$. In the full proof, we work on a subinterval $[q_*,1]\subsetneq [q_0,1]$ and choose $\varphi$ such that $0\leq \sss\leq q_0-q_*\ll 1$ almost surely, thus circumventing these issues. See \eqref{e:qbar.and.qstar} and Definition~\ref{d:t.smooth}.}

\begin{proof}
For the purposes of this proof let us abbreviate $\rho=\rho_{\vY}$. 
We then calculate
\begin{align*}
&\bE \int_t f(t,\hvY(t))\,dt
= \int_{s,x} \varphi(s,x) 
	\bE \int_t
	f(t+s,\vY(t)+x)\,dt \,ds\,dx\\
&\qquad=
	\int_{s,x} \varphi(s,x)
	\int_{t,y}
	\ind\{t+s\in[0,1]\}
	f(t+s,y+x)
	\,\rho(dt\,dy)\,ds\,dx\\
&\qquad= \int_{s',x'}
	f(s',x')
	\bigg\{\int_{t,y}
	\varphi(s'-t,x'-y)\,\rho(dt\,dy)
	\bigg\}
	\,ds'\,dx'\\
&\qquad= \int_{t,y}
	f(t,y)
	\rho*\varphi(t,y)
	\,dt\,dy\,.
\end{align*}
This proves the claim.
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.504289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_47e2239f9167cd76e728fd7541ba5837bc1a7f9c94e6aeec3a4d94df7e67c83d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 77 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $\xi \in W$ be arbitrary. A path $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T_0],W)$ for some $T_0 \in (0,T]$ is called a \emph{local mild solution} to the RPDE \eqref{RPDE} with $Y_0 = \xi$ if $Y' = f(Y)$ and
