{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.128927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_480c1a9fd9a9f0635e5f1696b6724aff1514ac701104a8d5d99de02b56d7bff7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:variables of arXiv:2510.09818, 'On the Fourier dimension of fractional Brownian graphs'] [LL25]
	For $q \ge 1$, let $\varepsilon \in \{-1,1\}^{2q}$ and $\sigma \in \Sigma(q)$ as defined in (equation b4 of the paper).
