{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.437494+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_480cd7d21bfb2ce33b0cb2020486deff803ee06e3d54d0d5e5c597c7b9b5d57f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2509.26254, '$K$-Branching Random Walk with Noisy Selection: \\ \Large Large Population Limits and Phas'] For all $t\geq 0$, we define the sequence of point measures $(M^t_N)_{N\in\mathbb{N}}$ by
\begin{equation}
M^t_N := \sum_{i=1}^{N^\gamma} \delta_{Z^t_{N,i}/c_N}.
\end{equation}
Assume that 
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i):] the sequence of initial configurations  $(M^0_N)_{N \in \mathbb{N}}$ admits a limiting log-profile $g^0 \in {\cal C}$,
\item[(ii):] the function $h$ is concave on its support, that is $\rho\geq 1$.
\end{enumerate}
Then, for all $t\in\mathbb{N}$, $(M^t_N)_{N \in \mathbb{N}}$ admits a limiting log-profile $g^t \in \mathcal{C}$. Further, $(g^t)$ satisfies a recursive equation in terms of the following discrete ``free boundary'' problem,
\begin{eqnarray}
\forall x\in\mathbb{R},  \ g^{t+1}(x) \ = \ s_{\sigma_t}\circ r(g^t)(x),  
\end{eqnarray}
where $\sigma^t$ is defined implicitly through the relation 
\begin{equation}
\sigma^t := \inf\left\{ \sigma :\: \sup_{z \in \mathbb{R}}s_\sigma(r(g))(z) \leq \gamma\right\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.578581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_480e241e39b5bf6f3db7a4211df4b7a80b8df0794f60e172f5766ed087a7ebcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] For every $\eta,\delta>0$ and every $\rho\in(0,\frac12)$, there exists $n_{\eta,\delta,\rho}\in\N$ such that, for every $n\geq n_{\eta,\delta,\rho}$, the region
    \begin{equation}
        \left\{
            (a,b)\in\R_+^2:
            ab\leq n^{-\frac23-\eta}
        \right\}
        \cup
        \left\{
            (a,b)\in\R_+^2:
            ab\leq\frac12-\rho,\quad
            \min\{a,b\}\leq n^{-\frac12-\delta}
        \right\}
    \end{equation}
    is contained in the frame set of the $n$-th Hermite function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

