{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.760770+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_481e658cfbb1e8bbd93e09e4711788a01f15f7042072afa9fac9505fa34eaca8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2609.00448, 'Equivariant formality and representation theory'] \textnormal{(cf. \cite[Theorem 6.2]{CFok}).}
	We have the ring isomorphism
	\[K^*(G/K; \mathbb{Q})\cong (R(K; \mathbb{Q})/i^*I(G; \mathbb{Q})\oplus\mathfrak{a})\otimes\bigwedge\nolimits^*P.\]
	Here $R(K; \mathbb{Q})/i^*(G; \mathbb{Q})$ is the image of the map $\alpha: R(K; \mathbb{Q})\to K^0(G/K; \mathbb{Q})$ defined by the associated vector bundle $\alpha(\rho):=[G\times_K V]$, $\mathfrak{a}$ is an ideal of the first tensor factor on the RHS. We also have that $j^*$ maps $P$ isomorphically onto $Q$. Moreover, $\text{dim }P=\text{dim }Q\leq \text{rank }G-\text{rank }K$, and equality holds if and only if $G/K$ is formal, if and only if $\mathfrak{a}=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4820db6a0f9cc46d19507349c485567e0bc8b30aa581fac921ae14b7b2515ed7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition HNNI-NEHU-MAIN of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $t \in \mathrm{supp}_t\ w_{q + 1,n + 1}^{(n)}$, the Newtonian pressure ${\mathfrak{p}_{q,n + 1}}\left( {t,x} \right)$ satisfies
