{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.298525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4856d406429ccd6fed46f68ef9db8e4293430c64fec97b8f397fd4fc2d46b9fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:SDPI:synchronous of arXiv:2605.16904, 'Positive-rate PCA and IPS with stationary Bernoulli measures are rapidly forgetful \footno'] Let $\Sigma$ be a finite set.
