{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.832310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_485cc7cd9a50a0d85dfac5b7faf72d4979f72e7831d19d7269b6af34f761ca91","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm eq:SigT2 of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] Let ${\boldsymbol{\gamma}} \in {\mathbb R}^{d_1}$ with ${\gamma}_i  > -1$, $1\le i \le d_1$ and ${\boldsymbol{\kappa}} \in {\mathbb R}^{d_2}$ with ${\kappa}_i > -1$, $1 \le i \le d_2$. Then
