{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.348724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_487e89bdddeda9faa1298807e6081b15afa14b3a542e99939c81e50b081e62d9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:4.3 of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] \sk{Assume that (equation eq:cond-far of the paper) holds, and} suppose that $\ell\in\bbr{1}{k}$, $m\in\bbr{1}{\ell}$ and $\sigma\in\Xi_{k-\ell}^{V\setminus\{x,y\}}$ satisfy (equation eq:cond-empty of the paper) and (equation eq:cond-few of the paper). Then,
