{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.761010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48a072d13d20d2e5d757fb67c67a719c7edd2109769e02ea3770eab0ad788eb9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.09246, 'Scaling limit of 1+1 dimensional directed polymer with power-law tail and spatial correlat'] Under conditions \textbf{(A)} and \textbf{(B)}, for any $p \ge 2$, there exists an absolute constant $K_p \le 14.7 \frac{p}{\ln p}$ such that the $L^p(\mathbb{Q})$-norm of the linear environment variable satisfies:
