{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.889466+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48a2d9360386129d57ae468f5e7d78c8cd6cd6daade0be2336398817b87ee0be","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:top:Lyapunov of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] There exist universal constants $c, C, C' > 0$ such that the following holds for any $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ and $\alpha > 0$:
\begin{proplist}
    \item If $\beta = o(1)$, then with probability $1 - \epsilon^{-2} e^{ - c \log m } - 2 e^{-cn\epsilon^2} - C' n^{-\alpha}$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \big|  
            \log s_1(X)
            -
            Z
        \big| 
        \;\leq\; 
        C
        \Big(
            \mfrac{\epsilon}{1-\epsilon}
            +
            \mfrac{\beta^2 \log m}{n}
        \Big)
        +
        \mfrac{(1+2\alpha) \log n}{2} 
        \;;
    \end{align*}
    \item If $\beta = \Omega(1)$,  $\log m = o(N^{1/3})$ and $N=o(n^3)$, then  with probability $1 - (1+ \epsilon^{-2}) e^{ - c  \, (\log m)^{3/4} } - 2e^{-cn\epsilon^2} - C' n^{-\alpha / 2}$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \mfrac{1}{\beta^2 \log m}
        \big|  
            \log s_1(X)
            -
            Z
        \big| 
        \;\leq\; 
        C \Big( \mfrac{\epsilon}{(1-\epsilon) \beta \log m}
                    +
                    \mfrac{1}{\beta (\log m)^{1/4}}
                \Big)
        +
        \mfrac{(1+2\alpha) \log n}{2 \beta^2 \log m}
        \;.
    \end{align*}
\end{proplist} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.249958+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48a78f53e0766128087a947868fc55a6a348a229d556748046f62681b0f7d91c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] Let $ x\in X $, $T\in\RR$, 
