{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.333802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48ae92faedfa24e6630b7f4c0c447931fbb05caaa60242a8c581035b51c2a960","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l2 of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] For all $ \lambda>\lambda_c $ and $ \varepsilon,\delta>0 $ there exist $ k=k(\lambda,\varepsilon,\delta) $ such that for all large enough $ \ell\geq \ell_0(\lambda,\varepsilon,\delta,k) $
