{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.926212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48b51512585e9d69f71160848fc11a54c83ba6c1c9aab38afd1dfc78eb8400ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2609.00988, 'Covering Projective Height Balls by Subspaces in Rigid Adelic Spaces'] There exists a constant $C_2\geq 1$, effectively computable from $d, r_2,|D_K|, R_K$ with the following property. For every rigid adelic space $F$ over $K$ and every $0\neq x\in F$ there is $a\in K^\times$ such that
