\end{equation}
where $\Psi_{m,p}$ is a smooth random variable depending only on $m,p$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.275022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48c716c38ebff7a93c42259b8ddac56d4d33c416612f69d57a3fba1545a5f81a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Full-process Sudakov comparison) of arXiv:2606.21137, 'A Sudakov--Fernique proof of Lehner-type edge bounds for matrix-valued GUE sums'] Assume $M\ge N$ and $A_i\succeq0$ for $i=1,\ldots,n$.
	Then
