\]
for every \(F : \Omega_{L,M} \to {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} _+\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.596381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48c9b11ed4208234d0da980e31169bd76e089df0be33cdda67ec084b9149607a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] For $A,B\in\mathcal K_{\X}^{\N^d}$, their multi-time convolution is the kernel sequence $A*B$ defined by

