{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.914560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48e07635811add205a1bcf3d1906b0f8e0fcfe916a97e96d72aa8781d061417b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:def-dpp of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let $ K: \mathbb{R}^{ d}\times \mathbb{R}^{ d} \to  \mathbb C $ measurable. A  point process $ \mathsf{P}$ on $ \mathbb{R}^{ d}$ is a DPP with kernel $ K$ if it admits factorial moments densities   of the form, for $ m\geqslant 1,$
