{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.027289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48e5600077b1d1945f417cffa9e80b95f8ba73f07eaac2becc316a0d5e291814","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2 of arXiv:2606.06859, 'The rectangular finite free heat flow'] For any monic degree-$d$ polynomial $p(x) = x^d + \sum_{i=1}^d a_{2i} x^{d-i}$, the coefficients of $p(x,t) = (p \boxplus^n_d G_{n,d}^{[t]})(x)$ are given explicitly by
