{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.903918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48e8fe73f3c88278a0e7d5bef4035e1a3169240ff051bb2294455bf5c0b3bcef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def GIIA of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A stochastic choice rule $c: {\cal G} \to \Delta(\Omega)$ satisfies \textbf{Generalized Independence of Irrelevant Alternatives} (\textbf{GIIA}) if for every $G, H \in \cal G$, and every $E, F \in \cal F$ with $E, F \subseteq G \cap H$, we have:
