{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.589008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48eb15ad66e46981121c84398b6438bbfda3306312a446a4b57e6cb4cc446f30","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem: OP-continuous-M of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] If $s\ge0$, and $\mathscr{p}\in \mathfrak{M}^s$, then  there
