{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.280061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48ec6b099f9a893fff80060a679569f01aa58b2e69769c787b478afaec289724","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2604.24684, 'Waning Immunity Fails to Restore a Positive Epidemic Threshold on Power--Law Networks'] Fix any $\tilde{\varepsilon}\in \left(0,\frac{1}{4\tau}\right)$, and set
$
\bar\varepsilon=\frac{\tilde{\varepsilon}}{4.4\tau}
$.
Let $G=G(n,\tau)$ be a power-law random graph on $n$ vertices with exponent $\tau>2$, and let
$
\bm d=(d_1,\dots,d_n)
$
denote its degree sequence. Suppose that $v$ is a vertex of degree at least $n^{2\tilde{\varepsilon}}$. Let $A_v$ denote the event that $v$ has at least $\lceil n^{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\rceil$ distinct neighbors whose degrees all lie in the interval $(n^{\bar\varepsilon},n^{3\bar\varepsilon})$. Then, for all sufficiently large $n$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}(A_v\mid \bm d)\ge 1-\exp(-n^{\bar\varepsilon(\tau-2)}), \qquad \text{on the event $D_{\bar\varepsilon}$ defined in \eqref{eq_D}. }
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.700941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48ed040f7c5747995ef15e7a33e8e743910e6a00c408fd7e6cbf4db23edaffd2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 30 of arXiv:2607.21062, 'A new probabilistic approach for\\ mean field games of optimal stopping'] {($\varepsilon$-Nash equilibrium for the $N$-player game).}
Let $\varepsilon > 0$. We say $\hat{\boldsymbol{L}} \in \mathcal{V}_{\mathbb F^N}^N$ is an $\varepsilon$-Nash equilibrium for the $N$-player game \eqref{payoff N-player}-\eqref{N-player SDE_0} if
