    \forall i \in \{1,\dots, N\} , \,\,\, \forall L \in \mathcal{V}_{\mathbb F^N}, \qquad \Lambda^{N,i}(\hat{\boldsymbol{L}})\ge \Lambda^{N,i}(L \otimes \hat{\boldsymbol{L}}^{-i})-\varepsilon.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.195121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48ee2bad847a6f22a8a8edbaacc8ce332342d831d4a57a0e6ced4286694f3889","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 19 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] If $S,S'\in \cS$ are $\vartheta$-regular for some $\vartheta>0$ such that for all $\p \in [k]_0$,  
