{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.712496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48ee577fa3d06bf0cb8bcf011a2ac5ad0f8e23a8de5ff00da54862c24130a634","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:scale of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] Fix $K \geqslant 1, s>0$ and $\beta>0$ and let $\left\{X_{n}\right\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of nonnegative random variables satisfying $X_{n} \leqslant \mathcal{O}_{s}\left(K 3^{-n \beta}\right)$ for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Then, there exists a constant $C:=C(s, \beta, K)>0$ such that the random scale 
