{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.842786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48efd482c1b84ebe7d1c93d7da99a55d2109cab2436d7ece8b94e12a81dff436","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:99 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] For $j,k,i,\Delta\in [\![-2\varepsilon n^{1/3},2\varepsilon n^{1/3}]\!]$ additionally satisfying $\Delta\geq 0$ and $i\geq 1$, consider the event $E_{i,\Delta}$ defined by
