{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.962173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48f48d8220b0046612616c2cc0a5000f067b53b158c212235a81c23175645676","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 10 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] For $m\ge 2$ and $\delta\in(-m,0]$, let $\beta:=(m+\delta)/(2m+\delta)$. Then for each fixed $i\ge 1$,
