{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.171207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49069a5f8b7fba7eb229d55449299f5225e4df2f0e689332aad648e7b0253734","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 47 (Estimate for Projected Payoffs) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. Define the dynamic obstacle $\Phi(x) := g(\langle h, x \rangle_H)$, where $g: \R \to \R$ is concave and $L$-Lipschitz, and $h \in \mathrm{Dom}(A^*)$. Let $u_\varepsilon$ be the unique mild solution to \eqref{eq:hjb_penalized}. Then, the penalty term $\Pi_\varepsilon$ defined in \eqref{eq:yosida_penalty} satisfies:
