{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.758136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49138b121736cd3be03b83f8a1e85f9e1c01b1b59cd284185e9fc66ba4344b5b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_regular_estimate_localized_eigenvalue of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under the assumptions of (theorem_localized_eigenvalue of the paper), the following bounds hold uniformly in $t\in[0,1]$:
