for any $a\in [\![{D}]\!]$ and $\mathsf M_0,\mathsf M_1\in\ha{M_t\left({z_t}\right),M_t^*\left({z_t}\right)}$, where ${\widehat{\Lambda}}_t$ is defined by ${\widehat{\Lambda}}_t=\Lambda-\Delta\left({t}\right)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.869143+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_491a2dc4d7693bd2b8c883421ca652d094e2fdff768bdea718f01b71dcccd82a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor box-polylogarithmic-comparison of arXiv:2609.03856, 'Consensus time for asynchronous $\ell^p$ relaxation: graph dependence'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~(thm:box-bounds of the paper), define
\[
 U_p(d,L)=
 \begin{cases}
  nd^{1/(p-1)}L^{p/(p-1)},&1<p<2,\\
  ndL^2,&p\ge2.
 \end{cases}
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{f_0\in[-1,1]^{[L]^d}}\mathbb{E}\tau_p(1/2;f_0)
 \ge c_p
 \begin{cases}
  U_p(d,L)/\log(en),&p\ne2,\\
  U_2(d,L),&p=2.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
Consequently, at fixed tolerance $1/2$, the upper and lower bounds in
Theorem~(thm:box-bounds of the paper) differ by at most
$O_p((\log n)^2)$ for $p\ne2$ and by at most $O(\log n)$ for $p=2$.
The causal-profile term by itself leaves a factor $d$.  Once the coupon term
is included, however, the pointwise discrepancy can be smaller; see
Remark~(rem:box-dimension-gap of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.414589+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_491caa18687810eb49e1d643359056a5991c51aeff0f398da439bd12a52acd56","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 82 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] For each $h \in [H]$, we define two holomorphic functions $\phi^+_h$ and $\phi_h^-$ in $\amsmathbb{M}_{h}$, which satisfy
