{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.811960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_491ef5a232daad2896f982c5124131e0762f32e3b9c566ea5f08438180fd5bde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:wellposed_viscous of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Let $d$, $s$ and $\alpha$ satisfy (hp:main_hp of the paper). For every $\nu>0$ and for every $M_0 \in \dot{H}^{-s}_{\div}$ there exists a unique strong solution $M^\nu$ to (equation eq:SPDE_viscous of the paper) in the class of solutions in $L^2_{t,\omega}(\dot{H}^{-s}_{\vee,\div})$ with sample paths in $C_t(\dot{H}^{-s}_{\div})$. Moreover, the solution $M^\nu$ satisfies $\mathbb{E} \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \|M^\nu_t\|^2_{\dot H^{-s}}<\infty$ and the following It\^o formula holds $\mathbb{P}$-a.s.:
    \begin{align}
