    as $n\to\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.355872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49239c1ba3bb401d3e649c2977889becfeb7212c3b1f64840cdee0c0f703b8d8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 227 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] In the symmetric spherical (resp.\ Ising) projection pursuit problem, we say that $\cA$ \textbf{$(\ioeps,\gamma)$-symmetrically attains} a target measure $\mu\in\cP_2(\bbR_{\ge 0})$ the output $\bx = \cA(\bG,\bg^{\aux})$ satisfies both of the following properties
    with probability at least $\gamma$:
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
         \item  
         $\bx \in S_N(\iota)$ (resp.\ $\Sigma_N(\iota)$);
         \item 
         $\bbW_2(\mu,\mu_{\bG,\sym}(\bx)) \le \ioeps$.
    \end{enumerate}
We say that $\cA$ is \textbf{$(\fq,\iotamsr,\iotasol,\gamma)$-symmetrically confined} to a subset $\cM\subseteq \cP_2(\bbR_{\ge 0})$ if the output $\bx$ satisfies both of the following properties with probability at most $1-\gamma$:
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item  $\bx \in S_N(\iotasol)$ (resp.\ $\Sigma_N(\iotasol)$);
        \item  $\bbW_\fq(\mu_{\bG,\sym}(\bx),\cM) \ge \iotamsr$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.334776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4923ea6500f7010c72bd1d577836e266b9c9a7bfa2f03548c8b046d592ca98b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor cv Hausdorff ball boundary of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] Jointly with~(equation eq cv subsequence of the paper) and~(equation eq cv ball of the paper), 
