{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.083925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4934187393ddf9a1f01bd9e5efc84dd18ac7ca1a9d43d824beaf37f1359ed68a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem conditional-energy of arXiv:2411.14236, 'Size of chaos for Gibbs measures\\of mean field interacting diffusions'] Let $\alpha \in [0,1/2]$. Denote
\[
A = \frac 1N \sum_{k \in [N]}
\Expect [ W_{-,*}(X^i, X^i) ].
\]
Then it holds that
\begin{multline}

\frac 1{N!}\sum_{\sigma \in S_N}
