{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.472846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49452d0c9a3352d4dd54db26d92f090e6edec6c9e7656363519b29576275b127","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 50 (Intersection-profile coefficient equivalence) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $m\ge1$, $2\le r<\infty$, and $1\le p<\infty$.  Put
