{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.702647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_495e790b6440c67d9885596ccd0b1ed9a7a96c3218a37295c1036a71ccb90b07","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 (the continuous Poisson solution) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[lemma]{lem:poisson-cont}
  The function $g_\star$ of \eqref{eq:pois-rep} lies in $C([0,\infty))\cap C^1((0,\infty))$ with $g_\star'$ locally absolutely continuous, solves $\mathcal Lg_\star=-\hat\eta$ a.e.\ on $(0,\infty)$, and has the boundary flux
  \begin{equation}
    \frac{dg_\star}{ds_G}(0^+)=-\hat\eta(0)\,\frac{e^{-\beta G(0)}}{\mu}
    \qquad\bigl(\text{equivalently }\ \mathcal Lg_\star(0)=-\hat\eta(0)\bigr).
  \end{equation}
  For $0<x\le1$, with $c_F\coloneqq -\hat\eta(0)/\mu$, 
  \begin{equation}
  \begin{aligned}
    g_\star'(x)&=c_F\,x^{1-\delta}+O\bigl(\snorm{\eta}_\infty x^{2-\delta}\bigr),\\
    g_\star''(x)&=(1-\delta)\,c_F\,x^{-\delta}+E(x),
    \qquad |E(x)|\le C\snorm{\eta}_\infty\bigl(1+x^{1-\delta}\bigr).
  \end{aligned}
  \end{equation}
For $x\ge1$, $|g_\star'(x)|\le C\snorm{\eta}_\infty/x$ and $|g_\star''(x)|\le C\snorm{\eta}_\infty$ a.e.; and $|g_\star(x)|\le C\snorm{\eta}_\infty\bigl(1+\log(1+x)\bigr)$.","status":"unverified"}

