{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.397898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_498400919ff468a17e31182f76d08e312af3d47842522f0ea5e67a2ec3f36446","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition definitionboxnew of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix three subsets $D_1,D_2,D_3\subset[n]$ with $|D_1|=|D_2|=|D_3|=c_0^2n/12$  and $D=D_1\cup D_2\cup D_3=[ c_0^2n/4]$. Fix two constants $\kappa\geq 2,\kappa'\geq \kappa$ and two integers $N\geq N_1\geq 2$. An $(N,N_1,\kappa,\kappa',D_1,D_2,D_3)$ box pair is defined as a pair of product sets $\mathcal{B}_1,\mathcal{B}_2$ of the form $$\mathcal{B}_1=B_1^1\times B_2^1\times\cdots\times B_{n}^1\subset\mathbb{Z}^{n},\quad \mathcal{B}_2=B_1^2\times B_2^2\times\cdots\times B_{n}^2\subset\mathbb{Z}^{n}$$ where we have
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item $|B_i^1|\geq N$ for each $i\in[n]$ and $|B_i^2|\geq N_1$ for each $i\in[n]$,\item $B_i^1=[-\kappa N,-N]\cup[N,\kappa N]\forall i\in D_1$,   $B_i^2=[-\kappa N_1,-N_1]\cup[N_1,\kappa N_1]\forall i\in D_2$.
    \item For each $i\in D$, $\max\{|x|:x\in B_i^1\}\leq \kappa'N$, $\max\{|x|:x\in B_i^2\}\leq \kappa'N_1$.
    \item $|\mathcal{B}_1|\leq(\kappa N)^{n}$ and $|\mathcal{B}_2|\leq(\kappa N_1)^{n}$.\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

