{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.564340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_498a53d4663616e12165c1dbb26f38886d58438c4fe005b29fb221bbee9711e5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition P:negative_gamma of arXiv:2512.21977, 'Repeat times and a two-weight UST model'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$. There exists a constant $A = A(\varepsilon) > 0$ such that for any $\gamma < 0$ there is an $n_0 = n_0(\gamma, \varepsilon)$ with
