{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.873940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49a88b2da66010a59a0974d06288713895947f35cdc54fc80370fff768cea2db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 (Representation at random times) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] For any adapted process $(V_t)_{t \geq 1}$ with $\E\bigl[\sum_{t \geq 1} |V_t|\,P(\tau = t \mid \cF_t)\bigr] < \infty$,
