{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.827138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49c306fdeeaa3f91b74474de90b721626a3f1ce00210d50c0bb002a07fc72d86","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th: stability_t_independent of arXiv:2609.00257, 'Stability estimates for the initial-to-final-state inverse problem'] Let $0<T<\infty$. Consider two time-independent potentials $V_1, V_2 \in L^1(\mathbb{R}^n) \cap L^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $n\geq 2$, $\| V_j \|_\delta< \infty$ and $\| \mathop\mathrm{Im} V_j \|_\delta \leq \frac{1}{4T}$ for $j\in\{1, 2\}$, satisfying the a priori assumption $\| V_1 - V_2\|_\delta \leq R_0$ for some fixed constant $0<R_0<\infty$. 
Assume also that $V_1$ and $V_2$ meet the integrability condition (equation eq: int_cond_V of the paper).

Let $\mathcal{U}_T^1$, $\mathcal{U}_T^2$ denote the corresponding initial-to-final-state maps. Then, providing that $ \mathrm{dist}_{\delta} (\mathcal{U}_T^1, \mathcal{U}_T^2)$ is sufficiently small, for any $\delta>1/2$ there holds

\begin{equation}
\|V_1 - V_2\|_{H^{-1}(\mathbb{R}^n)} \lesssim \mathrm{dist}_{\delta} (\mathcal{U}_T^1, \mathcal{U}_T^2)^{\frac{2}{n(n+2)}}.
\end{equation}

Additionally, for $\delta>n/2$, the following improved stability estimate holds

\begin{equation}
\|V_1 - V_2\|_{H^{-1}(\mathbb{R}^n)} \lesssim \mathrm{dist}_{\delta} (\mathcal{U}_T^1, \mathcal{U}_T^2)^{\frac{1}{n}}. 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

