{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.980647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a0c41333b3dae4430ab496b05cf5c26dec44f8158208e8caad2312048ee84cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Fictitious mean-field critical behaviour of arXiv:2508.18809, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation III: The upper critical dimension}'] Suppose that $d=3\alpha$ and that the modified hydrodynamic condition does \emph{not} hold. There exists $\lambda_0>0$ such that the following hold. 
