{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.571450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a0e3258cbdd5d65ccc3c50e3965f33ddf586b05b7160d2747211f963d2696dd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 5 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>6$. There exist $c,C,M>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
