{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.557440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a62cabe1350900458930995ee8ccb3dc81bc844831d0c0170a8041ef5848c43","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defs 9 (Liftings) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] A \emph{lifting} is a map~$\ell\colon \mcL^\infty(\mssm)\rar \mcL^\infty(\mssm)$
satisfying
\begin{enumerate*}[$(a)$]
\item $\tclass{\ell(f)}=\class{f}$; 
\item if $\class{f}=\class{g}$, then~$\ell(f)=\ell(g)$;
\item $\ell(\car)=\car$;
\item if~$f\geq 0$, then~$\ell(f)\geq 0$;
\item $\ell(a f+b g)=a\ell(f)+b\ell(g)$ for~$a,b\in \R$;
\item $\ell(fg)=\ell(f)\ell(g)$.
\end{enumerate*}

A lifting is \emph{strong} if, additionally,
\begin{enumerate*}[$(a)$]\setcounter{enumi}{6}
\item $\ell(\phi)=\phi$ for~$\phi\in\Cb(X)$.
\end{enumerate*}

A \emph{Borel} \emph{lifting} is a lifting with~$\A=\Bo{\T}$.

As a consequence of~\iref{i:d:Liftings:1}, a lifting~$\ell\colon \mcL^\infty(\mssm)\rar \mcL^\infty(\mssm)$ descends to a (linear multiplicative order-preserving) right inverse~$\ell\colon L^\infty(\mssm)\rar \mcL^\infty(\mssm)$ of the quotient map~$\class[\mssm]{\emparg}\colon\mcL^\infty(\mssm)\rar L^\infty(\mssm)$.
As customary, by a (\emph{strong}/\emph{Borel}) \emph{lifting} we shall mean without distinction either~$\ell$ or~$\ell$ as above.","status":"unverified"}

