{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.386281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a7329382cd798f13fde93f8312a20096c45fa13e8278a1f765ba4b7cf0de827","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition dd-opt-prop of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let \(\mathcal{A} =\Lambda_{\text{glob}} (\kappa,\alpha, 0)\) and \(\mathcal{B} =\Lambda_{\text{glob}} (\zeta,\beta, 0)\) be drift-diffusion generators on \(\mathbb{R}^d\). Then the Markovian transport derivative is given by
