{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.282863+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4aad746202501b919f131253d166352e430da5f52b0d90336d5908911a9b7afe","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 14 of arXiv:2606.21778, 'Pontryagin Maximum Principle in Free Probability Theory'] A free backward stochastic differential equation (fBSDE) on $[0,T]$  is a time reversed free stochastic differential equation 
