{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.205175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ab2412d0c5038453aa3d100931af92692a686ab8c5bffa72fb533f8d1d06923","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 1 (Planar skew bang-bang diffusion with piecewise constant coefficients) of arXiv:2512.09136, 'On the Green's functions and Martin boundary structure of a planar diffusion in a disconti'] We define a planar skew bang-bang diffusion associated with coefficients $(\Sigma^+, \Sigma^-, \mu^+, \mu^-)$ and with the skew vector $q$, as a continuous adapted process $(Z_t)_{t\geq0} = (A_t, B_t)_{t\geq0}$ on $\mathbb{R}^2$, 
    such that $Z$ can be expressed 
