{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.997543+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4abfadf00b341d741b9cf2a2493dab4cb0ef32342d56a29cba0d4317265ec4cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:u-concentration of arXiv:2609.02820, 'Sharpness and critical scaling of parking'] Let $K$ be a finite-range, translation-invariant transition kernel on
	$\mathbb{Z}^d$. Let $g_n^K(z)\coloneqq\sum_{j<n}K^j(0,z)$, and let
	$v_0=0$ and $v_{n+1}=(\eta+Kv_n)^+$ for i.i.d.\ $\eta(x)$ satisfying
	$\mathbb{E} e^{\theta|\eta(0)|}<\infty$ for some $\theta>0$. Then there is
	$C<\infty$, depending on $K$ and the law of $\eta(0)$, such that, for every
	$n\geq1$ and $r\geq2$,
	\begin{equation}
		\bigl(\mathbb{E}|v_n(0)-\mathbb{E} v_n(0)|^r\bigr)^{1/r}
		\leq C\bigl(\sqrt r\,\|g_n^K\|_2+r\|g_n^K\|_\infty\bigr)\,.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.879578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ac10692baf83f264cb1058f11dfc2e56a24e5b3c89c0be5cad002c64e0a43e2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Qleqr of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] If $Q$ is a quadratic form on $\mathbb{R}^m$ and $\lambda\in \mathbb{R}$, then we write
  \begin{equation}
    Q\leq \lambda \quad \iff \quad Q(x)\leq \lambda \|x\|^2,\, \forall x\in \mathbb{R}^m\setminus \{0\}
  \end{equation}
  and similarly for $>,\leq$ and $<$. In particular $Q>0$ means that $Q$ is positive definite.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.120789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ac2464e0d299fe8956f014c9d24d77d8c2d8d3dbed77dc4f0e08d9ea78983fc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2608.26642, '2608.26642'] The function $\varphi_q^\mu(x)$ is continuous on $\R$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C_q^\mu$ such that $\varphi_q^\mu|_K$ satisfies the following equation:
