{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.424179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ac2cff587663e94f45ac659a83b5fcc6334d08397d0c70133b36f979f4c5056","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 151 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] If the discrete ensemble satisfies Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, \ref{Assumptions_basic}, \ref{Assumptions_offcrit}, \ref{Assumptions_analyticity} and its equilibrium measure has no saturations, then we have an asymptotic equality of distributions as $\N \rightarrow \infty$
