{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.750350+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ac44af85600753ce691e9ea84fce77f795b24ff46759ef10e0ebb5568d9762a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RBM-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $H = L^2(\mathbb{R})$.  The seed functions $\psi_{t,a,n}$
and $\phi_{t,a,n}$ defined in
\S(sec:RBM-kernel-reform of the paper) satisfy the linear problem
(equation eq:dc-clean-linear-d1 of the paper)--(equation eq:dc-clean-linear-S3 of the paper)
and its adjoint
(equation eq:dc-clean-adjoint-d1 of the paper)--(equation eq:dc-clean-adjoint-S3 of the paper)
with $\partial_1 = \partial_t$, $\partial_2 = \partial_a$,
$S_3 = e^{\partial_n}$ and constant scalar edge weights
$(c_1, \lambda_1) = (1, -\tfrac{1}{2})$,
$(c_2, \lambda_2) = (1, -1)$.
Explicitly:
\begin{align}
\psi_{t,a,n+1}
&= \partial_a \psi_{t,a,n} + \psi_{t,a,n},
 \\
\partial_t \psi_{t,a,n}
&= \tfrac{1}{2}\partial_a^2 \psi_{t,a,n}
   + \partial_a \psi_{t,a,n}
   + \tfrac{1}{2}\psi_{t,a,n},

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\phi_{t,a,n}
&= -\partial_a \phi_{t,a,n+1} + \phi_{t,a,n+1},
 \\
\partial_t \phi_{t,a,n}
&= -\tfrac{1}{2}\partial_a^2 \phi_{t,a,n}
   + \partial_a \phi_{t,a,n}
   - \tfrac{1}{2}\phi_{t,a,n}.

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.781630+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ac4c2caa35316630e118da7b907e0a37f5fd4e9f5c8c6b6e4fbc6e209adeea7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem rationalencodingOSp of arXiv:2412.00593, 'A new approach to strong convergence II.\\The classical ensembles'] For every $h \in \mathcal{P}_q$, there is a rational function of the form 
