{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.284812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ac7603d3056e6b7b51aa3eca6b167f89dcd8d3d61a58b33ed2d8422baee74d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma1 of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Assume that  $({\bf A}_0)$ and $({\bf H}_4)$ hold.
Then, for any $p>0,$   $t\ge0$ and $x\in\mathds R^d,$
\begin{align}
