{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.116476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ad4786d455e2903da74ce382e579f2cbf30d320ec4af5218073348fc4171420","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] Let \(d(x)=\dist_\omega(x,S)\). At every $p\in S$, there are holomorphic coordinates $(z_1,\ldots,z_k,w_1,\ldots,w_{n-k})$, centered at $p$, such that $S=\{z=0\}$,
\begin{equation}
  d^2=|z|^2(1+\rho(z,w)),
  \qquad \rho=O(|z|+|w|),
\end{equation}
with all higher derivatives of $\rho$ uniformly bounded on smaller coordinate balls, and
\begin{equation}
  \omega=\ddbar\bigl(|z|^2+|w|^2+\Phi(z,w)\bigr),
\end{equation}
where
\[
  \nabla^j\Phi=O(|z|^{3-j}+|w|^{3-j})\quad(0\le j<3),
\]
and all higher derivatives are uniformly bounded. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.874311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ad545c584906b18722c2eab08b2b42ec284feedf288f9516a265bd050e73e6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 (Path-time mixed coincidence identity) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] Let $\Pi_{1,t},\ldots,\Pi_{W,t}$ be strictly positive adapted factors with $0 < Z_\tau(\alpha) := \E\bigl[\prod_i \Pi_{i,\tau}^{\alpha_i}\bigr]
< \infty$.  Then for every $Q\ll\widehat P$ with
$Q(\{\Amart{\tau}_t\prod_i\Pi_{i,t}^{\alpha_i}=0\})=0$,
\begin{equation}
  \log Z_\tau(\alpha)
  = \sum_{i=1}^W \alpha_i\,\E_Q[\log \Pi_{i,t}]
    + \E_Q[\log \Amart{\tau}_t]
    - \KL(Q\|\widehat P)
    + \KL(Q\|Q_\tau^\alpha),
\end{equation}
where the optimizer is
\begin{equation}
  \frac{\dd Q_\tau^\alpha}{\dd \widehat P}(\omega,t)
  = \frac{\Amart{\tau}_t(\omega)\prod_i \Pi_{i,t}(\omega)^{\alpha_i}}{Z_\tau(\alpha)}.
\end{equation}
Dropping the nonnegative residual $\KL(Q\|Q_\tau^\alpha)$ recovers the variational form (a supremum over $Q \ll \widehat P$), attained at $Q_\tau^\alpha$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.667719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ad722c7aeb46ea492850a4889ff9023de84a993173a51650d1812cb3115fa3c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_bound_on_last_point_if_close_to_mu_c_appendix of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] If $R > R_{\mu_0}(\varepsilon)$, then for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $w \in \Omega_{n}^{(0)}(\mu,2^{-R}\varepsilon)$,
