{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.056065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ad9b840544af0efac543683109328a605f3e07114e8a575bc7644466bfc9317","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 (Semi-concavity of the free energy) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] There exists a constant $C<+\infty$ (depending only on $\xi$) such that, for every $N\in\N$, $c>0$, $t,t'\geq c$, $q,q'\in \mcl Q^\sS_{\uparrow,c}$ with $\dot q-\dot q' \in L^2$, and $r\in[0,1]$, we have
