{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.196029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ade4f656de6792f21d1a1fb5eafe41038d55d2997f416f7f172ff407db7eb89","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 24 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] We say a shuffling process $\bn$ is \textbf{weak-$c$-$(\chi,\rho,\varphi)$-almost $\mu$-like} if there exists another shuffling process $\hat\bn$ which is $(\chi,\rho,\varphi)$-almost $\mu$-like such that
