{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.741109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b476cea3bdd0f7a7f3ede0f280515ff0a1d8523fb2b79ead509cf0807b9fb93","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 19 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] We keep the assumptions and the notation of Proposition \ref{rwergo}. Let $F \! :\! \obbT^\bullet\! \to \bbR$ be 
a measurable function 
such that $\bE [|F(\bT, \boo)|] \leko \infty$ and such that $F(T, \boo) \eqo F(\mathtt{cent} (T, o))$ for all $(T, o)\ino   \obbT^\bullet\!$. Then 
\begin{equation}

