\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.686163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b497f75e27e7ee8e48d4b60ab43e4e85f416d12fdd2bb6d84e34b473fa89731","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defsDF of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] For each diagram $\Gamma$, we define its associated diagram function as
\begin{equation}
F_{\Gamma}(\{n_j\}) := F_{\Gamma,\Sigma}(\{n_j\}) =
\sum_{\eta: V(\Gamma) \to [N]}
\sum_{\substack{
t_j \ge 0,\; w_e \ge 1 \\
2t_j + \sum\limits_{e \in \partial D_j} w_e = n_j
}}
\Bigg(
\prod_{(x, y) \in E_{\mathrm{int}}}
p_{w_e}\big(\eta(x), \eta(y)\big)
\prod_{(z, w) \in E_{\mathrm{b}}}
\big(A^{w_e}\big)_{\eta(z)\eta(w)}
\Bigg),
\end{equation}
where the second summation runs over all integers \( t_j \ge 0 \) and \( w_e \ge 1 \) satisfying the constraint \( 2t_j + \sum_{e \in \partial D_j} w_e = n_j \) for every $j$.
Analogously, the corresponding diagram function for the variance profile $\widetilde{\Sigma}$ is denoted by $\widetilde{F}_{\Gamma}(\{n_j\})= F_{\Gamma,\widetilde{\Sigma}}(\{n_j\})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.718474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b4e0b33df8927f65a92ff1849ce2497d369de43029a740eb22b3909a42b105c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 29 (Deterministic bias, fully overdamped regime) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:diagonal-covariance} and~\ref{ass:power-law}, in the fully overdamped regime $\eta\lambda_1\le c_0(1-\rho)^2$ with a sufficiently small universal constant $c_0>0$, we have:
\begin{equation*}
    \cS_{\nesterov}(k)
    \eqsim
    \begin{cases}
    1,&\qquad k\lesssim \frac{1-\rho}{\eta},\\
    \left(\frac{1-\rho}{\eta k}\right)^s, &\qquad k\gtrsim\frac{1-\rho}{\eta}.\\
