{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.322443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b6cf638feff958dfdec72d62b82163d3730935f67a67cb29415c84f989cd708","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.rescaled_Schauder of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Fix $z_0$.  Suppose $g$ solves~(equation eq:linear_kinetic of the paper) in $Q_2(z_0)$ with coefficients satisfying~(equation defn:coercivity_assumption of the paper)-(equation defn:bounded_coefficient_assumption of the paper). Suppose that $g \in L^\infty_m$ for some $m \in \mathbb R$.  Assume, further, that there exists $\alpha\in (0,1)$ with $\mathcal A, \mathcal B, \mathcal C \in C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_2(z_0))$.  Then
    \begin{equation}
        [g]_{C^{2,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_{\frac{r}{2}}(z_0))}
