{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.145233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b79ac788776a019bf7628c026a92fbca5c5a6d38a383a7a30bb2e333e1e59d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $\beta\in\bbR$ and $s\in\partial \cA_\tau$. Let $\phi_\e(s)$ be the average of $\phi$ over $A_\tau\cap \partial B(s;\e)$. In the sense of vague convergence of measures on the space of distributions, the limit
