{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.034091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b86976d92bcf4b0466d6372234b4714b432fa8b9afd8c7b4e514646954b4f62","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem reg of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] Assume that  $\alpha \in  [1,2)$ or $\alpha \in (0,1)$. Assume that  $L = (L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is a L\'evy  process  satisfying  \textbf{(H)} and \textbf{(R)} in   Hypothesis (hyp-nondeg1 of the paper) in the former case or Hypothesis (hyp-nondeg3 of the paper) in the latter case.  Assume also that  $\beta\in(0,1]$ is such that
 \begin{equation}
1< \alpha + \beta <2 .
 \end{equation}
 Assume that   $b\in C_{\mathrm{b}}^{\beta}(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{R}^d)$.

 Then the following assertions hold.

\begin{itemize}
\item[(I)]
For every
 $\lambda\geq 1$ and  $f \in C^{\beta}_{\mathrm{b}} (\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d)$,
   there exists a unique
  $u= u_{\lambda}(f) \in C^{\alpha + \beta}_{\mathrm{b}}
  (\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d)$ which is a   solution to the following uncoupled system of linear equations
  \begin{equation} 
 \lambda u -  {
\mathscr A} u  - b \cdot Du = f \;\;  \mbox{ on }\mathbb R^d.
 \end{equation}
These solutions have the following two properties
\begin{align}

\lambda\Vert u_\lambda\Vert_0\leq \Vert f\Vert_0,
\end{align}
and
\begin{align}

  &\lim_{ \lambda \to \infty} \Vert Du_{\lambda} \Vert_{0} =0.
    \end{align}

\item[(II)]\ For every $\lambda_0 \geq 1$,
  there exists $r_0>0$ and a continuous   function
 \begin{matriz}
(0,\infty) \ni r \mapsto c(\lambda_0,r ) \in (0,\infty)
 \end{matriz}
which is constant  on $(0,r_0]$ and increasing on $[r_0,\infty)$
    such that  for every   $\lambda \ge \lambda_0$, every $r>0$ and every
    $b \in C^{\beta}_{\mathrm{b}} (\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d)$: $\Vert b \Vert_\beta \leq r $,    the unique element $u_{\lambda}$  introduced in Part I above satisfies
     \begin{equation} 
 \lambda \Vert u_{\lambda}(f)\Vert_0 + [Du_{\lambda}(f)]_{\alpha + \beta - 1}
  \le c(\lambda_0,r ) \Vert f\Vert_{\beta}, \;\; f \in C^{\beta}_{\mathrm{b}} (\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d).
   \end{equation}

\item[(III)]

For every $\ensuremath{\varepsilon}>0$ and every $M>0$ there exist constants $\lambda_0{}_{,M}\geq1$ and  $C_M>0$ such that if  $\lambda \geq \lambda_0{}_{,M}$ and  a vector field  $b\in C^{\beta}_{\mathrm{b}} (\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d) $   satisfies  $\Vert b\Vert_{\beta}\leq M$,
 the unique solution   $ u_\lambda \in C_{\mathrm{b}}^{ \alpha+\beta}(\mathbb R^d, \mathbb R^d) $ of the equation  (equation eqn-wee of the paper)
satisfies the following two conditions
\begin{align}
&\| Du_\lambda\|_0 \leq \ensuremath{\varepsilon} \Vert f\Vert_{\beta},
\\

&\| u_\lambda\|_{\alpha+\beta} \leq C_M \Vert f\Vert_{\beta}.
\end{align}

\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.141775+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b89659c2e94ab5e73a4b5098d05bc6b3ea62d81fe4698ccbeba1b6fbb1f58ee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2604.05910, '\textbf{Well-posedness and Hurst parameter estimation for fluid equations driven by fracti'] Let $\xi\in \cB_\infty$.~We call a process $\omega\in C([0,T];\cB_\alpha)$ which satisfies  the variation of constants formula 
