{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.056024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b8f5dc5f3aeccb7b7eec1ccb32e6f83a1692cff9ac3c74f9e5e894990a6d22e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.law_dalpha of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] The law of $\alpha^{-1}(U)$ is $\mathrm{d}\alpha$, where $U$ is a uniform random variable over $[0,1]$. Consequently, for every bounded measurable $h:[0,T]\to \mathbb{R}$, we have that $\int_0^1 h\circ\alpha^{-1}(s)\mathrm{d} s = \int_0^T h(t)\mathrm{d}\alpha(t)$. Moreover, $\supp \mathrm{d}\alpha = \overline{\alpha^{-1}((0,1])}$ and
\begin{align}
    \alpha^{-1}\circ\alpha(t+) = t,\quad \forall t \in \{0\}\cup \supp\mathrm{d} \alpha.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.539798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b924a23a3f4936745270f287755524bdfad500de8a41bed89ff2f006c01b791","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm optimal_corrector of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For $d\geqslant 3$, there exists an exponent $s := s(d,\mathfrak{p}) > 0$ and a constant $C := C(d,\mathfrak{p})\leqslant \infty$, such that for every $x,y \in {\mathbb{Z}^d}$ and each $\xi\in \mathbb{R}^d$, 
		\begin{equation}

			|\chi_{\xi}(x)-\chi_{\xi}(y)|\boldsymbol{1}_{\{x,y\in \mathscr{C}_{\infty}\}} \leqslant \mathcal{O}_s(C|\xi|).
