		By our choice for $v_m$, we also have that for $x\sim y, x\in \mathscr{C}_{\infty}\cap {\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m$, $y\not \in \mathscr{C}_{\infty}(\mathbf{a}) \cap {\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m$,
		\begin{equation}

			|\nabla v_m(\mathbf{a})(x,y)| \leqslant \mathcal{O}_s(C|\xi|)+|\mathscr{C}_y(\mathbf{a})\cap {\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m| \cdot |\xi|.
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.196264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4b948c261bed6e279219c4ff819d519f59e7bdfde9e2edc03d9767791a971f41","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 27 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] For any $y\in \mathcal A_{\rmleft}$, $z\in \mathcal A_{\rmright}$  and $x\in A_{y,z}$,
    if $\mathbb E |\cI(B_x)| < N^ {c_F+\delta}$, then for any $a>0$ independent of $N$:
    \begin{align}

	\mathbb P\left[\big| \iota(x)-Nt_x]\big| \geq  N^{ \max(c_F,\delta)+\frac{a}{2}+\delta}\right]
	&\leq e^{-\Omega(N^{a-o(1)})},\\

	\mathbb P\left[\big| \tau(x)-N(t_x+\lambda_x)\big| \geq N^{\max(c_F,\delta)+\frac{a}{2}+\delta}\right]
	&\leq e^{-\Omega(N^{a-o(1)})}.
