{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.515712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4bb6239c3904c637ca13712814c8853e4fe0a9cb9f1f28f3a81ad98e2b84cd20","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 ({\cite[Theorem 1.4.7) of arXiv:2608.28528, 'Strong solutions of SDEs with critical discontinuities in diffusion coefficients'] {Ku}}]
Let $ \{X_n(x) \mid x \in I = [0,1]^d \}$ be a sequence of continuous random fields with values in a real separable
semi-reflexive Fr\'echet space $S$ with seminorms $\|\cdot\|_N$, $N=1,2,\ldots$. Assume that, for each $N$, there exist
