{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.024923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4bc11477d601f4ba29dbfec2331155ab5fc13e8fc168dfc7aefa3be3b7745b53","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2606.06757, 'Path-Dependent Ergodic Optimal Control \\ and Backward Stochastic Differential Equations'] We say that a family of measures $(m_t)_{t \in \R}$ on $\C_{\theta}$ is an \textnormal{evolution system of measures} for the transition semi-group $P_{s,t}$ if $m_s P_{s, t} = m_t$, \textnormal{i.e.} 
