{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.225675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4bf280c2cbc49265c6fb31610ab2b3e93f98ce31ad6b300fa4ae1b212a199163","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:overdamped of arXiv:2512.18598, 'Long-time reverse transportation inequalities for non-globally-dissipative Langevin dynami'] Under Assumption (ass:farfield of the paper), for any $T>0$ and $x$, $x' \in \mathbb{R}^d$, one has 
