{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.124064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c0c858abb82f96cd563ec6ef6ac9ffa836d9357ff3468b4cb7e02c2685ccc76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:hardcheeger of arXiv:2510.00748, '\bf On irreducible central limit theorems'] Let $G=(V,\mathcal{E})$ be a finite graph, respecting Convention (conv;simple of the paper) and such that $|V|=N$, and let $\mu_k$ be the $k$-th smallest eigenvalue of its normalized Laplacian ${\ensuremath{\mathcal L}} $, for $k=2,\ldots,N$. Then, there exists an absolute constant $C>0$ such that, for every $k=2,...,N$, there exists a partition $S_1,...,S_k$ of $V$ with nonempty subsets verifying
