{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.893628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c0e68058e7c1b58e83cfaec38b5c46d0f6ea1ac35758b5e128fe8b4940a1bf3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:technical of arXiv:2606.30475, 'Ancestries in random $d$-DAGs'] With notation as before, suppose there exists a constant $\kappa>0$ such that
 \begin{equation}
  0\leq q_n(i,j) \leq \kappa \frac{j}{n^{d+1}} \frac{i^d}{(1-j/n)^d}
 \end{equation}
 for all $n\geq 1$, $i\in[n]$, and $j\in[n-i]$. Moreover assume that $n q_n(i,j)\to \hat q(\alpha,\beta)$ for all $i$ and $j$ such that $in^{-(d-1)/d}\to \alpha >0$ and $j/n\to \beta \in(0,1)$. Then
