 \end{multline}
 as $n\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.587346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c0f0069918ee3095a4167d8b5cbdf32c2d734d6294a86e6c9165c9c035b55fd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2609.00884, 'The weakness of typicality'] A $\mathsf{P}$-instance $X$ is \emph{rarely solved} if
