{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.340024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c119a8e08d7f7475a615281eba998bd20e40d7e1f2ec23888be786b01303eb4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:control_mesoscopic_energy of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Suppose that Assumption (ass:forcing_regularity_iteration of the paper) holds. Let $\mu>0$, $r\in (1,\infty)$ and $p_0\in (2,p)$.
Then there exists a constant $R_0>0$ depending only on $\mu,p,q,r,p_0$ and $d$ such that the following assertion holds. For all local solutions $(v^N,\pi^N,(\widetilde{\pi}^N_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha})$ to the stochastic Stokes system (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_original_iteration of the paper) on $Q$, the following uniform control of the energy at the microscopic scales holds
