{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.018538+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c1704c5bbda8fa419c716a303075150bc0cce71b46dbd80cc2e0df68ac328a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 1 (A first general non-asymptotic bound) of arXiv:2605.05986, '\bf Convergence rate of the occupation measure of { classes of ergodic processes toward th'] Let $p\!\in (0, +\infty)$ and let $d\ge1$.  There exists a positive constant $K_{p,d}$ such that for every  $\mu,\nu\!\in{\cal P}_p(\ER^d)$
