{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.085016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c1724be8ea647279a73680b0d93747802694ed431685c5917fbbd292d03b5b4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 25 of arXiv:2608.27934, 'An example of biquandle and an invariant of long virtual knots defined through it'] Suppose that two long virtual knots $K_{1}$ and $K_{2}$ commute. 
