{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.971637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c1b8e85d8e047017b15150c84f5de5099a2eb6fac500a943cae8d4aa859194c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:iso_action of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Given $\underline{\tau}, \underline{\sigma} \in \boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$ and $f\in\mathrm{Iso}(\underline{\tau},\underline{\sigma})$, we define an induced linear isomorphism $\hat f: \mathcal{H}^{\underline{\tau}} \rightarrow \mathcal{H}^{\underline{\sigma}}$ and, for any $k \in \{1,{\mcb{n}}\}$, a bijection $\tilde f^{[k]}: (\R^k)^{N(\underline{\tau})} \rightarrow (\R^k)^{N(\underline{\sigma})}$ by setting
\begin{equs}
\hat f:\mathcal{H}^{\underline{\tau}} 
\ni
\bigotimes_{n \in N(\underline{\tau})}
e_{n}
&\mapsto 
\bigotimes_{m \in N(\underline{\sigma})} e_{f^{-1}(m)} \in \mathcal{H}^{\underline{\sigma}}\;,\\
\tilde f^{[k]}:(\R^{k})^{N(\underline{\tau})} 
\ni
\big(x_n: n \in N(\underline{\tau})\big) 
&\mapsto 
 \big(x_{f^{-1}(m)} : m \in N(\underline{\sigma})\big) \in (\R^{k})^{N(\underline{\sigma})}\;.
\end{equs}
We also lift $f$ to a map $\mathbf{f}:{\mcb{B}}[\underline{\tau}]\rightarrow {\mcb{B}}[\underline{\sigma}]$ by setting $$\text{$\mathbf{f}$}F() \eqdef \big(\mathrm{Id}_{\R^{\mcb{n}}}\otimes \hat f\big) \circ F(\tilde f^{[{\mcb{n}}]} \, )\,.$$ 
Overloading notation, we also lift $f$ to a map $\text{$\mathbf{f}$}:\text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\underline{\tau}]\rightarrow \text{${\mcb{C}}$}[\underline{\sigma}]$ by setting $$\text{$\mathbf{f}$}F() \eqdef \hat f \circ F\big( 
 (\mathrm{Id}_{[0,1]}\otimes \tilde{f}^{[1]})  \big)\,.$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.403760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c1c6aaa36615969cf6438c46e1f4af74e78b6ceac71e8f33febeb076581dfb9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem estemps of arXiv:2412.06480, 'A SIR epidemic model on a refining spatial grid \\ II-Central limit theorem'] For any $T>0$, there exists a positive constant $C$ such that
	\begin{eqnarray}
	\sup_{0\le t\le T}\Big(\big\Vert \overline{u}_\varepsilon(t)\big\Vert_{L^2}^2+\big\Vert \overline{v}_\varepsilon(t)\big\Vert_{L^2}^2 +\big\Vert \overline{w}_\varepsilon(t)\big\Vert_{L^2}^2\Big)\nonumber \\
	&& \hspace{-5cm} +C \int_{0}^{T}\Big(\big\Vert\nabla_{\varepsilon}^{+}\overline{u}_{\varepsilon}(s)\big\Vert_{L^2}^2 +\big\Vert\nabla_{\varepsilon}^{+}\overline{v}_{\varepsilon}(s)\big\Vert_{L^2}^2+\big\Vert\nabla_{\varepsilon}^{+}\overline{w}_{\varepsilon}(s)\big\Vert_{L^2}^2\Big) ds \le C\eta_{_T}e^{CT} , 
	\end{eqnarray}





	where $ \displaystyle\eta_{_T} :=\int_{0}^{T}\Big(\big\Vert u_\varepsilon(s)\big\Vert_{\mathrm{H}^{-1}}^2 + \big\Vert v_\varepsilon(s)\big\Vert_{\mathrm{H}^{-1}}^2\Big) ds.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

