{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.859882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c310e7258feef8fe17a3743ce3e065d9a0ae8c82cc1e7fb23f070e3192ab475","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 18 of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] Let $a \in \R$, $\alpha \in \R$, and $k \in \N_0$. Let $g$ be the smooth function $g(x) = x$.
