{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.359867+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c3e503b6acaa6e9c10f19caf1620b405ff48c35650e66b677dd50995202d6b9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop th.infty of arXiv:2411.13099, 'Long time behavior of killed Feynman-Kac semigroups with singular Schr{ö}dinger potentials'] Assume    {\rm \textbf{[c1]}}   and assume also    {\rm \textbf{[S1]}} or {\rm \textbf{[S2]}}.   Let $\mathbf W$ be defined by (equation eq.W of the paper).  Then, when $|x|\to  +\infty$,  $ \mathscr L^{oL}   \mathbf W(x) /{\mathbf W(x) } \to -\infty$. 
