{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.401061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c5bbe35cecf8a19bc98b5d9d84f2f6f988c64e43d5c4a4799e89800f46adf31","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lmm 17 of arXiv:2608.31054, 'Revisiting Picard's proof of the Picard--Weber--Weck selection theorem'] Let $1\leq i \leq d$ and $  k = (k_1,\ldots,k_d)^\top \in \N_0^d$, $  u = \varphi_i^{(  k)}   e_i$. Then, $  u \in D((\Rotcirc)^\ast (\Rotcirc))$ and
