{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.699940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c6c56f226a1244b950d806f9cd6f8d58ff1dcf6bd88c6cd5be9014baf4bcf62","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:resonance of arXiv:2609.00668, 'Rigidity of Euclidean Minimal Hypersurfaces under Nonuniform Diagonal Dilations'] Pair-sum resonance can preserve nonflat minimal geometry under genuinely nonuniform diagonal dilations.
\begin{enumerate}
