{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.748601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c6d223b29063282c705143bf01b9343f33a2b1567b87073ca471d615572f334","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] For parameters $c\in \N_0$ and $b\in \C$, the \emph{multiplicative Laguerre polynomials} $L_n^*(x; b,c)$ are defined by
