{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.919427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c8c4ddbc1e5822ce4b16aaf28198563485b7bb880b160746929d25542347819","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem \cite{hoffman2006stable}, Th. 5 of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] For $ \mathsf{P}$ a stationary point process, almost surely, in the stable mariage allocation, all points of $ \mathsf{P}$ are allocated a territory of volume $ 1$, forming a fair partition. Furthermore, a.s.,\begin{itemize}
