\item Any bounded subset of $ \mathbb{R}^{ d}$ only intersects finitely many territories.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.794046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c8f2d3559789f06edd2e95c6968aae3587cd1c4f8234a08f8f3c7bfd71b0d18","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2609.00209, 'Exit Times for Brownian Motion and Location Detection'] Let $\tau_{\mathcal P}$ denote the exit time of a Brownian motion from $\mathcal P$. With $\mathcal E_n$ as in Proposition \ref{Prop:exhE2P}, we have
