{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.348611+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c903f2c74471451e7aebd069bc8f463febb8028dc6c50764d2666ea5ea65c7c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:omega-prop of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] We have, for each $m \in \mathbb{N}_0$,
\begin{equation}
\alpha_x \le \pi_x(m)\left(\alpha_x+m\right) = \pi_x(m+1) \left(m+1\right) \le \alpha_x\,e^{\alpha_x\sum_{j=1}^m \frac1j} \; \text{.}
\end{equation}
Moreover, for $m \ge m' \ge 1$,
\begin{equation}
1 \le \frac{ \pi_x(m)\,m } { \pi_x(m')\,m' }  \le e^{\alpha_x \sum_{j=m'}^{m-1}\frac1j}  \; \text{.}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.640563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c9243a0b8c526609b8c323475c79d0610b5734ff11c76dc538ab42e6c2398fb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 31 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] We define a measure $\mu_{\beta;S}^{(n)}$ on $(\L^+,\L^-) \in \left[0,\infty \right)^{G_n} \times \left[ 0,\infty \right)^{G_n}$ via
	\begin{multline}
		\d\mu_{\beta;S}^{(n)}(\xi^+,\xi^-) \propto Z^{G_n}(\L^-)  Z^{S}(\L^+) \times \exp\Big( 2\beta(\L^-,J\L^-) + 2\beta(\L^+,J\L^+)_S - 2\beta \sum_{\substack{x \in X \\ y \in S}} J_{xy} \L^+_x \L^+_y\Big) \\ \times \exp(- \textstyle\sum_{x \in X}\I(\L^+_x,\L^-_x)) \d\l_2^X(\L^+) \d\l_2^X(\L^-) \times \d\l_2^S(\L^+)\d\l_2^S(\L^-).
	\end{multline}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.562756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c92da62f0ad6ded9a2c6bb96f7e6ab86ce0c291f2315b2fbaf2dff767e5667f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Consider the iterative edge-colored graph process on $V$ and $\d^{(g)}$ and $X^{(g)}$ for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$. Let $x_{\max}^{(g)}$ be the maximum degree in $(V,X^{(g)})$, and let
		\begin{align}
			d_{\max}^{(g)}&:=\max\{d_1^{(g)},\ldots,d_n^{(g)}\},
			\\\Delta^{(g)}&:=d_{\max}^{(g)}\left(x_{\max}^{(g)}+\sum_{h=1}^{g}d_{\max}^{(h)}\right)+m^{(g)}\sum_{h=g+1}^{\chi}\frac{(d_{\max}^{(h)})^2}{m^{(h)}}.
		\end{align}
		Consider the asymptotics as $m_{\min}:=\min\{m^{(1)},\ldots,m^{(\chi)}\}\to\infty$, and assume that $\Delta^{(g)}=O((m^{(g)})^{\sfrac12}/(\log m^{(g)})^2)$ for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$. Then each iteration $g=1,\ldots,\chi$ has probability $O(\Delta^{(g)}/m^{(g)})$ of rejection. In particular, for $m_{\min}$ large enough, there exist edge-disjoint simple graphs for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$ with degree sequence $\d^{(g)}$ and with no edges from $X^{(g)}$. Furthermore, any such graphs are sampled with probability $e^{O(\mathscr{E})}\mathscr{P}$, where $\mathscr{E}:=\sum_{g=1}^{\chi}\mathscr{E}(m^{(g)},\Delta^{(g)})$ and
		\begin{align}
			\mathscr{P}&:=\exp\left(\sum_{g=1}^{\chi}\left(\tfrac12\lambda_{\d^{(g)}}+\tfrac14\lambda_{\d^{(g)}}^2+\tfrac12\sum_{h=g+1}^{\chi}\lambda_{\d^{(g)},\d^{(h)}}^2+\mu_{\d^{(g)}}^{X^{(g)}}\right)\right)
			\\&\quad\cdot\prod_{g=1}^{\chi}\left(\frac1{(2m^{(g)}-1)!!}\prod_{i=1}^{n}d_i^{(g)}!\right),
		\end{align}
		which is asymptotically uniform if $\mathscr{E}=o(1)$. The total number of such graphs is thus $e^{O(\mathscr{E})}\mathscr{P}^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.189803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c9702c6387b45fa8500f8d759f567caf7cfd1d1a506516e2d987d274aeb2c83","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 12 of arXiv:2604.19200, 'Stochastic $\Sigma$-convergence in Orlicz setting and Applications'] The formal derivative of order $\alpha \in \mathbb{N}^{d}$
		is defined to be the formal operator on $\mathcal{X}_{A}^{\Phi}$
