{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.349156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cb1b63fc88112ea10f3986200c43e63819a4e9b7ccae34bddf97de0ce192e25","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:meta of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For the chain $(\ensuremath{\mathcal M}_{\hat\alpha,k}(t))_{t\ge0}$, the following two claims hold true:
	\begin{enumerate}[(a)]


		\item For every $m, m'\ge 1$ with $\Omega_{k,m}\neq \varnothing\neq \Omega_{k,m'}$ and $\eta\in \Omega_{k,m}$, we have 
	\begin{equation}
		{\bf r}_{\hat \alpha,k}^\ensuremath{\mathcal M}(\eta,\xi) = 0\; \text{,}\;\;\quad \text{for all}\ \xi \in \Omega_{k,m'}, \ m'>m\; \text{,}\;\; 
