{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.284832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cbfe1a40a49eaefdb84a437708b6e824663c465ce74e431cb14c0f4f24ecb68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theo:melroel of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Let $w$ be any positive and continuous function on $\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}$, $((\nu^{K}_{t})_{t \in [0,T]})_{K \in \mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of processes in $\mathbb{D}([0,T], (\mathcal{M}_{w}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}),\mathrm{w})$ and $(\nu^{*}_{t})_{t \in [0,T]}$ a process in the space $\mathcal{C}([0,T], (\mathcal{M}_{w}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}),\mathrm{w}))$. Then, the following assertions are equivalent
\begin{itemize}
