\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.589318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cc0162c87cd93ecd0dcd4c1210bbc406fce66e1ddaeb0394ac2e67b357c8af3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm def:decoupling_function of arXiv:2606.06187, 'How to Study Reflected Brownian Motion in a Quadrant via Kernel Functional Equations?\\ \m'] We say that $D$ is a decoupling function of order 1 if and only if $D$ is rational and satisfies (equation eq:G->F of the paper). Such a function exists if and only if
