{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.269313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d0add69fb6cb24ffec322d4af7fa54cbedd7d61ae951fd49a364eb93b7f8f70","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$  and $\delta>0$ with $\phi(\lambda,\delta)>0$. Then, for any  $\epsilon>0$ there exists a finite set $A\subset \bZ^d$ such that
