{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.576744+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d2f03584af33f1902123275696683782334dec66dd9af432222c10d2b532e0a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 (Heat Flow Decay) of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Let $(R_{t}, t \geq 0)$ be a diffusion semigroup, and let $\mu$ and $\nu$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assumption}. Then there exist $C > 0$ and $T_0 > 0$ (both depending on $\mu,\nu$) such that for all $t \geq T_0$,
