{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.308227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d303552c4bb885335c949743945ded9d4a341a4645474dc4ccaed96a0e76ec6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 86 (Controlling the difference between the discrete and continuum heat operators) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Fix $\alpha<0, \tau>1$. Let $K_N$ be as in Definition \ref{dnlnkn}, and let $K : C^{\alpha,\tau}_\mathfrak s(\Psi_T) \to C^{\alpha+2,\tau}_\mathfrak s(\Psi_T)$ by \begin{align}

 			Kf(t,x):= \int_{\Psi_T} G_{t-s}(x-y)f(s,y)dsdy,
 		\end{align} where $G_t$ as usual is the deterministic keat kernel on $\mathbb R^d$. Then we have the operator norm bound $$\|K_N-K\|_{C^{\alpha,\tau}_\mathfrak s(\Psi_T) \to C^{\alpha-1,\tau}_\mathfrak s(\Psi_T)} \leq CN^{-1/4}.$$


  Here, $C$ is independent of $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.011598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d30c2a6722495f4526fbf38f0823dd0e283e15a16967309327c9ed0649f3dd1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 33 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] On the canonical-row tower $X_u$,
\begin{equation}
 P_{u,\epsilon,\mu}(h,h_z)
 =\rho_*\left[
