{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.335708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d51d7a50bbbb1f01a20857d97b79ee2aee3d3be9e3604ac804b024769800c8e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition degree_def of arXiv:2606.17425, 'Order statistics for edge eigenvectors of Wigner matrices'] Consider an inner factor $\mathrm{IF}(k, s, \mathcal{I}, \mathcal{J})$ as in (equation general_term of the paper). Let $d(k, s)$ denote the number of off-diagonal factors in $\im \prod_{i=1}^{n_1(k, s)} G_{u_i v_i}$, not counting the $G$-factors containing a $q$-index. Further, let $\hat{d}(k,s, l)$ be the number of off-diagonal factors in $\prod_{j=1}^{\hat{n}_l(k,s)}  G_{\hat{u}_j \hat{v}_j} $. 
