{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.708629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4db68c3bdc8f78679f2c2f3ae4e616ea2effb813ac32bc979e00c3892bf97eb3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Voter model) of arXiv:2609.01143, 'The voter model on the hyperbolic graph'] Let $V$ be finite and let $Q=(Q_{ij})_{i,j\in V}$ be an irreducible Markov generator, with $q(i):=-Q_{ii}$.  For $\xi\in\{0,1\}^V$ and $i,j\in V$, let $\xi^{i\leftarrow j}$ be obtained from $\xi$ by replacing the opinion at $i$ by that at $j$.  The voter model $(\xi_t)_{t\geq0}$ with copying kernel $Q$ is the Markov process on $\{0,1\}^V$ with generator
\begin{equation}
\cL f(\xi) = \sum_{i\neq j}Q_{ij} \left(f(\xi^{i\leftarrow j})-f(\xi)\right).             
\end{equation}
Thus site $i$ updates at rate $q(i)$ and, when it updates, copies $j$ with probability $Q_{ij}/q(i)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.069505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4db6ef361f600a5bd964c8206e77b299e116a63deab524ea68b6282d48fb6afc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.01742, 'Large deviation principles for SPDEs with locally Lipschitz coefficients'] Assume that Hypotheses \ref{cond-initial}, \ref{cond-dif}  and  \ref{3} hold. If $L_{\sigma}>0$, then
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{P}\left\{\left|u_{N+1}^{ \varepsilon,h_\varepsilon}(t,x)\right|\geq e^N\right\}\leq \exp\left(-\frac{N^{\frac{3}{2}}}{2^{8}\e L_{\sigma}^2t^{\frac{1}{2}}}\right)
\end{align*}
uniformly for all $t>0$, $x\in\R$, $\e>0$,
$$N\geq \max\left\{\left(\max(2^{13}\e^2L_{\sigma}^4t,2^{11}\e^2L_{b}t)\right),4\left[\log \left(4\left(\|u_0\|_{L^\infty(\R)}+1\right)\right)+64M^4L_{\sigma}^4t\right]\right\},$$
and for every $M\geq L_b^{1/4}L_{\sigma}^{-1}$.
 If $\sigma\in L^{\infty}(\R_+\times\R)$, then
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{P}\left\{\left|u_{N+1}^{ \varepsilon,h_\varepsilon}(t,x)\right|\geq e^N\right\}\leq \exp\left(-\frac{e^{2N-4L_bt}}{8\left(4\e+1\right)\left(\|u_0\|_{L^\infty(\R)}+\|\sigma\|_{L^\infty(\R+\times\R)}t^{\frac{1}{4}}+1\right)^2}\right)
\end{align*}
uniformly for all $t>0$, $x\in\R$, $\e>0$ and
\begin{align*}
N\geq\frac{1}{2}+\frac{3}{2}\log2+2L_bt+\frac{1}{2}\log(4\e+1)+\log\left(\|u_0\|_{L^\infty(\R)}+\|\sigma\|_{L^\infty(\R+\times\R)}t^{\frac{1}{4}}+1\right).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.355643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4db851f052d0122c42cea90d25212f7eda705e7a033b7ee0eb9480c8fa9015bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem SupremumInequalityUnderMixing-geometric of arXiv:2412.01635, 'On the Weak Convergence of the Function-Indexed Sequential Empirical Process and its Smoot'] (Geometric mixing conditions)\\

	Let $\mathcal F$ be a set of Borel maps $\mathcal X \to \mathbb R$ that satisfies $\sup_{f \in \mathcal F} |f(x)| \leq 1$. Furthermore, suppose there exists $\beta \in (0,1)$ and $C_\beta \geq 0$ with $ \alpha^X(t) \leq C_\beta \beta^t, t \in \mathbb N_0, $ 	
	and that it holds 
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^1 \log^2 N_{[]}(\varepsilon, \mathcal F, \rho_\nu) d\varepsilon < \infty
	\end{equation}  
	for some $\nu > 2.$ Then there exists $\kappa > 0$, a constant $C \geq 0$ that only depends on $\nu$ and the mixing coefficients and $\lambda,\Lambda: (0,\infty) \to [0,\infty)$ with $\Lambda(\delta) \to 0$ as $\delta \downarrow 0$ such that for each $\delta > 0$, $n \in \mathbb N$ and $1 \leq i \leq j \leq n$, with $m = j-i+1$, we have 
	\begin{align*}
		& \EOuter{ \sup_{\rho_\nu(f-g) \leq \delta} \left|S_{n,i,j}(f) - S_{n,i,j}(g)\right|^\nu} \leq C \left[ m \left( \Lambda(\delta) + \lambda(\delta) m^{-\kappa} \right)^2 \right]^{\frac{\nu}{2}}.
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

