{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.251351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4de7d257d6d0466d8055455c850520e502874ed03570b13252f2d99eff5a4782","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 62 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Let $A,D$ satisfy \eqref{eq:costanti}; let $q \in (0, \varepsilon_0)$ and $k\in \mathbb N$ be such that $k \le \ell_0 (q)+5$; and set
	\begin{flalign} 
		q' \in [q - 2^k  N^{D \delta-1}, q]; \qquad \mathsf{t} = 2^k q^{-1} N^{1+6A\delta}.

	\end{flalign} 
	Consider the Glauber dynamics $(H_t)_{t \ge 0}$ starting from an initial condition $\mu\in\mathcal P^+$ (recall \Cref{def:P+}) and assume that, w.o.p. under $\mu$,
	\begin{flalign}

		H_0 (w) \le \mathcal{H}_q (w) + N^{\delta-1}, \quad \text{for each $w \in \mathcal C^q_k:=\mathcal{B}_{k+1}^q \cup \bigcup_{j=1}^k \mathcal{A}_j^q$}. 
	\end{flalign}

	\noindent Then we have w.o.p. that, for any $t \in [\mathsf{t}, N^{5}]$,   
	\begin{flalign} 
		H_t (z_0) \le \mathcal{H}_{q'} (z_0), \qquad \text{for each $z_0 \in \mathcal{A}_k^{q'}$}.
	\end{flalign}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.095819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4def53361d408f8f3dac1e74a9d90b699fcb1016a796b521f2e3f80acbd85bc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem111 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Assume ((h of the paper)), and let $p\ge 2$.
  Then there exist $\Gamma_6=\Gamma_6(p,a,h)>0$ and $\Gamma_7=\Gamma_7(p,a,h)>0$ such that if ((init of the paper)) holds and
  $t\in (0,T_{max}]$ is such that ((uut of the paper)) is satisfied with $\delta_1=\delta_1(h)$ as in Lemma (lem11 of the paper), then for any choice of $r>2$
  such that $r\ge p$,
  \begin{eqnarray}\label{111.1}
	\hspace*{-4mm}
