\end{equation}
for any fixed $\xi>0$, uniformly in $z\in\mathcal{D}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.613078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4dff1034d65a3a9b2ffa3d7f9e8994bc66361ef3d533b880d52074797a0787d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:Dtmoment2 of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] There exists $C>0$ such that (for any $n\in \mathbb{N}$ and $t\in{\mathbb R}$) the following holds:
