{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.623326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e18e4d09eabfeaa5c99c99b75d8f58a07fc0fb855c1183455392c2c8f0047cf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 73 (Algebraic ancestry and analytic critical cost) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] For a cutoff \(N\ge2\), the split ancestry Rees module is
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr R^{\rm anc}_{\le N}(H)
 :=H\oplus
 \bigoplus_{n=2}^N\ \bigoplus_{r=1}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor}
 z^{-r}\operatorname{Ran}P_{n,r}.

\end{equation}
The symbol \(z^{-r}\) records the algebraic normal order
\(F_rL_n/F_{r+1}L_n\).

For tensors set
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr K_0^{[0]}:=\mathbb R,
 \qquad \mathscr K_1^{[0]}(H):=H,
 \qquad \mathscr K_n^{[0]}(H):=\mathfrak A_1^{(n)}(H)\quad(n\ge2),

\end{equation}
and, for \(n\ge2\), \(r\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr K_n^{[r]}(H):=
 \mathfrak W_{\rm mf}^{[r]}(H^{\otimes n}).

\end{equation}
Thus cost zero means trace class in every cut, while cost \(r\) permits the
critical profile \(\phi_r(N)\).  The inclusions
\(\mathscr K_n^{[r-1]}\subseteq\mathscr K_n^{[r]}\) define the analytic
critical boundary
\begin{equation}
 \partial_{\rm cr}^0\mathscr K_n(H):=\mathscr K_n^{[0]}(H),
 \qquad
 \partial_{\rm cr}^r\mathscr K_n(H)
 :=\mathscr K_n^{[r]}(H)/\mathscr K_n^{[r-1]}(H),
 \quad r\ge1.

\end{equation}
The truncated analytic Rees space is
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr R^{\rm cr}_{\le N}(H)
 :=\bigoplus_{n=0}^N
   \bigoplus_{0\le r\le\lfloor n/2\rfloor}
   z^{-r}\mathscr K_n^{[r]}(H),

\end{equation}
with the degree-one summand understood as \(H\).  The direct Rees sum carries
its product quasi-topology.  By contrast, the quotients
\(\partial_{\rm cr}^r\mathscr K_n\) are used as algebraic associated-graded
spaces; no Hausdorff quotient topology is implicit.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.592671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e1a43d5bb78f761a4fe647b5206a4ffaaf932623deee969a802fbda024f9660","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem1 of arXiv:2608.30592, 'Infinite Matrix Operators and $E$-Frames in Hilbert Spaces'] Suppose that $E$ is invertible and $\Psi=\lbrace \psi_k\rbrace_{k=1}^{\infty}$ is a sequence in $\mathcal{H}$. Then
