{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.599320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e1fc153864126f87605e07e70c4fb3c995b2775d36e09e8b3d210866aff5f85","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2411.15724, 'Wasserstein Convergence Rates for Empirical Measures of Random Subsequence of $\{nα\}$'] Let $X_1,X_2,\ldots$ be i.i.d. random variables, and let $\alpha \in \mathbb R$. \footnote{Note that in this lemma, $X_1$ is not required to be integer-valued, and $\alpha$ is not required to be irrational.} Set $\mu_n = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{j = 1}^{n} \delta_{\{ S_j \alpha \}}$, $n \geq 1$. Then the event
