{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.446365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e4d1bced57c8f7b6496ab669b85c39ef2b398c02c90b98abf9c07918466a0c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2606.15842, 'A small noise approximation for Muller's Ratchet'] Let $(E,r)$ be a complete and separable metric space, $\mathcal D \subseteq \mathcal M(E)$ linear, and $G^{(1)}, G^{(2)} : \mathcal D \to \mathcal M(E)$. Assume $G^{(1)}$ is the generator in the sense of bounded pointwise limits of the semigroup $S$ (i.e.\ $(S_{h}f(x) - f(x))/h \xrightarrow{h\downarrow 0} G^{(1)}  f(x)$ boundedly for all $f \in \mathcal D$, $t\geq 0$, and $x\in E$). 

Let $X$ be a solution of the $(G^{(1)} + G^{(2)}, \mathcal D)$ local martingale problem with càdlàg paths, and $\tau \geq 0$. Fix $f \in \mathcal D$ and assume
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(i)] $S_{t} f \in \mathcal D$ and continuous, for all $t \in [0,\tau]$,
    \item[(ii)] $t \mapsto G^{(2)} S_{t}f(x)$ is right-continuous for all $x$ on $[0,\tau]$,
    \item[(iii)] there exist $L \in \mathcal M(E)$, such that for all $t \in [0, \tau]$ and $x\in E$ 
\begin{align}

    &|S_{t} f(x) | + |G^{(1)} S_{t}f(x)| + |G^{(2)} S_{t}f(x)| \leq L(x),
\end{align}
and
\begin{align}

    & \mathbb E\big(\sup_{0\leq t \leq \tau} L(X(t))\big) < \infty.
\end{align}
\end{itemize}
Then
\begin{equation} 
  M_f(t) := S_{\tau-t} f(X(t)) - \int_0^t G^{(2)} S_{\tau-s} f(X(s)) \, ds,
  \qquad 0 \le t \le \tau
\end{equation}
is a martingale. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.358137+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e4d29b512bab93cbe09001f418392df308f8735bfa5e5b14ad0c52d8ebe6a63","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Let \((\mathcal{T}, d) = (\mathcal{T}_g, d_g)\) be a random rooted ordered real tree encoded by a random \(g \in C_{\rm bridge}\).  
