{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.593253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e80ee2f08c2e1101029c9d1a917e65b66cde9f260637bdbab9fd8ea860cd691","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm local LIL of arXiv:2411.15681, 'Strassen's local law of the iterated logarithm for the generalized fractional Brownian mot'] Assume $\gamma\in (0,1)$ and $\alpha\in(-1/2+\gamma/2, 1/2)$. Then   for every  $t_0>0$,
