{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.711416+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e826771015c126d2b3015e3aefc9ffbb9e970d93632ebb80d2d108641349299","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:triple_crit_process of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] For  any fixed number  $\gamma > 0$ and  a perturbation operator $\mathfrak{A}$, we define  a \textbf{tricritical point process}  as  the random point process on $\mathbb{R}$ whose $k$-point correlation measures $R_{k}^{\mathfrak{A}}(\gamma; dx_1, \dots, dx_k)$ are the unique Radon measures determined by the  sinc-transform identity: for any $t_1, \dots, t_k > 0$ and $m \in \{4, 8, 10\}$,
\begin{equation}
    \int_{\mathbb{R}^k} \prod_{j=1}^k \frac{\sin^{m}(t_j \sqrt{-x_j})}{(t_j \sqrt{-x_j})^{m}} \, R_{k}^{\mathfrak{A}}(\gamma; dx_1, \dots, dx_k) = \sum_{\Pi \in \mathscr{P}([k])} \prod_{\pi \in \Pi} \tau_{\mathfrak{A}}(\{t_j\}_{j \in \pi}).
\end{equation}
Here the deformed limiting cumulants $\tau_{\mathfrak{A}}$ are defined by the sum over connected typical diagrams:
\begin{equation}
    \tau_{\mathfrak{A}}(\{t_j\}_{j \in \pi}) = \sum_{\Gamma \in \mathcal{T}_{|\pi|}} \gamma^{|E|-|V|} \int_{0}^1 \cdots \int_{0}^1 \left[ \prod_{j \in \pi} \mathcal{Q}_m(\xi_j) \right] \mathcal{F}^{\mathfrak{A}}_{\Gamma}\bigl(\{\xi_j t_j\}_{j \in \pi}; \{z_i\}_{i=1}^r; \gamma^\alpha\bigr) \prod_{j \in \pi} d\xi_j,
\end{equation} with $\mathcal{Q}_m$  defined in (equation eq:Pt_def of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.888892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e83b6b4b245fe311c1f96bd7bf04cb74eae8bdb5c3ae4d4cd46502a40386dcb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:scasca of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Assume that $\phi_\ell\randin \mathcal{C}^\infty(M)$ is a sequences of Gaussian fields that satisfies a $\mathcal{C}^3$ scaling limit as in (def:scalim of the paper), in the range $(0,\rho)$, with parameters $\mathsf P_\ell=(K, \sigma_\ell,\lambda_\ell, 0,\rho)$. Assume that
