{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.747319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e9d7ac28c45d9861a0d43709a819fa2b993a117c331db95cf5b8d3421080d78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:conv_traces of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let $X_{11}$ be regularly varying with index $\alpha\in (0,2)$ and let $\ell \geqslant 1$ and $k_1, \dots, k_{\ell} \geqslant 1$. Then we have the convergence in distribution 
    \begin{equation}

    \left(\operatorname{Tr} \big[ {\mathbf Y}_n^{k_1} \big], \dots, \operatorname{Tr} \big[ {\mathbf Y}_n^{k_\ell} \big] \right) \stackrel{\rm d}{\rightarrow} \left(Z_{k_1}^{(\alpha)}, \dots, Z_{k_\ell}^{(\alpha)} \right) \,, \qquad n\to\infty\,,
\end{equation}
where $\big(Z_k^{(\alpha)}\big)_{k \geqslant 1}$ is an $\alpha$-family defined in Definition  (def:alpha_family of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.139866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea16422e774f0c8a4870971082d07e5de13a5296e614609c9d854b0c9711e36","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:consistent of arXiv:2510.13572, 'Coalescence in Markov chains'] A probability measure $\mu$ on $\mathcal{F}_S$ is \emph{consistent} with $P\in\mathcal{P}_S$,
in which case we say that the pair $(P,\mu)$ is \emph{consistent},  if
\begin{equation}
p_{i,j} = \mu\bigl(\{f\in\mathcal{F}_S: f(i)=j\}\bigr), \qquad  i,j\in S.
\end{equation}
Let $\mathcal L_P$ denote the set of probability measures $\mu$ on $\mathcal{F}_S$ 
that are consistent with $P\in\mathcal{P}_S$.  \hfill $\blacktriangleleft$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea1fc2aafafe3569d88d346092201866fe05d969d0a84dabd28185a608db48f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem LUE soft left2 of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Consider an LUE $L_{a,N}$. Suppose there exist $\Theta_1,~\Theta_2\in \mathbb{R}$ such that $0<\Theta_1\le\frac{N}{n}\le \Theta_2<1$ and $\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{N}{n}=\gamma\in(0,1)$ where $n=N+a$. Then on any $A\subset[s,+\infty)$ for $s>-\infty$, with the same parameters as in Theorem (LUE left soft of the paper), for $N\in\mathbb{N}$ large enough,
