{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.908466+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea7ce67c4396afd781826774bee90f6cdf4ca35087d614313fad345512293bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:conjugate-expo-kernel of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] For $ \theta \in \mathbb{R}, z,w,v\in  \mathbb C$
\begin{align*}
 \mathsf{C}(e^{ i\theta }z,e^{ i\theta }w) = &\mathsf{C}(z,w),\\
 \mathsf{C}(z + v,w + v) = &e^{ i\varphi (z,v)}\mathsf{C}(z,w)e^{ -i\varphi (w,v)}
\end{align*}where  $ \varphi(z,v)  =-i z  \bar v/2 + i  \bar zv /2 $ is real valued because $  \bar \varphi  = \varphi $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.521675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea94eb72f9ff6719495d672285c59b11c0edceba6e5b1ba0e3f0006399bb18e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lcft-H-conf-infty of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] Suppose $\beta_1,\beta_2,\beta_3\in\mathbb{R}$ and $f:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}$ is the conformal map with $f(0) = 1$, $f(1)=\infty$ and $f(\infty) = 0$. Then 
