{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.947922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eaafeba6dbca31abc37cb3799048cf1412e99ab55066a0951f3294324599ce7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Gittins Index, Gittins index policy) of arXiv:2606.24703, 'Scheduling jobs with unknown size distribution in a M/G/1 queue: the shifted empirical Git'] \ \\
   The Gittins index function at age $x$ of a job with  size
   measure $\phi$ and remaining probability function $\bar{F}$ is

    \begin{equation}

      \nu(x) := \sup_{y > x}\frac{\pr (X \leq y | X>x)}{\E(\min(X,y) -x | X>x)} =  \sup_{y > x} \frac{\int_{x}^{y}  d\phi(u)}{\int_{x}^{y} \bar{F}(u) du}.
    \end{equation}
    The corresponding Gittins index policy works as follows:
    Whenever the  age $x$ of the current active job is preemptable ($x\in \XP$), the Gittins index policy activates one  job with the maximal current Gittins index.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.776860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eab5977bb2ee4d511a9a94bf556e66672c2572f25640992c91ff2bf2620eb63","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma heat_kernel_from_Z_to_T of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] For any $x \in \mathbb{T}^d_L$, $n \in \mathbb N$, and $L \in \mathbb N^+$, we have 
