    \end{align*}
for some $C = C(\alpha, L)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.333709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eac27e0525ce18815271e1264a3897a0a0645affbdf60d55478f97e02db127f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2512.05466, 'Stochastic Flows and Marked Stable Processes'] (\cite[Proposition 3.8]{aidekon2023stochastic}, \cite[Proposition 2.17]{AWYskew})
    Let $\overline{\delta}\colon \bR \to \bR$ be a deterministic drift function and $\overline{\delta}^*(x):=\overline{\delta}(-x)$, $x\in \bR$. If ${\mathcal S}$ is a $\rm BESQ(\overline{\delta})$ flow (resp.\ killed $\rm BESQ(\overline{\delta})$ flow), driven by ${\mathcal W}$, then its dual
    \begin{equation}
    \big( \cS^*_{r,x}(a) := \inf\{ b>0: \cS_{-x,-r}(b)>a \}, \; x\ge r\big), \quad r\in \bR, a\ge 0
    \end{equation}
    is a killed $\rm BESQ(2-\overline{\delta}^*)$ flow (resp.\ a   $\rm BESQ(2-\overline{\delta}^*)$ flow), driven by $-{\mathcal W}^*$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.874136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eacc8ca23defa8ad7cfbb9b21a68c14af261a8d8772b5fb7b2794f393e84870","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm aoinP of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $a_0\in \interior(P)$, then there is a non empty open set $U\subset\mathbb{R}^m$ such that
