{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:27.993383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eeb986c447d9d096f1ee4af502f1a31d24cbca375ae02f17f4f0e155da622bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem weakconvgapsthm of arXiv:2608.04730, 'A new look at some aspects of one-dimensional random sequential adsorption and its continu'] Consider the probability  measures $\{\mu^{\text{gaps}}_k\}_{k=2}^\infty$ defined in (equation muk of the paper), where $g_{k;l}$ is as in (equation lgaps of the paper) and $m_k$ is as in (equation mk of the paper). Then
