{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.549756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ef7dabed15ed6b7dfeb4e293f7cc5a1183a9add0754649dff07eab4c1a2fc05","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th9 of arXiv:2411.17104, 'Two-barriers-reflected BSDE with Rank-based Data'] Assume that (\textbf{A1)}-(\textbf{A3)} are satisfied. If for each positive $R$, there exists a positive function $\zeta_R$ on $[0,\infty)$ with
