{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.600672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ef8122e55a51e86aed9033d50672ec9faa96a888fbad1c4bf7ff2fee59831d9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:Yproperty of arXiv:2411.10586, 'A convergence framework for Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble\\ via pole evolution'] For any particle-generated Nevanlinna function $Y:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}\cup{\mathbb R}$, the quantity ${\rm Im}[w]{\rm Im}[Y(w)]$ is monotone in ${\rm Im}[w]$; the derivatives of $Y$ satisfy
