\item $r\in[n^{5/6},0.499 n]$, and $6\log n\le k\le o(n/\log n)$. 
\end{enumerate}
Moreover, suppose that $t':=t-\frac{n\log n}{k}$ satisfies $|t'|\le \frac{n(\log\log n-\omega(1))}{2k}$. Then, we have 
$$|s_\l(k)|^{2t}\le \exp\left(-2r\log n+r\log r-\omega(r)\right).$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.365675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f12e2fd3586c80ca0d36a0a0f027fdfbb7d11385f018979f44eceee8efbf2b4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 24 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] There exist a universal constant $C_{4,d}$ depending
