\end{align*}

\noindent
for any fixed $\xi_1,\dots,\xi_k \in [-L_\varepsilon, L_\varepsilon]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.640478+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f3281f50876727a3a71094c020bc7c4b57ac3807f07073b11c1050726a76a3f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma}, and \ref{ass:k:positive}.  Then, for every $x_0\in\Cc$, there exists a weak solution $U$ of the invariant-coordinate equation \eqref{eq:u:SDE}, started from $U(0)=w(x_0)$, such that
