{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.240648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f335cd928e8ff29fc20570931c9a84bb814e6cc10647352fdaf9c4e95f1a5f9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Psi properties of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For any $\boldsymbol{F} \subset \mathbb{T}_N$ and $M_0>0$ such that 
    (equation eq: cost of inserting loops not large of the paper) holds, and
    for any $(\boldsymbol{F},\varepsilon,M_0)$-good path collection $\mathcal{A}$, there exists a mapping $\Psi$ from $\mathcal{A}$ to $2^{\Omega_{T_4}}$ such that:
    \begin{subequations}

        \begin{align}
            & \text{For any } \omega \in \mathcal{A} \text{ and } \widetilde{\omega} \in \Psi(\omega) \text{, we have } \mathbb{T}_N \subset \widetilde{\omega}[0,T_4] ;\\ 
