{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.856683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f3bbbc1ade8ff29a69fa3ddb2bd4bcab283b57a81f397e7bbd68130dbc0b2d5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def1 ch5-d1 of arXiv:2410.23995, 'Sample path properties of parabolic SPDEs with non constant coefficients'] Assume $({\bf H_{\Gamma}})$ and $({\bf H_{\Lambda}})$. A jointly measurable and adapted real-valued random field $(u(t,x),\, (t,x)\in [0,T]\times D)$ is a {\em random field solution} of the SPDE (equation 5.1 of the paper) if, for all $(t,x)\in [0,T]\times D$,  the following identity is satisfied:
