{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.319584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f3d85a151a002f61b7bae16a9d55627660d67cc25ef68ab363c80f5c1d8d561","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:rieszcomp of arXiv:2411.09058, 'Time-dependent averages of a critical long-range stochastic heat equation'] For any $0<\alpha,\beta,\alpha+\beta<d$ and $x\neq y$,
    \begin{align*}
      \int_{\mathbb R^d} \|x-z\|^{\alpha-d} \|z-y\|^{\beta -d}dz=k_{\alpha,\beta,d} \|x-y\|^{\alpha+\beta-d}, 
  \end{align*}
  with the coefficient \begin{align*}
    k_{\alpha,\beta,d} =\pi^{d/2}\frac{\Gamma(\frac{\alpha}{2})\Gamma(\frac{\beta}{2})\Gamma(\frac{d-\alpha-\beta}{2})}{\Gamma(\frac{d-\alpha}{2})\Gamma(\frac{d-\beta}{2})\Gamma(\frac{\alpha+\beta}{2})}.
  \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

