{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.201381+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f42ecc3199813afd5b66de6cc7b5f2e058650a20665b6ad58d7e03af6052036","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_cov of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Let $\nu =\nu_{L,M}$ be the canonical Ising measure (equation RestrDU of the paper) with positive definite interaction matrix $\L$
