{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.923633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f47ce759d572d74d2576d4e3f90d443d2da8c5557344f6f5055b4ef9b6e25c8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition goodrepeated of arXiv:2412.02087, 'The spectral distribution of random graphs with given degree sequences'] [Bounds on ``good" repeated edges] Suppose there are $r$ distinct ``good" repeated edges with multiplicities $\alpha_i\geq 2$. The following bound is achieved
