{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.337282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f5fc45e13b8137bbec7a45961e25b0ce8ca32930fe3a38bfbe60ea543a659b5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition newCminus of arXiv:2607.19651, 'Metastability and phase transition in a social network model with multiple opinions'] For any opinion $o\in\mathcal{O}$, a consensus set for $o$ is defined in the following way
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{C}^o = \{u \in \mathcal{S}:u\neq 0, u(a,o)\geq 0 ,u(a,p)\leq 0, \forall a\in\mathcal{A}, \forall p\in\mathcal{O}\setminus\{o\}\}.
\end{equation}
Note that for any $u\in \mathcal{C}^o$, there exists at least one actor $a\in \mathcal{A}$ such that $u(a,o)>0$.
    A consensus set for another opinion than $o\in\mathcal{O}$ is defined as follows:
    \[
    \mathcal{C}^{-o}=\bigcup_{p\in\mathcal{O}\setminus\{o\}}\mathcal{C}^p .
    \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.925591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f67599d13f49804a8315d8187c35911ffa3f3c31aec411958ac81a06b269072","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 21 (\Cref{thm: restate of pnkt and nu} in the text) of arXiv:2603.27433, 'The $k$-cycle shuffling with repeated cards'] For $n=\omega(1)$ and $k\ge 2$, the following holds. Let $t':=t-\frac{n\log n}{k}$. Let $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ be defined as in \Cref{defi: Pnk and its convolution}, and $\nu_{n,k}^t$ be defined as in \Cref{defi: construction of nu}. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Suppose that $2\le k\le o(n/\log n)$, and $t'=cn/k$, where $c\in\R$ is an absolute constant. Then, we have $$d_{TV}(P_{n,k}^{*t},\nu_{n,k}^t)=o(1).$$ 
\item Suppose that $2\le k\le n^{c_0+o(1)}$, where $c_0\in[0,1)$ is an absolute constant, and $|t'|\le \frac{n(\log\log n-\omega(1))}{2k}$.
Then, we have $$d_{TV}(P_{n,k}^{*t},\nu_{n,k}^t)\le n^{c_0-1+o(1)}.$$ 
