{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.991518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fd5046191089ddbfdbc0f525366b6373a076441d66722d20ddbe579a71274d6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 110 (cf. Theorem \ref{T:length} and {\cite[Theorem 1.4) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {Mak24}}]
Let $K_n$ be the complete graph and assume that $(\omega_e)_{e \in E}$ are independently uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$. Then for $\beta = \beta(n)$, we have with high probability (and in $\P$-expectation) that
\begin{equation*}
        \bE^\omega_{n,\beta}\big[ L(\cT) \big] = 
