{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.778582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fdbd0bd4ac74e7cd93b33c223ef8bead7932a51638ae46c37c4296c46aca9e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:parity of arXiv:2608.01253, 'The pseudo-quantum representation of \\finite reversible Markov chains'] Run the uniformised chain of (sec:setup of the paper), a Poisson$(\Lambda)$ clock with
$P$-moves at the ticks, and start the doubled chain at $(i,+)$. At time $t$ the
doubled chain is at $(j,+)$ if the original chain is at $j$ after an even number of
ticks, and at $(j,-)$ if after an odd number. Consequently, for the embedding
$\widehat\pi_0=\binom{\pi_0}{0}$,

\begin{equation}
\widehat T_t\binom{\pi_0}{0}
=\binom{\,e^{-s}\cosh(sP^{T})\,\pi_0\,}{\,e^{-s}\sinh(sP^{T})\,\pi_0\,},
\qquad s=\Lambda t,

\end{equation}

so the two sheets carry the even and odd halves of the Poisson representation
(equation eq:poisson-rep of the paper), and their sum returns $T_t\pi_0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.521488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fdc084f9a7da9da28d7175911295ab414defb0c1b3a7e9c79961313fc3fcd46","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:plaquette-loop-cluster of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] For any bad plaquette configuration $P \sse \mc{P}_{\Lambda}^+$, let 
