{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.700973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fe772b8d89fbc438a3faa02754ef112d0b2ad649045a3b2fb526765934a7581","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.06011, 'Strong averaging principle for multiscale time-inhomogeneous SDEs with multiplicative $\al'] Suppose that Assumption \ref{cond} holds. Then for any $s<t<t+\Delta\leq T$ with a given $T>s$ and $\Delta> 0$, there exists $C_{\kappa,p,s,T}>0$ such that for all $p\in[1,\alpha)$,
