{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.508449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ff34b63556ca49336c35c68e09075e9069f55111f54be80f4a0c2dc086cb337","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c.mean-and-median of arXiv:2505.15283, 'Quantization of Probability Distributions via Divide-and-Conquer: Convergence and Error Pr'] For $f(\mu)= \bar{\mu}$ and $f(\mu) = \mathrm{med}(\mu)$ we have that the general upper bound of~(equation e.ttr-error of the paper) holds with 
