{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.746691+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ff365623087ecc4a3ad4a1d55d07cdb0146389af1ab920966f145f02945cd8d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Let $\{X_n;n\geq 1\}$ be a sequence of identically distributed random variables in the sub-linear expectation space $\sles$ with $C_{\V}[X_1^2]<\infty$. Then there exists a sequence of positive constants $\{\kappa_i;i\leq1\}$ with $\kappa_i\downarrow0$ and $\kappa_i\sqrt{i/\log\log i}\rightarrow\infty$ such that
