{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.744667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ff75541e1899f6c776e12218904bd9b5ab0a1edc23aaefbf053ff7255690b46","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 (Bounded support condition) of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] A random matrix $X$ is said to satisfy the {\it bounded support condition} with parameter $q$ if
\begin{equation}
\max_{i,\mu}\abs{x_{i\mu}} \prec q, 
\end{equation}
Here $q$ is a deterministic parameter, typically satisfying \(n^{-1/2} \le q \le n^{-c_\phi}\) for some small constant \(c_\phi>0\). Whenever \eqref{eq_support} holds we say that $X$ has support $q$. In particular, under the arbitrarily high-moment assumption (\ref{eq_highmoment}) one may take $q=n^{-1/2}$ by Lemma \ref{momentmethod}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.743275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fff90ccf47c96c255f670b3017269867be2d59bd739d85238154f7aec9aadef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 59 of arXiv:2506.10494, 'Geometric Jensen-Shannon Divergence Between Gaussian Measures On Hilbert Space'] Let $\Ncal(m_0,C_0)$, $\Ncal(m,C)$, $\ker(C) = \ker(C_0) = \{0\}$, be two equivalent Gaussian measures on $\Hcal$, with
