{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.833869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_505213ffec021cd7042d30813da807e924939a8faf5493936c739f6be9a9b544","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Polymers starting uniformly from a small ball) of arXiv:2608.13359, 'Fractional moments of the Stochastic Heat Flow and\\2D Directed Polymers'] There are constants \(c,C>0\) such that, for all \(p\in (0,1)\) all \(N\in \N\), 
