  where \(\cV(T) \coloneqq \int_0^{\infty} \frac{T^s}{\Gamma(s+1)} \dd s\) is the Volterra function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.971679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_505445deae8393c1575506bdeef29fa4ce1cde010ec57aa5fa697d8edde3887d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 41 of arXiv:2606.13459, 'Symmetric Cooperative Motion in Higher Dimensions'] Let $(w_{N})_{N \in \N}$ and $(z_{N})_{N \in \N}$ be two sequences in $L^{1}(\R^{d}\times[a,b])$ which have an approximate temporal modulus of continuity $\om$. Then for all compact $D \subset \R^{d}$, 
