{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.581814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5059eeb2cac673940aac9c5c30b0bb1db01590798242905d6f07fbb8b2016566","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Prop.503 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p\geq 1$, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $n $ and $t $ such that 
