{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.332801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_505d69028e75bf2f8eaeca3398017362ad9b00c5fd0aab25f1020189400fe6b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 of arXiv:2607.14718, 'Anchored Nash inequalities and heat kernel bounds for a class of random conductance models'] Suppose there exist $p, q \in (1, \infty]$ satisfying \eqref{a1-1-2} such that \eqref{a1-1-1} holds. Further, assume that the interpolated anchored Nash inequality \eqref{p2-2-1} holds, and there exist $m_{0} > d$ and $K_{1}, K_{2} \in (0,\infty)$ such that

  \begin{align}
    \mu_{2}(y)
    \;=\;
    \sum_{z \in \boldsymbol{V}} W(y,z)\, d(y,z)^{2}
    \;\leq\;
    K_{1}\, \theta(y),
    \qquad \forall\, y \in \boldsymbol{V},
