{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.889294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5061fa3b6ac579f9fe79774dca212c90ba15f4fcecadb141b0ae314f6a0f9313","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Aronsz and AT of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $A,B\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ be finite subsets and let $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{>0}^A$ and $\beta\in \mathbb{R}_{>0}^B$. Denote by $g$, respectively $g_{\alpha}$ and $g_\beta$  the AT metric on $\mathbb{R}^m$ of the GRF $\mathcal{E}_{\alpha}\odot\mathcal{E}_{\beta}$, respectively of $\mathcal{E}_{\alpha}$ and $\mathcal{E}_{\beta}$. Then for all $x\in \mathbb{R}^m$ we have
  \begin{equation}
