{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.388745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5068263c8b98788d0ea5d2a268f138d6d701102432691461f26063bcd43e99bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma polynomial moments of arXiv:2412.07936, 'Simple Norm Bounds for Polynomial Random Matrices via Decoupling'] Let ${\bf H}({\bf x}) : \Omega \rightarrow \mathbb{H}^d$ be a function with ${\bf x} \sim \gauss{0}{\mathbb{I}_n}$. For $t=1$ and $t \geq 1.5$,
