{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.908766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5095d078ff81b627e2134cf4489659353d7f541eed3652aa43b5e742a9e6dcf7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2603.26303, 'Spectral Gap of Biased Adjacent-Transposition Chains'] Let $f\in \mathbb{R}^{\mathfrak{S}_n}$.
Then, for $n\ge 3$,
\begin{equation*}

\langle f,K^2f\rangle\ge \frac{1-2m_{\mathbf p}\cos(\tfrac{{\pi}}{n})}{n-1}\langle f, Kf\rangle.
\end{equation*}
In the case of equality, there exists a non-negative constant $c$ such that
\begin{align}
    \mathsf E_r \mathsf E_s f&= 0 \qquad\qquad\quad \ \ \;\text{ for $|r-s| \ge 2$;}  \\
