{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.770452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50c3dbb61325ba8d66763b0599f4be9a83b6e872a040fac29ad8011e1e429fc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq: spatialPA split up of arXiv:2411.02917, '\hspace*{2mm}\\[-16mm] Stein's Method for Spatial Random Graphs'] Let $(\Xi,\Sigma)$ be the graph constructed by the spatial preferential attachment model. 
Consider a function $h:\mathfrak{N}\times \mathcal{X}\times\mathfrak{N}_2\to\R_+$ that evaluates the edge structure of a (typical) vertex in the spatial preferential attachment model. Then  
\begin{align}
    \E\bigg[\int_{\mathcal{X}} h(\Xi-\delta_{(x,s)},(x,s),\Sigma\vert_{\langle \Xi-\delta_{(x,s)},(x,s)\rangle}) \, \Xi(\diff (x,s))\bigg] = \int_{\mathcal{X}} \E\bigl[h\big(\Xi,(x,s),(\Sigma_2^{<s},\Sigma_2^{>s})\big) \bigr] \, \alpha(\diff (x,s)),
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{L} \bigl( \Sigma_2^{<s},\Sigma_2^{>s} \bigm| \Xi, \Sigma \bigr) = \mathcal{L} \bigl( \Sigma_2^{<s} \bigm| \Xi_{s-}, \Sigma_{s-} \bigr) \otimes \mathcal{L} \bigl( \Sigma_2^{>s} \bigm| \Xi \bigr)$ is the product measure of outgoing and incoming edges for the additional vertex $(x,s)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

