{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.452895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50d3ca44f3c584b8063e4a10514779c34c66f62eb28a363de3d2480a21a353ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm : MAIN of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Assume~(equation ass : Intro/main_thm/SubcriticalAtom of the paper) and~(equation ass : Intro/main_thm/exp_moment of the paper). The process $\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( \SPT \aftergroup\egroup\originalright)_{n\ge 1}$ follows the large deviation principle at speed $n$ with the good rate function
    \begin{align}
        \notag \FdT : \mathcal F_{\mathrm b}  &\longrightarrow \intervalleff0\infty \\
        D &\longmapsto
        \begin{cases}
            \FdTmon(D) &\text{ if } D \in \RegPD[\mu],\\
