   \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.222716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50dc2bccf82925e3392a0f7defe5e3558b2a857d67d71da561162494e58ead9c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: 2625 of arXiv:2607.05848, 'Mesoscopic eigenvalue statistics for correlated random matrices'] Recall that we fixed $\hat{\epsilon}\in(0,\beta_{*}/3)$ satisfying $[E_{0}-\hat{\epsilon},E_{0}+\hat{\epsilon}]\subset\mathcal{I}(3\epsilon_{0}/2)$.
