{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.267589+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50deaec5aefa2c9d82638df582b880e972dc96849700a26120e4d0b1c33c70db","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Deff 2 of arXiv:2604.20435, 'Stochastic Extinction with Relaxed Boundedness Conditions'] A function $f$ is said to be uniformly integrable w.r.t. a family of probability measures $\C$ if for any $\eps$, there is a $K$ such that


