{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.886858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5125a8b9779971f2f508468f57c5a555fcf60df4eed01da815c5c624460611f9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Fix two non-negative integers $m,k\in\ZZ_{\geq 0}$  such that $m\le k<\alpha$. Then with $u=-m$, $v=-k$ we have
  \begin{multline}
     \GG_N(\alpha,-m,-k)=  (-1)^{k+m} \tfrac{(k+m)!}{k!^2m!^2} \Gamma (\alpha )^{2 N}\\+
     \sum_{j=0}^{k-m-1}
   (-1)^j {\binom{m+k}{j}}\, \tfrac{ 2 (k-j)(k-m-j-1)!}{(2k-j)!} \Gamma (\alpha +j-k)^N \Gamma (\alpha -j+k )^N
