    \\ +\psi(i+1)+\psi(1+i+k-m)- \psi(1+k+m-i) -\psi(1+2m-i) +\tfrac{1}{m-i}\Big] \\ \cdot  \Gamma (\alpha+ i-m )^N \Gamma (\alpha- i+m)^N.
 \end{multline}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.874689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_512924c566abb4bab6d8fe10f499ed22652b0d38ad62915d22b40d2895e5e2b3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro basicproperties of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] The following hold:
    \begin{coroitems}
        \item $0 \leq \varepsilon_n \leq (b-a)^n/n!$. Consequently, $\varepsilon_n \to 0$ and $\{\varepsilon_n\}_n \in \ell^1(\mathbb{N})$. 
        \item $\varepsilon_n = (b-a)^n/n!$ for all $n \geq 0$ if and only if $X = a$ a.s., and $\varepsilon_n = 0$ for all $n \geq 1$ if and only if $X = b$ a.s.
