    +
    \tau_{m,b,a} \quad \text{a.s.}
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.298200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51332eb341d37f536a7653b6b5027b5b4ae94e2582d8db9335e592cf79bd4a13","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma MarkovFell*** of arXiv:2604.21591, '\bf Long-time dynamics of stochastic 2D hydrodynamic-type evolution equations driven by mu'] Assume that the hypotheses of Theorem (2DHD-the3.3-0 of the paper) and (equation LSWs6.3 of the paper) hold. Then $\Psi(t,\tau), t\geq \tau,$ is a continuous non-autonomous dynamical system associated with ((2DHD-1.1 of the paper)). More precise, $\Psi(t,\tau):\mathcal{P}_4({H})\rightarrow \mathcal{P}_4({H})$ satisfies that for any $\tau \in \mathbb{R}$,

