{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.701870+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_513413b1ed53bddfde23e8cd17ad657bb9fc3bc805550ca7b274a00ed694e77d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor typeIVandC of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] There exists a constant $C>1$ that depends on $\mathbf{k}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{k}_{l}$ and $\sigma$, and is uniform in $N$, such that for all $N\ge 100$,
