{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.329227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5135010e06a101603f5901aec2d960626b7e6e7e0848fb209b0aee48681e0fc3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: Fan Process of arXiv:2609.03755, 'The Scramble Number of Outerplanar Graphs'] Let $G$ be a maximal outerplanar graph on $n$ vertices with $n\geq 8$ and $\left( v_i,v_j\right)$ an interior edge. If $\deg\left( v_i\right)>\sqrt{2n}$ and $\deg\left( v_i\right)\geq \deg\left( v_j\right)$, then there exists a set $\mathcal{H}$ that satisfies the following:
    \begin{enumerate}

        \item $G\setminus\left( \mathcal{H}\cup \{v_i,v_j\}\right)$ is separated into components $C_1, \ldots, C_m$ such that $|C(C_i, G\setminus C_i)|\leq  3\sqrt{2n}+8$. That is, the outdegree of each component is at most $3\sqrt{2n}+8.$ 
        \item $|\mathcal{H}|\leq 2\left\lfloor \frac{\Delta}{\sqrt{2n}}\right\rfloor-2$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.165633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_513735442119068219aaac0d55aeec1869daae5ae17cdedc62c19fb5c1a482d6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm_UniformlyFredholm_SardSmale of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let ${\mathbf{X}}$ and ${\mathbf{Y}}$ be second-countable tame Fréchet manifolds.
