{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.441543+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_514d7040e92b56afb039ea42431251ff01b1ef7ed3f6ec9ea1d2ece26a6d7ec6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:B.9_Chebyshev of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] For any  fixed  number $t>0$, let $n = \lfloor tM\rfloor$, then for  $y\in\mathbb{R}$,
