{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.647813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5151483850cbcaed1d168d1746d84a5af97625f968b1ca129c8c68fd33f1e7bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: Skorohod-l2 of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] Suppose $u\in L^2(\Xi;\mathcal{H})$, that is, $u$ is an $\mathcal{H}$-valued square-integrable random variable. We say that  $u$ is ($L^2$-)Skorohod integrable  if there exists an $L^2$-integrable random variable denoted by $\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)$ such that for any $F\in \mathbb{D}^{1,2}$, we have
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)F\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\langle DF, u\rangle_{\mathcal{H}}\right] 
\end{align}
with $|\mathbb{E}\left[\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)F\right]|\leq c\Vert F\Vert_{L^2({\mathbb P})}$, where $c$ is a constant depending on u. We call $\boldsymbol{\delta}(u)$ the $L^2$-Skorohod integral of $u$ or the divergence of $u$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.350854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5151f4ad6663c02dbb8bb5a339da425bd1d2d707d4f67fd3f5f35aa2f7eea92f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_steinmethod_xlessthanl_gendif of arXiv:2509.18045, 'Density convergence on Markov diffusion chaos via Stein's method'] Fix  $x\leq \ell$ and $k\in \mathbb{N}$. Let the function $h$ in the ODE (equation equation_stein of the paper) be 
    \begin{align*}
        h(y):=\mathds{1}_{\{y\leq x\}}\frac{-2a(y)+b'(y)}{b(y)},\quad y\in \mathbb{R}\setminus \left\{y\in(-\infty,x]:b(y)=0 \right\}.
    \end{align*} 
Then a solution $g_x: \mathbb{R}\setminus \brac{\left\{y\in(\ell,u)^\complement:a(y)=0 \right\}\cup\left\{y\in(\ell,u)\cup (-\infty,x]:b(y)=0 \right\}}\to\mathbb{R}$ to (equation equation_stein of the paper) exists and satisfies for every $y$ in its domain, 
\begin{align}
     \left\vert  g_x(y) \right\rvert&\leq \mathcal{V}_3(y):= \mathds{1}_{\{y\leq \ell\}} \frac{\left\vert -2a(y)+b'(y) \right\rvert}{\left\vert b(y) \right\rvert\left\vert 2a(y) \right\rvert }\,;  
    \end{align}
and
\begin{align}
    \left\vert  g'_x(y) \right\rvert&\leq \mathcal{V}_4(y):= \mathds{1}_{\{y\leq \ell\} } \brac{\abs{\frac{(1+b''(y))b(y)-(-2a(y)+b'(y))b'(y) }{b(y)^2a(y)}}+\abs{\frac{-2a(y)+b'(y)}{b(y)4a(y)^2} }}. 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.853908+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5153ba43371da082a40b77e6f2799113ef845ece697a69931b9c1ebf740857dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2609.00105, 'Weighted composition operators and classification of weighted Hardy spaces'] Let $\mathcal{H}$ be a weighted Hardy space with the scalar Pick property and let $\rho$ be a bounded non-zero functional on $\mathcal{H}$. Then the following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\rho(\phi g)=\rho(\phi)\rho(g)$ for all $\phi\in\operatorname{Mult}(\mathcal{H})$ and all $g\in\mathcal{H}$.
        \item $\rho(fg)=\rho(f)\rho(g)$ whenever $f,g\in\mathcal{H}$ such that $fg\in\mathcal{H}$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.846015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5154e3e8635832d4901145e7c3b0659dd48f988016a300c2973189c746c3fa0f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:weightedPinsker of arXiv:2607.07598, 'Universal Central Limit Theorem for non-exchangeable interacting diffusions'] Let $P$ and $Q$ be probability measures on a measurable space $\mathcal{X}$. Let $\psi\ge0$ be such that $\int_{\mathcal{X}} \psi^2\,\mathrm{d}(P+Q)<\infty$. Then, with $|P-Q|$ denoting the total variation measure of $P-Q$, we have
		\begin{align} 
			\bigg(\int_{\mathcal{X}} \psi\,\mathrm{d}|P-Q|\bigg)^2
			\le
			2\,H(P\,|\,Q)\int_{\mathcal{X}} \psi^2\,\mathrm{d}(P+Q).
		\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.290803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5157cf12d5a4ccf69bc9a6ac6f4565ba6aff17373300fe8c1487d01053a89713","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Assume the linear growth condition \eqref{LG-condition-existence}. Suppose $X = (X(t))_{t \in [0,T]}$ is a solution to equation \eqref{path_dependent_sde_existence}
