{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.823011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5164af68086dc9907f939828f2d52c4d883b1de8087393adae02139a9a9788a9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] For any $p\geq 1$,  suppose that assumptions of Lemma \ref{thm:opao1} are satisfied with $q:=(p+p_0)\vee 2$ for some positive constant $p_0$.
		 Then, there exist two positive constants $C$, $ \varrho$ and a unique invariant probability measure  $\mu\in \msr P_p(E)$ such that $\mu P_t=\mu$ for every $t\geq 0$, and 
		\begin{equation*}
