{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.123049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5175403a4ba471176531b45804293b2e3354a56d153158f9e2dfddc5e70691cd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:support of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] Assume $\theta:=\lambda v>0$. If $c<1$, there is a unique $s_*>0$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
  cs_*^2\mathbb{E}\frac{R^2}{(1+cRs_*)^2}=1.

\end{equation}
With
\begin{equation}
  x_-:=\mathbb{E}\frac{R}{1+cRs_*}-\frac1{s_*},

\end{equation}
one has $x_->0$ and
\begin{equation}
  \operatorname{supp}\mu_{c,\lambda,v}=[x_-,\infty).

\end{equation}
If $c\ge1$, then
\begin{equation}
  \operatorname{supp}\mu_{c,\lambda,v}=[0,\infty).

\end{equation}
In particular, the support is unbounded whenever $\lambda v>0$.","status":"unverified"}

