{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.128940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_517d96167b6a0439a95dd66fd5bdfb14cfbe67cdbbcc3872be4bd78f28b86350","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:deconv of arXiv:2411.16058, 'Gaussian deconvolution on $\mathbb R^d$ \\ with application to self-repellent Brownian mot'] Let $d > 2$, let $a_d = \frac{ \Gamma(\frac{ d-2 } 2 ) }{ 2\pi^{d/2}}$, 
