{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.160726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_517ff862ecff12b0a7d0027e3bf8c56fc31b4fea4a527f391ae37f01fa570126","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma fgt-simpl-structure of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\textbf{\textup{C}}$ be a simplicial model category, and let $\textbf{\textup{D}}\subset\textbf{\textup{C}}$ be a full simplicial subcategory closed under weak equivalences. Assume moreover that $\textbf{\textup{D}}$ is locally fibrant. Then the inclusion $N(\textbf{\textup{D}}_0)\hookrightarrow N_\Delta(\textbf{\textup{D}})$ of the nerve of the underlying unenriched category induces an equivalence after localizing at the weak equivalences.
