{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.283894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51807823642794cb755ad48e8a276d34531752cac93fdbc399c469a07aa79913","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2606.22044, 'Degenerate Stochastic Delay Modified Equation: Approximation of Stochastic Variance Reduce'] Let $g \in \mathcal{G}_{1}^{2}$, $\eta\in(0,1)$ and $m\eta\geq1$. Then, for any $y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$, $s=0,1,\cdots,N$, it follows
