{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.918180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51a053cc57d4acb61ffe278651712cd275512d250315910423c3f76f9f6da42c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:cluster-process of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let   $ \mathsf{S}$ the spectral measure of $ \mathsf{P}$ . Assume $\mathbf E \#\mathsf{P}_{ 1}^{ 2}<\infty  $. Let the random Fourier-Stieljes transform $ \varphi (u) = \int_{}e^{ iu\cdot t}d\mathsf{P}_{ 1}(t)$. Then $ \mathsf{P}^{ \mu }$ is locally square integrable and has the spectral measure 
