{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.349394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51d4d84c192eb30461b93c58c919bb5049ebcf26a3236ced5b02146d97f867f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nu-self-adj of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For all $m\le k$, $M_{\hat\alpha,k,m}$ is self-adjoint as an operator on $L^2(\varsigma_{\hat\alpha,k,m})$, where 
