{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.574710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51e233469c8c18c7c94c1a009e07ed0c5930f8bb901b9565cf4af33598c13bf8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem S theorem of arXiv:2509.04349, 'Precise asymptotics for the norm of large random rectangular Toeplitz matrices'] Let $\mathbf{T}_{p\times n}^{(s)}$ and $\mathbf{C}_{p\times n}^{(s)}$ be sequences of rectangular symmetric random Toeplitz and circulant matrices defined in (equation elements of Ts of the paper) and (equation elements of Cs of the paper) and satisfying assumptions (equation Lyapunov of the paper) and  (equation new asymptotic regime of the paper). Then, as $n$ diverges to infinity, the spectral norms $\|\mathbf{T}_{p\times n}^{(s)}\|$ and $\|\mathbf{C}_{p\times n}^{(s)}\|$ satisfy
