{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.242680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_520a24e03c174a6513735fb51bd06f6148ecd664ce65bfc65cb6a8c987c1261e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:stability of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] There exist constants $c,C>0$, depending only on $(B,\lambda,\Gamma)$ and $\epsilon$, such that the following stability result holds uniformly over $z\in \cU_{\Gamma}(\epsilon)$. If $(\widetilde{M},\Delta)$ satisfies
