{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.191161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_522cb5c6324f7cb9a1971ef0ae128f54abbed9078554ea9272b2ddc0b3ca571a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn ising of arXiv:2608.06500, 'Free energy of Ising models under a spectral condition'] For a weighted graph $G=(\text{\boldmath $A$},\text{\boldmath $h$})$ on $[N]$, the \emph{Ising
    model} is the probability measure $\mu_G$ on $\{-1,1\}^N$
    assigning a mass of

    \begin{align}
    \mu_G(\text{\boldmath $\sigma$})=\frac1{Z(G)} \exp\left( \frac12\<\text{\boldmath $\sigma$},
    \text{\boldmath $A$}\text{\boldmath $\sigma$}\> + \<\text{\boldmath $h$}, \text{\boldmath $\sigma$}\> \right)
\end{align}

    to spin configurations $\text{\boldmath $\sigma$}\in\{-1,1\}^N$. Here,

    \begin{align}
    Z(G) = \sum_{\text{\boldmath $\sigma$}\in\{-1,1\}^N} \exp\left( \frac12\<\text{\boldmath $\sigma$},
    \text{\boldmath $A$}\text{\boldmath $\sigma$}\> + \<\text{\boldmath $h$}, \text{\boldmath $\sigma$}\>
    \right)
    \end{align}

    is the \emph{partition function} of the model. We furthermore
    define the \emph{normalized free energy} or \emph{free energy
    density} of the model as

    \begin{align*}
F(G) = \frac1N \log Z(G).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.025686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_522e3dfd9d946865591fe347bf6bf7a29f2390ede22bac6355ea206e97e39538","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.26501, 'Explicit Bounds on the Entropy of Piecewise H\"{o}lder Graphon Models'] Let $X\subset\rr^s$ be a $s$-cube of side length $\ell$. Divide $X$ into $m^s$ disjoint $s$-cubes of side length $\ell/m$, which we refer to as cells. If $A\subset X$ is a relative polytope, let $N$ be the number of cells which intersect the boundary of $A$. Then 
