{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.550010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5287c736b912804d5cc64c2ba0d0088f8258c3813d0fa4731bd0d1fde47cb7c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma exp of arXiv:2411.17104, 'Two-barriers-reflected BSDE with Rank-based Data'] For any fixed positive constant $A$, there is a positive $C$ and a function $\phi (x):=(\frac{1}{2}\log(1+|x|^{2})+1)^{2}$ such that
