{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.935964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5291f2cbbe586c56daf832e6cd96346ec3b9889bd887f1d9b1b8820ec0a3d81c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm|generalUpperBounds of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] The sequences $(\mathcal U_k)$ and $(\mathcal L_k)$ satisfy 
\begin{eqnarray} 
&& \mathcal U_{k+1}\leq \mathcal U_k -\mathcal L_k\quad\mbox{and}\quad \mathcal L_{k+1}\geq \mathcal L_k-\mathcal U_k, \end{eqnarray} for all $k\geq 1$. Moreover, for all $k\geq 2$,
\begin{eqnarray}
&& \mathcal U_k \leq 2^{k-2}\quad\mbox{and}\quad \left|\mathcal L_k\right| \leq 2^{k-2}. \end{eqnarray}
Also, for all integers $k \geq 2$, the following holds:
\begin{eqnarray}&& \mathcal U_k \geq \binom{k-2}{\lceil\frac{k-2}2\rceil} \quad\mbox{and}\quad \left|\mathcal L_k\right| \geq \binom{k-2}{\lceil\frac{k-2}2\rceil}.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

