{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.607624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5299c60e342346250bad8f1981633ea7fd68fe7120305befcdca6499be1bb97e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:est-S3 of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] For any $\beta\in(1-\frac{\alpha}{2},(\alpha-1)(1+\alpha))$ and $0<\epsilon$ there exists a constant $N=N(\alpha,\beta,d,\|b\|_{{\mathbb C}_{\boldsymbol{a}}^{\beta}},\epsilon)$ independent of $n$ so that for any $(s,t)\in[0,1]_\leqslant^2$ and any $\sigma$-algebra ${\mathscr G}\subset{\mathcal F}_{s}$ the following holds
