{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.832497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_529eb4781f89d2eb6c11bcca87632cdb7e8a7a1c3d31ee515cc4ac42cdf2bb48","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma continuous-to-discrete of arXiv:2606.25135, 'Convergence Rates for Semistochastic Processes'] Let $\pi$ denote the stationary distribution for a continuous-time Markov process $\{X_t\}$  with Markov semigroup \, $\mathcal{U}^t$ and let $\Delta t > 0$ be a fixed time increment.  
