{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.168500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52aef62ca18afbb62405773fdce1b1043c54709dfabe1776a1e1f3068fb5d4bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.18427, 'Expected perimeter and area of the convex hull of planar Brownian motion stopped upon exit'] Define the almost surely unique random time at which the maximum horizontal displacement $M$ is attained by
\begin{equation}
    T = \argmax_{0 \le t \le \tau_\bbD} X_t.
\end{equation}
We show that
\begin{equation}
    \bbE[M^2 - Y_T^2] = 1 - \log 2 + \int_{\pi}^{2\pi} \frac{\cos u}{u} \D u \approx 0.210624.
\end{equation}
Consequently, the expected area of the convex hull of $\bfW$ when it first exits $\bbD$ is
	\begin{equation}
		\bbE[\sfA_{\tau_{\bbD}}] = \pi \,\bbE[M^2 - Y_T^2] \approx 0.661695.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.396176+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52b0a5647f472e02aca30c8161f347b831c3dc5e3c5b430c95acbd91fc235c60","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 1. dfn: resistance forms associated with electrical networks of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] [{Resistance forms associated with electrical networks}]  

  Let $G$ be an electrical network.
  For functions $f,g: V_{G} \to \mathbb{R}$,
  we set 
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{E}_{G}(f, g) 
    \coloneqq 
    \frac{1}{2} 
    \sum_{x, y \in V_{G}} 
    \mu_{G}(x,y) (f(x) - f(y)) (g(x) - g(y))
  \end{equation}
  (if the right-hand side is well-defined).
  We then set $ \mathcal{F}_{G} \coloneqq \{ f \in \mathbb{R}^{V_{G}} \mid \mathcal{E}(f, f) < \infty \}$
  and, for each $x, y \in F$,
  \begin{equation}
    R_{G}(x,y) 
    \coloneqq 
    \sup 
    \{
      \mathcal{E}(f, f)^{-1} \mid f \in \mathcal{F},\, f(x)=1,\, f(y) = 0
    \},
  \end{equation}
  where we define $\sup \emptyset \coloneqq 0$.","status":"unverified"}

