{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.720129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52b48576fc62490621ed8eeba54d52122e24fe712998e997eb0eb2464b1c7ae5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi mean of arXiv:2411.04157, 'Stochastic homogenization of dynamical discrete optimal transport'] We say that $(\theta_{xy})_{x,y\in \mathcal X}$ is a \emph{family of mean functions} if the following conditions hold:
