   & \qquad +C_\epsilon \int_{\vec{x}_0} \left(W_1(m^N_{\vec{x}_0}, \mu_0)^{1/2}+ W_1(m^N_{\vec{x}_0}, \mu_0)^{1/2-\epsilon}\right)  \left(k W_1(m^N_{\vec{x}_0\in \{\mathbb{R}^d\}^N}, \mu_0)^{1/2}+ M\right)\mu_0^{\otimes N}(d\vec{x}_0). 
 \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.145748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52b5017914afbd62bd959801bfce90a02447304a98e1cdd37b0586ee09108dad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] For any $a,b,c>0$ and with $\mathbb{a}$ as in~\eqref{eq: gamma correlated BM},
