{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.763988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52c2470a2ba16a4d89429c433266b821a52c662b741fdf738eca8ddb491ccf8e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 (Class $C^1(\mathbb{R}^2)$) of arXiv:2605.18198, 'Large deviations of crowding in finite $\beta$-ensembles'] A map $Q$  is said to be a continuously differentiable function on $\R^2$ if the first partial derivatives
	\(
