{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:08.922193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52c255105e0bcc6e979aca99d621442a565db20d59ca2215fe5c00ef7e7abc5f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:type2constant of arXiv:2411.10633, 'A Geometric Perspective on the Injective Norm of Sums of Random Tensors'] Given $r\geq 2$ an integer and $2 \leq p < \infty$ we define $\mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)$ the Type-2 constant of the $\ell_p$ injective norm of order $r$ tensors to be the minimal number, such that for all positive integers $n$ and tensors $T_1, \ldots, T_n \in (\mathbb R^d)^{\otimes r}$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb E \Big\| \sum_{k=1}^n \varepsilon_k T_k\Big\|_{\mathcal{I}_p}^2 \leq \mathcal{C}_{r,p}(d)^2 \sum_{k=1}^n \left\lVertT_k\right\rVert_{\mathcal{I}_p}^2.
\end{equation}
The $\varepsilon_1, \ldots, \varepsilon_n$ are i.i.d. Rademacher random variables (i.e.: $ \varepsilon_k = 1$ or $\varepsilon_k = -1$ with probability $\frac12$ each).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.821920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52c6790cefba0b7107007e6d8aec75dedca442c6cf236820b49f4c7a67e7e672","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] \cite[Lemma 6.4.1]{Maostochatic}
