{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.251599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52d35af44ecb9f274d351179e356ecc5cee229a97fdd08af4e90d5cbc15d1952","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 65 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Let $K,  D $ satisfy \eqref{eq:costanti}. 
	Let $0<q\le \varepsilon_0$, 
	denote $\ell_0 = \ell_0 (q)$ and let $k \ge \ell_0$ be an integer such that $q \ge 2^k N^{K \delta-1}$. Set 
	\begin{flalign}

		\begin{aligned}
			& q' \in [q - 2^k N^{D \delta-1}, q]; \qquad \mathsf{t} = 2^k q^{-1} N^{1+11K\delta}
		\end{aligned}
	\end{flalign}
	and denote $\ell_0' = \ell_0 (q')$. Consider the Glauber dynamics $(H_t)_{t \ge 0}$ starting from an initial condition $\mu\in\mathcal P^+$ (recall \Cref{def:P+}) and assume that, w.o.p. under $\mu$,
	\begin{flalign}

		\begin{aligned} 
			& H_0 (w) \le \mathcal{H}_{q'} (w), \qquad \text{for each $w \in \bigcup_{j=1}^{k} \mathcal{A}_j^{q'} (N^{A\delta})$}; \\
			& H_0 (w) \le \mathcal{H}_q (w), \qquad \text{for each $w \in \mathfrak{X}$}.
		\end{aligned} 
	\end{flalign}
	Then we have w.o.p. that, for any $t \in [\mathsf{t}, N^{5}]$, 
	\begin{flalign}

		H_t (z) \le \mathcal{H}_{q'} (z) + N^{\delta-1}, \qquad \text{for each $z \in \mathfrak{X}$}.
