\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.008237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5337deffc3db73b0fac6b1b402cbf0d3e1ba7d31d0cc4d425005f9bc6b1b226a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:gamma-properties of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] Under Assumptions (ass:LR of the paper), (ass:diff2 of the paper), and~(ass:SC of the paper), the Malliavin covariance operator $\gamma_t$ defined in (equation eq:malliavin-cov-def of the paper) is a random, positive, self-adjoint, trace-class operator on $H$, satisfying:
