{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.216922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53401758b84256f76291c777fc5aeba072d639e821f8ef388d170e612391ba71","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.00233, 'A survey on mapping class groups of 3-manifolds'] Let $G = (V,E,\alpha)$ be the not necessarily simple, undirected, vertex-decorated graph with vertex and edge set
\[
\begin{aligned}
V &= \{ M_j \mid 1 \leq j \leq n \} \cup \{ * \} \\
E &= \{ B_h \mid 1 \leq h \leq k \} \cup \{ T_i \mid 1 \leq i \leq m \}
\end{aligned}
\]
and vertex decoration determined by
\[
\alpha(M_j) = [\text{the diffeomorphism class of $M_j$}], \quad \alpha(*) = \emptyset
\]
where the edge $B_h$ connects the distinguished vertex $*$ to the vertex $M_j$ if $B_h$ is a boundary component of $M_j$, and the edge $T_i$ connects the vertices corresponding to the neighbouring components $M_j$ (which may be equal).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.166193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5344d9255eaf90fbd96ddf6ce3f1815ec5f0b0cab2235198e01f0a8387f9bbb7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma minors of delta matrix of arXiv:2609.04072, 'Oort's conjecture for split unitary Shimura varieties'] Let $(\delta_{i,l}^j)_{(i,j,l)\in \llbracket1,g\rrbracket^2\times \llbracket0,N-1\rrbracket}$ be a family of elements of $\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p$. Define the $(g'+1)\times g$-matrix $A_1(\underline{X})\in \operatorname{Mat}_{(g'+1)\times g}(\mathcal P)$ as:
\begin{equation}A_1(\underline{X}):=
    \begin{pmatrix}

		\sum\limits_{l=0}^{N-1}\sum\limits_{i=1}^g\delta_{i,l}^1 X_{i,l} & \dots & \sum\limits_{l=0}^{N-1}\sum\limits_{i=1}^g\delta_{i,l}^g X_{i,l}  \\
		X_{1,0}^{p^{r_1}} & \dots & X_{g,0}^{p^{r_1}}\\
		\dots & \dots & \dots
		\\
		X_{1,0}^{p^{r_{g'}}}& \dots &X_{g,0}^{p^{r_{g'}}}
	\end{pmatrix}
    \end{equation}
    Then the matrix $A_1$ admits a non-zero $(g'+1)$-minor if and only if one of the following conditions is satisfied:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item There exists indices $(i,j,l)$ with $l>0$ or $i\neq j$, such that $\delta^j_{i,l}\neq 0$,
        \item there exists indices $(i,j)$ such that $\delta^i_{i,0}\neq \delta^j_{j,0}$,
        \item there exists an index $i$ such that $\delta^i_{i,0}\neq 0$ and $0\notin \{r_1,\dots,r_{g'}\}$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.160023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53502f73f1555fba76548728d8eceba0c7b1395090acf4a6027388dfc1a85cf6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 (Cutoff estimates) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Let $J_\nu$ be the cutoff used in
\eqref{eq:Friedrichs-mass}--\eqref{eq:Friedrichs-momentum}.  If
$0\le r\le q$, then
\begin{equation*}
 \norm{(I-J_\nu)f}_{H^r}
 \le C\nu^{r-q}\norm f_{H^q},\qquad
 \norm{J_\nu f}_{H^q}\le C\norm f_{H^q}.
\end{equation*}
In particular, for a family bounded in $H^s$,
\[
 \norm{(J_\nu-J_\mu)f}_{H^{s-1}}
 \le C(\nu^{-1}+\mu^{-1})\norm f_{H^s}.
\]
For a family bounded only in $H^{s-1}$, the estimate actually used on the
nonlinear hyperbolic right-hand side is
\begin{equation*}
 \norm{(J_\nu-J_\mu)f}_{H^{s-2}}
 \le C(\nu^{-1}+\mu^{-1})\norm f_{H^{s-1}}.
\end{equation*}
Moreover, for a coordinate derivative $\partial_k$ and an integer $m\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \norm{[J_\nu,a]\partial_k f}_{H^m}
 \le C_m\left(\norm{\nabla a}_{L^\infty}\norm f_{H^m}
 +\norm{\nabla a}_{H^m}\norm f_{L^\infty}\right),

\end{equation}
with a constant independent of $\nu$ whenever the right-hand side is
finite.","status":"unverified"}

