{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.932382+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_536573ffb387c7ecfd4afb8ee68437937e672cf95806eef3b5305c39df3eb46d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 30 (Bounds for the transition probabilities of $M$) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] Fix two constants $c_1,c_2>0$ with $c_1<c_2$. Then there exist $c>0$ and $C>0$ such that the following is true:
