{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.474148+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5394093198f4457e840c84b684755ee05f43f9fe55dffb4354558c11bae64847","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma restr-equiv-rQ of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be a continuous group homomorphism, and let ${\mathcal{F}},{\mathcal{F}}'$ be collections of closed subgroups of $G$ and $G'$, respectively, such that $\alpha(H)\in{\mathcal{F}}'$ for every $H\in{\mathcal{F}}$. Then 
    \[
