{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.608273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53a25dfab9905cac028b9804f6008876583c73567d3529dda151e9726db18904","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:avg_meas of arXiv:2412.05239, 'Conditions for uniform in time convergence: applications to averaging, numerical discretis'] Suppose (ass_avg_meas of the paper) holds. Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\mathbb{R}^n\times \mathbb{R}^d$. Then there exists a constant $\tilde{\mathbf{C}}>0$ such that for all $t\ge 0$ and $\delta>0$,
