{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.553383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_540e93a29ed4872ea17c3d47384c5577440ae464dbaf9e0c6ecc669f5af519a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:leaf_and_tree of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] For all $x\in [n]$ and $u\in [0,1]$, we have
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\bigl[u^{d(x)}\mathbf{1}_{x\in \mathcal{Q}_n\cap \mathcal{T}_n}\bigr] = g_k(u\eta_k) - \frac{c_{\textrm{approx}}^1(w,u)}{n}+O\Big(\frac{1}{n^2}\Big),
\end{equation}
where  $d(x)$ is the number of $\mathbf{w}$-preimages of $x\in [n]$ and $c_{\textrm{approx}}^1(w,u):=  \mathbb E_{\scriptscriptstyle BGW}[u^{Z_k}c_{\textrm{approx}}^{\tau_{\mathbf{Z}}}(w^2)\mathbf{1}_{Z_{2k}=0}]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.616779+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_541307951ea328e12600bf82aa731c72b25ac2a2461db8b4d07ddcf21d41b5b3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:massive_infrared of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] ~
