{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.358807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5413bc9bd9429e5b470365c5b4ee71a18a65c608c934d1078dcf15b412906592","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bayes_opt_denoiser_linearization of arXiv:2608.23938, 'Generalization, memorization, and overfitting \\for diffusion models trained in the lazy h'] Suppose that Assumptions~(ass:high_dim of the paper) and~(ass:input_dist of the paper) hold. Let ${\boldsymbol v}\in\mathbb{R}^d$ with $\|{\boldsymbol v}\|_2=1$. Then there exists a constant $c>0$ such that
