\item $(\Gamma^2) = (\Delta^2) = - 1/4$ and $(\Gamma \cdot \Delta) = 1/2$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.189792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5413e3590c08ec9c862ebf1d97ce56fe539e6dc8b339972bf76b9e5620e1ee02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:gibbs cond of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Let $c\in \R$ and let ${\mathcal M}(c)  \subset\P(\TkaXinf)$ be the set of minimizers of the constrained optimization problem 
