 {R} (c) :=   \min_{\rho \in {\mathcal A} (c)} I^\k (\rho), 

   \end{align}
   where $I^\k$ is the large deviation rate function of $\{U_n\}$ from Theorem (\oldref{thm:ldp-Un}). 
Then for any open set ${\mathcal O} \subset\P(\TkaXinf)$ with ${\mathcal M} (c) \subset {\mathcal O}$, the conditional limits (equation eq:general cond limit of the paper)-(equation eq:general cond limit other way of the paper) hold. In other words, if $c > \sref$ (resp. $c < \sref$)  
then $\{U_n\}$ asymptotically lies in ${\mathcal M}(c)$ given $\{\mathbb{E}_{L_n}\sqpr{S_h}\geq c-\delta\}$ (resp. $\{\mathbb{E}_{L_n}\sqpr{S_h}\leq c-\delta\}$).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.879186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5416470f8f2ffbf7b3414439b837f771fa59e873811e1658c36d574b73ebf0a0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Abelian of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Let $G$ be a locally compact topological group with Haar measure $\mu$ that acts on $\mathcal{X}$. We then have
