{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.489355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_541a372a779979b76df4acf5fa13b71c9ae59c596ccc16ae4da7987be496e01f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 (The potential is proportional to $H$ in the Kähler case) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Suppose $\kappa_i \equiv 0$ for all $i$ (the Kähler condition \eqref{eq:kahler-condition}). If $( H, F_1, \dots, F_r, \varphi )$ solves the system of Proposition \ref{prop:soliton-ode}, then

	\[
	\varphi' \;=\; c\, H
	\]

	for a constant $c$; equivalently $\varphi(s) = c \int H\, ds + \text{const}$. Consequently the soliton system reduces to

	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{gathered}
			c\, H' \;-\; \frac{H''}{H} \;+\; \sum_{i=1}^r n_i \left( \frac{q_i^2 H^2}{2 F_i^4} \;-\; \frac{q_i H'}{F_i^2} \right) \;=\; \lambda \,, \\
			p_i \;-\; q_i H' \;-\; \frac{q_i H^2}{2} \sum_{j=1}^r \frac{n_j\, q_j}{F_j^2} \;+\; \frac{c\, q_i H^2}{2} \;=\; \lambda\, F_i^2 \quad ( i = 1, \dots, r ) \,,
		\end{gathered}
	\end{equation*}

	for the unknowns $( H, F_1, \dots, F_r )$ and constants $( c, \lambda )$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.464716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_541bad54ff2f764f0354d59b1f79448e203f5447284aa0b6c0b4e88d327e54e3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 44 (Identities for $\gtorus$-gradients) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The following identity holds for scalar functions $\phi$ and $\psi$: 
