{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.885087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5485ec4c6365f79e8a7ea54c4b3fae5b9e4e40425e961601125bbde1fd3ff96d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem cor:sources break detailed balance of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] Assume that $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ is a mass action chemical system with sources and sinks.  Let $\mathcal W_r $ be the set of the cycles associated with $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \emptyset ,  \mathcal K, \emptyset )$ and  $ \mathcal W$  the set of the cycles associated with $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$. 
  \begin {enumerate} 
 \item  Assume that
\begin{equation} 
\log \left( \frac{\alpha_k }{\beta_k }\right) =E(k), \quad \forall k \in \Omega_c^{\mathcal W} 
\end{equation}
where $E \in \mathbb R^M $ is the  solution to 
 \begin{equation} 
 S_\rho^T  E = \ln \left( \dfrac{ K_{ - \rho} }{ K_{  \rho } }  \right)  \ \forall \rho \in \{ 1, \dots, r \}
\end{equation} 
and where 
\begin{equation}
    \Omega_c^{\mathcal W }:= \{ k \in \Omega : \exists w \in \mathcal W  \quad (\mathbb S_r  \pi_R w ) ( k ) \neq 0   \}. 
\end{equation}
Then the chemical system  $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ satisfies the property of detailed balance. 
 \item    Assume that the chemical system $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ satisfies the detailed balance condition and 
 \begin{equation} 
 |\mathcal W| >  |\mathcal W_r |. 
 \end{equation}
Then either \begin{enumerate}
\item the chemical rates in the set $ \mathcal K_s =\{ \alpha_k , \beta_k \}_{ k \in  \Omega_c} $ satisfy (equation eq for the parameters of the paper)  
\item or the property of detailed balance is unstable, i.e. for every $\delta >0$ there exists a set $ \mathcal K^\delta =\{ K_\rho^\delta , K_{- \rho}^\delta \}_{\rho=1}^r $ such that 
\[ 
\max_{ k \in \Omega } \left( |K_\rho - K_\rho^\delta | +  | K_{-\rho} - K_{-\rho}^\delta | \right)  \leq \delta
\]
and such that the chemical system  $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K^\delta, \mathcal K_s )$ does not satisfy the detailed balance property. 
\end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

