{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.725265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54883aaf06b27b0a70e914def152cef53b14af6362c39d90e34ed5b03964d1fb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:pLaplace-pure-diffusion_PDE of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] Let $p>2$, $z\in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $a: \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathcal P_* \to \mathbb{R}$ and $\mathcal P_*$ be as in (equation eq:a_pure_Ito_diffu_pLaplace_nl of the paper) and (equation eq:P_star_pure_Ito_diffu_pLaplace of the paper), respectively. Then $u^z(t,\cdot) \in \mathcal P_*$ for every $t>0$, $a(x,u^z(t,\cdot)) \geq 0$ pointwise in $(t,x)$, and $u^z$ is a distributional solution to the pure-diffusion FPE 
