    The constant $C_{\rm diff} > 0$ depends on upper bounds for $\tau$, $|v_0 - v_\tau|$, $\|\lambda\|_{\rm path}$, $\|\mathcal B\|_{\rm path}$, and $\|\mathcal C_-\|_{\rm path}$ as well as lower bounds for $\tau$ and $r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54a32b105183bf34472693a8869f2cdb04d1126750dd6ffc7e0ee92f92a5d5db","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi construction of mu of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Suppose $t\in\mathbb{Z}$. Set $t':=t-\lfloor\frac{n\log n}{2}\rfloor$, and $\gamma_t:=\exp(-2t'/n)$, which is the same as in (defi: construction of nu of the paper). Let $\mu_n^t$ denote the measure on $\mathfrak{S}_n$ defined by the following sampling process: first, sample $M_t\in\{0,1,\ldots,n\}$ according to the distribution 
$$\mathbf{P}[M_t=k]=\begin{cases}\mathbf{P}(\Pois(\gamma_t)=k)/\mathbf{P}(\gamma_t-l^{1/3}\le\Pois(\gamma_t)\le \gamma_t+l^{1/3})&\gamma_t-l^{1/3}\le k\le \gamma_t+l^{1/3}\\
0 & \text{else}
\end{cases},$$ 
then sample a uniformly random subset $S_t$ of size $M_t$ in $[n]$. Finally, sample a uniformly random element of $\mathfrak{S}_{[n]\backslash S_t}$ and view it as an element of $\mathfrak{S}_n$ by fixing all of the elements in $S_t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.718281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54a36affb7c4340340ce3f4b20b5ff06dedd84d8908271c4f573247290dd656f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eX_definition of arXiv:2604.16206, 'Extrapolation of max--stable random fields with Fr\'echet marginals'] The \textit{max-stable predictor} of $X_{t_0}$ is given by
	 \begin{equation}\notag
		\hat{X}_{\hat{\mathbf{\lambda}}} = M(\hat{\mathbf{\lambda}},\mathbf{X}(\mathbb{T}_f)) = \max\limits_{j=1,\ldots,n} \{\hat{\lambda}_j X_{t_j}\},
 \end{equation}
	where the vector of optimal weights $\hat{\mathbf{\lambda}}=(\hat{\lambda}_1,\ldots, \hat{\lambda}_n)$ is a solution to minimization problem 
\begin{equation}\begin{split}
	\Psi(\lambda) := & 2\mathbb{E}\left(e^{-(X_{t_0} \vee \hat{X}_\lambda)^{-\alpha}}\right) - \mathbb{E}\left(e^{-\hat{X}_\lambda^{-\alpha}}\right) - 1/2 \\ + & \gamma\left(\frac{1}{3} - \mathbb{E}\left(e^{-\hat{X}_\lambda^{-\alpha}} \vee Y \right) + \mathbb{E}\left(e^{-2 \hat{X}_\lambda^{-\alpha}}\right)\right) \longrightarrow \min\limits_{\mathbf{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^n_+}, \end{split}
\end{equation}
	 $Y$ is an independent copy of $e^{-\hat{X}_\mathbf{\lambda}^{-\alpha}}$, and $\gamma>0$ is a penalty weight.  If it is not possible to generate $Y$, one can use an alternative form  of the 2-Wasserstein metric in (equation eq:2Wasserst of the paper) and write
	  \begin{equation}
	\begin{split}
		\hat{\mathbf{\lambda}} &= \argmin\limits_{\mathbf{\lambda}\in\mathbb{R}^n_+} \left\{2\mathbb{E}\left(e^{-(X_{t_0} \vee \hat{X}_\mathbf{\lambda})^{-\alpha}}\right) - \mathbb{E}\left(e^{-\hat{X}_\mathbf{\lambda}^{-\alpha}}\right) -1/2 \right. \\
        &+ \left. \gamma \left(\frac{1}{3}+ \int\limits_0^1 F(u) \left(F(u)- 2u\right) du \right) \right\}
	\end{split}  \end{equation}
	with $F$ being the distribution function of $e^{-\hat{X}_\mathbf{\lambda}^{-\alpha}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.299172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54a8642be8844cb120c01f54d8479c49bc3bc707fab35f5e940bcea1179fba3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:PCA:relative-entropy:step of arXiv:2605.16904, 'Positive-rate PCA and IPS with stationary Bernoulli measures are rapidly forgetful \footno'] Let $\Phi$ be a PCA with a strictly positive local transition rule $\varphi\colon\Sigma^N\times\Sigma\to(0,1)$, where $N\ni 0$.
	Suppose that $\Phi$ admits a stationary Bernoulli measure $\lambda=\lambda_q$.
	Then,
	\begin{equation}
		D_J(\mu\Phi\relto\lambda) \leq
			(1-\kappa)D_{N(J)}(\mu\relto\lambda)
	\end{equation}
	for every probability measure~$\mu$ and every finite set $J\subseteq\mathbb{Z}^d$, where
	$\kappa \coloneqq \min\big\{\varphi(a_N,b)/q(b): a_N\in\Sigma^N,b\in\Sigma\big\}$ and

	$q_\mathsf{min}\coloneqq\min\{q(a): a\in\Sigma\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.394094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54af74a47d56b584dcb65ede67cd0f6dfe094d38cf59f34e83abb048a1899023","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:h of arXiv:2607.22333, '\large \bf COLLISION AND NON-COLLISION FOR DIFFUSIONS ON CONFIGURATION SPACE'] There exists a family  of even functions $h_\varepsilon\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb{R})$, $0<\varepsilon<1/4$, such that
