{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.658550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54ec7e76ba53673ea722f7393c91d72f4c54aef3db0b7f0d3a21f2fd15564844","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Co ratio of arXiv:2604.07183, 'Stopping on the last success with unknown odds: asymptotic minimax optimality of the plug-'] Fix~$p_0\in(0,\frac12)$ and~$a\in(0,1)$. Then,
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}
\frac{\sup_{p\in[p_0,1)}\bigl(V_n(p)-W_n^{\pi_a}(p)\bigr)}
      {\sup_{p\in[p_0,1)}\bigl(V_n(p)-W_n(p)\bigr)}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt a}
\ >\ 1
.
\end{equation}
In particular, the worst-case deficit of every sample-splitting rule~$\pi_a$, $a\in(0,1)$, over~$[p_0,1)$ is asymptotically larger than that of the plug-in rule, by the factor~$1/\sqrt a$. Equivalently, in view of Theorem~(thm:minimax_sharp of the paper), no~$\pi_a$ with~$a<1$ is asymptotically minimax optimal, its asymptotic minimax deficiency being~$1/\sqrt a$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.051293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54efbb0ca4cc5902cd7b6712e2742f89c55a129a5db6c68ba68b1daf74248d25","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:HB-BAOAB of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Let $(X_k,V_k)_{k\ge0}$ be the BAOAB chain, with $\xi_k$ the Gaussian variable used in the $k$th step. Let $\xi_0\sim\mathcal N(0,\mathrm{Id}_d)$ be independent of $(\xi_k)_{k\ge1}$, or alternatively let $\xi_0$ be the zero vector, and define the auxiliary variable $X_{-1}$ by
\begin{equation}
 V_0=\frac{2\beta}{(1+\beta)h}(X_0-X_{-1})
 +\frac{\varsigma}{1+\beta}\,\xi_0-\frac h2\nabla U(X_0).
\end{equation}
Then, for $k\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 X_{k+1}=X_k+\beta(X_k-X_{k-1})-s\nabla U(X_k)+\widetilde\zeta_{k+1},
 \qquad
 s=\frac{h^2}{2}(1+\beta),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
 \widetilde\zeta_{k+1}=\frac h2\varsigma\,(\xi_k+\xi_{k+1}).
\end{equation}
If $\xi_0\sim\mathcal N(0,\mathrm{Id}_d)$, the sequence $(\widetilde\zeta_k)_{k\ge1}$ is a centered stationary $1$-dependent Gaussian sequence with
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E[\widetilde\zeta_k\widetilde\zeta_k^\top]=\frac{h^2}{2}(1-\beta^2)\mathrm{Id}_d,
 \qquad
 \mathbb E[\widetilde\zeta_k\widetilde\zeta_{k+1}^\top]=\frac{h^2}{4}(1-\beta^2)\mathrm{Id}_d.
\end{equation}
If (equation eq:vpair-baoab of the paper) is imposed with $\xi_0=0$, then $\widetilde\zeta_1=\frac h2\varsigma\,\xi_1$ has the smaller covariance $\frac{h^2}{4}(1-\beta^2)\mathrm{Id}_d$, while (equation eq:zetacov-baoab of the paper) holds from the second update onward.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.537109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54f2aa95b3fab22537f159e3a2bcc9f9c970ccf4eeafba23bad83c9c72f411ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:RGP-H7 of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The dressed observable satisfies the mixed diamond
