{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.769268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_551206935989cbd35bee4adc1bc8558fa11a38f7e8c3b4f609b15d23df640367","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the same notation as in Definition \ref{Def.AvoidingLawBer}. Fix $k \in \mathbb{N}$, $M \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \cup \infty$, $T_0, T_1 \in \mathbb{Z}$ with $T_0 < T_1$, and $\vec{x}\,^b, \vec{y}\,^b, \vec{x}\,^t, \vec{y}\,^t \in \mathfrak{W}_k$. We assume that 
