{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.422482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55162a84a78b2c0e6c29ff5a59b1d7bf8fb3c676d29b1fef0ac380a6bcf90b51","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition moment cumulant of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] In an operator-valued free probability space $(\mathcal{A},\mathcal{B},\Delta)$, we define the corresponding (operator-valued) free cumulants $(\kappa_{n}^{\mathcal{B}})_{n\in\mathbb{N}},\kappa_{n}^{\mathcal{B}}:\mathcal{A}^{n}\rightarrow\mathcal{B}$ by the moment cumulant formula :
        \begin{equation}
            \Delta(a_{1}\cdots a_{n})=\sum_{\pi\in NC(n)}\kappa_{\pi}^{\mathcal{B}}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{n}),
        \end{equation}
        where arguments of $\kappa_{\pi}^{\mathcal{B}}$ are distributed according to the blocks of $\pi$, but the cumulants are nested inside each other according to the nesting of the blocks of $\pi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.442714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5516b09f12d9caa3de4ddc0243f19fc97f0d302dfd128f59b8af83f53eaa061e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:cor-K-sum of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] For any given real numbers  $t_1,\dots,t_s>0$,    $\tau_1,\dots,\tau_q$ and  $a_{q+1}, \ldots,a_{r}\in (-a,a)$, suppose that 
\begin{equation}
    n_i\,N^{-1/3}\;\longrightarrow\;t_i, \quad i=1,\ldots,s,
\end{equation}
and  \begin{equation}
N^{1/3}(a_j-1)\;\longrightarrow\;\tau_j,
\quad j=1,\dots,q, \end{equation}
as \(N\to\infty\).   Then the  scaled cumulants 
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to\infty}
\frac{\kappa_{\widetilde X}(n_1,\ldots, n_s)}{(n_1+1) \cdots (n_s+1)}=\widetilde{\mathcal{K}}(t_1,\dots,t_s):
=\sum_{\Gamma\in\mathcal{T}_s}
\mathcal{F}_\Gamma(t_1,\dots,t_s).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.542902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_551707dce2f6ac8b1380dea3c5f1669ecaf4e65c41aa37f7dbd7e905e09ca69d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:matrix_local of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] For $(z_1,w_1)$ and $(z_2,w_2)$ in a neighbourhood of $q_{\infty}$, let
~$z_i=1+\frac{Z_i}{N^\frac{1}{2}}$,~$i=1,2$, and set
\begin{equation}
\tilde g(\ell x+i,2y+j)=\prod_{m=1}^i(1+\alpha_m^{-1}\beta_m)(1+\alpha_{m+1}\beta_m^{-1})\alpha_{i+1}^{-j},
\end{equation}
and let~$\nu$ be given in~(equation eq:period_function of the paper). Then, as~$N\to \infty$, 
\begin{multline} 
\boldsymbol{\mathcal{M}}_{i_1,j_1,i_2,j_2}\left(z_1,w_1;z_2,w_2\right)

= \nu(\ell-i_2,j_2)\frac{Z_1^{i_1}}{Z_2^{i_2}}\frac{\tilde g(\ell x_2+i_2,2y_2+j_2)}{\tilde g(\ell x_1+i_1,2y_1+j_1)}\frac{N^{\frac{i_2}{2}}}{N^{\frac{i_1}{2}}}\left(1+\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{|Z_1|+|Z_2|}{N^{\frac{1}{2}}}\right)\right),
\end{multline}
where, assuming $|Z_k|\leq N^{\frac{1}{2}}$, the implicit constant in the remainder term is independent of $Z_k, x_k, i_k, y_k, j_k$, $k=1,2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.830828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55188a5d2e906e25b86366be6c7b5f75e80b3b5992f80acacde78fb76ad6836a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:mmdc-homogeneous-stationary of arXiv:2606.24881, 'Queues with Correlated Service Times --- the $M/M_D/c$ Model'] For the homogeneous $M/M_D/c$ model under the stability condition
(equation eqn:stability of the paper), the stationary probability vector $\pi$ is given by
\begin{align}
\pi_k &= P_k(r)\pi_{c-1}, \qquad 0\le k\le c-2, \\
\pi_{c-1}
&=
\left(
\sum_{k=0}^{c-2}P_k(r)+\frac{1}{1-r}
\right)^{-1}, \\
\pi_n &= \pi_{c-1}r^{\,n-(c-1)}, \qquad n\ge c-1,
\end{align}
where $0<r<1$ is the unique solution of the characteristic equation
(equation eq:char-eq of the paper), and $P_k(r)$ is determined recursively by
(equation eq:Pseed of the paper) and (equation eq:Precursion of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.859853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5519337c5696b00b31d152feca9e79a354207680759be66f0ce32bfd8e9c18f5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem finite-persistence-claims of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Assume Assumption~(ass:gen-ass of the paper) is satisfied. Then, with regards to the process $(\mathscr{T}_{t})_{t \geq 0}$, we have the following claims:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  We have $\lim_{n \to \infty} \max_{u \in \mathscr{T}_{\tau_{n}}} \outdeg{u, \mathscr{T}_{\tau_{n}}} = \infty$ almost surely. 

    \item  If $\sum_{i=1}^{\infty} (X_{i} - X'_{i})$ converges almost surely, then for any $u, v \in \mathcal{U}$ we have 
    \begin{equation} 
    \Prob{\win(u,v) \cup \win(v,u)} = 1.
    \end{equation}
    \item  If $\sum_{i=1}^{\infty} (X_{i} - X'_{i})$ diverges almost surely, there exists an increasing function $\phi\colon \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that, for any $u \in \mathcal{U}$, $j \in \mathbb{N}$ we have 
    \begin{equation} 
    \Prob{\exists k \leq \phi(j)\colon \sum_{\ell = 1}^{k} X(uj\ell) < \sum_{\ell = j+1}^{k} X(u\ell)} \geq 1/2.
    \end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.793549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_551975477e90cd2867ebd8e17eef0a1cd9222b18b382db8733e112f3f6fd4cb7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 75 (BPHZ renormalisation) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] There exists a linear map $\cA$, acting on Feynman diagrams, such that 
