{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.581669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_551ee9daa0bcb79de89c882eaf6d183a30fd4adffc9d2184d3da5057fc9f3a14","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Polynomial Gaussian envelope) of arXiv:2609.01319, 'Matched Queries for Curvature and Density at Branching Junctions'] Fix a compact $\cQ\subset\R^D$. There are $c>0$ and constants $C_{m,\cQ}$ such that the following holds. Let $v\in\Sph^{D-1}$, $u\ge0$, and let $q_t=uv+t\xi$ for $0\le t\le1$, with $\norm{\xi}\le u/2$. For every fixed mixed-derivative order $m$ of $K_z(q)=e^{-\norm{z-q}^2/2}$ in $(z,q)$,
