			 for each $t \in [\mq^{-1} N^{1+10B\delta} \omega,N^{5}]$  and $ z \in \mathcal Y^-$ such that $ \mathtt{d}_z \in (L^{-2} \mathfrak{d}, L^2 \mathfrak{d})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.893444+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_552b6efd1a4f6d68a78bc0a0fe1be8da4df2fab521e74e1ddc5775a500d89d27","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] Assume that Assumption~\ref{ass:main} holds with \(b_0>\Xi(0)\) and \(K/\kappa\leq 2\). Then it holds that
