{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.653364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_552be87b0a267c525315fedbad713ce62a51709d0d55b417e294cf16e6e9998a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lm:Tube-Lemma of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] Fix an oriented rectangular loop $\ell$ with both dimensions at least $100$ strictly contained in the interior of the finite lattice $\Lambda_L$. Then for any plaquette count function $K: \mc{P}_{\Lambda_L}^+ \to \N$, we have
