{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.311793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_553157508d4c1c1f8a8d4da4f62e6646293a13342fba16f8935b330eb4c0b562","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:fixed f and stable laws of arXiv:2605.31356, 'P\'olya--Schur problems and free probability'] Let $f\in\mathcal{LP}_{M}$ for some $M\geq 0$. \begin{enumerate}
		\item If $\sigma^2>0$ and $f_n(z)=f(n^{-1/2}z)$, then \begin{equation}
