{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.496976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5532edd8281a645c0b9d862c1d9025a2cfac3a928ee719cd8b730c85e58a15b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma defect-inverse-sign of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $L:[0,1]\rightarrow \lbrack 0,1]$ be a
continuous strictly increasing map with inverse $T=L^{-1}$. Define the
symmetry defects 
\begin{equation}
D_{L}(x)=L(x)+L(1-x)-1,\qquad x\in \lbrack 0,1],  
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
D_{T}(u)=T(u)+T(1-u)-1,\qquad u\in \lbrack 0,1].  
\end{equation}
Then the following implications hold 
\begin{equation}
D_{L}(x)\leq 0\ \forall x\in \lbrack 0,1]\quad \Longrightarrow \quad
D_{T}(u)\geq 0\ \forall u\in \lbrack 0,1],  
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
D_{L}(x)\geq 0\ \forall x\in \lbrack 0,1]\quad \Longrightarrow \quad
D_{T}(u)\leq 0\ \forall u\in \lbrack 0,1].  
\end{equation}
In particular, whenever $D_{L}$ has a constant sign on $[0,1]$, $D_{T}$ has
the opposite constant sign on $[0,1]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.658673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55347aecc78e33b0cb1858fabf7f38963575c1f5f74c534e84c3f8c7335ba635","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] For $s\in\mathbb{R}$, the standard homogeneous Sobolev spaces $\dot{H}^{s}$ and inhomogeneous Sobolev spaces $H^{s}(\R^{d})$ are defined by
