{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.905238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_553487f42a05420d66e8931dd73ac5bd2c26ca7d87f31ec8af6b670c890ad174","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:entropy-production of arXiv:2607.19583, 'Density-Dependent McKean--Vlasov Diffusions: Subgaussian Occupancy Bounds and Polynomial P'] Let $\mathbb{Q}^N$ be the law of $N$ independent copies of the limit diffusion (equation eq:limit-sde of the paper), so that $Q_t^N = p_t^{\otimes N}$. Let $\mathbb{P}^N$ be the law of the interacting particle system (equation eq:particle-system of the paper) on the canonical path space $C([0,T]; (\mathbb R^d)^N)$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{i\le N} \mathbb E_{\mathbb{P}^N} \sup_{s\le T} |X_s^{i,N}|^2 < \infty,
\end{equation}
the particle system admits a unique weak solution, and the marginal relative entropy satisfies
