{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.936365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5540632631ff1145617fcd69614a177083daae63926233d2234506c373a97201","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Definition-Proposition of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Let $A$ be defined as follows by duality.
    \[\forall\,  \alpha \in  \Omega^1(D,\mathfrak{g}),  \langle A, \alpha \rangle \coloneq \left \langle \xi_\sigma  , (r,\theta) \mapsto -\int_{r \xrightarrow{\theta} 1} \alpha \right \rangle.\]
The well-defined random de Rham current $A$ is called the axial-gauge Yang--Mills distributional $1-$form. 

