{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.620912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5568f2b8346f0504d2f8013a67520d98f7844b1f7700b71de7ef0b3938a054a7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma SL_facts of arXiv:2601.04997, 'Fluctuations of the Boundary-Driven Symmetric Zero-Range Process from the NESS'] For each $j=0, 1, 2$, the system $\textsc{SL}_j(A)$ satisfies the following:
