{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.811999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_556f8fac4c8ac403bf4fac0e0d6dc446c7901f2b5403a8c2c634e2942d4abc31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:landscape-symmetries of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] {dov}, [dv2]}]
    The directed landscape $\mathcal{L}$ satisfies the following properties.
    \begin{enumerate}[label={\rm(\roman*)}]
        \item\textup{(Independent increments).}
        For any finite collection of pairwise disjoint time intervals $(s_1,t_1),\dots,(s_k,t_k)$, the random functions
        \[
            \mathcal{L}(s_1,{\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}; t_1, {\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}), \dots, \mathcal{L}(s_k,{\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}; t_k, {\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}})
        \]
        are independent.
        \item\textup{(Metric composition).}
        Almost surely, for any $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}$ and any $r\in (s,t)$, we have
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}(s,x;t,y) = \sup_{z\in \mathbb{R}}\left(\mathcal{L}(s,x;r,z) + \mathcal{L}(r,z;t,y)\right).
        \end{align*}
        In particular, we have the \emph{reverse triangle inequality} $\mathcal{L}(s,x;t,y) \geqslant \mathcal{L}(s,x;r,z)+\mathcal{L}(r,z;t,y)$ for all $r\in (s,t)$ and all $z\in\mathbb{R}$.
        \item\textup{(Translation invariance).}
        For all $(r,w)\in\mathbb{R}^2$, we have the following equality in distribution of $C(\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow})$-valued random variables:
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}(s,x;t,y) \overset{d}{=} \mathcal{L}(s+r, x+w; t+r, y+w).
        \end{align*}

        \item\textup{(Scaling invariance).}
        For all $\lambda>0$, we have the
        following equality in distribution of $C(\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow})$-valued random variables:
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}(s,x;t,y) \overset{d}{=} \lambda^{-1/3}\mathcal{L}(\lambda s, \lambda^{2/3}x; \lambda t, \lambda^{2/3}y).
        \end{align*}

        \item\textup{(Shear invariance).}        
        For all $\nu \in \mathbb{R}$, we have the following equality in distribution of $C(\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow})$-valued random variables:
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}(s,x;t,y)
            \overset{d}{=} \mathcal{L}(s, x+\nu s; t, y+\nu t)
            + \frac{(x-y-\nu(t-s))^2 - (x-y)^2}{t-s}.
        \end{align*}
        As a special case, for all fixed $s<t$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}$, we have the following equalities in distribution of $C(\mathbb{R})$-valued random variables:
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}(s,{\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}};t,x)
            \overset{d}{=} 
            \mathcal{L}(s,x;t,{\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}) 
            \overset{d}{=} \mathcal{L}(s, 0; t, {\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}})
            + \frac{2x}{t-s}{\raisebox{1.1pt}{\hspace{0.6pt}\scaleobj{0.55}{\bullet}\hspace{0.75pt}}}
            \;
            - \frac{x^2}{t-s}.
        \end{align*}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.526377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55709e0b559323c972e2f39d0c58811ae139a482b53eeee8c6801116df207e0c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:finite_energy_flow}
