{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.330200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55892c7ec842e37075e13b359ee9f8da9e52552c38e587745a6d52e9a5bba22e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2506.22020, 'Norm-dependent Lamperti-type MAP representations of stable processes and Brownian motions '] Let $(\xi,\Theta)=(\xi_t,\Theta_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a $\mathbb{R}\times E$-valued MAP. By a {\it L\'evy system} for $(\xi,\Theta)$ we mean a couple $(H, L)$, where $H$ is an additive functional $t\mapsto H_t$, and  $L$ is a kernel from $(E,\mathcal{E})$ to $(E\times\mathbb{R},\mathcal{E}\bigotimes\mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R})),$ such that for every bounded measurable function $f:\mathbb{R}^{2}\times E^{2}\to[0,\infty)$, $\boldsymbol{\theta}\in E$ and $t\geq0$,
