{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.447729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5589dff22e8e70924338e39fd74b6bb5aa66252d8cbef026ac280ee68bd89e8a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 (Kakutani-Fan-Glicksberg) of arXiv:2606.15843, 'Long-time behaviour of DLRA for SDEs'] \cite[Theorem 1]{fan1952fixed}
    Let $\scr P_2$ be a locally convex 
    Hausdorff topological vector space, and let $\al K_M^\kappa\subset \scr P_2$  be a  nonempty, compact and convex set. Suppose $f:\al K_M^\kappa\to 2^{\al K_M^\kappa}$  be a set-valued function on $\al K_M^\kappa$ (where $2^{\al K_M^\kappa}$ is the set of subsets of $\al K_M^\kappa$) satisfying the following conditions:
    \begin{itemize}
