{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.793838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55959ed622c287cfcae034d4078c35de542b854dee3465e4b138dc9ee127cbd3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:minimizer of arXiv:2605.31054, 'On the empirical spectral distribution of matrix perpetuities'] Let $a\geq1$ and $b>1$ and assume that $(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_N)$ has density given by (equation eq:LambdaDens of the paper). Then, the (random) probability measure 
