{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.286619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5597299f4da86f79787a96a269955ac6e37cf9b2d5a5ee22c07e042e1febaaa0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $\left(\mathcal{X},\rho\right)$ be a separable metric space and $p\geq 1$. Given two probability measures $\mu,\nu\in\mathcal{P}^p(\mathcal{X})$, $\mathcal{W}^p(\mu,\nu)$ defined as
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathcal{W}^p(\mu,\nu) := \inf_{\pi\in\Pi(\mu,\nu)} \left[\int_{\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{X}}\rho(x,y)^p\pi(dx,dy)\right]^{1/p}
    \end{equation*}
    is called the $p$-Wasserstein metric.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.762179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_559747dde1babf2266abb30bdf7f233f5fd2d556e633dbdbeb69b8ad9e97590a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:int_0^t e^(delta/epsilon)|A^(1/2)u|ds of arXiv:2411.02459, 'Existence and higher regularity of statistically steady states for the stochastic Coleman-'] Under the same hypothesis of (thm:well-posed of the paper), let $U(t)=(u(t),\eta(t))$ denote the solution of (equation eqn:react-diff:mu of the paper) corresponding to initial condition $U_0\in\mathcal{H}^0_\mu$. Then for all $0<q\le\delta$, where $\delta$ is the constant from (equation ineq:<T.eta,eta> of the paper), there exists a positive constant $c=c(U_0,q)$ independent of $t$ and $\mu\in\mathcal{M}_\delta$ such that 
