admits $\nu=\mathcal{S}_{\boxplus}^{*}[\mu]$ as a solution.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.961625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55ad3caf25907ed5bdd44127dcd0699142c177ea24717b4fb6bf9da9b6919a6f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] Under Assumption \ref{asmp:state_dynamics}, there exists a jointly measurable version of $(t,x,\omega)\mapsto X^x_t(\omega)$ such that on compacts of $\mathcal{S}$,
