\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.598713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55b888e58601eb51379a19fcff4969ea9b8721290b3d73f4d6bfa8f7ebb34db7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp proposition1 of arXiv:2411.15724, 'Wasserstein Convergence Rates for Empirical Measures of Random Subsequence of $\{nα\}$'] Let $X_1,X_2,\ldots$ be integer-valued i.i.d. random variables with characteristic function $\varphi$, and let $S_j = \sum_{i = 1}^{j} X_i$. Let $\alpha$ be an irrational number such that
\begin{align} 
\| q \alpha \| \geq C q^{-\gamma}
\end{align}
holds for any $q \in \mathbb N$ with some constants $\gamma \geq 1$ and $C > 0$.
Suppose that there exist real numbers $0 < \beta \le 2$, $c > 0$ and an integer $D > 0$ such that for any $x \in \mathbb R$,
\begin{equation} 
1 - |\varphi(2\pi x)| \ge c \| D x \|^{\beta}.
\end{equation}
Set $\mu_n = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{j = 1}^{n} \delta_{\{ S_j \alpha \}}$, $n \geq 1$. If $\beta \gamma = 2$, then for any $p \in \mathbb Z^+$ and
$\kappa n^{- \frac12} \leq \varepsilon < 1/2$, where $\kappa > 0$, there exists $C' > 0$ such that for any $n \geq 2p$,
\begin{align*}
\mathbb E \left[ \int_{\mathbb{T}} |\nabla (-\Delta)^{-1} (f_{n, \varepsilon} - 1)|^{2p} \, \text{\rm{d}} \mu   \right] \leq \frac{C' (\log n)^p}{n^p}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.236495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55b8a7b4f16bb55bb4dc127c08db0d7454ad82d519540333091185f66a34d3d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor_inj_norm of arXiv:2507.06522, 'Balanced multi-species spin glasses'] Assume $p\geqslant3$ and the entries of $T = (T_{i_1,\dots,i_p})_{1\leqslant i_1,\dots,i_p\leqslant d}$ are independent standard normal random variables.
