{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.054737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_55d91a6b569e38a4429a7eba8bd3b4bf7a063cb44d35c0c41a289131facbdf3e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:C1_positive of arXiv:2607.13302, 'Extending an Order-Statistic Characterization of the Exponential Distribution'] Assume that $j,k,n,r$ are integers, $1\le j<k$, $n-k>k-j$, and $r\ge 0$. Let
\[
