{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:49.557906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5608d07304c1ee660005e5f3d4a8e8fdb87811720ea5b3e4956f33097106d7d2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defs 16 ({\cite[Dfn.~4.2,  Thm.~4.5) of arXiv:2509.06869, 'Infinite Interacting Brownian Motions and EVI Gradient Flows'] {AmbGigSav14}}] 
The {\it Cheeger energy}~$\Ch^{\mssd, \nu}: L^2(\nu) \to \R_+ \cup\{+\infty\}$

 is defined as 
