{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.874524+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56165b397fd063d4df4956ef11c52188d148052a85b4b879d8b942ecae21e5d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $\mathcal{E}, \mathcal{E}'$ be Gaussian exponential sum and let $\mathcal{E}\odot\mathcal{E}'$ be their Aronszajn multiplication. For any tuple of independent Gaussian exponential sum $\mathcal{E}_1,\ldots,\mathcal{E}_{m-1}$, write $\mathrm{E}:=(\mathcal{E}_1,\ldots,\mathcal{E}_{m-1}):\mathbb{R}^m\to\mathbb{R}^{m-1}$. Then, for every open set $U\subset \mathbb{R}^m$, we have:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}\#\mathcal{S}\left\{\mathcal{E},\mathrm{E};U\right\}+\mathbb{E}\#\mathcal{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}',\mathrm{E};U\right\}\right) \leq \mathbb{E}\#\mathcal{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}\odot\mathcal{E}',\mathrm{E};U\right\} \leq \mathbb{E}\#\mathcal{S}\left\{\mathcal{E},\mathrm{E};U\right\}+\mathbb{E}\#\mathcal{S}\left\{\mathcal{E}',\mathrm{E};U\right\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.702935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_561988b92dddc1d3bcddb379e9266b3483a6946e359dc1b9b968029d1a044907","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Main a priori estimate) of arXiv:2608.29726, '\LARGE A Priori Estimates for Singular Fractional Stochastic Burgers Equations'] Let \((\alpha,\gamma)\) satisfy
