{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.964802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_563ecc6f5a08f23976fd43fdf8619fc9846f6b48dd94b88c7d537f7d5207a6e5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2607.28614, 'Tampered Memory Elephant Random Walk on one-dimensional integer lattice'] Let $S_n$ be a TMERW. 
Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a collection of sets that are not necessarily nested, such that $\frac{\mid D_n \mid }{n} \rightarrow 0, \text{a.s.}$, as $n \to \infty$. Then, we have the following phase transitions into diffusive, critical, and superdiffusive regimes given by 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item If $ p < 3/4$ and $\frac{|D_n|}{\sqrt{n}}\stackrel{L^2}{\longrightarrow} 0 $, then 
\begin{equation*}

\frac{S_n}{\sqrt{n}} \stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N \left(0, \frac{1}{3-4p}\right).
\end{equation*}
\item If $p =\frac{3}{4}$, and $|D_n| = \mathcal{O}(n^{\gamma}), \text{ a.s.}$ for $0 \le \gamma < 1/2$, 
\begin{equation*}
\frac{S_n}{\sqrt{n \log n }}\stackrel{d}{\longrightarrow} N (0,1).
\end{equation*}
\item For $\frac{3}{4}<p<1$, and $|D_n| = \mathcal{O }(n^{\gamma}), \text{ a.s.}$ for $0 \le \gamma < 2p-1$, then there exists a random variable $L$ such that
\begin{equation}

\frac{S_n}{n^{2p-1}}\rightarrow L, \text{ a.s.}
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.905883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5641cd5e1a635d90095604872b0e6323d04d40df8b728a22da9ecd369024ecab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Restatement 17 (Restatement of Theorem~\ref{thm:introduction-higher-codimension}) of arXiv:2609.00922, 'The Morse Index, Nullity and Jacobi Fields of Constant-Curvature 2-Spheres in Complex Proj'] Let $N\ge n\ge1$, let $k\in\{0,\ldots,n\}$, and put $\lambda=n-2k$.  Then
