{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.362574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56470da0b276944393855348ef93e30de6fa881613e3e3cb788ff227ca4561d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.21669, 'Discontinuous transition in 2D Potts:\\ II. order-order interface convergence'] There exist constants~\(C,c>0\) such that, for any~\(n,m,k\geq 1\),
