{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.679716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_564812516dde03a44013781a3d15a982fc9b4d3e58b12c989da6928ebfac2dfb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem FMEthm of arXiv:2605.28430, 'Limit theory for Lipschitz-localized statistics in random geometric models'] Let $\tilde{\mathcal{P}}$ be a simple, marked point process on $\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{K}$ and let $\psi : \mathcal{N}_{\mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{K}} \to \mathbb{R}$ be $\prec$-continuous at $\infty$.  Assume that for all $l \in \mathbb{N}$
\begin{equation} 
\int_{(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{K})^l}\mathbb{E} ^!_{\bk {\tilde{y}}1l}[| D^{l}_{\bk {\tilde{y}}1l}\psi(\tilde{\mathcal{P}})|]\;\tilde{\alpha}^{(l)}(\mathrm{d} \bk {\tilde{y}}1l) < \infty
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation} 
		\frac{1}{l!}\int_{(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{K})^l}\mathbb{E} ^!_{\bk {\tilde{y}}1l}[ D^{l}_{\bk {\tilde{y}}1l}\psi(\tilde{\mathcal{P}})]\;\tilde{\alpha}^{(l)}(\mathrm{d} \bk {\tilde{y}}1l) \to 0 \ {\rm{as}} \ l \to \infty.
\end{equation}
Then $\mathbb{E} [\psi(\mathcal{P})]$ has the following {\em factorial moment expansion} (FME)
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E} [\psi(\tilde{\mathcal{P}})] = \psi(o) +
\sum_{l=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{l!}\int_{
(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{K})^l }D^{l}_{\bk {\tilde{y}}1l}\psi(o)\;\tilde{\alpha}^{(l)}(\mathrm{d} \bk {\tilde{y}}1l).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

