{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.267987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5648b1120a95e08e062dc1d515d2bf2115ccbfae256c3e19a744e5a7eae398ea","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mydef defin of arXiv:2411.08430, 'The Restricted Isometry Property of Block Diagonal Matrices Generated by $\varphi$-Sub-Gau'] For an Orlicz $N$-function $\varphi$ satisfying $Q$-condition, a zero-mean random variable $\xi$ obeys $\varphi$-sub-Gaussian distribution, if there exists a constant $a\geq 0$ such that the inequality 
