{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.506558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5658bb90414712e513c02d6e50e81d41f00551e649eb580c82b496968b0dad37","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:ConfInvariance of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] Let $q \geq 1$, $\nu$ be a doubling measure on $X$ and assume that $\Psi(x,r) = \mu(B(x,r))$ for all $x \in X$ and $r > 0$.
