 \qquad b_n=\frac12\log\frac{n+1}{n},
\end{equation}
where the error is uniform over the torsion-free ambient group and the
finitely supported law of $X_1$. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.424745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5677ed5301a604ac139259dd767ba6225c0361b7deb50715197595d222ad991e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:subexp-counter-strict of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:subexp-counterexample}
Fix \(p\ge3\) and \(\alpha\in(0,2)\).  There exists a symmetric probability law \(\mu=\mu_{p,\alpha}\) with a strictly positive \(C^\infty\) density such that:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=2em]
\item \(\mu\) has Weibull tails of index \(\alpha\) and all moments finite; when \(\alpha\ge1\), it is subexponential in the sense of (def:subexp of the paper);
\item \(\mu\) matches the standard Gaussian moments through order \(2p\);
\item for some compact interval \(B\subset(0,\infty)\),
\begin{equation}
 \liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log\mathbb E_\mu\operatorname{Crt}_N^J(B)
 \ge0>
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log\mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_N^G(B).
\end{equation}
The same strict inequalities hold for local maxima, with the Gaussian
term interpreted via a \(\limsup\); after replacing \(B\) with \(-B\),
they also hold for local minima.
\end{enumerate}
Thus \(2p\)-moment matching does not imply universality of these unregularized
energy-window counts for any subquadratic Weibull tail.  In particular,
the failure occurs within the subexponential class for every
\(\alpha\in[1,2)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.834105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_567936122e757e7f61cae1d3a14e53a9f5a05a95d4cf12c4db2529ebb7622f6d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Total-progeny Radon--Nikodym derivative) of arXiv:2607.16833, 'Dynamical Equations for Poisson Galton--Watson Trees and Component Densities of Sparse Inh'] For every $u,v>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\dd P_{\alpha,u}^{\Lambda}}
      {\dd P_{\alpha,v}^{\Lambda}}(\mu)
 =\left(\frac uv\right)^{T(\mu)-1}
   e^{-(u-v)A(\mu)},
 \qquad P_{\alpha,v}^{\Lambda}\text{-a.e. }\mu.
\end{equation}
In particular, all finite-total-progeny laws with positive parameters are
mutually absolutely continuous.","status":"unverified"}

