{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.357049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56805c011cc97754f6d75735f5c11e9ef5dc920e7648a05a0016959fa4b2eaae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that Assumptions {\rm\ref{A1}} and {\rm\ref{A2}} hold. For any $p\ge 4$ and  $T>0$, there exists a constant $C_{p,T}>0$ such that for any $\varepsilon>0$, $x\in\RR^{n}$ and $ y\in \RR^{m}$,
