{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:45.011330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_568fff44300f8d95f68775b7d782c25b09b2ec08ecd566803d0f337c4a748f25","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Random time distortion) of arXiv:2605.11877, 'Fluctuation analysis for a randomly perturbed dynamical system with state-dependent impuls'] For $\eps \in (0,1)$, let $G_\sfN^\eps \in \filt$ be an event satisfying, among perhaps other assumptions, the requirement that for all $\omega \in G_\sfN^\eps$, we have $|\tau^\eps_n(\omega)-t_n| < \alpha/4$ for all $0 \le n \le \sfN$
. Define now the random time distortion $\lambda^\eps$ by
\begin{equation}
