{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.644877+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56b3d3ab36c90b8c266ca9009c05d8fb97f516f18c4d45b7341fca7b7194494e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cont-XOR of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D\subset\mathbb C$ be a bounded, simply connected domain. Let $\tau$ be the continuum XOR-Ising model with free/free boundary conditions in $D$. Then, there exists a collection $(\mu_k)_{k=1}^\infty$  of measures supported on $(C_k)_{k=1}^\infty$ such that 
    \begin{align*}
        \tau = \lim_{N\to \infty}\ \sum_{k=1}^{N} \xi_{k} \mu_{k},
    \end{align*}
    where $(\xi_k)_{k=1}^\infty$ are i.i.d. symmetric signs. The sum converges almost surely in the Sobolev space $H^{s}(\mathbb C)$ for $s<-1$, under \emph{any ordering} that is independent of the collection of signs. Moreover, 
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item The excursions $C_k$ are connected and pairwise disjoint almost surely.
        \item Each measure $\mu_k$ is a deterministic function of the respective excursion $C_k$.
        \item The set of excursions $(C_k)_{k=1}^\infty$ is locally finite. That is, almost surely for any $\rho>0$ there are  finitely many $C_k$ with diameter greater than $\rho$. 
        \item For any continuous, bounded function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$, 
        \begin{align}
        \mathbb E\left[\sum_{k=1}^\infty(\mu_k,f)^2\right ]<\infty,
        \end{align} 
        and thus 
        \begin{equation}
           (\tau,f) = \lim_{N\to\infty} \sum_{k=1}^N \xi_k(\mu_k,f) \quad\text{in}\quad L^2(\mathbb P).
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}
    The same statement holds for\footnote{In this case, one needs to be careful to work in a domain $D$ whose boundary has small enough dimension (or, instead, restrict to the local Sobolev space $H^s_{loc}(D)$).} the XOR-Ising model with $+/+$ boundary conditions in $D$ by adding a symmetry-breaking (positive) measure $\mu_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.793575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56b4d7aa47b42a280b639a96b1b65349b5566fa07c41e08b1e12bc2064ea60fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:11.1 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that for all $p_1\leq q_1, p_2\leq q_2$, and all $z\in \mathbb{Z}^2$ satisfying $p_1,p_2\leq z\leq  q_1,q_2$, and all $r\in (0,1)$, we have
