{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.669452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56bec59e431179282a441a483456342a7b65bfbfad3a700ce0b1bafd4c40f696","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Sharpness of the cubic order) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] Fix \(0<a<b<\infty\) and \(R_0\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}\), and put
\(K_0=[a,b]\times\{0,\ldots,R_0\}\).  There are positive constants
\(A_-,A_+,B_-,B_+\), depending on \(K_0\) and \(\lambda\), such that
\begin{equation}
