{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.559514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56c66649c409acdd0b23cf535414c914448d26896a8cd93bc4738e9bd3d0695c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-properties-of-a_k of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Functions $a_k$ defined in (equation eqn-a_n of the paper) satisfy
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] 
$a_k \searrow \1_A \mbox{  as } k \to \infty$.
\item[(ii)] The support of $a_k$ is contained in $S_{\frac{\alpha}{2}}$.
\item[(iii)] For future reference we also show  that
\begin{equation}
a_k(u) \leq \left(\frac{2}{\alpha} \@ifstar{\oldabs}{\oldabs*}{u}_{U^\prime}\right)^{\ell} \qquad \mbox{  for all } u \inU^\prime, k \geq 2, \ell\ge 1.
\end{equation}
\item[(iv)] For $u_1,u_2 \in U^\prime$
\begin{equation}
\vert a_k(u_2)-a_k(u_1) \vert
\leq  \frac{k^2}{a^2}\@ifstar{\oldnorm}{\oldnorm*}{f}_{\mathrm{Lip}} \@ifstar{\oldabs}{\oldabs*}{u_1-u_2}_{U^\prime} \bigl( \rho(u_1,A)+ \rho(u_2,A)\bigr),
\end{equation}
where  $\@ifstar{\oldnorm}{\oldnorm*}{f}_{\mathrm{Lip}}$ is the Lipschitz constant of the function $f$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56c6866993a36d681af7a6fb6bf6292cad08c9b84c4594392a5fda0f92e53e29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma Ratio 1 of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $K>0$ and $E_t=E_t^1 \text{ or } E_t^2$. Then, there exists some $u \ge 0$ \textcolor{black}{(depending on $t$)} such that
