{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.750200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56dc213e1b964d2ab61cf4cda21e19693a12086aaa7bb8c7b7e672f8501b397a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.02725, 'Mixing of general biased adjacent transposition chains'] For every $\ep>0$ and any fixed $\delta>0$, there exists $C(\ep)$ such that for any $(p_{i,j})_{1\le i< j\le n}$ which satisfies $\ep$-positive bias, the adjacent transposition Markov chain $\Mnn$ has mixing time\footnote{Here we are using $\widetilde O$ to mean up to polylogarithmic factors in $n$; the implicit constant here may, and in fact does, depend on $\eps$. However, the constant in the $\widetilde O$ is independent of $\delta$.} 
    \[ n^2(1-o(1)) \le \Tmix (\delta) \le C(\eps) n^2 + \widetilde O(n \log (1/\delta)).
    \] 
    In particular, the family has \emph{pre-cutoff} (see~\cite[Chapter 18]{LP}): there exists $C(\eps)$ such that for any sequence of $\Mnn^{(n)}$ with $\eps$-positively biased $\vec{p}\,^{(n)}$, for any fixed $\delta \in (0,\frac{1}{2})$, 
    \begin{align*}
         \limsup_{n\to\infty}  \frac{\Tmix(\delta)}{\Tmix(1-\delta) } \le C(\eps) <\infty \,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.345967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56dcdb0f3acf24e26a8a1b8ddb433408cf82dcbae11521832f46baa23808a219","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 42 of arXiv:2506.15044, '2506.15044'] \normalfont
We say that $H$ is $\mathbb{B}$-integrable w.r.t. $X$ in the domain of $\mathbb{B}$-inner semimartingales (or simply, $H$ is $(X,\mathbb{B})$-integrable), if there exists an inner decomposition $X=M+A$ ($M\in (\mathcal{M}_{\mathrm{loc}})^{i,\mathbb{B}}$ and $A\in (\mathcal{V}_0)^\mathbb{B}$) such that $H\in \mathcal{L}_m^{\mathbb{B}}(M)\cap\mathcal{L}_s^{\mathbb{B}}(A)$.
In this case, the $\mathbb{B}$-process defined by
\begin{equation}
H_{\bullet}X=H_{\bullet}M+H_{\bullet}A
\end{equation}
is called the stochastic integral of $H$ w.r.t. $X$, and $X=M+A$ is an $(H,\mathbb{B})$-decomposition of $X$. The collection of all $\mathbb{B}$-predictable processes which are $(X,\mathbb{B})$-integrable is denoted by $\mathcal{L}^{\mathbb{B}}(X)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.802040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56e29e2198b18b794ffd1ba03a72156e829c4f3577a98ea286e1ead31c9a061d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Sobolev estimates) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Let $s\ge 0$, and $\psi_0\in H_t^{\frac{s+1}{3}}(\mathbb{R})$, $\psi_1\in H_t^{\frac{s}{3}}(\mathbb{R})$ satisfy \eqref{supp-cond}.  Then, the solution of \eqref{HNLSreduced} represented by the formula \eqref{sol_for_reduced} satisfies 
\begin{equation}
    \|v(\cdot,t)\|_{H^s_x(\mathbb{R}_+)}\lesssim (1+e^{cT'}\sqrt{T'})\sum_{b=0}^1\|\psi_b\|_{H_t^{\frac{s+1-b}{3}}},\quad t\in [0,T'],
\end{equation} where $c$ and the constant of the inequality may depend only on the fixed parameters such as $s,\alpha,\beta$, and $\delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.915862+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56e3f336607c016376d35323fa66a3ed739dd45e8f780e86cf9844223a24ee35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.01419, 'A model of opinion dynamics evolving via a preferential attachment mechanism involving mul'] Consider the model described in \S\ref{subsec:model_growing_sample_size}, and assume that the limit $\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}(n+1)^{-1}k_{n}^{-1}s_{n+1}$ exists and equals $\eta$ for some $\eta\in(0,1)$. Assume that the first two criteria of \eqref{k_{n}_sequence_conditions} are satisfied, and that 
