{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.733888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56e4db766dd8b15a3e012ccf4b0ded95b7c8f1dc97d90fda404fa3f084a2af2f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:ghf_tightness_hoelder_approx of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $\mathcal {K}_{\alpha,C;r}$ be given as above. Let $(\mathbf{P}_n)$ be a sequence of probability measures on the space of non-empty compact metric spaces equipped with bounded functions, equipped with the GHf topology. Fix $\alpha > 0$. Suppose that for every $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $C>0$ such that for any $r > 0$ there is $N \in \mathbf{N}$ such that
