{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.934676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56f0fdb6f21a468e35731ee9faa92735df93087ee7633c81b07252c2abfd32ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:duality of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Assume that $(X_t)_{t \geq 0}$ is a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $X_0 \sim\eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}_{tem}^+)$, $p \geq 2$ and such that (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper) holds. Let $Y_0 = \mu $ for $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F^+$. Then, there exists $T_0>0$ such that there exist processes $(J_t)_{t\geq0}$ and $(Y_t)_{t\geq0}$, taking values in $\mathbb{N}\cup \{ 0\}$ and $\mathcal{M}_{reg}^+$, respectively, that are independent of $X$ and such that
