{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.590694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56fa7cea27957297bd9f11977db3170dd1822a6bb07a991311ec7700eda57064","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_singlerec of arXiv:2411.09976, 'Occupation times on the legs of a diffusion spider'] For $n \geq1$, 
\begin{align} 

\nonumber
\mathcal{L}_t\Bigg\{ \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left((A_t^{(i)})^{n}\right) \Bigg\}(\lambda) = \sum_{k=1}^{n}& \frac{n! D_k^{(i)}(\lambda)}{(n-k)! \lambda^k} \mathcal{L}_t\Bigg\{ \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left( (A_t^{(i)})^{n-k} \right) \Bigg\}(\lambda)\\ 
&+ \frac{n!}{\lambda^{n-1}} \mathcal{L}_t\Bigg\{ \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}(A_t^{(i)}) \Bigg\}(\lambda)
- \frac{n!}{\lambda^{n+1}} \sum_{k=1}^{n} D_k^{(j)}(\lambda),
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{L}_t$ denotes the Laplace transform with respect to $t$ of the function in curly brackets, $\lambda$ is the Laplace parameter, and  
\begin{equation}
D_k^{(i)}(\lambda) := \frac{\lambda^k}{(k-1)!} \int_0^\infty \mathbf{g}_\lambda(\mathbf{0},(y,i)) \mathbf{E}_{(y,i)}(H_\mathbf{0}^{k-1} \mathrm{e}^{-\lambda H_\mathbf{0}}) \beta_i\,m(\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} y). 
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $X$ is self-similar, then  for any $\lambda>0$, 
\begin{equation} 
\mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left((A_1^{(i)})^{n}\right) = \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left(A_1^{(i)}\right) - \sum_{k=1}^{n} D_k^{(i)}(\lambda) \left( 1 - \mathbf{E}_\mathbf{0}\left( (A_1^{(i)})^{n-k} \right) \right), 
\end{equation}
and, in particular, $D_k^{(i)}(\lambda)$ does not depend on $\lambda$ for any $i=1,\dotsc,R$ and $k=1,2,\dotsc$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.743275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56fb14f2ba2604ff13c0b28dd7fc375adf3909e5274a8db7be1df75b0ece65d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 45 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] We fix $\alpha \ino (1, 2]$. Let $\mu$ satisfy (\ref{hypostaintro}). Let $\tau_\infty$ be a GW($\mu$)-forest  (Definition \ref{GWfordef} $(\textbf{b})$). Let $\nu$ be a supercritical offspring distribution whose mean is denoted by $\ttm_\nu$. We assume that there is  $\ttb\ino ( \frac{2\alpha}{\alpha-1}, \infty)$ such that $\sum_{k\in \bbN} k^{1+2\ttb} \nu(k)\leko \infty$. Let $(\bT, \boo)$ be an invariant GW($\nu$)-tree (Definition \ref{definvRW}) that is independent from $\tau_\infty$. 
We recall the definition of $\mathscr Q_n $ from the convergence (\ref{remindcv}). We recall 
from (\ref{vutchi}) the definition of $\sigma_\nu$. Otherwise, we keep the previous notation. 
Then, conditionally given $(\bT, \boo)$, the following joint convergence 
\begin{eqnarray}

\Big(\mathscr Q_n ,  \tfrac{1}{ \sigma_\nu \! \sqrt{a_n}} \widehat{\cW}_{2n\cdot }(\tau_\infty),  \tfrac{1}{ \sigma_\nu \! \sqrt{a_n}}\widehat{\cW}^*_{n\cdot }(\tau_\infty)    \!\! \!\! \!\! \!\! \!\! \!\!  \!\!     &, &\!\! \!\! \!\! \!\! \!\! \!\!  \!\!    \tfrac{\sigma_\nu}{ \sqrt{a_n}} \widehat{W}_{2n\cdot }(\tau_\infty),\!  \tfrac{\sigma_\nu}{ \sqrt{a_n}} \widehat{W}^*_{n\cdot }(\tau_\infty)\Big) \nonumber  \\
&\underset{n\to \infty}{-\!\!\!-\!\!\!-\!\!\!\longrightarrow}& \big(  \mathbf g_1, \mathbf d_1, X, H, H, \widehat{W},  \widehat{W} , \widehat{W},  \widehat{W} \big)
