{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.712939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_572cd3f6ce0f0e7f61da8143067136f531cd55a253263cc9e3f286794171908d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma quantitative CLT of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] For each exponent ${\delta> 0}$, there exist finite positive constants $C,s$ depending only on the parameters $d,\mathfrak{p}$ and $\delta$, such that for every $y\in\mathbb{Z}^d$, there exists a nonnegative random time $\mathcal{T}_{par,\delta}(y)$ satisfying
		\begin{equation}
			\forall T\geqslant 0,\qquad \mathbb{P}_\mathfrak{p}\left(\mathcal{T}_{par,\delta}(y)\geqslant T\right)\leqslant C\exp\left(-\frac{T^s}{C}\right). 
		\end{equation}
		On the event $\{y\in\mathscr{C}_\infty\}$, for every $x\in \mathscr{C} _\infty$ and every $t\geqslant \max\{\mathcal{T}_{par,\delta}(y),\vert x-y\vert\}$, we have
		\begin{align*}
			\vert p^\omega(t,x,y)-\theta(\mathfrak{p})^{-1}\bar{p}(t,x-y)\vert \leqslant C t^{-\frac{d}{2}-(\frac{1}{2}-\delta)} \exp\left(-\frac{\vert x-y\vert^2}{Ct}\right).
		\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.670972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_572df849f641557be4ff6cab179636849c23c63ddc95d275bcbbee9baf24395d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] For $ m \in \mathbb{N}$, an element $x \in \{ 0,1\}^{G}$ is called an $ \mathbf{m}$-\textbf{net} (with respect to distance $d$ on $G$) if the set $ \{ g \in G: x_g =1\}$ is a maximal $m$-separated set. In other words, it is
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $m$-covering i.e. for every $ g \in G$ there exists $h\in G$ such that $ d(g,h) \leq m$ and $x_h= 1$, and
    \item $ m$-separated i.e. for every $ g $ with $x_g = 1 $ and $ h $ such that $ d(g, h) \leq m$ we have $ x_{h}=0$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.731221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_572e2d96288a536d04f63555cafb6bbd5468204327f32380cf682b848ecbdff3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lA1Delta of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] Let $r\in[2,\infty)$. Then, for any $\gamma\in [0,1]$
