{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.008110+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57544da4e0e294c2ee19b9007dd7c864fcd31ab9afb7dd7f3e2ff7257c71bc09","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 (\cite{BGP}; see also \cite{AKP}) of arXiv:2609.02808, 'Minimizers of Laplace eigenvalues under a lower curvature bound'] A geodesic metric space $(X,d)$ has \emph{curvature $\ge1$ in the sense of Alexandrov}
if every point has a neighborhood $U$ such that, for every geodesic triangle
