{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.520262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57783301a23645aac67004083ba98113b960a7c6171a159305816d38bc79c89c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Exact variational formula) of arXiv:2609.02595, 'Minimal Radial Sub-Gamma Envelopes for Infinitely Divisible Random Vectors'] For \(V_X(t)>0\), extend \(M_t(s)\) by infinity whenever \(K_X(st)=\infty\), and use \(1/\infty=0\). Then
\begin{equation}
 C_X(t)=\max\left\{0,\sup_{s>0}
 \frac{1-M_t(s)^{-1}}{s}\right\}.
\end{equation}
Moreover:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(C_X(t)<\infty\) if and only if \(K_X(st)<\infty\) for some \(s>0\);
\item \(C_X(t)=0\) if and only if
\begin{equation}
 \nu\{x:\ip{t}{x}>0\}=0;
\end{equation}
\item if \(C_X(t)<\infty\) and
\(\int|\ip{t}{x}|^3\,\nu(dx)<\infty\), then
\begin{equation}
 C_X(t)\geq \max\left\{0,\frac{\kappa_3(t)}{3V_X(t)}\right\},
 \qquad \kappa_3(t):=\int\ip{t}{x}^3\,\nu(dx).
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:09.016830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5778476dabfcc4182395f6b00608ee6f55c430695ba578f0d4b257055ad77afa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:psa_algebra of arXiv:2609.01697, 'Unique ergodicity of projective cocycles over the 2D stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] In the case of PSA the generators are band-limited Fourier multipliers,
  \begin{equation}
    H^k = e_k\, g_k(D) ,
    \qquad
    g_k(l) = \frac{\langle l^\perp, k\rangle}{|k|^2} ,
    \qquad
    |g_k(l)| \leqslant \frac{|l|}{|k|} ,
  \end{equation}
  so that $g_k \in S^1$. Moreover
  \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
      [\Delta, H^k] & = e_k\, q_k(D) ,
      \quad &q_k(l) && = P_k(l)\, g_k(l) , \\
      \bigl[[\Delta, H^k], H^{-k}\bigr] & = d_k(D) ,
      \quad &d_k(l) && = -\frac{2\langle l^\perp, k\rangle^2}{|k|^2} ,
    \end{aligned}
  \end{equation}
  with $P_k$ as in~(equation eq:DeltaL_bracket of the paper), and $q_k, d_k \in S^2$. More generally every $A \in \mathfrak{g}_{\mathrm{PSA}}$ is a finite sum $A = \sum_{m \in F_A} e_m\, p_{A,m}(D)$ with $p_{A,m} \in S^2$. Any such $A$ belongs to $\mathrm{Op}^{\beta_\star}$ and is bracket-regular in the sense of Definition~(def:bracket_regular of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.161487+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5778e0f494a68a1a8daa54779fb99e842ae842a9637474177031ac8f1e576adb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem_1JetExtensionMap of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let $d,k \in {\mathbf{N}}_0$.
  There is a \defined{$1$--jet extension map}
  \begin{equation*}
    \ext^{(1)} \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace \mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R}^d) \oplus \mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R}^d)^k \to \mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R}^d \oplus \mathbb{R}^k)
  \end{equation*}
  such that
  for every $(f,g_1,\ldots,g_k) \in \mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R}^d)^{k+1}$ its extension $F \coloneq  \ext^{(1)}(f,g_1,\ldots,g_k) \in \mathscr{S}(\mathbb{R}^d\oplus\mathbb{R}^k)$ satisfies
  \begin{equation}

