  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.327607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5779f8629d37bf6b59a7423bd6088aa4d316897ba933570c6740092e8b745762","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop gl-spectra-compact-generators of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The $\infty$-category ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-gl}$ is stable and compactly generated by the objects $\Sigma^\bullet_+\big(\textbf{\textup{L}}(V_H,-)\times_\varphi G\big)$ where $\varphi$ runs through homomorphisms $\varphi\colon H\to G$ of compact Lie groups (up to isomorphism), and $V_H$ is a fixed faithful $H$-representation. In particular, ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-gl}$ is presentable.
    \begin{proof}
        As in the equivariant case (Proposition~(prop:equiv-sp-compact-gen of the paper)), stability follows from the previous proposition, and it will suffice to show that the homotopy category is compactly generated in the triangulated sense by the given objects. This is in turn the content of [schwede-stiefel]*{Corollary A.19}.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

