{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.445520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_577e9ca4413a3c72c10efe2de2a3b0f34fb4f940890af92c481d0dd3ee9eb583","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:delocXY/IVGFFheight of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] There exist an inverse temperature $\beta_{\mathrm{Deloc}} \in (0 , \infty)$ and a constant $c_0 > 0$ such that 
