{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.238579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_579c10b9c1972c680ff9b78771c36d0ccefafb632e35304b91579675228a3e66","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.14427, 'A criterion for proving entropy chaos on path space'] Consider a sequence of diffusion laws $\PP_N$, $N\in\NN$, on the same filtered space $(\Omega,\mathcal F_{[0,T]})$, where each $\PP_N$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the Wiener measure $\WW$ on $\Omega$,
  weakly converging to a probability measure $\tilde \PP$ with $\sup_{N\in\NN}\KL(\PP_N|\mathbb W)<+\infty$.
  Then, for any bounded continuous function $K:[0,T]\times\RR^{}\rightarrow\RR^{d} $ we have
  \begin{align*}
  \lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}   \EE_{\PP_N}\left[ \int_0^T  K(X(t),t) \cdot \dd X(t) \right]
  =
    \EE_{\tilde \PP}\left[ \int_0^T K( X(t),t)\cdot \dd X(t) \right]
    ,
  \end{align*}
  where $X(t), t\in [0,T]$ denotes the canonical process on $\Omega.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.761784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57a2ac1487bc357418401d1160f13bd720bbc497953e3df7687de27e763cee6a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma bound on alpha norm difference kernel ito mbm of arXiv:2604.27682, 'Multifractional Stable Motion with Random Hurst Exponent'] Fix $\alpha \in (0, 2)$, $0 < \underline{H} < \overline{H} < 1$ and a modulus of continuity $w : \mathbb{R}_{\geq0} \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$. There exists a constant $C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H})$ such that for all $\epsilon \in (0, 1)$, all functions $H:\mathbb{R} \to [\underline{H}, \overline{H}]$ admitting $w$ as a modulus of continuity and all $h \in (0, \frac12$),
\begin{align}
\int_{-\infty}^{t-\epsilon} \left|(t+h-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha} - (t-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha}\right|^\alpha \, dx &\leq C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H}) \, \epsilon^{\alpha(\underline{H}-1)} h^\alpha,  \\
\int_{t-\epsilon}^t \left|(t+h-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha} - (t-x)^{H(x)-\frac1\alpha}\right|^\alpha \, dx &\leq C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H}) \, h^{\alpha(H(t)-w(\epsilon))},  \\
\int_t^{t+h} (t+h-x)^{\alpha H(x) - 1} \, dx &\leq C(\alpha, \underline{H}, \overline{H}) \, h^{\alpha(H(t)-w(h))} .
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.727182+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57a2f83c541bfdc7e349a976a8a7b64e222129d972735fdb60f38f54053abf7e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2511.14379, 'Stability of storage processes with general release rates'] In addition to $\textbf{(C1)-(C2)}$, assume that $\bar\upnu(0)=\infty$ and the following conditions hold:
