{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.891726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57a8e947c9fa09154b076f93b60a3f97f09bb6a83d71bcefe7c2e57aa432a92b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:pythKL of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Assume that $\pi,G,P,M,\mathcal{X}$ satisfy the assumptions as stated in Theorem (thm:bisection of the paper), and $M \in \mathcal{D}(G,\nu)$. Assume that $P_{da}(G,\nu) \in \mathcal{D}(G,\nu)$. We have
