     |t-s|\bigg)
        \end{align*}
        In particular, if the sequence of initial data $\mathfrak H^N(0,\bullet)$ is a good sequence in the sense of Definition \ref{goodseq}, then we have that the above quantity is bounded above by $C  \|\phi\|_{C^{p+2}}^2 |t-s|^{\e},$ with $\e$ as in Theorem \ref{goodseq}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:15:16.648266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57c8faa210460500ed3421c881b95f56b5ea93cc2cef0763edd7be2c876c8d2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.30736, 'Stability results for distribution-dependent stochastic Volterra equations'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{theorem:approximation_weak} for all compact $K \subset \bR^d$ there is an $C > 0$ such that
