{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.076423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57ce9fe24b7b3fefd9b086db71680308f5bb37489a30a7f345cb8c564f5ac46d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 5 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{P}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and $F_{\mu}^{-1}$ be its representative in $\mathcal{U}^2(\mathbb{S})$ as defined in \eqref{inverse}. Then, the following holds for    any fixed {$h\in T/{\mathbb N}^*$}:
