{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.406323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57de2783c02b5988b23cd0a14177cad2539b2427b00188ee75985c490f7925e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2. thm: convergence in Mdis of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Let $\nu, \nu_{1}, \nu_{2}, \ldots$ be elements of $\mathcal{M}^{\mathrm{dis}}(S)$.
