{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.306740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57f397d284da8ec77d6b3219b043a75cdefff267eb442cc803ce11441c9bfd8a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.03755, 'The Scramble Number of Outerplanar Graphs'] A \emph{bramble} $\mathcal{B} = \{B_1, \ldots, B_m\}$ is a collection of connected subgraphs of $G$ that all pairwise ``touch". We say two subgraphs $B_i$ and $B_j$ ``touch" if either:
    \begin{enumerate}
