{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.457467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58076ac719d1bdf1b74879cd7fe9e1de9a0a90c355f23b451d0dbc6b09654b4c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:2G of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Fix small constants $\epsilon,\tau>0$. Then, for any deterministic matrices $\|A_i\| \lesssim 1$ and vectors $\|{\bm x}\|, \|{\bm y}\| \lesssim 1$, the following isotropic local law: 
	\begin{equation}
		\Big| \big\langle {\bm x}, \big(G^{z_1}(\mathrm{i} \eta_1)A_1G^{z_2}(\mathrm{i} \eta_2)-M_{12}^{A_1} \big) {\bm y} \big \rangle\Big| \prec 
		\frac{1}{\sqrt{n \gamma}\eta_*},
	\end{equation}
 and the averaged local law: 
	\begin{equation}
	\Big|\big\langle \big(G^{z_1}(\mathrm{i} \eta_1) A_1 G^{z_2}(\mathrm{i} \eta_2)-M_{12}^{A_1}\big)A_2 \big\rangle\Big|\prec
	\frac{1}{\sqrt{n\ell}\gamma }\wedge \frac{1}{n \eta_*^2},
\end{equation}
hold uniformly for any $ |z_i|\leq 1+\tau$ and $\ell \geq n^{-1+\epsilon}$ with $\eta_*:=\min_{i=1,2}|\eta_i|$, $\ell:=\min_{i=1,2}\rho_i|\eta_i|$, and the deterministic matrix $M^{A}_{12}=M^A_{12}(\mathrm{i}\eta_1,z_1,\mathrm{i} \eta_2,z_2)$ is defined in ((eq:defM12 of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.794481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_580852daa0f3a7f4f5c4426f23f2a5fcfe52087ef5a0435f80271b2c4a725508","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:converge2general of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $\pi$ be the discrete uniform distribution, $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $Q \in \mathcal{Q}$ be a permutation matrix. Let $\Pi$ be the matrix where each row equals to $\pi$. We have
	\begin{align*}
		D^{\pi}_{KL}(\overline{P}(Q) \| \Pi) &\leq  D^{\pi}_{KL}(P  \| \overline{P}(Q) ) +  D^{\pi}_{KL}(\overline{P}(Q) \| \Pi) = D^{\pi}_{KL}(P \| \Pi),
	\end{align*}
	and the equality holds if and only if $\overline{P}(Q) = P$. 

	Similarly, if $P$ is further assumed to be $\pi$-reversible, then
	\begin{align*}
		c_{KL}(\overline{P}(Q)) &\leq c_{KL}(P).
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.745513+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_580c10ce2c263b576fd196f296b435a2f2fa3850561bab9342e0ef92b008172e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-vector-exact-fourier-dimension of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume that the dyadic vector-weight law is energy-admissible. Let \(\mu\) be the limiting dyadic vector-weight cascade measure on \([0,1]\), and set \(M=\mu([0,1])\). Then, almost surely on \(\{M>0\}\),
\begin{equation}
\dim_{\mathrm F}(\mu)=\dim_{\mathrm E}(\mu)=\dim_2(\mu)=D_E(X).
\end{equation}
In particular, if \(D_E(X)>0\), then for every \(0<\sigma<D_E(X)\)
there is a finite random constant \(C_\sigma\) such that
\begin{equation}
\lvert\widehat{\mu}(\xi)\rvert
\le
C_\sigma \lvert\xi\rvert^{-\sigma/2}
\end{equation}
for all sufficiently large 
\(\lvert\xi\rvert\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.821795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_580e6f403d03fae09d3d709c9dad79194eb2b79a0769cf9c387b57894c36dcec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:crossing_bound of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] There exist constants $C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:displacement of the paper)}}(\Gamma_+, d), c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:displacement of the paper)}}(\Gamma_+, d) > 0$ such that, if $Y \sim \poisson(\Gamma_+ T)$ is independent of the random walk $S$ on $\mathbb{Z}^d$,
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}\Big( \max_{0 \le k \le Y} \|S_k\| \ge s \Big)
    \le C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:displacement of the paper)}} e^{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:displacement of the paper)}} \, s \log(1+s/T)},
    \qquad T \ge 1.
  \end{equation}
  In particular, there exists constants $C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:crossing of the paper)}}(\Gamma_+, d), c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:crossing of the paper)}}(\Gamma_+, d) > 0$ such that
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}_\rho \Bigg(
      \begin{array}{c}
        \text{some particle starting at a site $x \in \mathbb{Z}^d$}\\
        \text{with $\norm{x}_{\infty} \ge s$ reaches $0$ by time $T$}
    \end{array} \Bigg)
    \le C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:crossing of the paper)}} \rho T^{d/2} e^{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:crossing of the paper)}} s\log(1 + s/T)},
  \end{equation}
  for any $T \geq 1$ and $s \ge 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.866064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_580e8c47aadd675d38f75ed873bfcb4b96c1f738f548c2af0beaaaf5dc721c11","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 of arXiv:2512.00213, 'On strong sharp phase transition in the random connection model'] Let $h\colon \BX\to\N$ be a measurable bounded function and $t\ge 0$. 
