{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.369499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58100ffbd2758e4db39c751a485f8905dbcb95275a70107c04a877a12cdd2b0c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 42 of arXiv:2512.07202, 'Hitting Probabilities for Hypoelliptic Differential Equations Driven by Fractional Brownia'] Let \( (u_t)_{0 \leqslant t \leqslant T} \) be a continuous stochastic process satisfying assumption $\mathbf{(A3)}$. Fix \( \beta > 0 \), \( 0 < a < b \leqslant T \) and \( M > 0 \). Then the following statements hold true.
