{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.736847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_581646594013b7f5ac21ee02ffce2b3a71f73b27a16e02d614f83e876827a48e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn eq:slope_ineq1 of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] We define a partial relation $\prec$ on (finite) fine slopes generated by the following inequalities:
    \begin{equation}
        s^\heartsuit \prec t^\diamondsuit
    \end{equation}
    whenever $s < t$ and $\heartsuit, \diamondsuit \in \{\natural, \flat, \sharp, \dagger\}$, and
    \begin{equation}
        s^\flat \prec s^\dagger \prec s^\sharp, \qquad \text{and} \qquad s^\dagger \prec s^\dagger.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.669357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58187cabbd95b428261beb034f6cbce84f900e2bbf6a0623a0ca90f69f0275aa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] A \textbf{perversity} 
   	$\bar{p}: \mathbb{Z}_{ \geq 2} \longrightarrow \mathbb{Z}$ is a function such that $\overline{p}(2)=0$ and
   	$\overline{p}(k+1)- \overline{p}(k) \in \{1,0\}$. The \textbf{complementary perversity} $\bar{q}$ of $\bar{p}$ 
   	is the one with $\overline{p}(k)+\overline{q}(k)=k-2$. Furthermore, the lower middle perversity is defined by $\bar{m}(k)=[\frac{k-2}{2}]$. Its complementary perversity is called the upper middle perversity and is defined by $\bar{n}(k)=[\frac{k-1}{2}]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.366355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_581a0f0b7e2decc963e258d7c637edaf9f092664c9eca0ebb4be6ccda4a4dabc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2606.02786, 'Non-local SDEs, critical drifts and local blow-ups'] Let the interaction kernel $K:\mathbb R^d \rightarrow \mathbb R^d$ be Borel measurable.
The following are true:

\begin{enumerate}

\item[{\rm (\textit{i})}] {\rm (Finite particle system)} Assume additionally that $K$ is weakly form-bounded with respect to the fractional Laplacian on $\mathbb R^d$, i.e. $|K| \in L^1_{\loc}(\mathbb R^d)$ and
$$
\||K|^{\frac{1}{2}}(\lambda+(-\Delta)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}})^{-\frac{1}{2}\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}}\|_{L^2(\mathbb R^d) \rightarrow L^2(\mathbb R^d)} \leq \sqrt{\delta}
$$
for some $\lambda>0$. For instance, $K$ satisfies the elliptic Morrey class condition $$|K|^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}} \in M_{1+\epsilon}$$
with sufficiently small elliptic Morrey  norm (see \eqref{morrey_e}). Then there exists a constant $C_{d,N,\alpha}$ such that if $\delta<C_{d,N,\alpha}$, then there exist (unique, see below) probability measures $\{\mathbb P_{x}\}_{x \in \mathbb R^{dN}}$ on the canonical space of c\`{a}dl\`{a}g paths $\mathbf{D}=\mathbf{D}_{[0,\infty[}$ that deliver a weak solution to the particle system
\begin{equation}

X_t^i=x^i-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1, j \neq i}^N \int_0^t K(X_s^i-X_s^j)ds+Z_t^i,
\end{equation}
where $Z_t^i$ are independent $\alpha$-stable processes, and determine a strongly continuous Feller semigroup via
$$
e^{-t\Lambda}f(x):=\mathbb E_{\mathbb P_x} f(X_t^1,\dots,X_t^N), \quad f \in C_\infty(\mathbb R^{dN}),
$$
where $\Lambda$ is an appropriate operator realization of $\sum_{i=1}^N (-\Delta)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}}_{x^i}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N \sum_{j=1, j \neq i}^N K(x^i-x^j) \cdot \nabla_{x^i}$ on $C_\infty$.

\smallskip

\item[{\rm (\textit{ii})}] {\rm (A priori Sobolev regularity for McKean-Vlasov equation)} Assume that $K$ satisfies the elliptic Morrey class condition $$|K|^{\frac{1}{\alpha-1}} \in M_{1+\epsilon}$$
with sufficiently small Morrey norm. Then, whenever $1<p<\frac{d+1}{d}$, for every $x \in \mathbb R^d$, the solution to the Cauchy problem for the McKean-Vlasov equation
\begin{align*}
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\lambda w +\partial_t w +(-\Delta)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}} w - {\rm div\,}\big((K \star w)w\big)=0, \\
w|_{t=0}=\delta_x,
\end{array}
\right.
\end{align*}
satisfies $w \in \mathbb{W}_\alpha^{\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}\frac{2}{p},p} \cap L^\infty(\mathbb R_+,L^1(\mathbb R^d))$ and
\begin{align}

&(\lambda+\partial_t +(- \Delta)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}})^{\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}\frac{1}{p}} w\notag\\
&\quad = (\lambda+\partial_t +(- \Delta)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}})^{-1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}\frac{1}{p}}\delta_{t=0}\delta_x - \nabla (\lambda+\partial_t +(- \Delta)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}})^{-1+\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}\frac{1}{p}}[(K \star w)w].
\end{align}
 Here we assume additionally that $K$ is smooth to ensure the existence and uniqueness of $w$, but the Sobolev norm $\|w\|_{\mathbb{W}_\alpha^{\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}\frac{2}{p},p} }$ is independent of the smoothness of $K$.
 \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.897504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_581a6d274676f0b1b7dcee79c2a24959da1d5c362f7404acb66ad4c23c5f6822","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop I<=00003D-Phi of arXiv:2603.27144, 'On the critical fugacity of the hard-core model on regular bipartite graphs'] There exist $C,c>0$ such that the following
holds. Let $G$ be a finite $\delta$-regular bipartite graph, satisfying
the local expansion property with parameters \emph{$C_{\mathrm{LE}},M_{\mathrm{LE}}$}.
Let $\boldsymbol{\sigma}$ be sampled from \emph{any measure} on $\Omega_{\mathrm{hc}}^{G}$.
Let $\lambda>0$. Then
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{|V|}I(\boldsymbol{\sigma})-\frac{1}{2}\tilde{\lambda}\le-\frac{1}{4}\tilde{\lambda}\mathbb{E}\boldsymbol{\Phi}+\frac{CC_{\mathrm{LE}}}{\delta}\left(\mathbb{E}\boldsymbol{\Phi}\log\frac{e}{\mathbb{E}\boldsymbol{\Phi}}+\frac{1}{M_{\mathrm{LE}}}\right).
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
I(\boldsymbol{\sigma})-\tilde{\lambda}\frac{|V|}{2}\le-c\tilde{\lambda}|V|\mathbb{E}\boldsymbol{\Phi}
\end{equation}
 whenever 
\begin{equation}
\tilde{\lambda}>\frac{9CC_{\mathrm{LE}}}{\delta}\max\left\{ \log\frac{e}{\mathbb{E}\boldsymbol{\Phi}},\frac{1}{M_{\mathrm{LE}}\mathbb{E}\boldsymbol{\Phi}}\right\} .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.057291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_581ce6ef9c1ad90b4e5289cddfc870dcafa89d4175523d10e2065f2eefbdbc74","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tail_prob of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $\{X_t, \ t\in T\}$ be the homogeneous Rademacher chaos of order $j$. Then for any $u > 0$,
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb P\left(|X_t| \geq ue\|X_t\|_2\right) \leq e^{-u^{2/j}}\,.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.499334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_581d27dbe29c0570910a07564bd2e71af9b79e8f0a96e3f994c08c5d68891460","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2608.28528, 'Strong solutions of SDEs with critical discontinuities in diffusion coefficients'] A Borel measurable vector field $b  :\mathbb R^{1+d} \rightarrow \mathbb R^d$ with $|b| \in L^2_{\loc}(\mathbb R^{1+d})$ is said to be form-bounded  if 
there exist constant $\delta>0$ such that the following quadratic form inequality holds for a.e.\,$t \in \mathbb R$:
\begin{align}

\|b(t,\cdot)\varphi\|_2^2   \leq \delta \|\nabla \varphi\|_2^2 + g_\delta(t)\|\varphi\|_2^2 \qquad \forall\,\varphi \in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R^d)
\end{align}
for some function $g_\delta \in L_{\loc}^1(\mathbb R)$. 

This is written as $b\in \mathbf{F}_{\delta,g}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.346079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_582120b12d7b6ad509891faf4ec98730f7280ca4c66f80c70e2e364a1ddc6e45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Quantitative homogenization) of arXiv:2604.21143, 'Quantitative homogenization for the critical long-range random conductance model'] Under Assumption~\textup{(U)}, let $\sigma \in (0,1)$, let $\mu \ge 0$, let $U \subset \Rd$ be a bounded domain with $C^{2,\sigma}$ boundary, and let $f \in C^{0,\sigma}(\bar U)$.
		For $\eps \in (0,1)$, let $u^\eps_\mu \colon \eps\Zd \to \R$ and $\bar u_\mu \in H^1_0(U)$ be the solutions of
		\begin{equation}

			\left\{
			\begin{aligned}
				\mu u^\eps_\mu - \mathcal{L}^\eps u^\eps_\mu &= f && \text{in } U \cap \eps\Zd\,, \\
				u^\eps_\mu &= 0 && \text{on } \eps\Zd \setminus U\,,
			\end{aligned}
			\right.
			\qquad \text{and} \qquad
			\left\{
			\begin{aligned}
				\mu \bar u_\mu - \frac{\E[\a(0,e_1)]}{2d} \Delta \bar u_\mu &= f && \text{in } U\,, \\
				\bar u_\mu &= 0 && \text{on } \partial U\,.
			\end{aligned}
			\right.
		\end{equation}
		Then there exist constants $C < \infty$, $c > 0$ depending only on $\mu$, $d$, $\lambda$, $\sigma$, $U$, and $\|f\|_{C^{0,\sigma}}$, and a random variable $\mathcal{X}$ satisfying
		\begin{equation}

			\P\bigl[\mathcal{X} > s\bigr] \le C e^{-c s}
			\qquad \text{for every } s \ge 1\,,
		\end{equation}
		such that for every $\eps \in (0,1)$ with $\left| \ln\eps \right| \ge \mathcal{X}$,
		\begin{equation}

			\left\| u^\eps_\mu - \bar u_\mu \right\|_{L^2(U \cap \eps\Zd)} \le \frac{C}{\sqrt{\left| \ln\eps \right|}}\,.
		\end{equation}
		Here $\|g\|_{L^2(U \cap \eps\Zd)}^2 \coloneqq \eps^d \sum_{x \in U \cap \eps\Zd} g(x)^2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.484187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5822231641b9c14f99a4c9501ef372629f8ea2f382c2d1246e444cd45d92f6a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 52 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $\eta>0$, $k\geq 0$, $j\geq 1$, $l\geq 0$, with $j+2l\leq 2k+1$, and $b\geq v\vee(2\lambda)$.
Then,
\begin{multline*}
\E\Big[\big\Vert
\ell_{0,b}^{2k+1-j-2l}V_{A_{0,b}}^{l}
\,:\Phi_{D\setminus A_{0,b}}^{j} :
\ind_{\{z\in A_{0,b}\text{~or~}\ell_{0,b}(z)=b\}}
\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}
\Big]
\leq
\\
C_{j,l}(1\vee\diam(D)^{j/4})
b^{4k+2-2j - 4l}
\\
