where $C_{j,l}>0$ is a constant depending only on $j$ and $l$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.994065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5824ac4bf7de6b63e4ae0db53db4521731292116d6388cb9b121ca2e04ba2a1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm g=1_general of arXiv:2608.25362, 'Fluctuations of the free energy of the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model with ferromagnetic i'] Let $\beta<1$ and $\gamma_N = 1 + \theta N^{-1/2}$ for some $\theta\in\mathds{R}$. Then
    \begin{align*}
        N F_N^{(J)}(\beta,\gamma_N)&- N\ln2 - \frac{N-1}{4}\beta^2 - \frac14\ln N \\
        &\overset{d}{\longrightarrow}
        \zeta_1 + \ln \int_{\mathds{R}} \exp\Big( \Big(\zeta_2 + \frac{\theta}{2}\Big)y^2 - \Big(\frac1{12} + \frac{v_2^2}{2}\Big)y^4 \Big)\,\frac{dy}{\sqrt{2\pi}},
    \end{align*}
    where
    \begin{align*}
        v_1 = \Big( -\frac12\ln(1-\beta^2) - \frac{\beta^2}{2} - \frac{\beta^4}{4} \Big)^{1/2},
        \qquad
        v_2 = \Big( \frac{\beta^2}{2(1-\beta^2)} \Big)^{1/2},
    \end{align*}
    and $\zeta_1 \sim \mathcal{N}\big( -\frac{\beta^4}{24}\,\E J^4 - \frac{v_1^2}{2},\; \frac{\beta^4}{8}(\E J^4 - 1) + v_1^2 \big)$ and $\zeta_2 \sim \mathcal{N}(0, v_2^2)$ are independent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.309009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5824fce58bd8961ea39dd2d605d3e0e829fc2bdf3dc9f28d2c870e115e5b748c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2606.24485, 'On the convex hull of a planar Brownian bridge with a random Gaussian endpoint'] Let $0<\sigma\le 1$, and let $\Phi$ denote the standard normal distribution function. Then for every $m\ge 0$,
	\begin{equation}
		\P(M_\sigma\le m)
		=
		\Phi \ob{\frac m\sigma}
		-
		e^{-2(1-\sigma^2)m^2}
		\Phi \ob{\frac{(1-2\sigma^2)m}\sigma}.
	\end{equation}
	For $\sigma=0$,
	\begin{equation}
		\P(M_0\le m)=1-e^{-2m^2},\qquad m\ge 0.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.489459+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_582fb99932d1c4fd2c093f205f001e1cebc8db39182847106f6da8e0efb6df52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 (The heat equation for $f_i^2$ in the Kähler case) of arXiv:2609.03332, 'Singularity Models of Finite-Time K\"ahler-Ricci Flows'] Suppose $\kappa_i \equiv 0$ for all $i$, and let $g(t)$ be a Ricci flow preserving the ansatz with fixed coordinate $u$. 
	Then each squared warping function evolves by the {linear heat equation with constant forcing}
	\begin{equation}
		\partial_t \big( f_i^2 \big) \;=\; \Delta f_i^2 \;-\; 2 p_i \,, \qquad i = 1, \dots, r \,.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.141291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58320815a7862bb14873d187947209a2846a3dc84a79cc1ded2dbce4f3acb8f4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition semigroup-representation of arXiv:2609.00425, 'Individual and Uniform Eventual Positivity of Self-Adjoint Semigroups'] The operator $A$ generates a self-adjoint $C_0$-semigroup $(\mathrm{e}^{tA})_{t \geq 0}$ on $\ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$. Moreover, one has
    \begin{align*}
        \mathrm{e}^{tA} = \mathrm{e}^{tA_0} + \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} h_n(t)\,q_n\otimes q_n,
    \end{align*}
    where $h_n(t) \coloneqq \mathrm{e}^{-(n-\delta_n)t}-\mathrm{e}^{-nt}$ for all $t\geq0$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.981432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5832eb4b1f5ab6189d96bf2fde215bf32bf6c72612051caf32bc062c4bf82dca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:subsupadd of arXiv:2608.19050, 'Online Permutation Embedding: \\ Optimal Stopping and Scaling Laws'] The constants $c_\mathrm{typ}$, $c_+$, and $c_-$ exist. Moreover, they admit the following estimates: for every $k \ge 1$, 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item 
        \begin{equation}\label{eq:betagamma}
        \Big(\frac{2}{(k+1)(k+2)}\sum_{j=1}^k \sqrt{\beta_j^-}\Big)^2 \leq \Big(\frac{2}{(k+1)(k+2)}\sum_{j=1}^k \sqrt{\beta_j^\mathrm{typ}}\Big)^2 \leq c_{\mathrm{typ}} \leq \frac{\beta_k^{\mathrm{typ}}}{k^2} \leq \frac{\gamma_k}{k^2}.
        \end{equation}
        \item 
        \begin{equation}
             \frac{\beta_k^+}{(k+1)^2} \le c_+ \le \frac{\beta_k^+}{k^2}\,.
        \end{equation}

        \item 
        \begin{equation}
             \frac14 \leq c_- \le \frac{\beta_k^-}{k^2}\,.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.584504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_583312d1c134b434d88b083751487e723d14aaea089c8388aeffa632a04547c0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:hyperunif of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] A point process $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ is  hyperuniform if \begin{align*}
       \frac{1}{n} \int (\xi(\Lambda_n)-n)^2\mathsf{P}(d\xi)\xrightarrow{n\to \infty}0.
    \end{align*}
    The process $\mathsf{P}$ is class-1-hyperuniform if  $ \int (\xi(\Lambda_n)-n)^2\mathsf{P}(d\xi)=O(1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.803927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5834321046582e7c89164b9cc618a65a60353bc4a584651b972372abbb160b06","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:stopping-criterion of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Define the \emph{online convergence indicator}
\begin{equation}
\Gamma_k := \frac{\widehat{V}_k}{\rho_k^2} = \frac{\rho_{k+1}}{\rho_k} - 1 \;\ge\; 0.
\end{equation}
Assume that a lower bound $\tau \le 1 - (\lambda_3/\lambda_2)^2$ is known (or estimated online; see (rem:tau-estimation of the paper)). Define the critical threshold
\[
\eta(\varepsilon) := \frac{\varepsilon^4}{8} \cdot \tau^2.
\]
Then the stopping rule ``stop at the first $k$ such that $\Gamma_k \le \eta(\varepsilon)$'' guarantees
\[
\|v_k - s_2 \phi_2\|_\pi \le \varepsilon,
\]
provided that $\alpha_2(k) \ge 1/2$ at termination (which holds for all sufficiently large $k$).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.948241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58387706d5715ccb9540757a6eb993b6ba79316b5d78468ba55f05a069c5e6a3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.24703, 'Scheduling jobs with unknown size distribution in a M/G/1 queue: the shifted empirical Git'] Let $\Delta \in \N$. Denoting $A := d(\widehat{f_{n, \Delta}}, f_\Delta)$. Then for all $i \in [0, \Delta]$:
    \begin{equation}
        \left(\frac{1 - \frac{A\Delta}{L}}{1+\frac{A \Delta}{\ell}}\right) \nu_\Delta(\frac{i}{\Delta})
    \leq \widehat{\nu_{n, \Delta}}(\frac{i}{\Delta}) \leq \left(\frac{1 + \frac{A\Delta}{\ell}}{1 -
        \frac{A\Delta}{L}}\right) \nu_\Delta(\frac{i}{\Delta}).
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.903127+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_583b21435a1abaaf1ef9b2e352dcbb2bbfe90cad1fe33d69ece0a6b437df8bea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem equiv-vf of arXiv:2412.05698, 'Controlled rough SDEs, pathwise stochastic control and dynamic programming principles'] Suppose that Assumption (assum-dpp of the paper) holds. Let $t \in [0,T)$, \(y\in \mathbb{R}^{d_Y}\) and \(\mathbf{X}\in {\mathscr{C}}^{\alpha}_T\). Put
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{A}^t:=\{\eta \in \mathcal{A} \ \Big| \ \eta \text{ independent of ${\mathfrak F}_t$ under }\ensuremath{{\mathbb P}} \},
\end{equation}	
\begin{equation}

\tilde \mathcal{V} (t,y; \mathbf{X} ) := \mathrm{inf}_{\eta  \in {\mathcal{A}^t} } J (t,y, \eta; \mathbf{X} ),
\end{equation}
where $J$ is given by (equation cost-rp of the paper).
Then we have
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}(t,y;\mathbf{X})=\tilde \mathcal{V}(t,y;\mathbf{X}).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.257734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_583bd88db0e4adec231eee2acab144930854fb96a98dc10594fea204dd1f16e1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:price-equality-minimax of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space, and $X:\Omega\to{\mathbb{R}\cup\{\infty\}}$ measurable.
  Then $\overline{\mathbb{E}} X = \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X$ if and only if
  \begin{equation}
    \sup_{P\in\Delta(\Omega)} \inf_{Z\in\mathrm{mdcl}(\mathcal{Z})} \mathbb{E}_P [X-Z] = \inf_{Z\in\mathrm{mdcl}(\mathcal{Z})} \sup_{P\in\Delta(\Omega)} \mathbb{E}_P[X-Z]~.
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.318170+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58422738689619b7e8bcdff0e28147f6f63688aea2bdc8d7c9c83e64369209a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ITS-carac of arXiv:2411.14926, 'Convex combinations of random variables stochastically dominate the parent for a new class'] A random variable $X$ is {\rm InvSub}\ if and only if
\begin{equation}

F_X(\tfrac{x}{\theta})+F_X(\tfrac{x}{1-\theta})\leq F_X(x)+1,\quad \forall x\geq0,\, \theta\in(0,1).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.703056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58432422f9b594dede917b7db7ca8edc19dfb7ac31051dd516ca2a9c61e5cc86","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.09840, 'Langevin dynamics along the zero set of real-analytic potentials'] For each singularity type $(\lambda,m)$ there exists a Radon measure $\mu_{\lambda,m}$ on $Z_{\lambda,m}$ with full support such that for any $f \in C_c(D_{\lambda,m})$,
\begin{equation} 
\beta^\lambda (\log \beta)^{1-m}  \int_D f(x) e^{-\beta V(x)} dx \to \int_{Z_{\lambda,m}} f \, d\mu_{\lambda,m}, \quad \beta \to \infty.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, the limit measure is the pushforward
\[
\mu_{\lambda,m} = \pi_* \rho_{\lambda,m}
\]
of a density $\rho_{\lambda,m}$ on the manifold $E_{\lambda,m}$ in \eqref{eq:E_A^*} that can be described as follows: for any $A \subset A_\crit$ with $|A|=m$, and any monomializing chart $(U,y)$ such that $E_A$ is $\{y_I = 0\}$ for some $I \subset \{1,\ldots,d'\}$, the density is given by
\begin{equation} 
\rho_{\lambda,m} = \frac{\Gamma(\lambda)}{(m-1)!} \, \frac{b(0_I, y_{-I})}{\prod_{i \in I} k_i} \prod_{i \notin I} |y_i|^{-2 k_i \lambda + h_i} dy_{-I}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

