{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.989122+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5857a46696960a71a0d98b72e3fea46d2ee7478099721e90c9b87c9d1562ec1a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def-PPP of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] For any  $\Lambda\Subset \mathbb{R}^d$ and any boundary condition ${\rm bc}\in\{ {\rm per}, 0, {\rm par}\}$, we write ${{\tt Q}}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\Lambda,\rm bc}})}}}$ for the distribution of the Poisson point process (PPP) $\omega_{\rm P}$ on $\Lambda\times{\mathcal C }^{\ssup\circlearrowleft}$  with intensity measure 
