{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.501987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_586b3282debe804ec808f86e84772cd84db7b8dd42dc08686465a8dc9a71a0bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:DPP-rigid of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Let $ \mathsf{P}$ a stationary DPP with   Hermitian kernel $ K$ such that $ x  \mapsto   K(0,x)$ is square integrable. 
