{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.132960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_586d1ee8e138c736f7fe2701162cd87684c48d3ed148b73a5b4d1959d21ea321","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem PiIShuf of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] For any word $I=(i_{1},\cdots,i_{m})$, one has
