{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.677782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58891230e5ff74a631cfe491c98e0b2f0db392ffebc3fec59606c3cb18307a73","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] Suppose Hypotheses \ref{PEeqAssum-2.2}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.3}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.4} and \eqref{PETNs-3.01} hold. Then the family $\{p_{\tau,t}\}_{t\geq \tau}$ has the following properties: 

