{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:00:15.222295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58b93929c0e3ecbe6214eb0805d2445e9e9f0c7d479af546f98e5264da4cf90e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 41 (Concentration of subtree sizes) of arXiv:2607.18201, 'Finding Adam in noisy trees'] For any fixed $y\in(0,1)$ and $\eps>0$, there exists $M=M(\eps)>0$ large enough such that for all large $n$,
