{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.759475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58b9689d347e0f14714de52fad0f44e7e45093342887bd8fdfb5730efc2d02c8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn eq:gibbs_potts of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] With $N_n(Q_n,\phi,{{\bf X}})$ as in (equation hamiltoniandef of the paper) and $\beta \in \mathbb{R}$, define the Gibbs measure
\begin{align}
	\frac{d\mathbb{R}_{Q_n,{ \beta},\mu}}{d\mu^{\otimes n}}(\mathbf{X}):=\exp\Big(n\beta N_n(Q_n,\phi,{{\bf X}})-nZ_{Q_n}(\beta,\mu)\Big),
