{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.752348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58b9d75bf2807340ef577ef931f32ebfb92f8151713f2e78ed44eac65389adf3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2511.02725, 'Mixing of general biased adjacent transposition chains'] Let $\chi(\cB) = \max_{j\in [N-1]} |\{i: (j,j+1) \in E(B_i)\}|$ denote the maximum coverage
    of an edge in $[N]$.
    For any collection of blocks $\cB$, we have the following:
    \begin{align*}
        \gamma(\Mnn([N]))\ge \chi(\cB)^{-1}  \cdot \gamma(\mathcal M_\cB) \cdot \min_{\eta, i} \gamma(\Mnn(B_i^\eta))\,,
