{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.246672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58f4d64a94ff8d6155751f1594858d1ae1890acea0fc10c0107d56593bd7a268","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 30 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any real numbers $R > 1$ and $\delta \in (0,1)$, the following holds w.o.p.  with respect to $\mathbb P^N_{a,b,c}$. Fix real numbers $a, b, c \in [R^{-1}, R]$; sample a uniformly random tiling on a hexagon $\mathfrak{X}_{a, b, c}$ and denote its height function by $H : \overline{\mathfrak{X}}_{a, b, c} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$. 

