{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.642673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58f97f338c5be4a2c239376bd1fbc4b28d480e25d26c19d2686b5ecf10de6487","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:gs-entire of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Let $\beta\in (0,1)$.  A Schwartz function $\phi\in\mathcal S(\mathbb{R})$ belongs to 
