{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.975931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58ff0a9c49615532ef7e8e012dab24bdca83ee9161c5539a89f9e7792fb55fbf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 47 (Localized exterior lift and exact area realization) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] Assume first that \(V_T\leq K\) almost surely for a deterministic
