{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.257653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5911cf24d661726940551152bcda76d6b22642a6865c4eee02779755087129d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let~\eqref{co:6} and~\eqref{eq:integrability condition} hold for $\rho > 0$ and $I$ be a positive solution to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} that admits a measurable locally integrable function $u\colon\R_{+}\rightarrow\R$ such that
