{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.857663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59425122c71a0cd97ad64594f77f7047938383b0d9f89bdd28e28b7f46c793f4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Predictive coincidence decomposition) of arXiv:2608.20337, 'Information on trajectories:\\ martingales and random times'] Let $\alpha_i \geq 0$ for all $i$ with $\bar\alpha := \sum_{i=1}^W \alpha_i
\geq 1$, let $Q_t^\alpha(\gamma) := \prod_i
P_t^{(i)}(\gamma)^{\alpha_i}/Z_t(\alpha)$ be the Gibbs law on prefixes, and let
\begin{equation}
  \kappa_t^\alpha(\gamma)
  := \sum_{x\in S} \prod_{i=1}^W
     P\bigl(X_{t+1}=x \mid X_{0:t}=\gamma; P^{(i)}\bigr)^{\alpha_i}
\end{equation}
be the one-step predictive coincidence kernel.  Then
\begin{align}
  Z_{t+1}(\alpha) &= Z_t(\alpha)\,\E_{Q_t^\alpha}[\kappa_t^\alpha],
    \\
