{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.087896+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_594607f1dcc020d050aef1ca6428f48d2c4b45115d33235febb84cd609c9a777","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-correspondence-pos of arXiv:2411.12623, 'Random signed measures'] There exists a one-to-one both ways measurable correspondence between a purely atomic measure $\mu\in\mathcal{M}_S$ and a counting measure on $S\times(0,\infty)$, $N_\mu$ say, given by $N_\mu(A\times B)=\sum_{i}\delta_{(s_i,\kappa_i)}(A\times B)$, where $\{(s_i,\kappa_i)_{i\in\mathbb{N}}\}$ are the atoms of $\mu$ with their respective values, thus $\kappa_i=\mu(\{s_i\})$, and satisfying
	\begin{equation}
		\int_{A\times(0,\infty)} sN_{\mu}(ds\times dx)<\infty,
	\end{equation}
	for every $A\in\hat{\mathcal{S}}$; the correspondence is the following: for every $A\in\hat{\mathcal{S}}$ and $B\in \mathcal{B} ((0,\infty))$ such that $0\notin\bar{B}$,
	\begin{equation}
		\mu(A)=	\int_{A\times(0,\infty)} sN_{\mu}(ds\times dx)
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		N_{\mu}(A\times B)=\lim\limits_{\varepsilon\to 0}\lim\limits_{n\to\infty}\sum_{j}\delta_{\mu(A_{nj})}(B_{\varepsilon}),\quad\text{for $B$ open,}
	\end{equation}
	\begin{equation}
		N_{\mu}(A\times B)=\lim\limits_{\varepsilon\to 0}\lim\limits_{n\to\infty}\sum_{j}\delta_{\mu(A_{nj})}(B^{\varepsilon}),\quad\text{for $B$ closed,}
	\end{equation}
	where $(A_{nj})$ is a dissection system of measurable subsets of $A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.302800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59481f8c4b6351309d0b29c2ed414cd09054c78b34909be672caf72ac847211a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop3.7 of arXiv:2604.22130, 'Reflected Stochastic Differential Equations Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Nonlinear C'] Let $S,\tilde{S}\in S_G^p(0,T)$ with $S_0=\tilde{S}_0$ and Assumption (ass1 of the paper) hold. Given $c_0,\tilde{c}_0\in\mathbb{R}$, let $(X,A)$, $(\tilde{X},\tilde{A})$ be the solution to the doubly reflected problem with constraints $l,r$ for $c_0+S$ and $\tilde{c}_0+\tilde{S}$, respectively. Moreover, let $(A^l,A^r)$, $(\tilde{A}^l,\tilde{A}^r)$ be the corresponding constraining processes. If there exists a nondecreasing function $\nu\in S_G^p(0,T)$ with $\nu_0=0$ such that $S=\tilde{S}+\nu$, then for each $t\in [0,T]$, the following relations hold: 
\begin{itemize}

\item[1.] $A^r_t-(c_0-\tilde{c}_0)^-\leq \tilde{A}^r_t\leq A^r_t+\nu_t+(c_0-\tilde{c}_0)^+$, q.s.;
\item[2.] $\tilde{A}^l_t-(c_0-\tilde{c}_0)^-\leq {A}^l_t\leq \tilde{A}^l_t+\nu_t+(c_0-\tilde{c}_0)^+$, q.s.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.802356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5949b6a0e2b6aa16504d2602df7909a942abd20dd254cdb97f224a3c5f134e6f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Strichartz estimate) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Let $s\in\mathbb{R}$ and $(\mu,r)$ be higher-order Schr\"{o}dinger admissible, i.e. 	$\mu,r\geq 2,$ and $\displaystyle \frac{3}{\mu}+\frac{1}{r}=\frac12.$ Then, the solution of the homogeneous Cauchy problem \eqref{cauchy1} satisfies the Strichartz estimate
	\begin{equation}
		\left\|y\right\|_{L_{t}^{\mu}((0, T); H_{x}^{s,r}(\mathbb{R}))}\lesssim \left\|y_0\right\|_{H_{x}^{s}(\mathbb{R})},
	\end{equation}
    where $H^{s, r}(\mathbb{R})$ is the Bessel potential space with the norm 
\begin{equation}
	\left\|f\right\|_{H^{s,r}(\mathbb{R})}
	:=
	\left\| \mathcal{F}^{-1}\left\{ \left(1+k^2\right)^{\frac{s}{2}} \mathcal F\{f\}(k)\right\}\right\|_{L^{r}(\mathbb{R})}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

