{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.767103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_594fcf037fbaacd9915abea7409c616e178d34a68db178ab347dca23cdbd1745","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:ext of arXiv:2508.21658, 'Infinite-dimensional stochastic differential equations for Coulomb random point fields'] \thetag{i}
A non-negative symmetric bilinear form $ (\E , \mathscr{D}_0 ) $ densely defined on $ \Lnu $ is called closable on $ \Lnu $ if, for any $ \E $-Cauchy sequence $ f_n\in \mathscr{D}_0$ such that $ \lim \| f_n \| _{\Lnu } = 0 $ as $ n \to \infty $, 
it holds that $ \limi{n}\E (f_n , f_n ) = 0$. 

\noindent \thetag{ii} 
If $ (\E , \mathscr{D}_0) $ is closable on $ \Lnu $, then there exists 
a closed extension of $ (\E , \mathscr{D}_0) $. 
The smallest closed extension $ (\E , \mathscr{D} ) $ is called the closure of $ (\E , \mathscr{D}_0) $.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.289254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59528c623b3fa9f43484ae670f021d29e912b8151693b2f463df4fbbd8c295be","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop GenDirFI-prop of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] For any $\zeta\in \mathcal{P}_{+}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$, the generalised Dirichlet form~(equation def:genDirichlet of the paper) and the generalised Fisher information~(equation def:genFisher of the paper) with respect to $\zeta$  satisfy the following.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Continuity: The maps $(\zeta,f)\mapsto \mathscr{E}_\zeta(f)$ and $(\zeta,\varphi)\mapsto \mathscr{R}_\zeta(\varphi)$ are continuous on $\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})\times \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}$ and $\{(\zeta,\varphi) \,:\,\zeta\in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}), \varphi\in  \mathcal D_\zeta(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})\}$ respectively. 

        \item Non-negativity: $\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f),\mathscr{R}_\zeta(\varphi)\geq 0$ with equality if and only if $f \in \left\langle {\mathbf 1} \right\rangle$ and $\varphi=\1$ respectively.
        \item Convexity: $\mathscr{E}_\zeta(\cdot)$ and $\mathscr{R}_\zeta(\cdot)$ are convex on their domains of definition.
        \item Connection: Let $f\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^{|\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}|}$ with $\mathbb{E}_\zeta[f]=0$. Then, for all $\delta \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ with $|\delta| \leq \frac12 \|f\|_\infty^{-1}$, we have $\1+ \delta f \in \mathcal D_\zeta(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$ and
        \begin{equation}
            \mathscr{R}_\zeta(\1+ \delta f) = \delta^2 \bigl(\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f) + \delta R \bigr),
        \end{equation}
        where the remainder term satisfies $|R| \leq 3 \|M\|_\infty |\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}| \|f\|_\infty^3$.  
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.416650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_595867fb1c66c6c8bbcedde73c79bad14a95c58b7811c7f2964243308baf05a9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2605.16072, 'Stochastic integration \\with respect to a L\'evy basis'] Let $\big(\Omega, \mathcal{F},P,(\mathcal{F}_k)_{k\in{\mathbb N}_0}\big)$ and $\big(\Omega', \mathcal{F}',P',(\mathcal{F}'_k)_{k\in{\mathbb N}_0}\big)$ be filtered probability spaces. 
	Then there exist constants $c_1,c_2>0$ such that, for every $n\in\N$, every adapted sequence 
	$(X_k)_{k\in\N}$ of real random variables on $\big(\Omega, \mathcal{F},P,(\mathcal{F}_k)_{k\in{\mathbb N}_0}\big)$ with corresponding decoupled tangent sequence $(Y_k)_{k\in\N}$ on $\big(\Omega \times \Omega^\prime, \mathcal{F}\otimes \mathcal{F}', P \otimes P', (\mathcal{F}_k\otimes \mathcal{F}'_k)_{k\in{\mathbb N}_0}\big)$ satisfy:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[{\rm (a)}]   $\displaystyle
		E_P\left[\left|\sum_{k=1}^n X_k\right|\wedge 1\right]\leq c_1 E_{P\otimes P^\prime}\left[\left|\sum_{k=1}^n Y_k\right|\wedge 1\right]$;
		\item[{\rm (b)}] $\displaystyle
		E_{P\otimes P^\prime}\left[\left|\sum_{k=1}^n Y_k\right|\wedge 1\right]\leq c_2 \sup_{\epsilon_1,\dots,\epsilon_n \in \{\pm 1\}}E_P\left[\left|\sum_{k=1}^n \epsilon_k X_k\right|\wedge 1\right]. $
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.054646+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5958ce729fe7079f0697e7d226e537a0a27644725536d507a4615aec668cd5e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lema_orig_teska of arXiv:2607.13302, 'Extending an Order-Statistic Characterization of the Exponential Distribution'] For $1 \leq j < k \leq n$ and any $r \geq 1$ it holds that
    \begin{align}
        &\frac{1}{(k-1)!}\sum_{i=0}^{r+1} (i+k-1)! \binom{n-k}{i} \genfrac{\{}{\}}{0pt}{}{k+r+1}{i+k} \nonumber \\
        & \qquad = \frac{1}{(k-j-1)!} \sum_{i=0}^{r+1} (k-j-1+i)! \binom{n-k+j}{i} \sum_{l=k-2}^{k+r-1} \genfrac{\{}{\}}{0pt}{}{l-j+2}{k-j+i} \nonumber \\
        & \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \times \sum_{s=0}^{k+r-l-1} \binom{n-k}{s} \frac{(s+j-1)!}{(j-1)!} \genfrac{\{}{\}}{0pt}{}{j+k+r-l-1}{s+j}
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.723929+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_595986e0c6788b14366324b24a8c500c5e9e91bab9570a046e9e57d099c11706","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:regularN of arXiv:2606.02340, 'Transitivity in Inhomogeneous Random Tournaments'] Suppose $W$ is a degree-regular tournamenton with $\zeta(W) \in [0, 1)$ and $T_n \sim T(n, W)$. Then the following hold: 
