{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.614330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_595bedb6acd361f34934e25c58e355af7ffaf3bdccd599e40795c4c91baa7685","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2506.09462, 'Transition Path Theory For L\'{e}vy-Type Processes: SDE Representation and Statistics'] The \textbf{$AB$-transition entrance distribution} in \(\bar{B} \cap (B + 1)\) is defined as:  
\begin{equation*}
    \eta^+_B(\d x) = \frac{1}{v_B^+}\rho(x)\overleftarrow{\mathcal{L}}\overleftarrow{q}(x)\d x, \quad x \in \bar{B} \cap (B + 1),
\end{equation*}
and analogously, the \textbf{$BA$-transition entrance distribution} on \(\bar{A} \cap (A + 1)\):  
\begin{equation}
    \eta^+_A(\d x) = \frac{1}{v_A^+}\rho(x)\overleftarrow{\mathcal{L}}\overleftarrow{q}(x)\d x,
\end{equation}
where \(v_A^+\) and \(v_B^+\) are normalizing constants such that these define probability measures.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.475529+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_595c738c9192501a7b4ee2b5557439db3bd17c5db699effb9ce73ac8cfddef2e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma restr-right-Quillen of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be a homomorphism of compact Lie groups. Then
    \[
        \alpha_!\colon\cat{$\bm{G}$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}\rightleftarrows\cat{$\bm{G'}$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}
	\nobreak
	\mspace{6mu plus 1mu}
	{:}
	\nonscript\mkern-\thinmuskip
	\mathpunct{}
	\mspace{2mu}
 \alpha^*
    \]
    is a Quillen adjunction with homotopical right adjoint.
    \begin{proof}
        By [barrero2021]*{Lemma~3.7(vii)}, the functor $\alpha^*$ is homotopical. On the other hand, Example~(ex:graph-restr-rQ of the paper) shows that if $H$ is any compact Lie group, then $\alpha^*\colon\cat{$\bm{(H\times G')}$-Top}\to \cat{$\bm{(H\times G)}$-Top}$ is right Quillen for the $\mathcal G_{H,G}$- and $\mathcal G_{H,G'}$-model structures; applying this for $H={\textup{O}}(V)$, we see that $\alpha^*$ preserves \emph{level} fibrations. Similarly, if $f\colon X\to Y$ is even a $G'$-global fibration, then this shows that
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                \alpha^*X(V)\arrow[r]\arrow[d,"\alpha^*f(V)"'] & \alpha^*X(V\oplus W)\arrow[d,"\alpha^*f(V\oplus W)"]\\
                \alpha^*Y(V)\arrow[r] & \alpha^*Y(V\oplus W)
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        is a homotopy pullback for all $H$-representations $V,W$ such that $V$ is faithful, i.e.\ $\alpha^*f$ is a $G'$-global fibration.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.725803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_595d16b922d389a30ab408e07dbe499049ed38eeaad31f2f860e4f4bed7f9f0a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma pair_moment_bounds of arXiv:2411.04322, 'Bounding Hellinger Distance with Stein's Method'] Under the remaining assumptions of (lemma_2 of the paper),
