{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.759950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59860586071a3552bdbca43b2f88203a01a659ea0329c7b9f9c8fccb29546a6d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz 67 of arXiv:2511.20322, 'Dissertation'] Suppose we are given a sequence $(\si_N)_{N\in \N}$ of random $J$-dimensional permutations, such that \assref{assum:limitCopulas} holds true.
Then $(X^N_t)_{t\in [0,1]}$ converges in distribution to a centered Gaussian process $W$, as $N\to \infty$, with
