{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.265629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_598777759dacf0ec169b0507ec75fc3a2ccdd50a2f3f3be887a161cf0d0a3532","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:recovery of arXiv:2603.14906, 'Four Levels of Thermodynamic Convergence of Singularly Perturbed Markov Semigroups'] Fix $t>0$. A sequence $(\psi_k)_{k\in\mathbb N}\subset C_b(\bar E;\mathbb R^n)$ is called a
