{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.641075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_598a6c15dac6ad8b618a93b0166f79f566316ed4efae109cad919e7bf8b3ee64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (\textsf{D\"obler--Vidotto--Zheng} {\cite[Theorem 1.2 and 
Corollary 1.3) of arXiv:2607.28742, '2607.28742'] {DVZ18}}] 
Fix an integer $q\geq 1$ and consider  $F\in\bC_q\cap L^4(\Omega)$ with $\E[ F^2] =1$.
Then,  with the notation \eqref{nota1},

