{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.694041+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5997d8abcb78b30439dd07ef882b316af4c522095c5792da49287c881f0c1dcb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:300.31 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is small enough, then, given any $0 < \eta' < \eta< \tfrac{1}{2}$ small enough (depending only on $\gamma$), there exists for each $\epsilon \in (0,1)$, $u \geq 0$ and $k \geq 1$ a probability measure ${\rm O}^{k,\epsilon}_u$ on $\mathbb R^{{\rm Q}(k)}$ (depending on $\eta',\eta$) such that, for any fixed $\delta > 0$, we have that,  as $n \to \infty$ followed by $k \to \infty$, 
