information and the resolution remains calibration-limited. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.301733+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_599d686bfa61461f6feae69fedcd7af90b424857f60e9796241357e512ed4ca3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:o8 of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $(x,t)\in\mathbb{R}^2$. Then for any $\xi_1<\xi_2$  and $c\in\mathbb{R}^2$, there exists $T_0 \in \mathbb{R}$ so that, for all $T < T_0$,
