{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.457706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59bd73ff36ccfeebf6f77d8803c3ee5ae1395cc8081710e12e771c80debee474","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro_edge of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Fix a small constant $\tau>0$. Then there exists a small $0<\omega_c<\tau/10$ such that, for any $z_i \in {\mathbb C}~(i=1,2)$ with 
