{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.745355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59c0254436fd9317c38de3dd29604b05d40c66d15c11e180d4818bb52200f240","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Laplace lower bound) of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Suppose Assumptions \ref{ass:b-sigma-local-properties}-\ref{ass:log-gradient-convergence} hold. Then, for any bounded, continuous $F$,
