{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.895549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59d780331e111162242faac8a97b83acbd1c91944915c99980aa99e9970473ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:corrector_construction of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] Suppose Assumption~(ass:P of the paper) and (ass:finite_H_-1_norm of the paper) hold. Then, for each $i = 1, \dots, d$,

