where $\mathrm{i}=\sqrt{-1}$.

\vspace{3mm}

\noindent 2. Suppose that $r_X+r_Y\not=0$. Then, as $x\rightarrow\infty$,
\begin{align*}
f_{Z}(x)\sim  \frac{\mathrm{e}^{-r_X^2/2}}{\sqrt{2\pi sx}}\exp\bigg\{-\frac{x}{s(1+\rho)}\bigg\}\sum_{k=0}^\infty d_k(r_X,\rho,1)\frac{s^k}{x^k},  
