{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.341014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a04d6daa0ae8a11a22eb008a9c4e70b8d40600a3de5a990288f67bc511e9815","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] For every $\epsilon>0$, there exist $w>0$ and $K<\infty$ such that, for all
