{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.894799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a0c84d3239736647cc677f0491cce6da0fafaf4338a32398522c305ee5c9f67","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.23989, 'Collision Properties in Discrete and Continuous Time on Bounded-Degree Graphs'] Let $G$ be a bounded-degree connected graph. Then:
