{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.935925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a202121b0816bcdaa8ac368c4430a53aa7acb3975bf72331b082025c790f4eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $(G_n)_{n \in \N}$,  $|G(V_n)| \asymp n^d$, be the sequence of boxes $[-n, n]^d$ in $\mathbb{L}^d$, $d \geq 5$. There exists constants $p^*, c_1, c_2, \gamma > 0$, all depending only on $d$, such that for a sequence of environment distributions $(\mu_n)_{n\geq 1}$ and $a_1 = a_1(n), a_2 = a_2(n)$ satisfying
    \begin{equation} 
    \begin{aligned}
        a_1 &:= F^{-1}_{\mu_n} \big( \frac{1}{2d - 1} - \frac{p^*}{2} \big), \\
        a_2 &:= F^{-1}_{\mu_n}(1 - p^* ), \\
        a_2 - a_1 &\ll \log n,
    \end{aligned}
