{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.828185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a4b946336273389360f9ff780250cdb9f7e4e4b0f81cabef770526122bb71e7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2604.10705, '#1'] A functional $F:[0,T]\times D([0,T],\mathbb{R}^d)\to \mathbb{R}$ is \emph{boundedness-preserving} if for every $t \in [0,T)$ and compact set $K \subset \mathbb{R}^d$, there exists a constant $C_{t,K}> 0$ such that:
