{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.340216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a4c10833f4b4869220c7885ff3d65703e213b1ee79718bdf61b465830e10ec0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:telescopic of arXiv:2605.03896, 'Dimer models on astroidal zig-zag graphs'] Let~$\mathsf f_+,\mathsf f_-\in F(\mathsf G_{\bm \beta^n})$ be adjacent faces with~$\mathsf w\mathsf b\in E(\mathsf G_{\bm \beta^n})$ as their common adjacent edge, and let~$\alpha$ and~$\beta$ be the strands containing~$\mathsf w\mathsf b$, as in Figure~(fig:fock_kast of the paper). Then
