{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.887315+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a515ee29c38f146a52584d7e65a970101af03e2a389e120b9898fd4edc90c06","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Let $u,v,\alpha>0$.  Fix $k=1,\dots$ and $u>t_1>\dots>t_k>t_{k+1}:=0$. Then
