{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.774892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a521b97d057c3027aff88722c303ce8b833dfa11107d33a0630de99739e841f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For $I\subset B_{N/2}$, let $I^+$ and $I^-$ be a partition of $I$ satisfying that for all $x\in I^-$, there is some $x'\in I^+$ such that $x\sim x'$. 
