{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.250966+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a53da835ca408f79ac93dd4bb352e818ed5f65ca8d168826b964da30aee1636","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] For $\mu\in(0,1]$, the flow $S_t$ is continuous from $L_\mu^2(\IR^d)\cap\Gamma H^2(\IR^d)$ to itself. In particular, we have
