{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.123161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a593705f752aec842fbe4a34f62cf7a381e322947c1cdbc11076b14f9131dc6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:disi of arXiv:2602.00853, 'Mixing times for the stochastic $p$-Laplace equation'] Let $r\geq 1$ be fixed.
Assume that there exists a unique invariant probability measure $\mu_\ast$ on $(H,\mathcal{B}(H))$ with finite absolute moment of order $r$ for the dual semigroup $(P^\ast_t)_{t\ge 0}$ on the space of probability measures on $(H,{\mathcal B}(H))$.
Then for any $x\in H$ and $0<s\leq t$
it follows that
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{W}_r(P^*_t\delta_x,P^*_t\mu_\ast)\leq \int_{H}
\int_{H}\mathcal{W}_r(P^*_s\delta_z,P^*_s\delta_y)P^*_{t-s}\delta_x(\mathrm{d} z)\mu_\ast(\mathrm{d} y).
\end{equation}
In particular, it follows that
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{W}_r(P^*_t\delta_x,\mu_\ast)=\mathcal{W}_r(P^*_t\delta_x,P^*_t\mu_\ast)
\leq \int_{H} \mathcal{W}_r(P^*_t\delta_x,P^*_t\delta_y)\mu_\ast(\mathrm{d} y).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.539405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a59aeb598972edec4b79d2ece7e138aae01bf701f0a17b924f51612ee33dc34","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 17 of arXiv:2603.28702, 'Distribution of the magnetization of the critical Ising model on sparse random graphs'] \begin{enumerate}
