{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.950864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a64e7baeb1ba4539c7f780fef2090db044f30d0254214e597799b6a9c550be0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] We consider $1 \le d \le N^{\delta/4}$ with $0<\delta < 1/3$. There exists a constant $C>0$ such that if $m \in \N$ satisfies $m \le  C^{-1} \sqrt{d} \log N$ and $\nu>0$ then 
