{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.973748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a6fd2c70c37b557405bf99eae0e52850654d68cdd4ae0e7ee889e06f30b0569","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop skew and LR coef of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] Given $m,n\ge 0$ and $\lambda,\nu\in\Sig_n$, we have
\begin{equation}\sum_{\mu\in\Sig_{2n}^+} c_{\mu,\nu}^{\alt,\lambda}(t)Q_{(\mu/0[2n])}(x_1,\ldots,x_m;t)=Q_{\lambda/\nu}(x_1,\ldots,x_m;t^2),\end{equation}
and
