{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.560627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a81c55c8ebc82567193215c9247539d6afd3b40b15e8b8a3812f76791f44430","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:Dprop of arXiv:2604.08129, 'Polarity of points for Gaussian random fields in critical dimension'] Suppose $\gamma d \le 1$.
Let $n = 2^p$ and 
\begin{align}
K_0 = \begin{cases} 4^{-1}(\log\log 8)^{-1} &  \text{if }\gamma d = 1,\\
\left[\alpha\left((\frac{3}{2})^{\frac{1}{1-\gamma d}}-1\right)/\log 8\right]^{1-\gamma d} & \text{if } \gamma d < 1,
