{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.825832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a84ed41bf44968fe856956a15098f8c2984cde7c7323a3fd2fcb360ce38b98e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma canonical-path of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] (Local canonical path method) For any birth and death process with the generator $\cL$, a subset $K$ of the state space $\Z_{\geq 0}$ and the stationary distribution $\nu$, we have the following inequality holds:
    \begin{align}
        \Var_{\nu_K}(f) \leq C_L \sum_{k: k,k+1 \in K} Q_K(k,k+1) (f(k+1)-f(k))^2
    \end{align}
    where the constant $C_L$ is defined as:
    \begin{align}

        C_L = \max_{k: k,k+1 \in K} \frac{\sum_{x,y \in K: x \leq k \leq y-1} |x-y| \nu_K(x) \nu_K(y)}{Q_K(k,k+1)} \, \forall f \in \ell_{2,\nu_K}
    \end{align}
    where $\nu_K(x) = \frac{\nu(x)}{\sum_{x \in K}\nu(x)} \, \forall x \in K$ and $\nu_K(x) = 0$ otherwise and $Q_K(u,v) = \nu_K(u) \cL(u,v) = \nu_K(v) \cL(v,u) \forall u,v \in \Z_{\geq 0}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

