{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.687792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5a87ab028dcfc30c35b64dc02a9e8e11d3a5ef1e49f8a4790ae0726ae0ab1c4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:higher_spatial_moments_ODE of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] Suppose at least one of the hypotheses of (equation HD+ of the paper) holds, let $n\geq 1$, and let $P_1,\ldots,P_n$ be monomials on $\mathbb R^d$ of total degree $p$. Then
