where $\Pi_{r,m}$ sends a length-$r$ word to its suffix of length $m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.564155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5abf45f0b5f4b12817531d3f8a7a2447ed24846e734721311b000a9dd249bee1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.drift-bound of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] There exists $C<\infty$ such that, for $\mathbb{Q}$-a.e.\ $\omega$ and every $(m,h,\rho)$ in the admissible regime~(equation eq.admissible of the paper), the following holds. Suppose that $z=(z_1,\ldots,z_d)\in H^1_0(\square_M;\mathbb{R}^d)$ solves, componentwise in $\square_M$,
		\begin{equation}
			-\nabla\cdot(\mathbf{a}\nabla z_i)
			=2\lambda 3^{-m} e_1 \cdot(\mathbf{a}\nabla w_{i,M}-\bar{\mathbf{a}} e_i)-2\rho 3^{-3m}(w_{i,M}-x_i)+2\lambda(\mathbf{a} e_1) \cdot \nabla z_i-2\rho 3^{-2m}z_i\, .
		\end{equation}
		Then the drift integral satisfies
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{aligned}
			\left|\lambda\sum_{i=1}^d\Xint-_{\square_M} z_i\bigl((\mathbf{a}-\bar{\mathbf{a}})e_1\bigr)\cdot\nabla z_i\right|
			&\le \frac{1}{16}\left(\rho 3^{-2m}\|z\|_{\underline L^2(\square_M)}^2
			+\frac12\sum_{i=1}^d\Xint-_{\square_M}\nabla z_i\cdot\mathbf{a}\nabla z_i\right)\\
			&\quad+C \rho^2 3^{2h-2m} 3^{-2\beta_h M}\, .
			\end{aligned}
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.866852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5abfac5f0ece2f5abfcabb536a6538bc376749698d9dbde232389a18440f38d5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 35 of arXiv:2512.00213, 'On strong sharp phase transition in the random connection model'] Let $n\in\N$ and $t\ge 0$. If $D^*_\varphi<\infty$ and $\phi^*_t(r)$ decay exponentially fast as $r\to\infty$, then
