{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.660619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ac8dd3f849ba4c08acde9ed71ecf311f10d8e9b569c7263371b0f89eeeaeb17","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma: intertwining sections of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] Up to passing to a finite extension of $X$, there is a measurable map $\sigma: \mathbb{Z}^d \times X \to \Gamma_0$ satisfying:
    \begin{enumerate}
