{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.989434+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5acadb6fd1dee35881b12c4f95db9d0eb72d4a29b84735fd2f38ac6e0aec6235","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cokernel distribution theorem 1 of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Let $G$ be a finite abelian group and $\mathcal{P}$ be a finite set of primes including those dividing $|G|$. 
Assume that a sequence $(k_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}$ satisfies the following:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for every prime $p$ in $\mathcal{P}$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item if $2 \in \mathcal{P}$, then for every $\delta>0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$.
\end{enumerate}
Then
$$
\lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong G\right) = \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G)|}\prod_{p\in \mathcal{P}} \prod_{i=1}^\infty (1-p^{-i})
= \prod_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.009054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5acd125d14791c5a8a2ebd3adf34cc61fca6f763d642e9a819ad1e506e9584d0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2609.02808, 'Minimizers of Laplace eigenvalues under a lower curvature bound'] Let $k\ge2$ and let $(g_n)\subset\Cc$ satisfy
