\end{equation}
Consequently, no minimizing sequence for $f_k$ collapses.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.963650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5acd274c8c21da0052e7fb90bb2e8005f2fea6cb64ecefe48b93172c88366a53","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 22 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] Fix $m\ge 2$ and $\delta\in(-m,0]$. Let $r_{i,3}$ be as defined in~\eqref{eq:r3}.
