{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.503868+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ae90f93fd8e4a12c4a8cfe130ba9cde601c0b59160764902a5b067853087a7c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:kingman-poisson-dirichlet of arXiv:2601.09537, 'Gene genealogies in haploid populations evolving according to sweepstakes reproduction'] The $\delta_{0}$-Poisson-Dirichlet$(\alpha,0)$-coalescent is a
continuous-time  $\Xi$-coalescent with $\Xi$-measure $\Xi = \delta_{0} + \Xi_{+}$  
