{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.333533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5af11c86a064ad01d73df8e14c885cf221dea2d2e09c601e83d417b1aad84d81","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-prelim-gap-est-final-constant-rounds of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Suppose that $\alpha > 1$ and
    \begin{equation}{}
        M \geq (\log n)^{99}, \quad 1-\delta \leq n^{-\frac{1}{100(\alpha+1)}} \,.
    \end{equation}
    Define $\mathfrak F(M,\delta)$ to be the collection of $(M',\delta')$ such that 
    \begin{equation}{}
        (1-(\log n)^{-2})M \leq M', \quad (1-\delta') \leq \max\left\{ \frac{\log n}{n}, (\log n)^2(1-\delta)^{\alpha} \right\}  \,.
    \end{equation}
    Given any $(\mathbf X_1,\ldots,\mathbf X_n) \in \overline{\Omega}_n(M,\delta)$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb P^\alpha_{n,\mathbf X}\left( (\mathbf X_1',\ldots,\mathbf X_n') \in \cup_{ (M',\delta') \in \mathfrak F(M,\delta) } \overline{\Omega}_n(M',\delta'), \mathcal L(\mathbf X')=\mathcal L(\mathbf X) \right) \geq 1-\frac{1}{\log n} \,.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.198328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5af160b7afafadf1575d4f4a6c3c55484527be9f54daec8237206303562dbc72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2608.22636, 'Q-Learning with Stable Infinite-Dimensional \\Linear Function Approximation'] Suppose $n\ge\ceil{n_0^{\mrm N}}$ and $0<T\le1$. Then, for every
