{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.471314+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5aff15207200eda175c743d03e131e6d4e54c64e7b255087f32fbdb793150ddd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 31 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] Let $f: X \rightarrow S$ be a projective surjective morphism of integral Noetherian schemes with $X$ normal, and let $D$ be an $\R$-Cartier $\R$-divisor on $X$. Then the following hold.
