{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.041974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b02f6c2bc8788dd8ff321de6ae659e8446a266f5aaa7c0d272ecb4496496c1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Let $\hat \tau\in \hat{\mathcal T}^F$. Let $M\in \mathcal M$ be a minimal class. The following properties are satisfied:
\begin{itemize}	
\item[i)] $\hat\tau$ contains no edges going out from $M$, if $\hat \tau$ is rooted inside $M$;
