{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.291489+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b11983ff571376b53f1899624d4a60b9d9ea02b1dfa351ab4841b2d1572da2f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:alternativeGradient of arXiv:2609.03094, 'Discrete Gromov--Wasserstein Duality: Algorithms and Isomorphism Testing'] For any $u\in\mathbb R^{r_0}$ and $\varepsilon>0$, let $x^{\star}_u$ be the unique solution of the regularized quadratic program $\min_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\frac 12 x^{\intercal}\mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal}\mathrm{B}_1x-u^{\intercal}\mathrm{B}_0x -\varepsilon \mathsf{H}(x)\right\}$. Then, $x^{\star}_u$ coincides with $x^{\star}_{(u,v^{\star}(u))}$, the unique solution of $\min_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\left(\mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal} v^{\star}(u)-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal} u\right)^{\intercal}x-\varepsilon \mathsf{H}(x)\right\}$, where $v^{\star}(u)$ is the unique solution of the strongly concave maximization problem 
    \begin{equation}

        \sup_{v\in\mathbb R^{r_1}} f_{u}(v)\coloneqq-\frac 12 \|v\|^2+\min_{x\in\mathcal K}\left\{\left(\mathrm{B}_1^{\intercal} v-\mathrm{B}_0^{\intercal} u\right)^{\intercal}x-\varepsilon \mathsf{H}(x)\right\}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

