{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.973559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b6e13f5dbc30c9e9051300fb5dabfc9d52a3213bd0cca7968649013b3be74fa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn collection-plaquette-ass of arXiv:2508.13827, 'Surface sums in two-dimensional large-$N$ lattice Yang--Mills: Cancellations and explicit '] Given a non-backtrack loop $\ell$, the \textbf{canonical collection} $\mathcal{K}_{\ell}$ of plaquette assignments associated with $\ell$ is the collection of finite plaquette assignments of the form $K = K_{\ell} + K'$ where:
