{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.973886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b7cc8040afaf9fa0bef1e8a3f066b028cc57e587157169620328c2947ad669b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm fixed K 't Hooft master loop equation for surface sum of arXiv:2508.13827, 'Surface sums in two-dimensional large-$N$ lattice Yang--Mills: Cancellations and explicit '] {borga2024surfacesumslatticeyangmills}}] 
	Fix a non-null-loop $\ell$ and a finite plaquette assignment  $K:\mathcal{P}\to\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$. Let $\mathbf{e}$ be a specific edge of the loop $\ell$. Suppose that the  edge $\mathbf{e}$ is a copy of the lattice edge $e\in E_{\mathbb{Z}^2}$. Then
	\begin{align}
		\phi^K(\ell) =&\sum_{\{\ell_1,\ell_2\}\in \mathbb{S}_-(\mathbf{e},\ell)}
		\sum_{K_1+K_2=K}
		\phi^{K_1}(\ell_1)\phi^{K_2}(\ell_2) - \sum_{\{\ell_1,\ell_2\}\in \mathbb{S}_+(\mathbf{e},\ell)}
		\sum_{K_1+K_2=K}\phi^{K_1}(\ell_1)\phi^{K_2}(\ell_2) \notag\\
		&+ \upbeta
		\sum_{p\in \mathcal{P}(e^{-1},K)}
		\phi^{K\setminus p}(\ell \ominus_{\mathbf{e}}p)
		-\upbeta\sum_{q\in \mathcal{P}(e,K)}
		\phi^{K\setminus q}(\ell \oplus_{\mathbf{e}}q),
	\end{align}
	where $\mathcal{P}(e,K)$ denotes the collection of plaquettes in $\mathcal{P}$ containing $e$ as one of the four boundary edges (with the correct orientation) such that $K(p)\geq 1$, and $K\setminus p$ denotes the plaquette assignment $K'$ such that $K'(p)=K(p)-1$ and $K'(q)=K(q)$ for all $q\neq p$.

	We also used the (more compact) notation $\sum_{K_1+K_2=K}$ to indicate the sum $\sum_{\substack{K_1,K_2:\\K_1+K_2=K}}$, where $K_1+K_2=K$ means that $K_1(p) + K_2(p)=K(p)$ for all $p\in \mathcal{P}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

