{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.524928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b8e6183656003f60cc2939890a81f347611529e9c34807c22608354bc24859d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr:exponential_decay_general of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] Let $u\in C([0, \infty); \mathcal{X})$ be a strong Markov process with state space $\mathcal{X}$ and natural filtration $\{\mathcal{F}_t\}_{t\in [0, \infty)}$\,. Let $T: C([0, \infty); \mathcal{X}) \rightarrow [0, \infty)$ be a stopping time satisfying the following properties. 
	\begin{enumerate}
	\item There exists some $t_0$ independent of $u[0]$ such that $\mathbb{P}(T < t_0) \leq \frac{1}{10}\, ;$
	\item There exist some Lyapunov functions $V, \Tilde V: \mathcal{X} \rightarrow [0, \infty)$ such that $\Tilde V \leq V$ and
	\begin{equs}

		\mathbb{E} V(u[T\wedge t_0]) &\leq \rho \Tilde V(u[0]) + C_1 \; , \\

		\sup_{a \leq t_0} \mathbb{E} \Tilde{V}(u[T\wedge a]) &\leq C_2 V(u[0]) + C_3\;,
	\end{equs}
	with constants $0 < \rho < 1$ and $C_1, C_2, C_3>0$.
	\end{enumerate}
	Then there exist constants $\gamma = \gamma(t_0, \rho, C_2), C= C(t_0, \rho) > 0$ such that for any $t \geq t_0$\,, we have
	\begin{equ}

		\mathbb{E} \Tilde{V}(u[t]) \leq C C_2 e^{-\gamma t} \Tilde V(u[0]) + C \big(\log C_2 + 1\big) C_1 C_2 + 2C_3\;.
	\end{equ} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

