{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.788535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bc08495c8d15ca258127803bae958c11a366a84f553f6d75973de12b34d5cde","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2609.00183, '2609.00183'] Let $u=(V,v):B_{\sigma}(x)\to (\RR^j\times Y_C^{N-j},d_G)$ be a local representation as in \cite[(16)]{dm} of a harmonic map from Riemannian domain $\Omega \in \RR^n$ into a  $N$-dimensional conical DM-complex $Y_C.$ For $k \in \{0,...,n-2\},$ we define
