{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.152765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bc7509d4a92ac94de39cc0eafa906e3a3740f807105a6afa1bdd08ff5e72b4a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] For arbitrary constants $q_1,q_2,a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$, there exists a function $g\in$  $C^\infty([0,T];\mathbb{R})$ such that
