{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.705971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bddcf10c28cd04dd9ab2de1cbfe905894ce99a7d5121f85493e7e188bd70046","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop dev-anti-conc of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $a_n,b_n = \Theta(n)$, $a_n \leq b_n$ be two sequences. Then, for any $\alpha, \beta \in (1/2,1)$ there exists a constant $C$ depending on $\alpha, \beta,$ and the sequences $a_n,b_n$ such that for all 
