{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.754231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bef88a0c952004e4501d5815af3b744589db125f163f7825f572996d53f2cd0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Maintheorem thm:brw of arXiv:2411.08018, 'Last passage percolation in hierarchical environments'] There exist $c,c'>0$ such that for all sufficiently large $n$, 
