{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.983667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c10803257110d8e63a1d0d756ed48e79d6c6fd305503a5717bd75ebca9a7191","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Planar weighted Gaussian inequalities) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] There exist finite constants $C_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)$ and $\rho_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)>0$, depending only on $(\gamma,Q)$, such that every such measure $\nu$ satisfies
\begin{align}
 \Var_\nu(f)&\le C_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)\int_{\C}|\nabla f|^2\,\D\nu,\\
 \Ent_\nu(f^2)&\le\frac2{\rho_{\rm wt}(\gamma,Q)}\int_{\C}|\nabla f|^2\,\D\nu.
\end{align}
The inequalities hold for every real-valued $f$ in the closed Dirichlet-form domain generated by $C_c^\infty(\C\setminus\{y_j:a_j>0\})$.  The constants are uniform in the number and locations of the points and in the individual exponents, subject only to this total-exponent bound. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.697441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c116315e74fda06eb9c1e0dd9602465681cfc7786dad0e3ce912fa331445aaf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: bub-trunc of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Let $\epsilon > 0$ be fixed. There exists a $C = C(\epsilon) > 0$ such that, uniformly in $M \geq 1$, in all $n \geq 2 M/ \epsilon$, and all $x_1, x_2 \in G(\epsilon, n)$, we have
