{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.381594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c27f5cfeb5fe61a879b4b6ae7e6d3467e34d8d50ce5d07cf13813c498c78acf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def1 of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] A measurable partition $\alpha$ of $\Omega$ is said to be a finite irreducible invariant set partition (with respect to $P$ and $T$) if $\#(\alpha)<\infty$ and  for any $A\in \alpha$, 
