{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.332011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c381023b6f734d5808c4cc029e5c1b916e501669defa1a6987c59ec7e3437e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2506.22083, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for the repulsive log gas in any dimension'] Suppose \cref{ass:potential0,ass:potential} are satisfied. Then, for any $\beta>0$ and $\bar{\rho}\in \cP(\Omega)$ with essentially bounded density there exists some
\[
