\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.013077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c5a9afb0066477ae4d57f7cfece3e9dd23a425d2624e97288907605dd85a310","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:sumoverUh of arXiv:2411.10829, 'Airy$_\beta$ line ensemble and its Laplace transform'] For any $h'\ge 0$, we have
\begin{multline}  
\sum_{\vec r\in\mathscr B^{{h'}}_+}\prod_{j\in J_\mathrm I} \frac{|U|+\vartheta_j\max_t \mathscr{H}(t)}{N} |w(\vec r)|<C\prod_{\ell=1}^m(2\sqrt{NN_\ell})^{k_\ell} N^{-|J| -\frac{1}{3}(|J_\mathrm {VI.2}|+\max\{|J_\mathrm {VI.1}|, |J_\mathrm {VI.3}|\}+|J_\mathrm C|)} \\ \times    \exp(-c{h'}^2)
\prod_{j\in J_\mathrm I} \frac{\vartheta_j^{-1/2} }{N^{1/3}}
\prod_{j\in J_\mathrm {IV},\vartheta_j\ne \varnothing} \frac{\vartheta_j^{-3/2} }{N^{1/3}}
\prod_{j\in J_\mathrm {IV},\vartheta_j=\varnothing} \frac{1}{N^{2/3}}
\prod_{j\in J_\mathrm {III}\cup J_\mathrm {VI.1}\cup J_\mathrm {VI.2}\cup J_\mathrm {VI.3}} \vartheta_j^{-3/2}.
\end{multline}
There is an extra factor of $N^{-1/3}$ or $(y-x)^{-1/2}$ in the right-hand side, under the condition (i) or (ii), respectively, specified in (prop:mbdc2 of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.807671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c62b516cd0a9f9e7e888e1ef98363dc7d11968630a8a5a0226dc9b20a596041","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d.depair of arXiv:2510.07682, 'From tug-of-war to Brownian Boost: \\ explicit ODE solutions for player-funded stochastic-'] Let $\rho \in (0,\infty)$.  A pair of differentiable functions $f,g:\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}} \to (0,\infty)$\hfff{fg} is called a $\rho$-Brownian Boost ODE pair\hfff{bbode} if it satisfies at every point on the real line
\begin{eqnarray}
 2 \rho f^{1+\rho} g^\rho & = & \, \, \, \, \, \, \big( f^{2\rho}- g^{2\rho} \big)f \, + \, \tfrac{1}{2} f' \big(f^\rho + g^\rho \big)^2  \, , \\
 2 \rho f^\rho g^{1+\rho} & = & - \, \big( f^{2\rho}- g^{2\rho} \big)g \, - \, \tfrac{1}{2} g' \big(f^\rho + g^\rho \big)^2 \, . \nonumber
\end{eqnarray}
A pair of functions $f,g:\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}} \to (0,\infty)$ is called {\em default} if $f(0) = 1$ and $g(0) > 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.763932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c6454be73ce29f4ae27087879d94cabd89a67f2a61be222687abc8b8b181006","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l5.1 of arXiv:2411.19255, 'Moderate, large and super large deviations principles for Poisson process with uniform cat'] For any $x,y\in \mathbb{Z}^+$ there exist random processes $\tilde{\xi}(t)$ and $\hat{\xi}(t)$
such that $\tilde{\xi}(t)\stackrel{d}{=}\xi_x(t)$, $\hat{\xi}(t)\stackrel{d}{=}\xi_y(t)$, and the following equality holds
\begin{equation} 
 \mathbf{P}\left(\sup\limits_{t\geq 0}|\tilde{\xi}(t)-\hat{\xi}(t)|\leq|x-y|\right)=1.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.824024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c668b49e63dbfb41e091b4abb61852c4bbcb230bd183d16ace62a4117c80535","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:farey-sixth-order of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] For each integer $N\geq1$, let $\mathrm{FV}(N)$ be the number of distinct
intersections of Farey lines of order $(N,N)$, and let $\mathrm{FR}(N)$ be
the number of connected regions into which those lines cut the open unit
square.  Then, as $N\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathrm{FV}(N)=\Theta(N^6),\qquad
