\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.881623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c69fffe1942dac92912566ca7486d6a7c46dadc2e841f03ae56c37efeb24eb8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2506.11707, 'Fluctuations of two-dimensional determinantal processes associated with Berezin--Toeplitz '] Given smooth functions $a, b : \C \to \R$, one has, in operator norm
