{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.962101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c91ea8f2266665d9cf8ef7b83f5a9ae7186bd4d64b72af07e322d13045d1de4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2605.28776, 'Limiting distributions of triangle counts in linear preferential attachment models'] For $m\ge 2$ and $\delta>-m$, let $\beta:=(m+\delta)/(2m+\delta)$. Then for all $t\ge 1, k\ge 1$ we have
 \begin{align*}
