{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.045194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ca98ba3455b7ae70fdf205b3f67e5639b2849913968bd93f9d9475b3cc0b804","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:codim-one of arXiv:2608.30700, 'Convex hulls and area minimizing currents in asymptotically locally hyperbolic manifolds'] In the setting of Theorem (thm:asymptotic-plateau of the paper), assume further that $p=n$. Write $\Reg T$ for the regular part of $\spt T$ and $\Sing T:=\spt T\setminus\Reg T$. Then $\Reg T$ is a smooth embedded minimal hypersurface, and the multiplicity is a locally constant positive integer on each connected component of $\Reg T$. Furthermore,
