{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.033281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cb4157ecc4ad907c680fb01fb267270eee4cf031bc0f12feb51109912174533","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6tmodp2 of arXiv:2609.03926, 'Overcolored Partition $k$-tuples Restricted by Parity of the Parts'] For prime $p$, integers  $n\ge0$, $r,s,\ell, k\ge1$ and $j$ such that $1\le j<p$, we have 
