{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.894739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cb76e425f5837bb9adab74a24bdf69297581192af1cd03d3910fe71cc378807","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm thm:ape of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let $(M,g)$ be a compact Riemannian manifold of dimension $n\ge 2$. Let $0< \eta_\ell\le \ell$ be two real sequences such that $\exists\lim_{\ell\to +\infty} \ell^{-1}\eta_\ell =1-\alpha $. Then, if $\alpha<1$, 
\begin{equation} 
{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left( Y_M([\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell])\right)=\Theta\left( \ell^{-n}\right)
\end{equation}
If $\alpha=1$ and $\liminf_{\ell\to +\infty} \eta_\ell =+\infty$, 
\begin{equation} 
 {\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left( Y_M([\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell])\right)\le
 \mathrm{O}(\ell^{-n})\left( a(\ell)+\frac{\ell}{\eta_\ell^2}\right),
\end{equation}
If $\alpha=1$ and $(M,g)$ has no conjugate points,
\begin{equation} 
{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left( Y_M([\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell])\right)\le \mathrm{O}(\ell^{-n})\left( a(\ell)+\frac{\ell}{\eta_\ell^2\log\ell}\right),
\end{equation}
In all above cases, $\varepsilon_\ell\to 0$ and Weyl law ((eq:weyllaw_interval of the paper)) is sharp:
\begin{equation} 
N^M_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}=\Theta(\ell^{n-1}\eta_\ell).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.207248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cbbb34c1d1d4970e57b568e9a0a14f5d616de16e94855724342f85583910a78","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Adjoint-Weight of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] For a weighted simplicial complex $(K,\mu)$ where $N_{\mu}$ is finite, there exists a  weighted simplicial complex $(K,\mu^*)$
 of opposite type such that
 \begin{equation} 
