{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.748514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ce23726043459c59e0c78b9ded5384861af175b6e9ed2e3a026d12d647e259c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Multiplicative heat flow and the asymptotic distribution of zeros) of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] Let $(P_n(z))_{n\in \N}$ be a sequence of polynomials  such that $\deg P_n = n$ for all $n\in\N$.
