{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.639774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d021521576f6bb9da8d9099346529ee0a8dcc36a317f0a2e5ef2bd3d7c015ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Degenerate existence with non-sticking boundary behavior) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let $x_0\in\Cc$. Assume \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma}, \ref{ass:k:dom}, \ref{ass:face:sign}, and \ref{ass:nonsticky}. Then there exists a filtered probability space carrying an $N$-dimensional Brownian motion $B$ and a continuous $\Cc$-valued semimartingale $X=(X_1,\ldots,X_N)$, defined up to its lifetime $\life{X}>0$, such that $X(0)=x_0$ and, for every $t\in[0,\life{X})$,
