{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.301456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d08b80e8c74694a2b918c12ee8b31f3edf1d82bb04e9470f5eee9d48d289414","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2604.22130, 'Reflected Stochastic Differential Equations Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Nonlinear C'] We call a sublinear expectation $\hat{\mathbb{E}}:L_{ip}(\Omega_T)\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ a $G$-expectation if the canonical process $G$ is a $G$-Brownian motion under $\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\cdot]$, i.e., for each $0\leq s\leq t\leq T$, the increment $B_t-B_s\sim \mathcal{N}(0,[(t-s)\underline{\sigma}^2,(t-s)\bar{\sigma}^2])$ and for all $n>0$, $0\leq t_1\leq \cdots\leq t_n\leq T$ and $\varphi\in C_{l,Lip}(\mathbb{R}^n)$,
\begin{align*}
\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\varphi(B_{t_1},\cdots,B_{t_n-1},B_{t_n}-B_{t_n-1})]=\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\psi(B_{t_1},\cdots,B_{t_n-1})],
\end{align*}
where $\psi(x_1,\cdots,x_{n-1})=\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\varphi(x_{t_1},\cdots,x_{t_n-1},B_{t_n}-B_{t_n-1})]$.  The triple $(\Omega,L_{ip}(\Omega_T),\hat{\mathbb{E}})$ is called the $G$-expectation space.","status":"unverified"}

