{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.731869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d0aadf7ac8bdcc958eab4dc284e4f1d1d868699ef5aa17c3e078d3ccbf24b77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop linearEmpiricalFluctuationCLT of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Assume the hypotheses of (thm:partitionFunctionBound of the paper), including (equation eq:logRateExtraAssumptions of the paper) when $\mathsf{s}=0$.  Fix $\beta\ge0$ and real-valued functions $\phi_1,\ldots,\phi_k\in L^2(\mu)$.
