{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.065438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d0f4031d2f3dc264f4595187b37f6cfbebe44dde61c006f0256729df213d589","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2606.00648, 'Asymptotic estimates for multiple point ranges of transient random walks on graphs'] If $(U_0)$ holds, then, for every $j \ge 1$, 
\begin{align*} 
