{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.734098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d1103a94bb0c8159528f1193469c07dedc269cddf007fec864f8c6387a12993","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Let $\mathcal{M}_E$ denote the collection of probability measures on $\mathbf{S}_N$ that are symmetric in $e_1$, and define two functions:
    \begin{align*}
        d(t) &= \max_{\mu \in \mathcal{M}_E } d_{\textsc{tv}} (P^t_{\mu}, \pi ) 
        \\
