{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.475972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d12f0d3d8b0da7c9a820e67cf488ca15710d5b1b8d3279d807a7e438cdcc679","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 75 (Evaluated tail--defect stability below the Hilbert endpoint) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $1\le r<2$, put $\theta_r:=1/r-1/2$, and retain the block
projections and effective ranks $d_{\lambda,\mu}$ from
Theorem~\ref{thm:below-Hilbert}.  Let
$K_{N;\lambda,\mu}\in
 \mathfrak W_{m,2}(\cH_{\R};Q_\mu\cC,P_\lambda\cE)$ be realized over
one common isonormal Gaussian process.  Suppose that there is
$M=(M_{\lambda,\mu})\in\ell^r(\Lambda\times\cM)$ such that
\begin{equation}

 d_{\lambda,\mu}^{\theta_r}
 \Prof_{m,2}(K_{N;\lambda,\mu})\le M_{\lambda,\mu}
 \qquad(N\ge1).
\end{equation}
Let $(F_R)_{R\ge1}$ be an increasing finite exhaustion of
$\Lambda\times\cM$, and assume that $\delta(N)\to0$ and
\begin{equation}

 \left\{\sum_{(\lambda,\mu)\in F_R}
 \left[d_{\lambda,\mu}^{\theta_r}
 \Prof_{m,2}(K_{N;\lambda,\mu}-K_{N';\lambda,\mu})\right]^r
 \right\}^{1/r}
 \le \delta(N)G(R),
 \qquad N'\ge N.
\end{equation}
Set
\[
 \tau_r(R):=
 \norm{M\mathbf1_{(\Lambda\times\cM)\setminus F_R}}_{\ell^r}.
\]
Then the evaluated reconstructions
\[
 T_N:=\sum_{\lambda,\mu}I_m(K_{N;\lambda,\mu})
\]
are Cauchy in $L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)$ for every $1\le p<\infty$, and,
with $p_*:=\max\{p,r\}$,
\begin{equation}

 \norm{T_N-T_{N'}}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \le A_m(p_*+2)^{m/2}
 \inf_{R\ge1}\{\delta(N)G(R)+2\tau_r(R)\},
 \qquad N'\ge N.
\end{equation}
The same estimate holds for the limit $T$ in place of $T_{N'}$.
If, for some $\theta_0,\sigma>0$ and $A\ge0$,
\[
 \delta(N)\lesssim N^{-\theta_0},\qquad
 G(R)\lesssim R^A,
\]
then
\begin{align}
 \tau_r(R)\lesssim R^{-\sigma}
 &\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \norm{T_N-T}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \lesssim (p_*+2)^{m/2}
 N^{-\theta_0\sigma/(A+\sigma)},
 \\
 \tau_r(R)\lesssim \ell_R^{-\sigma}
 &\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \norm{T_N-T}_{L^p(\Omega;\Sch_r)}
 \lesssim (p_*+2)^{m/2}\ell_N^{-\sigma}.

\end{align}
The conclusions remain valid for fixed finite-overlap colorings, with
the right-hand sides multiplied by
$(\chi_+\chi_-)^{1-1/r}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.846713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d18a2b30024bc58a778b1bd914ec1dd14ea4b023b2dc7cdea2774924ae05b0d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Wicksformula of arXiv:2510.01021, '\Large Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities\relatedv'] Let $g_1,\dots,g_n$ be iid $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$ random variables and let $u:[2p]\to[n]$ then
