{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.200612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d195f8c73751c3747a7af5387e4ca8cc530120407970189662846abfff0e277","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation given by \eqref{eq NS},\eqref{eq xi} and any $B_0,\gamma,\alpha>0$, there exists $N\in\N^+$ such that if the sequence $\{b_j\}_{j\in\N^+}$ satisfies
