{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.206656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d1f680d96e169982d0f76ad852f9ee8ca934aa6d09e30a38a663253750640a1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi Equ:Weight-cond of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] A simplex $\sigma$ in a weighted simplicial complex $(K,\mu)$ is called \emph{divisibly weighted} if all the vertices of $\sigma$ can be ordered as
 $\{v_0,\cdots, v_k\}$ such that
   \begin{equation} 
     \mu(v_0)\, |\, \cdots\, | \, \mu(v_k).
   \end{equation}
  If all the simplices in $(K,\mu)$ are divisibly weighted, 
  the weight function $\mu$ is called \emph{divisible}
  and $(K,\mu)$ is called a \emph{divisibly weighted simplicial complex}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.959082+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d242af129abdeb54312ba6a42d12d2f9e0b85bf2e62ccdbbb2736530176579b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2412.05764, 'A method of solution for the inverse problem for $h$-functions of planar Brownian motion'] The periodic Hilbert transform takes the form
