{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.142909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d42e1acdadae239236779561a121ca3776358b5243dc6b33ad5676a2cd69218","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:guerra-interpolation of arXiv:2605.03718, 'Potential Hessian Ascent III:\\ Sampling the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick Model at $\beta < 1/'] Let $\{H_0(\sigma)\}_{\sigma \in \Sigma}$ and $\{H_1(\sigma)\}_{\sigma \in \Sigma}$ be two independent Gaussian processes. Then, the Guerra-interpolated Gaussian process $\{H_t(\sigma)\}_{\sigma \in \Sigma}$ is given as
