{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.110386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d43caf15769b9e7f9e22ca19dd736295d721ae330d39e8bb5f6869303683c03","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma unregu of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] For any $g\in{\rm Lip}(1)$ and let $f_{g}$ be the solution to equation (equation stablestein of the paper), then for any $y\in(-\infty,\infty)$, we have
