{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.033018+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d43d0fe671685aca03a64c4202a169753a06d301b281a2bc36a5efee7c5f1ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem uno of arXiv:2512.17727, 'Stochastic transport equation with L\'evy noise'] Assume that  $\alpha \in [1,2)$ and $\beta \in (0,1)$  satisfy condition
(equation eqn-beta+alpha half of the paper). Assume that $b\in C_{\mathrm{b}}^{\beta}(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{R}^d)$.
Assume that   $L = (L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is a L\'evy  process  satisfying \textbf{(H)} and \textbf{(R)} in Hypothesis (hyp-nondeg1 of the paper).
Then the global existence and the pathwise uniqueness hold for Problem      (equation eqn-SDE of the paper)-(equation eqn-SDE-IC of the paper). \\
 Moreover, if $X^x = (X_t^x)_{t\geq 0}$,  $x \in\mathbb{R}^{d}$, denotes
   the unique solution of Problem (equation eqn-SDE of the paper)-(equation eqn-SDE-IC of the paper) with $s=0$, then the following conditions are satisfied:

