{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.978540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d4f5bcf9bb2d24fcdb41f99bff46d1724b7e8a86edf011013ccfe6993195d5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 (No nonzero finite-level primitive) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] For every Hilbert space $H$ and every $q\ge2$,
