{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.956833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d6c992578e68e09530a2dd0c5f1d834f1242ac7f2b8d1f9428464ecec19b663","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:near-fittest-path of arXiv:2508.12464, 'On the Fitness Landscape in the $\NK$ Model'] Let $n\geq 10$ and $\eta\in (0,1)$. For any $\alpha$ with
\begin{align}
    0<\alpha<\frac{\eta}{5\sqrt{2\ln 2}},
\end{align}
there exists some $N_0$ depending on $\eta,\alpha$ such that for any $N\geq N_0,$ with probability at least $1-\omega e^{-\eta^2N/(n^2\omega)}$, whenever $\check\sigma$ and $\hat\sigma$ satisfy
\begin{align}
		\min\Bigl(\frac{H_{N,K}(\hat \sigma)}{N},\frac{H_{N,K}(\check \sigma)}{N}\Bigr)\geq M_{N,K}-\eta,
	\end{align}
we have that
	\begin{align}
		\nonumber   \min_{0\leq l\leq n-1} Q(\sigma^{(l)},\sigma^{(l+1)})&\geq 1-C\Bigl(\frac{1}{n}+\eta\Bigr),\\
		 \min_{0\leq l\leq n-1} R(\sigma^{(l)},\sigma^{(l+1)})&\geq 1-\frac{C}{n},\\

        \min_{1\leq l\leq n-1}\frac{H_{N,K}(\sigma^{(l)})}{N}&\geq M_{N,K}-Cn\eta.
	\end{align}
    Here, $\omega>0$ and $C>0$ are absolute constants independent of all other variables. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.783689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d6dba1c252ffa16db84daa197135287acb0629a90ae873bda3aba29222ee159","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 26 (Total-variation principle for dissipated-energy Einstein--Navier--Stokes flows) of arXiv:2608.31171, '\bf Finite-energy spacetimes with torus symmetry. \\ \Large Cauchy stability of Einstein--'] Under the conditions in \autoref{proposition-JJJ-NS}, the following total variation bound holds for sufficiently regular solutions: 
