{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.065534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d700fdbbeeb0436d8d60eba917c63fd25549c17858bda3bc631a049551278d0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Defintition_operator of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] We denote by $A$ the diagonal operator with Fourier symbol $-\lvert m\rvert^2 g(|m|)$, namely 
