{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.486957+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d710f63735033bfe0dd4e552c528320306344b3cca5a3c771a5639ca02dd3b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 86 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] For $n\geq 1$ odd,
the Wick power $:\Phi^{n}:$ can be decomposed
\begin{displaymath}
:\Phi^{n}:~= 
\sum_{m=0}^{+\infty}
\sum_{j=0}^{+\infty}
\Big(
\sigma_{m,j}
\sum_{0\leq k< \lfloor n/2\rfloor}
(-1)^{k} \dfrac{n!}{2^{k} k! (n-2k)!}
V_{A^{\rm gen}_{m}}^{k}\psi_{n-2k,m,j}
\Big),
\end{displaymath}
and 
\begin{displaymath}
\E\big[\big\Vert :\Phi^{n}:\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\big]~= 
\sum_{m=0}^{+\infty}
\sum_{j=0}^{+\infty}
\E\Big[\Big\Vert
\sum_{0\leq k< \lfloor n/2\rfloor}
(-1)^{k} \dfrac{n!}{2^{k} k! (n-2k)!}
V_{A^{\rm gen}_{m}}^{k}\psi_{n-2k,m,j}
\Big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}
\Big],
\end{displaymath}
for every $\eta>0$.
For $n\geq 2$ even,
the Wick power $:\Phi^{n}:$ can be decomposed
\begin{multline*}
:\Phi^{n}:~= 
\sum_{m=0}^{+\infty}
\sum_{j=0}^{+\infty}
\Big(
\Big(
\sum_{0\leq k< \lfloor n/2\rfloor}
(-1)^{k} \dfrac{n!}{2^{k} k! (n-2k)!}
V_{A^{\rm gen}_{m}}^{k}\psi_{n-2k,j}
\Big)
\\
+
\ind_{\inter(\Gamma_{m,j})}
(-1)^{n/2} \dfrac{n!}{2^{n/2} (n/2)! }
(V_{A^{\rm gen}_{m}}^{n/2} - V_{A^{\rm gen, +}_{m-1}}^{n/2})
\Big),
\end{multline*}
with the convention that for $m=0$, 
$V_{A^{\rm gen, +}_{-1}} = 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.142872+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d73799a075bed7c7ed3c07a414d9c8ba1c5c3c57150bf12334f414a57355e71","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2604.05910, '\textbf{Well-posedness and Hurst parameter estimation for fluid equations driven by fracti'] {\em(Young integral)}
    Let  $\xi\in\mathcal{Y}$. Then 
     there exists a map $\mathcal{I}: \mathcal{Y} \to C([0,T];\cB_\delta)\cap C^\gamma([0,T];\cB_{\delta-\gamma}) $ such that $\mathcal{I}_0=0$ which satisfies for every $0\leq s \leq t\leq T$ and $0\leq \theta<2\gamma$ the estimate:
    \begin{align} 
    \| (\delta^S \mathcal{I}(\xi))_{s,t} - S_{t-s}\xi_{s,t}\|_{\delta-\gamma+\theta} \lesssim [W^H]_\gamma \|\xi\|_{\mathcal{Y}} |t-s|^{2\gamma-\theta}.
    \end{align}
    In particular, the convolution 
   \begin{align*}
      \mathcal{I}_t(\xi) := \lim\limits_{\pi\in\cP([0,t]),|\pi|\to 0} \sum\limits_{[u,v]\in\pi} S_{t-u}\xi_{u,v} 
   \end{align*}
   exists in $\cB_{\delta-\gamma}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.947891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d771cc7c8b4b1d98f04eccaffcf987ed5a8b33046167e487f5c31b519feb5f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:geometry of arXiv:2608.30254, 'Exact Recovery Thresholds for Weighted Data Selection\\ in Vector-Valued Linear Regression'] $W^\circ=W^\circ P_T$; the first-order condition
$\sum_{i=1}^NM_i=0$ holds; and for every $H\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times d}$,
\begin{equation}
  L_D(W^\circ+H)=L^{\star}_{D}+\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N\lVert Hx_i\rVert^2 .
\end{equation}
Consequently the full-data minimizer set is
$\{W^\circ+H: HP_T=0\}$; if $T=\mathbb{R}^d$ the minimizer is unique.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.424330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d783b6a3db92659a0bf5aa7cd8b293435c17fee54b4c96fd82d05c93d0243b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 153 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider a discrete ensemble satisfying Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, \ref{Assumptions_basic}, \ref{Assumptions_offcrit}, \ref{Assumptions_analyticity} and suppose that the equilibrium measure has no saturations. Let $\eps>0$ be small enough, so that the $\eps$-neighborhoods of the bands are pairwise disjoint. Let $L \in \amsmathbb{Z}_{> 0}$ and a $L$-tuple of integers $\boldsymbol{k} \in [H]^{L}$ both independent of $\N$, let a (possibly $\N$-dependent) $L$-tuple of functions $\boldsymbol{f}(z)$ such that $f_l(z)$ is a holomorphic function of $z$ in a $\N$-independent complex neighborhood of $[\alpha_{k_l}-\eps,\beta_{k_l}+\eps]$ for any $l \in [L]$. Assume there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that $\max_{l} \sup_{z} |f_l(z)| \leq C$.

 Let $\textnormal{\textsf{\textbf{Gau\ss{}}}}[\boldsymbol{f}]$ be a $L$-dimensional random Gaussian vector with covariance
 \begin{equation}

\textnormal{\textsf{Cov}}_{l_1,l_2}[\boldsymbol{f},\boldsymbol{f}] = \oint_{\gamma_{k_{l_1}}} \oint_{\gamma_{k_{l_2}}}
 f_{l_1}(z_1) f_{l_2}(z_2)\,\mathcal{F}_{k_{l_1},k_{l_2}}(z_1,z_2)\,\frac{\dd z_1 \dd z_2}{(2\ii\pi)^2},
