{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.251026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d89d2d9077b369650c2d917cb96f133f17a746124526549677eed16c8dd9328","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_mu_stir_pi_alpha of arXiv:2412.09532, 'Percolation on the stationary distributions of the voter model with stirring'] Let~$\Lambda \subset \mathbb{Z}^d$ be finite and~$E,F \in \mathcal G_\Lambda$ be an increasing and a decreasing event, respectively. In the space of the graphical construction, we consider an~$\mathcal F_t$-measurable random configuration~$\eta \in \{0,1\}^\Lambda$ with the property that the coalescing random walks started at~$\{x \in \Lambda: \eta(x) = 0\}$ do not coalesce until time~$t$. Then for any~$\alpha \in (0,1)$ and~$\mathsf v \ge 0$
    \begin{align*}
        & \mu_{\alpha,\mathsf v}(E) \leq \mathbb{E} \Big[ \pi_\alpha(\zeta: \zeta \vee \eta \in E) \cdot \prod_{ \substack{ x,y \in \Lambda \setminus \Xi \\ x< y} } \big( 1+ h(Y^x_t,Y^y_t) \cdot (\widehat{\alpha}^{-2}-1) \big) \Big], \\[0.2cm]
