{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.987386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d9f9480dc33f9c7fe3bfaf9834cc7faefdfa40d32b9dc18363804f10635697a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:4.1 of arXiv:2608.27474, 'Nonlocality of Cover-Time Changes Under Edge Addition'] Let \(H_s^\lambda(S)\) be the \(G_\lambda\) hitting time of \(S\). Then

\begin{equation}
\boxed{
H_s^\lambda(S)-H_s^0(S)
