{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5db45ff6a6cffb324492836e30dfc9882c46cebc1173fa0cad992b809e906e16","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:conc_density of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Let $(X_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be an ergodic diffusion with invariant measure $\mu$, let
$\overline{\rho}_t(V)$ denote the empirical density according to Definition~(def:empirical_density of the paper) with 
ergodic (time-independent) mean $\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t]$, and
let $\nu \ll \mu$ with $\mathrm{d}\nu/\mathrm{d}\mu \in L^2(\mu)$. 
Then for all $t > 0$ and
$a > 0$,
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\overline{\rho}_t(V) - \E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] \geq a\right)
  \leq
  \left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
  \exp\bigl[-t I^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] + a)\bigr],

\end{align}
where the Cram\'er transform
\begin{align}
I^\rho(s) \equiv \sup_{k \in \mathbb{R}}\bigl[k s - \Lambda^\rho(k)\bigr],

\end{align}
is defined as the Legendre conjugate of the principal eigenvalue $\Lambda^\rho(k)$~(equation eq:Lambda_rho_dirichlet of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.521055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5db9011fc3c7be7ea09c7a892c0bf39479b3ba160dabdfdc10dca534a48cf9c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:large_t of arXiv:2512.17808, 'Zeros of polynomial powers under the heat flow'] For any polynomial $P$ and any $C>0$, there exists a (large) $t_0>0$ such that for all $t>t_0$ the following holds. For all $z\in D:=\{z\in\mathcal D_t: |z|<C\sqrt t,|z\pm 2\sqrt t|>2t^{1/3}\}$, the maximally relevant saddle point $u_t^*(z)$ is well defined and satisfies either
\begin{align*}
\Bigg\lvert\frac{u_t^*(z)}{u_t^+(z)}-1\Bigg\rvert<t^{-1/6}\qquad \text{or}\qquad \Bigg\lvert\frac{u_t^*(z)}{u_t^-(z)}-1\Bigg\rvert<t^{-1/6}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.874128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5db9c3092921050ba5862c9f48d1587090389df261f9cc84e3a206b5333f3ae4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 40 (Coefficient-map transfer) of arXiv:2607.16724, 'Algebraic Transfer for Operator-Valued Gaussian Chaoses: Oriented Schatten Profiles and Si'] Assume $\kappa_r(\Phi)<\infty$ and that $\Phi$ maps finite-rank operators to
