{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.146081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5dc8f092aac1de30e1c207f287115d86388d6570b0c44d9973677e57f8a68d69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollaryatthebeginning of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] Let $ \mu_{k,n}$, with $k,n\geq 1$ be centered probability measures with uniformly bounded supports, such that 
