{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.787676+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5dcc981c34c115c58fe0fc3adf3a5a98614d9d99639b0881381af966d0872d62","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 50 (Fractional Sobolev spaces) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For $s\geqs0$, the \emph{fractional Sobolev space} $H^s(\Lambda)$ is the 
space of functions $f\in \H = L^2(\Lambda)$ such that 
