    \end{align*}
    for every $ \varphi \in c_{ 00 } ( \mathbb N^M) $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:17.749158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5df24266bb5dab0710158080d88ab774f58373082dee86bfdcea822abe0f403f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 (Repeated action of $x\partial_x + b$ and the asymptotic distribution of zeros) of arXiv:2511.01456, 'Zero distribution of multiplicative Hermite and Laguerre polynomials'] Let $(P_n(x))_{n\in \N}$ be a sequence of polynomials  such that $\deg P_n = n$ for all $n\in\N$. Let also $(b_n)_{n\in \N}\subseteq \C$ and $(c_n)_{n\in \N}\subseteq \N$ be sequences such that $b_n/n\to \beta$ and $c_n/n \to \gamma$ as $n\to\infty$, where $\beta\in \C$ and $\gamma>0$ are constants.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] The positive case: If each $P_n$ has only zeros in $[0,\infty)$ and $\llbracket  P_n \rrbracket_n$ converges  to some probability measure $\rho$ weakly on $[0,\infty)$, and if $b_n\in \R\backslash[-n,0]$ for every $n\in \N$ and $\beta \in \R \backslash [-1,0]$,  then   $\llbracket (x \partial_x + b_n)^{c_n} P_n(x)\rrbracket_n$ converges  to $\rho \boxtimes \nu_{\beta, \gamma}$ weakly on $[0,\infty)$. Here, $\boxtimes$ denotes the free multiplicative convolution of probability measures on $[0,\infty)$.
\item[(b)] The unitary case: If each $P_n$ has only zeros on the unit circle  $\{|z|=1\}$ and $\llbracket  P_n \rrbracket_n$ converges weakly to some probability measure  $\rho$ on $\{|z| = 1\}$,  and if $\Re b_n = -n/2$ for every $n\in \N$ (implying $\Re \beta = -1/2$), then   $\llbracket (x \partial_x + b_n)^{c_n}  P_n(x) \rrbracket_n$ converges weakly to $\rho \boxtimes \nu_{\beta, \gamma}$. Here, $\boxtimes$ denotes the free multiplicative convolution of probability measures on the unit circle.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.585493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5dfdc251acd3b0032cd43449d9cd194a5660a88bfacce78f9415d2f746c1504b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.05679, 'Small ball probabilities and Chung's law of the iterated logarithm for Gaussian Volterra p'] Assume that Condition \eqref{eq constant cond} holds. There exists a constant $K_{5,2}$ such that for all $\varepsilon \in \left(0, 2/K_{5,1}\right)$ and  $\theta >\varepsilon / 2 $,
