{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.834539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e10c52e08409cd822361cc1f17ac53a520d22c9989639c1a7158b8780717770","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2604.10820, 'A Strict Gap Between Relaxed and Partition-Constrained\\ Spectral Compression in a Six-Sta'] If $T$ is positive self-adjoint with eigenvalues
