{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.893384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e13843080b69afc3bb10564274b11d9e49929688b8aa2902c32390681334a36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sources of arXiv:2606.30475, 'Ancestries in random $d$-DAGs'] For $M>0$, denote by $Z_M$ the number of sources (that is, vertices with in-degree 0 in $G_n$) among the first $\floor{Mn^{d/(d+1)}}$ vertices. As $n\to\infty$, we have
 \begin{equation}
  Z_M\stackrel{\mathrm{d}}{\longrightarrow} \mathsf{Poi}\left(\frac{M^{d+1}}{d+1}\right),
 \end{equation}
 with convergence of all moments. In particular, the threshold for source nodes in $G_n$ is $n^{d/(d+1)}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.384672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e13f66e80cc9bcbb095f2b0b1614130de8603fbaa7b2807ae40cb0498fbe274","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.03248, 'Connections between colored restricted $b$-ary and ordinary partitions'] Let $\lambda_1=\dots=\lambda_\rho$ in \eqref{3.10}. Then the following hold:
