{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.862854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e13fca04a3a91fd6b6307b3296a001a7603d14659671fd5ce87ec763c405748","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.16502, 'Asymptotic Behavior of Path Functionals for Vector-Valued Gaussian Processes at High Level'] Let \( \bm{W}(t), \ t \in E \) be a continuous stochastic process, \( G : \R^d
  \to \R \) a Borel function bounded on compacta and \( \mu \) a finite measure on
