{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.706025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e1f5b8dafe9f9809009189290b2c1478f6640aafe6b71a4ef5c3f397a96d0b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cert of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Under (eq:fibres of the paper), the following are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item $k(C)/k(u)$ is Galois with cyclic Galois group.
\item There are integers $l_1,\dots,l_r$ with $\gcd(n,l_j)=d_j$ for all $j$ and $\gcd(n,l_1+\dots+l_r)=d_\infty$ such that

\begin{equation}
D=\frac1n\Div\Bigl(\prod_{j=1}^{r}(u-a_j)^{l_j}\Bigr)
\end{equation}

is principal.
\end{enumerate}
When (ii) holds and $v$ spans $L(-D)$, there is $c\in k^\times$ with

\[
v^n=c\prod_{j=1}^r(u-a_j)^{l_j},\qquad k(C)=k(u,v).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.249254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e1fb9bbdb89f80be746097cc9483b76f6feb9a76012ac2ed76fc6a42829cdf4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:egu of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space, and $X:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ a variable.
  Then the \emph{upper game-theoretic expectation of $X$}, with respect to $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$, is given by the following equivalent definitions (see Proposition~(prop:egu-equiv-defs of the paper)).
  \begin{align}
    \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X
    &:= \inf_{Z\in\mathcal{Z}} \sup_{\omega\in\Omega} X(\omega) - Z(\omega)

    \\
    &\phantom{:}= \inf\{\alpha\in\mathbb{R} \mid \exists Z\in\mathcal{Z} \text{ s.t. } Z + \alpha > X\}~.

  \end{align}
  We define the \emph{lower game-theoretic expectation of $X$}, with respect to $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ by $\underline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X := - \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}}(-X)$.
  When $\overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X = \underline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X$, we write $\textsf{\textbf{E}} X := \overline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X = \underline{\textsf{\textbf{E}}} X$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.627903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e233af6eddd29abe2195de02bf360ed4612aaa27da30d615b7393d96770a92e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:upper_lower_general of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\bm{X}$ be in the domain of non-normal attraction of an $\alpha$-stable process $\bm{Z}$.\\ 
{\normalfont(a)} Let $\alpha\in(0,2)\setminus\{1\}$ and Assumption~(\nameref{asm:C}) hold for some $\delta>0$ and $p\ne\alpha-1$. Suppose $G$ is $C^1$ with derivative $\widetilde{G}(t)/t$, where $|\widetilde{G}|\in\mbox{SV}_0$. Further suppose there exists some $\phi\in\mbox{SV}_0\cap\mbox{SV}_\infty$ satisfying $\phi(x)\geqslant\sup_{t>0,y\in[x\wedge 1,x\vee1]}\widetilde{G}(yt)/\widetilde{G}(t)$ for $x>0$. Define $L(t)\coloneqq |\widetilde{G}(t)|/G(t)$, then, for any $q\in(0,1]\cap(0,\alpha)\setminus\{\alpha/(p+1),\alpha/(\alpha\delta+1)\}$ with $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^q]<\infty$, we have $\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^t,\bm{Z})=\mathcal{O}(L(t)^q)$ as $t \downarrow 0$ and
\begin{align*}
    \max\{\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^t_1,\bm{Z}_1)
    ,\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^{2t}_1,\bm{Z}_1)\}
    \geqslant \frac{q\log 2}{3}\mathds{E}\big[|\bm{Z}_1|^q\big]\cdot L(t),
    \quad \text{for all sufficiently small }t >0.
\end{align*}
{\normalfont(b)} Define iteratively the functions $\ell_1(t)=\log(e+t)$ and $\ell_{n+1}(t)=\log(e+\ell_n(t))$ for $t\geqslant 0$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$. Suppose $G(t)$ is eventually equal to $\ell_n(1/t)^{q_n}\cdots\ell_m(1/t)^{q_m}$ where $1\leqslant n\leqslant m$ in $\mathbb{N}$ and either $q_n,\ldots,q_m\geqslant 0$ with $q_n,q_m>0$ or $q_n,\ldots,q_m\leqslant 0$ with $q_n,q_m<0$. Then $G$ satisfies the assumptions of Part (a). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

