{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.732600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e42d87244c276cfcd2a16bed562f39cd4ad0d7b6b858cf3db2cba0f29f18aef","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 90 (Uniqueness on successive time intervals) of arXiv:2607.10813, '2607.10813'] Let $\Xi$ satisfy Definition~\ref{def:Xi-assumptions}, and let $Z,\widetilde Z\in\mathcal Z_T$ be two
