{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.770255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e47ff9fab5556448dc61ea40884acab46ea61208f95b8943c758b2801e6c451","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz thm:powers-bernoulli of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d,k\in\mathds{N}$, $s,\alpha,\beta,\gamma\in\mathds{R}$, $p,q\in (0,\infty]$, $r\in (0,\infty)$, and $\mu,\nu \in (-\infty,0]$.
Assume that $a$ follows a Besov--Bernoulli{} prior and $f$ follows a Besov--Bernoulli{} prior, both with parameters $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\mu,\nu,k)$ and template random variable $X$, satisfying
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases} \:\exists\: \eps>0:\,\mathds{E}\bigl[\left\lvertX\right\rvert^{(1+\eps)\max\left\{r,p\right\}}\bigr]< \infty&\text{if }p\in (0,\infty),\\
\:\exists\:  R>0:\, \left\lvertX\right\rvert\stackrel{a.s.}{\leq}R&\text{if }p=\infty.\end{cases}
\end{equation}
If Property A'' is satisfied, then $\mathds{E}[\left\lVerta\right\rVert_{b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)}^r]<\infty$.
If Properties A'' and B are satisfied, then $\mathds{E}[\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)}^r]<\infty$.
In particular, $f$ belongs to $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)$ almost surely.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.983242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e4819ecc778fca2f8c809ff33a19c9787a26d74a3ecf41a39123c7cfaefdd86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_8 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $\lambda_1,\cdots, \lambda_k$ be as in ((poloi_1 of the paper)). If
