{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:17.696678+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e50eccd4faf683f2f7276b2aa8ef30c98ce22695b798479e8cbff2aa1c4db60","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor: cycle-negl of arXiv:2604.08462, 'Convergence of $k$-point functions in\\ high dimensional percolation'] Suppose $S$ is an undirected graph with $k+1$ leaves. We assume $S$ contains a cycle
\[\gamma= (u_0=u,u_1,\ldots,u_\ell,u_{\ell+1}=u_0)\]
