{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.058808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e564b6d33fce67b850c598c08d4cf3fa1eab06f919f05bb95cb5e883040728d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Robust2 of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Suppose $p=2q$ for some integer $q\geq 2$ and $(a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n)\in \mathbb{R}^n$ satisfies $\sum_ka_k^2=1$. Furthermore, suppose $X$ is a symmetric random variable and $X_1, X_2, \ldots, X_n$ are iid copies of $X$. Let $r_k=r_k(X)$. Then $S=\sum_ka_kX_k$ satisfies the following bounds.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $(r_k)$ is log-concave, then $r_1^2-r_2\geq 0$ and
\begin{align*}
\| S \|_p^p\leq \gamma_p^p\| S \|_2^p-2^q\gamma_p^pr_1^{q-2}(r_1^2-r_2)\Delta_q(a);
\end{align*} 

\item If $(r_k)$ is log-convex, then $r_2-r_1^2\geq 0$ and
\begin{align*}
\| S \|_p^p\geq \gamma_p^p\| S \|_2^p+2^q\gamma_p^pr_1^{q-2}(r_2-r_1^2)\Delta_q(a).
\end{align*} 
\end{enumerate} Moreover, the constants are asymptotically sharp near the Gaussian extremizer. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

