{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.629214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e72112b553ca116b46f74917844a90297343343e46b6e61ffc772cb8bf3cc8c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 10 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] We define the function $\I : \R \times \R \to \R \cup \left\{ \infty \right\} $ given by 
\begin{equation}
	\I(x,y) = 
