{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:31.000898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e785fc606ce3da93081a72c83c649455d8a69fc7e0b8518fe3c5e261e829d5d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 49 (Factor capture and positive exhaustion) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] One has
\begin{equation}
 0\le\widehat N_q\le QR^2\Id.

\end{equation}
Applying the top-eigenspace rule to
$\widehat E_q=R_q^*\widehat N_qR_q$ gives
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{a,q}\norm{P_{\widehat V_*}r_{a,q}}^2
 \ge
 \widehat\kappa_{Q,d}
 \frac{\widehat{\mathfrak H}_Q(A,r)}{R^2},
 \qquad
 \boxed{\widehat\kappa_{Q,d}=\frac1{dQ^2}}.

\end{equation}
At extraction level $J$, stop when
\begin{equation}
 \widehat{\mathfrak H}_Q(A,r)
 \le
 \widehat\delta_J
 :=
 \frac{dQ^2R^4}{J}.

\end{equation}
Fewer than $J$ promotions occur, and along the nested trajectory
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{j\ge0}
 \widehat{\mathfrak H}_Q(A^{[j]},r^{[j]})
 \le dQ^2R^4,
 \qquad
 \widehat{\mathfrak H}_Q(A^{[J]},r^{[J]})
 \longrightarrow0.

\end{equation}
Consequently every proper residual--residual raw contraction and every
active--residual raw contraction tends to zero, while residual covariance is retained.","status":"unverified"}

