{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.016603+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e78e0dbc83cb77fa0ee888426675bd1fb4b72ee17f3d1b240f68d897058d890","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:positive_parity_implies_signed_monotonicity of arXiv:2605.15401, 'Noise Tradeoffs, Stationary Information Flow, and Structural Balance in Unit-Birth Network'] Assume that for each ordered pair $j\neq i$ such that $f_i$ depends nontrivially on $x_j$, the map $x_j\mapsto f_i(x_{-i})$ is globally either nondecreasing or nonincreasing. Then the following are equivalent:
