{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.515063+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e876e0649f44c2371fc5b29c2b314708544c2caaca47f111f3dd0e4934a6bd4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition \cite{Tor18}, Section 11.1 of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] Say that a $ \rho $-hard sphere configuration $ P\in   \mathscr  N$ is  {\it locally jammed} if each $ x\in P$ has $ d + 1$ neighbours preventing it from moving, i.e. there are $ x_{ 1},\dots ,x_{ d + 1}\in P$ at distance $ 2\rho $ from $ x$ which do not lie in a half space having $ x$ on its boundary.

