{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.644492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5e9c64776e55bc8ce7bf6f17e7dc453e0e8b96809f80cd647cf36e592a4c315c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:resolvent-directional of arXiv:2607.03639, '\vspace{-0.6in}An AI-Assisted Solution to the Signed BAR Conjecture: Uniqueness in the Har'] Let \(x\in E\). There is a bounded linear functional
\(\Lambda_x:H_x\to \mathbb R\) such that, for every \(w\in G_x\), the one sided
directional derivative exists and satisfies
