    With probability at least $1-e^{-c(\log T)^2}$, for any $t\in [T, 2T]$, and $\sqrt w\in {\mathcal D}$, it holds
    \begin{align}
        \left|Y_t(w)-\sqrt{w}\right|\leq \frac{{\rm Im}[\sqrt w]^{1-\delta}}{{\rm Im}[w]}.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.771477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eabe28fad25a1c3561625219e5a398af6c9bed4e06645f53c44ab6436162535","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:zb_nu of arXiv:2411.08220, 'Nonlocal operators with Neumann conditions'] For $x>0$ and $y<0$, we have
