{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.840826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eafbe91a81d70f59439a5ffb00e123eeed9ddee9a3a49dc41272e72e2beb73b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 12 (Bruhat--Schwartz space) of arXiv:2609.03647, 'Extension Problems for the Vladimirov--Taibleson Operator and the Hierarchical Laplacian'] The Bruhat--Schwartz space $\mathcal{S}(X)$ is the set of locally constant
