{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.317253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eb30d2d4a0fa91b83f89c4cea7cad610692b96b35643e371a468ee780f6a96a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2601.10359, 'An Operator It\^o Formula for Volterra Gaussian Processes:\\ The Intrinsic Bracket via Cau'] Let $X$ be a centered Volterra Gaussian process satisfying the Decreusefond--\"Ust\"unel conditions (Definition~(def:DU of the paper)), with operator triple $(D,\delta,\Pi)$ satisfying Assumptions~(ass:chain of the paper)--(ass:energy of the paper) (verified in Proposition~(prop:voltverify of the paper)). Let $\varphi\in C^3_b(\mathbb{R})$. Then for all $t\in[0,T]$,
\begin{equation}
\varphi(X_t) = \varphi(0) + \delta(\varphi'(X)\Pi DX\cdot\mathbf{1}_{[0,t]}) + \frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \varphi''(X_s)\,d\Gamma^X(s),
\end{equation}
where $\Gamma^X(s) = \left\|\Pi DX_s\right\|_\mathcal{H}^2 = R^X(s,s) = \mathbb{E}[X_s^2]$ is the (deterministic) energy function, the last integral is a Stieltjes integral against the bounded variation measure $d\Gamma^X$, and the equality holds in $L^2(\Omega)$. When $\Gamma^X$ is absolutely continuous with density $\dot{\Gamma}^X$, the correction reduces to $\frac{1}{2}\int_0^t \varphi''(X_s)\dot{\Gamma}^X(s)\,ds$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.892011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eb87e574ab35f5457fc4a117d27262191f3b0b6a0d448e9b744a5f7328a8a26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (Moderate deviation principle) of arXiv:2606.18866, 'Cram\'er-Type Moderate Deviations for Engel's Series via a Martingale Approach'] Let $(a_n)_{n\geq 1}$ be any positive sequence satisfying
\begin{equation}
 a_n\to\infty,
 \qquad
 \frac{a_n}{\sqrt n}\to0.
\end{equation}
Then
\[
 \frac{\log q_n-n}{a_n\sqrt n}
\]
satisfies on $\R$ a moderate deviation principle with speed $a_n^2$ and good rate function
\[
 I(x)=\frac{x^2}{2},\quad x\in\R.
\]
Equivalently, for every Borel set $B\subset\R$,
\begin{align*}
 -\inf_{x\in B^\circ}\frac{x^2}{2}
 &\le \liminf_{n\to\infty}\frac1{a_n^2}
 \log\Pp\left(\frac{\log q_n-n}{a_n\sqrt n}\in B\right)\\
 &\le \limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac1{a_n^2}
 \log\Pp\left(\frac{\log q_n-n}{a_n\sqrt n}\in B\right)
 \le-\inf_{x\in\overline B}\frac{x^2}{2}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.056151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eb962f36a4768ae7080d692e86ef4038aa0dd2877f9efa31d949a5bf9e57b19","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 (Equivalence in the rational case) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Assume that there are $\M\in\N$ and a weak partition $(\sfM_s)_{s\in\sS}$ of $\{1,\dots,\M\}$ such that
