{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.613376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5eb994de8ca0c2cdb14ccb0114f721c87a3ed4c6db84566dff978245c801a162","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $k\in \NN$. There exist $k$-dependent constants $C,c$ such that for all $x$ satisfying $|x|\leq n^{1/9}$ and all $n\in \NN$ and $\alpha>0$, we have
