{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.353793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ec0cf697826bd065f6e6d000cfacf0d9816e653e6c71d90c36096a3571238b6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Global 3G inequality) of arXiv:2606.17501, 'Critical spectral behavior and large deviations for geometric $\alpha$-stable processes'] Suppose $G(x,y)$ is the global Green function of a geometric stable process on $\mathbb{R}^d$.
